orum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T13:15:50-08:00","id":332447,"title":"","content":"Demon update. Our intrepid villains investigate the dam. Note Kilroy\u2019s journal covers two sessions.<br /> <br /> <i>Session V</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> A bit less than an hour later, I interrupted Liz and Jack\u2019s little picnic at the lakeside. The good g-man was indisposed when I got there, fucking a goddamn fish broad. To be fair, she did have certain assets that weren\u2019t particularly fucking fishlike. And even so, he found time to pump her for information, in addition to the rest of the pumping going on.<br /> <br /> The long and the short of it, we had two angles there, both of which we decided to pursue with a bit of B and E after dark. For one, we needed to figure out if Mr Langley Fuckhead was going to be fucking copacetic to head up our soon-to-be fish cult. Billy knew right where his office was, so that was stop the first. With any luck, he\u2019d have information there on how to get to the lower levels. Apparently, the others had gotten us signed up to moonlight as goddamn exterminators now, as job the second was to deal with a Rattus problem for the Santa-like old man who parcelled out the Aether. All I gotta say is that the damn Aether better get me fucking drunk or something. Goddamn charity work.<br /> <br /> <br /> They say you oughta be careful what you wish for, cause it just might come true. In that case, I wish I had a billion dollars, a few spare Maseratis, a couple of Venom GTs, a hot girlfriend with commitment issues and a goddamn fucking pony. If that turns out half as well as my previous tongue-firmly-in-cheek wish for alcoholic Aether, I will be at worst some kind of bee-keeping smash and grab from being set for fucking life.<br /> <br /> To back up and let us get from point A to point B: after 15 minutes of wheedling Liz into slumming it with us at the shitholes around the dam, 20 minutes of scarfing down a fucking greasy-ass burger and fries, and a couple of hours of seeing how much I could scandalize the couple sitting next to us without getting them to call a goddamn manager, we were back at the dam without another soul in sight. The handful of shitty cameras they had around the place were easy enough to avoid, by being careful. Liz might have fucking overdone it a little, but we all got through without being seen. Meanwhile, security was just completely fucking fucked - every door we ran across just swung open at a goddamn touch, left ajar by the most ideal of coincidences. Even Langley\u2019s office was carelessly left right the hell open.<br /> <br /> We split up the searching duties. I have a better eye for the lay of the land, and the g-man knows his way around a computer, so I rustled through his desk and file cabinets while Billy gave his computer a once over. He found, mixed in with an frankly fucking impressive collection of insulting limericks concerning Cleveland Shooter, enough to make a damn strong case that Langley was spying on the dam for some fucking outside party, a party that was concerned with the occult matrix and nighttime security. My gut says it's the goddamn vampires, even if, as Billy pointed out, the description fit us just as well. My gut also says the redhead Gloria Langley was concerned about was Puriel, with possibly even less evidence, but there it was.<br /> <br /> Most of what I found was innocuous dam supervisor shit, until I\u2019d dug down to the bottom of the drawer hoping to find a bottle of something. Admittedly, given his cheerio, can do attitude, and god fucking awful puns, I was more likely to find uppers than downers stashed away, but a woman can hope. Instead of either of those, I found a knife, made of bone and painted with blood. The look of the thing, especially in light of the shit Billy found, had us figuring it was an Angel\u2019s bane. We wound up taking the knife, vampires be damned, mostly as insurance in case we ran into the Angel whose bane it was. Billy was concerned with fucking up Valefor\u2019s day, but most likely Langley is working for the occult-ish faction, so worst case, the older vampires try to pin the theft on Valefor\u2019s patsies, with no evidence.<br /> <br /> We also managed to figure out where the hell Shooter\u2019s office was and how to get downstairs. Unfortunately, Shooter\u2019s office has so far remained untossed, by us at least, as right about then 3 gees and their dog walked into the complex. Liz and Billy fucked off downstairs, while I snuck off to get a half decent look at them.<br /> <br /> If I wasn\u2019t a Demon, it would have been the damnedest thing. Two city flatfeet and a state trooper, along with a Great Dane that got its cues from goddamn Scooby Doo. To top it all, they acted like they had reason to believe something was screwy, but they had their radios completely off. Public flatfeet of any type just don\u2019t fucking do that. Something stank, and it stank like Angels. Four of them, as no fucking dog I\u2019d ever seen outside a cartoon looked around quite like that. I had a thought to give them a looking over, see if I couldn\u2019t read anything, but it was too goddamn likely they had some kinda senses going themselves, so in the end I just fucked off downstairs myself.<br /> <br /> The lower level was pitch black, so Liz put on her sunglasses and took the lead. It wasn\u2019t too long before we came to a heavy door, that was this close to having actually latched the last time someone went through. Fucking lax security. A little bit after that, Liz called a halt. On the floor was a skateboard. A fucking skateboard! Around ten feet past it was a bit of razor wire strung across the one path at about neck height. Further past that, the floor was covered in newspaper, barely managing to kinda obscure the homemade bear traps scattered about the place.<br /> <br /> I cursed under my breath at whoever thought it was a good fucking idea to let a bunch of goddamn dog-sized humanoid rat-fuckers watch the goddamn Home Alone movies. They had the whole fucking nine yards - slingshots with small metal shivs for ammo, fucking fishing wire tied to a goddamn boiler door, a hallway sized rubber band that took two of the fuckers to pull back. There was even a goddamn bucket of caustic Rattus blood on top of a slightly ajar door to cap things off.<br /> <br /> I cleared some of the fucking bear traps by sending the skateboard careening through the first few. It wasn\u2019t all that useful, except to have one of the Rattus, the jumpiest of the little fuckers, to go off a bit prematurely. We all went full demon form, and I switched up my treads for a hover thing anyway, so none of us wound up spending much time on the goddamn floor.<br /> <br /> That first ambush was full of lucky motherfuckers. One of them got a decent shot at me, leaving a deep scratch down my rivet arm. The rest mostly went after Billy and not a single one of the regular bastards did anything but bruise him a little. I teased him some, after the last of the fuckers left a sharpened piece of scrap metal stuck deep in his shield.<br /> <br /> \u201cNext time, I\u2019m stealing your damn shield.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man turned to me, his face serious. \u201cIt\u2019s a Process. You can\u2019t mimic its effects with your own Amorphous Process.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes at him. \u201cFine, ruin all of my fucking fun. I\u2019ll steal your goddamn armor then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is within your capabilities, yes.\u201d<br /> <br /> We got around the fishing wire and boiler trap by having Billy jet forward at the last minute and grab hold of the door. The dumb ass rat fuckers tugged on the wire until it snapped, then fucked off. Liz glued the door in fucking place, so at least if they tried to set it off behind us they get caught in their own damn trap. The comedically oversized slingshot similarly relied on not being seen. The setup was fucking gruesome. The ammo they had were limbs of some sort, removed from the vaguely Santa-like old man\u2019s torso, with the protruding bone fucking sharpened into a goddamn point. The torso stood guard over the T-intersection they were hiding behind, impaled on a fucking stake. The ambush was easy to avoid by flying above its line of fire and filling the two fuckers full of lead though.<br /> <br /> Past them we found a pair of rooms, full of fucking glowing golden honeycomb topped off with Aether. There was also another Rattus, not the smartest rat in the sewer. Or maybe it was - that\u2019s not a particularly fucking telling bar. It certainly wasn\u2019t going to be winning any goddamn awards other than a Darwin, as it was dead on the floor from eating a spray of bullets it had served to itself. I grabbed the SMG it left behind and stashed it in my bolthole.<br /> <br /> All of our cell phones went there too, after we stocked them and ourselves with a full load of Aether. Billy analyzed the Infrastructure. Mostly nothing new, except that the Aether it was collecting could be moved via bees, ostensibly for stealth transportation purposes, as few Demons would suspect that a truckload of bees was moving Aether for the fucking God-Machine. Far more importantly, the bees would translate the Aether-pollen they gathered from the honeycombs into the honey they made. And, since honey can be made into alcohol... Aetheric alcohol. I\u2019m not sure I\u2019ve ever heard a better fucking pair of words, other than eager redhead, or free booze, or paying client. OK, so maybe I can think of lots of better pairs of words, but that\u2019s just because I have a halfway decent fucking imagination, not because Aetheric alcohol isn\u2019t God\u2019s gift to thirsty Demons.<br /> <br /> There was only one place left to explore, other than out, and it was a fucking nasty goddamn place. Billy neatly sidestepped the bucket of acidic Rattus blood, giving us all a good glimpse of the four generators, including the unpowered radioactive one that served as the linchpin. We also got way more of a look than any fucking person ever wanted at another Rattus. It was bigger than it brothers, armed with two shivs and sporting three eyes, three balls and the mange. He threw himself, screeching, at Billy, and actually managed to punch through that armor of this. Didn\u2019t help him much though, as Billy responded by putting lead right in the center of his three eyes.<br /> <br /> On the way out, we didn\u2019t find anymore Rattus, though we had a far closer encounter that I ever fucking wanted to have with a few of their traps. The machinery ended at another heavy metal door. This time it was unlocked without me even needing to tweak reality, as a good quarter of the door, including the goddamn locking mechanism, had been bitten off. It led to a cave full of steel barrels, with with similar teeth marks. The owner of said teeth was no fucking where to be seen, so we made it further down through the dam into a room that opened up into an underwater cave.<br /> <br /> I shifted out and back into my Demonic quantum state so I could swap out my jet pack for an aquatic adaptation. Good thing too, even if it did cost me a hell of a lot to do so. It took me around twenty minutes to find a safe route out. Even that route was fucking pushing it, but the other two got out without any trouble, when we could travel the exact best route without any exploring.<br /> <br /> We met up with Jack at the cars. He mentioned the flatfeet had spent a lot of fucking time milling around them, so I gave them a check up myself. I found a GPS tracker on each and figured I\u2019d see how long they\u2019d chase after a stray dog that happened to have picked up a bit of a bug problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> Turns out they were too goddamn quick on the uptake for that particular trick. As soon as I hit city limits, I noticed I\u2019d picked up a tail, a white sporty thing, driven by a Mormon looking mother fucker, and his mirror opposite, a bald fucker in an Animal t-shirt, white goggles, a pair of neon red short shorts and combat boots. That\u2019s my kinda fucking style right there, it\u2019s just too bad one of those fuckers screwed around with my goddamn car. I\u2019m gonna say it was the Mormon motherfucker. Mr. Short Shorts is clearly above such bullshit.<br /> <br /> I kept an eye on them for a bit, to make sure it was a tail before I made a quick J-turn and gunned it down the road, weaving in and out of traffic. They stuck close right at first, but I quickly pulled ahead. I was goddamn close to losing them when my car\u2019s engine died completely. A million plans rushed through my head, from possessing my car and let the dead engines be damned, to going full demon form and flying the fuck off, but so far, those two fuckers hadn\u2019t seen shit and there was no need to play my hand now. So I forced the wheel to the side. There was just enough momentum to roll me about halfway off the road and give me room to dive out and duck into a bar nearby.<br /> <br /> Mr Short Shorts came out after me, but I was in the bar and lost in the crowd before he got there. He didn\u2019t stick around long, not that I didn\u2019t expect him to be right outside the fucking door, waiting. There were at least three exits to the place, so I had something of a chance. Still, not good enough odds for my taste, so I stuck around until closing time, and had a few drinks to calm my temper. Fucking Angels fucking with my goddamn car.<br /> <br /> There were still plenty of folks at the bar at closing time for me to stick with a crowd out the door, but the Angels were nowhere to be seen. The real bulls were out in force, just about to tow my goddamn car, but I played it fucking nice, swore my face blue that I was waiting on my own tow truck, \u201cyes officer\u201d and \u201cno officer\u201ded at all the right places, and they let it go, this time. I tossed the GPS trackers in the nearest gutter the cops couldn\u2019t see me at and fucked off home in a way that took me around my asshole to get to my ear. Fucking Angels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Old Man and the Sea Monster</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Abduction Protocol</u></b><br /> <br /> Once I had utilized my newly developed mending embed to facilitate Speed's and my own recovery from our injuries, she deposited me at Clytemnestra's house in the body of the security man. I made use of my fellow unchained's guest wing, stripping and then binding myself to a chair quite securely before exiting the human's body and assuming Billy Mack's once more.<br /> <br /> The man was quite calm under the circumstances, which speaks rather highly of his training and the caliber of Tomorrow Transhuman's security personnel. My abilities revealed that he was far more concerned with what Sanderson or Carla Pierce would do to him for disloyalty or that there was such a thing as Sanderson's monster more less what it might do to him or his family if he failed his master than he was of what I might do to him. It set an unfortunate starting point for the interrogation but I was able to gain some basic knowledge of the facilities security from him. The areas of note, the uppermost floors and the lower ones, are outside of the standard human security forces.<br /> <br /> Once I had gained what he was going to tell me, we began to negotiate for his life. He seemed a bit confused at first but once he decided that I was serious he gave consideration to what he could offer up to save himself. In the end, he agreed to give me his ex-girlfriend if I spared his life. We signed the contract and then I used my memory editing to remove his memories of everything that had happened after the fight and replace them with some slightly hazy but clear memories of alien abduction. I then drove back to the alley and left him unconscious and naked there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Peterson Chemical</u></b><br /> <br /> Clytemnestra returned home late the next morning, after I had slept and while I was enjoying some breakfast prepared by her staff. She was clearly unnerved and explained that she was having intermittent visions of ghosts. It seems most likely it was a side effect of feeding upon Robin Graves' essence. I am not familiar with what the woman is or with the practice of feeding upon essence the way Clytemnestra does so I cannot be certain. At some point, I would like to investigate this intriguing effect but I am doubtful that either Clytemnestra or Graves is likely going to be keen on being subject to my scientific curiosity. Pity.<br /> <br /> In light of her altered awareness, I drove us to the office. Speed was there, but not functional. Quietus was also present, having been laying low to insure that the angel at the train station did not trace him back to the rest of us or the agency. After some discussion, the three of us decided to investigate Peterson Chemical.<br /> <br /> The building was simple and not heavily guarded. It seemed designed to avoid notice as its main defense, and to be fair, had we not seen the trucks at the Diablo Dam we would most likely not have found it.<br /> <br /> We made our way inside and I set to discerning the infrastructure\u2019s purpose while my companions kept watch over the security guards present. The results were not what we had expected. The facility was producing a chemical designed to keep something very large in a state of high REM sleep while not effecting reptoids or humans and being easily filtered. I considered altering the chemical output and some ideas for how to neutralize the compound or adjust it's effects to include reptoids came to mind. However, I was not about to do such without knowing exactly what sort of monster they were keeping sedated in Diablo Lake.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>What Lies Sleeping</u></b><br /> <br /> Quietus and Clytemnestra agreed that it was worth investigating and so we set out for Diablo Dam after renting some SCUBA equipment. Entering the lake, we were soon able to locate the monster. Clytemnestra also spotted a pair of aquatic cryptids. They seemed more interested in withdrawing than aggression. Our powers identified them as scouts for the God Machine's agent at the dam but they seemed less than pleased with that arrangement.<br /> <br /> I approached them and was able to communicate my desire to speak. They agreed and we returned to the surface. The principle was a female, Ganora. She was the alpha of this pack of a dozen or so cryptoids. She was quite open about her desire to take control of the dam and lake. I quickly pointed out that neither the God machine nor the mundane human authorities would allow her and her people to hold the dam for any length of time. She was disappointed, but seemed to understand the necessity well enough. After some negotiation, we roughed out a plan to forge a mutually beneficial pact. I discussed it with the others and Quietus was very interested in working out a reasonably effective bargain.<br /> <br /> Ganora was quite agreeable to the deal when I presented it to her, and had there not been concerns with Langley Fitzgerald's suitability to lead the human contingent of our newly minted fish goddess' cult we would have finalized things. The delay was disappointing to Ganora, but again she was reasonable and understood the need for caution. As I spoke to her, I assured her further of our intentions and both to distract her from impatience and cement myself and my fellows as friend and ally to her I employed the charm. She was most responsive and I made a point of encouraging her and showing an interest despite her inhumanity. As things progressed, it became clear she was agreeable to cementing our alliance in a most traditional and intimate manner. I had not explored intercourse with a non-human before and the prospect intrigued me.<br /> <br /> I took a moment to inform Clytemnestra and Quietus that I was going to spend some time getting to know our new ally intimately while we waited for it become late enough to infiltrate the dam. They seemed mildly surprised but as demons, neither of them are overly hidebound non-humans. Ganora took me to one of the underwater grottoes that dot the lake and we spent the remainder of the afternoon exploring and enjoying each other physically. She seemed quite satisfied when I left to return to the surface and I feel confident that she feels some affection and trust for me at this point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Those Dam Rats</u></b><br /> <br /> Speed had woken and joined us while I was enjoying Ganora. As expected, she had some colorful comments about my choice in sexual partners but nothing that seemed beyond the usual for her. It was still a little early and so we chose to find a small diner to eat and wait for the dam to reach the lowest levels of activity.<br /> <br /> Once we felt the timing was optimal we made our way to the dam. Quietus remained with the cars to keep watch over our means of departing the area. Speed's embed proved quite adept at getting us inside and allowing us to freely investigate the dam.<br /> <br /> We began at Fitzgerald's office. I took to his computer while Speed and Clytemnestra tossed the physical space. We both found several items of interest. He is not, as I feared, a God Machine cultist. However, he is already very much the agent of some other group with an interest in the Diablo Dam. While there is no hard evidence, my initial theory is that he was sent by the Ordo Dracul vampires. He's investigated the dam's nocturnal security and taken steps to weaken it. Speed located a dagger made of bone and painted with blood, certainly a bane, most likely for an angel. Yet his notes on the his investigation of the occult matrix show a far less developed knowledge of the occult. He is thus clearly working for some group with advanced lore which all fits with the vampires. Of course, he could be the pawn of some as yet unknown player. We shall have to investigate his loyalties further to know for certain.<br /> <br /> We decided to keep his talisman, just in case we encountered the angel it was made for. I had located information on the hidden infrastructure as well as Cleveland Shooter's office. We opted to move on Shooter's office first, but the arrival of a group of security caused us to change plans. Clytemnestra and myself made for the lower levels while Speed took a closer look. Two local police, one state trooper and one hyper intelligent dog, all acting in concert and under radio silence. It was suspicious behavior for actual law enforcement but seemed quite in keeping with angels impersonating such. We chose not to test our theory.<br /> <br /> The lower level was sealed by a door of most impressive stature, which Speed was able to find conveniently unlocked due to her powers. We passed and sealed it behind us to slow or turn back the investigators. But as we made our way through the darkened inner workings of the dam's occult infrastructure, we discovered the rattus.<br /> <br /> The entire area was laden with makeshift traps of a particularly clever and devious nature. The cryptoids themselves were diminutive but likewise armed with weapons they had crafted from the materials available to them. Sadly, they seemed unwilling and most likely unable to communicate dispute my efforts. However, they were no match for us in combat. The three of us shifted to demonic form and we made our way through the rattus and their traps and ambushes.<br /> <br /> Along the way, we found the gristly remains of the old man that Ganora had told us oversaw the dam's infrastructure. They had murdered him and used his body as both bait for a trap and the primary armament for it. As with their other clever efforts, it was not up to the task of demons. At the heart of the structure, we found one more rattus that had died trying to figure out the old man's weapon and a particularly large and further mutated specimen lurking in the actual reactor chamber. That chamber is highly toxic, I will have to make sure to warn Ganora to limit her people's exposure to it.<br /> <br /> The focal point was a power collector, which had been damaged by the rattus but was still intact. As expected, it was a storage center for Aether, though quite novel. It was fashioned in a honeycomb and seemed suited to actual beekeeping which would allow the bees to transport the energy in a manner that would be quite inconspicuous. Speed seemed most interested in the prospect that this honey could be processed into mead, and I have promised her that I shall make her some. However, we lacked any proper means of transporting any meaningful amount of honey with us so it will have to wait.<br /> <br /> We did gather our fill of Aether and store what we could in our phones for later. The way back seemed perilous with a quartet of angels so we moved deeper, seeking the lake access Ganora and her people had been using. We found it, along with signs of some very large and aggressive cryptoid that did not match anything we'd encountered. We braced ourselves and waited as Speed became submersible and explored the underwater cave. There was no sign of the creature and we were able to exit without further incident.<br /> <br /> Quietus reported that the angels had examined our cars and Speed located tracking devices on both. I expressed some interest in remaining to update Ganora on the escalation of the rattus threat and what we had discovered, but no one else wanted to remain. The prospect of a decent bed was also quite tempting to me so I did not argue once a plan to return soon was established. We shall need to set up a means of communication with our cult as soon as possible. The lake and dam are an inconvenient drive to handle everything in person and we need to be accessible to them in an emergency.<br /> <br /> Speed took the tracking devices and left in her car. She has plans to send the angels on a wild goose chase I believe. I drove Clytemnestra and Quietus back myself. My hostess has plans to spend the night with her minion so I had her drop me off at the office. I shall bed down in the cot here in my lab tonight. I am feeling rather tired after the day's events.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Rattus are a variety of Cryptid I will not be sad to never meet again.<br /> <br /> So, the rest of that story. We snuck into the Diablo Dam to try to see what we could find below. Quietus is less a sneaker so he kept watch. Lucky bastard. The first part was not so bad; we searched Langley\u2019s office for info and found evidence he is spying for someone, though we are not sure who. Kilroy suspects Vampires. I would suspect Valefar except that he seemed surprised by what we found about the dam. Of course, Demons are notorious liars, don\u2019t cha know?<br /> <br /> What? Would I lie to you sweetheart?<br /> <br /> Our perusal was interrupted by the arrival of a group which I am pretty sure were Angels. They had access via the door and there were three, plus a dog I am fairly sure was also an Angel. We elected to go deeper inside and avoid the matter entirely, Angels or no. Kilroy had found a way down, so we slipped into the lower part inside the dam.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d say it was a mistake, but it was part of what we were there to do. The lower part of the dam was a hellhole. Rattus are some form of mutant rat Cryptid, and they were apparently carrying on a guerilla war with the humans and angels of the dam. They had, in fact, killed \u201cthe old man\u201d we were looking for and riddled the area with traps. Awful creatures. Darling, if you hear a place is infested with Rattus, keep away.<br /> <br /> We eventually found our own way out. Well, we left via the river, to avoid the probably-Angels above. We found the cars were bugged, but Speed took the bugs for disposal. With that, we headed to town.<br /> <br /> Once I got a bath and change of clothes, I called for Cec\u00edlia to come. I enjoy pacting with mortals, and carefully took a few bits of her soul I gave her much in return\u2026money, influence, greater beauty. She will be our office manager, and will be almost as memorable as I am. I kept Cec\u00edlia for the remainder of the evening. When she emerged from my private wing the next day she was a new woman.<br /> <br /> You should come visit. I can show you my private wing. You won\u2019t survive, my love, but it will be totally worth your while. No? Ah well, you really don\u2019t know what you are missing.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session V</i><br /> <br /> Rattus are of course another Cryptid (I am having way, way too much fun with Cryptids) and it was my job to make the trip through the dam as exciting as possible. The Rattus would not stand up to a straight up fight so it was largely overcoming their traps.<br /> <br /> Given the nature of the session, a lot of it was taken up dealing with the rat traps.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s all for now, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T16:56:31-08:00","id":334644,"title":"","content":"So, I am curious about something. RAW the God-Machine doesn't use / cannot detect Aether but both Speed and Kilroy mention the infrastructure collectin and/or storing it. Is that something you changed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T18:49:54-08:00","id":335662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=334644#post334644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I am curious about something. RAW the God-Machine doesn't use / cannot detect Aether but both Speed and Kilroy mention the infrastructure collectin and/or storing it. Is that something you changed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Machine doesn't use Aether in the sense that a combustion engine doesn't run on smoke. A device that generates waste usually has a place where it dumps or vents that waste, particularly if it's designed with attention to not having too much unintentional impact on its surroundings, hence why so much of the sample Infrastructure includes the place where the Aether gathers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-09-2014, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T00:40:32-08:00","id":335884,"title":"","content":"The G-M Infrastructure at the Dam is actually storing Essence. There is a good deal of Aether there, however, produced by the Essence it is storing. It's build up is part of why the area is so cryptid-happy. The PCs (outside Clytemnestra, who can drain it with a Demonic Form power) can't directly use the Essence for their powers, but can find some uses for it.<br /> <br /> Some of the journals do imply otherwise, but that is what is going on. When it references plugging in, that is using the system for draining Aether in (I think) the rulebook.<br /> <br /> ETA: Or what Satchel said, basically. Did not see that when replying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T14:59:20-08:00","id":336338,"title":"","content":"OK, so it was more just the way the journals were written. I just wanted to be sure. Your APs are too good for me to allow myself to be confused by anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> hence why so much of the sample Infrastructure includes the place where the Aether gathers. </div> </div> </div>This came across to me as more where it unintentionally gathers. It is explicitly stated that Angels cannot sense Aether, the G-M sometimes uses Cryptids as Aether-hounds for this reason. Not that in any specific story could have more of a Aether aware G-M, I just read it as a general anomaly to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T15:14:42-08:00","id":336368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=336338#post336338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This came across to me as more where it unintentionally gathers. It is explicitly stated that Angels cannot sense Aether, the G-M sometimes uses Cryptids as Aether-hounds for this reason. Not that in any specific story could have more of a Aether aware G-M, I just read it as a general anomaly to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <i>also</i> explicitly stated that all the Machine's operations run on the conversion of Essence <i>to</i> Aether and, as I've pointed out elsewhere, &quot;cannot see Aether&quot; is pretty much equivalent to &quot;cannot see B-movie radiation&quot; in terms of limitations on tracking; it's a rationale for the Unchained not tripping flags with every expenditure and for the Machine to allow cryptids to hang around its exhaust ports, not an indicator that the thing that <i>sets</i> the perceptions of angels has a gaping blindspot concerning its most fundamental processes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-10-2014, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T16:40:01-08:00","id":336450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=336368#post336368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's <i>also</i> explicitly stated that all the Machine's operations run on the conversion of Essence <i>to</i> Aether and, as I've pointed out elsewhere, &quot;cannot see Aether&quot; is pretty much equivalent to &quot;cannot see B-movie radiation&quot; in terms of limitations on tracking; it's a rationale for the Unchained not tripping flags with every expenditure and for the Machine to allow cryptids to hang around its exhaust ports, not an indicator that the thing that <i>sets</i> the perceptions of angels has a gaping blindspot concerning its most fundamental processes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that goes more to the <i>scope</i> idea of the Machine. I am not (usually) consciously thinking about the carbon dioxide in my exhales but the creation of it is a fundamental part of my operation. So it makes sense to have the G-M target it sometimes but generally I wouldn't, it would just be a byproduct that it doesn't use.<br /> <br /> I believe we have cluttered Baron's thread enough with this. If you wish to continue we could start a new thread to discuss this (because I do enjoy a lively debate).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T18:30:23-08:00","id":340315,"title":"","content":"I fear I was actually being a bit careless about using Aether and Essence somewhat interchangeably, which Kilroy (being the particular and detail oriented demon he is) would not have done. I am sorry for the confusion. Thank you for reading and commenting, it was something I might not have noticed I was doing otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-15T08:49:33-08:00","id":340849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=340315#post340315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fear I was actually being a bit careless about using Aether and Essence somewhat interchangeably, which Kilroy (being the particular and detail oriented demon he is) would not have done. I am sorry for the confusion. Thank you for reading and commenting, it was something I might not have noticed I was doing otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm just happy that my being pedantic can be useful for once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T13:49:21-08:00","id":346950,"title":"","content":"Heh well it is nice to see some chatter either way.<br /> <br /> Time to check in on the Seattle area Ring. Today is building cars and setting up a Numbers Station. Fun for the whole family.<br /> <br /> <i>Session VI</i><br /> <b><br /> Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> A good... well, a night\u2019s sleep later I was still fucking pissed at the goddamn angels breaking my fucking car. I shouldered my way through the door with its frosted glass window, mad enough to spit goddamn nails at anyone who got on me for it. No one did, so I stomped my way up to the lab to get some fucking science coffee and what I found stopped me in my goddamn tracks.<br /> <br /> The g-man had spent his morning hours doing some virtual legwork, such as it is, on Fitzy boy. It seems that, originally, the good dam manager was a goddamn music teacher. At a guess, I figure he was employed by a school, a church or some fucking rich fucks, considering money, organized religion and \u2018for the the children\u2019 are some of the long-standing big excuses for intolerant bullshit, and he was fired for performing as Bernice Burnhart in the Sisters of Chaos, a fucking drag queen punk band. I\u2019ll give them one them for free, they had a hell of a fucking schtick. Music wasn\u2019t half fucking bad either.<br /> <br /> Once we pulled ourselves away from the fucking train wreck of the drummer deep throating his drum stick, we got to the plotting. The vamps had to be dealt with, if we were gonna get more than a fuck\u2019s chance in heaven of having Billy\u2019s little fish woman cult take off. Killing Fitzy boy wouldn\u2019t do us any favors - either the vamps would replace him with a devil we didn\u2019t know, or the God-Machine would. As it is, Fitz is the fucking weak link in the system.<br /> <br /> We kept the band playing, cause, like I said, fucking goddamn train wreck. Even after the drummer stopped with the blow job, it was more than a little distracting. \u201cAssuming he\u2019s single - and I\u2019m sure he is, considering...\u201d Liz waved vaguely at the screen.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey now,\u201d I protested, \u201cBernice is in a fucking committed relationship with Henry.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz arched one of her perfectly maintained eyebrows. \u201cWell I do hope he puts a ring on it after that, I hate to think he would dishonor his guitar that way. Anyway, as I was saying, assuming he\u2019s single, they likely simply used a pretty girl - or boy - to get him to make promises and take some blood.\u201d<br /> <br /> We all agreed but he was still our best fucking connection to the vamps that didn\u2019t involve getting the anarchist Demon involved. Our plan for dealing with Fitzy boy involved less eyelash batting and more strong arming our fucking way into his place and having a conversation that might involve the 38. Less subtle and enjoyable (for him) to be sure, but les stomach turning than the vamps method, and safer than going through Louis. We might be able to pass it off as interest in the person who fucking stole the goddamn angel\u2019s body, or trade him info on Sanderson, but that\u2019s dicey. I\u2019d rather keep the fucker in the dark than try to pull the wool over his eyes. We all would.<br /> <br /> And then. Oh, and then, Liz and Billy had the best goddamn idea to ever cross anyone\u2019s mind, fucking ever. Billy started it. \u201cWhat we need it a non-descript, high performance vehicle.\u201d<br /> <br /> From the way Liz looked at me, I could tell I had a far off look in my eyes. \u201cWell, Speed, what\u2019s on your mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> I could see her in my mind\u2019s eye, and she was a goddamn beauty. \u201cA Mustang GT, s\u2019gotta be. The new model is hot, fucking lightweight as hell, and line-lock comes goddamn standard even. Black, of course. Might catch a few eyes, of folks who knew their damn cars, but not like the fucking black widow mobile. Out of the box, she won\u2019t be quite up to spec, not the way we want, but I could always do a little supernatural souping up, as the occasion calls for.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd that would run us how much?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSeriously?\u201d She nodded. I gave her a number.<br /> <br /> \u201cDone.\u201d She didn\u2019t even bat an eye. Rich fucks.<br /> <br /> \u201cI could even do a little mechanical souping up, and make it easier for you to glean more using your embeds.\u201d Billy offered. He smiled charmingly. A little creepy from the g-man.<br /> <br /> I turned back to Liz. \u201cThat\u2019d change the number to...\u201d I did some quick calculations in my head and got her a new number, figuring in parts and garage rental.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd done.\u201d<br /> <br /> And so it was that Christmas came goddamn early for this motherfucker. The second dealership we went to had exactly what I wanted and let me drive it off the lot. As a bonus, I didn\u2019t even feel too slimy for dealing with the fucking salesman. I knew a guy who knew a guy etc with a decent rental garage, so we went straight there. The sight of me, Liz and Vivian pulling up in that fucking beautiful machine, and setting up to do some serious modification got us a bit of an audience that didn\u2019t thin out until after we\u2019d gotten the lowering springs installed.<br /> <br /> That was good, as the \u2018police car special\u2019 I\u2019d tracked down might have raised an fucking eyebrow or two. Then, again, maybe not. I did pick a goddamn garage from my little black book. All in all, we spent about eleven hours working on it. Longer, if you count in all the breaks. The Chinese we ordered didn\u2019t cause much of a delay. But then one kind of interior work led to another, and well, Vivian didn\u2019t have a goddamn gaping side wound anymore...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The next day started in a way I\u2019d not had a day start in a while. Somehow, somewhere, Vivian had found enough shit in my hellhole of a kitchen to make fucking french toast. Eggs and bread, sure - I make a mean grilled cheese and I can fucking scramble eggs - but hell if I know where the fuck she found cinnamon. And the milk was apparently actually some shitty-ass Kahlua creamer some fucker gave me as a goddamn \u2018bonus\u2019. The actual milk had turned. So I guess abominations of nature have a use sometimes, if you\u2019re fucking creative enough.<br /> <br /> To top it off, Vivian wasn\u2019t wearing anything but a rumpled shirt of mine. And it was her first time, last night - well, Kilroy\u2019s first time as her, at least. I\u2019ve definitely still got it, even if it had been a bit of a dry spell since I\u2019d fucked off to Seattle. Unfortunately, the g-man was back in the game before we left, since Vivian couldn\u2019t really afford to get associated with the agency, or it with her to be truly fucking fair.<br /> <br /> The office\u2019d been open a few hours when we got to there, thanks to Liz\u2019s abso-fucking-lutely stunning find of a secretary. Cecilia certainly a goddamn lovely dame, and quite the cunning linguist it seems. Certainly nothing to regret coming to work with, and a much better idea than dressing up a goddamn hobo and propping them up at a desk. I\u2019m the one getting fucking propped up by desks in this joint. Liz\u2019s spun story is that the whole goddamn lot of us are pagan gods, hounded from our fucking rightful places by angels, acting as agents of the jealous Christian god. Conveniently close to the truth, semantically speaking, if not theologically.<br /> <br /> Billy checked out his goddamn numbers station recordings right off. There had actually been some kind of fucking activity to note - one of them had an off-schedule broadcast about an hour after the goddamn motherfucking angels broken my damn car, and the Frog station has started up again, unusually varying in speed this time. All breaks from the norm duly fucking noted, we sat down to work out own own goddamn numbers station.<br /> <br /> See, Billy wanted a way to get in touch with his fishy twist. So we hit upon the idea of a fucking shortwave radio, encoded, of course, since cell phone reception is pretty shit out there. We decided on \u2018The Final Countdown\u2019 and \u2018The Lion Sleeps Tonight\u2019 as bookends to our broadcasts, played on a goddamn fucking theremin. Played pretty damn well, to be fair. As a bit of a distraction amongst the encoding, just before the closing bit, we\u2019d have a countdown running, the first broadcast having a nine digit number as its last string, and have it go down by one each transmission. Some conspiracy squint is going to be shitting their pants over that one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cI want to control the dam! ...for you, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll say this for Ganora - she\u2019s goddamn enthusi-fucking-astic. And she certainly has far more of a rack than any goddamn fish-creature has any right to. Her loyalty, on the other hand, might need some fucking work. Still, a good working partnership doesn\u2019t have to go much past quid pro quo and she does realize she needs our goddamn help.<br /> <br /> She was more goddamn intrigued by the rattus than worried, and waffled between being pleased or displeased by the fact the old man had been put on fucking ice. Billy Mac did try to explain why the hell keeping the rattus as servants might not be the best idea. \u201cThey seemed...\u201d<br /> <br /> She interrupted. \u201cAtavistic?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, I do suppose that term would work to describe their behavior.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat what they said about me. I dunno what it means...\u201d I had to suppress a snicker. \u201cYeah...\u201d she breathed.<br /> <br /> That was a catchphrase, it seemed. Liz certainly shot me fucking longsuffering looks every time the fishbroad exhaled another extended \u201cYeah...\u201d Still, she could be taught, and BIlly had her all set up to transmit and receive signal to and from us, with enough goddamn time left over for us to sit around and wait for Fitzy boy to fuck off home.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <b><br /> The Lion Counts Down Tonight</b><br /> <br /> <u><b>The Sisters of Chaos</b></u><br /> <br /> The cot in my lab is surprisingly comfortable, even after spending a few nights in the luxury of Clytemnestra's guest wing. And not unexpectedly, I awoke to find none of my fellow unchained had chosen to come into the office at a decent hour. So I put the coffee distillation on and began to see what I could dig up on Mr Fitzgerald. I really do need to see about a more sophisticated rig now that I have a stable location and access to Clytemnestra's wealth. But for the task at hand, Vivian's old backup (dispute the case being dropped, her good rig was never released from evidence, a fact she did not let me forget) was sufficient.<br /> <br /> My inquiries turned up some typical results, the digital flotsam that all actual people accumulate in this information age. I was able to determine that Mr Fitzgerald has a degree in music and teaching, and was employed for a time as a music teacher. A somewhat atypical background for someone in utility management, but it seems his side passion for performing in a drag queen punk band may have resulted in him being fired and blacklisted from jobs involving contact with minors. Pity, the man (and honestly the entire band) seems quite creative and talented. As a result, he returned to get a degree in business management and was hired to run the Diablo Dam.<br /> <br /> Once Speed and Clytemnestra arrived, I caught them up on what I had leaned and we discussed our options in moving forward with subtly putting the dam in the lovely Ganora's grasp, which so long as she remains in our own gives us control of the dam's extensive Essence generation capacity.<br /> <br /> We mused on several options while continuing to watch the clips of the Sisters of Chaos performances. It seems likely Fitzgerald was chosen as the vampires' agent due to his position and the ability to get someone close via his performances as Bernice Burnheart. This means that his removal would not likely set their plans back that far and would leave us with some other and now unknown agent to deal with. Also, it is entirely possible that Cleveland Shooter's desire to remove him may be motivated by a desire to place a more reliable God Machine agent in direct control of the dam. So for the time being at least, we are going to leave Fitzgerald in place.<br /> <br /> He is also our best option for contacting the Ordo Dracul. Valfore may or may not know how to contact them but asking him would risk drawing his attention to the dam and quite frankly, his anarchist nature makes that a poor idea. The amount of collateral damage destroying the dam would bring is well beyond what we want to deal with.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra seemed confident that Robin Graves while somewhat aware of the Ordo Dracul's leader did not know her, and thus would not be able to put us in contact.<br /> <br /> And so we shall be paying Miss Burnheart a visit after hours to politely discuss a meeting between ourselves and the vampires. If some sort of peaceful arrangement can be reached, all the better. The more conflict at the dam the more likely we are to draw too much of the wrong sort of attention to our plans there. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Two Girls, One Car</u></b><br /> <br /> The discussion of traveling to the dam and of Speed's encounter with angel's while disposing of the trackers from our last trip prompted us to consider our available transportation. We have nondescript vehicles and we have high performance vehicles (well, Clytemnestra does and we have access to them by extension) but the need for something that was both came up. Speed, naturally, had some thoughts on exactly which model and make of car would suit our needs and was also quick to suggest the best modifications to make it suit us better. Clytemnestra did not bat an eye at the costs involved.<br /> <br /> So it was that a couple of hours later we were pulling into a rental garage that Speed had some connections with to engage in some intense auto work before returning to the dam. As I had promised Speed that once I was intact, she could spend some time with Vivian I'd changed forms. According to her, working on the new car was a perfect date. I don't think Vivian would have particularly agreed, but I found the night interesting enough. We certainly had a fair amount of attention from the other patrons and staff despite Speed's clear interest in my current form. I suppose lesbians doing auto work does appeal to a certain stereotypical male fantasy. I used my embed to download mechanical skills several times while Speed assisted. We worked late into the night, even with ordering take out rather than stopping. It would have been a bit less but Speed's patience wore thin and she seemed rather interested in seeing that the back seat of the car was properly broken in. I was a bit surprised that she didn't want to wait for me to clean up and change, but then Vivian does have a tomboyish appeal and I guess the grease and dirt and sweat added to it. Whatever the case, once she did make her move I found myself quite disinclined to stop her and more than a little eager to finish the work afterword so we could resume. And once we'd finished the modifications, she drove us to her apartment where she spent the rest of the night acquainting me with the pleasures of female sexual stimulation.<br /> <br /> The next morning, I woke and found one of her button-down shirts to wear while making breakfast After the previous evening, it seemed only fair to treat her to a proper morning after. Of course, her kitchen was far from well stocked or entirely fresh. But with a bit of ingenuity I managed French toast. I had apparently not mentioned previously that I had not had the occasion to have sex as Vivian before and that seemed to please Speed even more. I am glad that she enjoyed herself, as I most certainly found it an enjoyable experience and I feel I have expanded my understanding of how to please a female sexually as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>By The Numbers</u></b><br /> <br /> I changed to Billy Mack since it is not a good idea for the agency to be associated with a known domestic terrorist. Speed made a show of being disappointed as her nature demands. <br /> <br /> Upon reaching the office, a check of the number station recordings revealed that approximately an hour after Speed's run in with the angels the Magnetic Fields station had an unscheduled broadcast. Interesting that they were not one of the ones active after the train station but the timing cannot be ignored. I shall need to look into the patterns on that one more closely at some point.<br /> <br /> The Frog Station has also gone active. While there is never a discernible pattern to the broadcast schedule, the croaking itself is normally consistent. This time the tempo of the croaking is slowly increasing. An interesting departure from the normal behaviour and worth noting. <br /> <br /> Having determined that neither land-line or cellular phone access would work to remain in contact with Ganora we decided to implement our own station for remaining in contact with my Neptunian paramour. Setting her up with the means to broadcast in an emergency is a bit more risky than a simple receiver but I feel it is worth while as otherwise she has no means to alert us to any happenings at the dam. I should also be able to make use of this station in my own plans to begin establishing a following among Vivian's fringe contacts.<br /> <br /> The format was chosen a bit whimsically to avoid any direct linkage to either the agency or the fish-people. We acquired a theremin and I downloaded the skill to play it. We chose the 80's rock anthem The Final Countdown and I recorded it's opening. Clytemnestra used her Vox embed to read the initial sequence as a chorus of five different voices. At Speed's suggestion we added a nine digit number that will decrement with each broadcast as a red herring. For amusement, I toyed with playing a few other songs on the theremin and ended up doing the Lion Sleeps Tonight which upon hearing we decided should be our closing. I am eager to hear what the local enthusiasts make of this new addition.<br /> <br /> <b><u><br /> An Afternoon Affair</u></b><br /> <br /> Once we'd finished the opening broadcast we packed our gear and took to the road in the new Mustang. Speed seemed quite pleased to be driving it full tilt and we made record time getting out to the Diablo Dam.<br /> <br /> Once we arrived, Speed met Ganora for the first time as I explain to her the current intention to approach the vampires and see if we could agree to work in concert at the dam. I also updated her on the state of the dam as we'd encountered it. Ganora seemed quite interested in finding a means of taming the rattus, which I confess would be more useful than destroying them though I am uncertain as to how successful such an effort would ultimately be. <br /> <br /> Once I had brought her up to speed, I brought out the equipment and she lead me to a safe location to set it up and then I spent a few hours showing her how to receive and decode the messages and how to compose and send one of her own if needed. She is a remarkably clever thing and caught on quite easily, which is good as we will be depending on her to oversee our interests here. I am not blind to her ambition but I feel certain that so long as the relationship remains beneficial she can be depended upon.<br /> <i><br /> End Session VI</i><br /> <br /> It should be noted Langley is not actually trans, hence the continued use of the \u201che\u201d pronoun. We would of course insist on proper pronoun use dealing with an transperson. Langley is a part-time drag queen. Geist has had a transwoman appear, and Changeling presently has two as regular characters.<br /> <br /> They modified the mustang (we used \u201cmuscle car\u201d from Armory for the base build) with improvements to handling and the \u201cpolice package.\u201d It will likely see further modification.<br /> <br /> There is sadly no version of \u201cFinal Countdown\u201d on Youtube being played by a Theremin, though there is \u201cThe Lion Sleeps Tonight.\u201d The Numbers Stations in NTDA are inspired by real world Numbers Stations. None are direct \u201ctranslations\u201d obviously. The Hot Cross Buns Station is inspired by the Lincolnshire Poacher Station (E3), the Naming Station somewhat by Nancy Adam Susan (E15), the Warner Brothers Station by the Yosemite Sam Station, The NATO Station by Phonetic Alphabet Station (E10), the Magnetic Fields Station by, well, the Magnetic Fields Station (E9), the Music Box Station by The Swedish Rhapsody Station (G2) and The Frogs Station by The Frog (XFR). Again, these are not direct ports but most similar stations, many have traits I made up for the in world station.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time, where we get the full band back together thanks to the magic of Skype, the team gets an actual case, and there is the confrontation with Langley and the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> In the meantime Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T02:57:04-08:00","id":367177,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the delay, there was a significant delay on journals. It\u2019s time to check in on our cast of Demons. Here they negotiate with Vampires and get a case not having to do with the God-Machine stuff they have been chasing. Admittedly, there is more to this than meets the eye.<br /> <br /> Kilroy's player is behind on journaling, and next session will probably combine this and next.<br /> <br /> <i>Session VII</i><br /> <b><br /> Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> The chuckle head made himself easy to spot. You\u2019d think we was running for fucking office, the way he was waving to everyone, alternately giving them gun fingers or chucking them on the shoulder as he passed. If there had been any goddamn babies, I\u2019d have laid even odds on him kissing them. I can\u2019t complain too much. It meant we had plenty of time to fuck off back to the car and be in prime position to tail him.<br /> <br /> The tail went smooth. As smooth as a top shelf vodka. The Mustang handled like a goddamn champ and it was all under the hood. There was nothing that screamed shamus, thug or trouble about my new beauty, just power and silk where no one could see. I could have followed the little fucker forever, but it wasn\u2019t long before he pulled up to a nice little one bedroom in the middle of a nice little suburb. Of course, the nice little corset he opened the door in didn\u2019t quite fit into this slice of pastoral perfection, or so all the pearl clutching aunties would have you believe. Neither did an admittedly ragged band of PIs, but a quick flash of a badge got us inside, which at least did a number on the incongruity.<br /> <br /> Any sense that this was going to be your average run of the mill shake down was tossed out the door right away as he offered us poisoned tea and coffee as starters. He was a cool customer. If I didn\u2019t think it\u2019d come out of it with a fucking horrible sense of humor, I\u2019d trust him to keep my ice chilled. He didn\u2019t bat an eye when Jack laid his gun out on the table and all I got was a raised eyebrow as I lounged behind him, jacket falling just so, to give my piece a view of the action.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust so we\u2019re clear,\u201d Jack started, settling into an offered seat. \u201cWe\u2019re looking for the people you work for.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my. Well, you\u2019ll want to speak with Shooter about that. I would just love to give you anything you need to have a gun-filled conversation with him. Shall I get a pen?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot that job...\u201d<br /> <br /> Langley raised an eyebrow. \u201cHarry then? He gets me in so much trouble. What has he done now?\u201d<br /> <br /> I butted in. \u201dNot that one either pally. The ones who gave you that fucking fancy knife, the one you kept in the back compartment of the second drawer of your work desk.\u201d<br /> <br /> He had turned to look at me, cigarette holder perched inquisitively on his crossed legs. He uncrossed them and crossed them again. The stockings were nice, I\u2019d give him that. The gams... not so much. \u201cOh. Them. I\u2019m afraid I\u2019m incapable of talking about that.\u201d He gave Liz a \u2018just us girls\u2019 look. \u201cMind control, you know. Quite incapable.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack gave him a hard look, but seemed satisfied with whatever he saw. And sighed. \u201cThat is a problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> Langley looked thoughtful, tapping a finger to his chin. \u201cI can put you in touch with them..\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd our problem appears to be solved.\u201d Jack sat back, looking satisfied.<br /> <br /> \u201cI will have to tell them you brought guns, naturally.\u201d Fitz-y boy raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged. \u201cI bring guns everywhere.\u201d<br /> <br /> The goober sashayed off to place his phone call. The cheerful and unconcerned demeanor was fucking getting to me, just a little, and the others agreed. I took advantage of his absence to do some shamus work. He wasn\u2019t actively using any Angelic powers, at least, and hadn\u2019t in the past day, as far as I could tell. Tweaking reality so that he was convinced he could tell little old me had enough different reasons for any given outcome that it wouldn\u2019t net us much, and there were risks. So, good old mind reading it was.<br /> <br /> Jack got him talking about things, though fuck if I could tell you what. It was enough to get a sense of what he\u2019d told the big man back home, which checked out, and what he expected to result, which was back up in numbers. He also took the opportunity to remind himself of the command that would send him fucking catatonic, in case we went against expectations and started putting the goddamn screws to him. A neat trick.<br /> <br /> I took the opportunity to go digging instead. We had a bit of a wait after all. He calls himself a fucking ghoul, which means he\u2019s got some kinda goddamn super strength, and can know people\u2019s secrets at a glance. That helped with the lack of pants-shitting terror. He knew, in a deep down way it\u2019s really hard to get outside of a damn crib or maybe the fucking looney bin, that none of us went in there intending on fogging him, or even hanging one on him. Even beside that though, the fucker was cool as a goddamn cucumber. I found a memory of him trading godawful banter with an Angel, just as tonedeafly as he was all night, right up until he gave the fucker a brand new air vent with the Angel\u2019s bane. He called them the robots, and was pretty damn sure Shooter worked for them. Swell.<br /> <br /> I get the concentration sapped outta me by Fitz-y boy offering another round of goddamn poisoned tea. More to the point, about that same time a pair of vans drove up, neatly boxing my beauty in. Only one of the vamps walked up to chin-wag at us, though he did have some fucking line of communication running between him and the goddamn vans. He was a dapper fucker, in a three piece suit complete with frilly-ass shirt and a goddamn top hat. He carried around a silver topped came like it was his fucking cock. He spent more time peering at his reflection in the large silver ball than looking at us. Regardless of where his eyes were, his hands were all over it. I almost suggested they get a damn room before he got the thing off in public.<br /> <br /> We switched up tactics with the arrival of the pretty boy. Fitz we were prepared to strong arm, just a little. This gee was a softer touch, so Billy and Liz took over from Jack and me, with Billy taking lead. The vamp spoke first. \u201cOur... esteemed associate has advised us you wish to speak with us. I am Dieter.\u201d<br /> <br /> I cut in. \u201cEsteemed associate? That does sound better than lackey.\u201d Fitz gave me a pained look.<br /> <br /> The g-man cleared his throat. \u201cIndeed. I am Kilroy. It would seem that we both have some interest in Diablo Dam. We merely wished to ascertain whether or not these interests are contradictory, with more than a few hopes that they are not.\u201d He spread his hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cI see. That would seem to require all of our cards on the table. For starters, you seem to know what we are and this have us at something of a disadvantage.\u201d The vamp looked down, following the path his fingers traced on the cane with his eyes.<br /> <br /> The g-man sidestepped the question. \u201cWe have a mutual enemy. Bickering weakens us both and might draw all the wrong sorts of attention.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, the robots - I wouldn\u2019t call them our enemy, per se. They are... a curiosity. Biomechanical. Compatible. Integratable.\u201d The purr in his voice was more than a little disturbing. \u201cIt is quite fascinating. You want to know our interest in the dam? It is a honey trap. More and more machines are sent, one by one, and every corpse leads us closer to answers that we seek.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack switched to Hawaiian. \u201cSo, what are we willing to shell out?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I certainly have no desire to let them know that I too am made of \u2018compatible, integratable, biomechanical\u2019 bits.\u201d Liz responded in kind.<br /> <br /> Our pow wow was interrupted by our host. \u201cDieter, can I interest you in a cup of blood?\u201d Langley gasped. \u201cOh, what a give away!\u201d He paused. \u201cPerhaps a cup of poisoned blood?\u201d Dieter ignored him, speaking into his ear curl.<br /> <br /> I switched back to English. \u201cLook, pal, here\u2019s the skinny. The name's Speed. We\u2019ve got ourselves a bit of a problem. We\u2019re something like agents, undercover from reality its-fucking-self. So we have you at a disadvantage. That\u2019s just too fucking bad. Best I can do... we\u2019ve got a few tricks. kinda like some of yours. Fitz there,\u201d I shoved my chin his way, \u201cis a ghoul. Got some sort of super strength bullshit and secret reading powers. Now, you know better than me that he couldn\u2019t have told me that.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked thoughtfully at his cane. \u201cYou understand , I can\u2019t make any alliances without speaking to our leader.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe white woman.\u201d \u201cThe dark eyed woman.\u201d Jack and I spoke close to simultaneously.<br /> <br /> The vamp continued. \u201c... yes, both of those are accurate descriptions. I can\u2019t make such alliances, but I can offer recommendations. Perhaps we might cede the dam to your interests, in exchange for the bodies of any foes you presumably would be dispatching anyway?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is certainly an intriguing offer,\u201d the g-man said, and meant it. \u201cI am something of a researcher myself. Possibly I might lend my expertise as well?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA bridge of trust is built a brick at a time. Perhaps. For now though - what are your interests in the dam? I have been, I feel, quite forthcoming. Surely you can reveal that much.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cThe honey, in your \u2018honey trap\u2019. Specifically, securing it as a source of sustenance for the nearby fish people. You know of them, surely?\u201d The vamp made an affirmative noise. \u201cWe\u2019re organizing them into a cult, and they need access.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well. As I said, I can make no promises. But I will speak to our leader. In the meantime...\u201d He offered a business card and took Billy\u2019s number in return. \u201cPerhaps you could cease harassing our esteemed associate. I believe I can offer 48 hours of unfettered access in return.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cSounds golden to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Langley piped up. \u201cTerrific! Well, not that it hasn\u2019t been a slice of heaven, but I do have some TV to catch up on, if you wouldn\u2019t mind scampering.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave the car a bit of a boost, to speed up the ride home. I kept one ear on the radio frequencies and one on the others. Liz was bemoaning the existence of our new found friends. \u201cHow dangerous can invisible vampires who want our parts be really? I need to install more burglar alarms in my house...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack snorted. \u201cI\u2019d install more guns in my pockets, were I you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz ignored him to continue complaining. \u201cAnd what is wrong with that goober? I have never met anyone so deserving of the moniker in my life.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cDear old Mrs. Fitz didn\u2019t love him enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr too much.\u201d The g-man offered. \u201cHe certainly is fascinating. Like a train wreck.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz rolled her eyes. \u201cDamn saboteurs. By the way, are we really considering killing for the vampires?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not anyone\u2019s hitman.\u201d Jack was quick to point out.<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t figure it like that.\u201d I tossed out. \u201cJust if we fucking killed one anyway, we don\u2019t need their fucking corpse. And if we get a goddamn bane out of it, and them out of Ganora\u2019s fins, why the hell not?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz sighed. \u201cAngels are delicious, that\u2019s for certain.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf we gave them an Angel you consumed, would that implicate more of your capabilities than we ought?\u201d Billy looked concerned.<br /> <br /> A mischievous look crossed her face. \u201cIt will appear as if a large spider had drained them of their fluids, and most spiders don\u2019t have gams like there. I won\u2019t even be implicated.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d go so far as to say very very few spiders have gams like yours.\u201d I winked at her.<br /> <br /> It was a short ride to Kiki\u2019s, where I stopped on the off chance the camps had put another fucking bug on my goddamn car. They hadn\u2019t. While we were there, I figured we might as well dip the bill. Besides, Jack hadn\u2019t experienced the trifecta of weed, sex and ozone that hit you after a step inside the joint. He seemed suitably impressed. We spent some time shooting the shit, with gyros all around. Jack stuck around to make new friends when I headed out to drop the rest of the lugs off and go hang out with my old friends, rye and rum.<br /> <br /> I walked into the agency the next morning at the crack of half eleven to my favorite music, full of words like \u2018retainer\u2019 and \u2018bankroll\u2019. Looked like the saps had finally run across a goddamn paying job and from a hell of a broad too. She was drop dead gorgeous, with eyes to die for and a body to match. It was far from hard to believe that some other gee, one Stefan, was bankrolling whatever the fuck the dame wanted.<br /> <br /> She was waving around a police report when I walked in. I grabbed it before Jack could and caught myself up. There was a stiff, Eugene Dodgeson, who, according to said police report, had done himself in while in a locked library in a locked house that belonged to some hoity-toity travelling antique collector type who was currently out of the country. It seemed a damn strange place to off oneself and I said so.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe didn\u2019t off himself.\u201d The dame all but stomped her pretty little foot as she said it. \u201cMy boyfriend did not kill himself!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, peaches, or you wouldn\u2019t be here.\u201d I gave her the soap and went back to the reports.<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe my associate was saying, even if it was his intention, why would he go there?\u201d Why indeed. He\u2019d been there before. The aforementioned bank roller was a mutual friend and ran a business taking care of rick bastards\u2019 summer homes while they were away. He\u2019d shown the pair of them around the fucking place. He\u2019d found the body too, when he noticed the library key was missing. Just the library key, which was found in the stiff\u2019s pocket, not the front door key, even though there wasn\u2019t any sign of a B&amp;E.<br /> <br /> The rod used was unregistered, with serial number intact and no history. The dame, Sandra, swore herself blue that it wasn\u2019t his. Unfortunately, the one she swore was his was also unregistered. The bulls had pegged her as uncooperative. It fucking figures. The cooperative ones so rarely darken my door. The mom was in the picture, and goddamn convinced it was scratch job, engineered by our soon to be client. Sandra did have an alibi. As did Stefan. They were together, \u2018hanging out\u2019. A little bit of grease stopped that thin-as-shit squeaking and she let spill that it wasn\u2019t all innocence and light like she made it out to be at first. So the two top suspects were fooling around with each other as an alibi for the death of the dame\u2019s steady. And they\u2019re both our clients. Fucking swell.<br /> <br /> Still, a read by Billy left him fairly convinced she wasn\u2019t the one who gave our new pal Eugene a new air hole, and not only was it something for him to be fucking curious at, it was paying 500 a day plus expenses, with two days up front. Cecilia drew up a contract and we split up for the leg work.<br /> <br /> I gave Mac a call, and grabbed a double sawbuck from the ready cash. Fuck, I love expense accounts. And it\u2019s even a legitimate business expense, no padding required. Mac wasn\u2019t against taking a break to catch up, especially if I was buying. On my way I got a text from Jack, with a name, William Dodgeson, and a date. Clear enough to see it was connected, if a bit vague on the how.<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe! Teamwork suits you.\u201d Mac popped up when I got there, ever the gentleman. He shook my hand firmly and sat when I did.<br /> <br /> I slid into the booth opposite him. \u201cWhat the fuck are you on about?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou! Your new team, new digs. I heard about the new shingle and it suits you. Speaking of new, that\u2019s a new model Mustang you pulled up in, if I\u2019m not mistaken.\u201d He smiled broadly.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh yeah. Company car. There are some perks to having to put up with a bunch of saps.\u201d I may have bragged for a bit. A bit.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, Gabe, I doubt you called me up just to show off your new car. What\u2019s up?\u201d Mac settled back, still smiling.<br /> <br /> I smiled back. \u201cNot just. Got an interesting case. My client\u2019s pretty sure that a gee named Eugene Dodgeson didn\u2019t off himself. 500 a day sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI heard about that one. The mom didn\u2019t manage to drum up 500 a day, did she?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah. The girlfriend.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSandra?\u201d He looked worried.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere more than one?\u201d I raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, just wanted to make sure. You do know you\u2019re working for the prime suspect, if it is murder?\u201d He looked at me sideways.<br /> <br /> \u201cI kinda figured. With the affair and all, it\u2019s where I\u2019d place my bet. Why\u2019d your boys in blue rule her out?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou got more out of her than us, if you know about an affair.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cWell, you know how good I am with the ladies.\u201d<br /> <br /> He raised an eyebrow. \u201cI mean, we suspected but... it wouldn\u2019t stick. About as much doesn\u2019t add up as the suicide theory, and we don\u2019t have to prove suicide beyond a reasonable doubt.\u201d He looked glum. He never has liked the idea of expediency in police work. \u201cAlso, if she did it, Stefan almost certainly helped. And the kid\u2019s scared witless at the thought of his business tanking as a result of all this. He'd have dropped the stiff somewhere else.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough. You, uh, know anything about a William Dodgeson?\u201d I fished. Usually I liked a little more bait, but Mac\u2019s good to me.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. A cold case, but it got brought up with this business. He\u2019s a big reason she\u2019s a prime suspect. She was there first.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStart from the top with this one, maybe?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnother dead kid. The brother. Shot dead in his own house. She was there earlier that day, but had an alibi for the time of the murder and no motive that we know of. A neighbor saw her run out around the time of the murder, but they had a quick change in tune before it came time to testify.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell isn\u2019t that a fucking angle. You are worth your weight in gold, you know that Mac?\u201d<br /> <br /> He patted his stomach. \u201cWell dang Gabe. That\u2019s a lot of scratch.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cWell, your weight in pancakes at least.\u201d I asked after the wife and kids, getting as far away from dead boys and suspicious girlfriends as I could get for awhile.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The others were back by the time I got back. I rummaged around for the office bottle and settled in for story time. Jack had drawn the short straw and gone to talk with the mother. \u201cFuck guys. This woman - she puts the Jesus in fucking Christmas. Get this, I start nice and simple:<br /> <br /> \u2018Well, ma\u2019am, I\u2019m looking into the death of your son.\u2019<br /> <br /> Well, she\u2019s right off into our client. \u2019Oh bless your heart. It was that Sandra girl, you know. She killed him. And his brother. Shot him too!\u2019 I figured you guys would want the info on that so I got a date and sent it along. \u2018She is an evil woman, evil!\u2019 She crossed herself. I would have thought it a little redundant, what with every open space in the fucking place being covered with another damn cross.<br /> <br /> I tried to steer the conversation to a more useful place. \u2018What about his friend, Stefan?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Stuffy jackass. He turned his back on his heritage, as soon as he made himself some money. Where do you go to church?\u2019 She patted my hand.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack got down the crazy woman's tone so well the shift from judgmental to conscientious gave me fucking whiplash. It did make me chuckle though. \u201cWhat of it Jack? Are you a good God fearing demon?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy responded. \u201cOf course I fear God. He\u2019s trying to kill me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged. \u201cI gave her a vague answer and asked where her sons had met Sandra.<br /> <br /> She looked bemused. \u2018I don\u2019t know. A bar probably. That\u2019s where those wily evil woman use alcohol to prey on good boys. Some place with the door to hell she walked out of, right in it.\u2019<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u2018Right. And they\u2019d been dating how long?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Five years, off and on. Sometimes he came to his senses. He was a good boy, you know.\u2019<br /> <br /> I gave my thanks and got the fuck out of there.\u201d Jack sat back, his hands behind his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe have any effects left behind?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cSure, I looked em over. Wasn\u2019t much. A password protected computer. A couple of new, unworn outfits.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot the kind of shit you find often in a fucking suicide\u2019s closet.\u201d I threw out.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, I guess not.\u201d Jack shrugged.<br /> <br /> Liz had stuck at the agency, doing some digging on the computer. She\u2019d found out about what Mac had said on the subject of brother Bill and absolutely nothing on the house. Suspicious amounts of nothing. Billy had been by Stefan\u2019s and gotten about the same, at least concerning the house itself.<br /> <br /> Billy began with the positives. \u201cStefan almost certainly didn\u2019t do the deed himself. In among the fears of losing business, or answering to his mysterious client, he was most afraid that Sandra had something to do with Eugene\u2019s death. Not precisely the fear of the guilty.<br /> <br /> I had just introduced myself when he drifted off into something like a soliloquy. After offering me a Cuban, which I accepted, of course.<br /> <br /> \u2018Ah, yes, this was a decidedly nefarious act, that should incite the curiosity of anyone! It requires, no, demands investigation. Why, we don\u2019t even know why he was targeted - any of us might be in danger!\u2019 He punctuated his speech with sharp nods.<br /> <br /> \u2018Of course. I have a few questions - do understand we are the very definition of discrete. But I must ask. Who owns that particular house?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Ah well, he is something of an eccentric man and values his privacy. It is certainly one of the more unusual homes under my custodianship.\u2019 He had the grace to look somewhat sheepish, at least.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWho the fuck talks that way?\u201d I interrupted Billy\u2019s recounting.<br /> <br /> \u201cGuys named Stefan?\u201d he offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cPeople from Trinidad trying to hide their accent.\u201d Liz stated. I gave her a look. \u201cWhat? I had a lot of time to look things up.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> Billy nodded approvingly and continued. \u201cWell, I kept trying to get him to talk about the house. \u2018I understand you have them a tour.\u2019<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u2018Well, yes. Perhaps I oughtn\u2019t\u2019ve. But... neither of them are thieves, and it seemed a harmless gesture, to show them such a curiosity. It was two whole weeks before... before Eugene passed.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Only the library key was missing, correct? And you found the front door locked?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Yes, yes, on both accounts. The missing library key was why I went in, and found the... the body. The strangest thing... the strangest thing is that Eugene had never even seen the library key itself, I would swear to it!\u2019 He looked at me, wide-eyed.<br /> <br /> \u2018Never?\u2019 I took a drag on my cigar.<br /> <br /> \u2018No. I use the master key. It\u2019s on my person at all times, as per my contract. The owner has some concerns of it being stolen. It was dreadful. The police wanted to take it in as evidence! I suggested they would have to meet me in fisticuffs, should they wish to procure it. They relented.\u2019 He managed to look very self-satisfied and exceedingly nervous at the same time.\u201d Billy grinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe did know that they might have done with a sharp left rather than a gentlemanly right?\u201d Liz laughed brightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don't think he\u2019s that foolish.\u201d Billy continued his bit. \u201cI did get a good look at that key. It was made of bone, too large to be a single one, but I couldn't find any joins. There was writing on it, ancient North African or Middle Eastern. I couldn't make it out. I left that off and started to get at the suicide angle.<br /> <br /> \u2018You\u2019re sure it couldn\u2019t be suicide? No recent changes in his mood or behavior? In cases like these, the smallest things can be of the most importance.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Certainly not!\u2019 He seemed incensed. \u2018Even if he were able to hide his despondency from me, his closest friend, he would simply not stab me in the back like that.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot even if he knew you were stabbing something of his?\u201d I quipped, a few hours late and a few offices off. Liz gave me a look.<br /> <br /> Billy ignored me. \u201cI had gotten Jack\u2019s text as well. So I asked Stefan about William\u2019s death. He looked startled, for a moment. \u2018Oh, uh, that has nothing to do with this. It was some... issue with his roommates?\u2019 That question mark hung right after it, almost tangible. I\u2019ll eat my hat if Stefan actually believed that story, even if he did believe or at least he hoped it was unconnected.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy had set up a meeting at the house, to let us take a peek at the scene. Liz, I think, wanted a peek at something else. His description of the property manager intrigued the shit out of her, as she wondered if he was \u2018bend you over a desk\u2019 hot or just \u2018buy me a nice dinner first\u2019. Billy went for the dinner, cause if nothing else, Stefan\u2019s idea of a nice dinner is probably goddamn nice. I guess she\u2019ll get to see for herself, fucking promptly at 6.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s a shame you never met Langley, Darling, he is a hoot. I confess my opinion of the Goober has risen. For a man he has decent taste in lingerie, and cigarette holders. We gave him what I will charitably call a surprise interview at his house the other night, and he was apparently sufficiently aware we were coming to dress for the occasion.<br /> <br /> Also, credit where it is due the man is unflappable. And I was wise enough to see him trying to keep us off guard; his apparent fearlessness, his offering poison, his direct references to mind control, his wardrobe\u2026all seemed intent to keep us in a state of disquiet and off our game while the interview took place. Frankly, I am taking notes.<br /> <br /> We wound up meeting the Goober\u2019s handler soon after, once he had changed into a sort of \u201cbondage Princess Peach\u201d long T-shirt. Dieter I did not like so much. I won\u2019t say he was disdainful exactly but he seemed\u2026unimpressed, distant, almost bored. He made very little eye contact, handling his cane and looking at it more than us. I think Speed read a bit more into that than I did, but she thinks about sex all the time.<br /> <br /> Oh no, of course I don\u2019t. I mean, I am now; I am looking at you Darling. How could I not be?<br /> <br /> The end results of our discussion was he could consult his leaders about any form of alliance, and we would not harass his \u201cesteemed associate\u201d for forty-eight hours, nor would they give us any trouble for a similar period of time. These vampires primary interest in us is our biomechanical bodies\u2026and I suspect they care little if they come from Angels or Demons. Of course, I doubt they quite realize just how much power they are provoking with trying to take the agents of the God-Machine\u2026they have not really drawn it\u2019s attention yet, but I suspect things will go poorly when they do. They know it is potent, and expressed interest in the remains of Angels we kill, but still.<br /> <br /> Even if it is Angels their attention is drawn toward, I am not comfortable with being, well, useful spare parts for an organization. I rather like being on top of the food chain. Of course, Angels are an issue, but I don\u2019t need more predators. My preference would be to destroy or consume these vampires, but they outnumber us, and while they may or may not outpower us they can move around us invisibly and have a fair amount of occult knowledge; provoking them is low on my to-do list.<br /> <br /> Eventually, he headed out, and the Goober sent us on our way. We stopped at Kiki\u2019s to show Quietus the place and went home.<br /> <br /> I think we had vague plans to go back to the dam and hear Ganora hiss \u201cYessssss\u201d at us more, but that got sidetracked by a case not involving Angels. I recall promising to fill you in on such things, so once I get a refill is as good a time as any.<br /> <br /> You have beautiful hands you know Kayla. Tasty too. But I was telling a story remember? And I can\u2019t have you for dinner till I tell you the resolution, which I can\u2019t just yet, obviously. It\u2019s\u2026probably a good thing for you this story came up, though.<br /> <br /> So I will give you the facts as I understand them, and see what you think. A young man named Eugene Dodgeson was killed by one shot from a pistol in a locked library on the third floor in a house belonging to a traveling antiquarian who was not home at the time. His girlfriend, Sandra, and a mutual friend Stephan believed this was not the case and bankrolled us to prove it.<br /> <br /> First we interviewed Sandra. Once that was done, we spread out, Quietus interviewed Eugene\u2019s mother, Speed interviewed a cop contact, Kilroy interviewed Stephan, and I did net research. Here is what we found:<br /> <br /> Sandra has been involved with Eugene for a number of years. Five maybe? His mother strongly dislikes her. She says she tends to get men wrapped around her finger, which is probably true. I mean, I am considering seducing her. For information, of course.<br /> <br /> Eugene had a brother, William. William was killed two years ago by a shooting. It did not appear to be a suicide, and he died where he was \u201cstaying.\u201d Sandra was the prime suspect, but lacked a motive. She had a flimsy alibi, and a neighbor said he saw her leave right after a shot was fired but recanted. We know of no reason for her to kill William, nor of them being in a relationship. Eugene\u2019s mother believes Sandra killed both her sons.<br /> <br /> Stephan is from Port-of-Spain in Trinidad and Tobago, Trinidad Island specifically. He speaks with an affected upper-class accent. He manages houses for wealthy people who don\u2019t usually live in the area. He provides staffing to prep them for their owners return, and security. Stephan showed this house to Sandra and Eugene two weeks before Eugene was killed. Also, Sandra and Stephan are having an affair.<br /> <br /> Stephan did not want to name the owner of the house and is afraid of him. The owner gave him a \u201cmaster key\u201d which must be on Stephan all the time. Kilroy examined the \u201cmaster key\u201d and noted it was magical and made of bone. The key can be changed to fit any lock in the house. Certain internal rooms are kept locked and have their own key. Eugene had the key to the library on him, but not to the front door. The police speculated the front door was unlocked, but Eugene insisted otherwise, and Kilroy believes him. Stephan says he never showed Eugene the separate key, and while unsure does not think he even mentioned it.<br /> <br /> The gun Eugene was killed by was not his, and he owned an impressive pistol with Sandra. Even if he did not want to use that, his mother had more guns at her house. Neither had ever seen the pistol used, and Sandra said he had a connection to his pistol that if he were to take his life he would have used it. Sandra and Stephan both insist he seemed fine.<br /> <br /> The library was on the third floor, and the windows were locked as well as the door to the library that was locked behind him. Stephan noticed the library key was missing, so went to see if anything had been stolen from the room and found Eugene.<br /> <br /> It seems like if we prove Eugene was murdered, Sandra would be the prime suspect, which makes her wanting it solved seem odd since she had a new man. At the same time, Eugene seemed to not want to believe she killed William. We speculated Sandra might be afraid whomever killed Eugene might try and kill her or Stephan, or even mistook Eugene for Stephan. So it is likely her skin she is scared for.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s what we had gathered initially. Refill my drink, my sweet, and I will tell you more. Or be my drink. Either or.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session VII</i><br /> <br /> Quietus\u2019s player had to Skype in. It was not ideal, but my internet and netbook cooperated.<br /> <br /> Dieter is a Mekhet, and his Auspex actually told him a lot about the PCs (I am using mostly 2e Disciplines and systems for Vampire now). It was enough to know what they represent and what kind of critters they are, and to plan their next move. Dieter was also fun to play. I took a little bit of Joel Cairo and cranked it up a notch, and used one of my walking sticks as a prop. He was fun to play, effeminate yet threatening and confidant\u2026not a pushover by any means. And of course there was Langley. He posed little threat to the PCs, but had very high Composure\u2026a reason he has been a good agent for the Ordo Dracul. As such, he was not likely to crack without some real work done on him.<br /> <br /> Still, I was quite happy with how the situation played out. I wanted a Noir style situation with untrusting individuals having a polite yet tense conversation in a situation that could explode any moment. I think it worked well.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have a lot to say on the other case, yet, except that locked room scenarios are fun.<br /> <br /> I can field any comments you have and answer any questions, as usual. See you in (hopefully) a week. I\u2019ve got Speed and Clytemnestra here now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T02:52:34-08:00","id":382837,"title":"","content":"Time for some Demon reports. The Agency did more \u201cmundane\u201d investigation of events focusing on the \u201clocked room\u201d murder. Let\u2019s see what they found.<br /> <br /> Note Clytemnestra\u2019s is written from her new Cover\u2019s perspective. Thus, she \u201ccheats\u201d a bit to put herself where events happen as Naomi. For the record, she was in her Elizabeth Covington Cover the whole time.<br /> <i><br /> Session VIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> When it came down to it, our resident femme fatale decided to go for the more dangerous of our clients, despite how nice a dinner Stefan might have gotten her. They both showed up, fucking precisely at 6pm, waiting for us at the scene of the crime. Well, the house of the crime at least. Jack talked Stefan into a short tour on the way to the actual scene, so I could have a chance to do some digging in their long term memory.<br /> <br /> Stefan was a goddamn open book, even if his surface thoughts were mostly focused on what a good looking chippy Liz was. She was certainly turning on the charms. Even if they were mostly directed at Sandra, I can\u2019t say I blame the man for being fixated. Still, a few minutes of digging got me an image of his client, a tall, powerfully built black man named Dantaine Ruhadze. The memories were all set at night, and usually featured him in a well-fucking-tailored suit, though occasionally he wore a deep purple Persian style robe. Stefan thought he was quite the looker, even if he didn\u2019t usually bat for that team, though compelling was the word he thought. I guess I could see the appeal, though most likely there was something about his presence that didn\u2019t translate into pure goddamn memory.<br /> <br /> I also got to solid up the pair\u2019s alibi. Stefan\u2019s memories of the night Eugene bit it did start out with the two of them together, in flagrante delicto while Eugene ate a slug. Their party continued until about midnight, long enough past the 10pm time of death to rule out minor errors on the part of the ME. And that wasn\u2019t even the goddamn end of Stefan\u2019s night. Sandra hadn\u2019t had time to get to her fucking car yet when another one, a dame called Vanessa (last names weren\u2019t precisely on his mind in the moment), burst in and immediately threw him down for a rough fuck on his nice tile floor. She wasn\u2019t really one for pillow talk, just a giggle and a wave as he watched her walk away. And man did he watch her walk away. She was a knock out, blonde in a way that meant disaster for anyone with a libido, and crazy in a way that trips all the right fucking triggers. She was five foot four of goddamn trouble. I have to meet this broad.<br /> <br /> Sandra, on the other hand, was not thinking about going down on Liz in the tea room. She sure as hell was not. So much not that every time she started to, she only gave herself a few goddamn moments to linger on the thought she wasn\u2019t fucking having before she shoved it off by remembering all the times Stefan refused to let her go down on him in the tea room. There was something of a theme. A distracting theme. Enough so that I couldn\u2019t tease out anything about the brother or anything related to the case. Hopefully Liz benefited from what I found out at least.<br /> <br /> Jack read the past quantum states of things once we\u2019d gotten to the library. From the look of things, some fucker had entered and left the library through a hidden goddamn passage that went through the walls of the place, exiting into most of the main rooms aside from the master bedroom. The only exit that had been used, aside from the library, was the door to the front room. It had been opened twice as well, in and fucking out. In the library, our boy Eugene had taken down a book, set it on the desk, and eaten a goddamn bullet, all without any sign of fucking struggle.<br /> <br /> The book he\u2019d taken down was still fucking missing, a fact Stefan took as well as a poke to the jaw. Liz got him up from his goddamn faint by the time we\u2019d established that Eugene didn\u2019t read any \u2018weird Bible languages\u2019 - that being Sandra\u2019s summation of the Latin, Greek and Aramaic that most of the nearby spirit summoning and binding books were written in. Jack got Stefan talking about the book, so I got a good picture of it from his mind. Dantaine had called it a goddamn collector\u2019s item, along with a Persian holy book and a small demon statue, both still in place in the library. It was bound in fucking human skin, and the lettering on it was none of the above. In fact, it wasn\u2019t in any extant language. It looked related to the script on the key, though not an exact match. After I sketched a few characters later, Billy figured it for Akkadian. Jack went with Voynich or some such shit, but I think his mother dropped him on his head as a child. In Stefan\u2019s memory, Dantaine was careful to keep from touching the book. It was fucking strange, considering the way he ran his fingers down the rest of the stacks, and rested his hands on the other collector\u2019s items. Something was up with that book, something that made whatever Dantaine is not want to touch it. Stefan also recalled it feeling interested in him, a goddamn odd feeling to lose track of without noticing.<br /> <br /> Billy had gotten a weird look in his eyes as he glanced around, and we switched to Hawaiian to chin wag things over. He\u2019d noticed a light occult matrix around the place. Nothing God-Machine oriented, but something like a goddamn ghost trap. Unless he missed his guess, the fact that Eugene\u2019s ghost didn\u2019t seem to be kicking around the place meant something had eaten his soul after it killed him. Or the poor bastard had hitched a ride. I gave Stefan and Sandra a once-over and they didn\u2019t have any guests. Of course, if he\u2019d gotten a ride on a flatfoot, that could explain it as well. And would be fucking hard to check.<br /> <br /> Jack wanted to check out the local Underworld anyway, and Billy was curious as shit, like usual, so I played around of bad cop, loud cop where I played both roles so that those two could fuck off to check for ghosts and Liz could go get head in the tea room. I\u2019d mostly given up on him being consciously helpful, so I pushed him on Vanessa instead. His eyes went wide as he responded, \u201cMs. Houston? Do you know her?\u201d He sounded nervous, almost scared. He collected himself a fucking moment. \u201cShe\u2019s the daughter of one of my clients. She serves as my main point of contact with him, in fact.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cDoes her father know about your points of contact with her?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sniffed, almost prudishly, which considering his memories, almost had me rolling. \u201cShe simply appreciates a gentleman of sophistication, that\u2019s all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, a quick fuck on the tile, that\u2019s what passes for sophistication these days?\u201d My smirk deepened as he had the kindness to at least blush, a little.<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t say she was sophisticated...\u201d I had to give him that. \u201cHow is this pertinent to your investigation? I mean, I did show her the house. She had heard of it... wait, no, she found the master key and was curious.\u201d<br /> <br /> Maybe this shit was more on track than I fucking thought. Anything to do with this damn house was at least tangentially related. \u201cYou\u2019re paying me $500 a day plus expenses to figure out how the hell things are pertinent. Are there any other boys or girls who you showed around the house after they were curious about your bone key?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked disapprovingly at me. \u201cYou make me sound like some sort of boorish predator. No, I haven\u2019t. And showing Sandra around was my idea, not hers.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stashed Vanessa away as someone to contact in a professional as well as personal context and switched gears on Stefan. After all, you have to keep them on their toes. Clients, I mean. They lie less that way. Personal contacts as well. Besides, something was still bothering me about the whole brother thing. \u201cSo, were you providing Sandra with an alibi when William was killed?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked confused. \u201cI... well... no, I didn\u2019t know she needed one, at the time...\u201d<br /> <br /> I interrupted his stammering. \u201cNah, I was being euphemistic. Were you fucking the dame then too?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Well. No. I don\u2019t think I had even met her yet. I know William disapproved of her. He took after his mother in that, and in her particular religious leanings. I mean, I myself am religious, but not to the point it becomes tiresome. Those two had no such distinction.\u201d He had a superior look on his face.<br /> <br /> Stefan and I kept up the friendly banter for long enough that the others got back with him none the wiser, or me either. Jack looked fucking tapped out, and both of the boys looked disappointed. Apparently the Underworld was more than a little dead. They did figure something gives ghosts a shitty feeling if they get close, even if the occult matrix didn\u2019t extend that far. Liz just looked pleased with herself. Lucky her.<br /> <br /> <br /> We stopped for dinner once we fucked off from mansion land, to give some time before we paid Stefan\u2019s office a visit. He shared his building with two other fronts. I was sure I\u2019d find the door unlocked, so the alarms on the glass weren\u2019t a big goddamn deal and the only camera watched the door to the antique shop, not the property management office. Unfortunately, a retired bull sat in his car, watching Netflix on some kind of shitty tablet. We didn\u2019t figure he\u2019d sit quietly while we just fucking waltzed in.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou could always seduce him.\u201d I waggled my eyebrows at Liz.<br /> <br /> She glanced at the car. \u201cSorry Gabe, I\u2019m saving the old girl for later.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a mock stern look. \u201cIf you can\u2019t seduce someone without fucking them, I, for one, am disappointed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAssumptions, my dear, assumptions.\u201d She raised a single eyebrow. \u201cI was referring to my jaw. Besides, it would be so much more fun for Jack to bust his windshield so that I could shift the consequences to someone half a block over there, wouldn\u2019t it darling?\u201d She smiled mischievously at the fixer.<br /> <br /> Jack was game and it worked like a goddamn charm. Inside the office, the computer and safe were behind a motion detector that Jack spotted easily. A quick check through the three closets found an entire fucking jar full of unused condoms, a number of spare suits and a hidden panel that took a six digit code. A moment of sappy goddamn inspiration and the code \u2018SANDRA\u2019 deactivated the detector and let us get started.<br /> <br /> The safe was full of keys, as we expected. Stefan had made it out like it\u2019d have been impossible to pick out the library key unless you knew exactly what you were looking for. That was only kinda fair. The set of keys belonging to that house were distinctive - if you had any inkling of an idea of what you were looking for, they\u2019d stick out like a nuclear family in a titty bar.<br /> <br /> Most of his files and records were fucking electronic, so the g-man handled that end. He wound up with a dossier on Dantaine, including a copy of the encryption program used to send messages to him and the account numbers for the European EFT account he paid Stefan from. And he sure as shit did. The fees he got from Dantaine were roughly three times what his other goddamn clients paid. The two of the had met as Dantaine left the antique shop next door, so that\u2019s another angle to follow.<br /> <br /> While in those records, Jack got Billy to note down some less secure empty houses, to give us a range of boltholes, in case the heat got bad. Then we moved on to the Vanessa angle. Their emails started off professional, the kind of shit you might expect between a property manager and his client\u2019s \u2018main point of contact\u2019. The tone got more and more flirtatious until it jumped right off the goddamn deep end. Grammar and punctuation flew out the window in favor of threats, racial fucking epithets and explicit descriptions of the sex she was going to have with him, whether the hell he liked it or not. Her wording got fucking weird too - who the hell uses the word quim anymore? Liz looked it over and decided they\u2019d started fucking before the nose dive, and from what Stefan had said, the visit to Dantaine\u2019s house came a little after. I don\u2019t think it was just me that read a faster down slide after the visit.<br /> <br /> Visiting Vanessa or the fucking antique shop wasn\u2019t going to happen at 10pm, so we called it a night. Liz went off to call up Sandra and pick up where they\u2019d left off in the goddamn tea room. She stayed on task long enough to ask Sandra about Vanessa though, which sounds like fucking superhuman restraint to me. Her opinion is that the blonde is hair-biting crazy, but that\u2019s about the extent of what she knows. Jack went off to who the shit knows, and I think Billy mentioned stealing Dantaine\u2019s identity. At the least, he sent out a text letting us know that the fucker was a vampire. He\u2019d done some digging with his identity theft and tracked down some blurry photos of Dantaine and his father Abdul, working as unspecified consultants for rich eccentrics all over the place. Not quite rock hard proof, but another little tidbit for the pile on the \u2018for\u2019 side.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d made a couple of stops before I\u2019d gotten to Johnny\u2019s. It was a nice place. The cabana boy made a better sour, but the booze was cheap, the bartender was exactly the right level of surly and the clientele didn\u2019t have me fingering my piece. I was settling down with a second whiskey sour, this one heavier on the whiskey, when the back of my neck started to prickle. No muggs had wandered in to ruin the moment, so I glanced outside just in time to catch one of the little river-muck lizard fuckers dart under my car. My fucking car! This one had a goddamn scorpion tail, a pair of fucking bat wings and a milky-ass eye to go with the teeth and claws the others had. And it was under my car.<br /> <br /> I sent a text to the rest of the agency, saying I\u2019d only had four drinks, but there was a goddamn lizard stalking me. Sure, that didn\u2019t count the round of beers I\u2019d gotten for me and the cute little redhead in the last place I\u2019d stopped at. And even less the fucking Sex on a Canoe the stuffed shirted jackass at Alfie\u2019s had tried to ply me with. Or the shots the long drink of birthday girl at the Hart had ordered for the whole bar, come to think of it. It was close enough anyway. Billy and Jack both said they were on their way. Liz offered to head over, but since she had our lovely little potential murderess/client all tied up, I figured we had it under control.<br /> <br /> The two lugs got there pretty quick, all things told. I met them outside. Billy was dead set against filling the fucker full of lead, worrying about the goddamn witnesses. I looked around. The skeevy as shit meth head Jack had just gotten done telling to fuck off was twitching his way to a new mark and made about the least credible witness you could find outside a looney bin and the dame a few cars over was too busy trying to get rid of everything she\u2019d ever eaten to notice and elephant being chased by the entire 5th precinct, much less a few private dicks popping some pills into a pile of fucking driftwood.<br /> <br /> Still, he and Jack started piecing together a plan of attack to get the little fucker out from under my car so Jack could give it a knockout punch while I answered a pair of texts from Liz: \u201cYou alive?\u201d followed up by \u201cI hope so.\u201d When I responded with \u201cIt\u2019s under my fucking car\u201d, her comeback of \u201cI didn\u2019t ask if you were pissed\u201d made me smirk. Then a movement nearby made me look up entirely too quickly, so that the vomiting dame and I both had to steady ourselves on the car next to mine. I was considerably the more graceful of the two of us, if I do say so myself.<br /> <br /> She was in a bad way and she knew it too. She had stumbled over to ask us to call an ambulance. That got Billy to give her a cursory glance. \u201cYou\u2019ll be fine. You should go back inside and drink something non-alcoholic, that\u2019s all.\u201d<br /> <br /> I might not be a fucking medic, but I know the difference between plastered all the way up to her brunette roots and whatever the fuck was wrong with her. She was with it enough to know too. \u201cNo really... I think I vomited up an organ over there...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy ignored her, turning back to Jack. \u201cNow, when I lure it out enough to attack, take your shot as soon as it is possible. I\u2019d prefer it alive, and you have the best chance at that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing man. Looks like a fast motherfucker, so make sure you\u2019re fucking distracting enough, right?\u201d Jack eyed the front bumper of my car with a look I didn\u2019t like.<br /> <br /> I grabbed his sleeve. \u201cDon\u2019t you fucking punch my goddamn car, you hear me?\u201d<br /> <br /> The fucker rolled his eyes at me. \u201cI won\u2019t hurt your fucking car.\u201d The dame retched some more, on her knees between my car and the next.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t want stomach acid on my car any more than I wanted the mugg punching it, so I gave her a shoulder and started guiding her inside. By the time we got there, I was all but carrying the frail, and the fucking vinegar smell wasn\u2019t doing great things for my stomach\u2019s back flips. I sat her down and asked the bartender for a water.<br /> <br /> I left that water on the table, as the lights in the bar let me catch what Jack and Billy both had missed: the blood bubbling around her mouth as she breathed heavily. I figured I could sure as shit get her to the hospital faster than a fucking ambulance, so I picked her up and carried her back out to the car, where the boys were still in the middle of fucking foreplay with the goddamn little fucker.<br /> <br /> By then I had remembered what the fuck vinegar reminded me of. Fucking mustard gas. Some motherfucker used goddamn mustard gas on a dame in my fucking bar, on my goddamn block. I shifted the frail so I was mostly supporting her on one arm, and shifted my other to my demon rod. I fired once, a solid shot. That pissed the hell out of the lizard fucker, who charged straight at the g-man and his shield. I\u2019m no dumbshit. If Billy wanted to tango with the fucker so bad, there\u2019s no reason at all not to use him as fucking cover.<br /> <br /> Billy missed with his shield, but the lizard\u2019s efforts to avoid it sent him right into Jack\u2019s fist. I picked the girl back up as Billy started stuffing the lizard fucker into the goddamn pet carrier he\u2019d brought along. I stood in front of the g-man. \u201cFix. Her.\u201d<br /> <br /> He stared at me blankly. \u201cI can\u2019t fix overindulgence. You\u2019re thinking of Liz.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not fucking alcohol. I know fucking alcohol. She\u2019s been dosed with mustard gas, you fucking prick.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack\u2019s eyes got wide, while Billy just looked fucking intrigued. Jack started ushering us towards my car. \u201cCan\u2019t you two motherfuckers fight this out in the car? You\u2019ve got Sanderson sending fucking monsters to knock you out and take you who the fuck knows where, and a chick getting mustard gassed doesn\u2019t make me feel any better about this place.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laid her down on the back seat. I tapped Billy\u2019s chest. \u201cYou are in the back. You\u2019re going to fix her, and we are going to figure out who the fuck is mustard gassing people in my goddamn bar.\u201d He looked like he was about to argue, but then he glanced at the girl, then at me and shrugged.<br /> <br /> He got her stabilized by the time we were back at the office. He even did it without hacking anything, so we could safely drop her off at the hospital, after we took a moment to replay her memories of the last few hours. It turns out she got a little too friendly with the male half of a his and hers pair of Germans, and had gotten gassed and drained of blood for her troubles. Fucking vampires. Fucking mustard gas breathing goddamn vampires. Her memories got vague after that, but it seems like something called them away before they could dispose of her and someone else objected to her being given a new air vent right there in the bar.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> I am so glad you like the place, Deanna. I\u2019ve only had it since I transferred here this semester, but I have tried to make it my home.<br /> <br /> Oh, the detectives I started working with? Oh sweetie, it was the most exciting thing. Can I get you something to drink? Tequila? A woman after my own heart.<br /> <br /> You are after my heart aren\u2019t you, sweetie?<br /> <br /> So we met the guy Stephan and the girlfriend of the poor Eugene guy Sandra at the house. With us was Gabe, who makes me look straight; Billy Mac, the consultant for the agency ex-big time government guy who is usually four steps ahead of whoever he is talking to or matching wits against\u2026don\u2019t play chess with him; Jack, who hurts people when we need it, and Liz, who my cousin Cecilia works for and who bankrolls the whole thing. Liz is smoking hot, but I somehow don\u2019t think I will ever wind up in bed with her. My job was to make accurate sketches of the sites, and I may have paused in drawing Sandra and Liz a few times to do something of that.<br /> <br /> Oh no, make yourself comfortable darling. I will be sketching you later.<br /> <br /> Aw, you are too sweet. How did you managed to be so sweet and so very attractive? I could eat you up. Have you made a deal with the devil? It\u2019s okay, sometimes I feel like I understand him all to well.<br /> <br /> Anyway, speaking of devils, we got up to the room and had a look around. Jack is there for intimidation, but he also has a keen eye. He is no Gabe, but then who is? Anyway, Jack puzzled out that there was a book missing from the shelf, which threw poor Stephan into a tizzy. Apparently the owner of the house, one Dantaine Ruhadze, had specifically shown Stephan that book as a collectors item, among others. Hell if I could pronounce it, and Sandra was giving Liz some pretty distracting looks while that was going on. While Gabe was talking to him about this Ruhadze guy, Jack was still hard at work investigating the room, and found a secret passage behind a bookshelf! Is that not just so Agatha Christie?<br /> <br /> We investigated the tunnel when lead to several rooms. Jack determined, though his own detective work, that only the door to the library and a door near the front door had been opened recently, so someone had gotten in, though that door, up to the library, and through there and back. He was sure that door had been opened exactly twice. Jack does some amazing stuff.<br /> <br /> So while we were discussing these passages, Gabe did one of the things she does best and buttonholed Stephan about this Vanessa girl she had figured out Stephan knew. Turns out she, Vanessa Huston, was the daughter of and primary contact for a client, and his relationship with her was not strictly professional. The man clearly has a vice for beautiful women. Who am I to judge? If Vanessa has anything like your scintillating emerald eyes, I would be helpless as a babe before her too.<br /> <br /> Of course I really like your eyes my dear especially up close\u2026ah, yes it is warm in here now that you mention it. As I said before, make yourself comfortable, sweetie.<br /> <br /> Anyway I wanted to see what everyone was really up to. Billy Mack and Jack were looking around for more ghost related stuff, and finding the house strangely ghost free, whatever that means. Honestly it sounds good to me. Liz and Sandra were in the tearoom it turned out\u2026I came in just in time to see Sandra\u2019s head in Liz\u2019s black-and-red miniskirt while Liz was leaning against the wall. It was super hot. Let\u2019s just say I\u2019ve managed to have something like that happen to me before, and while it was a lot of fun I don\u2019t think going into detail will do me any favors here.<br /> <br /> Well now, that\u2019s a bold suggestion. That\u2019s about all that happened at the house anyway\u2026<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> You know I could get used to someone fixing me breakfast. You all right? I suppose I need not ask. You just look a little pale is all, maybe you should get some rest today.<br /> <br /> Anyway, what I did not get around to telling last night was that we actually broke into Stephan\u2019s office. Just got underway and already with some shady dealings. Don\u2019t worry sweetie no one will ever know I was there.<br /> <br /> We waited until someone was going by and the security schlep (there is always one) was not looking, and Jack broke a mirror and hid so it looked like the other guy. Gabe got us in. There was a motion detector, but Gabe also hacked the box to turn it off. She is good at this stuff.<br /> <br /> Do you need to lay down? Okay.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack took over the computer while Gabe checked the safe. The keys were there as described. We took pictures of\u2026the\u2026Deanna? Are you?\u2026right. So we did that and Billy found information on the Dantaine guy.<br /> <br /> We then went about\u2026Oh did you faint? Oh dear. <br /> <br /> Oh good you have a pulse. I\u2019m not done with you yet.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session VIII</i><br /> <br /> Those with a greater familiarity with Vampire: The Requiem may have an idea of who these mysterious vampires are. I should give the group a break\u2026they are getting really tired of vampires IC at this point. Though I find it mildly hilarious to hear Demons discussing how vampires are untrustworthy.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for the next set of journals, where they get an additional client, and learn about chemtrails. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:55:15-08:00","id":388851,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look in on Demon. Our Agency gets a new case! Quietus had to miss.<br /> <br /> <i>Session IX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Saturday I got to the office before the client, if not by a whole fucking lot. Billy had just poured me a cup of his science coffee when Cecilia poked her head in to let us know there was a \u2018gentleman with a case\u2019 waiting downstairs. I sauntered down after Billy and held up the wall while he got our potential client\u2019s angle.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello. Mr. Harvey Cannon, yes?\u201d Having a secretary cut the hell down on the pauses for name-fishing. \u201cMy name is William Mackenzie, and this is my associate Gabe.\u201d I nodded to the dumpy little man and took a sip of coffee.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, a pleasure, a true pleasure, I\u2019m sure.\u201d He looked around, taking the place in. He looked a little disapprovingly at Cecilia sitting behind her computer but didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Mr. Cannon, what can we do for you?\u201d Billy prompted.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, right. Well, you see, I\u2019m a bail bondsman.\u201d He passed Billy a business card. \u201cAnd I\u2019m looking for someone.\u201d I craned to see the card, but as soon as I saw the logo, things clicked. I\u2019d never met the guy, but he had a rep. A good one, for the most part. He\u2019d play you straight, and not charge any fucking non-white fee. He was also crazy as a goddamn cuckoo. More poignantly at the moment, he had his own fucking bounty hunter, and never called on outsiders that I knew of.<br /> <br /> Billy wasn\u2019t as familiar with his outfit. \u201cA bail jumper, I presume?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh no, no. No. My bounty hunter has gone missing.\u201d He held up a finger. \u201cBefore you suggest it, I\u2019ve been to the police. He is black though, and they don\u2019t always jump on that. But this man is reliable, a good boy. A family friend! Drake Paulson Jr. His father, Drake Paulson Sr of course, worked for me too, as a bounty hunter. Met him in New York. But he was in Vietnam, and the Agent Orange they injected him with got activated by the chem-trails. Just a couple of days after he retired too...\u201d Crazy as a goddamn cuckoo.<br /> <br /> Billy nodded seriously as I chuckled into my coffee cup. \u201cHow long has Drake been missing? Was he on a job?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCouldn\u2019t be longer than a week and a half - that\u2019s when he brought in the broad who stole all those groceries and then jumped bail to go whoring in Olympia. Once they have you by the balls...\u201d He shook his head. \u201cAs far as the job, he wasn\u2019t on one for me. He\u2019s very professional, very good at his job. Always available when I need him, a chip off the old block, just like his old man. He did take some side jobs. A man\u2019s gotta eat, right? Always did good by me though, a good boy. A family friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> I set my coffee cup down and went for my flask as Billy showed superhuman restraint to calmly ask, \u201cSo, was he on one of these side jobs?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHrm? Oh, right. I don\u2019t know. I went to his house, because he wasn\u2019t answering his phone. He didn\u2019t answer his door either, so I let myself in. I have a key, his father gave it to me. He\u2019s an old family friend...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDamn those chem-trails\u201d I raised my flask for a fucking toast.<br /> <br /> \u201cExactly! Exactly. I knew I could count on you. You understand... But yes, I looked around a little, but I didn\u2019t find anything. He did have a computer, but I\u2019m not very good at them. The chips, you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Even Billy looked slightly hesitant. Maybe I was projecting. \u201cThe chips?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe chips! On the computers and the cell phones. They tell the government everything! It\u2019s how they\u2019re watching these days. You can tell by the names - \u2018Windows\u2019? It\u2019s a dead giveaway. It\u2019s how you look into something, for God\u2019s sake! And \u2018Apple\u2019? Clearly referring to the tree of knowledge. It\u2019s like they think we\u2019re stupid.\u201d He looked at Billy, wide-eyed.<br /> <br /> \u201cOr it\u2019s a riddle, to let them know who\u2019s paying close enough attention, so they know who to watch.\u201d Billy tossed out there. Harvey paled and swallowed, glancing around again.<br /> <br /> I almost choked on my rye and muttered to him under my breath, \u201cWell aren\u2019t you a fucking helper?\u201d<br /> <br /> Harvey took a moment and then picked the thread back up. \u201cYes, well, that aside, Drake\u2019s a good boy, a chip off the block, a patriot just like his father...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGoddamn those chem-trails!\u201d I took a swig to stop from laughing.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight! He had an office, in my building. Come by anytime, I\u2019ll be there. No secretary, half the women in this city are racists - they don\u2019t respect him. I had to let them go. But I\u2019ll be there. If you get any names, run them by me. I know most of the scum he might have made enemies of. Like that Lin Ho fella. Drake brought his daughter in. Lin made a big fuss over it, dotes on her, you understand. Once they have you by the balls... And here, have my key. You take care of that - his father gave it to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was just about to toast the damnation of the chem-trails again when I glanced at Cecilia who was biting her lip to keep from laughing. So I winked at her instead and let Billy take the key. \u201cI\u2019ll take good care of it, Mr. Cannon,\u201d he promised.<br /> <br /> Before he let go of the key, he gave Billy a funny look. \u201cHow do you know so much about these things anyway?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI used to work for the government.\u201d Oddly enough, that seemed to fucking relax him and he let Billy have the goddamn key.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, they let you go when you knew too much, huh? They trying to kill you?\u201d He laid a finger on the side of his nose.<br /> <br /> Billy said \u201cNot yet\u201d precisely at the same fucking time I said \u201cProbably.\u201d Harvey looked delighted and signed the contract Cecilia drew up with no argument. As soon as he left, we heard gales of laughter from the files room.<br /> <br /> I called up Liz, who hadn\u2019t shown up yet. \u201cHeya sweetheart. While you were getting your beauty sleep, some motherfucker showed up missing his bounty hunter.\u201d<br /> <br /> I could hear the ever-so-slight smile in her voice. \u201cOf the New England Fuckers?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cProbably. I think he\u2019s from New York or some shit at least. Anyways, he wants us to find out if it was the chips or maybe genetically transmitted Agent Orange activated by chem-trails\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf the New England Trails as well, I presume? Also, he does know that Agent Orange doesn\u2019t work that way?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cYou are more than fucking welcome to explain that to him. Just let me know beforehand, I\u2019ll bring the goddamn popcorn.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. Oh darling, before I forget - Sondra asked me the strangest question. She wondered if we thought perhaps Stefan had killed Eugene. I pressed her as to why and she said she had no reason, but was quite clearly lying.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fuck?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are, as always, succinct and concise. I only mention it as something you might press her on when next we meet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing doll. Would it be impolite to start off by asking her if she knows she was fucking him at the time?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes dear. Would that stop you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cNot one fucking bit.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Liz showed up at the office not long after, in her Black Widowmobile. Since there was no real fucking need for discretion or any shit like that, I even got to drive it to Drake\u2019s place, a one-story house in the suburbs. There were no cars in the driveway, but nothing looked displaced outside. The g-man pointed out the fucking windows were made of bulletproof glass and the door was reinforced. Not uncommon in his line of work, I suppose, but hell if it wasn\u2019t kinda out of place in the neighborhood. If some fucker had tried to break his way in, there'd be way more damage.<br /> <br /> Inside was similarly untouched. There were no signs of a scuffle, no signs of a hasty retreat. Really, no goddamn signs he intended to be away from any extended length of time. Dinner defrosting in the fridge, mail stacked up on the mat, that sorta shit. His gun case was missing a shotgun and a pistol and plenty of ammo for each. So wherever he\u2019d gone, he\u2019d gone loaded for goddamn bear.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack went right to the computer. His login password was \u2018chemtra11s\u2019, though other than that, there wasn't any fucking evidence that Harvey\u2019s batshit was catching. His files were well-organized and Billy was easily able to find the most recent emails. They were a conversation with a Michael White at <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#81f3e4e5f2f4efc1e6ece0e8edafe2eeec\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"c6b4a3a2b5b3a886a1aba7afaae8a5a9ab\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. The job he proposed wasn\u2019t particularly fucking unusual for a bounty hunter - a runaway teenager to be picked up off the streets and returned to her parents, preferably without any drugs she might have had on her at the time. Drake\u2019s initial response was fucking strange, from a man who was generally professional in every other email. He blew him off, told him not to contact him again with a few succinct and concise comments on Michael\u2019s character. Michael persisted, claiming that the problems that came up last time wouldn\u2019t again, as the people responsible had been fucking sacked. That plus a heavy dose of goddamn guilt tripping got Drake to agree, though he claimed he was going to go with her to her parents, armed. That certainly explained the gun case.<br /> <br /> The earliest email Drake received from <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#5a283f3e292f341a3d373b333674393537\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"89fbecedfafce7c9eee4e8e0e5a7eae6e4\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> was on Monday, the latest Tuesday. There was not a single goddamn email relating to any of the past business they\u2019d apparently had. There were pictures of the runaway in question, one Yolanda Jones, and the usual sorts of details.<br /> <br /> His case files, however, were more helpful as to the history of their relationship. They were kept in an external hard drive (the one without the porn) which Billy was about to unlock with the password \u2018eissales\u2019. His case files referring to Michael included the other man\u2019s address, the password to his electronically locked door, which room he keeps his gun in and which one he fucking sleeps in. See, Drake had found one of the girls he\u2019d picked up for Mr. White in a brothel he\u2019d been visiting looking for one of Harvey\u2019s bail jumpers and had not taken it fucking well. He\u2019d even gone to the police but something had kept them from doing anything about him.<br /> <br /> So we split. Billy and Liz went to the nut\u2019s office, to run the name by him and see if there was anything to be fucking gleaned from whatever the hell he kept in that office. I went to go use the expense sheet to work myself into the red with Mac as far as owed lunches went.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, you prove she did it yet?\u201d He gestured at me with a fork full of fries. \u201cYou know, my wife\u2019s gonna kill you if she finds you keep taking me to these dives.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think she did. Mostly cause she was fucking Stefan at the time. And I do mean at the time of death, literally, so unless your ME is off...\u201c I shrugged. \u201cAnd hey, I don\u2019t pick the place. We could always go somewhere with more green and less grease.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy would I want to do that?\u201d He checked his burger and then doused it in ketchup.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cRight. Mind saying that for a tape recorder? Your wife might not take me at my word.\u201d He smiled and shook his head. \u201cAnyway, it\u2019s definitely not suicide either, unless the missing book grew legs and the secret passage closed itself.\u201d<br /> <br /> His face lit up like the neon lights at a Las Vegas cathouse. \u201cThat house did look like the kind of place that would have a secret passage.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah. Went all around the goddamn house, hidden doors to everywhere except the fucking bedroom.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI would have been shocked if it did. Did you get to see the bedroom?\u201d I shook my head. \u201cIt\u2019s a fucking fortress. No windows, doubly thick walls, and to get in requires a special key and a password typed in some kind of cuneiform alphabet. Even Stefan couldn\u2019t get in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo shit. That client of Stefan\u2019s sure does seem like a fucking weird character. I\u2019ll be sure to keep you in the loop, let you know if there's anything prosecutable there. I actually had a question about a different case, kinda hoping we might be able to clean something up you bulls can\u2019t touch. Do you know anything about a Michael White, anything to do with teenage girls and sex slavery?\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac sighed. \u201cYeah...\u201d That didn\u2019t sound good, but it sounded like what we suspected - an honest goddamn cop being held back by a fucking dishonest system. \u201cHe doesn\u2019t exist.\u201d On the other hand, maybe it didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fuck do you mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere is this bounty hunter, Drake Paulson. He works for that cuckoo bondsman, Harvey Cannon. They\u2019re both following their father\u2019s footsteps.\u201d I had to stop myself from toasting the chem-trails. \u201cCannon\u2019s dad was a real hardass after he got back from the war. We could never prove he murdered those jumpers, though we almost had him on that one he pushed into the car crusher. Harvey met Drake\u2019s father in New York, I think. Anyway, Drake came in one day with some cock and bull story about this Michael White. We didn\u2019t realize it was bull at the time, so we looked into it, but all the girls we tracked down didn\u2019t know anything about a Michael White. The office Drake said Michael worked out of was a laundromat and the house he said he lived in had some random family in it, 2.5 kids and all. Some of the higher ups figured something spooked him, or he found religion and turned over a new leaf and invented this Michael character to hang with the rap.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cAnd you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was there when he came with to the laundromat and he either believed his story or is a really really good actor. What\u2019s your interest anyway? Drake decide to give the private side a try since the public let him down?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot this time. He\u2019s missing. Cannon\u2019s the client, wants him found.\u201d I leaned back in my seat, staring off into space. Something just didn\u2019t add up.<br /> <br /> Mac looked concerned. \u201cRight, I think I heard something about that. The brass figured he skipped town or got back in the biz, for real this time. Well, as far as Mr. White goes, Drake did show us some emails and the the tech guys traced them to an area of downtown nearby the laundromat. To be fair, about half a dozen Starbucks were also \u2018nearby\u2019. The girls\u2019 stories were all consistent. Drake picked them up, dropped them off and a severe looking Asian woman delivered them to the brothel. A real dragon lady type, you know? She didn\u2019t talk at all, just pointed. The brothel they were brought to didn\u2019t know any Michael White either. What precisely put you on his trail? ...Gabe?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my way out of my reveries, trying to piece things together. \u201cHis last job. Michael asked him to find Yolanda Jones. Promised \u2018the people responsible for the incidents last time\u2019 had been sacked...\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac interrupted. \u201cWhat? The people responsible for the slavery ring that Mr. White ran had been fired? That got him working for this guy again?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I figured he was stupid or idealistic or both. He did promise to show up armed and escort her personally to her parents. I me would have been dead fucking sure it was a trap. Maybe it was. Or, like the brass think, a cover for getting the hell out of dodge.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac had opened up his laptop. I waited a second while he read something. Man I needed a drink. I tried not to in front of Mac though. Not in public, at lunch at least. \u201cAha.\u201d Mac said after a moment. \u201cI thought I recognized the name. 15, 16 or so?\u201d I nodded. \u201cShe likes meth. Her dad\u2019s in the hoosegow, and is going to be there for awhile. She\u2019s been in juvie herself a couple of times already. She hasn\u2019t been reported missing, but her mom doesn\u2019t have the highest level of trust in the system. I have an address, if that might help. I mean, I can\u2019t officially condone... whatever it is, but... I trust you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks Mac. That\u2019d be great.\u201d I fidgeted with a fork, thinking.<br /> <br /> He watched me for a few seconds before breaking the silence. \u201cGot a hell of a case myself this morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cOh yeah?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. Big time weird shit. An older wealthy couple in town. They were found dead this morning. That\u2019s not the weird part.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cLots of people die.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe was stabbed repeatedly, there was a big struggle on the bed they were found in. That\u2019s not the weird part.\u201d<br /> <br /> I made a show of considering it. \u201cStabbing\u2019s fairly run of the mill as far as murder goes. And most people wouldn\u2019t take it lying down.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s right. She drowned. That\u2019s the weird part. She was dry as a bone, and lying next to him, but her lungs were full of water.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFull, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked a little nonplussed. \u201cYeah, I guess. The ME said so.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cWell, if the girl scouts taught me nothing else, and they did, they taught me that you can drown in a teaspoon full of water and that\u2019s not hard to keep the clothes dry. Full lungs does make it fucking weird though. Have any motive? Crazy fucking home invasion?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shook his head. \u201cNah, that\u2019s the other weird part. Every single picture in the bedroom was overturned, but other than that and the bed, nothing had been touched.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell shit. There\u2019s certainly enough weirdness to go around this week at least.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The other two got back before me. Not a fucking shock since Harvey\u2019s paranoia about chips meant all Drake\u2019s files there were physical and quickly rifled through. They also only included shit he did for Harvey. Their other bit of business sent Harvey home with a headache, as the name Michael White left him ramming against some sort of mind control or fucking memory erasure. Something I\u2019m sure he blamed on the goddamn government. It did leave Liz convinced that Mr. White is an Angel. That is the sort of bullshit name an Angel would like, I gotta give her that.<br /> <br /> Billy also took the time to check over the numbers stations. The usual suspects had their usual broadcasts as usual last night and the naming station had one of its sporadic broadcasts. So, if any of the number stations are tied with the faction of vamps those mustard gas breathing fuckers belong to, it\u2019s likely to be the naming station.<br /> <br /> We also went over our play with Vanessa. \u201cThe way I see it, we work a honey pot kind of angle. Our beautiful socialite just happens to run into her fellow beautiful socialite self and chats her up while the hardboiled PI pouts in the corner and reads her mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNow Speed, if you wish to be the one chatting up the lovely Vanessa, just say so. I\u2019m far from unwilling to throw myself under that particular bus, but I have been getting my fair share of tail lately.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave Liz a crooked grin. \u201cGee thanks for your gracious leavings there sweetheart. Nah, it makes more sense for me to be reading auras...\u201d<br /> <br /> She interrupted me. \u201cI\u2019m sure her aura covers her tits as well, that should hardly be difficult.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c... and minds.\u201d I continued. \u201cFor the case.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Right.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked at her. \u201cBesides, you\u2019re far more likely to get more information the traditional way as well. I mean, I\u2019m sure I could get her into bed, or onto the fucking floor, as the case may be, but you are a bit more fucking refined than little old me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well. Like I said, I am far from unwilling.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, sure. Just try to have her mind run to things other that your tits?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow about my eyes?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That night we had a previous engagement, so we hit up the fucking antique shop instead. At first glance, there didn\u2019t seem to be much up Dantaine\u2019s alley. The merchandise seemed to be predominantly Asian in origin, though there was the obligatory Catholic corner, filled with gold crosses and images of Mary. There was a handful of jewelry pieces, as well as an overlarge halberd, all kept at, or over, the clerk\u2019s desk.<br /> <br /> Once I got past the clerk\u2019s vague fantasies of falling into Liz\u2019s tits, or, to be fair, maybe her eyes, his mind was an open book as far as everything I needed went. He remembered Vanessa pretty clearly. No too fucking long ago, she\u2019d had Frank, the other clerk, an older Asian gee with one eye, put aside a rabbit statue for her. Our boy here, Henry, had been there when she picked it up later. She\u2019d found the statue cute. He\u2019d found it goddamn creepy. I think I\u2019d side with him on that one.<br /> <br /> Dantaine was easy to pull up as well. An Algerian cat, he was nice enough to help Henry out with his goddamn French, even if Henry did have a tinge of fear in his memories. He had a standing request to set aside any Egyptian pieces they came across. He also had a standing request to never be sold, even accidentally, anything from \u2018Frank\u2019s special source\u2019. A quick rifle back through what I\u2019d read showed that this had the same resonance as the creepy/cute rabbit statue of Vanessa\u2019s.<br /> <br /> So I looked into this special source. Luckily for us, Henry had gone with Frank, once, to a shop called \u2018The Road to Hell\u2019 where the creepy old proprietor, one Mr. Ox, would occasionally give Frank things. These things would always be off the shelf within 24 hours. Now, our dear Mr. Henry was not of the stoutest fucking character, so the fact that the shop and its proprietor gave him the willies didn\u2019t carry much water with me. But his partner backed him up. Frank seemed afraid of Mr. Ox himself, only stopping by out of some fucking sort of obligation.<br /> <br /> According to Henry, the next time he drove to the strip mall The Road to Hell had been in, it wasn\u2019t there. So after Liz broke his heart and tented his pants by letting him watch her walk away, we headed to that strip mall. I was following his memory but when we got there, I had to replay it all again, cause it couldn\u2019t possibly be right. I knew that strip mall, and nothing of the sort was there. Except for fucking today, apparently.<br /> <br /> I looked up at the sign saying \u2018The Road to Hell\u2019. \u201cI would have fucking sworn there was a CD store here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy looked around. \u201cNo Demonic or Angelic activity, but this shop shouldn\u2019t be in this reality.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s what I fucking said.\u201d I glanced at the two of them before shrugging and going in, swinging the door wide open.<br /> <br /> I left aura sight and mind reading running and gave the creepy old fucker matching Mr. Ox\u2019s description a look over. Something went wrong with both. Mind reading got me an absolute blank and his aura just fucking flat out lied. If that man wasn\u2019t supernatural, I will eat my goddamn hat without sauce. For the rest, I can believe he wasn\u2019t being directly controlled right enough, and sadistically jovial certainly fucking fit.<br /> <br /> He kept his piehole flapping at Billy pretty fucking exclusively and his very first goddamn word set my back up and had my hand resting on my rod. \u201cKilroy. Welcome to The Road to Hell.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou seem to be mistaken. I am William Mackenzie. A pleasure to meet you, Mr...?\u201d The g-man was calm and even, as fucking usual.<br /> <br /> \u201cMr. Ox. You can call me Mr. Ox. Well, Mr. Mackenzie, you have taken something that belongs to other people.\u201d In some states, his smile would have consisted of sufficient evidence to stand my ground. It was certainly enough to make me want a drink even without the threat of his words.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not sure what you are referring to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mr. Ox was quick to reply. \u201cThe soul of Vivian Marley.\u201d I\u2019m not sure what it was, but something about that pronouncement almost had me looking around for the ghost of Christmas Whenever the Fuck to show up next. Maybe it was the last name. Mr. Ox continued. \u201cA special place was being carved out for her. There are those in the Thousand Hells that would be displeased. It would be wise, should you have the opportunity, to begin making recompense.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll take it under advisement. I do find this line of conversation disconcerting...\u201d Not that you could see it on the g-man\u2019s face.<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue true, but sometimes one must face the uncomfortable. The hells are all about restitution. Perhaps you might become a bad luck farmer. But you have other business now. What has set your feet on the road to hell?\u201d His smile grew wider. I left-handed my flask, not wanting to fucking move my right from my piece.<br /> <br /> \u201cA creepy rabbit statue.\u201d The motherfucking g-man smiled the fuck back.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh yes, of course. It is a terrible thing, removing someone\u2019s agency. Sometimes, doing such to someone undeserving can set one\u2019s feet on a similar path. For instance, if a young woman, drunk on her own power and wealth, used words like \u2018slut\u2019 and \u2018bitch\u2019 to remove someone\u2019s agency in her own life, to destroy her livelihood despite being left alone with children... then, well, should a similar fate befall her, it would simply be karma, would it not?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d Billy did look thoughtful.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I am merely an agent of karma. You understand. We are both shin, after all.\u201d When he said the word shin, something clicked. Prior to that, he had been speaking English, I\u2019m fucking sure of it. But \u2018shin\u2019 smoothly transitioned the rest of the sentence into Mandarin. I considered for a moment, and he continued in Italian. \u201cI have nothing for you right now. If you return later, perhaps I will have a story for you, and if you enjoy the story, perhaps you might begin repaying Vivian\u2019s debt. Should you look, your feet shall always find the Road to Hell.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy nodded. \u201cGiven what I am, I doubt I am ever very far. Good day Mr. Ox.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood bye, Mr. Mackenzie.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz was the first out of the fucking door, and I didn\u2019t turn my back on the old man, but we all got out of there intact, as far as we could tell. The CD store I had expected was back, and less than a second had passed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, fuck. Just so you know, if you come back, Billy boy, for one of his goddamn stories, I am not fucking coming with, and bad luck farming better come with 500 a day plus expenses.\u201d I finished off my flask. \u201cSpeaking of, we need to connect this back to our current 500 a day.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, if she saw the book while under the mind-weakening influence of the statue, she was likely particularly susceptible to its pull. The overlapping influences might account for the increased downslide we noted after her visit.\u201d Billy pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s fair. And Eugene might have been chosen by the book, which makes up for the fact their connection is fucking tenuous. Well, it\u2019s something to rummage for anyways.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe should also look into this story of Mr. Ox\u2019s. Karma is not the same thing as justice and I for one would like to know whether we ought attempt to break the statue\u2019s hold or simply put her out of her own and everyone else\u2019s misery.\u201d Liz put in.<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like a way to kill and hour or two.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It took some digging but Billy eventually tracked down a likely candidate. A Chinese language site with consumer warnings told a story of a widow, Angie Ho, who opened a restaurant using a loan from the bank Vanessa\u2019s father ran. Out of the blue, the bank turned against her, increasing her rates and payments without warning and hitting her with every goddamn fee in the fucking books. The restaurant wound up being repossessed and she killed herself. The kids were 3 and 5 at the time, which would make them somewhere around 7 and 9 now. Vanessa had been 17 at the time.<br /> <br /> By the time he\u2019d tracked all that down, it was time to head to Alfie\u2019s for Langley\u2019s show. On the way, Billy got a call. As Vivian was with us at the time, Naomi answered, modifying her voice to sound like the g-man. \u201cHello?... No, that is certainly a cause for concern... How long?... Let me consult with Gabe.\u201d She placed a hand over the receiver and continued to speak using Billy\u2019s voice. \u201cA burglar alarm went off at Harvey\u2019s office.\u201d I made a J-turn and sped up, heading that way. She went back to the phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re heading there immediately... No, you stay at home, we\u2019ll handle it... which letter was that?... Q?... As the third letter, you say?... Right, we\u2019ll keep an eye out for government license plates.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian started complaining as soon as Naomi hung up the phone. \u201cI hate having to change back and forth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy the fuck do you need to do that? You don\u2019t honestly think there will actually fucking be actual government agents there do you? The Agent Orange hasn\u2019t gotten to your head?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess...\u201d<br /> <br /> I burned the road to get us there in two shakes as Vivian made up her mind to stay in her current state. I went around back to keep a bead on the other exit, while Vivian and Naomi went in the front. It couldn\u2019t have been a minute before I heard yelling and above it Vivian calling out \u201cAngel!\u201d to carry.<br /> <br /> I booked it around the corner, shifting quantum states as I did, trading some of my standard sensors for red running lights and silvered ceramic resistors covering my chassis and swapping my wheels for a plasma drive. I scanned the radio channels as I went, hoping to scramble any outbound communications.<br /> <br /> Two shots from my rivet gun put the cloud of darkness with spidery wings down, and my quick arrival drew the initial volley. My resistors took the first hit, but the second one stung a bit. Clytemnestra got the still human looking one\u2019s attention by calling it dinner and raking it with her long spider legs, but the one shot that winged her was its last, as Kilroy gave it a new air vent between its eyes. I dragged the two of them and their Glocks into my bolthole before we took a look around to figure out their angle.<br /> <br /> Their IDs were generic, low level shit, declaring them John Smith and James Johnson, from the government. They were clearly low rank Destroyers, probably sent to destroy whatever evidence Drake had, as it was his office they were tossing and his burglar alarm that they set off. According to the others, the Angels had figured that they'd been ribbed. I\u2019d give a lot to know who they thought set them up.<br /> <br /> Harvey was pleased as goddamn punch to hear that government men from the government were the ones breaking into his fucking place. He was shocked they were after Drake\u2019s office, and not his own vault full of research into the dangers and effects of Agent Orange. After I assured him it was safe, he made plans to head over, just to check. We jetted, so that Harvey couldn\u2019t memorize the tits of anyone else in the office, or question why I brought the sketch artist and the hacker to the gunfight and not the g-man. Plus, we still had a show to get to and a contact to shore up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Do you know the name Harvey Cannon, my dear? No? It\u2019s fine, he is a bail bondsman, and quite mundane, as far as I can tell. He is also as given to conspiracy theories as any of Kilroy\u2019s minions. He was in to give us a case to find Drake, his Bounty Hunter, who had gone missing. He had an amusing variety of muddled conspiracy theories\u2026 chemtrails activate agent orange injected into Vietnam vets and the like. Also that the government spies on you though the chips in your computer. Insane as he is, his observation that something called \u201cWindows\u201d can be used to spy on you does involve some interesting symbolic thinking.<br /> <br /> We went to the residence of the Bounty Hunter and wound up having a look around. Kilroy used his computer and found he had been in touch with a Michael White, which is suspiciously angelic sounding to me. Don\u2019t you think Kayla? Yes, yes I bet you do. Anyway, he had done some work for White, something had gone wrong, and he was rather upset with him. White promised those people had been fired. It seemed odd, till Speed did some digging\u2026then it seemed awful.<br /> <br /> Apparently Drake was \u201crescuing\u201d girls that White was selling into sex slavery. He discovered this and went to the police, who uncovered no trace White existed, and circumstantial evidence Drake made him up. Main thing was busting all these people did not make sense to them, and they never pressed charges on Drake, though I think he was still being investigated.<br /> <br /> We planned to check the home of the latest runaway, but we decided to investigate the other case first. Checking Cannon\u2019s office only showed he was not lying, which was our assumption. However, we were called back that night because of a burglar alarm. It was actually Drake\u2019s office inside the Bail Bonds place\u2026and there were two low ranking Angels moving around. They died fighting us. I did not eat either up them so there is still some room in my tummy, just for your information.<br /> <br /> Oh you had me thinking about dinner. The other thing was we went to check on the Sandra case. So\u2026apparently there was some sort of cosmic justice going on there, maybe? As meted out by a \u201cMr. Ox\u201d for Vanessa running some poor girl when she was a teenager, apparently out of spite. I am unsure how I feel about that. Mr. Ox, who has a magical store called \u201cThe Road to Hell,\u201d was interested in cultivating us as \u201cBad Luck Farmers\u201d to mete out some of this justice.<br /> <br /> What? Oh, so the antique place, one of the people running it was a \u201cBad Luck Farmer\u201d for Mr. Ox to pay off some sort of Karmic debt himself. Mr. Ox gives him things, he puts them in the shop, people buy them with a Karmic Debt to pay. Apparently for Vanessa it was some sort of rabbit. I honestly\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026What? Oh I suppose it does sound like some sort of horror anthology, now that you mention it. I wonder if the idea is taken?<br /> <br /> Is Mr. Ox an Angel? I don\u2019t think so. I certainly hope not. What would give you that idea?<br /> <br /> I see. Interesting. I guess that technically would make him an Angel if it is true but\u2026I\u2019m not sure.<br /> <br /> You are a clever one, cute and clever, it seems. Why don\u2019t you come over to the house and\u2026<br /> <br /> Right, because I am hungry. Yes, definitely too clever.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session IX</i><br /> <br /> Session went well, new plot since they were getting close to winding up the old one. Harvey was really fun to play and had the group in stitches at times.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ox, much like Dantaine Ruhadze, is a character from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\">Balance of Shadows</a>, my<b> Geist</b> campaign. He is a complicated figure. He is somewhat based on a character from <i>Vampire: The Masquerade Bloodlines</i>, but I\u2019ve taken a number of liberties with him hashing out his back story and role in the cosmos.<br /> <br /> Speed Demon\u2019s player has created a handy chart with the current plots outlined from an IC perspective. <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Plots_zpso7w4pdqf.jpeg\" target=\"_blank\">Check it out</a><br /> <br /> We are adding a player, who appears in the end of the next session. Looking at a Destroyer Saboteur/Integrator, which is complicated. That brings the cast to a number I am more comfortable with, especially given Quietus\u2019s player frequently has to miss.<br /> <br /> You can meet him then. Comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T18:17:20-08:00","id":389212,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Agent Orange they injected him with got activated by the chem-trails&quot;<br /> WWI Vampires... Why does it have to be WWI Vampires? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s right. She drowned. That\u2019s the weird part. She was dry as a bone, and lying next to him, but her lungs were full of water.\u201d<br /> <br /> Death by Bound, mayhaps?<br /> <br /> Interesting. Mr. Ox does not appear to be one of the Unchained(at least, from our hero's reactions), meaning he's probably one of those Inferno things I know nothing about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T22:35:35-08:00","id":389457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=389212#post389212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WWI Vampires... Why does it have to be WWI Vampires? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's mostly Harvey being crazy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cThat\u2019s right. She drowned. That\u2019s the weird part. She was dry as a bone, and lying next to him, but her lungs were full of water.\u201d<br /> <br /> Death by Bound, mayhaps? </div> </div> </div>maaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaybe<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Interesting. Mr. Ox does not appear to be one of the Unchained(at least, from our hero's reactions), meaning he's probably one of those Inferno things I know nothing about. </div> </div> </div>Mr. Ox isn't a Keberoi, but is more closely related to them than an Inferno Demon. &quot;Demon&quot; is a good colloquial term and poor technical term to describe him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: