href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T01:49:03-08:00","id":406506,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check in on the agency. After the run in with some Angels they go to take in a concert. Afterwards, Quietus gets restless. Note we introduce a new PC at the end of the session, Jared Evans/Fulgur<br /> <br /> <i>Session X</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> \u201cYou sure know how to treat a female impersonator, but Henry baby - just the tip means just the tip.\u201d Langley started off the show with exactly the level of fucking class we expected. A punk cover of La Bamba led straight into the centerpiece of their show, a goddamn spoken word punk ballad about being Dave Thomas\u2019 bitches while his daughter Wendy watched from behind one way glass. I went to the bar one verse in and got a double handful - I knew I\u2019d fucking need it. Naomi called up a friend and Jack sat restlessly, while Vivian played like she didn\u2019t know us, wanting to distance that cover from the agency, at the very least as far as the goober knew. They ceded the stage to the next act with a punk version of the fucking theme to goddamn Mr Rogers. Ignoring the whiplash from the goddamn ridiculous levels of what-the-fuck that lived in their lyrics, the fuckers were more than decent musicians who put on a hell of a show. I wandered over with Jack and my fifth to rope the band after they\u2019d cleared off.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, you came!\u201d Langley palmed a Magnum condom and dropped it to the floor from behind his guitar. \u201cHenry, you rogue! I can\u2019t take him anywhere. Sorry gentleman, I\u2019m not in charge of the drinks - I can\u2019t poison you this time.\u201d He smiled, charmingly for a doofus.<br /> <br /> Jack and I traded some banter with him before the fixer settled in for the soft touch. \u201cSo, how\u2019d you learn to play like that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, my mother was in a rock band, perhaps you heard of them - the Flaming Tampons?\u201d Jack and I shook our heads. \u201cThey opened for Bikini Kill, you know. My father...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWas her guitar?\u201d I interrupted, leering at Henry.<br /> <br /> \u201cWas French-Canadian, actually. It\u2019s why I\u2019m allowed to say things like repertoire.\u201d His French accent was atrocious. \u201cHe had a thing for punk girls. I was a great disappointment, not having been born on stage. My mother did try.\u201d<br /> <br /> By now, Vivian had drifted over to make her play. \u201cSurely they couldn\u2019t blame you for that?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked at her, dramatically downcast, and laid a hand over his heart. \u201cNo, but I can.\u201d<br /> <br /> I left Vivian fighting the good fight while Jack chatted up Langley\u2019s band mates. I believe I heard something about Henry\u2019s preference for being on top before I got out of earshot. A quick stop by Naomi\u2019s table got me both her belief that Langley didn\u2019t have any vampire handlers in the place and proof that she was finger fucking the shit out of her friend Deanna. I kept the bartender company and the whiskey bottle moving until Vivian wound up going home with the goober, Naomi fucked off with her finger fuckee and Jack left his new boyfriends behind. With any luck, tomorrow\u2019s bring an end to the Stefan case, and we could focus on the probably-a-fucking-angel Michael White.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The best laid plans, and all that fucking shit, right? Turns out we wrapped up the Stefan case about 12 hours ahead of schedule, thanks to Jack. The fucker woke me up with a phone call. \u201cThe fuck you want?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was manic energy in his voice. \u201cYour ass, here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t get my ass anywhere, bub. Wrong tubing.\u201d I checked the time. Fucking 2:07. I must have just dropped off.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, I\u2019ve gotten enough ass tonight. I need your help, here, now. I just got done fucking Vanessa.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou need help fucking Vanessa?\u201d I sat up and ran my fingers through my hair.<br /> <br /> I could hear him staring at the phone, somehow. \u201cNo. Look, Liz\u2019s lay Robin says she has a spirit in her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I checked a can on my bedside table. It was flat. And probably a few days old. I checked the next one. \u201cS\u2019it shaped like a rabbit?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cJust get the fuck to Kiki\u2019s...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, sure.\u201d I shrugged into my jacket and buttoned up another button or two, crooked, probably. Fuck it. The third can was flat too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Jack was twitchy as shit when I got there, motioning me into a booth, ducking down to hide from Vanessa, who had a ring of admirers. A pair of the goddamn hippiest looking motherfuckers I\u2019d seen in a week of fucking Sundays were at a nearby booth and some motherfucker in a goddamn bunny suit loitered at the door. Jack glared him aside as I walked in.<br /> <br /> Apparently, our paranoid fixer had been antagonizing Ms Houston, flirting with every other goddamn bird in the joint, while making sure she knew she was being passed over. The next thing he knew, he was trying out the nice shoes line on her and they were in the back room, fucking each other\u2019s brains out. Or at least her joints. Whatever Robin is, she can read people\u2019s physical states, and according to her, she managed to fuck her spine up in a serious way.<br /> <br /> I explained the rabbit situation to him, while he obsessed over the fact she was being supernatural in public, like we\u2019re the only ones allowed to play with the toys. Sometimes the bad guys aren\u2019t obliging enough to fight with one goddamn hand behind their backs. Still, the poor lug was spooked. If I\u2019d been less drunk, or less woken up at 2 in the goddamn morning, I might have given him less of a hard time. Still, he\u2019s a big boy - I\u2019m sure he\u2019ll be fine.<br /> <br /> He\u2019d called me in to help tail her, so we did. Her next stop was Mavericks, so I got to check in with good old Bobby Right. The fucker was in fine form, as usual. He\u2019s a pig and a cad, but he keeps the drinks coming and even holds off on the grab ass. Well, he holds off when it\u2019s my ass involved. He sent one of the girls on his arms off with a pat on her ass as he came over to clap me on the shoulder. \u201cGabe! You missed the wet t-shirt contest!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t be here every goddamn Saturday brother.\u201d I nodded once over my shoulder. \u201cThis is Jack. Works with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Bobby extended his hand. \u201cBobby. Bobby Right. You can call me Mr Right, all the ladies do.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes and grinned broadly at Jack, and held my arm out. He was looking at Bobby\u2019s hand like it was going to fucking bite him. \u201cNow Jack, don\u2019t go flirting with every dame this time, huh?\u201d Now he was looking at me like I\u2019d grown another head. \u201cI\u2019m just saying. Got you in a fuckton of trouble last time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Bobby looked sympathetic. \u201cVitamin D supplements, man, can\u2019t recommend those babies enough. And you should never feel bad if you need a little blue pill for Round 7. No shame in it.\u201d He splayed his hands out to emphasize his point and glanced over at the bar and my outstretched arm. \u201cRick! The woman who gets more pussy than you ever will needs a drink!\u201d How can you not like the guy, I ask you?<br /> <br /> Rick brought me my drink and Bobby wandered off to go hit on some hot young doll. I settled in to watch Vanessa work for a second before I turned on the aura sight and mind reading sensors. The dame was of two fucking minds, that was certain, and the one I\u2019d have called \u2018not her\u2019 was definitely calling the goddamn shots. She was a bundle of nerves when \u2018she\u2019 wasn\u2019t pleased as punch with \u2018herself\u2019. Her surface thoughts hammered the point home, filled as they were with resigned dread over who she would have to fuck next.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t dwell on it. Honestly, it just about matched up exactly with what we expected, given Mr. Ox\u2019s cackling description. I dived in to her memories to try and solve out fucking case, instead. It was touch and go for the first few minutes of digging, but I managed to tease out memories of the night Eugene offed himself.<br /> <br /> We hadn\u2019t been far from right in the way we\u2019d tumbled it. One thing we missed in our angle was that the book didn\u2019t actually influence anyone. Well, not fucking directly anyway. The goddamn rabbit in her fucking head recognized it as a kindred goddamn spirit and decided to break out its fucking playmate all on its own. It put the whammy on Eugene and was working on the ritual to let the book hitch a ride out in him when Vanessa strapped on some brass ones long enough to get the mugg to pull the trigger. The two days of torture that came after did a number on her inclination to do anything so ballsy again.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll say one thing - Jack sure knows how the hell to sober a girl up. I rode out the rest of the goddamn thankfully vague memory of fire and pain and kept up my concentration. I wagered someone would care about what got her into this fucking mess. Her memories of Angie Ho weren\u2019t nearly so painful, but they were dusty and mothballed enough to take some digging. She\u2019d gone into Ho\u2019s restaurant looking for free food and when the shit she kicked up when Angie wouldn\u2019t give it to her got her kicked the hell out, she fucked the widow over. She regretted it, and felt guilty in that vague way you do about shit you fucked up as a kid.<br /> <br /> I shook my head and accepted the refill Bobby waved my way. I motioned Jack away from his attempts to flirt with every girl there, in some kind of effort to reassert his rugged masculinity I'm sure, and into a relatively private booth. I filled him in on what I\u2019d found. \u201cSo I\u2019m going to see if I can\u2019t fucking get her to invite me home, and I\u2019ll toss the book and statue through the first fucking doorway I see.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked at me like he didn\u2019t understand the Navajo I was speaking in. The Naomi devil on my shoulder asked, \u201cWouldn\u2019t it be easier to just follow her home? Or do you just want to get laid that much?\u201d<br /> <br /> I waved my hand to dissipate what I was pretty sure was a hallucination and addressed Jack. \u201cI want to see if I can\u2019t get her out of here before she fucking rapes someone again or gets raped herself. I\u2019ve had to make enough excuses in my time - I\u2019ll get out once I\u2019ve got the goods.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That didn\u2019t go quite as planned, but at least the fall back plan of tailing her home was something I was both good at and had the equipment for. Creepy rabbit statues prefer cock, apparently. After sitting around drinking until her body gave out, I was ready to drive. I souped up the car more than was strictly necessary; I\u2019m not sure the broad would have noticed an 18 wheeler on her six. She even forgot to lock the door, as we found after giving her time to fall the fuck asleep.<br /> <br /> It was the easiest tossing I\u2019d ever been part of. The book was all but on the goddamn coffee table, and the statue had been tossed aside, empty. I wasn\u2019t sure what good it would be, but I\u2019m sure Billy\u2019d appreciate a look, so in they both went, through the nearest door to my bolthole. I didn\u2019t trust just my gloves, but using a pair of pillows as potholders seemed to have no side effects.<br /> <br /> The fucking sun was peeking over the goddamn horizon when we got back to the car. The shafts of light shot straight the fuck through my goddamn skull as I dropped Jack off at the office. The dark of my apartment was a welcome relief, and the hit from the first bottle that came to hand helped even more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I got into bed eventually, I suppose. At least that\u2019s where the hell I woke up, some fucking time around noon, to my phone chirping at me. Naomi\u2019s first message flashed across my screen. \u201cWe made a friend today <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u201d I started tying my response as a second message scrolled its way across my notification bar. \u201cA new friend is a ray of sunshine :0)\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck friends. Do I need to come in?\u201d I sat up and massaged my temples with one hand, flailing for some fucking pain pills with the other.<br /> <br /> My phone chirped again, too soon to be a response, then fucking again before I downed a handful of the pills I found. I've got to change that damn perky high pitched piece of shit sound. \u201cA Demon contact of Kilroy\u2019s is at the office.\u201d was the first and the response was \u201cFuck friends usually come in you\u201d.<br /> <br /> I growled at my phone and tossed it to the other side of the room. I stumbled to the kitchen. Picking up the fucking coffee can, I looked at it, then at my recently cleaned coffee maker, then back to the can before I set it back down and stomped back to get my goddamn phone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I shouldered my way into the fucking office. \u201cJust so you fucking know,\u201c I announced to the room at large, \u201cI only showed up for the goddamn coffee.\u201d I held my hand out and Billy Mack put a mug into it. I took about a third in a gulp, and topped it off with whiskey, stirring it in with my finger.<br /> <br /> The kid keeping Billy, Jack and Naomi company managed to barely let his blue eyes be seen as he looked out from beneath his silver bangs and worn hoodie. I wonder if his parents knew where he spent his Sunday afternoons. He stuck out his hand. \u201cHi! I\u2019m Jared.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked skeptically at his hand for a moment. Naomi patted the kid on the shoulder. \u201cDon\u2019t worry - she\u2019s much more reasonable after a few drinks. Give her five minutes.\u201d I sneered at her.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack continued the introduction. \u201cI ran into him in New York, and worked with him on a few things.\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned to look at him skeptically instead. \u201cWhen he was 12?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jared sighed. \u201cI promise, I\u2019m legal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat, to buy fucking cigarettes?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sputtered. I grinned into my coffee. \u201cHey, you try falling in the body of a ten year old!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat does sound pretty shitty, kid.\u201d I offered my hand. \u201cGabe. Welcome to Seattle.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack had left it to me to fill everyone in on the angles we\u2019d picked up last night. After I was done, the g-man asked, \u201cSo, do we feel we should remove this rabbit spirit or merely leave the girl to her karma?\u201d<br /> <br /> I snorted. \u201cWell, I for one am an agent of justice, not fucking goddamn karma, and if there was any justice in this, it\u2019s well fucking past.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. She was 17, after all. Humans have...\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi interrupted the g-man. \u201cI\u2019m 19!\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack cleared his throat. \u201cHumans have poor judgment. At 17 they have poorer.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBesides, it\u2019s not fucking stopping at her and I have a motherfucking score to settle.\u201d Jack punctuated this with a fist on the table. Naomi put a hand on his shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cBilly, if you tried to possess her, what would happen?\u201d she asked softly.<br /> <br /> He thought for a moment. \u201cWell, if I were successful in gaining control, the spirit would be ejected into Twilight. Should it maintain control instead, I would be forced back into one of my usual quantum states.\u201d He paused, considering. \u201cUnfortunately, I do not believe it would be drawn back into the rabbit statue. We would have to bind it somehow if we did not want it free.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI bet Dantaine would know how to deal with it. His house is a spirit trap, after all. We even have a way of giving him a heads up!\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi had a point, and it was fucking tempting, but... \u201cI\u2019m not saying the thought of foisting one of our problems on the goddamn vampires doesn\u2019t fucking tickle the shit out of me, but dicking over a client is bad fucking business. And getting out client\u2019s biggest client pissed at him is a hell of a dicking.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d She looked disappointed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could use his library though. There was a whole shelf of summoning and binding literature.\u201d Billy Mack mused. \u201cAnd if we did it there, the spirit trap would be a fall back at least.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI bet Stefan would let us in again. Especially since we\u2019ve gotten the goddamn book back and might be getting him his sophisticated fuck back.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> Jack looked at me. \u201cWe\u2019re not gonna leverage the book for anything, make some extra money?\u201d<br /> <br /> I put my head in my hands and started counting on my fingers. \u201cOne - the book is the only proof we have that any story we might tell Stefan is true and/or relevant. Two - see my previous fucking statement re: the dicking over of clients and hells of dickings. Three- Jesus fuck people.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mac nodded at Jack. \u201cWe are good, Jack. I managed to acquire Dantaine\u2019s bank account info, should we need a cash influx.\u201d Who needs hangovers with fucking coworkers like these?<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are we going to tell Stefan anyway?\u201d Jack asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe truth?\u201d Naomi shrugged. \u201cDo we have some kind of responsibility to protect him from the spooky?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t see why the shit we should. It\u2019s backed up by the goddamn book and his own experience, which is better than facts for most fuckers. And it\u2019s mostly likely to get us what we fucking want.\u201d I looked around at the others and didn\u2019t see any strong disagreement. \u201cSounds like a plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi turned to the kid. \u201cSo, you want some extra pocket money? I could get my cousin to draw up a contract for some part time work.\u201d<br /> <br /> He gave her a lopsided smile. \u201cSure. I am a broke college student after all. And this does sound like fun...\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> So you were curious about the concert, my dear. It went pretty well. And yes, we might want to meet at Alfie\u2019s at some point and take in a show. It is not a bad place. A little Alternative, perhaps, but this is Seattle; that happens here. And honestly since slipping on Naomi I feel rather at home there, while, honestly, feeling sort of like I missed the heyday of it. Perhaps a little like a ghost.<br /> <br /> But this particular evening was nothing so much \u201cAlternative\u201d in the rock genre so much as the Sisterhood of Chaos punk band. Langley is, if nothing else, a performer. I have no idea how good a manager he is, but his capacity for strong expressions and complete lack of anything approaching shame worked to his advantage. He had many conversations with his guitar \u201cHenry\u201d about their relationship. They had some covers of non-Punk songs like \u201cLa Bamba\u201d, some covers of punk songs, like \u201cBlitzkrieg Bop\u201d or \u201cTime Bomb.\u201d They also had some original stuff, like a rambling, Dead Milkmen-esque song about becoming sex slaves of Dave Thomas, Founder of Wendy\u2019s and a mash up that by the end went from The Wall into Mr. Roger\u2019s Neighborhood opening theme.<br /> <br /> I sent out for dinner, and she was well dressed. Deanna is a sweetheart. She wants to get serious. How do you feel about a rival, my dear?<br /> <br /> Oh yes, Robin. Can\u2019t forget Robin. It\u2019s been just sex so far with her.<br /> <br /> The others went to interview Langley after the show. Kilroy was Vivian and attempted to go separately despite being talked directly to a bit. She wound up picking up Langley, which surprised me. What must Henry have thought? Quietus meanwhile chatted up the band, though not that way. Speed mostly drank and watched Deanna enjoy herself.<br /> <br /> Speed and Quietus got into some hijinx while Kilroy was \u201cbusy\u201d and I was having my meal. I had to Halo Deanna in her sleep to keep her together. Girl needs more protein apparently. Anyway, they wound up following Vanessa and managed to steal the book she had taken from the library, as well as the bunny the Spirit in her head had traveled in.<br /> <br /> So, I met a new Demon, a Destroyer, the next day. Langley had dropped Vivian off at the University, so she went to my dorm after Deanna had headed out and changed into Billy Mack. I had offered to take him to the office, but as we were walking across campus to grab a bite he saw a friend and they talked. I stepped away to sketch some buildings I wanted to do line art of later, but Billy reeled me back in after a few minutes to introduce his silver (dye) haired friend as Jared Evans, a fellow Unchained and I think Saboteur. <br /> <br /> Oh don\u2019t get that face. You are just too pretty to frown.<br /> <br /> They met in\u2026New York, I think? I am unsure. We went to the office and found Quietus there. He crashed there after chasing Vanessa and was not in a good mood. The poor dear I decided\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026It is technically true I have never seen Quietus in what I would call a \u201cgood\u201d mood no. I would say maybe it is a Destroyer problem but Jared seemed cheerful.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we got together and discussed findings some. I just left Naomi on. Cec\u00edlia was not there to pester me about eating enough. We discussed last night\u2019s events some (Speed eventually deigned to show) and Jared seemed interested and apparently had some compatible skills, so I discussed maybe him working with us. I did not see Kilroy\u2019s eyebrow go up, so it seems it may work out. Hopefully anyway.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s new with you Darling?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session X</i><br /> <br /> Bobby Right is not an NPC original to me. He first appeared in a different GM in our group\u2019s Changeling game. While trying to think of sleazy barkeeps I kept coming back to Bobby, so I emailed my fellow GM for permission to use the character. It\u2019s not the same character exactly (that would be complicated) but very similar and my take. My friend was kind enough to email the picture and what info he had. It is a hella sleazy looking picture.<br /> <br /> Fulgur, or Jared Evans, is a Destroyer Integrator/Saboteur, who wants to essentially break down and rebuild the God-Machine before integrating. The Player has had a busy month, so a lot of his finishing up the character was at session, thus the brief appearance at the end. We should be seeing more of him soon.<br /> <br /> This week\u2019s session was Valentine\u2019s Day, which both Quietus and Fulgur\u2019s player would have to miss. We moved the game to Friday, with the hope of Quietus at least showing since the others could do either day. Was not the case sadly, but Speed, Clytemnestra, and Kilroy found themselves quite busy, and Speed and Kilroy had a magical adventure. More on that next time, comments and questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T02:46:40-08:00","id":423928,"title":"","content":"So the last session fell on Valentine\u2019s Day. Quietus and Fulgur\u2019s players would have to miss. So we rescheduled for Friday as it was\u2026better for certain parties anyway. As it turned out, they could not make it anyway, so it was usual trio. And they had a magical adventure. Magical, I tell you. Let\u2019s Speed and Clytemnestra tell you all about it.<br /> <br /> Fair Warning, Speed is not happy. Even less than usual.<br /> <i><br /> Session XI</i><br /> <b><br /> Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The kid had classes to get to or some fucking shit, so he and Naomi fucked off after not too long. Billy settled down with the goddamn book and statue to give them a once over. He started with the fucking rabbit statue. On one hand, it was able to contain the shit out of vice spirits. On the other hand...<br /> <br /> \u201cJust to remind you, next time you go to talk with the goddamn Mr. Ox, purveyor of statues carved from motherfucking ghost dicks, you are going by your fucking self.\u201d I waved my empty mug at him while going for a refill.<br /> <br /> Ever the pedant, Billy pointed at the back of the piece of shit statue, saying, \u201cActually, this part is a breast and this... is...\u201d He trailed off after he looked up to see my eyebrow hightailing it for my fucking hair line.<br /> <br /> \u201cBy your goddamn fucking self.\u201d Billy ignored me in favor of rambling on about what sort of thing Mr. Ox was. I muttered into my coffee. \u201cA purveyor of goddamn ghost dick statues, is what he is. Fucking shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz picked that moment to come sashaying back in, just in time to hear that and ask \u201c... do they vibrate?\u201d Billy held up the statue by way of explanation. \u201cOh. Never mind then.\u201d She waved her cigarette holder dismissively.<br /> <br /> \u201cHell, I\u2019m even more fucking happy I didn\u2019t touch the goddamn thing.\u201d I started going through the drawer near the science coffee.<br /> <br /> The g-man glanced over at me. \u201cIn case you need to, the left ear is entirely non-dick.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sneered at him and wandered off to see if we had anything more substantial that the pack of crackers I had found in my jacket pocket, leaving the two of them to discuss how you\u2019ve never lived until you\u2019ve fucked someone on a table that was also an goddamn accountant. Liz sure is a damn trick. Fucking rich fucks.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t find anything, but it took me awhile before I wandered back in to find a much more serious as shit Billy Mack. After about half an hour of intrigued looks and worried fucking frowns, Billy set the goddamn book down and sighed. \u201cThis is bad. Very bad.\u201d<br /> <br /> Apparently the goddamn spirit inside the book was Pazanak, the 3rd fucking Vessel of Iniquity. It could be released, and that would let us scratch the book. At that point, the Vessel would be both more goddamn powerful and capable of being fucking pinked himself. He figured the rabbit spirit was another one of these fucking Vessels of Iniquity, but a less powerful one.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell shit. I don\u2019t suppose either of you fuckers have a way to make absofuckinglutely sure Stefan doesn\u2019t give any more goddamn tours?\u201d I asked after he finished filling us the hell in.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe will just impress upon him that we are speaking of biblical levels of power. He may only be as religious as is convenient, but this is a serious inconvenience for him.\u201d Billy pointed out. \u201cYou know, we truly ought inform Dantaine of the occult goings on at his residence. Professional courtesy.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put my head in my hands. \u201cProfessional. Courtesy. Is not dicking over your clients.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy held up his own fucking hands. \u201cFine, fine. I suppose we can see how he responds to our requests.\u201d<br /> <br /> I snorted. \u201cHe\u2019s not stupid enough to not let us in the library.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. And we can counsel him to inform his employer himself.\u201d Billy nodded. \u201cAnd perhaps we might also recommend he not buy anything from the antique shop.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Stefan hoofed it over to the agency about an hour later, giving us plenty of time to have breakfast at the fucking corner diner. When our client got there, Billy Mack started the goddamn show, while I propped up a wall nearby and Liz looked pretty. He gave a version of the story that didn't involve us using any goddamn supernatural power, just doing a little occult research and mundane surveillance. He bought it hook, line and fucking sinker.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I would certainly be happy to allow you access to the library to restore Ms. Houston to her self.\u201d Stefan straightened his tie with a jerky motion, swallowing hard.<br /> <br /> Billy glanced at the phone he kept for Vivian. \u201cI am sorry, I really have to take this. Gabe, if you would...\u201d He raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing pal.\u201d The g-man nodded to Stefan and shut himself in his office. \u201cYou\u2019re on the clock or some shit now, yeah? Would 6, 7 pm work?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTonight?\u201d He looked taken aback.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs soon as fucking possible. This thing\u2019s bad goddamn news. I don\u2019t want to give it any fucking time to realize the book is gone and start shit.\u201d I levered myself off the wall and stood straighter, catching his eye.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight, of course. Um, yes, 7 will be fine.\u201d He looked away first.<br /> <br /> I pulled one of the front desk chairs out and spun it around so I could sit on it backwards. \u201cAlright, well, I think that\u2019s our business fucking done. Some free advice, if you\u2019ll listen?\u201d He didn\u2019t say anything when I paused, so I continued, holding up a single finger. \u201cOne: don\u2019t give any more tours.\u201d<br /> <br /> He protested at that. \u201cYes, of course. It was clearly a momentary lapse in judgment that will not happen again.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised a second finger, ignoring him. \u201cTwo: you need to tell the owner of the house what happened. We won\u2019t, but only cause we\u2019re discreet and professional.\u201d I may have emphasized both those words overly much. I did manage to stop from looking at Liz when I did. \u201cBut this gee is clearly a fucking powerful occultist and will probably know the moment he walks through the goddamn door, if he doesn\u2019t already fucking know. You might win points by fessing up on your own.\u201d<br /> <br /> Fuck me if the fucker didn\u2019t put on his dignity like a goddamn coat. \u201cI will take it under advisement.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing bub. You\u2019re the boss. One of us will be at your house at 7 pm sharp.\u201d I ducked down to rummage for the office bottle while the little fucker took the dismissal for what it was and fucked off.<br /> <br /> A couple of pulls later Vivian poked her head out of Billy Mack\u2019s office and motioned us in. \u201cSo... Michael White...\u201d She paused, grinning mischievously. \u201c...is a bridge builder.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stared at her. \u201cThe fuck?\u201d<br /> <br /> She continued. \u201cAnd he would just feel terrible if Drake was hurt working on a case for him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you telling me Michael \u2018I\u2019m probably a fucking Angel\u2019 White just called you up out of the goddamn blue to say not fucking it?\u201d I continued staring.<br /> <br /> \u201cYup! Well, Skyped, technically.\u201d She kept grinning.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, please tell me you recorded it dear.\u201d Liz moved over to where she could see the screen and put a hand on Vivian\u2019s shoulder.<br /> <br /> Vivian turned to look up at her, faux offendedly. \u201cWhat do you take me for? Of course I did.\u201d I moved around to join them as she hit play on the video.<br /> <br /> The fucker didn\u2019t have to say more than 3 goddamn words before I hated his guts. The shit eating grin, the constant hand gestures and enthusiasm grated like a rusty fucking knife on Hell\u2019s goddamn chalkboard. At least he didn\u2019t beat around the fucking bush. He lied like a goddamn rug, but there was no bush beating.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re working on Drake\u2019s disappearance, right? Mr. Cannon hired you? I assume my name is familiar - I\u2019m sure you all are excellent detectives, top of the line. So I am - as you already know - something of a secondary employer for Drake. And I want to do anything - anything - I can to get him back. I know - I know - it\u2019s bad form to hire a bounty hunter to find a bounty hunter, but you\u2019re detectives - just terrific ones, I\u2019m sure - it\u2019s what you do. Me, I\u2019m something of a bridge mason. I build bridges - make connections - and I want to get you connected to Drake. It\u2019s what I do.\u201d<br /> <br /> When he finally let Vivian get a word in edgewise she asked, \u201cHe was working for you when he disappeared specifically, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> He had his hands out flat in front of him to ward her off before she even fucking finished. \u201cThere was a job offer on the table, yes, but he\u2019d never confirmed. I sent him the details - there was some negotiations - but he never confirmed.\u201d He looked at something off screen. \u201dAh here we go - my \u2018trackers\u2019 found a missing young woman in a \u2018high risk\u2019 area.\u201d And yes, he used the goddamn finger quotes around \u2018trackers\u2019 and \u2018high risk\u2019. \u201cNot particularly dangerous for a grown man, but not the best place for someone of my...\u201d He waved his hand over his face. \u201cI sent him the details - where she\u2019d been seen, her name, that sort of thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian interrupted him. \u201cI don\u2019t suppose you could send me those as well?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, of course! I\u2019m here to help. It should be there... now!\u201d He smiled wide. \u201cWe had some trouble in the past. Nothing major, nothing serious - we were both at fault really, a misunderstanding. But hey, I can\u2019t blame a man for following his conscience - I wouldn\u2019t hire anyone without a strong moral compass, of course. But I thought this would be an opportunity to mend fences - to build bridges.\u201d He made a fucking annoying gesture like he was hitting a chisel with a hammer, grinning widely.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you very much Mr. White. I appreciate all this.\u201d Vivian gestured at her computer and smiled back. \u201cIs there a way I can reach you, if new information comes to light or if I think of another question?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCertainly! If you leave a message here, I\u2019ll respond within 48 hours or so - I\u2019m a busy man and bridge masonry requires a lot of travel.\u201d He winked at her. \u201cEmail might be better - same username at gmail - but I\u2019m sure you know that, you all must be excellent detectives.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks again Mr. White. I\u2019ll be sure to let you know if you can help.\u201d Michael responded with some goddamn double gun fingers accompanied by another wink and thank fucking god the call cut out.<br /> <br /> We all sat silently in shock for a few moments. \u201cWas that Dubai?\u201d Liz asked once she had recovered.<br /> <br /> I looked at Liz quizzically, replaying it in my mind. \u201cWell Jesus fuck, I guess it is. Bridge building really does require travel.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz tapped Vivian on the shoulder. \u201cYou also haven\u2019t lived until you\u2019ve won a free night with a prostitute because you guessed their gender after they orally pleasured you with everything covered but their mouth.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stared at her, then at Vivian,then at Liz again. I shrugged. \u201cWe\u2019ve got a couple more stops on our list to buzz now. Since the library\u2019s closed until 7, wanna come along Vivian?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> She did, so the three of us made our way to the northern part of downtown, where the address of the sometime laundromat, sometime office suite took us. Vivian took in the half a dozen Starbucks nearby and started giggling goddamn disturbingly. I took the high road, and didn\u2019t fucking ask.<br /> <br /> The address did have an illusory outer cover of the laundromat. Between the scorch marks and bullet damage, the office space beneath the illusion had clearly been the site of some kind of fucking shoot out, sometime in the last few days. A closer look showed the outlets had been ripped the fuck out and the entire electrical system was compromised as hell in a way that made it seem like this was a Demon or even a whole fucking Ring's handiwork. It was currently being guarded by a quartet of humans overseen by a Man in Black awfully fucking reminiscent of the ones at Cannon's office. From the way they were stationed, they were most likely a sentry force, set to slow down an attacking force long enough for the big fucking guns to show.<br /> <br /> We had no intentions of tangling with said big fucking guns, so we left to check out the address Drake had on file as White's. On the way we spit balled theories about the Demons that assaulted the place \u2013 whether Drake had pushed someone into a Fall, or had been and Angel and Fallen himself, or possibly was simply a fucking Stigmatic. Even if we didn't draw any conclusions (other than he was highly unlikely to have Fallen himself , considering he went to the fucking police), the conversation was more fruitful than the fucking trip. The house was a simple fucking suburban home, lived in by a simple fucking suburban family with 2 of their proverbial 2.5 kids. Jennifer and H. Mason... Mason. Fucking bridge builder. They did have a legitimate digital footprint, as best Vivian could tell in the field but... Mason. That calls for more goddamn scrutiny.<br /> <br /> Still, that left us with plenty of time to go talk with Yolanda Jones and her mother. I stopped off at a gas station to let Naomi join us as 'rich bitch' was going to open as few doors as Michael's pasty white fucking face. Same for the g-man for that matter, but Vivian was already with us.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Mrs. Jones opened the door a crack in response to our knock. \u201cWho're you?\u201d Her voice was rough and unsophisticated but not outright hostile, yet.<br /> <br /> \u201cName's Gabe. Gabe Norton. Sorry to bother you, but is your daughter around?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her brow furrowed. \u201cNo. What d'you want?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you reported her missing, maybe to this man?\u201d I showed her a picture of Michael.<br /> <br /> \u201cDunno him,\u201d she muttered. \u201cWouldn't report her missing neither, she's fine. Just with her boyfriend.\u201d<br /> <br /> I brought up a picture of Drake. \u201cWhat about him? Is he familiar?\u201d<br /> <br /> She squinted at my phone. \u201cYeah. Yeah, I know him. What was his name? Something famous... Drake? That sounds right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you know him?\u201d I prodded.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cHe came by, what was it? A few days ago. Something. He was asking questions.\u201d She looked thoughtful. \u201cSame ones as you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you tell him anything?\u201d She gave me a suspicious look. \u201cHe's gone missing ma'am. Looking for your daughter 