Dickinson poem.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi smiled again. \u201cTrue. But if her knows anything about it, he might think you were putting on a display of being blitzed out of your mind, and not realized you were putting on a display of being blitzed out of your mind while being blitzed out of your mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian looked back and forth between us and started counting on her fingers whenever Naomi said blitzed. \u201cSo... he knows that we know that he knows but there's no land war in Asia. Right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d I nodded.<br /> <br /> Vivian fell over onto my shoulder. \u201cI think I should stop drinking and go home.\u201d<br /> <br /> Between the two of us, we managed to get Vivian in the car. I tried to help keep her awake to make it easier on Naomi when they got to Liz's place. \u201cSo, Vivian, did you molest Fitzgerald? Cause we're not supposed to.\u201d<br /> <br /> She giggled. \u201cA lady doesn't discuss her sexual activities with managers of power plants. Or with their guitars.\u201d Of course, she then went into far more goddamn detail that I ever fucking wanted. I was grateful when we got to my shithole apartment. I'd just gotten my key in the front door when Vivian stuck her head out the window and yelled \u201cThere can be only one...\u201d Cuckoo fucking dames.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> <br /> You look dubious. Yes, I was researching occult bindings last evening. Of course I can do research all by myself! I am a big girl! I did not plan it that way of course.<br /> <br /> Okay, well after taking Jared back to Uni, I came back to find the rest of the gang minus Quietus discussing our next move. The plan was to tell Stephan what was going on and then to go research how to bind the spirit in the library. It was some sort of \u201cvessel of iniquity\u201d which sounded bad, but it was a lesser spirit of some greater \u201cvessel of iniquity\u201d which also sounds bad.<br /> <br /> Okay, yes, fun, but bad.<br /> <br /> Kilroy somehow managed to restrain himself from making them walking bombs of chaos, and we figured we would need to research a ritual to bind it. Thankfully, we had a huge occult library and Stephan had a key, we just needed to access it.<br /> <br /> Stephan was hardly a roadblock. He agreed to give us access, and we decided to go there about seven. These revelations may have had him rethinking Sunday evening church. Everything went smoothly there, aside from Michael White Skyping.<br /> <br /> Oh man Michael White. \u201cMike\u201d as he called himself. You don\u2019t get a different incarnation to do a Messenger\u2019s job. Only Kilroy actually directly dealt with him, but he would not stop talking. Everything was smiles and thumbs up. He was all smarm and advertising slogans.\u201d Bridge Building\u201d Ugh, he must be a Psychopomp. Good people, useful people, dreadful for speaking engagements, usually try to knock you up if you sleep with them. Yes yes I know you want to build. Put on a rubber and look pretty.<br /> <br /> Anyway, After we all (well, not Quietus, which is why Kilroy\u2019s pad still works) watched the video sort of slack jawed at this maniac, I noted he was in Dubai, where I had had some epic parties. No evidence he knew what he was dealing with\u2026well, except that he Skyped us from Dubai.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that abomination dealt with, we set out to tie up loose ends. I had volunteered to check out places on the list, Speed insisted on going, and Kilroy was gonna research, but we had time so we all went. The Laundromat was indeed an office and Infrastructure\u2026it was guarded by a low ranking Angel and some cultists\u2026and had been hit recently, probably within the last week. Unsure of the success, but they had hacked anything electric they could, and there were a lot of bullet holes and some sort marks. Interesting. Kilroy had shifted to Vivian by then, so spent her time hacking Starbucks into attacking each other. Noble I guess.<br /> <br /> The house seemed totally normal. We did not investigate inside. Speed insisted I put Naomi on before going to talk to Yolanda, Kilroy had Viv at that point anyway. Naomi looks less like \u201cThe Man\u201d than Liz apparently. Probably the cigarette holder. Checking on Yolanda revealed she may be missing, she was \u2018staying\u201d with her boyfriend \u201cCrunchberry\u201d (I thought only men had boyfriends named Crunchberry) and was hiding from the cops. She had met Drake but had no idea who Michael White was or how he would know about her business.<br /> <br /> Then the first address Drake was sent to. It was a burned out ruin. Shortly after entering, Kilroy went down a staircase and vanished. After a full investigation, Speed, being a Psychopomp herself, figured out it was the drawn gun, and went down the staircase herself and vanished, after telling me to get Quietus to send him to the staircase and vanish. Perhaps fortunately, he phone was out of juice.<br /> <br /> So there I was in a burned building in the bad part of town alone. I am loyal to my Ring, but Frye\u2019s dog I ain\u2019t. I got out of there after about twenty minutes. I had about an hour till the meeting, so I went to the caf\u00e9 and hung out with folks, met a young woman with long legs I will be painting named Linda, then slipped Liz back on went to meet Stephan.<br /> <br /> Speed and Kilroy were having a magical adventure of learning in a magic forest, but someone had to actually take care of business. Of course, Quietus was the obvious choice, but he was unreachable and did not realize we needed him, so I had to girl the hell up and do it. Stephan was surprised to meet just me but I smoothed things over not being a Psychopomp, and returned the big evil book to the hopefully safe library, and set about to research.<br /> <br /> Research is not my strong point. But I was still in there for <i>over an hour</i>, and did some note taking of what books were useful whenever Speed and Kilroy were done with their magical adventure. Eventually, I needed some fucking coke and left. But still, see? I was in fact in a library when I said I was doing research so\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh Speed and Kilroy? They did emerge eventually. Actually I had slipped Naomi back on and picked them up. I was thinking of inviting Linda over to sketch her legs, but it did occur to me that, you know, half my ring was missing, so I should be alert to help. That meant having local news on so I could hear about speeding cars or explosions. As it turned out, they called me, and I picked them up.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll let them tell you what happened.<br /> <br /> We discussed it in one of Speeds favorite bars, and even met creepy cane vampire guy. Fortunately, he only recognized Speed. Apparently we are friends with the Ordo Dracul, yay?<br /> <br /> Afterwards, I took the kids home\u2026they had had a long day. And then went to do some sketching. I need to get some work out that is really my work. So quiet evening, overall. You?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XI</i><br /> <br /> For the record, Dieter did not make any sexualized motions with his cane. Speed Demon has issues. As noted before, being somewhat inspired by Joel Cairo he has a tendency to handle his cane and look away from the person who is speaking. It\u2019s great fun as I bring out a cane for him.<br /> <br /> Speaking of such things, Michael White was fun to run. Put on my best snake oil salesman and ran with it. He\u2026had the effect I was hoping for.<br /> <br /> So Kilroy found something in the Hedge, something very bad. Rest assured, he will show up again. Was he connected to White? Seems likely. This rabbit hole seems to go very deep.<br /> <br /> Snow and moving will keep the numbers down, but usual suspects this next session. In the meantime Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T06:19:19-08:00","id":424061,"title":"","content":"Ah, the Hedge, and all its magical wonders! I'm surprised they didn't try to frolic with the pixies! Also, I LIKE Creepy Legbreaker-Employing Talking Owl for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T12:29:12-08:00","id":424364,"title":"","content":"Thanks! He was fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T13:59:48-07:00","id":441833,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check in on our antiheroes. Again, weather was not on our side; the snow did not keep the game from happening, but Fulgur\u2019s player and Quietus\u2019s player were ultimately unable to make due to all the fallout of the snow-in. So usual suspects, but we had some fun. Check it out. <br /> <br /> Oh, it\u2019s worth noting Clytemnestra\u2019s Cult believes her Cover Naomi Cruz is a member, not their Spider Goddess.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> The next day I wandered into the office at the crack of 11, having not gotten any goddamn smiley face punctuated emergency texts that morning. Billy Mack looked me over as he handed me my coffee. Sure, I\u2019d slept in my suit. It\u2019s far too much fucking trouble to do otherwise. Or at least it felt that way last night. And it\u2019s the only one I have, at least that I can find. I really need to get around to fixing the fucking hole that Sanderson broad put in my other good one. Maybe Jack knows a discrete tailor that works on the cheap.<br /> <br /> I spun a chair around and sat down, taking a sip of the goddamn dark coffee. \u201cLiz in yet?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy shook his head. \u201cNo. And Naomi has classes all morning I believe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took another sip. Looked around. \u201cYou called Stefan, told him you\u2019d be around again tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, but Liz told him yesterday that we would.\u201d Billy Mack continued tinkering with whatever.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is a peach, isn\u2019t she?\u201d I took a sip \u201cSo, we going to check out those other two addresses? And not walk down any weird feeling staircases?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy looked affronted but before he could say anything, Cecilia poked her head into the lab. \u201cThere is a... Jimmy Marsh here? Who can lick his own eyeball?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, yes. That would be how we know it\u2019s him.\u201d Billy Mack responded to her disgusted look.<br /> <br /> I switched to the cover language we use around Liz\u2019s cult. \u201cThink we should fill him the hell in? About the goddamn White situation? It\u2019ll get back to Scarecrow, but that\u2019s no fucking bad thing necessarily.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy nodded. \u201cGo ahead and send him back, Cecilia, if you would.\u201d<br /> <br /> She left, shuddering and muttering about fucking eyeballs. I smirked at Billy. The fucker ignored me as Jimmy joined us. \u201cOh good,\u201d he began, \u201cScarecrow\u2019d be peeved if you weren\u2019t OK.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cAny fucking reason we wouldn\u2019t be?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked between us quickly. \u201cOur, uh, red haired friend killed a group of Demons a couple of miles south of the city. Me being the liaison between you and him, Scarecrow sent me to check it wasn\u2019t you. The Fools are alright too, and probably Valefar. I mean, I didn't check up on him, but I assume... She didn\u2019t leave any identifying bits, though. Set a forest fire.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head sadly. \u201cNo respect for the environment.\u201d I stared at him and Jimmy\u2019s eyes kept darting between us until the g-man continued and gave Jimmy the fucking Cliffs notes version of the Drake case.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t recognize that address or that name.\u201d He looked thoughtful. \u201cThat doesn\u2019t mean Scarecrow had nothing to do with it of course. He only tells me what I need to know, and I know I don\u2019t need to know much. Safer that way, all around. Though it might have been nice to know Valefar existed before he walked out of my closet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHuh?\u201d I said, fucking eloquently. This shit I had to hear.<br /> <br /> \u201cYup. Right out of my closet. He made it dark enough I had to put on my heat sight to tell he wasn\u2019t just a disembodied head. He quoted Sympathy for the Devil at me...\u201d<br /> <br /> I interrupted him. \u201cBetter than goddamn Emily Dickinson.\u201d He looked confused and I waved him on.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight, well, he wanted to let me know he was displeased with Scarecrow\u2019s increased activity. I told him I was just a liaison, but I dunno if he cared. It was not a... comfortable conversation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOdd.\u201d Now Billy was the one looking thoughtful. \u201cIt seems as if his problem is with Scarecrow specifically, not territoriality in general, as he was perfectly courteous to us, when he stopped by with the proverbial fruit basket.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. You probably don't need to worry about him, he just makes me nervous.\u201d Jimmy shuddered. \u201cAnyway, I should tell Scarecrow about this Michael White guy, but I can just tell him he\u2019s someone to watch if you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy waved the offer away. \u201cAnything we said is fine to let Scarecrow know about. I wouldn\u2019t want to put you in a position to have to hide things from him - it wouldn\u2019t be polite.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled and split, putting his goddamn human suit back on first. Billy watched him leave and commented when he was gone, \u201cPerhaps the eyeball licking is a flirting behavior among the Reptoids.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stopped, coffee halfway to my mouth. I put it down slowly. \u201cPlease, please tell me you\u2019re not going to fuck the goddamn lizard man too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wasn\u2019t intending to.\u201d He shrugged and continued with his scientific analysis of fucking lizard man romance. I stopped listening until \u201cI do not think I will introduce him to Ganora. I\u2019m not sure about her reaction.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked at him. \u201cJealous?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked at me blankly for a few seconds. \u201cNo. She might eat him.\u201d My smirk deepened but that line of conversation got cut short by a heated exchange in Portuguese from the lobby.<br /> <br /> I leaned in the doorway to better hear Cecilia flapping her gums at Naomi, chewing her the hell out for wearing non-flattering clothes. When Naomi met Liz, Cecilia warned, she needed to make a good impression. I let that go for a few minutes, to see how fucking long Cecilia could keep it up before walking more loudly out to the lobby. \u201cNaomi, you ready to go sketch some places of interest?\u201d I didn\u2019t see anything wrong with how she was dressed.<br /> <br /> When we got in the car Naomi rolled her eyes in Cecelia\u2019s direction. \u201cWhatever. I look great. I would totally do me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy nodded approvingly. \u201cI\u2019ve been with Vivian. Before the pact. She had daddy issues.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThose are the best.\u201d Naomi sighed.<br /> <br /> I spoke up before she could begin to wax fucking rhapsodic on the virtues of daddy issues. \u201cSo, to the goddamn angel death traps.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight!\u201d Naomi nodded. \u201cI mean, they\u2019re probably trapped right? Maybe even different traps?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy smiled. \u201cUnless he\u2019s a one trick bridge builder.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cHow many others were there?\u201d Naomi asked, holding onto the oh shit handle as I took a sharp turn.<br /> <br /> \u201cTwo.\u201d The Mustang stopped on a fucking dime at the light.<br /> <br /> \u201cProbably not a demon then, since it\u2019s three total, not four.\u201d The g-man pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cFour is our lucky number after all.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> The first building we checked out wasn't a goddamn burnt out husk like yesterday\u2019s adventure, but it was still in fucking bad shape. About a block and a corner away from the Hedge-trapped staircase, it had probably been a cubicle farm in a past life. Now it was all open space, boarded up and sketchy as shit. Naomi raised an eyebrow and gestured us ahead. \u201cAge before beauty.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sneered and Billy Mack shrugged and he went on in. The main attraction inside was the large empty central room, fucking littered with alcohol containers. The middle of the room was clear, however. What was also clear was that violence had been done there, and not in the too distant past. The lingering smell of blood spoke to that, and the bloodstains I found spoke more. They were small, not the remnants of a human bleeding out, or even of a serious goddamn cut.<br /> <br /> We also found some kind of fucking old-fashioned cash register, tucked to the side. It seemed to have been moved and opened frequently, and I could tell it was unlocked looking at it, which was good since there was no sign of a goddamn key. Probably was used as storage and not a safe, considering. I gave Billy a look as he went to mess with it. The g-man returned it, and continued. Thankfully, touching the fucking thing didn\u2019t teleport him to the moon of some shit. Instead, he just found it empty.<br /> <br /> Putting it all together, it looked like we stumbled on the site of an illegal boxing ring. \u201cThis is a goddamn weird fucking place to send Drake.\u201d I commented after I let the others know what I suspected.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe it\u2019s an illegal boxing ring run by the Klan.\u201d Naomi suggested.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, there\u2019s lots of ways it could be dangerous to him. But it still doesn\u2019t seem like a threat in line with the fucking staircase.\u201d I ducked my head outside to see if there were any bums hanging around who might know something about the place.<br /> <br /> Naomi followed me out. \u201cOoh! Zombie hobo boxing ring!\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a look and called out to Billy. \u201cLet\u2019s check out that last one. I think I can see it from here.\u201d<br /> <br /> That last one was an old theatre. The front door just beyond the ticket taker\u2019s booth had a fucking heavy lock on it that was hanging open. The door opened directly into the auditorium, which was as dark as the devil\u2019s goddamn asshole.<br /> <br /> As soon as we opened the doors, we all heard two fucking human sized things with wings fluttering in the cat walks. That was the last goddamn thing I wanted, since a firefight would make it unlikely that I\u2019d get any good info on the boxing ring any time soon. Billy Mack, on the other hand, was fucking thrilled at the idea of a mothman specimen to examine. I managed to talk him down, helped by the fact that the mothmen themselves had no designs on us from the look of it.<br /> <br /> Light would sure as shit have changed that, so Naomi was in charge of looking the place over, with a few pointers from yours truly. She found no signs of any bullet holes, or any struggle whatsoever, so if Drake did make it to here, he didn\u2019t pick a fight with the buggers.<br /> <br /> We started back to the car and I laid out my plan. Billy didn\u2019t need my help reading his goddamn books, so I was going to stake out the ring, see if anyone set up shop tonight or barring that if any bums frequented the area. The pickings for a stakeout were fucking slim I noticed glancing around. An old Walmart with a heeled meth head standing guard. The Hedge-trap. A bar with a Spanish name and a rough as shit looking crowd. I turned to Naomi. \u201cHey, you speak Spanish.\u201d I jerked my head towards the bar.<br /> <br /> \u201cI, um, yes? You want to go in and announce that you\u2019re my dyke? That\u2019ll get us both stabbed. Or that you\u2019re my white friend who\u2019s totally cool, a real reverse Oreo?\u201d She looked at me incredulously.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, I\u2019m fucking with you. I\u2019ll park myself on the second floor of our favorite burnt out husk, should be safe enough up there even without the goddamn mirror skin. People aren\u2019t in the habit of looking up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked concerned. \u201cWhy is that a requirement?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cI\u2019m tapped. Don\u2019t have the fucking juice to get there or back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not good.\u201d He put a hand to my shoulder and I felt re-energized. \u201cThat should be enough and a spare.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my shoulders and cracked my neck. \u201cThanks man.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I dropped the others off and swung by the store to get some cheap as shit booze. I stashed the bottles beside me in one of the less fucking unstable portions of the second floor of the burnt out husk and got set to hunker down for awhile.<br /> <br /> Hunker down I did, until shortly after the goddamn sun set. We\u2019d caught a break - from the look of things there was a fight tonight, or at least some kind of event. Even fucking better, Herb was in among the crowd of mooks. There was also a broad in the crowd, in some kind of old-fashioned getup straight down to the fur stole over her shoulders. She was a classy bird, though her eyes made her out to be a cat, with the way they glinted in the light.<br /> <br /> The sentry guarding the door was a well-heeled Asian gee. The pistol was plain to see. The pair of Mac-10s, not so fucking much. He held the wall up casually, but he gave me a thorough glance over as I walked up. He stopped me and stood in front of the door. \u201cNo guns. You can leave it with me or in the register\u201d He indicated the register Billy Mack had been poking at, which was being watched over by an older mugg. He grunted when the door guard told him what was what and took my rod.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile I took in the lay of the land. The broad was wandering around with a beer bottle, curiously unmolested by the rough goddamn lugs who made up the rest of the audience. Maybe not so curious - she seemed to be in charge, considering her route kept taking her past the announcer\u2019s desk, where she\u2019d fiddle with a cell phone. Still, the lack of grabass seemed more out of fear than respect, so maybe she had more to her than a pretty face and a taste for fancy clothes. Maybe her cat\u2019s eyes weren\u2019t just a trick of the light. Or maybe security was just that tight. I glanced at the gee at the door, but decided to feel Herb out first.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo where\u2019s a motherfucker get a drink around here?\u201d I slid into the seat next to Herb, smiling.<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cBYOB thing, I think.\u201d I looked at the bottle of Night Train I\u2019d brought as a bribe and grimaced. Still it didn\u2019t look like I\u2019d need it to loosen up any goddamn tongues - the Asian gee looked to be a classier sort of tough - and there was no point in letting that shit go to waste. I opened it up and took a swig. Herb watched. \u201cYou following me?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was just a hint of a smile creeping up on his rocky face. I returned it. \u201cNah. Was in the neighborhood earlier looking for a fucking missing gee and saw the signs. Thought it seemed like something to get a piece of, or see if my guy got a piece too goddamn much.\u201d I gave a description of Drake.<br /> <br /> Herb watched another young Asian guy and an older white gee get prepped for a match. \u201cDunno anything about that. I just get told when a fight\u2019s happening and sometimes get