o this place?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe was a bounty hunter, on a job for Michael White.\u201d That registered. His eyes went wide. \u201cYou know our friendly neighborhood bridge builder huh?\u201d I was careful not to say mason. If he was connected, there was no point in emphasizing something that could have him realize just how much we know.<br /> <br /> He shook his head again, unconvincingly. \u201cI don\u2019t know anything about any Michael White. And you shouldn\u2019t have anything to do with a shark like him.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cRight, sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked serious. \u201cI mean it. He\u2019s a big fish and you shouldn\u2019t have anything to do with him.\u201d<br /> <br /> I returned his look. \u201cThanks for the help, bub. It\u2019s my shitty luck, he probably ran afoul of the goddamn staircase.\u201d I ran my tongue over my teeth. The Night Train made them feel fuzzy. I took another swig.<br /> <br /> Jake glanced at the broad. \u201cStaircase?\u201d<br /> <br /> Another bite. \u201cYeah, the fucking funny feeling one in the burnt out place a block or so over.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked at her again. \u201cSome people here are interested in keeping people away from that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat right? Maybe I ought to let them know Michael White is handing out its fucking address to bounty hunters.\u201d I watched him carefully. He shrugged and let it hang. I started walking away.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey! If anyone gets grabby, just let me know. Or Herb, that\u2019ll probably be faster.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cSure thing buddy.\u201d<br /> <br /> Herb watched me walk over. \u201cJake any help?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSome.\u201d I slid back into my seat and kept an eye on the broad.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. He\u2019s an alright sort, even if he might be part of the gangs. They say he walked up and asked for a private conversation with Rosanna,\u201d he indicated the announcer, \u201cand after that he 