 /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. In a fucking ladylike way. Of course. \u201cI could simply shift into my demon form, collapse its wave function once it materializes and drain its essence.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSimply huh?\u201d She glared at me. I raised my hands up. \u201dI kid, I kid! Seems like a good plan to me. No way we\u2019ll get out of having Stefan there though. If Jack\u2019s back from that divorce case, he could conk the fucker. If not...\u201d I thought for a moment. \u201cWell, I could get mind-shittingly wasted, and you could shift the consequences to Stefan. Billy fixes up some memories and we\u2019re good to go.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz\u2019s eyes lit up and she mused, \u201cI\u2019ve never eaten a lust spirit before.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cWell, I would not want to stand between you and a new experience.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know I would only knock you aside gently and into something soft my dear.\u201d She grinned wickedly.<br /> <br /> I finished my coffee between filling them in on what happened at the fucking boxing ring. The g-man crossed his arms. \u201cOdd. It certainly doesn\u2019t seem to match the staircase in threat level...\u201c He was interrupted by a knock on the door. \u201cCome in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey. This, um, just got dropped off. A health food tray, I think? The courier didn\u2019t say anything about it.\u201d She handed Billy a goddamn meat and cheese platter with a small card on it before going back to her desk. The card read \u2018Eat healthy new neighbor - Dr. Samuel Miles\u2019.<br /> <br /> I caught Billy\u2019s eye. \u201cWell?\u201d He made an inquisitive noise. I gestured at the tray. \u201cYou are fucking fond of putting mysterious things in your mouth.\u201d<br /> <br /> He gave me a disapproving look which I returned with a smirk before turning to his computer and running a quick search. Dr Samuel Miles worked for Seattle Downtown Practice, whose office, true to its fucking name, was downtown, and nowhere near close enough to count as \u2018neighbors\u2019. His \u2018Dr\u2019 stood for psychiatrist but that shit was all the internet had on him. No records, no personal life, no nothing.<br /> <br /> \u201cAngels wouldn\u2019t send gift baskets...\u201d The g-man picked up the card to see if there was anything else on it.<br /> <br /> Liz chuckled. \u201cUnless by gift baskets you mean hunters.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rarely,\u201d I said, watching unbelieving as Billy Mack took a goddamn bite from one of the slices of meat. We waited quietly, staring at each other, for one minute. Two. \u201cWell, that was anticlimactic.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is not bad.\u201d Billy offered the tray to me. I stared him down until he put the fucking thing aside and picked up his goddamn phone. Whoever he called picked up after a few rings. \u201cYes, may I speak with Dr. Samuel Miles?\u201d The conversation was not long and he gazed thoughtfully at his phone after he ended the call. \u201cThat was strange, Dr. Miles certainly works there, but I do believe the secretary was somewhat afraid of him. Or of his usual clientele. She was certainly taken aback at the idea of him sending a thoughtful gift basket. Anyway, he is in sporadically, and she will inform him that we have called.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood enough or it\u2019ll have to be for now. Though, the afternoon is our oyster. We could drop in. I\u2019d rather track Jack down though.\u201d I glanced at the cheese but decided on a coffee refill instead. \u201cI wanna know why the bridge fucker sent him to those three places.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, there might not be a reason why other than the God Machine said to.\u201d Liz pointed out helpfully.<br /> <br /> I sat down and rubbed my eyes. \u201cFuck. Goddamn cock-shitting mother goat fucking piece of shit.\u201d I said without heat, aimed at the floor. \u201cFine. I still wanna get a handle on Mr. White and anyone that fucking scared of the bastard knows something more than what we have.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cProbably. But first, I think we should hit the dam. We could all use a bit more juice.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I poured on the speed as I drove us to the dam, radars be fucked. It was much easier to think while I was going so fast and the smooth gear shifts of the Mustang were as soothing as top goddamn shelf whiskey. Once Id\u2019 gotten in the zone, I broke the silence. \u201cWe\u2019re not going to molest Fitzy boy, are we?\u201d<br /> <br /> We\u2019d traded Liz for Naomi just outside of town and she smiled. \u201cNo dick banjo then?\u201d She moved one hand like she was pulling something taut and made strumming motions with the other. I stared at her. \u201cWhat?\u201d She kept making the motion and I kept fucking staring. I took an opportunity to pass someone that I caught out of the corner of my eye. She put her hands up. \u201cRight, OK! I forget, you\u2019re a dyke! Just... eyes on the road?\u201d<br /> <br /> A smile crept up my face. I stared at her a few more seconds before winking and putting eyes front. \u201cI just don\u2019t want fucking Dickinson boy to be mad at me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack piped up. \u201cSpeaking of vampires that unreasonably annoyed Gabe at Johnny\u2019s, we should probably speak with Valefar before eviscerating the mustard gas breathing fellows. We don\u2019t want to step on his toes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want to eviscerate them. Just punch the motherfucking shit out of them. They pop back up like daisies right?\u201d I grinned at him. \u201cBut yeah, we should at least let him know what\u2019s up.\u201d<br /> <br /> The drive to the dam didn\u2019t take very long. Neither did Ganora once we\u2019d hit the side of the lake. \u201cI haven\u2019t laid the egg. Yet.\u201d Naomi and I shared glances of equal parts fucking terror and goddamn disgust. \u201cNeed something else?\u201d She paused. \u201cLovin\u2019? 