st forgotten I was not really Naomi Cruz before the evening was over, worrying about if I had put off Linda, dealing with math homework and Deanna\u2019s tendency to message me several times a day. Or hour if she is on a roll. I thought about calling her over to let out some frustration but it was rather late, and I need to sleep alone with Naomi some to maintain the Cover. So spent the night sleeping at the apartment.<br /> <br /> I still implied to the others my day was a non stop sexfest. I can\u2019t ruin the mystique, after all.<br /> <br /> Tuesday was classes in my major, which were much easier to deal with. When I showed up we reviewed the findings from Speed\u2019s scouting and Kilroy\u2019s research. Shockingly, part of Kilroy\u2019s plan, which made sense, I guess, was for me to try and fail to seduce Speed to weaken the Vice Spirit for binding.<br /> <br /> You can imagine how that went over with me.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like failing to seduce ANYONE. Much less Speed who leers at anything without a penis between nineteen and forty, and some beyond that range besides. If I can\u2019t seduce Speed I may as well become a nun. This Vice Spirit is not worth it.<br /> <br /> I counterproposed that I attack and restrain the Vice Spirit and drink it\u2019s Vice Essence. My spidery limbs and adhesives will make it all but immobile, and using wave function collapse will ensure it cannot shift to a Twilight form. We assume it will Manifest; Kilroy plans to possess Vanessa, knocking it out of her body. It can stand there like a jackass and be bound, or it can Manifest to try to fight us, and I make it a lunchable. Well, assuming it can\u2019t lust whammy Kilroy. He seems resistant to such we will see.<br /> <br /> A \u201cDoctor Samuel Miles\u201d sent us some food while we were talking. Which was odd. He barely had a footprint in the world. Kilroy called them up but the receptionist said he was not there and gets few calls. A weak cover? I don\u2019t know. Before I got in the day before, Jimmy the Lizard came in and mentioned a group called the Fools. Something with them maybe?<br /> <br /> Regardless, we needed Aether, Speed was about tapped and Kilroy was low. So we went to the dam. I changed to Naomi and rode on up. We met creepy Ganora, who was getting ready to lay an egg. Ewww?<br /> <br /> Quite right.<br /> <br /> We decided to slip up from below rather than from the dam to collect the Aether. Ganora had mentioned some Rattus but we were not concerned. Still, we spent the Aether to partially transform and ready our weapons and senses. We elected not to turn on the lights as we went, lest we alert the Rattus.<br /> <br /> If only we found Rattus.<br /> <br /> What we found was an Angel. Almost certainly a Destroyer, though possibly a fairly combat focused Guardian. Bloody, jagged, with metal coming from her mouth and a voice like dental drills, taunting Rattus to come out to her. Several others were there, probably weaker Angels.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve seen some creepy shit in my time, but she took the cake. We quickly withdrew, as she only barely missed finding us\u2026she heard us, and even attacked the wall where Speed was.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, we really needed the Aether at that point. We had burned a lot of our last Aether on prepping for combat, and were frankly unprepared for facing the Vice Spirit. I MIGHT have been okay. But the others were tapped. We decided to wait it out\u2026it seemed like it was making a withdrawal, so odds are it would not be there long, and we did not need the Essence, just the Aether.<br /> <br /> We waited three hours. Kilroy banged the fishwoman again.<br /> <br /> Finally she left and we snuck up, grabbed our Aether and ran. We had time to get back but just barely. We had an exorcism get to.<br /> <br /> New glass?<br /> <i><br /> End Session XII</i><br /> <br /> Demon Aether economy is interesting. It is reminding me more of <b>Geist</b> at this point than, say,<b> Changeling</b> or <b>Vampire</b>, though Demons have a LOT of powers they can use for free on the one hand compared to Sin-Eaters, they also can\u2019t store up nearly as much of it on the other hand.<br /> <br /> Our new protector made about the impression I was hoping. The picture of her is very disturbing, and it had the intended effect on the players. They sort of passed it around and stared at it and decided even when they thought she was outnumbered they did not want to deal with that\u2026thing.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sure Samuel Miles is a perfectly nice chap.<br /> <br /> In other news, Cryptids are far, far too much fun.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that\u2019s about all for this time. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T01:43:27-07:00","id":459758,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to wrap up the Sondra case. This time we also get a journal from Fulgur<br /> <br /> <i>Session XIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Billy Mack got a call from the kid on our way to meet with the client. I swung wide to pick him up. It was nice to have a fucking appreciative audience for once. But eventually the others pulled him away from the sun roof and filled him in. Something Liz said, probably about the goddamn ghost dick statue, got me staring at her. \u201cUm. Gabe. The road is... it\u2019s that way.\u201d Liz pointed out the windshield.<br /> <br /> I smiled and winked at Jared. \u201cI have fucking great peripheral vision.\u201d I turned back to looking at Liz in the front seat. \u201cIsn\u2019t that right Liz?\u201d<br /> <br /> What she gave me back might have been called a grimace on a less pretty bird. \u201cYou are the only person I know who can shoot a gun and stare at my tits at the same time. Those are her two favorite things.\u201d That last was aimed at Jared, as she began ignoring me in favor of finishing up the description of our crazy fucking plan.<br /> <br /> We tweaked it a little, since the kid was kicking the shit with us. He could also collapse the spirit\u2019s wave function, to make sure it stayed soled. So he got that gig, to let Liz focus on holding the fucker still. My job was to distract our client from noticing the kid hiding on the goddamn ceiling to get a drop on the action and to get mind-fuckingly shitfaced so that Stefan would be too out of it to catch onto the giant spider eating the lust spirit.<br /> <br /> The plan went off without a single goddamn hitch. I tried hard not to laugh at Stefan\u2019s statement that \u2018Lady\u2019 Vanessa would be another 15 minutes, as she was \u2018working late\u2019 but failed utterly. That did give me plenty of time for the get drunk part of the plan, and got Stefan worked up into way too fucking much of a tizzy to notice Jared. Liz shifted the consequences and I left Stefan in a dazed heap to start pacing the room, rod in one hand, rye in the other. After all, my usual buzz went along with the consequences.<br /> <br /> The three of them did their thing and after awhile I put away my piece, since they had it well in fucking hand. I still circled the place with a jerky pace, stopping to give the kid a hit from the flask when his bit was done, despite his enthusiastic \u201cBusting makes me feel good.\u201d Just one hit though. He doesn\u2019t take shots of straight 151 well.<br /> <br /> Once Kilroy got the spirit back in the goddamn statue, he looked around. I went over to Stefan, motioning the kid to follow. \u201cDrop the broad and earfuck the lug. I\u2019m ready to file this under closed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnce I exit her, she will be conscious. And will remember what happened before I took over.\u201d<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra spoke up. \u201cI could put her to sleep.\u201d<br /> <br /> I waved them on. \u201cGreat. Then you earfuck the pair of them with a perfectly normal exorcism that left them tired enough to crash here for the night.\u201d I paused. \u201cJared Whatever-the-fuck your middle and last names are. We are not stealing from our clients. At least not that brazenly, Jesus fuck.\u201d<br /> <br /> He put the goddamn wallet back in Stefan\u2019s pocket, without taking anything, as best I could fucking tell. He did flip through the stiff suit\u2019s fucking phone for a few moments before putting that back as well. \u201cOk, ok, I was just looking for a little drinking money...\u201d He trailed off and his eyes went a little wide as he saw Liz biting Vanessa, draining her until she passed out before beginning to glow.<br /> <br /> I clapped him on the shoulder. \u201cDon\u2019t fucking worry, you\u2019ll get used to it. Eventually.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> The kid was serious about getting a drink that didn\u2019t come from my flask, so we hit up Kiki\u2019s. Naomi and Vivian joined us, Vivian still nursing a goddamn hell of a hangover. She ordered a greasy fucking breakfast as step one of a cure, and Jared provided a bit of hair of the dog for step two.<br /> <br /> \u201cHurricane, Kamikaze, Margarita, Sex on the Beach.\u201d he said, pointing at Naomi, me, Vivian and himself in turn. Not a bad fucking round, especially since he was paying.<br /> <br /> The usuals were mostly there, sans Robin, a fact that disappointed the shit out of Naomi. There was also a suit, a real fucking butter and egg man, surrounded by a gaggle of broads. Naomi nudged me, in between complaints about a lack of birds named Robin hereabouts. \u201cThe gentleman over there is interested in acquiring Carla Pierce, by the way.\u201d<br /> <br /> I glanced that direction, then leaned back in my chair to get a more natural angle. \u201cSanderson\u2019s twist?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, the one Mrs. Sanderson fears will replace her. Also a boat, but that seems less interesting.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian glanced up from the laptop she had been muttering over. \u201cHe\u2019s afraid of Sanderson. And Herb.\u201d<br /> <br /> I complained about goddamn charity work, just to keep my hand in and cover my scrutiny. \u201cHe\u2019s keeping an eye out for someone. A meeting, perhaps? Or just wanting to avoid Herb?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jared excused himself and went off to chinwag with one of the suit\u2019s hanger ons. I kept an eye on him while we continued our chatter. Well, Naomi and I did. Vivian kept sending fucking death glares at her computer, occasionally muttering and flipping it off. Jared came back after a detour to the can. \u201cRight on the first one. A meeting with that Carla Pierce you mentioned. Mr Erwin there asked her. She didn\u2019t seem too thrilled at the idea.\u201d<br /> <br /> As if on cue, Carla walked into the bar. A handsome woman, she was dressed in a suit this side of severe and a no-nonsense attitude. She scanned the crowd, her gaze lingering on me just a touch too fucking long for comfort. I sighed. \u201c:I guess it was too fucking much to ask that I was just a family problem for Sanderson.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi smiled. \u201cDon\u2019t sell yourself short Gabe, what if you charms and witticisms had made their way to her ears completely independently of her capacity as personal security for Mr. Sanderson?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sneered at her and put on my dark glasses to activate aura sight and mind reading. \u201cWee, neither of the fuckers are supernatural. She\u2019s fairly fucking certain I\u2019m a threat, but not dead set on the goddamn idea.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian looked up briefly again, this time from some goddamn phone she and Jared were tinkering with, somewhat concerned. \u201cThat\u2019s... not so good. She kills people she feels are threats. Well, has them killed . Though, thinking about it, Mrs. Sanderson is a personal threat, not a job-related one, so maybe you\u2019re good? Also, she\u2019s afraid of Mr. Sanderson, in a turn on kinda way, and Herb, in not a turn on kinda way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m always good.\u201d I smiled at Vivian and delved into Carla\u2019s thoughts. I snickered. \u201cWell, she\u2019s frustrated she can\u2019t just seduce Erwin and get this shit over with. So either he bats for a different team, or she\u2019s not nearly so good at that as I fucking figured. If things go south, she\u2019s got a button in her right inside jacket pocket that will call in some kinda fucking backup.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi looked frustrated. \u201cI can\u2019t quite tell whether he\u2019s blackmailing, threatening or concerned for her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCarla thinks he\u2019s testing her loyalty. He\u2019s suggesting there is some kind of fucking threat to her within the organization, on Sanderson\u2019s side.\u201d I focused and managed to pull the memory of me to the surface. The goddamn security team reported that someone of my description survived an encounter with Gina, so there must be something odd about me. I was clearly combat-capable and despite my wound never appeared at any goddamn hospital, so I must have a supernatural healing factor. That\u2019s all they had though. Thin at best, no real fucking angle.<br /> <br /> Naomi picked up the slack in the silence I left digging that up. \u201cWell, she keeps implying that he has a guard, and he keep ignoring it, so probably he doesn\u2019t have one but doesn\u2019t want to let on? Also, he think he works for a god.\u201d<br /> <br /> That sure as hell distracted me. \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cApparently, Sanderson is not that god she should be working for,\u201d she said, still listening intently.<br /> <br /> I swapped focus and started going through his fucking mind. I realized after a few moments. \u201cGod\u2019s just fucking lingo he\u2019s using for the broad\u2019s benefit. Whoever he works for is just another goddamn supernatural in a suit. Erwin there figures he\u2019s on the same level as Sanderson.\u201d I dug a little deeper. \u201cThe hell kinda name is Erasmus?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe kind you pick to sound cool? I mean, I can\u2019t really say anything,I picked Clytemnestra.\u201d Naomi offered.<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cHe is a little out of date, so maybe I\u2019ll give him that. According to him, he\u2019s been fucking asleep for the past century or so. Our boy there really is a butter and egg man, and Erasmus\u2019 only link to green. Gonna get a boost out of it, some sort of fucking ritual to make him more powerful and resilient.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf he\u2019s the money man, why\u2019s he meeting with Carla?\u201d Naomi said, one ear still on the pair\u2019s conversation.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m getting there Princess, don\u2019t fucking rush me.\u201d I winked at her. The going was a little rougher, but I dredged up their meeting regarding the bird. \u201cWell then. Maybe god wasn\u2019t so fucking far off. Erasmus believes Sanderson can create life whole cloth. He\u2019s looking to either get a piece of that action or ice it as a goddamn threat and he\u2019s figured Carla as the best way to get at him.\u201d I smirked at Naomi. \u201cHe\u2019s pretty sure she\u2019s got a ready supply of his DNA and that Sanderson\u2019ll eventually bump her off...\u201d<br /> <br /> I was interrupted by a fucking loud crash as an entire goddamn tray of drinks found its way onto Erwin Holt\u2019s lap. The kid was loitering over there and I just barely saw his hand dipping into Carla\u2019s jacket pocket and then his pants pocket. She didn\u2019t notice and neither did he. But I saw enough to head to the bar for a refill and get lost in the crowd on the way.<br /> <br /> Good thing I did too. Her backup was fucking quick to respond to the panic button,guns drawn. Carla barked out orders in accented Arabic, pulling her own piece to cover Erwin and sending her people to find the \u2018second subject\u2019, presumably yours fucking truly. The bartender roared a stop to the shenanigans, so Carla gave Erwin 60 seconds to get the hell out and made tracks herself,<br /> <br /> I gave it some time before joining the three at our table again. Naomi was chiding the pair of Saboteurs. \u201cAre we proud of ourselves?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jared smiled broadly. \u201cIt was like synchronized swimming!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust like we planned.\u201d Vivian\u2019s attention was back on her laptop,a number having been acquired from the waitress she shielded from the chaos. \u201cApparently Erwin doesn\u2019t like being caught in the rain.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe were plotting but... You said this Erasmus dude thought he was a god? Like, a real god? Cause I killed a god back in 900, and I\u2019m pretty sure he was just this really tall dude.\u201d The kid was still riding high on the thrill.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe did have some kind of fucking mind control shit at least. He showed that off as an opener. Nothing else in the memories I watched.\u201d I shrugged and finished off my drink.<br /> <br /> A new arrival had us all look up to the door. Louis didn\u2019t give any goddamn sign he recognized me and had no fucking reason to recognize the other, so Naomi and Vivian stepped off and came back as Liz and Billy Mack. When they joined me and Jared, Louis came over.<br /> <br /> \u201cLouis, darling, it\u2019s so nice to see you.\u201d Liz greeted him.<br /> <br /> Louis nodded. \u201cI thought that might have been you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cI am glad you have not run into any trouble.\u201d Louis raised an eyebrow. \u201cWe heard Puriel destroyed a number of Demons outside of town recently.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, yes, your redhead. She is interested in that dam, is she not?\u201d He let that trail off.<br /> <br /> Liz picked up a different fucking thread out of the silence. \u201cI suppose so. Louis, my dear, we\u2019d been hoping to run into you, as it were. There are a couple of vampires we\u2019ve encountered at our watering hole. An Aryan looking pair?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey breathe fucking mustard gas, if that helps.\u201d I butted in.<br /> <br /> Louis leaned back. \u201cAh, the heavy hitters brought in by the Invictus to counteract the Carthians. He\u2019s an ex-soldier and she was.. well, technically, a field nurse, but she might as well have been called a soldier.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf they\u2019re working for, what the fuck was it, the Invictus, it\u2019s be no skin off your nose if they happened to, say, get punched in the face a little?\u201d I asked,<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. They were brought here to kill vampires, however, Keep that in mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> I waved aside his concern. \u201cSure, sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> Louis leaned forward and tried putting the question to us directly this time. \u201cWhat have you found out about the dam?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey have a new Destroyer accompanying outgoing shipments.\u201d Liz described Metalmouth. \u201cI do use she rather loosely here. Her breast shaped bits were probably drills.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cEverything else was.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cInteresting.\u201d Louis looked thoughtful. \u201cAnd if I may, what was the situation here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRabble rousing. Hijinx. A meeting of parties interested in the Sanderson situation. It was getting somewhat tedious.\u201d Billy Mack smiled slightly.<br /> <br /> Louis raised an eyebrow. \u201cI had gotten the impression he was involved.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnother question, if we may, Louis.\u201d He inclined his head towards her. \u201cDo you know anything about a Michael White?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Angel?\u201d Liz nodded. \u201cI have no idea why he is not Fallen. He\u2019s a rogue element, occasionally working at cross purposes to other Angelic actions. He has all the signs: a personality, his own volition, personal malice. He\u2019s even harvesting his own personal backup of Essence, but he is definitely still plugged in. Take care in your dealings with him. He makes me look like a nice person and I...\u201d The shadows around him deepened. \u201c... am not a nice person. If you want to know capabilities... He\u2019s definitely a messenger. He\u2019s got the regular gamut of social maneuvering powers.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked mortally offended. \u201cHe doesn\u2019t have the chops! He sounded like an idiot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen he meant to.\u201d Louis shrugged. \u201cIf he does Fall, there\u2019s a 50/50 chance he\u2019ll be useful to the cause at all, so I haven\u2019t made any effort to tip the scales. It is possible that he is a Demon that has learned how to fake the connection.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat could be useful, I suppose.\u201d Billy Mack mused.<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps. Well, my curiosity is sated, for now. Enjoy your evening, ladies, gentlemen. \u201cThe spook left and took his shadows with him.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Gabe, with the green light, do you have a plan for the vampires?\u201d Liz raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> I put on my confused face. \u201cPunch them in the goddamn mouth?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked at me. \u201cSo we\u2019ll be taking that up pro bono?\u201d<br /> <br /> I flipped her off. Jared started giggling. I gave him a look, but he was looking down at his own phone, for once. \u201cErwin thinks \u2018Sanderson\u2019s agents\u2019 busted up the meeting.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stared at him. \u201cHow the fuck do you know that?\u201d I flipped Liz off again when she glanced back at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Um, Vivian and I wrote an app that I put on his phone before I gave it back. It sends all his texts to me as well as to whoever he says to. See?\u201d He showed me the messages on his phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat at least is clever.\u201d Liz said as I flipped her off. \u201cWell, I have a secretary and a pile of cocaine waiting for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAw, I was hoping to his another stop.\u201d The kid looked disappointed.<br /> <br /> Liz glanced at him and smiled. \u201cSure. The secretary\u2019s not going anywhere.\u201d<br /> <br /> He returned her smile. \u201cWhat about the mountain of cocaine?\u201d<br /> <br /> She tapped her chin. \u201cIt\u2019s not really a mountain, more of a small hill.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA mole hill?I hear you can turn them into mountains.\u201d I smirked at her and flipped her off again. \u201cWhat about Mavericks? You\u2019ll love it kid. Though, it is Tuesday...\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz rolled her eyes. \u201cPerhaps I will see that secretary. You three enjoy yourselves though.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kilroy's Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Idol Hands</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Hedgeover</b><br /> <br /> I really have no excuse for the poor judgment I displayed last night. It is true, I was rattled somewhat by the effects of that ocular oracular Hedge fruit but I still should have known better than to attempt to match Speed's fortitude in the consumption of alcohol. The appearance of Dieter while I was so indisposed could well have gone far more poorly than it did. And while I was able to get a decent night's rest and rise at a reasonable hour as Billy Mac, Vivian will have to recover at some point from my indiscretions and based on how I was feeling before I shifted quantum states I fear it will be a decidedly unpleasant and tragically lengthy process. Perhaps it is time to further investigate one of the embeds or exploits that allow the separation of quantum states. That would allow Vivian to suffer through her alcohol poisoning without lowering my efficiency.<br /> <br /> I shared a ride to the office with Naomi before she made her way to campus for her classes. I should see about securing some transportation of my own. The Winnebago is not well suited for city driving nor is it inconspicuous in the least. Though perhaps it could suit Vivian's needs. Her cover's lack of meat-space interactions does allow me to take certain luxuries with the cover but it would be good for her to have a home and the nomadic existence suited her lifestyle rather well before our merger.<br /> <br /> The morning passed quietly and while I waited for my fellow unchained or a client I took the occasion to update Billy Mac's Facebook and check up on the shadier corners of the internet as Marley^s_Gh05t (A handle that predates her meeting me ironically). It did remind me that now that I have settled in it really is time to acquire Vivian a machine worthy of her reputation and talents. I rather suspect being seen with something as plain as this laptop would be quite out of character for her. I should ask around when I have some time, I'm sure I can barter the account numbers I took from Stephan's computer for some suitable hardware and a bit of illicit software to trick it out.<br /> <br /> <b>Cryptid Mating Habits</b><br /> <br /> Speed was the first to join me in the office. She arrived late in the morning but before noon. We had just started to discuss the day's plans when Cecilia poked her head in to let us know that Jimmy Marsh was there and that he could lick his own eyeball.<br /> <br /> Jimmy had come to confirm our continued existence. It seems that Puriel had killed a group of unchained south of the city. And, in keeping with her modus operandi, she had started a significant forest fire while reducing her victims to unidentifiable fragments. Jimmy was relieved to discover that we had not been incinerated since that would have upset Scarecrow. He mentioned another ring, the Fools, and that they were likewise still intact. He seemed less pleased that Valefar was most likely not among the deceased. Of course, once he recounted his meeting with our fellow demon, I could not really blame him. Valefar's dislike for Scarecrow runs quite deep apparently. There is obviously some history there. Sadly, I doubt there is an unbiased account of it, which is concerning as I suspect that we will come to find ourselves dealing with the fallout of their personal disagreement at some point.<br /> <br /> Once Jimmy had enlightened us, I shared the basics of our case involving the missing bounty hunter Drake and the suspected angel Micheal White. Jimmy was not familiar with White or the raided infrastructure but he offered to pass it along to Scarecrow since he is kept rather intentionally unaware of things that he is not directly involved in, both for his own well being and to protect Scarecrow's operational security. I was a bit surprised that he also offered to keep the details as discreet as he could. I assured him that I would not have shared anything with him that I did not want Scarecrow to know. I like the reptoid well enough and it would be rude to place him in such a position.<br /> <br /> At that point, Jimmy said his goodbyes and was on his way. I mused on his habit of eye licking aloud. It is likely a means of identifying himself to other reptoids (though certainly there are less obvious ways that would not reveal him to hostiles). It might also be flirtatious, based on his tenancy to do it in the presence of attractive females. I believe Speed may have misinterpreted that for interest on my part, or perhaps she simply found it an opening to comment on my choices of sexual partners since making her acquaintance. At any rate, I assured her I was not considering a liaison with Marsh. I have no desire to complicate our relationship with Scarecrow by emotional entanglements with his operative. There are plenty of other reptoids I can investigate without such concerns.<br /> <br /> I did also remark that I should keep him from meeting Ganora. Speed gave me a rather juvenile smirk and asked if I was jealous. I had to pause a moment before answering her. I told her that I was more concerned that she might react to his advances by eating him, which would clearly be problematic.<br /> <br /> Though, to be completely honest, the thought of Ganora with another male does provoke a certain negative emotional response. A most human and curious reaction and one I should be watchful of. It would not do to allow such feelings to cloud my judgment.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra, still wearing Naomi, entered shortly after Jimmy's departure. Speed and I were privy to a rather amusing conversation as she arrived and her cousin Cecilia chided her on not being suitably presentable for their Goddess. As entertaining as it was, Speed and I interrupted and collected her to investigate the remaining two addresses Michael White had sent Drake.<br /> <br /> <b>Entertaining Venues</b><br /> <br /> The remaining addresses proved to be rather curious. The two locations were near the building with the Hedge gate. The entire area was in a state of urban decay, the sole holdout of functional civilization was a lone bar of rather seedy demeanour that catered to a decidedly Hispanic clientele.<br /> <br /> The first of our two sites proved to be some sort of underground and unsanctioned fighting ring. The second was an old theater that a pair of moth-men had taken up as a nest. Neither seemed particularly hazardous for a man of Drake's capabilities nor likely was the hiding place of a runaway girl.<br /> Speed elected to stake out the area in hopes of asking either the local homeless or, with luck, those involved in the fighting club if they had seen or heard of either Drake or White. I gave her some of my Aether since she was depleted before we went our separate ways.<br /> <br /> <b>Research and Planning</b><br /> <br /> Having already spent time in the library, Clytemnestra elected to spend the evening working on strengthening her Naomi cover. Stephen met me at the mansion and was as helpful and yet antsy as always. The library was absolutely amazing, even better than my earlier perusal of it had led me to expect. I was easily able to find everything I needed to formulate a binding ritual for the Vessel of Iniquity. The only real concern was insuring the spirit remained in proximity to the statue after being ejected from its current host. A suitable source of lustful activity would keep it from departing in self-preservation and distract it, though it would also empower it. Alternatively, a display of temperance would weaken and distract it, though would not force it to remain. However, the mansion does feature a ritual room in the basement equipped with an occult circle capable of trapping it reliably.<br /> <br /> The next day, we all gathered at the Night Train offices to exchange notes and formulate our plan of attack. Speed reported that the fighting club was run by a female Changeling going by the name Rosanna who apparently carried herself with an air of refinement somewhat at odds with the venue. She is aware of and seems interested in keeping people away from the Hedge gate. She did not, however, appear to be familiar with Micheal White. Herb is apparently a regular attendee and occasional participant. It does not surprise me and I think I would enjoy seeing him demonstrate his prowess again at some point. The security was also of interest. An apparently capable human named Jake handles it and made a point of informing Speed Demon that he knew absolutely nothing of Micheal White and that she would well served to do the same.<br /> <br /> As for the Vessel of Iniquity, I proposed that we should have Stephen bring Vanessa to the mansion and down to the basement where the mystic circle could hold the spirit once I possessed her. I suggested that Clytemnestra attempt to seduce Speed Demon while she tried to resist. It seemed reasonable enough to me, if Speed Demon did resist the advances it would weaken the spirit. If she succumbed, then the spirit would still be distracted. Speed Demon seemed agreeable enough but Clytemnestra did not seem pleased with the idea. Her counter proposal was to simply bind and feed upon the spirit if it manifested. With the circle to prevent it from escaping, it will have to do so to disrupt the ritual. Speed Demon's role will be to contain and protect Stephen. Also, she will drink heavily before the ritual so that Clytemnestra can shift the consequences of her intoxication to him. Once we complete the binding, I shall edit memories as necessary. Both Speed Demon and Clytemnestra seem pleased with this plan of action and it should produce the desired results.<br /> <br /> <b>Don't Look a Gift Basket in the Mouth</b><br /> <br /> We had just sorted out our plans and had finished contacting Stephen to have him bring Vanessa to the mansion that night when Clytemnestra's minion poked her head in. A gift basket of meats and cheeses had been delivered with the note 'Eat Healthy New Neighbor' attached. It had been sent by one Dr Samuel Miles.<br /> <br /> There was some discussion over who this individual was and why he had reached out to us. A quick check confirmed that he had a practice in downtown and no other digital footprint. As it seemed unlikely that an Angel would send a gift basket (unless perhaps in the form of an oddly named hunter) the likely situation is that he is a fellow Unchained. Perhaps a member of the Fools that Jimmy mentioned. Neither Speed Demon nor Clytemnestra seemed inclined to try the gift, even after I sampled a bit. No matter, it shall give me something to placate my human need for sustenance while working for a while.<br /> <br /> I did attempt to call Dr Miles at his practice. The secretary seemed quite surprised to field a call for him and told me he wasn't in. I left a message thanking him for the thoughtful gift. Clearly a matter to follow up on later.<br /> <br /> <b>Developments at the Dam</b><br /> <br /> We made our way to the Diablo Dam to fill our batteries before confronting the Vessel of Iniquity. Speed Demon made impossibly good time as always. I must confess, I am pleased with the Mustang's performance after our work to modify it. There is some room for further improvements, but it suits Speed Demon quite well. Also, she seems to clearly enjoy driving something worthy of her abilities.<br /> <br /> Traveling to Diablo was also an opportunity to speak to Ganora and update her on the situation. I will not lie, I was looking forward to seeing her. I was not expecting what awaited me when we did however.<br /> <br /> Ganora is with child. My child.<br /> <br /> She was pleased to see us, as always, and inquired as to the nature of our visit. She also informed me that she had not yet laid the egg. She is carrying it much as a human might at present. I explained that we had come to gather Aether from the dam's Infrastructure. I inquired about the rattus and while she did not go into detail she did express that they had been troublesome. I told her we would try to reduce their threat while we were there.<br /> <br /> Both Speed Demon and Clytemnestra seemed to find the situation off putting. Reproduction is one of the decidedly new facets of our existence and certainly a matter of great significance. I must confess, I had not thought on it overly much myself before this point. Academically, I know that the offspring of the Unchained are not entirely human though the exact effects are, to my knowledge, unpredictable. Further complicating this is that Ganora, despite her appearance, is entirely non human. I have no information on cryptid demon hybrids. I shall have to research the matter.<br /> <br /> I am to be a father.<br /> <br /> In my existence as an Angel, I have played this role. It was often a fitting and suitable cover for protecting and guiding a scholar or inventor while they furthered the God-Machine's plans. But this is something wholly different. This life is my doing. Kilroy is immortal, but William McKenzie is not, nor is he overly young. He was never born, a figment invented whole cloth by the God-Machine. But now that construct is part of me, and some measure of it will live apart from me. Billy Mac's child will outlive him. Or will it? The very realization that this is not a fact troubles me. My offspring will be one of Ganora's people. His or her well-being is tied to their own. I find myself reconsidering the pact we had planned.<br /> <br /> I am worried about the mother of my child.<br /> <br /> Ganora is very useful to us. To me. Yet it is self deception to claim that I am not rapidly becoming emotionally compromised where she is concerned. My goal to see her and her people secure and safe has become less objective, less pragmatic. They are not simply valuable tools or even soldiers in the war against the God-machine. I want to see them free of its mechanizations. I am feeling a very human instinct toward my unborn child and by extension its mother. Yet I am also feeling the lingering vestiges of my design and programming. I was a shield, a protector. I still am. Human instinct and angelic design are in convergence.<br /> <br /> I am entering very dangerous territory here. I cannot be fully objective with regard to this situation. This wellspring of instincts and emotions within is fascinating and unfamiliar. I have such questions. Will our spawnling favor Ganora or myself in appearance? What elements of Kilroy will bleed into it? Will it... love me? Is that part of what I am feeling now? For Ganora? For this child?<br /> <br /> I will move forward with the pact. I will strengthen Ganora. I will secure her control of the lake and the dam. I must remain aware of these feelings but I shall not attempt to avoid them, despite the urge to. I am simultaneously excited and afraid of how this development is effecting me but I choose to embrace it.<br /> <br /> It shall be a grand experiment.<br /> <br /> We entered the dam through the underwater passages. Ganora swam in with us but did not enter the Infrastructure proper. We made ourselves ready in case of rattus, but found something infinitely more deadly.<br /> <br /> We were alerted by the sound of bees and correctly guessed that agents of the God-Machine were present to collect Essence. What we did not anticipate was