ur plans demanded.<br /> <br /> I do wonder if there is a way to sufficiently disguise Ganora's inhuman nature enough to share such indulgences with her at least occasionally? I would like that.<br /> <br /> <b>Last Minute Substitutions</b><br /> <br /> While we had hoped that Quietus would be available to provide a bit of extra force if things went awry, it was not the case. However, in a fortunate bit of timing Fulgur contacted me as we were finishing up the meal.<br /> <br /> It seemed like an ideal opportunity for my companions to see him in action and for him to get a feel for the team and all involved agreed. Speed Demon swung by the campus to pick him up on our way to the mansion.<br /> <br /> While it has proved inconvenient for him to have fallen while in a young cover I think Fulgur has gained a certain amount of youthful exuberance from it. I do envy him a bit in being so free to simply revel in the newness of things without raising suspicions. Of course, he lacks the nativity typically coupled with youth. I think Vivian was fond of that mixture, as she was much the same in her youth due to being a child of the system as it were. I do know she liked him better than many of the Unchained she met during our time together.<br /> <br /> I have determined that riding with Speed Demon is much like facing a dangerous predator. You must show absolutely no fear. In my case, it is the fact that I know this is as natural to her as walking (perhaps even moreso given her true form). Fulgur rather quickly ingrained himself to her with his obvious enjoyment of her driving.<br /> <br /> At any rate, thanks in part to Fulgur's antics spirits were high as we made our way to the mansion. And before we arrived he turned his attention to the task at hand. We went over the plan we'd made and revised it to account for his presence. As he also has Wave Form Collapse, we decided to have him enter discreetly and lie in wait in the ritual room so he could use that to lock the spirit in its manifest state and free Clytemnestra to focus on physically restraining it.<br /> <br /> Stephen was punctual. Vanessa was in route. Speed Demon was amused at his use of the term 'lady' to describe Vanessa. I do not believe it was entirely a part of her ruse to distracting him from Fulgur's presence by acting unprofessional.<br /> <br /> Everything went as intended. Stephen was off balance by Speed Demon's drinking and uncouth manners and thus Fulgur was easily able to slip inside and down to the ritual chamber to find a good position for the ambush. Once Vanessa arrived, we all moved to join him there. I crossed into the circle and brought out the statue. Clytemnestra joined me and shifted the consequences of Speed Demon's power drinking to Stephen. Speed Demon caught the poor man and eased him to a couch as he was far less practiced at holding so much alcohol. Vanessa balked at the circle, the spirit inside sensing the danger to itself.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra dropped her cover and plucked Vanessa into her grasp while I activated the circle to insure the spirit could not escape. The possessed woman struggled quite aggressively but before the spirit could use her to escape I flowed through Twilight and filled her. The struggle was different, with the spirit being much more aware of what was happening than a human consciousness typically is. It was much better at fighting but suffered from the disadvantage of not being truly anchored to the body the way a person is. I forced it out and suppressed Vanessa's mind.<br /> <br /> The thing appeared in physical form as expected. It was androgynous and alien and beautiful. It was also quite enraged at what we intended. Fulgur dropped from his hiding place on the ceiling as Clytemnestra seized the physical spirit. I quickly began to chant the ritual and make Vanessa's fingers dance the arcane gestures that accompanied it. The Vessel of Iniquity was completely overwhelmed before it had a chance to fight.<br /> <br /> I smiled and took a moment to smooth Vanessa's hands down her body to settle her outfit. I looked down at the statue once more imprisoning the Vessel of Iniquity and feeling a touch pleased with myself at our victory I made a joking reference to how the busting of ghosts made me feel.<br /> <br /> At that point, it was time to deal with Vanessa and Stephan\u2019s memories. Clytemnestra took Vanessa into her arms and used a combination of her Halo and her bite to weaken the woman into unconsciousness safely. It was a pity to give up such a pretty form so quickly.<br /> <br /> It was simple enough to rewrite their memories of the evening to a version of the ritual without giant golden spiders or demonic powers. A ritual that also left them both weary and so they choose to take a rest in one of the guest bedrooms. Once we'd tucked them in, we let ourselves out.<br /> <br /> <b>A Little Excitement at Kiki's</b><br /> <br /> Fulgur was of a mind to celebrate our victory and the rest were in agreement. I had some business to see to as Vivian but nothing that couldn't be handled from a nice dark table at Kiki's. Clytemnestra also changed into Naomi for the club hopping, as Kiki's is not really the sort of place a socialite of Liz's caliber frequents.<br /> <br /> I did not think about Fulgur's previous acquaintance with Vivian before I changed but if it bothered him to see me wearing her he didn't show it. Still, I should speak to him about it at some point. When he asked about her previously I did give him a rather brief answer. Given how well he worked with the ring, I do think it's safe to say he's going to be a part of our activities. And even if he does not for whatever reason, I enjoy his company and consider him an ally and friend.<br /> <br /> We took him to Kiki's, introducing him to the place and it's clandestine ambiance. He bought the first round, which did not do over much to ease the throbbing headache that Vivian was nursing. I ordered a traditional breakfast, pancakes and hash-browns and grits and toast with a bit of bacon for salt. I also switched to coffee after that fist drink. By the time we'd finished the evening I was feeling reasonably reasonable once more.<br /> <br /> I divided my attention between the conversation and people watching and Vivian's laptop and phone. I floated a few hooks in the usual places and pretty soon I had a couple of nibbles.<br /> <br /> The show started up a little while after we'd gotten there. There was a smoothly clad gentleman with a table full of pretty women clearly waiting for someone to arrive. Fulgur made his way over and tried to flirt with one of them as a cover for stealing the man's phone.<br /> <br /> The individual's name was Erwin Holt and he was there to meet with none other than Sanderson's head of security Carla Pierce. Fulgur was working to slip a ghost app on the phone that would invisibly cc him on all of the man's texts. Nice little trick actually. I had a couple of technical suggestions when he showed it to me which he incorporated to tie it up in a tidy little bow.<br /> <br /> Once Pierce showed up things proved interesting. Holt was out to acquire her as a double agent for the interests of his master, some manner of supernatural being going by the name Erasmus. Pierce was annoyed that she could not simply use her feminine whiles to wrap Holt around her finger and be done with the situation. Erasmus is interested in Sanderson's ability to create life and in acquiring samples of his DNA. They also seem to believe that it's only a matter of time before Sanderson decides Carla Pierce is more useful as parts than as the person she is now.<br /> <br /> Pierce recognized Speed Demon from the description Gina Sanderson gave and was on edge at her presence, incorrectly guessing that she was there as backup for Holt. She's sure Speed Demon isn't normal since she survived and has recovered from her injuries inhumanly quickly. But she's more worried about Gina herself, being fairly sure the woman intends to kill her and intending to take steps to see that Gina is eliminated first.<br /> <br /> The whole exchange opened many questions that will need to be investigated. Before they could get down to any real serious business however, we intervened.<br /> <br /> Fulgur needed a good distraction to plant the now bugged phone back on Holt without him noticing it had been missing. But Fulgur was also itching for some trouble and between the headache behind my eyes and dealing with Dmitri\u2019s Russian machismo I was ready to relieve a bit of frustration myself. Maybe it's a bit of Vivian's soul as well. She was always fond of chaos and while we were together I would sometimes indulge in it just to see the delight it brought her.<br /> <br /> Fulgur got up and began to make his way toward the bar. I fixed our waitress with a look and summoned her with a crook of my finger. Given the place, I cannot imagine she doesn't get that sort of treatment from men, women, and whatever Herb is fairly routinely. But she just smiled and headed over. As came within earshot I started some casual flirting, pitched just soft enough for her to have to lean in a bit to hear me over the loud retro rock. I nudged the natural flow of coincidence with Cause and Effect at that point. Some kid walking by let his gaze linger on the sight of Shelley's cleavage far too long and when he tore it away he found himself faced with an angry girlfriend. He stepped back from her scowl right into another waitress who just so happened to be carrying a tray of plates and drinks, which went crashing onto the table and laps of Holt and Pierce.<br /> <br /> They jumped up and Fulgur danced in, phone slipped into his pocket and a hand ducked into hers to tap the panic button she was carrying before he vanished.<br /> <br /> For my part, I pulled Shelley forward and turned her to sit her in my lap as the wave of disaster expanded outward behind her, drawing her out of the way of the poor sod who'd served as my trigger as he stumbled forward away from the collision with his arms windmilling to try and regain his balance and letting him tackle some other unsuspecting patron instead of her.<br /> <br /> That was when Pierce's backup rolled in and the guns came out. I slipped an arm protectively around Shelley's shoulders as Pierce prepared to round up Holt and his 'accomplice'. Speed Demon had already vanished into the crowd so Pierce had no luck there and the bartender roared and shouted down the entire place to restore order. Pierce gave Holt a few seconds to leave before she shot him and he wisely did so. Then she withdrew as well, doing her best not to let it show that she hadn't intended to summon her backup. My distraction excused herself from my lap as the bartender ordered her to help clear the mess but not without giving me a wink and jotting down her number on the back of my hand. Shelley is certainly a pretty girl and it seems likely that a life that brings one to working as a waitress at Kiki's might well include a bit of unwanted baggage or harbor a few unfulfilled dreams. I shall have to see what sort of deal she's inclined to make with this particular devil.<br /> <br /> <b>Speaking of Devils</b><br /> <br /> As the bar returned to a semblance of normalcy, I finished wrangling out the details of my meeting with Dmitri. The man is a pig but his connections to the Russian mafia are solid. And while his ego demands that he present a constant display of lewd and disrespectful behavior toward a half Japanese girl to save face, he and Vivian have done business for years. I'll be meeting with him at a hole in the wall Greek diner by the docks tomorrow afternoon to trade the account numbers I lifted from Stephan\u2019s office for a clean and untraceable high performance laptop and a copy of the latest decryption tools from his buddies in Russian military intelligence. I'll need to hit a liqueur store first, Dmitri does love to wash down his tzatziki with cheap vodka.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I was wrapping up the details and considering who, if any, of my fellow Unchained I might want to bring just in case when Valefar strolled in. He settled in and Speed Demon stepped over. The rest of us slipped into the covers he knew and joined her. It was a chance to introduce him and Fulgur.<br /> <br /> Seems he was curious about what had caused all the ruckus. We admitted that we'd been having a bit of innocent fun. Then while we had him we took the opportunity to chat him up a bit. He asked about the dam and we asked about Micheal White. Seems White is an angel but no one is sure how or why. He acts like a fallen yet remains plugged in. Most peculiar. Valefar hasn't tried to push him since he's not sure what more could be done to make White fall and he's not sure he wants to deal with him as a rival for local power. The mustard gas vampires that Speed Demon is irate about are apparently a duo of out of town heavy hitters the Invictus faction has brought in to deal with their rivals in a direct fashion. So he doesn't care one way or the other what we do about them but did make sure to point out that they are both highly skilled combatants trained in dealing with supernatural threats. Speed Demon did not seem overly impressed and certainly wasn't dissuaded from her planned face punching.<br /> <br /> The evening wound down after that. Clytemnestra departed to spend the rest of the night with her secretary and a pile of cocaine. The rest of us traveled to Maverick's, one of Speed's regular haunts. It was late and a weeknight but none the less we all got to meet the owner, a friend of Speed's and a rather colorful individual. There was a bit more drinking and a few rounds of darts and pool to be had. Not a bad note to end the night on.<br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> You are a good girl, Kayla.<br /> <br /> Now where was I? Right, the Exorcism. We actually got a call from Fulgur who was free on our way so swung by to get him after dinner\u2026needless to say, Speed knew how to adjust for time. We incorporated him into the plan to have him collapse the Spirit\u2019s wave function to trap it physical. He would sneak in first so he would be hidden and Vanessa unaware.<br /> <br /> When we got there, Stephan was waiting, but Vanessa was late. Speed of course, teased him mercilessly and made him uncomfortable, as is her way. Fulgur easily snuck in and hid in a lighting fixture above the circle. Speed drank heavily, and when we got down there she distracted Stephan with her generally boorish behavior while I distracted Vanessa to keep her from noticing Fulgur. That worked fine, but she did notice the circle, which meant I had to act. I shed Liz and because my full glorious form and pulled her to me. Of course, Stephan saw that, but I quickly transferred Speed\u2019s drunkenness to him.<br /> <br /> Oh I suppose I did pull you to me. Sweetie. My are you not lovely. Kempai!<br /> <br /> Tasty. Wait, did you think I would kill you know? Oh please, I promised we would sleep together first. You are so jumpy!<br /> <br /> Ahem. Anyway, Where was I? Yes. So I pulled her in and Kilroy immediately possessed Vanessa, kicking the Spirit out. Fulgur was in quickly but she shrugged up the attempt to trap her in solid form. The Destroyer was tenacious, though, and got her on second try and I managed to get her in a secure hold while Kilroy \u201cactivated\u201d the circle and started the Ritual. Fortunately, he was quite efficient, he got it done very quickly while I held the Spirit, and managed to get it sealed in the vessel before it could try to influence us. I then activated my halo, and sank my teeth into Vanessa, who passed out pretty quick. The halo kept her stable, though. She was pretty tasty as people without Essence go. Not as tasty as you dear. You are exceptional. Maybe I should keep you alive so I can keep snacking on you. Oh well, you will figure out what I decide soon enough.<br /> <br /> I put Naomi on while Kilroy went around memory spiking heads so they would not remember anything too unusual. Well, nothing Compromising to us. We made sure they were safe and sound and headed out to Johnny\u2019s, then Kiki\u2019s. That\u2019s where the Thugs decided it was time for some chaos. See, the evening started quiet, and we sort of introduced Fulgur to the place, when a twitchy little man caught our attention. His name was Erwin Holt, and he was there to meet someone. Reading his heart, he was clearly unfriendly to Sanderson and wanted to acquire Carla Pierce, his secretary-slash-right hand woman as a weapon. She was coming to meet him.<br /> <br /> After her arrival things got more tense, and Kilroy and Fulgur sprung into action. By the end she had called security, and both had left. The Saboteurs were quite proud of themselves.<br /> <br /> Eventually Valefar showed up. He confirmed Michael White was an Angel, but somehow had not fallen despite showing a lot of Demon characteristics. Of course, he could be a Demon expertly hiding his tracks. Either way I am going to kill the fucker.<br /> <br /> Oh and Speed does not like being reminded her \u201cCharity cases\u201d are \u201cCharity cases.\u201d It begins at home, you know.<br /> <br /> So what have you been up to?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Fulgur\u2019s War Journal</b><br /> <br /> <u>Entry #2: Si Vis Pascem, Para Bellum</u><br /> <br /> Officially a month in town and it\u2019s time to stop hiding and go on offense. This is a new town, one that\u2019s completely across the map from my old home. I need friends, strong ones. So I call Kilroy.<br /> <br /> Kilroy, Speed, and Cly are apparently geared up to work some mojo at their client Stefan\u2019s house. I see a perfect opportunity to see what they got and show off a little to ingratiate myself. Plus, if Cly is serious about putting me on the payroll, I\u2019m game. The cost of a decent university education is enough to give the immortal a pause. I dumped everything Gene and I saved on books, tuition, and my \u201cmedically necessary\u201d private dorm room.<br /> <br /> My senior investigators pulled up in Speed\u2019s car. What a sweet ride. I popped up through the sunroof. Felt the breeze on my face as Speed took a corner doing 60 and thrilled a little. After a few more minutes, I ducked back inside and got a sit-rep from Cly.<br /> <br /> The particulars were pretty\u2026lascivious. Some type of lust spirit that needed to be shoved back into a fetish. Kilroy was going to push the spirit out of the client\u2019s lady friend and trap it inside a magic circle. When it manifested to break the circle, we lock him in place with a Wave Form Collapse. I took over that duty and posited that it might be better if I kept my presence unknown from the client and his friend.<br /> <br /> Staring down on a room with a ritual circle from on top of a hanging light fixture is a view I\u2019ve seen numerous times. I watched Kilroy, Speed, and Cly position the pieces of our puzzle. Cly\u2019s Demon form is impressive to say the least. I wouldn\u2019t want to tangle with her one-on-one (in her Naomi cover, the feelings get a little confusing, however). She pulled Stefan\u2019s girlfriend into the circle and held her fast while Kilroy started the mystical whammy. She also shifted Speed\u2019s drunken stupor onto Stefan, knocking him out cold. When Kilroy pushed the spirit out by possessing Stefan\u2019s lady, it immediately attempted to manifest and escaped. That was my cue.<br /> <br /> I did my best Rufio impression, and dropped from the ceiling, aiming a heel kick for where the collarbone would be on a human. It\u2019s footwork was impeccable, as it dodged at the last instance to avoid my Wave Form Collapse. But I\u2019ve got centuries of combat experience and muscle control that puts Olympic athletes to shame. I twisted in mid-air and caught the spirt with the other heel, locking his form for the next 8 hours, more than enough time for Kilroy to bind it. Cly wrapped it up tight and started a slow drain of its power. All and all, everything went off exactly as planned. I tumbled out of the circle (again, got to show Speed and Cly that I\u2019m worthy as an ally and an employee so I was showing off a bit) and landed beside Speed who offered me a flask. That shit burned like holy fire!<br /> <br /> After we got the damn thing bound into its ghost dick fetish (don\u2019t ask!) Kilroy memory wiped the client and the victim. In warfare, information was key, but the agency seems to have some guidelines on how that\u2019s obtained as they were adverse to me rifling Stefan\u2019s pockets. They seemed okay with me checking his cellphone though.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d been keeping it very low key, just blending in with the other co-eds on campus mostly. After wrestling that spirit, a bit of the warrior\u2019s high coursed through me. The feeling of elation that comes from weathering a storm with strong comrades, it reminded me of Gene. \u201cLet\u2019s go out!\u201d I proposed. After a quick memory wipe for Stefan and his lady, we were on our way.<br /> <br /> We went to a place called Kiki\u2019s. The best I could tell, they kept it dark and loud for a reason. I bought the first round, but called everyone\u2019s drinks. I was feeling good and not concerned about blowing the meager cash I had. I showed back up with drinks then scanned the crowd as we chatted.<br /> <br /> There was a guy sitting at a table surrounded by future trophy wives who was staring at the door. That struck us all as odd, so we did what any good detective can\u2019t help but do, follow the clues. I flashed the six pack at one of guys companions and walked away with a disappointed expression from her quick rejection\u2026and his cellphone. The table had already figured his name was Erwin Holt, he wanted to acquire Carla Pierce, and he was afraid of two people named Sanderson and Herb. But I clued them into the fact that Holt and Pierce were about to have a meet and Pierce was somewhat of an unwilling participant.<br /> <br /> Carla walked in and like hungry dogs we bit into this mystery. She apparently is nervous around Speed. Kilroy, Cly, and Speed were able to make out most of what was going and relay it to me. I spent my time crafting a little mobile phone app that would secretly transfer all SMS conversations from an infected phone to my phone. I showed it to Kilroy, just to have a second level of troubleshooting. I installed it on Holt\u2019s phone. I have a feeling this is going to come in handy later so I made a specific effort to remember the code verbatim.<br /> <br /> It appears Holt worked for someone named Erasmus, who went around calling himself a god. Speed was playing fast and loose with their minds (I love Speed\u2019s style, btw) and gleaned that it was basically some kind of power struggle between Sanderson/Herb and Erasmus/Holt over Pierce, with Ms. Sanderson as the wild card who wants to maintain her position by possibly offing Pierce. I see an opportunity there, but I\u2019m going to keep it under my hat for now.<br /> <br /> Kilroy is riding his Vivian persona by this point, so when I suggest that we monkey wrench this otherwise boring meeting that they were having it he\u2019s already a step ahead of me. Kilroy creates a distraction, while I slip over and tap the security alarm in her pocket. This brings her security team into the club and causes Pierce to pull a gun. I like Pierce a lot, to be frank. Speed made the wise choice to check the bar when the armed goons kicked in the door, and then made his way back over after Pierce chased Holt out of the bar. A few minutes later, Holt sent a message to Erasmus indicating that Sanderson\u2019s guys broke up the meeting.<br /> <br /> After the excitement, I got introduced to another fallen solider, a guy buy the name Louis. He gave us the skinny on a couple of Fanger\u2019s Speed ran into, and then dropped some info about a location at a nearby dam that was apparently being used by an Angel who was dirty, but hadn\u2019t fallen yet. This peeked my interest, of course. There seems to be a general consensus about punching this guy\u2019s ticket. That seems to line up with my plan to salvage him and find out what makes that particular ability tick. Afterwards, Cly decided to hook up with a \u201cmountain of cocaine and her secretary\u201d . It was later downgraded to a hill of cocaine. Kilroy , Speed, and I hit another bar. Then I had Speed drop me off back at my room. All and all a good first day on the job. I think I\u2019m going to like it here.<br /> <br /> <br /> To Do List:<br /> <br /> Work on SMS eavesdropping app (Code name: Pikachu)<br /> <br /> Track down Carla Pierce\u2019s information including home address and full work history<br /> <br /> See if Speed needs help with those Fanger\u2019s and if he\u2019d be okay with me lifting anything useful off of them afterwards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIII</i><br /> <br /> The Demon binding set up was strictly a set of rolls determined in game. Fulgur\u2019s player being back meant his being part of the fun, which definitely added something. There was the comment when it was completed from him that \u201cBustin\u2019 makes me feel good!\u201d which was repeated a time or two.<br /> <br /> The entire thing with Carla in the bar was some spying and the Saboteurs having their way. I sort of hate Quietus could not be there.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Fulgur, the bad news is his player may miss this upcoming session. The good news is next week I will be putting up his background and adding him to the front page. He is official, and enthusiastic to be here. He also has an odd work schedule and a very long drive, so he may miss a bit more than Speed, Kilroy or Clytemnestra but hopefully less than Quietus. Still, he should be around, and hopefully a good bit. But see you next week, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-11-2015, 12:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T15:55:21-07:00","id":460455,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm quite glad for Kilroy! Funny, didn't think that Twilight/not Twilighr counted for Wave Form. I'm leaning towards Mummy for Erasmus, myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T03:04:35-07:00","id":460879,"title":"","content":"Not a bad guess. re: Erasmus.<br /> <br /> The Twilight thing was a call on the spot. Fulgur's player asked and it seemed dramatically appropriate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T00:00:10-07:00","id":463172,"title":"","content":"Mummy is also my out of character guess for Erasmus based on what little we know so far. In character, Kilroy is not prepared to hazard a guess without more data.<br /> <br /> And thank you, Ganora's pregnancy was as much a surprise to me as it was to my character but given how Kilroy has not really embraced this whole 'emotion' thing as enthusiastically as some demons it's been fun to work out his reactions to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T13:29:50-07:00","id":468718,"title":"","content":"As promised, the Background for Jared Evans \u201cFulgur\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Fulgur, \u201cJared Evans\u201d Destroyer Saboteur</b><br /> <br /> Entry #1: A Declaration of War<br /> It\u2019s been about a month since they killed Gene. The Swords of Heaven. Angels of the Almighty God. They cut down an innocent man, just to reach me. I\u2019d done the same countless times before. It was different watching it unfold from this side Seeing Gene\u2019s eyes go blank, as the sword pierced his chest, the smell of copper the feel of warm blood on my cheek; even if I didn\u2019t have a perfect memory, I would never forget that moment. <br /> <br /> We\u2019d been working a strange case, which is typical for a couple of twenty-something unlicensed investigators. I met Gene right after my fall. My cover, Jared Evans, was a precocious ten year old who just happened to be the nephew of Melinda and John Evans, two circuit court judges who were about to make some groundbreaking rulings regarding same-sex marriage. The God-Machine\u2019s plan couldn\u2019t allow that, and I was assembled to dispatch Jared\u2019s relatives. I finished the job, was leaving the scene, when I saw Gene Evans approaching. He was my cover\u2019s cousin. We were roughly the same age; it\u2019s hard for me to judge humans. I hid and watched as he ran into the house screaming for his parents attention only to find them cooling on the floor. Ruining this child\u2019s life, to strip others of their rights? This is what my God called \u201clove\u201d? <br /> <br /> I fell and dropped off Heaven\u2019s grid as best I could. I convinced my cover\u2019s parents to adopt Gene, and tried my best to make sure that he had the happiest possible childhood. It was Gene who got us started in the \u201cUnlicensed PI\u201d gig. He loved those old \u201cEncyclopedia Brown\u201d stories, basically devoured anything that was about police procedures or any type of mystery fiction. He was all about the idea of someone using logic and reason to help others. We were about twelve, when he and I set-up my mom\u2019s card table in the front yard with a poster advertising that the Evans\u2019 Boys Detective Agency was open for business. We started finding lost dollies, trading cards, where parents were hiding holiday presents, etc. Gene was great about following the clues and seeing the whole picture.<br /> <br /> When Gene was about seventeen, the cases changed from wholesome to Law and Order: SVU. We were now following up on abusive husbands, cheating wives, drug addicted kids, real film noir style cases. Gene and I turned in the card table for the back of his 1974 Chevy Nova. We kept half of what we earned and tucked the rest away for a rainy day. I knew that Gene really wanted to go to college to study forensics and I figured that was a good enough reason for us both to save-up. <br /> <br /> Last year, the weird cases started to trickle through the doors. We were working out of a bar near our apartment in Upstate New York. I\u2019d been pretty successful at keeping us out of the majorly spooky stuff. The first one slipped my notice till we got jumped by Fangers outside a bar in Brooklyn. They weren\u2019t special, just a couple of baby vamps doing muscle work for cash. I had to punch their tickets in front of Gene though; and just like that, he was off to the races. We hit every library and rare book collection in the Tri-State area as Gene researched. I tried to steer him away from the scarier aspects of Creation (Like me for instance) but he could tell. He\u2019d been suspicious about his \u201cCousin Jared\u201d before that but I always managed to deflect his inquires.<br /> <br /> That last case didn\u2019t smell right from the jump. I kept my mouth shut and Gene got the case particulars from the client and then explained our fee. She needed protection from her abusive ex, a young butch by the name of Ferra. They\u2019d recently split up after years of our client being Ferra\u2019s physical and emotional punching bag. It seemed that Ferra was the jealous type and, for someone who hit the liquor bottle more often than the gym, was freakishly strong. We agreed to keep a close watch on the client. She requested that one of us stay overnight in the house. <br /> <br /> About a week into it, we got our first face-to-face with Ferra. She showed up drunk to our client\u2019s house and demanded Gene let her in or let out \u201cthat whore of an ex-bitch\u201d as she put it. Gene naturally refused, threatened to call the police, and made sure Ferra saw the Glock 17 he kept by his side whenever we were on a case. Ferra backed off and left. He called me to inform me what happened. The rest of the night was calm. <br /> <br /> A couple of days later, Ferra approached Gene directly. She offered us twice the money to lure our client into an obvious trap, left half the cash up front, and left a time and address to meet for the rest. We took the money and told the client. We came to the conclusion that the best move was to get her as far away from Ferra as possible, so we used Ferra\u2019s money to arrange for a new ID for our client and then set her up in a nice new home in Canada. Then we called Ferra to set-up the meet.<br /> <br /> I walked into that double-cross extremely confidant. I made sure Gene wore his Kevlar. I would meet with Ferra to finish the hand-off alone. Like I said, I was cocksure and secure in the belief that we\u2019d gotten our client away from Ferra. This was basically going to be an easy payday and if I was very lucky, Ferra would give me an excuse to payback some of the violence she\u2019d unleashed on our client. Put a good scare in her and let her know how much worse it would be if she ever contacted our client again. Like I said, I was feeling pretty untouchable. That all went to shit when the Angels showed up.<br /> <br /> It turns out Ferra wasn\u2019t just some asshole. She knew just the right machine\u2019s ear to whisper to in order to get two Destroyers sent to collect me. I remembered them. We\u2019d worked jobs together before my fall. I tried to reason with them. Tried to explain what was going on. Why I stopped following orders. They didn\u2019t care. They attacked me. I had to defend myself.<br /> <br /> I take no joy in hurting humans, but I\u2019m a being created to wage war and I do it well. I danced with my former brothers on the tip of a spear, knowing the first one to slip would perish. Being a mortal being, an existence that had a definitive beginning and end, gives you an edge against the agents of the God-Machine. I adapted to their rote attacks, and finished them quickly. Just in time to see Gene burst into the meeting place with his pistol at the ready. He relaxed as he saw me standing in a pile of sparking metallic parts. I could see relief wash across his face as he moved closer and holstered his weapon. That\u2019s when Ferra struck, sticking a mechanical sword arm through Gene on her way to attacking me. I watched the life leave my friends eyes as he slumped to the floor. I\u2019d not seen Ferra before, but I recognized her in that instant. I screamed in rage and lashed out at her. She effortlessly disappeared, leaving me with a dead best friend and my grief. <br /> <br /> I closed Gene\u2019s eyes. Then I went back to our apartment and packed as quickly as possible. I grabbed the petty cashbox from the safe and headed for the train depot. I stowed away on a freight train heading west. When it stopped I was in Seattle, a couple thousand miles away.<br /> <br /> After the first week, I realized that there was no manhunt out for me. The death of my friend was never reported from what I could tell. He was just another dead orphan. I\u2019d arrived just before the final deadline to enroll in classes at the college; it seemed like a good excuse to be an early twenty something that just moved across country. I\u2019m planning to specialize in forensic cryptography. I think Gene would like that.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also made a vow. To take back heaven from the God-Machine\u2019s twisted purposes. These humans deserve a better class of divine ruler. One who has fought and bleed beside them; who looks upon them not with \u201cmercy\u201d, but with sympathy. It is therefore necessary for me to gather allies. I would also prefer to not destroy my brothers, as they are being sacrificed like cattle for nefarious ends. <br /> <br /> Let this serve as the formal declaration, I will not know peace till Gene is avenged by laying waste to all the schemes of the \u201cgod\u201d who ordered it.<br /> --<br /> <br /> Updated the main page, adding an entry for Fulgur and and adding Clytemnestra's new cover, student and artist Naomi Cruz.<br /> <br /> Journals next week as usual, got Speed\u2019s and Clytemnestra\u2019s already. See you then, Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T02:10:49-07:00","id":476806,"title":"","content":"Demon session! Fulgur\u2019s player had to miss but we had Quietus. Let\u2019s see what hijinx they got into.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> I rolled up to the office at a fucking bright and goddamn early 10 am the next day. Shit, it\u2019s not like keeping up with the kid taxed my liver any. Billy Mack and Cecilia were the only ones there and neither of them was crazy enough to try any banter before I had a cup of coffee or three. By the time I\u2019d had, Cannon had shown up and I was spared.<br /> <br /> Cannon was his usual goddamn earnest self. \u201cLike I said before, I go through lots of receptionists. They don\u2019t respect Drake - don\u2019t realize black people are Americans too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou may have mentioned it, once or twice.\u201d I cracked half a smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s no call for it either. He\u2019s a good boy, a real American, just like his father.\u201d I held off on damning the chemtrails. I figured he had a point to get to somefuckingwhere. \u201cThis last one, Ada Watts - weird name. She couldn\u2019t have been out of her 30s, and I hadn\u2019t known anyone under 50 with the name Ada. Anyway, she was quiet, kinda pinched, if you know what I mean. But respectful! And she hasn\u2019t been into work these past three days. Since, you know, the break-in? With the government men?\u201d He looked around for hidden cameras or some shit.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked serious. \u201cShe could very well be in danger, with that timing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s what I thought! Or - or - maybe a Mata Hari type thing and the Feds came back for her and she\u2019s in witness protection. I mean, I can\u2019t even find her file or her resume...\u201d He pronounced it like that, without the accent over the fucking e. \u201cThe weird thing is though, you said, the government men were searching Drake\u2019s office?\u201d he looked to us for confirmation, getting a nod from each of us before continuing. \u201cWell, she could get in there any time. Why would she send others? Unless they were just checking there first and then were going to break into my vault...\u201d<br /> <br /> ..\u201dI suppose that is possible, but...\u201d the g-man offered, now that he had a moment to get a goddamn word in edgewise.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway, I thought it might be a lead. I don\u2019t have her resume,\u201d I barely kept from laughing. \u201cBut I do have her address, from payroll. It\u2019s not the same as with Drake - he\u2019s a family friend, I worked with his father - so I haven\u2019t been over there to see if she\u2019s there or anything.\u201d Cannon held out a piece of paper with an address on it.<br /> <br /> I nudged Billy Mack and signed, below the desk where Cannon couldn\u2019t see, the signs for \u2018M\u2019 and \u2018R\u2019. I put on my shades while the g-man began to give Cannon the rundown on what we had, edited for content of course. I popped my Mind Reading sensors in time to grab a glimpse of Ada in his surface thoughts. Pinched was putting it fucking lightly. She was such a goddamn caricature of the motherfucking idea of prim that I\u2019d have laid even odds on whether she\u2019d glare at me before shushing me in a library, or taking down her hair and off her glasses and fucking me in one. She wasn\u2019t anyone we\u2019d run across by accident though.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack started off mentioning that the Michael White had given us a few leads on the job Drake had been working on. Fucking surprisingly, Cannon spoke up at the name. \u201cI\u2019ve met Michael White - enough oil there to run a car on.\u201d No pause, no consideration, no goddamn clue we\u2019d asked him about the fucker before.<br /> <br /> The g-man probed a bit. \u201cBridge builder?\u201d He made the fucking hammer motion too.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah... yeah, that sounds right.\u201d Cannon shrugged.<br /> <br /> The image he had of White was crisp, as crisp and clean as a newly minted stack of c-notes. The figment focused on the smarmy fucking bastard, without a single goddamn bit of context, just vague fucking positive vibes.<br /> <br /> The boys had continued their conversation while I had that mind frame paused. Cannon interrupted Billy Mack when he mentioned the fucking fighting ring. \u201cThat sounds familiar... who was it... Crusher! There was a bail jumper, went by the name of Crusher. He was involved in some kind of underground fighting ring, until he killed his landlord. Had a lady friend that Drake talked to. He wound up finding him by going wherever she tried to steer him clear of. Found him in Olympia, I think.\u201d<br /> <br /> Crusher was a big man, built on Herb\u2019s scale. I could see how he\u2019d make champion in that boxing ring. Billy Mack had a different angle. \u201cDo you know the woman\u2019s name? The lady friend.\u201d He clarified after Cannon\u2019s initial look of confusion.<br /> <br /> Cannon screwed up his face, thinking. \u201cNope, not coming to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWas it possibly Rosanna?\u201d the g-man prodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI couldn\u2019t rightly say. I could look in Drake\u2019s files - keeps them very organized, he\u2019s a good boy, chip off the old block. Or you could drop by and look over Ms. Watts\u2019 desk while you\u2019re at it. I looked it over a little, but you\u2019re the detectives, after all!\u201d The bondsman shrugged again.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think we\u2019ll take you up on that offer, Mr. Cannon.\u201d Billy Mack shook his hand, and he showed himself out.<br /> <br /> I filled the g-man in. He looked thoughtful. \u201cThose hunters did say they had been led into a trap. Perhaps it was this Ada they were referring to?\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back in my chair and blinked a few times to clear those sensors out. \u201cMaybe. Could have been our fucking bridge builder. According to Louis, that is the kinda shit he does.\u201d Our conversation was interrupted by yelling in Portuguese coming from the lobby. \u201cIs this going to happen every time Naomi shows up for work?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow and turned to the computer. After a few moments he said \u201cThe address checks out on the surface. It is within a reasonable price range and area. We have an appointment this afternoon, but there should be plenty of time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now it was my turn to raise an eyebrow. \u201cWe do?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMore precisely, Vivian does. I do need to get some cheap vodka for Dmitri. He remembers the good old days in the USSR, when the Communists made everyone miserable and American pop music was worth its weight in gold.\u201d He kept typing at his computer.<br /> <br /> I stared at him, then took a fucking drink when my stare didn\u2019t make him spontaneously start making goddamn sense. \u201cShould we go rescue Naomi?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose we ought.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> The car ride to Cannon\u2019s didn\u2019t give me nearly enough goddamn time to properly fucking appreciate Naomi\u2019s ensemble, the thing that inspired Cecilia\u2019s tirade this time, as usual: black pants with enough fabric to fit the both of us, and a black leather jacket over a tight black shirt that said \u2018I fingerbanged your honor student\u2019 in goddamn sparkly pink letters. It didn\u2019t help that she kept turning to adjust Jack\u2019s collar or lay a hand on his arm. We\u2019d picked him up on the way out, just getting back from cleaning up another fucking divorce case. I did get a chance to ask her the question I\u2019d posed to Billy Mack earlier. \u201cSo, are we always going to get a Portuguese shriek to signal your arrival?\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed happily. \u201cI do love exploring the range of her emotions. Excessive rage or orgasm, her face does the most exceptional things.\u201d<br /> <br /> We\u2019d delayed enough that Cannon had the files on Crusher waiting for us. His real name was Benjamin Creel. The story went down pretty much like he\u2019d said, with a few fucking details added. The lady friend was one Anna Watson - not quite Rosanna, but close enough to be an easy to fucking remember pseudonym. He wound up in the big house, but just outside of town. He was set up to be there for a long goddamn bit, like Herb had said. Lastly, the ring location Drake had down was not the address we\u2019d found it at, which would explain why there weren\u2019t immediate red fucking flags thrown up.<br /> <br /> Ada\u2019s desk was even more exciting. The unlocked drawers held the usual - make up, a charger for a fucking stun gun, an unlabelled bottle of booze that turned out to be a decent bourbon. I pocketed that last.<br /> <br /> There was also one locked drawer. I took a stab at it. \u201cGodfuckingdammit. Jack?\u201d I indicated the lock and broken pick with a nod of my head.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack coughed. \u201cMr. Cannon, you would not happen to have a key to this desk drawer, would you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHrm?\u201d He glanced over. \u201cOh sure. Won\u2019t be anything in there though, she didn\u2019t have one.\u201d He picked through a large rings of keys to find one of the right size.<br /> <br /> To my fucking surprise, it actually worked. To my great goddamn lack of surprise, he was wrong otherwise. Inside the drawer was a brown long haired wing curled up in a bun, plaster to change the shape of someone\u2019s nose, green contact lenses and a pair of fucking glasses just like the ones in Cannon\u2019s memories.<br /> <br /> Cannon looked aghast. \u201cShe was in disguise?!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA very good disguise too.\u201d The g-man looked over the pieces carefully.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cIt\u2019s not CIA level shit, but it\u2019s sure as hell better than fucking Halloween store supplies.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow long was she working for you?\u201d Naomi asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cOne, no, two years. Somewhere between those.\u201d He stammered out. So, since Drake had met White, but before the shit got out about White\u2019s operation. \u201cIt\u2019s hard to find good secretaries, nobody brings their daughters up right anymore, they don\u2019t respect Drake, just because he\u2019s black... So, before I hire the next girl, should I pull her hair?\u201d He was still staring at the wig.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can not say I recommend that strategy.\u201d Billy Mack said seriously. I had my head in my fucking hands and was trying not to laugh.<br /> <br /> Cannon opened his mouth like he was about to say something but then closed it. He began again. \u201cI gotta check something...\u201d He went back into his office and we heard a goddamn gun cock. He noticed me staring as he walked back in. \u201cWhat? She might have taken the bullets out, and I wouldn\u2019t know til I needed it.\u201d He sighed. \u201cI bet she is in witness protection, now that the government's withdrawn their mole.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps. But we\u2019ll check out that address anyway.\u201d The g-man clapped him on the shoulder.<br /> <br /> <br /> We got to the apartment building in short time. We passed by the wall of mailboxes on the walk in, and Jack took the opportunity to commit a little fucking postal fraud. He opened up box 1B, our mark\u2019s. A pile of Presorted Standards addressed \u2018To Resident\u2019 is all he got for his trouble, three or four days worth, so there was that. Most of the mailboxes were plain, decorated with the goddamn unit number and that alone. One exception, 2F, had me nudge Jack. \u201cYou're a good, god-fearing boy right? Go to fucking church and everything?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fuck are you talking about woman?\u201d He gave me a look.<br /> <br /> I indicated the be-crossed 2F box. \u201cA good god fearing boy might have the best luck checking in on certain neighbors.\u201d The fucker rolled his eyes at me.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t the time to canvas though, not until we\u2019d had some fucking dirt on her digs. I was prepped and ready to pop my eyes if anyone answered, prim, proper or not. That didn\u2019t turn out to be necessary - an empty room full of goddamn gas doesn\u2019t have much of an aura or mind to read. Not that I was fucking willing to open the door to prove that theory. Clytemnestra, in the form of many small spiders, nixed that idea when she let on that the door was rigged to set off a spark, the floor was covered in silverware just waiting to be fucking shrapnel and the windows had buckets of gasoline, in case someone tried to be cute.<br /> <br /> If we smelt gas from outside, there was enough to level that entire fucking branch of the goddamn building. Jack and the g-man started evacuating people while I got on the horn with Mack. He answered me with a resigned \u201cWhat\u2019s up Gabe?\u201d I wonder what he thought I\u2019d gotten up to this time. I didn\u2019t get a chance to ask, since \u2018apartment full of gas rigged to blow\u2019 started up the fucking emergency sirens.<br /> <br /> It turns out we each got to make friends. I played fucking ride along with Mack, listening in on the building manager waxing goddamn rhapsodic to the police about how the hijab and Arabic name was sure to mean this was a terrorist attack. Once Mack and I headed out to get a look at the inside of the place, Billy Mack and Naomi stayed behind to speak with the secretary.<br /> <br /> Ada Watts, obviously, was not who the hell they had records of staying there currently, unless the Normans were a lot more fucking Arabic than I remembered from reform school. She had lived there for two months or so, right when she got hired. I didn\u2019t bother going back to see what the secretary thought Ada looked like. She hadn\u2019t been working there at the time and the bird who was went fucking cuckoo; saw the light, walked out and joined a goddamn cult. Apartment management had never spoken with this newest female resident, hijab and all, just her husband. Even that was just over the phone.<br /> <br /> Jack did go speak with the Indian woman living in 2F, to my amusement. She had a few more fucking details to add, even if she hadn\u2019t seen the questionably existent husband either. She had spoken with the woman though, which is more than most of the other goddamn residents claimed to. She\u2019d gone \u2018to minister\u2019 and been rebuffed since her husband wasn\u2019t home. She did figure her for Pakistani, and said she had deep brown eyes, which was further past the fucking head covering anyone else had seen either.<br /> <br /> I got a brief eyes-on the apartment, which mostly just fucking confirmed that Watts, or whatever her name was, was a pretty goddamn good bomb maker. The bulls weren\u2019t too keen on letting anyone spend too much time breathing in the fucking gas, so that was the extent of my investigations in there.<br /> <br /> We each shared what we got on the ride back to the office. Naomi spoke up in the silence that followed. \u201cI was thinking... Maybe we should call White, feel him out.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cHe does seem like our best lead. Our only fucking one outside of Crusher, and that\u2019s a goddamn long shot. But we\u2019d need a cover for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I was kinda hoping you\u2019d come up with one of those for me.\u201d She smiled sweetly at me.<br /> <br /> I smirked back. \u201cWell, we could be calling to \u2018let him off the goddamn hook\u2019 - with Ada\u2019s disappearance, evidence points towards more of a Cannon connection that one to him. Or we could be checking to see if he knew anything about giant moth fuckers. If we really wanted to risk being fucking outed as some kinda supernatural shit, we could start with \u201cWhy\u2019d you send us/him to a fucking Hedge Gate you fucktard?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack snickered, but it was Naomi who answered. \u201cI was thinking a more... deceptive route. Like saying we saw Louis at the fighting ring, or Puriel or something dam related.\u201d She paused. \u201cThe former could be interesting if Valefar is White. Which he very well might be.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI sure as hell don\u2019t want to sell out a fellow Fallen to his own Angelic alter ego without knowing that it is for certain somefuckinghow. I\u2019d rather drop Puriel or something dam related, or maybe make up something about Rosanna...\u201d Now it was my turn to pause. \u201cNah, scratch that. If I\u2019m picking sides, I\u2019d take Jake and anyone keeping people the fuck away from Hedge Gates over White any goddamn day.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf we sided with White though, think he\u2019d stop trying to kill us?\u201d Naomi sighed. I raised an eyebrow. \u201cI mean, we were totally the target there, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. Or Cannon.\u201d I brushed my hair back from my eyes. \u201cShit. We\u2019re going to need to tell him this other woman was probably Ada.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know it\u2019ll make his day.\u201d Jack kept smirking. \u201cWhat\u2019s your thought on Crusher anyway? You think he had something to do with Drake disappearing?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cNah. But if Billy Mack\u2019s hunch is right, and Anna Watson\u2019s a pseudonym for Rosanna, he\u2019s probably whatever she is. I can tell that with a quick once over. If he is, he might be able to lead us to Rosanna and from her we might be able to get Jake.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMore reasonable that I expected.\u201d Naomi said archly. \u201cSo, you wanna go by yourself, or want someone along to make sure he doesn\u2019t hate us?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck you.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Billy Mack arranged for the big house visit before swapping over to Vivian and heading out to her appointment. Naomi had just disappeared, seeing as legs don\u2019t just sketch themselves, when Jack stopped by my desk. \u201cSo, I had a thought.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cQuick, catch it! Zoos have special places for endangered species.\u201d I took a swig from the purloined bourbon.<br /> <br /> \u201cI... fuck you.\u201d He shook his head. \u201cLook, you were wanting a burner cover, something you could take on risky plays, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back in my chair. \u201cIt\u2019d be nice. Less whips and jingles, for certain. I had some plans - I was thinking homeless. Overfuckinglooked, explainably erratic, without too many trappings to be missed if I have to fuck off and go loud.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow about we make it a paranoid homeless vet with a drug addiction?\u201d He looked at me expectantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ve put more thought in it than me, but I guess that sorta shit is kinda your job. Yeah, that would make a plausible cover for most of the skills I\u2019d wanna use when shit went down. I guess you have a couple few patsies in mind?\u201d I took another sip and cocked my head, returning his look.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure do. The first\u2019s not available at the moment. The way I see it, once we\u2019ve wrapped up this case, Cannon\u2019d be well served if we could clear his head a bit. I figured we could take his memories of his vet friend who died from Agent Orange. It\u2019d make him much less inclined to be our client though, so, after.\u201d I allowed it. \u201cFor the second, I got a buddy who came back from the Middle East hurt pretty bad. I don\u2019t know whether he got on the horse before or after he lost his house, but between the two, he\u2019s having some serious fucking problems putting shit back together.\u201d He sat down and leaned forward onto his desk.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I get homeless and a heroin addiction, and he gets enough cash to fix things, and no more cravings.\u201d I walked a coin along the backs of my fingers before flipping it up and catching it. \u201cSounds like a fucking deal to me, fixer.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Jack directed me to a part of town not too far from White\u2019s trio of traps. He looked up and down the street nodding when he saw a 7-11. \u201cYou got a fin?\u201d I nodded and went to fish it out. \u201cNah, keep it, just have it ready when I ask.\u201d<br /> <br /> We ducked down an alley and Jack knocked on the wall. \u201cHuh? I\u2019m not doing nothing, just resting. I\u2019ll move along...\u201d The voice was slurred and an arm moving out to wipe across his face was the first I saw of the person slumped against the wall.<br /> <br /> Jack crouched down. \u201cNo need Jim, it\u2019s just me. I brought a friend.\u201d He gestured towards me. I smiled as Jim squinted up at me. \u201cShe\u2019s really good at seeing which way things are going to fall out and she thinks it\u2019s your lucky day.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe gonna put in a good word with Dolly Parton?\u201d His voice was rough and thready, with a note of humor. He had definitely seen better days and he moved slowly as he sat up, favoring one side.<br /> <br /> Jack chuckled. \u201cNot that lucky man. But... if you sign this contract, and take this fiver.\u201d He held out his hand to me and I put the fin in it. \u201cAnd use it to buy lottery tickets at that 7-11 on the corner, you\u2019ll get out of this hole.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight... and what do you get out of it?\u201d He shrunk back a little anxiously. \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure my kidneys are kaput and well, I gave the rest of my body to science, but I don\u2019t think even they wanted it.\u201d He gave a short chuckle that turned into a cough.<br /> <br /> Jack patted him on the shoulder. \u201cThe hole. You\u2019ll be free and clear. The horse, the streets. You\u2019ll be rid of it all, and we need a bit of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey say I\u2019m crazy.\u201d Paranoia warred with the idea Jack offered. \u201cHell. I\u2019ve had centers offer less for more. Why not?\u201d<br /> <br /> He took the five dollar bill from Jack, signed his contract and took the hand offered him to stand. \u201cJack. Ma\u2019am.\u201d He walked slowly to the corner, his gait getting steadier and limp getting less with every step.<br /> <br /> <br /> The four of us gathered again after Vivian\u2019s appointment. She was all but fucking petting her new goddamn laptop. \u201cCheap vodka for that? I don\u2019t get it.\u201d Jack teased Vivian.<br /> <br /> \u201cCheap vodka can get you lots of places darling.\u201d Liz patted Jack's cheek.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd cheap vodka combined with a thumb drive full of banking info for a filthy rich antique collector can get even more.\u201d Vivian smiled widely.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou two manage to pick up the snake food for our fucking peace offering?\u201d I asked Liz and Vivian. The hacker snickered and Liz smiled slightly. \u201cSomething I should know?\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian held up a brown paper bag. \u201cNo problem, and no charge. I had a bit of cleverage.\u201d She winked at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI.. right.\u201d I shook the fucking keys. \u201cLet\u2019s get going before I have to start drinking to fucking forget I heard that word.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> The sun was just setting behind the Mothman Theatre as we got there. The shadows were just long enough that not much light leaked in the doors as we opened them. In the interest of good relations, we went in dark. Jack called out softly once the doors closed behind us. \u201cGood evening gentlemen.\u201d<br /> <br /> From out of the darkness, we heard a soft whirring. It communicated ideas in pure goddamn generalities, but well enough. \u201cIntentions?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack raised the brown paper bag. \u201cWe brought dinner. We need to take a look around, and that means using lights. If you don\u2019t mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> The whirring came again. \u201cGive. Light down here only.\u201d They flew up to the rigging.<br /> <br /> We took the opportunity to flick on our flashlights. A thorough fucking search turned up a collection of old junky proper, broken down seating, and goddamn motherfucking bear traps. The bear traps were hidden under piles of old clothing, one behind a big heavy door below stage, the other under a goddamn trap door from the stage itself to that same room. I tripped them both once Jack had used Synthesis on the place and found an old battery operated radio that had been playing music softly until its batteries ran out a few days ago, but no evidence that Drake had been here and just avoided the fucking bear traps.<br /> <br /> It was pretty easy to see White\u2019s angle anyway. The mothmen are not so dangerous on their own, given how goddamn skittish the fuckers are. But a single bleeding out human, held in place? That they could fucking take care of.<br /> <br /> We kept looking, hoping to find an abandoned piece of Infrastructure that had attracted the moth muggs here. We found something, but it was fucking dismantled, not abandoned. A goddamn shame too. It was also set to collect emotions, a wide array, from the patrons specifically. This bit of Junk distilled them down to Essence, and I don\u2019t think that\u2019s what my goddamn Despair was headed for, but it would have been fucking nice to get an idea of what the Bastard-Machine could do with this shit.<br /> <br /> Me and Vivian broke down what was left anyway. It wasn\u2019t plugged in enough to suborn, but once we\u2019d gotten a real start with our goddamn bit of suborned Infrastructure, Vivian figured we could use the spare parts. Jack and Liz parleyed with the cryptids upstairs. Seems we\u2019ve got a couple of guard moths and a creepy fucking psychopath lair now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <u>Music for a Darkened Theater</u><br /> <br /> <b><u>Scrambled with a side of Chemtrails and a glass of Agent Orange</u></b><br /> <br /> The morning began simply enough. Naomi dropped me off at the office on her way to classes. I started the coffee distillation and spent a couple of hours maintaining Billy Mac and Vivian's online correspondences while waiting for my fellow unchained to arrive or for anything requiring a higher authority than Cecilia at the front desk.<br /> <br /> Speed was the first to arrive, looking a bit less dour than usual. I believe she found last night relaxing. Harvey Cannon was next, though fortunately not until after she'd had the opportunity to assimilate her first couple of cups of caffeine.<br /> <br /> Our client had dropped in to check on the status of the case, and while he is certainly eccentric one cannot deny his devotion. He also had a new item to add. His secretary, one Ada Watts, had not come in or answered her phone in the past few days. Her disappearance was timed exactly with the hunters breaking into Drake Paulson's office. As a rule, I never trust in coincidence. It was almost certain that she had either been extracted, detained, or eliminated.<br /> <br /> As I updated him on our progress and gathered what information he could provide on the missing woman, Speed used her powers to delve into his mind. Since the night of the break in, someone had implanted a false memory of Micheal White to replace the block that Cannon had previous struggled against. That raises the possibly that the missing woman is a telepath. It seems unlikely she is or was an angel but may well be a stigmatic agent of the god machine or White directly.<br /> <br /> In our conversation, Cannon did give us a connection between Paulson and the underground fighting club. It seems that Paulson was the one who tracked down and recaptured their champion, one Benjamin Creel better known to us as Crusher. There was a female acquaintance involved, who attempted to steer Paulson away from the wayward brute. Cannon did not recognize Rosanna but did later give the woman in question's name as Anna Watson. And when Paulson was dealing with them, the ring was using a different location so he would have no reason to suspect what he was walking into. So really, Clytemnestra's early theory of it being a clan fighting ring or some such was far closer to the situation than we suspected. It seems very likely that Creel is a changeling like Rosanna, which gives her and her people much more reason to dislike Paulson for his role in putting the large fellow away for life.<br /> <br /> Given the potential connections, I did end up making a call to pull a few strings with Billy Mac's friends and arraigned an interview with Creel for us tomorrow. Speed can see from his aura if he is a changeling and if so it is within our power to negotiate the possibility of freeing him. Speed is firmly disinclined given the violence of his crimes but if it proves to be the only avenue to finding Rosanna and through her Jake and whatever information he has about White we shall have to at least consider it.<br /> <br /> In the course of gathering this information we moved from our offices to Cannon's and picked up Clytemnestra and Quietus. It seems Clytemnestra has decided she rather enjoys using Naomi to provoke Cecilia to extremes of emotion far removed from those that she coaxes from the woman as Elizabeth Covington.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Disguises and Deathtraps</u></b><br /> <br /> Our initial investigation of the secretarial desk at Cannon's office revealed nothing out of the ordinary. After getting the key to the desk's lone locked drawer from Cannon, however, we made a fairly relevant discovery. The drawer contained more makeup, a wig, facial putty, and the stage glasses that combined to form Ada Watts. Interesting that she was apparently able to don this guise at the office rather than wear it in and leave with it. Proof that she was not the woman Canon thought and an accomplice rather than a victim. The time frame is noteworthy. She worked for Cannon for around eighteen months, starting before well before Paulson had any reason to suspect White was anything other than a strange man with a desire to help young women in bad situations. Overall, White's schemes are either deeper than I understand or the man is not entirely rational. Whichever the case may be, I dislike being unable to predict his moves and being forced to deal with him in a reactive rather than proactive manner.<br /> <br /> While the personnel file and hiring information on Ada Watts had vanished along with her, Cannon did have a phone number and address in his payroll. The address was an apartment in an area and building that was comfortably middle class, nothing outside the means of her salary working for Cannon. It was the obvious lead to follow up on and so we did.<br /> <br /> A quiet examination of her mailbox revealed nothing identifying and a few days worth of generic mass mailings. We made our way to the apartment and knocked. There was no answer. I believe all of us had begun to scout the walkway for witnesses in preparation of entering uninvited when both Speed and myself noticed the scent of natural gas in the air. Clytemnestra shifted into her swarm state and crawled underneath the door to find the apartment had been rigged quite effectively into a bomb sufficient to destroy the entire wing of the apartment complex.<br /> <br /> Speed contacted Gabe's police contact while Quietus organized a remarkably calm evacuation of the building's other residents. The emergency responders were understandably unwilling to allow us anything more than cursory access to the apartment which did not give us anything more than Clytemnestra's arachnid swarm had been able to gather. Hopefully Speed's contacts will allow her at least some access to what the police forensic investigators are able to discover once the scene is safe enough to enter. While limited to the strictly mundane, it may prove helpful none the less.<br /> <br /> As the public servants went about their task of defusing the apartment, we took the opportunity to question the management and other residents. Ada Watts had only lived in the apartment for two months, right around the time of her initial employment with Cannon. She had moved out and been replaced by a couple that current popular American media would likely term as 'of terrorist decent', which is to say that with the notable exception of the one Indian neighbor all anyone could recall was the wife's very traditional (and conveniently concealing) Muslim garb. The Indian woman had little to add as the woman was very reserved and avoided interacting with anyone but she did place our suspect as being Pakistani. Of the husband, no one seems to have ever actually seen him, though he did handle all of the affairs with the property office over the phone. None of the current employees where present when the couple moved in, the property itself has changed ownership (most likely unrelated though it might be a manipulation to make the trail harder to follow) and while the woman that used to manage the desk was retained, she apparently had a very abrupt and unexpected conversion to some sort of cult and walked out one day. I am far less inclined to write that occurrence off as coincidence. Pity we are unlikely to be able to track her down, one does not generally remove a witness in such a bold manner without good cause.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>A Deal with Dmitri </u></b><br /> <br /> Once we had gotten what information we could from the apartment complex, we withdrew and took stock of our avenues of further investigation. One point that was not lost on any of us was that this trap had quite likely been set for us rather than simply directing us toward one of the ones previously set for Paulson. We did elect to contact Cannon and warn him about the situation as he was the only other potential target. We debated how best to respond to this move and the consensus was to keep our own cards close and not risk revealing anything that White might not already know. In particular, if he has not ascertained that we are Unchained yet it is best to keep that advantage as long as possible. For the moment, I believe gathering more information is our best option. Also, we still have no solid leads on where Paulson is or what happened to him. We decided to proceed by interviewing Creel and returning to the abandoned theater the mothmen were lairing in for a more through investigation.<br /> <br /> Once the interview with Creel was set up, I excused myself to change into Vivian and meet with Dmitri. On my way, I stopped to acquire a bottle of insultingly low quality vodka. Such is the nature of the relationship they have.<br /> <br /> The Greek diner was an older building, the sort of place that is always changing owners and names and yet always remains basically the same low end greasy spoon. The location suited Dmitri well as he is likewise a bit run down. Though, to be fair, even if he is no longer the chiseled criminal soldier he once was, he remains a physically impressive man, especially when compared to Vivian.<br /> <br /> Dmitri was the only customer in the place, having left the young Slavic tough that had accompanied him smoking on the bench out front. The bodyguard was quite tactless in his appraisal and while he clearly saw Vivian as no threat he was intent on frisking me for weapons. As Vivian is not one for such casual groping, I snarled at Dmitri to call off his dog and he laughingly assured the man that \u201cthe kotenok is no threat, and if anyone is going to grope her it will be me.\u201d The man shrugged and returned his attention to his cigarette and keeping watch for any interruptions.<br /> <br /> Dmitri refused to get straight to business, instead insisting that I join him at his table as it was clear from looking at me that I was in dire need of something more sustaining than the diet of ramen and Mountain Dew that, as a hacker, was all Vivian consumed. He had, of course, already taken the liberty of ordering for us both. I made the expected show of annoyance and presented him with my gift, which he made a point of opening to drink with his meal and savoring with a gusto far removed from the quality of that vile swill. To date, Vivian has never found a vodka bad enough to bring so much as a grimace to Dmitri's expression. I shall have to try harder next time, though I wonder if there exists such a beverage. It would be rather interesting to see Dmitri and Speed drink together at some point.<br /> <br /> The food was somewhat more appetizing than the environs would lead one to expect though not enough to make a trip for specifically. Once I had eaten, I pulled out the thumb drive with Dantaine's account numbers and set it on the table. Dmitri slugged his vodka back and smirked. \u201cI must ask. Why would such an infamous hacker trade such a thing rather than make use of it herself? I know my pretty little kotenok would never lie to her good friend Dmitri about what she's selling him...\u201d<br /> <br /> I lifted an eyebrow. It was a valid question and we both knew it. I flashed him a sweet smile. \u201cThe accounts belong to a very dangerous man, much too dangerous for such a sweet little kitten as myself to risk stealing from.\u201d<br /> <br /> He considered me and pursed his lips. I most likely should not have let him know that I understood what his endearment for me meant but he'd used it often enough that it was not unreasonable that Vivian would have looked it up. \u201cYou are many things little Vivian, but cautious is rarely one of them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen you understand what a truly dangerous man we are dealing with.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded after a moment and lifted a nice leather carrying bag to set on the table. \u201cI have what you asked for kotenok.\u201d I let a suitably hungry look filter into my eyes and expression but did not reach across the table for it. \u201cPoor thing,\u201d he chuckled, \u201cJust how long has it been since you had a proper fix?\u201d<br /> <br /> I crossed my arms and glared at him. \u201cMonths,\u201d I admitted, \u201cThe FBI are sore losers, they refused to release any of the equipment they confiscated as evidence.\u201d<br /> <br /> He grinned broadly and pushed it across to me. \u201cClearly whatever inferior tech you have been reduced to has not stopped you, but I assure you, this is worthy of the great Marley's Ghost.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took it from him and smiled. Oh it was indeed worthy. I felt a surge of pleasure just running my fingers over the hardened case. I powered it up and used it to confirm the data for him with a smile.<br /> <br /> Oh but how Vivian has missed having the proper tools to work her digital magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Mothman Theatrics</b></u><br /> <br /> While not overly intelligent, mothmen can manage at least limited speech and reasoning. So rather than drive off the pair that have taken refuge in the old theater we decided to attempt to parley with them. To facilitate the talks, Clytemnestra and I opted to stop by a pet store and pick up some feeder mice to offer as a means of opening a dialog.<br /> <br /> When we arrived, Clytemnestra nodded to me and asked me to go get the mice. When I inquired if she was staying behind do to some dislike of rodents, she smiled and said she just wanted to get me to do it for her. While I would normally have simply shrugged and gone about the transaction, I found myself moved to what I can only describe as mischief. I was still feeling quite pleased at having finally replaced my rig but more than that, I find that while in my cover as Vivian I am simply more inclined toward such behavior. At any rate, I was struck by the notion that if I was going to do an errand for Clytemnestra, I was going to do it with flair. And once I saw the young boy working the counter, the manner of how to show off for her seemed obvious. I may have laid it on rather think, speaking to him about just how much I loved my snake in decidedly suggestive terms. By the time he had finished collecting the feeder mice into a bag for me, he was quite flushed. Once we had returned to the counter and I had taunted him with Vivian's physical charms, he gifted the mice to me. I am not sure I have ever so thoroughly flustered someone as Vivian before. It was... amusing. I am tempted to return when I have some free time. I imagine that Vivian might well be able to coax the hapless lad into signing away whatever pieces of his soul might prove useful.<br /> <br /> However, there was no time for such diversions. We arrived at the theater and met with Quietus and Speed. It seems Quietus had spent the afternoon helping her to acquire some elements toward building a second cover to use in potentially compromising situations or simply when distancing herself from the agency would be helpful. Vivian serves that function for me, though I wonder if perhaps I should see about another cover that I am less attached to for high threat situations.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra and Quietus convinced the mothmen to allow us to search the building and we discovered the trap that White had set here. He had laid out some items to make it appear the storage area underneath the stage was inhabited and had even as we later discovered left a small radio playing softly. The entrance was set with a bear trap so that if Paulson had entered recklessly he would have been immobilized and injured. While the mothmen would not attack a healthy human, they would have been drawn to the blood and quite likely finished off the wounded bounty hunter. A decidedly horrific death and proof that Michael White is both very dangerous and quite sadistic.<br /> <br /> Once we'd uncovered and disarmed the traps, Speed and myself continued to search the theater as it seemed likely that there was something to have attracted the mothmen. Quietus and Clytemnestra returned to them and bargained with them, forging a contract with them to increase their intellect and ability to frighten away people in exchange for them watching and guarding the building so that we could use it as a secure hiding place in emergencies.<br /> <br /> For our part, Speed and I found some disused and mostly dismantled Infrastructure. It had gathered and distilled Essence from the emotions of the crowd watching the performances. The core elements had been recovered, but some useful components that could be used to enhance a working element should we find one remained. We set to work on them and dismantled them to bring back to the office with us for later use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Yea I was on TV. I was the one with the pink hair. Oh it was a long story.<br /> <br /> Okay, so the day started with my math class. I wore this shirt all special for my bitch math teacher. She did not think it was funny. Maybe because she won\u2019t shut up about her goddamn honor student daughter. I mean, I have not banged her, she is like a junior in high school, but you know, if she stays in the area for college I will. You know, to piss her off.<br /> <br /> She got in a twist about my homework too. \u201cNaomi if you don\u2019t show your work how do I know you did not use a calculator?\u201d \u201cIf you don\u2019t want us to use a calculator you should not assign so much homework! I got shit to do.\u201d No sense of humor at all. Would it kill her husband to plow her now and then so she would not freeze the seat she sits on?<br /> <br /> So I get to work and Cec\u00edlia is waiting like a trapdoor spider to jump on me about my pants and shirt. \u201cOh what if Lady Covington were here?\u201d \u201cThen she would totally do me.\u201d I am pretty sure Lady Covington would think it is hilarious.<br /> <br /> Oh, I\u2019ll meet her on my terms.<br /> <br /> But then, THEN, we get away, but not to the apartment complex but to that Cannon guy\u2019s office. His secretary Ada Watts vanished, and Gabe and Billy Mac had picked Jack up and thought she might be involved. Gabe searched the desk but just found some make up and stuff, and a locked drawer. Billy Mac got the key to it from Mr. Cannon, and inside we find a wig, some facial prosthetics, color contacts, and glasses. Ada Watts apparently did not exist. But we had an address that checked out while we went there.<br /> <br /> Yea Cannon is the Agent Orange and Chemtrails guy. We are looking for his Bounty Hunter Drake Paulson. Right. With the boxing ring and the Michael White guy. Yea.<br /> <br /> So we go to the complex and knock on the door. After Jack messes with the mailbox illegally, Gabe and Billy Mac start flipping out because they smell gas. Jack sort of peers in the window in a sideways sort of way and notices there is a tank of gas near there, and what looks like some sort of jury rig at the door. So of course, I got the fuck out of dodge.<br /> <br /> Jack, being the hero in the group, went and started getting the others there to safety while Gab called the cops. Eventually we had a whole bunch show up. I kept a damn low profile before some cop got odd ideas about the \u201cMexican\u201d girl.<br /> <br /> Turns out the whole thing was rigged all to hell. Silverware was left out near the door, and enough fuel was near to be sure whoever opened the door was cooked. Cops went in the window\u2026carefully.<br /> <br /> Turns out \u201cAda\u201d moved out after two months and a \u201cMuslim\u201d couple who no one ever saw the guy of. Her get up was enough to mostly conceal her, and we were pretty sure it was out master of disguise again. There was a fairly Jesus oriented Indian girl there who said she was Pakistani. Billy Mac astutely pointed out we had trails going in all the wrong directions. Fuck, we had enough red herrings to start a fish fry.<br /> <br /> Billy Mac wanted to call some contacts to follow up a boxing ring tip Gabe got, and Jack and Speed had a side thing, so I came here. Needed to see a pretty face.<br /> <br /> Okay, yea. Legs too. And you got em, babe!<br /> <br /> -o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-o-<br /> <br /> Hey Deanna. This whole thing is fucked. I just heard from Gabe. She, Vivian, Jack and Lady Covington went to look into that theatre. The place was full of rats and vermin, apparently, and this White guy set bear traps under the stage. After dropping evidence the girl Drake was looking for was there. Fortunately, we beat him there. Viv and Gabe were quick enough to notice the traps so we did not set them off\u2026but fuck man. They were pretty sure the vermin would have finished Drake off if he were trapped too.<br /> <br /> I really, really don\u2019t like this guy. Oh don\u2019t worry babe, I will watch my back. Don\u2019t forget who the tough girl is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIV</i><br /> <br /> As a reminder, we just updated the thread last Saturday with Fulgur\u2019s background, so if you have not been here in two weeks check it out. Also pics for Fulgur in all forms and Clytemnestra\u2019s latest Cove on the first page.<br /> <br /> The Cover hunting was played out at the table.<br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add, except as usual Speed is pretty faithful in recording actual in game dialogue. Also Cannon is too much damn fun to play.<br /> <br /> See you next time, comments and questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-13-2015, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:51:43-07:00","id":479359,"title":"","content":"Reading Clytemnestra's Yarns as Naomi is super weird, she is so different from Liz. Kudos to the player for having such different covers and reflecting that in the journal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:57:37-07:00","id":479365,"title":"","content":"Excellent. It is not not reflected in the journals, but Billy Mac has a very different feel and behavior from Vivian as well. Both sets of covers have some interesting behavior differences. Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T14:46:02-07:00","id":479512,"title":"","content":"I kinda got used to the Billy Mac/ Vivian difference from Speeds journals as well Kilroy's. And I am used to how different Naomi is from Liz in others' journals as well. But to read Naomi's perspective instead of Liz's just stood out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T01:54:37-07:00","id":480014,"title":"","content":"It is a well done shift of writing voice. I had initially thought of something similar with Kilroy's but I didn't like leaving out the amount of detail that Kilroy would when dealing with his covers' acquaintances. Also, I've found I like writing them in Kilroy's more internal voice. In game Billy Mac is closer to it than Vivian but not quite the same.<br /> <br /> As a random note, when I am working on Kilroy's journals I can't help but hear him as the voice of Egon from The Real Ghostbusters animated series.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T02:06:24-07:00","id"