yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T18:03:07-07:00","id":486891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=486881#post486881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a quick question which may have been answered but I don't want to spoil the rest of the plot before reading ahead : at the train station, you have things in boxes, presumably Cryptids but what are the guys the characters describe as &amp;quot;reptoids&amp;quot;? Are they from a book I haven't read yet?</div> </div> </div> </div> They're one of the sample kinds of Cryptids from the D:tD core,a sort of &quot;take that&quot; to the &quot;lizard-men rule the world's governments!&quot; Conspiracy theories. They are uplifted small reptiles with the ability to shapeshift, but are cowardly and tend to lose control of their abilities when afraid. They're used by both Unchained and the Machine for low level spywork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T20:49:04-07:00","id":486990,"title":"","content":"Ah Darn, I'll have to reread it, I totally missed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-21T00:40:09-07:00","id":487083,"title":"","content":"ZealousChristian24 is on the money with the Reptoids. I find them terribly amusing myself. Jimmy Marsh is a recurring character I like a lot (and use Patton Oswalt for due to the &quot;Foil&quot; video)<br /> <br /> The things in the box, never stated outright, were Pandorans, being delivered for study. The woke up due to Herb.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T14:09:24-07:00","id":491937,"title":"","content":"Okay it is time to check up on our favoeite Demons. If they are not your favorite Demons I will let it go\u2026this time.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> The night was still fucking young, so we decided to take a peek at the goddamn laundromat, in case things had cooled down any. Jack wasn\u2019t with us that first visit, so we filled him in on the way.<br /> <br /> He and Liz were the two fuckers with night vision, so they went in for a closer look. I leaned against the car and took stock of the surroundings as best I could. There were a few street lights still on, scattered around the goddamn place, just none on the actual strip the laundromat belonged in. There was the usual amount of cars for an afterhours strip mall, just enough to be hiding a whole fucking squad of Angels, especially if you got those damn pin-standing ones.<br /> <br /> A shout from the laundromat grabbed my attention. It was Jack. \u201cWhat? I can\u2019t even walk down the damn street now?\u201d He was glaring at the inside of the Infrastructure, but kept on walking to circle back around to us at the car. \u201cThere\u2019s a night watchman, but that\u2019s it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz ghosted up behind him, laying a hand on his arm. \u201cIt also appears to be in considerably better repair than last time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian peered over at the door. \u201cI could jump him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck, so could Jack.\u201d I gave her a look. \u201cHe probably has an alarm or some shit. We need to fly a little more under the radar than that.\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes at me. \u201cLet me rephrase. I could jump into him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Why the fuck not?\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> She got close enough to see the watchman, but didn\u2019t disappear. After a few moments, she raised her voice like someone trying to fucking talk through glass. \u201cWhat are your hours?\u201d I couldn\u2019t hear a response, but I could fucking guess. She made a show of reading the door slowly.<br /> <br /> She was just back to the car when I noticed 3 new cars driving up. She was about to say something when 5 lugs piled out. \u201cIn the car.\u201d I said, not moving my mouth and moving casually to do so my own goddamn self.<br /> <br /> I kept an eye on them as I pulled out, keeping with the fucking casual motif. One of them got out a phone and pointed it where I would normally have pulled out from behind one of the parked cars. I gave up on casual, and ducked and fucking swerved out of that lot like my goddamn life fucking depended on it. Jack started his phone strobing and held it out to fuck with any footage they might have gotten. Between us, I think we got off clean. I started driving aimlessly, turning frequently and keeping an eye out for tails.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo... the watchman wasn\u2019t human.\u201d Vivian offered once we were a few minutes out.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. So it\u2019s still too goddamn hot for a look-see.\u201d A non-descript white sedan stuck with us for a couple of turns. I made three in quick fucking succession and it continued straight. There was a small scratch just above the right headlight. I\u2019d know it again if they caught up with us. \u201cSo, what the fuck is plan B?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could go looking for vampires...\u201d The hacker shrugged.<br /> <br /> I grimaced as I glanced in the rearview \u201cWhy? He might quote Dickinson at me again.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz grinned mock sympathetically. \u201cThe culture just doesn\u2019t wash out, does it?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sneered as Vivian chuckled and responded, \u201cNo, the mustard gas breathing ones. I was thinking, if we really wanted them out of the way, we could lure them through the Hedge Gate.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat... that is fucking brilliant.\u201d I smiled at her quickly before checking the goddamn passenger mirror on her side.<br /> <br /> \u201cI mean, it depends on the objective here. If it\u2019s just to make you feel better, there are better ways to do that...\u201d Vivian raised an eyebrow and gave me a wicked smile back.<br /> <br /> I smirked at her and my smirk deepened as Liz looked back and forth between us quickly. \u201cJust not in the car, right? Right?!\u201d I looked at her, eyes wide and innocent. She narrowed her eyes at me. \u201cSo, for the case. Our options are to shake White down, talk to Creel or explore the Hedge, correct?\u201d<br /> <br /> Now it was my turn to look fucking concerned. \u201cWhen the fuck did going back into the Hedge get on the list?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t say it was a good idea, but you were talking about having sex while driving so I didn\u2019t think good ideas were required.\u201d She gave me a half smile, one eyebrow raised.<br /> <br /> \u201cPutting that aside, I think that shaking White down should wait til we know more about Creel.\u201d Vivian tapped her laptop. \u201cWe need more information.\u201d I nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI agree as well. I mostly bring it up as I had another thought as to how we might lead him astray.\u201d Liz paused fucking dramatically. \u201cWe tell him we found Drake, and we\u2019ll be having an extensive interview the next day. Then all we have to do is decide how to deal with the inevitable people he\u2019ll send.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI like it. And unless he\u2019s got an agent in the Hedge, or he actually kidnapped Drake himself and just sent us on a wild goose chase, it won\u2019t be obvious or obviously supernatural.\u201d Jack said. Another white car. A different dent.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd as far as that third thing...\u201d Vivian began. I groaned. \u201cIf we can get in touch with Rosanna, maybe she\u2019ll help us look - and I promise not to eat any eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> With nothing more productive to do, we went bar hopping, hitting Johnny\u2019s and a couple of other places. After I dropped the others off, I kept on drinking until sleep showed the fuck up.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack had his nose deep in the goddamn internet when I got to the office. I ignored him in favor of a cup of science coffee but once that was done, I glanced over his shoulder and did a fucking double take.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho the fuck is the Absorbing Man?\u201d I topped off my second cup with a little from my flask.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe superhero identity of Crusher Creel.\u201d Billy Mack said matter of fucking factly as he scrolled through the page.<br /> <br /> I scanned the page myself. \u201cWhat kind of fucking nerd builds a fake identity based on the goddamn Absorbing Man?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack switched to a tab with Crusher\u2019s rap sheet and mug shot. \u201cThat kind?\u201d He shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cLiz\u2019ll like him.\u201d I looked at Jack, who was flipping through his fucking phone. He held it up. \u201cSays he once got turned into cocaine that gave you superpowers when you snorted it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stared at him. \u201cI did not need to spend memory storage capacity on that.\u201d He shrugged. I shook my head. \u201cFucking nerds.\u201d<br /> <br /> The door opened abruptly and Liz shut it behind her quickly. She shifted states to Naomi pretty goddamn quickly. \u201cWell that was weird.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat used to getting yelled at by Cecilia already?\u201d I smirked at her.<br /> <br /> She looked at me almost confusedly for a second. \u201cNo. Stuff at school. Some teacher killed herself, and Deanna - that girl I was violating at the concert? - and Adria were drunk in my apartment when I got these last night.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack crossed his arms. \u201cIf that\u2019s weird, I guess neither of them is a roommate?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNope. Neither of them have a key. They were still kinda out of it when I had to leave for class. Deanna did wake up enough to propose to me again.\u201d She smiled to herself. \u201cThen I had to come here. I can text them and ask them what happened.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack was back at the computer. \u201cThat\u2019s an odd coincidence.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat is?\u201d Naomi kept poking at her fucking phone too.<br /> <br /> \u201cZelia Fisher, the first year chemistry teacher who killed herself - she didn\u2019t have keys for the building she was found in either. There are not many other details however, or any red flags in her digital footprint.\u201d He turned back around.<br /> <br /> Naomi\u2019s phone chirped. \u201cDeanna says she was tipsy, went by the apartment, the street light went out and then I woke her up.\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned to Billy Mack. \u201cThink you could see how local that power outage was?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think...\u201d He left it at that for a moment as he stared off into fucking space. He brought up a few more web pages. \u201cAha. A number of social media accounts from campus are saying there was a power flicker at some point - clocks flashing, computers restarted. None of them noticed it go out though.\u201d Naomi was about to say something when the g-man got a goddamn concerned look on his face. \u201cWait. None of those accounts posted anything between midnight and 1 AM. Nothing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s sure as shit not right. What time did the teacher die?\u201d I finished my fucking coffee.<br /> <br /> He looked back at me. \u201cMidnight.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed, then brightened. \u201cHey! In this world of Big Brother surveillance buzzword buzzword chemtrails the fuck ever... social media logs locations, right? Can you get a map of locations before and after the blackout, maybe let us trace some kinda of fucking pattern or at least a goddamn epicenter?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi snorted. \u201cI\u2019ve got a good guess of an epicenter.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, yeah. But it\u2019s always good to get more than one fucking angle.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Since we planned on walking Crusher out of big house on the pretext he was some deep under fucking cover FBI agent, we stopped by the Big and Tall on the way to the goddamn hoosegow. Jack had hammered out the contract that would do the heavy lifting. In exchange for him \u2018giving\u2019 us his conviction, we\u2019d hook him up with a bulletproof alternate ID, a bolt hole with all the goddamn fixings, and more fucking cash that I\u2019d seen in a hell of a long time. Considering that non-metaphysically, that was four ticks in the \u2018Him\u2019 column of the score sheet, he\u2019d owe us, at least a little.<br /> <br /> After a shortened round of paperwork, thanks to the g-man, and a minimal groping to check for goddamn birthday cakes, we got in to see Crusher. I\u2019d popper my sensors before he got there, and gave Jack the signal as soon as he did. Fucker was the same sort of critter as Rosanna. Not shy either. \u201cWith no disrespect intended, who are you and what do you want?\u201d He spoke slowly, with a deliberate seriousness. His voice was strong and deep and definitely matched the big bull of a man.<br /> <br /> Jack took the lead, playing the fixer role. \u201cThat depends on you and our conversation. Have a seat.\u201d Crusher say, casting a fucking weather eye around him. \u201cI hear you\u2019re in for a long stay.\u201c The big man smirked. \u201cI understand the Lost don\u2019t care for the concept of incarceration.\u201d<br /> <br /> That caught his attention, but didn\u2019t kill the smirk. \u201cNope.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wanna help you out with that, but I need a few things myself.\u201d Jack followed Crusher\u2019s glances around the goddamn room. We both noticed how often they fell on the door and occasionally the ceiling. And how he seemed to be calculating just how much fucking closer to the outside he was now.<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t show any signs of bolting yet. \u201cFair enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe need to have a conversation with Rosanna and Jake.\u201d Jack watched him carefully.<br /> <br /> The big man\u2019s attention snapped the fuck into focus, even more than when Jack mentioned the Lost. \u201cWhat are your intentions towards her?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack held up his hands. \u201cTo have a conversation, that\u2019s all. I\u2019m not offering nothing either - we can get rid of your conviction, make it like it never even happened.\u201d<br /> <br /> The suspicious look didn\u2019t leave his face. \u201cLast time I followed someone out of a bad situation, it got worse. If you know the Lost, you know there\u2019s people who want to take us back - I gotta make sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t have any intentions of doing anyone wrong.\u201d Jack gave him a fucking understanding look.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe got a deal then? I tell you how to talk with Rosanna and you agree not to hurt her or me? That seem fair?\u201d Crusher was staring goddamn intently at Jack, focused on him completely.<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cYeah. Yeah it does.\u201d He glanced at us significantly. \u201cI have a very similar proposal for you.\u201d He laid out the deal we\u2019d discussed.<br /> <br /> The fish balked at the \u2018vacation\u2019. \u201cI gotta be here. I\u2019m Pledged to protect Rosanna.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLocation\u2019s not an issue. I can be anywhere, and the safe house can protect more than one.\u201d Jack brought out the goddamn paperwork.<br /> <br /> Crusher scowled at it. \u201cWho do you answer to anyway?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack\u2019s emphatic \u201cNo one\u201d seemed to satisfy the big man there, but he didn\u2019t move to take the fucking pen or stop scowling.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, I can read, but not real well. I want someone educated to look that over before I sign it.\u201d He went to cross his arms, switching to resting them on the table when the handcuffs got in the way.<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cThat\u2019s fair. Do you have a lawyer or someone you trust with this kinda thing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRosanna won\u2019t do me wrong. If she OKs it, I\u2019ll sign.\u201d He got a stubborn look on his face. \u201cSides, I got something I wanna do before I leave.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked at Jack and back to Crusher. \u201cIf you acquire any more charges before you are released, the contract we have here cannot nullify them.\u201d<br /> <br /> The big man shrugged. \u201cThey won\u2019t be killed in any way a single human could manage. But if not maiming anyone is part of the contract, I can abide.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smiled. \u201cNah, it just can\u2019t nullify anything if you get caught.\u201d<br /> <br /> Crusher nodded, and considered for a moment. \u201cYou know, I don\u2019t intend any of this to insult your honor. I just know you from no one. I have been utterly betrayed once and it changed me to the very core of my being. I will be dead before I allow it to happen again. I just want someone more educated looking it over.\u201d His fucking speech over, Crusher leaned back in his chair, as best he could while cuffed.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing man. No insult taken.\u201d Jack gathered up the paperwork and stashed it away.<br /> <br /> Negotiations over, Crusher gave us a number for Rosanna, and the name of a club she frequents. Billy Mack decided to feel him out on the other details of the case. \u201cHave you ever encountered a man named Michael White?\u201d<br /> <br /> He thought for a second. \u201cI think so? The name rings a bell.\u201d<br /> <br /> That was enough like Cannon\u2019s first response that I went fucking digging. I found a memory of Crusher speaking with a younger Asian gee who claimed to represent White. He\u2019d been trying to get Crusher to throw a goddamn match and got a knockout punch for his trouble. I went fishing instead. \u201cHe might have been involved with fight rigging?\u201d I figured it was easier to jog his memory than go looking for more, if it even fucking existed.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah, that guy. That\u2019s how I heard of him. Knocked his guy out cold.\u201d He rubbed his chin. \u201cThat bounty hunter picked me up not long after. I wonder if they were related.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomewhat, though not in your particular situation. Drake has worked for White in the past, but is currently at cross purposes, after learning some of White\u2019s less than palatable inclinations.\u201d Billy Mack explained.<br /> <br /> \u201cHuh. Good taste. I regretted not killing that bounty hunter til now. But he reminded me of someone.\u201d He had a goddamn far off look in his eyes. It wasn\u2019t hard to guess that Drake reminded him of a younger self. \u201cIf he\u2019s at least got the good enough taste to not associate with fight-throwers, I guess I won\u2019t track him down or anything. I\u2019m very good at finding people.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back in my chair. \u201cIn that case, we might have a favor to ask, once you\u2019re out.\u201d I glanced at the others. \u201cFull fucking disclosure - it\u2019s really Drake we\u2019re after, in the end. He\u2019s disappeared, possibly tricked by the fucker White into the goddamn Hedge.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cMaybe. Once I\u2019m out.\u201d<br /> <br /> We took our leave, promising to be back with Rosanna\u2019s seal of approval as soon as we fucking could. A snap caught my attention as we reached the door. I looked back at Crusher, who had a pair of shiny bracelets, each with a short length of chain. \u201cOops. Your handcuffs broke.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> So, Kayla, drawing on your knowledge of occult stuff, tell me what passes through your mind as I describe this scenario.<br /> <br /> Midnight. Seattle University. A female first year instructor, Chemistry, hangs herself in one of the hospitality rooms at midnight. The door is locked, she has no key and is not known to possess one. The 12-1 AM hour sees a power outage, and absolute silence on campus. This goes unremarked on by any student, aside from some notes after one on social media that there was a power flicker earlier. Two girls, intoxicated, drop by Naomi\u2019s apartment on the edge of campus. They remember the streetlights going out and were woken by Naomi on the inside, but don\u2019t recall going in\u2026indeed, the door was locked and they, too, lack keys. They don\u2019t know times; it was \u201cafter 11\u201d but the power surge was after midnight for certain. Kilroy is doing some digging, to see if he can find an epicenter. I am guessing the room of the hanging.<br /> <br /> It may be some Infrastructure. We should investigate the room at the very least.<br /> <br /> Anything else?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know of any surge of Angelic activity. We swung by the Laundromat a little while earlier, like nine-something, and Kilroy got the attention of a Guardian (I assume) Angel inside, but he just summoned back up. Like human backup. I assume anyway, not positive we did not test them. But regardless, it was not a high-pressure situation and was, as far as I know, the only Angelic activity that night. But I don\u2019t know what Valefar or The Fools were up to.<br /> <br /> Honestly much of our activity today was stuff with the school. Looking things up and such. We did deal with the Changeling thug though, Crusher.<br /> <br /> We met him at the prison. I think his initial plan was to use the visit for an escape. If I had to sum him up, the words would be \u201chuge\u201d and \u201csuspicious.\u201d He quickly arranged for Quietus to be pulled into a Pledge, but it was nothing Quietus took issue with, since we are not planning to attack Crusher or Rosanna in the next month.<br /> <br /> Crusher sort of knew Michael White. White wanted him to throw a fight. He had not connected White and Drake Paulson till we brought him up. He seemed less hostile to Drake than we expected, apparently feeling some affinity for him. He regarded Rosanna as a good friend, he may be a bodyguard for her. He was less connected to Jake, which seemed to disappoint Speed.<br /> <br /> Oh yea, his alias is apparently a comic book character. Boys.<br /> <br /> He and Quietus were vaguely macho at each other a bit, but the takeaway is he gave us enough info to contact Rosanna. He did not sign a contract for a Pact wanting someone \u201csmarter\u201d to look it over for him. He nominated Rosanna. So the next step is talk to her about Drake and White, and Jake, and get her to get us in touch with Jake. Have her okay it and we spring Crusher and Quietus gets a piece for a new Cover, and, well, we proceed based on what Jake says.<br /> <br /> Unless you have any more ideas about the University\u2026?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XV</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add in terms of mechanics. There was some discussion and rules checking on gadgets, as we looked at having Quietus make a gadget for the car to let it drive into the Underworld to evade pursuers in car chases. Of course, we have to have at least one car chase in the Underworld before it is done.<br /> <br /> For those who enjoy my Actual Plays, I have started a Crossover one set between 1920 and 1949 called <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-world-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play\">The Golden Eagle</a>. It should be taking place across Europe and the Levant, as a group of Supernaturals drawn togather by a strange artifact and mysterious patron work to survive in the post Great War era as Fascism and other dark forces rise . No Demons among the PCs but they will be appearing in game, as will Angels, and the God-Machine has a role to play in the background story. I expect most games will have their critters show eventually. There will be some pulp and noir elements worked in, so if you enjoy that sort of thing check it out. And don\u2019t forget to check out my Geist game (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\">Balance of Shadows)</a> and Changeling (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\">Malibu Dream House</a>) as well.<br /> <br /> Well, see you next time. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T15:00:24-07:00","id":509258,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check in on our team from Demon. This session they start a new case and make a grievous error.<br /> <i><br /> Session XVI</i><br /> <b><br /> Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> We got a late lunch/early dinner on the way back. Once we were out of the goddamn hoosegow, I went over our options. \u201cSo we\u2019ve got the broad to talk to, and whatever fucked up shit is going on at the school. or we could always pay a visit to the fucking Works, and put those parts from the goddamn Mothman Theatre to some good fucking use.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe should talk with Rosanna today,\u201d Jack pointed out, \u201cso we can spring Crusher tomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cSure. You wanna make that call? If she remembers talking with me, and is the \u2018Anna\u2019 from Drake\u2019s notes, it might be a shitton more adverserial than I figured. She has a hell of a poker face.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged and dialed the number Crusher gave us. When he responded, it was in Spanish. \u201cHello ma\u2019am, my name is Jack Stone. I met with Creel today and have some paperwork he wanted you to look over for him...\u201d He nodded. \u201cYou will... A proposal - all on the up and up. He claimed a lack of education, but he seems quite wise to me...\u201d He smiled in agreement with whatever the hell her response was, glancing at me. \u201cYou have every right to be concerned over safety. Why don\u2019t you pick a place and a time so you can make it as safe as possible... Got it.\u201d He wrote down an address labeled The Last Drop. \u201c9 o\u2019clock?...I do travel with some associates, will that be a problem? They can stay in the car...\u201d I gave him a look. \u201cGood deal. See you at 9.\u201d<br /> <br /> My objections to our staying in the fucking car were forestalled by Billy Mack musing \u201cI wonder if she has tips for my dinner date?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe hell?\u201d Jack looked confused.<br /> <br /> \u201cVivian\u2019s dinner date, really, with the Gentry on the other side of that gate.\u201d The g-man looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> Jack kept staring at him. \u201cMaybe not a topic for our first discussion.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, no, of course not. If anything, I might mention that I have a... friend that has had some problems since falling through that gate.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Over dinner Billy Mack compiled the data his program had retrieved. The blackout covered a roughly circular area, with about a mile radius and centered exactly where the hell we expected, the Asbury Room where Zelia had hanged herself. It didn\u2019t cover all of campus, or only campus, thanks to the fact that the Asbury Room isn\u2019t in the fucking center of campus. Plus, the campus wasn\u2019t a goddamn perfect circle. It did cover a large portion of it though. The g-man also did some digging on the professor herself - she was from Idaho, had gone to school in San Francisco and was newly arrived to the area. Enough meat to back it up and no particular red flags.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe should get some fucking eyes on the scene, look into the site ourselves.\u201d I said, once he relayed all that shit to us.<br /> <br /> \u201cI imagine I should change then - Vivian would look less out of place.\u201d Billy Mack looked at his hands and fucking g-suit.<br /> <br /> Jack chuckled. \u201cYou are a little wrinkly for a college student.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou could be an adjunct though.\u201d Naomi gave him a hell of an appraising look.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot a bad fucking plan either. You talk with faculty and grad students, Naomi asks around the undergrads, and Jack and I take a look at the goddamn room itself.\u201d I stood and stretched, tossing down a few bucks tip and winking at the cute waitress a table over. \u201cLet\u2019s get the hell to it.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Jack and I found the door to the building left propped open just a hair, and slipped in. I could see why Naomi called it \u2018the alumni building or something\u2019 - it was full of rooms with old fucking money names as well as numbers. The building as a whole surrounded a courtyard with a fountain on three sides, the fourth side being a blank wall. Despite that, the building we found ourselves in was goddamn \u2018L\u2019 shaped, not the U we fucking expected, at least that was accessible from the outside without going through the courtyard.<br /> <br /> There was in fact a door to that last leg of the building in the courtyard, labeled \u2018Asbury Room\u2019. A quick fucking glance as we ghosted up caught a pair of twists, students by the look of them, talking goddamn excitedly beneath the chandelier Zelia had hanged herself from.<br /> <br /> I signaled Jack to wait and activated my sensors. Whatever had gone down the night before, it wasn\u2019t fucking Angels, or at least they didn\u2019t use any goddamn Numen. I checked that first. Neither of the students were supernatural. Neither of them were supposed to be there either. I started my mind reading on the shorter one first. She had long dark hair under some kind of black fucking bowler, accented by a goddamn flower. She had an excess of eye makeup and a rapt look on her face. That\u2019s all I got though, as my mind reading bounced right the fuck off her. The taller one, with short dark hair and a slightly nervous look, was an easier touch. She was focusing on how much trouble they\u2019d be in, how cool it was to be there, and how fucking intriguing the idea of asphyxiation was.<br /> <br /> I passed all that shit on to Jack, who proceeded to merrily kick the goddamn door down. \u201cWhat are you doing here?\u201d he roared. \u201cActive crime scenes are illegal to trespass on.\u201d<br /> <br /> The one with the hat answered. \u201cI work in here sometimes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDoing what?\u201d He glared at her.<br /> <br /> \u201c...stuff.\u201d The taller girl hid her head in her hands and tried to duck behind eye-makeup girl.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow long do you want to stay in school?\u201d He moved further into the room.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cOh, you know, a couple of years.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe week?\u201d Jack growled.<br /> <br /> Her eyes widened and the nervous one eeped. \u201cYes sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFind your dorm.\u201d He indicated the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> The inside of the room was creepy as fuck. Goddamn gilded couches, wooden accents that were probably fucking mahogany or some shit, and a fucking plethora of hunting trophies. A boar, a wolf and even a goddamn moose gave their heads up to decorate the walls of that place and every fucking one of them were looking at us, not to mention the dead white men paintings.<br /> <br /> I started looking around while Jack used Synthesis to find no signs of a concealed struggle in the time line. We didn\u2019t get very far before the inner door opened. 6 foot 6 of pure crotchetiness topped by a full goddamn head of white hair stepped out. \u201cWhat are you doing here?\u201d he creaked ponderously.<br /> <br /> Jack took the lead while I held up the fucking wall and tried to get eyes on what the hell was past him. \u201cRunning off students.\u201d<br /> <br /> His eyebrows knitted. \u201cYou are not alumni. Or police.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe are investigators though.\u201d Jack offered his badge for inspection.<br /> <br /> The tall man looked at it and looked slowly back up. \u201cThere is nothing to investigate.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smiled. \u201cAnd who decides that?\u201d<br /> <br /> The man frowned. \u201cThe police have determined that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, they don\u2019t always determine correctly.\u201d I almost got a decent goddamn look in, but the man shifted before I could note anything more than a door to the side. It seemed fucking empty.<br /> <br /> \u201cYour lack of concern for the opinions of the police is noted. I invite you to leave.\u201d He continued frowning.<br /> <br /> Jack held his hands up. \u201cI don\u2019t get many invitations. If we can help each other in the future...\u201d He left that hanging and held out a card.<br /> <br /> The tall man took it. \u201cI am Dr. Stein. I can usually be found in the Nursing building.\u201d<br /> <br /> I snickered and held the door open for Jack. \u201cSee ya later Frank.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked goddamn disapprovingly at me and turned to go back into the inner room. I got my best look as he turned and before the door fucking closed. It was in fact fucking empty, but there was a second door I hadn\u2019t seen earlier. If we hadn\u2019t cased the place earlier, I would have sworn it led outside. The framing and geometry of it all but fucking demanded it.<br /> <br /> So we checked out the wall on that side of the building a-fucking-gain. We were right about the doors. There weren\u2019t even any goddamn windows. None at all for that section of the building, except for the ones leading to the courtyard. I judged the distance in my head. If the two doors off the office led to anything in this quantum reality, they were the tiniest fucking broom closets ever.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack called us just as we finished circling the goddamn building for the fourth fucking time, a conference call with him, us and Naomi. \u201cThere are no faculty around at this time, but I have spoken with a few of the grad students here at the chemistry department. They didn\u2019t know much about Zelia herself, as she is so new. They\u2019ve had plenty to say about the room. Everything in it was donated by the same family, the Asburys naturally. They are even local.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat room is really fucking creepy. I\u2019d hate to visit their house.\u201d I broke in.<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed. There is apparently a door that people have caught glimpses of that leads nowhere, which has been dubbed the \u201cDoor to Hell\u201d, as the Asburys are demon worshipers, of course.\u201d It took time to realize when the g-man was joking, but eventually you get the trick of it. \u201cSo yes, creepy, but also incredibly expensive.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWho the fuck cares? It\u2019s too creepy to use as fucking furniture, and it\u2019s not like it\u2019s fucking money in the goddamn back or some shit.\u201d I raised an eyebrow at Jack. He shrugged. \u201cAnyway, what\u2019s up?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf the college didn\u2019t accept the furnishings, the Asburys might not give actual money.\u201d Billy Mack sounded exceedingly patient. I hate it when he sounds patient. \u201cDid you get to go through the office there?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack spoke into the speakerphone. \u201cNah. A Dr. Stein stopped us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou met him?\u201d Naomi sounded delighted. \u201cHis first name\u2019s Norman, by the way, not Frank.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell that\u2019s a goddamn opportunity missed. I\u2019m gonna call him Frank anyway.\u201d I grinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cEveryone does. Cassandra agrees with you, about the room?\u201d She ended it with a question mark, as if to make sure I didn\u2019t think it was about the goddamn Dr. Stein. \u201cShe says it\u2019s bad, and she knows creepy. She\u2019s kinda the spiritual leader of the campus pagans.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs far as Zelia goes, I got her office number but that is about it.\u201d Billy Mack tried to get us back on fucking track.<br /> <br /> Naomi made noises of agreement. \u201cYeah, not even anybody who had her as a teacher knew much about her. They were surprised and all, she hadn\u2019t seemed sad or anything. So, Gabe, what was Stein doing? In the office?\u201d<br /> <br /> I snorted. \u201cStopping us from going in.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave up on turning the discussion to whatever the hell he\u2019d called about. \u201cDid he feel like Herb by chance?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi chimed in quickly and I echoed her \u201cNope.\u201d She continued. \u201cFeels kinda like John Wayne, really.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, if I were a zombie making man, I might make them like John Wayne.\u201d Billy Mack sounded awfully goddamn sure of that.<br /> <br /> \u201cReally? Not Mr. Rogers?\u201d Naomi asked. A pair of wandering students came nearby and Jack wandered off to menace them into getting the fuck away.<br /> <br /> The g-man considered for far too fucking long a moment, in that he considered it at all. \u201cWell, it depends on what you need a zombie for.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing untoward, I\u2019m not that kinda girl.\u201d She sounded scandalized.<br /> <br /> Jack came back. \u201cWhat are they talking about?\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cFucking zombie Mr. Rogers. The answer to your second question, why? is I\u2019ve got no goddamn clue.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi sighed herself, then her voice brightened. \u201cOh, Cass said there was someone who was particularly interested in the room.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do they look like?\u201d Jack asked, rubbing his temples.<br /> <br /> She thought. \u201cDresses like a hippy...\u201d She paused. \u201cWears... hats?\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cLong hair, fucktons of eye makeup? Runs around with a girl whose gams go on for goddamn days, short dark hair, kinda timid?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah!\u201d She snapped her fingers. \u201cThat\u2019s Angela, and Am. That\u2019s short for Amsterdam. Her real name is China, but she didn\u2019t like it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. We chased them out of the room before Dr. Stein showed up. Why don\u2019t you go check out that lead. I think this one\u2019s tapped out for now. Might need to try again later, more quietly. What about you, Billy Mack? What\u2019s in her office?\u201d Jack took up the reins of keeping us on fucking track.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d the g-man responded.<br /> <br /> I exchanged glances with Jack. \u201cWhy the fuck not?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s locked. That\u2019s why I called.\u201d I made strangling motions at the phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll be there soon. You two go ahead and keep talking about fucking.\u201d I hung up.<br /> <br /> <br /> The door failed to open when I walked up and I could tell it wasn\u2019t gonna fucking behave no matter what quantum reality I poked at. So I gave it a goddamn piece of my fucking mind while I picked the lock.<br /> <br /> The room had been fucking picked clean. The methodical piles and still haphazard arrangement of the same had me figuring it was the bulls. They had missed one thing - a notepad sitting near the phone. Jack tossed it on the top of a stack he handed to me and so the impression left by the last note written on the previous sheet was fucking obvious. A quick pencil rubbing later got us \u201cAsbury Room, 11:15\u201d in Zelia\u2019s handwriting.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack had gone straight for the computer. He found a number of email exchanges between the dead professor and good old Dr. Norman Stein. He seemed to be mentoring her in some capacity. Didn\u2019t really match up with my fucking impression of him, but everybody has their own goddamn way to grieve.<br /> <br /> We checked up on a few things while we had employee-level access to the campus systems. Stein\u2019s office was in the Nursing building, like he\u2019d said, which was too far from the Asbury Room to have arrived from there in response to anything we did, barring a fucking teleporter. The office itself in the Asbury Room was assigned to the nameless \u201cStaff\u201d. We also got a picture for Dr. Cross, someone that Naomi told us was concerned about Angela\u2019s behavior re: the room.<br /> <br /> By that time it was near enough to 9 o\u2019clock that we needed to start for The Last Drop. Naomi stayed on campus, following up on the lead with Angela. She kept Jack updated, sending him texts about the fact that the crazy broad thought that the Asbury Room is where she\u2019s supposed to be, and is her friend, to the point that she\u2019s brought people there to fuck. She stole a key at one point and has a duplicate. She wears it on a chain around her neck, so lifting it is not really a fucking option to save her from her goddamn self.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rosanna was there when we arrived at The Last Drop coffee house. She was sitting near a side door labeled Employees Only, not quite directly underneath one of the many fucking clusters of cobwebs. A record player played soft jazz from a corner, the windows were fully fucking covered by Venetian blinds and multiple handwritten signs requested that we not touch the spider webs.<br /> <br /> We all activated our sensors going in, to be as well armed as we could. Billy Mack managed to quickly convey that her major points of leverage were her fear of the fucking Gentry, her love for Crusher and her dread of major amounts of change. I scanned the other patrons, and the employees. The hipster couple had nothing special going on, and neither did the old man reading in the corner opposite the record player.<br /> <br /> The baristas, on the other hand, were both Changelings. At first glance I thought they were related. Watching them as they made my goddamn Irish Coffee, it seemed more like they were made from the same mold, with the only difference being one\u2019s dark stringy hair versus the other\u2019s lank blonde hair. They seemed duty bound to watch over Rosanna, though neither seemed particularly handy in a fucking stand up fight. There was no body language indicating physical backup, so when it came, it was likely to be mystical.<br /> <br /> I spiked my coffee from my flask as Jack laid the fucking contract out. Rosanna seemed nervous, glancing frequently at the baristas and the spiders. She gave the contract a cursory look before peering at Jack. \u201cWhat are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked sad. \u201cI can\u2019t actually answer that. Not from lack of want, mind you. From lack of ability.\u201d<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t seem reassured but started flipping through the damn contract. \u201cYou must understand, our enemies also make deals. And there are people working against Crusher. We have been looking into it while he is...\u201d She shuddered a bit. \u201cRelatively safe in prison. Not that I relish the idea.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack flipped to the \u2018vacation\u2019 portion of the deal. \u201cAs you can see, this takes away his conviction plus some. He\u2019ll have a safe house, for a month - you can look into things and he can be free.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and continued looking it over. \u201cForgive me, but we do not live in a kind world. What do you get out of this?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHis conviction.\u201d Jack indicated the relevant line.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what does tha...\u201d She trailed off as she noticed the line of nine spiders arrayed on the nearest web, all different species that I\u2019d noticed a few minutes ago. I smirked and topped off my coffee. This place was fucking creepy too.<br /> <br /> Her thoughts mirrored mine. \u201cThis is a creepy place. I don\u2019t believe you intend me harm, but those who do often meet an end here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is hard to explain, but we do benefit from taking unwanted things, like this conviction, from people.\u201d Jack answered the question she never quite finished.<br /> <br /> She nodded and finished her second read-through. \u201cYou seem to have created a fair contract here. I will not trick you into a pledge like Crusher did - and I\u2019m sorry for that, by the way. He\u2019s...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOver protective?\u201d I offered.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cOf me. He doesn\u2019t even like me coming here. Not only enemies of the kind have disappeared. I would, however, appreciate your word as a gentleman that this will not harm Crusher.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGladly.\u201d Jack smiled broadly.<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. Uh, one moment.\u201d She walked over to the barista\u2019s station and asked them a question, gesturing at the fucking spiders. Their voices also came from the same goddamn mold.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe are following the terms you gave.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou do not get to requisition further.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack narrowed his eyes as she hurried back. \u201cIf you need an escort out...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, no. I\u2019ll be fine. They - their faction - have the upper hand in the city at the moment. But they\u2019ll not do me harm.\u201d She assured him. \u201cIs there anything else?\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned forward in my chair. \u201cYou said you checked into people who were going after Crusher? Has a Michael White come up?\u201d<br /> <br /> She knit her brow. \u201cNot in the investigation. I have heard the name before though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe tried to get Crusher to throw a fight?\u201d I prompted.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, that sounds right. And... and you mentioned him, at the fights.\u201d She narrowed her eyes a bit. \u201cYou were looking for Drake, the bounty hunter that brought Crusher in.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back and held her enraged gaze. \u201cYup. A man your man Crusher doesn\u2019t want dead, so you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her voice came out with a fucking hiss. \u201cYou don\u2019t get to hurt Crusher and live!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, sweetheart, you want to protect someone from the fucking legal system, I\u2019d suggest getting a better lawyer, not going after bounty hunters. Besides, White plays a long con, and has a goddamn hate-on for Drake, for whatever fucking reason. I wouldn\u2019t put it past him to have set this up.\u201d I finished my fucking coffee.<br /> <br /> Her nostrils flared as she got her goddamn temper under control. \u201cFine. Because you\u2019ve helped us, he gets off once, with a scar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd if you find him in the Hedge?\u201d I raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> She chuckled darkly. \u201cIf he hasn\u2019t run into Mr Smile... He\u2019s weaker than the other Gentry nearby, but that\u2019s just relative. He\u2019s looking for a prize, something they\u2019ve never seen before, so they\u2019ll let him back to his realm.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo that\u2019s what his name is. Tall, slender, theatre mask for a face?\u201d Billy Mack looked at Rosanna. She nodded. \u201cMy friend Vivian ran into him, when White tricked her into the Hedge.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes widened. \u201cI suggest your friend Vivian leave town.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is safely tucked away, don't worry.\u201d The g-man smiled reassuringly. It was a little creepy.<br /> <br /> Rosanna sighed and turned to me. \u201cHas your bounty hunter friend broken any promises? That would make him easier for Crusher to find.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at the others. \u201cHe didn\u2019t show up for work because of a second job, technically. I dunno if it was of his own goddamn will though, or if that fucking matters.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I won\u2019t ask Crusher not to help. I\u2019ll call him in the morning and let him know I approve of the contract.\u201d She stood to go.<br /> <br /> We stood as well, but I stopped her before we moved away. \u201cOne more thing. Any way you could put me in touch with Jake?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked confused. \u201cThe fighting ring door guard? He\u2019s not a Changeling.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. But he tried to warn me to stay the fuck away from White, and I wanna know why.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I\u2019d be happier if I gave him your number rather than the other way around.,\u201dThere was uncertainty back in her voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing, princess. Here\u2019s another card - he might still have one, but just in case.\u201d She took the offered card. \u201cYou\u2019re a doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> I kept an eye on her as she walked over to the barista. The three of them waited on a pair of fucking replacement baristas they summoned up with a call button. Then they went into the back. Billy Mack was fiddling with his phone as we left, but put it up after some kind of feedback shocked the hipster broad hard enough to send her coffee flying towards the nearest web. Jack, ever the gentleman, stomped the goddamn fuck out of the spider that fell nearest. Saboteurs make a hell of an exit.<br /> <br /> <br /> We picked up where we left off with the campus investigation, and made our way over to Zelia\u2019s townhouse. My luck decided to fucking hold this time, and I found the door unlocked. Naomi let Jack know she was headed to the goddamn Asbury Room to make out with Angela, giving herself an hour and a half deadline for checking back in before a rescue broke the fucking door down.<br /> <br /> For the most part, the townhouse was a repeat of her office. It had clearly been searched by the bulls as well, who\u2019d left everything neatly fucking stacked. As far as I could tell, they\u2019d been just as thorough. It was hard to know for sure, because the area near her computer had been completely fucking tossed. Drawers emptied and their contents scattered on the floor, documents spread out all over the place and every nearby container fucking upended.<br /> <br /> I managed to find a fingerprint on one of the drawers and Jack gathered up what appeared to be a work-in-progress novel manuscript. Billy Mack copied over a digital copy of the fucking same, for analysis. He also found a series of emails exchanges in her personal email account with <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#affbc7cafbc7c6ddcbe6efc8c2cec6c381ccc0c2\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"184c707d4c70716a7c51587f75797174367b7775\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>. The most recent one had them asking her if she\u2019d had the dream again and to describe it in detail. She never did describe it, at least not over fucking email, though she did tell whoever was on the other end that she\u2019d had it again, and it had seemed more hungry. There was no indication of who the hell TheThirdI was, other than the fact they were local enough that the two had met in person.<br /> <br /> Once he\u2019d followed that trail to its end, it had been about 45 minutes since Naomi\u2019s timer started, so we started moving towards campus. Fifteen minutes later, she gave us a call, so we decided to meet up at another fucking coffee shop, this one without any goddamn spiders.<br /> <br /> We went first and filled her in on the conversation with Rosanna and the state of Zelia\u2019s townhouse. \u201cSo that\u2019s about it for our fucking end. You have fun?\u201d I leered at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs a matter of fact, I did.\u201d She looked smug. \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure Angela\u2019s mostly straight, but if a girl\u2019s heteroflexible, I know how to make them flex. That room was super creepy though - it didn\u2019t help that it seemed to specifically not like me much after I bit her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t suppose you took a break from your fucking creepy make out session to get a look at that side room?\u201d I raised an eyebrow<br /> <br /> She looked mock-offended. \u201cOf course I did! It was empty, like you said. The side door was to an office space. It actually fit the Euclidean space or whatever , so it was really really small. The Door to Hell was locked. On the plus side, the whole watching thing wasn\u2019t so much going on in there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo interrupting Lurches?\u201d I gave her a lopsided grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cNope. Angela says Dr. Stein is harmless, by the way, and since she\u2019s objectively wrong about both that and the room, I bet they\u2019re related. Cass says she\u2019s open to spirits, whatever that means.\u201d She took a sip of her hot chocolate and sighed happily. \u201cI\u2019m gonna corner Am, I think, and try to get her feelings on things. Apparently all I have to do is imply she won\u2019t survive the experience to make her flex.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWill she?\u201d Jack asked.<br /> <br /> Naomi smiled. \u201cSure, she\u2019s just this natural victim, you know and definitely pings as prey, right?\u201d She looked around for confirmation. We all shrugged. \u201cAnyway, it\u2019s why I don\u2019t think Angela\u2019s behind the suicide directly, cause Am is a much more clear choice for some kind of sacrifice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough.\u201d I topped off my coffee. \u201cLook, if we\u2019re gonna fucking go for this, especially if our next step is to harass Dr. Cross about the well-being of a goddamn student, we need a client. It looks better and opens more doors. You could do it, Naomi. It\u2019s a little weird, you being on the payroll and all, but it just has to look good on paper, and you have reason enough to ask your bosses for help.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing... boss.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Sup cutie! I wanted to give you an update on the whole mystery thing and see if you could help me with something.<br /> <br /> Not that kind of help me with something, I am tired and going to be crashing out for the night here in a few minutes.<br /> <br /> Do I even need to remind you of your home invasion this morning? A gal needs her privacy.<br /> <br /> Okay, so since everything was coming up fishy, we decided to go investigate. I talked to Cassandra first, who felt that the room was bad Juju and should be avoided. She did note Angela Wilcox had something of a fixation on it, even a key to it. She also said Angela was \u201copen to spirits\u201d so we will have to see what that meant. Also, the room was all donated by a single family.<br /> <br /> Communicating with the rest of the team, I found out Gabe and Jack met Angela and Am Loughton at the Asbury room but chased them off, and were chased off by Dr. Frankenstein. They also got a bad vibe from it. Billy Mack talked to some adjuncts and got where Zelia\u2019s office was.<br /> <br /> I found Angela and Am, and confirmed Angela has a key to the Asbury room where the suicide took place. Like, she wears it with her pentacle around her neck. Her pentacle.<br /> <br /> Pentacle, not pentagram. You are a terrible pagan. A pentacle is an amulet. A pentagram you draw.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if a pentacle has a separate pentagram on\u2026look, it does not matter. The thing she wears around her neck, that thing? She also has a key to the Asbury room on it. And the pentacle. She also\u2014<br /> <br /> Yes, going to church also makes you a bad pagan. But we have already established that you are, no need to find more reasons.<br /> <br /> No, going with your mom does not make it worse, it mitigates it a little but no you are a terrible pagan. They won\u2019t let you into pagan heaven now, or whatever. Can we go on?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think you are getting into Valhalla whatever kind of pagan you are.<br /> <br /> Okay. Anyway turns out Angela was pretty keen on the room as Cassandra said. She actually lifted the key and had a copy made she wore around her neck. She snuck in a lot and even scored with one of the hockey guys in it.<br /> <br /> That reminds me, did you say Adria was Canadian? Oh. Okay, maybe I just ran into a lot of Canadians when\u2026<br /> <br /> Wait what? What the hell is politically Canadian? What does that even mean? So she is politically Canadian?<br /> <br /> Wait, and Clint is also not Canadian but politically Canadian? I don\u2019t\u2026<br /> <br /> You know what, lets move on.<br /> <br /> I also found out that Dr. Kris-Kross has the idea Angela is \u201ctroubled\u201d and Angela feels like she is crimping her. Not had a chance to look into that yet.<br /> <br /> Wait do you mean gay when you say Canadian? Is that a\u2026.okay. I was gonna say that is\u2026.what?<br /> <br /> Nope leaving it again.<br /> <br /> Yes I know Dr. Carter is \u201cpolitically lesbian.\u201d It makes me want to punch her. This has nothing to do with politically Canadian though, right? Good. I\u2019d really rather not punch Adria.<br /> <br /> What the hell was I talking about?<br /> <br /> Okay, so I called Gabe, Jack and BM, and they were totally not breaking into Zelia\u2019s office, where they found she had a memo to meet someone in the Asbury room at 11:15. They then went to deal with an agency matter at The Last Drop.<br /> <br /> Yea, the place with the Gothlets.<br /> <br /> Ok, so, I was chatting with Angela and Am and suggested if Angela was so keen on this room maybe she should show it to me in a flirtatious manner. Oh my gods she was all too eager to show me the room and see if I \u201cfelt it too\u201d So we went, with Am trundling along behind us, after messaging the agency to come if I had not texted in 90 minutes.<br /> <br /> Long story short, we fooled around. The room was none too pleased when I bit her\u2026yea I felt the weird being watched sensation. Am was\u2026overcome\u2026by the moment\u2026and when I menaced-flirted with her went a little crazy. Girl has a self-destructive streak. I would not make bets of her hitting 30, much less a ripe old age. We will see if she makes 20.<br /> <br /> We left, and I quickly touched base with the Agency. They searched the house and found someone had searched there who did not search her office, and were not with the police. Also, a book she was working on I think. We met for coffee (not at The Last Drop) and I returned here.<br /> <br /> Now, we need a reason to investigate. I can hire the agency, but that would just be suspicious. I wanted to suggest you hire us\u2026don\u2019t worry you won\u2019t pay anything whatever Gabe says (I know I can get Lady Covington to help with it if Gabe decides to be a cunt, trust me I have the inside track). That gives us reason to look around. Of course, we would not mention your name unless we had to.<br /> <br /> Well, for one thing you found yourself unconscious having gotten into my apartment through the locked door. That is a start.<br /> <br /> I understand sweetie. We will speak after class. Sleep good and take care.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVI</i><br /> <br /> The major error was giving the Autumn Court open season on them by killing their spider. Those spiders and webs are partly bait to give them license to make people\u2019s life hell. But they got beats!<br /> <br /> It was a good investigation session, and we moved the story forward a bit. <br /> <br /> Am/Amsterdam/China name was based on the sheer amount of people I knew in college who gave themselves or were given odd nicknames. It seems to be a thing. At least it was a thing and I assume it still is. The mental gymnastics of \u201cI was named China but I wanted a different country and liked Amsterdam because pot and Amsterdam is not a country I guess but I don\u2019t want to go by the Netherlands so I went Amsterdam but it is long so people call me Am\u201d is actually fairly simple compared to how some of them got bizarre names.<br /> <br /> I have no idea what the hell Politically Canadian means either, to be completely honest with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Okay, well hope you enjoyed. Another spooky session in two weeks. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:08:28-07:00","id":513067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=509258#post509258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea what the hell Politically Canadian means either, to be completely honest with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Socialist, but polite about it. ;-D<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:26:37-07:00","id":513228,"title":"","content":"LOL probably. I was telling the players at some point there will be a Political Canadians rally at the school. I don't have any specific plans for what will happen yet, but it should be fun.<br /> <br /> We had the whole crew last session, should be a fun time. Jared is totally Politically Canadian too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T13:37:20-07:00","id":525857,"title":"","content":"So, the University case. It\u2019s time to get caught up on what the Agency is doing on this case.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> On the way to my appointment, the damnedest fucking feeling came over me. I shook my head, trying to clear it, and jammed my foot to the floor as we pulled onto a straightaway. My brow knit as the car slowed down in response. I took my foot off the pedal and the car continued to slow the hell down, but not at the rate I\u2019d expect, with no fucking gas. I glanced at Jack\u2019s unconscious form in my front seat, only to have my attention jerked away by a sudden acceleration.<br /> <br /> I tried the brakes, hoping to figure out what the hell was going on with my baby from the outside. White would just have to deal with the delay. The pedal wouldn\u2019t budge. I glanced around. The embankment was fucking steep and the ground rocky and besides, even if I had a decent chance of making the roll out, I had four packages to deliver. I am a goddamn Psychopomp. I finish the job.<br /> <br /> I fought with the car and scanned the desolate area, but nothing worked the way I expected and there was no one around that might be fucking with me. The only sign of civilized life, human or otherwise, other than me, was my car, the four Fallen in it, the road and a rapidly approaching train. A quick calculation made it clear we were on a collision course. I tried for a J-turn, one last desperate measure to get control of my goddamn car back.<br /> <br /> For a half second, the car turned with my steering and I thought I was free. But it wasn\u2019t enough. It went too wide and the end of screeching turn had my car stopped, straddling the goddamn tracks, facing the direction I\u2019d come from, with the fucking train yards away on my left.<br /> <br /> The impact was a rending scream of metal and then pain. The unsecured unconscious forms of the others got thrown around the fucking car. Vivian was impaled on the front of the train, same as me. Jared had been thrown from the goddamn wreck entirely. Jack\u2019s neck was at a wholly unnatural angle and a shard of something had lodged itself into Liz\u2019s skull via her eye.<br /> <br /> A tap on the crumpled side of my car took my attention from the mangled bodies. Michael White gave me a shit-eating grin through my shattered window. \u201cThanks pal! I knew I could count on a Psychopomp to make a delivery right on time.\u201d His voice came from the other side of a long dark tunnel and his soft chuck on my shoulder turned out the rest of the lights.<br /> <br /> <br /> I woke up, gasping for air. My hands went to my side and shoulder, and didn\u2019t find blood, or bandages or any evidence of fucking train impalement. A small cold object rolled to touch my back and it shattered against my goddamn bedroom wall before I even registered that it was just a half-empty bottle.<br /> <br /> A dream.<br /> <br /> \u201cGoddamn, motherfucking piece of shit sucking bastard...\u201d It was awhile before I had a thought that wouldn\u2019t be a series of bleeps on network television.<br /> <br /> <br /> I stumbled into the goddamn office, wincing against the noon-ish sun. I tossed the empty in my right into the trash inside and finished off the one in my left as I rummaged around for my office bottle.<br /> <br /> The others were having some kind of pow-wow in the lab, even the fucking kid. I didn\u2019t show the relief I felt at seeing them all alive and well. At least, mostly well. Billy Mack and Jack looked as bad as I fucking felt. \u201cSo, did the shit-eating bugger of a goddamn bridge fucking builder fuck with you too?\u201d I slurred as I waved at them. Billy Mack just looked at me. \u201cThe dreams, jackass, the fucking dreams. It\u2019s goddamn Michael White, trying to get in out goddamn heads with some dream fuckery Numen.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jared looked smug. \u201cIf so, he likes me. Nothing but cute girls and good times.\u201d<br /> <br /> I growled incoherently at him. Naomi looked at me warily. \u201cI didn\u2019t have any... bad dreams either. Are you sure it was Michael?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy the fuck wouldn\u2019t he fuck with you?\u201d I narrowed my eyes and jerked my head towards Jared. \u201cHe\u2019s the new kid, so fuck him anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack cleared his throat. \u201cIf I know the Numen you are referring to, he would have had to see us yesterday. If it was him, which is not necessarily the case, he might simply have caught us without her - there were plenty of such situations.\u201d<br /> <br /> I collapsed onto a chair and took another drink. \u201cFuck.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWith a few strings pulled, I could have a goddamn army. This fucker needs to stay out of my head.\u201d Jack started cracking his knuckles.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought you were building them up for a cult?\u201d Naomi ventured. \u201cIt\u2019s more our idiom, you know?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jared looked thoughtful. \u201cA guerrilla army would fit our idiom...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack waved the suggestion away. \u201cI don\u2019t do well with animals. \u201c Jared suppressed a smirk.<br /> <br /> I stood up grandiosely, then steadied myself on a desk. \u201cFuck that shit. We should just fucking beat up the goddamn bridge builder our own fucking selves.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI gotta say it - I don\u2019t wanna, but I gotta - I agree with Gabe\u2019s drunken ramblings.\u201d Jared shrugged.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked dubious, but didn\u2019t fight it, just changed the subject. \u201cNaomi, you had something you were about to suggest?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI think Deanna should hire us. Liz can supply the cash discretely, and Deanna has reason to a) hire a detective, considering her lost time and b) hire us specifically, because she knows me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing sweetheart.\u201d I waved her on fucking magnanimously. \u201cJust have Cecilia draw up a contract.\u201d I peered at Jacob. \u201cYou get filled in kid?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, I did. I think we should lean on Dr. Stein. My gut says he knows something.\u201d The look in his eyes went hard for a moment.<br /> <br /> \u201cOn that note, he has a concealed carry permit and if his records from when he was an ME with the police are any indication, a good shot. Also, his time on the force might explain why he took such a disliking towards Jack with his comments on their abilities.\u201d The g-man raised an eyebrow at him.<br /> <br /> Naomi winked at Jack. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, rebels are hot. All I know is that he\u2019s creepy and has a super morbid sense of humor.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do believe that gallows humor is required for MEs.\u201d Billy Mack turned his chair around to face us.<br /> <br /> Jared started counting on his fingers. \u201cSo we have three leads: the room, Dr. Stein\u2019s presence in the same and the Katherine-Lisa thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> I held up my hands in a T-shape. \u201cHold up, time out, stop, pause, what the shit?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded at a stack of papers on the desk near the computer. \u201cI analyzed the two versions of Zelia\u2019s manuscript last night. The computer version is newer, with some more work having been done. The only other difference is the helpful mentor character\u2019s name, which changed from Katherine, spelled the same as the good Dr. Cross, to Lisa.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, so it changed cause she met her, or cause the character\u2019s based on her but the name thing was goddamn creepy or she\u2019s based on her but their relationship outside the fucking book changed, huh? Or something...\u201d I trailed off, thinking.<br /> <br /> \u201cOr Katherine killed her and changed the name when she ransacked the desk.\u201d Jared pointed out.<br /> <br /> I peered at him again. \u201cAre you required to distrust people whose first name is Doctor at that age especially, or did one bite you as a smaller kid?\u201d<br /> <br /> He rolled his eyes as Naomi spoke up. \u201cThere\u2019s also the Asbury family, as a lead.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack turned his chair back to the computer. \u201cHm. Their fortunes appear to have declined rather. Some bad luck on the market. They do still have a house here in town. Donald Asbury, in his 80s, and Mary and Clayton, in their 50s, live there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like an opportunity to me.\u201d Our fixer grinned widely.<br /> <br /> <br /> First though, we had to spring a mug from the goddamn hoosegow. Before we left, I ran my hands over my baby\u2019s frame, checked her out under the hood and ran a quick systems check. Naomi went back in for something, keeping it out of my line of sight and ducking in just before I revved the engine.<br /> <br /> As I stepped out of the car at the big house, Naomi ambushed me. I caught a faceful of flowery fucking smelling shit and then a couple more squirts for full goddamn saturation. I spluttered. \u201cThe fuck was that for?\u201d Some of the lingering scent got in my mouth and I spat.<br /> <br /> Naomi shrugged and smiled brightly. \u201cYou smell less like booze now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I glared at her and took another swig. I finished my flask off as we walked into the outer building and tossed it to the desk guard. He fumbled it and it clattered to the desk. \u201cI\u2019ll be wanting that shit back when we're fucking done. Won\u2019t go through the goddamn metal detectors.\u201d<br /> <br /> He stood up and leaned over the desk. \u201cDamn right you can\u2019t. Who do you think you are? What are you doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFBI business, so back the fuck off.\u201d I jerked a thumb towards the g-man.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded resignedly and told the fucker out appointment ID number or some shit. The desk guard took our escort aside and had a conversation that involved way too fucking much looking at me until I smirked at them and waggled my fingers. The new one blushed and kept an eye on me all the way back to the visiting room.<br /> <br /> \u201cThese cuffs insured?\u201d We heard the big man\u2019s voice before we saw him.<br /> <br /> Jack smiled. \u201cHow you holding up?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d Crusher grunted, stretching. The cuff chains snapped. \u201cRosanna called, said you were legit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood to hear it.\u201d Jack spread out the contract and offered Crusher a pen. \u201cWe brought you a suit. Hope it fits.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cWe had to get it off the rack, but then, that was too.\u201d He indicated the convict\u2019s current getup.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd orange doesn\u2019t match my eyes.\u201d Crusher grinned wolfishly as he signed where Jack indicated. \u201cAnything else you fellas and ladies need?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re still looking for that Drake gee. If it makes a difference, he might be in the goddamn Hedge.\u201d I leaned back in my chair, balancing on two legs of it.<br /> <br /> \u201cHeh. Well, if he is, I recommend you let us deal with it.\u201d He stood up and stretched again.<br /> <br /> I handed him his new suit. \u201cI won\u2019t argue with that. We still owe a fucking talking owl a goddamn book.\u201d<br /> <br /> By the time I\u2019d argued my flask back from protective custody, Crusher had changed and was walking out with us. \u201cWant a ride into town?\u201d I offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you don\u2019t mind.\u201d Billy Mack grinned. Jack looked like he was about to call shotgun, but graciously ceded that to Crusher and sat next to Naomi, who preemptively had her hands on the oh shit handle.<br /> <br /> <br /> Once we'd dropped off a slightly green Crusher, I pointed the car back towards campus. \u201cSo, speaking of students, like we totally were, I dunno, this morning?\u201d Naomi looked at Jared to confirm. He nodded. \u201cJared and I are going to be building a cult of them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. I am building a cult of paranormal, specifically UFO, enthusiasts myself.\u201d Billy Mack had moved to the front and turned to look back at them.<br /> <br /> Jared raised an eyebrow. \u201cProbies, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt makes for a good cover story.\u201d The g-man shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cI just wanted to make sure we didn\u2019t have a left hand right hand situation, and wind up investigating ourselves.\u201d She smirked. \u201cAnd speaking of investigating campus things, since we\u2