t\u2019s not a thing, really.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMind if I live tweet this? It\u2019s getting really good.\u201d Jared smiled broadly and shook his phone. The two girls ignored him. He texted \u2018re:Cross - stigmatic\u2019 to the rest of us.<br /> <br /> After a suitable amount of grovelling form Cassandra, Naomi softened and then went emotionless. \u201cThat was a test, Cassandra, and you have been proven worthy to see us as we truly are.\u201d Cassandra looked confused, the in awe, then faint, as Clytemnestra and Fulgur revealed themselves and the spider fed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Okay here is your first report, you ready?<br /> <br /> Well get ready damnit, I need to go talk to Am in a few.<br /> <br /> Okay, so we returned to school and split up. Gabe went to examine the Asbury room environs. Jack and I went to talk to Dr. Crisscross, Billy Mack and Jared went to talk to Dr. Frankenstein.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack and Jared got decent information. Well, Billy Mack had early figured out he was in \u201cME\u201d, which apparently means he is a coroner. Was a coroner? I don\u2019t actually know what \u201cME\u201d means. Anyway, at the interview Frankenstein was fairly helpful, apparently. He has connections to some stuff the Agency is looking into, though he may be unconnected to this mess outside of mentoring Zelia. I don\u2019t actually remember her last name now. He knows Dr. Hardgrave is a vampire, which is news to me.<br /> <br /> Everyone knows there are vampires. I don\u2019t\u2026<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t take his class. Duh.<br /> <br /> Anyway, his connection seemed peripheral, though he got some info on that other stuff. Did I tell you about the Sanderson stuff? I will later. Anyway main thing is he has been chasing away people from the room, as he thinks it is sinister, and has done so more lately.<br /> <br /> Jesus Gringa, if you don\u2019t think he is really a vampire fine. I don\u2019t care. You wanted answers, I give you answers, okay? I don\u2019t give a fuck if you believe him. I don\u2019t know that I do. How about you not ask him about it in case you are wrong, yea?<br /> <br /> Smart girl.<br /> <br /> Jack and I spoke to Dr. Crisscross, and I got some info. She got uncomfortable when I mentioned Cassandra, so I decided to speak to her about it. She had a \u201chunch\u201d that Zelia was in trouble, and now has one that Angela is. She said I should talk to her. Jack and I agreed her \u201chunches\u201d were probably psychic in nature, and she did not want to say that because we would blow her off. We tried to get more info but she hammered on that we needed to save Zelia.<br /> <br /> Oh, and while I bemoan how many people around here only speak one language, I have to say Dr. Crisscross spoke fluent bitch. I had a good conversation with her in bitch right off and some earlier on in the conversation before Jack, who for obvious reasons is not fluent in bitch, suggested I go so he could continue to the conversation in English. Whatever, Jack.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure she wants me.<br /> <br /> So Dr. Crisscross needs me, to swoop in and save Angela, and\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh! Yea her name was in the story. The story Zelia wrote, Deanna. Yea. As a mentor figure. Interesting eh? May be a connection, maybe not. Billy Mack is scanning some prints now, I think, from the house.<br /> <br /> Gabe broke into the Asbury room, as having her talk to people is a lot like throwing a rabid dog at kindergarteners. It\u2019s all tears, screaming, and lawsuits, and you probably need to shoot up with a needle to get over it. Not everyone has my charm. But it worked, as she is as good a detective as she is terrible a speaker. Well, in this case burglar and detective.<br /> <br /> So yea, there is something evil under the Asbury room. Well, possibly in it, draining under it. It\u2019s sort of a dark force that is otherdimensional and intelligent. As a detective you hired and speaking as a much better pagan than you, I advise you not go anywhere the fuck near there. We are dealing with it.<br /> <br /> What? Nah we got it. Billy Mack is with the FBI, what do you think the FBI does anyway?<br /> <br /> No, that is the CIA. You don\u2019t know the difference between the FBI and CIA? What generation Chinese are you again?<br /> <br /> No, the NSA profiles Arabs and wiretaps everything. Different people.<br /> <br /> I did not actually watch X-Files. That was a movie right?<br /> <br /> Look, the important thing here is Billy Mack is on it. He will get it covered. But we need to know who maybe helping this force. Which is why you need to be fucking careful, Deanna.<br /> <br /> Jared and I spoke to Cassandra. Okay are you ready for this? Cassandra seduced Dr. Crisscross. Yes she did. Yes. She. Did. She totally did! No seriously, she did. I turned on the waterworks and lets just say she owes me bigtime.<br /> <br /> No she did not \u201cjust admit it\u201d but Jared and I shook it out of her.<br /> <br /> Did it for you babe!<br /> <br /> She did not have much information about the room past that. Her \u201cbad vibes\u201d thing did turn out true though.<br /> <br /> So yea, now we see if Angela is a victim or perpetrator. Or maybe both. Jared should be coming, so that will help. New report later hon, be careful!<br /> <br /> Yea, I am sure Jared is totally politically Canadian.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVII</i><br /> <br /> So Fulgur and Clytemnestra decided to start a cult in the University. Thus their approach of Cassandra Bale at the end.<br /> <br /> Speed Demon, Kilroy, and Quietus were victims of Oneiromancy from the Autumn Court. That was all so far.<br /> <br /> And an Abyssal Intrusion in the University. And there may be more to it than it seems. Fulgur\u2019s comment was due to a Dramatic Failure on his Occult roll.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoyed. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 05-24-2015, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T15:01:25-07:00","id":543060,"title":"","content":"More mysteries are solved, and more is peeled back to find the rot beneath. This session pretty much covers the evening after the last session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> After I brought the two fellas by the agency and saw them off, I gave Mac a call. \u201cHey bub.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey Gabe - please tell me that nothing is on fire or rigged to explode.\u201d There was a smile in the public dick\u2019s voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m fucking hurt. You think I would only call if something was on fire or rigged to explode? Nothing like that here.\u201d I paused. \u201cThat I know of. Any goddamn thing ever come of that?\u201d<br /> <br /> I could almost hear him shrug. \u201cNot really. The feds are breathing over our shoulder but haven\u2019t called dibs or anything. They\u2019re letting us do the leg work, which has got zilch - no recognition from the Pakistani or Arabic community, nothing from the local mosques, no ones ever actually seen the husband. I\u2019m figuring it was just a disguise.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOccam\u2019s fucking Razor is with you there.\u201d I tried to steer him down the right path without letting on that she used to be the prim as hell, lemon sucking librarian type.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere was that bank robbery in New York,\u201d he mused. \u201cUnder the hijab she was a blonde law students. It makes for a good one. Is that racist?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fuck?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sounded resigned. \u201cAh, I dunno. Your bail bondsman buddy, Cannon, has been ranting about how racist we are long and loud enough, I guess he\u2019s getting to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cYeah, he does that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou guys aren\u2019t though. Racist. Specifically. He\u2019s pretty sure the KKK running Seattle are gonna be coming after you.\u201d He smirked.<br /> <br /> I put my feet up on the desk and leaned back. \u201cIt is a big goddamn responsibility, you know? Though, I always thought it was the fucking chemtrails I had to worry about, not our goddamn KKK overlords.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, well. Fair warning and all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. Uh, anyway, got a bit sidetracked - I wanted to let you know about the suicide case.\u201d I gave the short and non-supernatural version. \u201cSo yeah, to sum up, turns out it actually was a fucking suicide, with a cult thing going on, and a goddamn love quadrangle.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t imagine your client liked that,\u201d he said sympathetically.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cYeah, but good news is not what the hell we\u2019re paid for.\u201d There was a brief silence. \u201cSo, yeah. I wanted to fill you in, and see if there was anything I could do for you. I\u2019ve been asking a lot of favors lately, and this isn't supposed to be a fucking one-way street.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI appreciate the sentiment, of course, but nothing much\u2019s on right now. There\u2019s that double homicide, the one where the wife drowned?\u201d I made an affirmative noise to answer the implied question. \u201cThat apartment got ransacked again, less carefully this time. Nothing was taken that we could tell and their vault sure wasn\u2019t touched. Only had a few legal papers in it anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNeed an extra pair of eyes on it?\u201d Of course, the police\u2019s post-ransacking ransacking would make Synthesis tough as hell, but we might be able to get something more than they could from it.<br /> <br /> I heard papers rustling on his end. \u201cNah, the guys on it are a bit twitchy at the moment. But if you hear anything about it...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing.\u201d I grabbed my jacket, checking for my fucking keys and headed towards the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cThough on the weird scale and speaking of suicides, that one at the college registers high for sure,\u201d he said, half to himself. \u201cYour cult thing wouldn\u2019t be involved there, would it?\u201d<br /> <br /> I stopped, and took a step back into the room. \u201cNah, that was a pretty goddamn small group and had nothing to do with the university. We're involved, a little bit, though - a friend of our intern lost some time that night and hired us to look into things. It\u2019s a fucking weird case, but she\u2019s paying and it\u2019s important to Naomi, so...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Well, got anything?\u201d He sounded mildly surprised.<br /> <br /> I played it casual. \u201cOther than that room is a fucking creepy place to off yourself in? Not much. The lost time thing seems to be widespread though, at least the goddamn digital footprint would say so.\u201d<br /> <br /> He got a conspiratorial tone in his voice. \u201cI hear creepy is an understatement. Eddie - Eddie Andres - took a sick day after his six hour shift watching over the crime scene and refuses to even go back to campus.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan\u2019t say I blame the poor bastard.\u201d I made sure the door was locked behind me.<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cWell, take care of yourself Gabe. And don\u2019t do anything to make the boys on the Landis case more twitchy.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cScout\u2019s honor.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> In the meantime, Jack and Billy Mack made the drive north of town to find the Asbury\u2019s house. It was a big place - three fucking floors, from the look of it and none of them skimping on space. A shutter or two were missing and a few others were on their way. The grounds were goddamn overgrown and the deepening shadows of twilight didn\u2019t do much to dispel the strong impression of \u2018haunted house\u2019.<br /> <br /> Jack used the large ornate knocker to rap on the door four times. No fucking answer. Billy Mack wandered off to check the grounds while Jack inspected the front of the house. After a moment, Jack\u2019s \u2018hsst\u2019 brought the other man back around the corner.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt looks as if no one has been about for...\u201d Jack turned the handle on the front door and pushed slightly. It creaked open. \u201cOh.\u201d Billy Mack continued in a goddamn stage voice, pitched to carry. \u201cI am concerned over the well being of the people in this house. Let\u2019s make sure they are safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack eyed him as they went inside. The first thing to hit them was the smell of fucking rot. Next, the grandfather clock that was ticking down the hall and a TV on in a different room. Billy Mack flipped the light switch a few times, but the house remained dark as shit, without even the thin light of twilight coming through the open door doing much to pierce the gloom.<br /> <br /> Jack took point, activating his night vision and mental resistance. They both had their guns drawn and by consensus, moved towards the sound of the TV. The TV room had a couch and a recliner, with the usual accompanying furniture. Arrayed on the seating, two each to the couch and chair, watching the static fuzz image on the TV with their goddamn glassy eyes, were four homemade adult human sized dolls. The facial features, stolen from more usual dolls, looked small and out of place on the stuffed stocking face. The two with fucking nail polish and caked on makeup made it clear there were stand ins for the four supposed to be living Asburys.<br /> <br /> The fucking light switch didn\u2019t work here either, though the gray and white static provided some flickering light. Billy Mack read the airwaves, trying to make out the words just under the static noise, but there was no signal to or from the set. Not even an electric one, Jack showed where he pulled the plug on the TV. Neither of them were surprised when it kept fucking running.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful. \u201cThis was the site of an Abyssal intrusion. The original cause is most likely not here any longer - it has likely been moved to the Asbury Room. But reality is damaged here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t suppose you have any reality duct tape on you?\u201d Jack\u2019s voice was pitched low to match Billy Mack\u2019s.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. But I could likely hack Peterson Chemical into making some for us. Or any Logistical Infrastructure. Or we could bring this to the God-Machine\u2019s attention...\u201d The fucker shrugged. Jack gave him a look. Billy Mack responded calmly. \u201cI agree. But it is an option nonetheless.\u201d<br /> <br /> They moved on to the hallway. At first glance, a tall gaunt person waited at the other end, staring at them with wide eyes and with arms crossed in front of them. A second look transformed it into the goddamn grandfather clock they\u2019d heard when they walked in, ticking at a shockingly reality compliant pace.<br /> <br /> A room and a staircase led off from this hallway. The rot smell came from upstairs. The room smelled of motor oil and shit and a dripping sound came from behind the closed door. Jack opened the door and his throat worked. He elbowed Billy Mack. \u201cLight.\u201d He brought his gun to bear.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack turned on his flashlight and took in the room quickly. A brownish red liquid dripped upwards, landing in a pool on the goddamn ceiling. Fucking insect eggs floated in the liquid and covered the twitching, vaguely human shaped mass that crawled along the floor. The light slipped over it with no change in its movements. \u201cThat is fascinating... I think that was one of the Asburys.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack aimed for the center of mass of the fucking thing but didn't fire. It stumbled into the wall, making absolutely no goddamn noise. \u201cWas being the operative word. Should I shoot it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI doubt it would have any effect. The person is undoubtedly dead. I believe the insects are burrowing into its nervous system, this causing the involuntary movements.\u201d Billy Mack leaned further into the room.<br /> <br /> Jack barred him from it and shut the door. \u201cNope. More to explore. Not going in.\u201d He turned Billy Mack towards the stairs and pushed.<br /> <br /> On the way up, Jack texted Naomi: \u2018If I\u2019m not back in 2 hours, burn Asbury House to the ground\u2019<br /> <br /> She responded quickly: \u2018don\u2019t make me damage this dyke cover. get out if you are in danger, this is no time for your macho bullshit\u2019<br /> <br /> He sighed and Billy Mack looked quizzically back at him. He waved the g-man off. \u2018I\u2019m fine, don\u2019t worry\u2019<br /> <br /> \u201815 minutes check ins, k?\u2019<br /> <br /> Jack pocketed his phone after responding \u2018OK\u2019 and continued up the stairs. The damage to reality was fucking worse, here, and the smell of rot as well. It was quiet, until they had taken a few steps down the long hallway. Then a loud goddamn thumping sound came from one of the three closed rooms.<br /> <br /> Opening that door, they found a skeleton in pieces lying on the floor. The walls and ceilings were covered in viscera, flesh and other organs, as if the body the skeleton belonged to had exploded up and out. The thumping noise came from a wardrobe along the wall. It sounded like something inside it was throwing itself at the door, which had two wood planks nailed across it, in addition to a fucking padlock keeping it secure.<br /> <br /> The thumping stopped, after a moment, replaced by a licking sound. The slamming resumed and they both backed out, shutting the door again, once Billy Mack had chemically analyzed the remains.<br /> <br /> The two open rooms off the hallway were unremarkable, empty and had been for a goddamn while. The next closed door was a woman\u2019s bedroom. Spray painted in red on the wall above the bed was the message \u2018You can\u2019t make me\u2019. A skeleton in a fucking bridal gown lay on the bed, dead from a gunshot to the head, a gun with an appropriate caliber lying on the bed next to her right hand. The last room had no such tableau, though it did appear to have been lived in. A man\u2019s room, so the crawling body downstairs was most likely a Mr. Asbury.<br /> <br /> Climbing the ladder to the attic seemed to lessen the feeling of broken reality, as they ascended into the smell of mothballs and old perfume. A child sized doll was staring at them as they entered the attic, sitting in front of an open dollhouse, a big smile on her face. She had on a blue dress and old fashioned perfume. When they moved further into the attic, they realized it wasn\u2019t a doll at all, but a very fucking dead, very goddamn well preserved little girl, about 6 years old.<br /> <br /> Jack looked at Billy Mack, who had moved to the little girl, shrugged and started going through the stacks of books. \u201cWell, here\u2019s the first hint that they caused an Abyssal intrusion on purpose.\u201d He indicated the small collection of occult tomes.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cShe died in 1957.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack did some calculations. \u201cSo, probably Donald\u2019s kid, and Mary and Clayton\u2019s sister?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat would fit with the ages.\u201d A music box started playing \u2018Alice Blue Gown\u2019. They both watched it for a moment.<br /> <br /> Jack patted the dead child on the shoulder. \u201cYou just sit tight Alice. We\u2019ll figure out what happened.\u201d A weird look came over his face. He gave Billy Mack a look. \u201cSomething just tried to get in my head.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked between the two of them. He handed Jack his fucking gun. \u201cJust in case.\u201d He turned to look at the kid. \u201cAlice?\u201d<br /> <br /> In his head he heard \u2018You need to fix me. They couldn\u2019t fix me. I want to play.\u2019<br /> <br /> He looked over the still child. \u201cWhat happened to you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2018The water was too deep. They couldn\u2019t fix me. You need to fix me. I want to play.\u2019 The voice was focused but faint.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s what we do Alice. That is your name?\u201d he asked in a soothing tone.<br /> <br /> \u2018Yes.\u2019 The girl\u2019s lips didn\u2019t move. \u2018They were supposed to fix me but it got bad down there. They couldn\u2019t fix me. And there was lots of screaming. You need to fix me. I want to play.\u2019 The presence in the his mind flickered. \u2018I need to rest now.\u2019 It faded out.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack caught Jack\u2019s eye and jerked his head towards the exit. He stayed fucking quiet until they hit the ground floor. \u201cShe said they were trying to fix her and weren\u2019t able to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked confusedly at Billy Mack and opened the basement door. \u201cFix what?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHer being dead.\u201d Billy Mack shone the flashlight into the almost disappointingly mundane basement. The furnace needed replacing fucking seriously and there was a bed set up in the corner, but that was it. The g-man glanced up at Jack staring at him, waiting at the top of the stairs. \u201cOh. She said the water was too deep. Drowning, I guess.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you.\u201d He rolled his eyes. \u201cDon\u2019t be an asshole when I\u2019m carrying both guns.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I was just coming up on the apartment complex the dead couple lived in when I got a call from a goddamn restricted number. I had promised that I wouldn\u2019t make the bulls twitchy, not that I\u2019d stay 100 yards away at all times. It was a fucking nice place, Mack had said they were wealthy. Nothing twigged at a glance and no one familiar caught my eye. I answered my phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe, was it? This is Jake. Rosanna said you wanted to talk with me?\u201d It sounded like the gee I\u2019d flapped gums with at the fighting ring.<br /> <br /> I started driving nowhere in fucking particular. \u201cSure do. You remember me, right? Took my piece, the 45 at the fight? Answered some questions about a Drake?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d He caught my goddamn angle. \u201cHerb pointed you my way then. This have to do with him?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNope. Michael fucking White. I know, I know, you don\u2019t know the fucker, but I was just wondering about anything you might know about what and why I shouldn\u2019t know.\u201d I checked for tails.<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cI was afraid of that. Look, the phone\u2019s not the best for this. You know Kiki\u2019s?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cI\u2019m familiar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMeet you there in 20?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I texted the others to let them know and headed over to Kiki\u2019s on my own. The radio was warning me about how fucking strange people could be as I walked in. I let my eyes adjust to the light on my walk to the bar and found Jake while I waited on my whiskey. I flipped on my sensors before I approached, and then off again as I got what I could from aura sight and hit a blank goddamn wall with mind reading.<br /> <br /> He seemed cheerful, if a little guarded and definitely had backup somewhere in the fucking place. I smiled as I slid into the booth across from him. \u201cThanks for giving me a call.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cNo skin off my nose.\u201d He glanced around and back at me. \u201cBefore we get into what I know - why do you want to? It really is in your best interest to be completely honest, so I can give you information the most tailored for your needs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFucker tried to kill me.\u201d My answer was quick. And mostly fucking honest. \u201cAnd my agency.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYour detective agency?\u201d He looked goddamn intense for a moment.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cThat is what I do. Tried to kill that Drake gee I was looking for, and probably succeeded there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s their connection?\u201d A look of concern crossed his face.<br /> <br /> \u201cDrake and the goddamn bridge building fuck? White hired him to rescue runaway girls. They butted heads when Drake found out the smarmy little shit was selling them into slavery.\u201d I took a drink.<br /> <br /> He glanced out into the bar. \u201cI wish I could say that surprised me. Though... you don\u2019t find many runaway girls at a fighting ring.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah. Don\u2019t find many at any of the three places he got sent last, especially since one is... infested with large animals and bear traps, the other has a goddamn Hedge gate in it and the other is a fighting ring run by a Changeling with cause to rip a certain bounty hunter\u2019s fucking head off.\u201d I watched him carefully. He smirked and raised an eyebrow when I mentioned large animals.<br /> <br /> His brow knit when I talked about the Changeling. \u201cWhat does Rosanna have against him?\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cSeems Drake was the bounty hunter that brought Crusher in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh.\u201d He smirked. \u201cYeah, that\u2019s up there on the list of things to do to get on her bad side. And I\u2019ve seen her tear out someone\u2019s throat with her teeth. They are an adorable couple.\u201d He took a deep breath and let it out slowly. \u201cSo, he wasn\u2019t sent to find someone who looks like me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot according to any record we fucking found.\u201d I leaned back.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. OK, good. So, your question.\u201d He leaned forward over his drink, looking at me. \u201cWhite is... connected to some very important people. And has finagled himself into a low level supervisory position, even though he certainly doesn\u2019t have their best interests at heart.\u201d He took a drink. \u201cYou seem knowledgeable about things, so it probably won\u2019t be a shock to you that neither Michael White nor these important people are human.\u201d<br /> <br /> I snorted. \u201cNah, I got that one.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled. \u201cIndividuals I\u2019m dealing with have something of a long con in place, to pit him against his important allies. People, for certain definitions of it, are working on a few projects relating to it. I could possibly arrange a distraction, if the water is too deep for you folks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI appreciate the offer, but we\u2019re not that fucking far under. But look, these important people. Any other details there? I don\u2019t wanna run over them by accident or some shit. After all, you know what they say...\u201d I continued in Inuit. \u201cAre you a fucking Demon or what?\u201d<br /> <br /> He smirked into his drink and continued in the same language. \u201cWell that makes things easier. I\u2019m Stalking Horse. Mrs. Clocks is around, but you\u2019ll excuse me if I don\u2019t out her without her permission.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis isn\u2019t one of my stalking horse covers, it\u2019s to aim the Summer Court at something if we really need it.\u201d He paused. \u201cThat sound awful callous. But they make a good boomstick. But anyway, you shouldn\u2019t be tainted by association with this guy.\u201d He gave me a card. \u201cI meant it about that distraction. It would probably mean blowing a cover so only ask if it\u2019s serious, alright?\u201d I nodded. \u201cTo translate from earlier. We - the Fools - want to isolate, analyze and possibly destroy the Command and Control Infrastructure in the Tower.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow and took a drink. \u201cWell. You guys really should learn to fucking dream bigger.\u201d<br /> <br /> He rolled his eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s a hard nut to crack, and White\u2019s our nutcracker. He thinks he\u2019s too good and or smart to fall, often works at cross purposes to other Angels and is a giant tool. If we maneuver it right, he\u2019ll make a hell of a distraction.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose we shouldn\u2019t storm his office and introduce his fucking face to my goddamn rivet gun then.\u201d I sighed.<br /> <br /> He looked torn. \u201cit wouldn\u2019t be the end of the world, and he is a sadistic bastard. It would send us back to the drawing board and the only other plan we\u2019ve come up with is to blow up Diablo Dam.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah let\u2019s not go with that one. I mean, if I get a fucking vote. Which I have no goddamn reason to have. But... yeah, no.\u201d I smiled and raised my eyebrows in a \u2018how about it buddy\u2019 kind of look.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, it\u2019s not our favorite plan either.\u201d He held his hands up. \u201cThough, thinking of the dam, there is Puriel.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cShe is something of a loose cannon, it seems like.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack took a drink. \u201cOur theory is that her task is to hide something and her interpretation of the best way to do that is to draw attention to everything else.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI...\u201d I paused. \u201cI can\u2019t fault her for that logic. I\u2019m sure the other Guardians in the area can, but I sure as hell can\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> He grinned and finished his drink. \u201cThat card has a number this cover can be reached on. I\u2019ve got a number of them... covers, that is.\u201d He tilted his head and shrugged. \u201cStalking Horse, you know. And boy howdy is the one the Tower is watching send lots of messages to no one. But this one\u2019s safe, like I said.\u201d He stood to go. \u201cPleasure \u2018meeting\u2019 you.\u201d Back in English. \u201cNice to see you again.\u201d Purple Haze played him out as I went to get another drink.<br /> <br /> <br /> The text I sent inviting everyone for a drink and chat \u2018after work\u2019 found Naomi at home, putting back together a very drained Am. She promised Billy Mack his blood sample and bowed out of the drink, asking to get caught up in the morning. It found Vivian and Jack in Angela\u2019s dorm room. They\u2019d slipped into the building without even having had to use the old \u2018Oops, I forgot my key!\u2019 excuse Vivian had prepared. A quick jab from Jack as soon as Angela opened the door got them in her room, no fucking questions asked.<br /> <br /> Vivian quickly got the blood sample and implanted false memories of Angela dozing off while watching TV. She wasn\u2019t waking up until sunrise, but covering their asses still came first, so that a quick getaway was still an option.<br /> <br /> Not ones to make the least of an opportunity, they tossed the place. Two themes emerged quickly. One: Dr. Cross was goddamn persistently concerned for the girl, sending email after email and even hand fucking written letters to the extent that Angela had a half filled out report against her for stalking.<br /> <br /> Two: Dr. Cross was absolutely, cockshittingly right and Angela was bug fucking nuts. She had a goddamn photo album full of pictures of that room, including some with Zelia hanging in them. She also had pictures of her naked, sitting on or touching every single fucking piece of furniture. In addition to her birthday suit, she had records of exactly which clothes she\u2019d worn in there. She\u2019d even done research into whatever fucking deities might be inhabiting the goddamn place.<br /> <br /> There were a couple of other things - Cassandra emailed her about a new font of inspiration and a special initiation, so either Naomi and Jared move fast or they need to move faster. She\u2019d noticed Dr. Stein keeping an eye on her and commented about it to a number of people using G-chat. But nothing too suspicious, besides the bug fuckery.<br /> <br /> By mutual agreement, Vivian pocketed Angela\u2019s necklace, the one with the key to the Asbury Room. With luck, my rivets would hold, but no sense in making it any easier than it had to be. After putting everything back in its proper place, they slipped into the hallway.<br /> <br /> Their actions were mirrored by a girl across the hall. As she closed the door behind her, she stared at the pair coming from Angela\u2019s room. Her eyes were fucking intense and she smirked, a little, as she walked past them into a room with three other girls watching the Legend of Korra.<br /> <br /> A quick fucking glance at the room she came from, and the presumption that it was hers revealed that her name was Heather Knight. At least, she didn\u2019t look like a Catalina Martinez.<br /> <br /> Vivian raised an eyebrow and muttered to Jack. \u201cShe\u2019s a pyromaniac and sadist who feels guilty about something, possibly her aspiration to destroy something beautiful.\u201d Jack glanced over at her, and Heather looked right the fuck back at him, meeting his eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan we help you?\u201d one of the girls asked, eyeing the pair loitering in the hallway.<br /> <br /> Jack looked lost. \u201cYeah. I was looking for Heather, Heather Knight?\u201d<br /> <br /> Heather spoke up. \u201cThat\u2019s me. Need something?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI think we might.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs there a problem?\u201d She didn\u2019t move.<br /> <br /> Vivian shrugged. \u201cIt\u2019s just probably something not best spoken about in front of everyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heather raised an eyebrow. \u201cAnd I think it\u2019s best not to leave with strangers.\u201d She emphasized \u2018best\u2019 and locked fucking eyes with Vivian.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s smart.\u201d Vivian smiled. \u201cMaybe just in the hallway?\u201d<br /> <br /> The small dirty blonde girl stood up. \u201cAlright.\u201d She moved out into the hallway, just far enough to not be overheard but still in sight of her friends. She crossed her arms. \u201cSo what do you want?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs there anything you want to tell us?\u201d Jack asked.<br /> <br /> She frowned. \u201cI\u2019m not the one who just came from a girl\u2019s room.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cActually...\u201d Jack smiled conspiratorially.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, but I came from mine.\u201d She rolled her eyes.<br /> <br /> Vivian indicated the goddamn room where Legend of Korra was still playing. \u201cNo, that one. The one that has someone in it you want to hurt.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heather smirked. \u201cDon\u2019t we all have someone like that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust try not to set her on fire.\u201d Vivian quipped.<br /> <br /> Heather frowned. \u201cLook, I get it. You\u2019re coming after me cause I saw something I shouldn\u2019t have. Why don\u2019t you just go, and I won\u2019t tell the campus authorities you were in Angela and Am\u2019s room?\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian chuckled. \u201cNo. We\u2019re talking because of your fondness for fire, your intense desire to hurt someone and that delicious feeling of guilt.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever.\u201d Heather scowled at her. \u201cLook. I won\u2019t tell, whatever. If you don\u2019t have any more random insinuations?\u201d She looked at both of them. \u201cFine.\u201d She walked back to her friend\u2019s room, a tight smile on her face. \u201cThey were just mistaken about something,\u201d she responded to an unheard question.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Deanna-<br /> <br /> Sending an email out as I won\u2019t be around right after class tomorrow.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve extracted some data from my time with Am. Hopefully will be useful after I pass it on to Billy Mack. He has some theories regarding her and Angela he wants to look into. More info when/if they look like they are true.<br /> <br /> Also, anything with the Asbury family is bad juju. I recommend avoiding anything with the name or having to do with it. I will explain later. Be careful.<br /> <br /> C Ya Babe!<br /> <br /> -Naomi<br /> <br /> o o o o<br /> <br /> Kayla,<br /> <br /> Sorry to email, but I needed to pass on some info and did not want to risk waking my dinner. She is still a bit fragile atm.<br /> <br /> Speed met a member of the Fools. Stalking Horse is his name and raison d'etre. There is also a Ms. Clocks. Don\u2019t know too much yet beyond Stalking Horse seems stable.<br /> <br /> There are two Abyssal Intrusions in Seattle. One is at the heart of the school we are investigating, under the Asbury room. The suicide may be to fuel it. Or a result of a human going crazy after exposure. The other is the house of the doners, more messed up but not growing. At this point, we are going to try to deal with it and not bring the ex-Boss\u2019s attention, but that\u2019s not totally off the board. Checking up to see how bad it is spread on Campus. We are looking at a few students and a couple faculty, will keep you updated.<br /> <br /> I will tell you more after some tests, but for now avoid University and Asbury house. All the campus, preferably. Once we have a little time, assuming Kilroy does not fuck anything they shouldn\u2019t and Quietus does not pick a fight with anything he shouldn\u2019t, we will be good.<br /> <br /> Stay safe sweetie. I miss talking to you. I don\u2019t, of course, need to tell you to delete this after you read it.<br /> <br /> Liz<br /> <br /> XOXO<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XVIII</i><br /> <br /> And here the <b>Beast</b> rules came out only one session too late<br /> <br /> The Fools name, for those who enjoy such references, come from their willingness to go where Angels fear to tread. Also, for the record, I was kinda proud of Stalking Horse\u2019s concept.<br /> <br /> Obviously, most of the session was dealing with the Abyssal Intrusion for Quietus and Kilroy. If Abyssal Intrusions sound like gibberish to you, look at <i>Summoners</i> and <i>Intruders</i> for <b>Mage: The Awakening.</b><br /> <br /> Most people would recognize the reference to <i>People are Strange</i> by the Doors and <i>Purple Haze</i> by Hendrix, but in Case you are not up on your <i>real</i> Oldies, here is <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nhmso6QmTiQ\" target=\"_blank\">Alice Blue Gown</a> performed by Edith Day. I have now made that song creepy for you.<br /> <br /> Thanks as always for reading, comments and questions welcome.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T14:14:24-07:00","id":562218,"title":"","content":"Still on the case, Quietus and Kilroy burgle some Ether while Speed meets a mysterious stranger.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Vivian was the only one who took me up on that drink, after swinging by Naomi\u2019s to get the blood sample. We filled each other in, had a few drinks then split off again, for more goddamn research, me and the fucking university library and Vivian at our lab.<br /> <br /> The next morning, if you wanted to be fucking gracious about it, we all gathered again. Well, me, Liz and Billy Mack did. I filled our butter and egg woman in on what went down in Kiki\u2019s, then started on my research.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, turns out our time line was completely fucked. The shit in the Asbury Room has been in there, every goddamn piece, since 1964. The bodies you found in the goddamn house may or may not be the 4 thought-to-be-living Asburys - there were 4 suicides in the family in the month just fucking before the donation.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack interrupted. \u201cDid you get names for them?\u201d<br /> <br /> I stared at him silently until just past the point of goddamn comfort. \u201cNo, I got my investigator\u2019s license from a goddamn Crackerjack box. Yes, I got their fucking names. The rest of the stuff about the family is the shit we got before. But there was yet another suicide connected to the room, back in 64, right after the fucking thing was moved in there. A member of the grounds keeping staff.\u201d I sneered at the g-man. \u201cAnd no, I didn\u2019t get his name. Cause not a single goddamn one of the records had it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cInteresting...\u201d Billy Mack mused.<br /> <br /> I leaned back in my chair. \u201cMaybe it\u2019s a cover up. Or, and I\u2019d toss this softball to Jack if he were here, maybe he was black in the sixties and the KKK that runs Seattle didn\u2019t give two shits what the fuck his name was. There\u2019s a gee in the history department, a Dr Schultz, that was faculty at the time. I figure we\u2019ll have a chat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat does sound like a worthwhile lead to follow up.\u201d Billy Mack nodded, and filled Liz in on the goddamn house and their fucking foray into Angela\u2019s room. \u201cAnd then... do you know a Heather Knight?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. She\u2019s a friend of Angela\u2019s, de facto head of the mean girls clique. A lot of girls are afraid of her, honestly.\u201d Liz fiddled with Naomi\u2019s phone, frowning.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cWith cause, perhaps, as she is a sadistic pyromaniac with strong feelings of guilt and an intense desire to destroy something beautiful.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz raised an eyebrow. \u201cI knew she turned me on for some reason. I thought it was her tits.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI bring her up because she saw us leave Angela\u2019s room and so Jack approached her...\u201d Billy Mack began.<br /> <br /> Liz put a hand to her mouth and looked at Billy Mack goddamn beseechingly. \u201cTell me he didn\u2019t do anything stupid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI could tell you that, if you like.\u201d Billy Mack offered seriously.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat man is good for two things. one is fighting and the other is not sweet talking.\u201d Liz sighed. \u201cI\u2019ll do some damage control as Naomi, see what I can do to mitigate this.\u201d She glanced at the fucking phone. \u201cSome serious damage control.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put down the bottle I\u2019d been nursing. \u201cShit get connected to you already?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomewhat.\u201d Liz said distractedly, typing on her phone. \u201cAngela is freaking out - short lived stabbing spree, getting sent to solitary and responding to all conversation with screaming level freaking out, and all because her necklace is missing. Heather has told Cassandra that she knows who took it.\u201d She smirked and her eyes sparkled for a moment. \u201cCassandra would just as soon she didn\u2019t have it, provided she calms down, but Am wants her new mistress to conjure up a new one. I do believe I\u2019ve thoroughly broken the girl.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked fucking concerned. \u201cBe careful - she may be habit forming.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked between the two of them. \u201cThe hell?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHer... blood, and well, flesh, tastes very good.\u201d Liz smiled guiltily.<br /> <br /> \u201cFurther, it appears to have been engineered that way, into a super food essentially. If you got Aether from consuming her, you would likely have gotten more than usual. Vampires and werewolves certainly would. And consuming only her flesh and blood would provide you with a nutritionally complete diet. Not a sustainable one but...\u201d He shrugged.<br /> <br /> Liz looked thoughtful. \u201cThe Aether cost would be prohibitive.\u201d She got lost in that fucking thought momentarily. Anyway, do you know why? Any other tests you need? I could get her to wherever - I could tell her to walk to University Bridge naked and she would.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI had thought Changeling, perhaps, so it might be useful to have her out where Crusher or Rosanna could looked for us. Nakedness would not be necessary.\u201d The g-man didn\u2019t respond to my leer.<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you checked her background yet? There might be some flags there, if she is a Changeling.\u201d Liz lit her cigarette and fidgeted with its holder.<br /> <br /> I played a game or two of trashcan basketball with myself while Billy Mack looked at the computer. \u201cLooks like we won\u2019t need to call Crusher or Rosanna after all.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz moved quickly to his side. \u201cYou found something? Team Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine?\u201d she read the highlighted line off the screen.<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cI didn\u2019t find anything out of place until I tried her middle name. C. Andrea Quinn had a moment of fame when she was 7, after an experimental treatment cured her of leukemia. It was administered by Team Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine, who is currently operating on some land owned by a Lee Potts, in E. Seattle. They have absolutely no web presence, not have they published academic papers concerning their apparent success stories.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think the only way that could sound more like the God Machine is if you turned it over and found Puriel\u2019s hand up its ass. But... why make someone delicious?\u201d Liz licked her lips.<br /> <br /> \u201cUnavoidable side effect?\u201d The g-man offered. \u201cIf this is the cause, we should definitely get a sample of her bone marrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat tasted good too. I\u2019ve never eaten someone's marrow before.\u201d Liz looked goddamn sheepish. \u201cI just couldn\u2019t stop though. Why design that? It wasn\u2019t poisonous, no one came after me, my powers worked fine... I\u2019ve never done that before though, or eaten internal organs. It took all I had...\u201d<br /> <br /> I interrupted. \u201cWhoa, whoa, whoa, dial it the fuck back -\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack was way too fucking calm about it. \u201cThat last one. Is she missing an organ?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Liz shook her head and fidgeted with her cigarette holder. \u201cShe\u2019s perfectly healed. It was just a lung and some small intestine, anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well then.\u201d The fucker fucking left it at that. \u201cAs to your question, it could potentially be a trap for werewolves? Perhaps something would have been triggered if you\u2019d consumed her completely, or were gaining energy from it.\u201d Billy Mack mused.<br /> <br /> \u201cIsn\u2019t it against their religion to eat people though?\u201d Liz asked.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cA trap to make the fuckers break the goddamn rules then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s possible.\u201d Liz shook her head to clear it. \u201cWell, I'm not a detective, but I fucked one once. It seems like there are two ways to get at this Team Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine - I could go in as a potential investor which might get us further safer, but could tip our hand. Or we could break in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI favor taking an outside look at the place before deciding. At the least, I should be able to tell if it is Infrastructure fairly easily. Then we can decide the best way to get inside.\u201d Billy Mack turned back to us from his computer.<br /> <br /> \u201cWanna give Jack a call and get him as fucking back up while we hit campus?\u201d I indicated Liz with a jerk of my head. \u201cWell, me and Naomi hit up campus.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shook his head. \u201cI think we should have as wide a range of capabilities as possible for that, not to mention more Aether and the cover of darkness. I was going to call him in as back up for a foray into Peterson Chemical though.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stood up, stretched and grabbed my fucking hat. \u201cSounds like a fucking plan to me.<br /> <br /> \u201cBefore you leave though,\u201d Billy Mack stopped us, \u201cthere was something in Angela\u2019s blood and she had it in common with Zelia. Nothing with Cassandra\u2019s blood.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd the something was...?\u201d I leaned against the wall.<br /> <br /> He got his results out and held them out. I grabbed them and gave them a fucking look see. \u201cElevated white blood count. As if they were fighting off some sort of infection.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell at least we have something to check.\u201d I shrugged and handed the goddamn r