rd was out about the fucking riveted door, I stopped by to check up on it. The rivets were still in place, so either no one had been by and noticed it, or whoever did didn\u2019t mind having the goddamn creepy fucking place sealed off. Most importantly,the goddamn Abyssal bastard didn't have a quick way to destroy the rivets or some shit. A quick glance satisfied me on that front, and I made my way to the history building.<br /> <br /> Dr. Schultz was a professor emeritus in the history department, so it was even fucking odds if he was in today at all. Luck was a goddamn lady, as I found office 104 occupied by a crotchety old man yelling into his office phone. \u201cKids like you, Dr. Stein, kids like you are messing things up. You\u2019re distracting the students with this nonsense about the room... are you there?\u201d He got louder. I wouldn\u2019t have bet on it being fucking possible, lucky streak or not. \u201cIn my day, people respected their elders... Did I ask you about the room? Kids like you are messing things up, distracting the students... are you there?\u201d Apparently Dr. Stein responded loud enough he could actually hear. \u201cOh, I\u2019m sorry. Carry on then, carry on.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stepped into the doorway and knocked on the frame as he hung up the phone. Aura Sight showed he was just as goddamn cantankerous as he sounded, but not supernatural. I played it polite and fucking respectful, and pitched my voice loud enough he could hear, but not so loud he\u2019d feel I was yelling at him. \u201cDr. Schultz?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked up at me. \u201cEh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy name is Gabe Norton. I\u2019m a private investigator, looking into some recent incidents on campus.\u201d I handed him a card. \u201cThough I was actually hoping to talk to you about some history, of the Asbury Room specifically.\u201d<br /> <br /> He took my card and studied it goddamn intently. \u201cIt was all donated by a bunch of bourgeois. Think they own the place, they do.\u201d He turned the card over, continuing his examination. \u201cThat\u2019s a very nice card. It\u2019s good women have cards now.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cAh, thanks. So, I was looking into it and noticed there had been another suicide in the room, shortly after the, uh, bourgeois donated the stuff.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. It was one of the groundskeepers, a colored boy. A real shame the way people reacted.\u201d He stared off into fucking space a bit, lost in thought, or maybe memories.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you remember his name? It\u2019s not in any of the records I could find.\u201d I prodded as gently as I fucking could.<br /> <br /> He looked at me, nodding matter of factly. \u201cIt\u2019s because he was colored.\u201d He narrowed his eyes, thinking hard. \u201cI can\u2019t recall. It was one of those colored name though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cChartreuse?\u201d I muttered under my fucking breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cEh? Speak up.\u201d He peered at me.<br /> <br /> I coughed. \u201cSorry, just talking to myself. Bad habit.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked suspicious. \u201cWell ever since, students keep going there to rebel against it with their long hair and their rock and roll cults.\u201d<br /> <br /> The name is what I really fucking wanted, and he wasn\u2019t going to be able to bring it out consciously. Talking and picking through people\u2019s brains is the goddamn master level of walking and chewing gum, and I haven\u2019t quite picked it up yet. So I made my excuses to Dr. Schultz, and still within eyesight. I started fiddling with my phone with an eye on the old bastard.<br /> <br /> After a second I had to stop myself from laughing. What kind of goddamn jackass thinks Daniel Thompson is \u2018one of those colored names\u2019? At least the memory was there and fairly simple to fucking dredge up. I spent another minute or two checking for any extra context without much to fucking show for it other than that Dr. Schultz was a halfway alright gee, colored names aside. He wasn\u2019t friends or anything with Daniel, but he was decent to the goddamn grounds crew, particularly after he noticed his peers being douchebags to them.<br /> <br /> I snapped out of it to head to the library to look into one Daniel Thompson, deceased. Turning to go, I almost ran into as pretty a doll as I\u2019d seen in a minute. She was a blonde, the kind to make a saint cry. She was 5 foot 6 of pure trouble, written all over her lips red enough to write a fairy tale about. Her pale skin contrasted with her old fashioned school uniform, a school uniform I was pretty sure they discontinued in the fucking fifties. A palpable aura of power and danger made me unsure of whether to read her her rights or ask her to marry me right then and there.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell hey there Princess -\u201d Smooth as butter.<br /> <br /> She interrupted me. \u201cYou were asking about the Asbury Room?\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow and checked her aura. Definitely supernatural. Going with stereotypes, I\u2019d have had her pegged as a vampire, but it didn\u2019t read like that. Didn\u2019t read like anything I\u2019d seen. \u201cI was. I\u2019m Gabe, Gabe Norton. I\u2019m a private investigator, looking into the recent weird events centered around that room.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you need to know?\u201d The hallway was still and quiet. Even Dr. Schultz\u2019 cantankerous mutterings seemed fucking muted.<br /> <br /> \u201cJesus, where do I fucking start?\u201d I thought for a moment. \u201cKnow anything about the weird fixation thing?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded gravely. \u201cThere is a powerful force in that room. It infects some people, which leads to this fixation.\u201d<br /> <br /> Something was bothering me and I needed to move. \u201cMind if we walk and talk?\u201d I indicated the hallway out.<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well. I\u2019ll meet you outside.\u201d She rounded a corner and her footsteps stopped immediately.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow and took a different route to the door, giving her her privacy. Outside was also still, without a single student in sight. \u201cIt always this quiet at two in the afternoon?\u201d She shrugged. \u201cRight. So, do you know of anyone who is infected?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat you don\u2019t, you mean?\u201d It was my turn to shrug. \u201cChina, perhaps. Angela is, definitely. Dr. Cross is, I believe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou a friend of Angela\u2019s?\u201d I got a coin out and started flipping it.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Her answer was definitive and short.<br /> <br /> I rolled my shoulders back and cracked my neck. \u201cLook sweetheart. Me and my people, we\u2019re looking to fix this problem. Anything you got that could help with that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow do you plan on fixing it?\u201d She kept her gaze on my face, looking me in the eye.<br /> <br /> I brushed my hair back from my face. \u201cThat\u2019s complicated.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled slightly. \u201cYou don\u2019t trust me. That\u2019s for the best probably. Too much trust is how this all started.\u201d<br /> <br /> I got caught imagining what her lips would look like with a full smile, and what it would do to her eyes. \u201cOh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe university didn\u2019t think to question why the Asburys might be so eager to get rid of such a collection.\u201d Her eyes were dark.<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough. Do you know much about the Asburys then, like, say, where the supposedly surviving ones are?\u201d I smiled at her, walking the coin over my fingers.<br /> <br /> She looked sad. Slightly, the way she looked any emotion. \u201cOne tried to get away, but didn\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> Slight or not, I winced inwardly. \u201cThe one that went to New York? Miranda, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d She was definitely a woman of few words.<br /> <br /> I kept pushing. \u201cDo you know where she is now?\u201d<br /> <br /> She paused, looking away. She seemed to steel herself and looked back at me. \u201cHere.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled and nodded. \u201cNice to meet you Miranda.\u201d I sighed. \u201cWell that was a bit of trust, so here's some back. We have access to something like, well, reality spackle, for the hole in reality that this powerful force has rotted out. We\u2019re kinda hoping that will provoke it into a form we can fucking deal with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI could possibly distract or goad it further as well,\u201d she offered, still serious and sad.<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds handy, as does your inside knowledge. There a way I can get in touch with you, to let you know if we need some help?\u201d I crossed my arms, leaning back against a tree.<br /> <br /> She gave me a number. \u201cThat reaches the dorm phone in Roland Hall room 125 from an off campus phone. It\u2019s safe to leave messages on the answering machine as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood deal sweetheart.\u201d A stray thought struck me and I chuckled. \u201cBefore I bug you more about your tragic past and all, I guess I oughta pay lip service to my nominal case. Do you have any idea why the whole goddamn campus blacked out for an hour after Zelia offed herself?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked intrigued, if fucking distantly. \u201cThe entity would have gained a measure of energy from the death. It was likely a backlash from the release of said energy, a side effect.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Princess. How\u2019d this all get started? It had something to do with Alice, right?\u201d I kept up eye contact with a sympathetic half smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes... Alice. She... she\u2019ll probably have to be dealt with as well. She was getting darker, tainted, before I escaped.\u201d She sighed. \u201cThe deal was a life for a life. But it kept coming up with reasons for more deaths - two for a child, and so on. Leo wound up trapped in a mirror and...\u201d She took a breath. \u201cIt was in a vase, originally. I\u2019m pretty sure at this point it\u2019s suffused through the entire Room though.\u201d She looked me in the eyes again. \u201cI\u2019m... clearly not well. I think Angela is meant to be my replacement. It is likely trying to get her pregnant. Dynasties and bloodlines are a big things to it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you know why it would choose Angela? Does she have any powers or traits that drew it?\u201d I let the past lie. That was enough story to paint a gruesome enough picture.<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cThe infection could give her powers though.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. The dame was as tight lipped as she was easy on the eyes. She implied more than she said and didn\u2019t say a lot. To be fair, my glass house was looking awfully breakable. \u201cWhat about you, beautiful? What\u2019s your deal? And to lay everything on the table, the corner blocked my eyes, not my ears. The whole no footsteps things is a damn neat trick.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI would rather not go into detail. But everything I have, I\u2019ve thrown at the intruder.\u201d She held my gaze goddamn proudly.<br /> <br /> I gave her a lopsided grin. \u201cThat lack of trust again, huh sweetheart?\u201d<br /> <br /> She tilted her head and paused, considering. \u201cI am glad you like my appearance. Yes. I hope that we can work together against the entity. But after... I don\u2019t know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I for one hope you don\u2019t wind up going too wild and can stick around for a bit.\u201d I smirked at her.<br /> <br /> Her brow knit. \u201cI don\u2019t... I don\u2019t go wild.\u201d<br /> <br /> My grin widened. \u201cNot even a little?\u201d<br /> <br /> She stared at me a moment, then some clarity crossed her face. \u201cYou are using some slang that I don\u2019t know?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I guess so.\u201d I raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re coming on to me then?\u201d She raised an eyebrow back.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cYeah, I guess I am.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled somewhat, not unkindly. \u201cI think a sexual relationship would compromise our efforts.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen I really hope you stick around a bit after.\u201d I pushed myself up off the tree and stretched. \u201cWell, I should get back to and fill in my people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well.\u201d She paused. \u201cOh, was it you who visited my family house?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot me personally. Friends of mine.\u201d She didn\u2019t seem upset by the intrusion.<br /> <br /> \u201cConvey my apologies then, that we did not have it prepared for guests?\u201d I nodded. She walked up to me and kissed me on the cheek. She smelled nice, like an autumn breeze through an flowering honeysuckle vine.<br /> <br /> Then she walked past me and it was like flipping a goddamn switch. The previous still and empty paths were as full as I would expect them to be, two pm on a fucking school day. The hustle and bustle flowed past me as I stood a little stunned for a moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back at the agency, I filled the others in on what the hell I\u2019d learned. Naomi\u2019s eyes lit the fuck up. \u201cIf that\u2019s a phone number to reach her, she\u2019s probably staying in that room. You should totally show up tonight with a bottle of wine.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stared at her. \u201cThe fuck, woman?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll need to change.\u201d She leaned over towards me and fucking sniffed. \u201cAnd a shower. And some makeup. When she looked at you, did she go for the soft?\u201d She waved her hands at my chest. \u201cOr the hard?\u201d She sketched the outline of my biceps.<br /> <br /> My stare turned into a glare. \u201cMy eyes, mostly.\u201d<br /> <br /> She tapped her lip. \u201cI can work with that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s no \u2018working\u2019 with anything.\u201d I gave her a warning look and changed the goddamn subject. \u201cAnyway, what happened with Heather?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi smirked. \u201cWell, she isn't going to hunt either of those two for punishment. Thanks to me, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned. \u201cThat\u2019s odd language.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYup!\u201d She seemed fucking gleeful. \u201cShe\u2019s something supernatural - she can conjure fire...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUseful for a pyromaniac.\u201d I interrupted.<br /> <br /> She smirked at me again. \u201c...and could tell something hinky was up with Vivian, that she could be punished for something but weird.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf Heather\u2019s big on this punishing thing, maybe Am is bait she set?\u201d Jack threw out there. \u201cBilly Mack filled me in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe did have something of a feral grin when talking about Am. Wolfish I might say. I might not.\u201d Naomi\u2019s grin wasn\u2019t far from feral itself. She sighed. \u201cIt is such hard work twisting people around you little finger. You -\u201d she pointed at me, \u201cshould be glad you don't socialize.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a drink. \u201cYou\u2019re a fucking bitch, you know that?\u201d<br /> <br /> She put a hand over her heart. \u201cI\u2019m just trying to get you tail. It\u2019ll work, I promise. Aggressive women are hot.\u201d Jack rolled his eyes. She narrowed hers at him. \u201cOh right, I forget, fainting couches and petticoats only for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou couldn\u2019t get within 10 yards of a petticoat without retching.\u201d Jack grinned at her.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cDepends on what\u2019s in it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOn a business note, we should probably get blood samples from Dr. Cross and Miranda, to see if they are infected. And we need bloodstained pieces of five different cars involved in someone\u2019s death.\u201d Naomi and I both turned to look at the g-man. He looked mostly at Naomi. \u201cThe most difficult to acquire material for the reality spackle. We\u2019ll need some precious metals as well and a few other things that are easily acquired with enough funds.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi sighed. \u201cSo Liz gets to buy a bunch of crap, and to have a romantic outing to a junkyard with Robin. Her lucky day. I can get Dr. Cross\u2019 blood. Or Liz. Maybe Liz would be best.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack snorted. \u201cFrom what I saw, Liz would definitely be best.\u201d<br /> <br /> She glared at him, then brightened. \u201cAnd Gabe can get Miranda\u2019s!\u201d She turned to me. \u201cSo once you seduce her and you know, develop a close emotional attachment, you can figure out whether we\u2019ll have to kill her to stop the infection spreading.\u201d I crossed my arms. \u201cSee, after, when you\u2019re cuddling, you do a little nibbling, then quick with the needle, then some more nibbling. They can\u2019t tell a bit of difference.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks for the tip?\u201d I went back to drinking.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou could always just ask her for it.\u201d Billy Mack offered. \u201cAnd say that you\u2019ll put it in a pendant to represent the eternal nature of your relationship.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi laughed. \u201cYou do have this lesbian thing down, Billy Mack.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Later that evening, I rolled my chair past Liz\u2019s office. \u201cSo, Liz, now that you\u2019re less of a bitch, any actual advice with the whole Miranda thing? She\u2019s a classier broad than my usual, and she\u2019s bound to be trouble, but...\u201d I let it hang.<br /> <br /> She chuckled. \u201cI am less of a bitch like this, aren\u2019t I?\u201d She looked at me thoughtfully. \u201cNaomi did have some good points - the wine,the shower and... you do have an unwrinkled suit?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI... have an iron. I think.\u201d I brushed my hair back.<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t laugh or even raise an eyebrow. She should give herself a goddamn bonus. \u201cAs for the rest, are you planning on some fun for a night, or more of a long term fling?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can handle just having some fucking fun for a night without asking for advice.\u201d I shrugged. \u201cUsually.\u201d<br /> <br /> She thought for a moment. \u201cIn that case, forget the wine, for now \u2013 you don't want to make like you need it to make friends, or that you're trying to get her drunk. And call first. Show up, show interest, do not show vulnerability. Don\u2019t make any plays unless she shows interest herself. Keep that butch charm up. And Gabe?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah?\u201d I rested my chin on the back of the chair.<br /> <br /> \u201cTry saying fuck maybe only every sixth or so word?\u201d<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> So I promised you an update on the whole Abyssal Intrusion thing, Darling, and I have one. Apparently a member of the Asbury family decided to make herself known\u2026though the whole thing is rather queer. Speed had been checking to be sure the door to the Asbury room was still riveted shut and was just talking to a professor when she appeared in the hallway. At least, Speed did not hear her approach. There was a whole rigmarole and playing coy, but the end result was she was the surviving Asbury who went to New York, but looked to be around twenty and was wearing one of the old uniforms the University had people wear back in the dark ages.<br /> <br /> Not literal dark ages, of course.<br /> <br /> While she was not very direct, she essentially said the family had been tricked into assisting the entity, which she said nothing really about being it was in a vase or urn or something, allegedly so it would restore their lost daughter Alice. It did not succeed, but they made it stronger, until they decided to shunt it to the University and save themselves. Yes, she was (I think) among those who decided to do this. But now she wants to fight the entity.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t trust her a bit.<br /> <br /> This is complicated by the fact Speed seems to be falling for her. It would be nice to see something happen to Speed to make her happy beyond more booze, but I hope she is careful.<br /> <br /> Other thing came up, unrelated as far as I know. Remember me mentioning Am, that I was going to bring into my cult as Naomi? Well everything went smooth till I decided to feed. She was tasty. Too tasty. I drank my fill, but after healing some went back for more. Then blood was not enough and I started eating her flesh and bones and organs. I barely stopped myself. Frankly, I\u2019ve been craving her meat all day, though I managed to have a brief conversation where I did not try to bite her.<br /> <br /> Having real concerns\u2026yes\u2026having real concerns about this turn of events, Kilroy did some research and found out she had Leukemia when very young and went to a local facility called \u201cTeam Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine\u201d which apparently cured her completely. While some news stories covered her and some other patients, Team Tomorrow has no web presence, and no mention in medical journals. We, of course, intend to investigate.<br /> <br /> Know anything about them?<br /> <br /> Awwww you are jealous. Sweetheart, you are my number one!<br /> <br /> My thought was she is some sort of honeytrap. But I am not sure the trigger. According to Kilory she would be more dangerous to a Werewolf or Vampire than to one of us, but who knows? The answers likely lie in TTCM.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t appreciate being caught in anyone\u2019s honeytrap though.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s where we stand now. What is new with you?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XIX</i><br /> <br /> The Chartreuse line, which stopped the game for a few minutes as we all recovered, was delivered by Kilroy\u2019s player. Given Kilroy was not present, Speed\u2019s player attributed it to her as it fit the narrative well.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add. Jack\u2019s player had to Skype in again but it worked out okay. Not as much fun as having him physically there but much better than having him absent.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add, but if you have Comments or Questions they are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T01:49:42-07:00","id":579645,"title":"","content":"Okay Session 20 is here. This time it is Speed and Jack commenting.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Sometime between me talking to her and the meet up time for our fucking stake out of Team Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine, Liz had changed into a little black number that hugged her in all the right places, tight enough to make a goddamn saint jealous. Jack spoke up first. \u201cGoddamn, woman.\u201d<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow. \u201cCorrect in one. I am, in fact, a goddamn woman.\u201d She looked down at herself, running her fucking hands down her side. \u201cI figure if someone sees me, they\u2019ll be a little distracted.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a unanimous \u201cuh-huh\u201d but the desire in Jack\u2019s eyes was a touch sharper and there was a goddamn determination that wasn\u2019t there before. I might be projecting, but I do believe our fixer has sets his sights way the hell outside his fucking league. I wish him luck - surely there\u2019s enough of the shit to go around for both of us.<br /> <br /> The Team Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine building was a nearly featureless white box, two stories tall. A single door was the only way in or out, without a single window or side door to be fucking found. A schluby gee stood in front of it, with a motherfucker of a dog. It had the build of a fucking doberman and was as tall in the shoulder as a goddamn greyhound. I popped my sensors to see exactly what the shit-flinging hell we were dealing with.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, neither of them are fucking supernatural...\u201d I began.<br /> <br /> \u201cBullshit.\u201d Jack eyed the dog.<br /> <br /> I smirked at him. \u201cI\u2019d say that was all science, Jacky boy. Some kind of dog-bug hybrid thing - it\u2019s got a hive mind, or some shit. Still guessing, the poor bastard there is around for his opposable thumbs. He can\u2019t be an effective partner with how terrified he is of the dog.\u201d I grimaced. \u201cHe\u2019s not around for his goddamn cunning intellect either. He\u2019s thinking way too much about fucking his high school aged daughter\u2019s friend for that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAt least it\u2019s her friend and not her?\u201d Liz offered.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cBonus points?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cBaby steps. An entirely different concept.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough.\u201d I shrugged. \u201cLemme see if I can find a memory of the inside of the fucking place.\u201d It was easy to find, the work of a moment. Naturally, this meant it was nearly fucking useless. On his orientation tour, this intellectual goddamn giant of a retired bull dismissed almost everything in the facility as \u2018eggheads doing genetic stuff\u2019. There was a mental note that nothing seemed illegal and I did have to agree with him that the eight dogs turning to look at you in fucking unison was goddamn creepy.<br /> <br /> While I was poking around, the others debated plans to get fucking eyes in there. We finally settled on Billy Mack doing some possession hopping, to get as far in as possible, so the rest of us settled in to wait. After a few minutes, the door guard came back out. A little while after that, Billy Mack\u2019s abandoned burner phone rang. At the same time, the goddamn bug dog started looking at the door and growling.<br /> <br /> Liz answered the phone in the g-man\u2019s voice. \u201cHello?\u201d<br /> <br /> After the first word, she put the fucking thing on speaker. \u201c- locked myself into the server closet. This has made the dogs suspicious.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo that would be why the fucker out here is herding the guard to the door?\u201d I asked Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> He made a considering noise. \u201cHe does have, as you said, opposable thumbs. There were some records on the guards computer, as well as a witness.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack stopped him. \u201cWait, what?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe guard was conversing with someone on Chat Roulette when I possessed him. She\u2019s rather pretty. The server here has much more extensive records, including detailed current surveillance on Am.\u201d We could faintly hear a slam as the fucker paused. \u201cI don\u2019t think I have time for what I need to do. I\u2019m going to pull the hard drive and try and make it out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack had a hard smile on his face. \u201cThat security guard you\u2019re in...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBenson.\u201d There was another crash on the other side of the phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cBenson.\u201d Jack rolled his eyes. \u201cHe has a walkie talkie right? Why not call in back up?\u201d<br /> <br /> The door guard picked up his own walkie talkie and spoke into it. I got a brief read of \u2018I knew it\u2019 from his surface thoughts before he fucking turned on the dog that was outside. It took a couple of shots to put the goddamn thing down, and I lost the thread of his thoughts as he went inside.<br /> <br /> A few moments later, Billy Mack burst out of the white building and slammed the door. He straightened his fucking tie and brushed his goddamn jacket off before walking calmly to where we were waiting. Once he got in the car, he said \u201cOn the plus side, his daughter\u2019s friend won\u2019t have to worry about getting creeped on ever again.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed and started the car up. \u201cFind any interesting shit at least?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMost of the interesting things were behind a door, locked by a key and a punch card, that also requires a recognized voice print and a retina check, none of which the night guards can get past. I did find that Carla Pierce had some work done right after she was hired by Sanderson. And Stein did as well, back when he worked on the force. Am had three treatments, Pierce one and Stein 4. Pierce\u2019s one is the same as one of Stein\u2019s, but otherwise there\u2019s no overlap.\u201d Billy Mack was distracted, looking like he was doing some calculations in his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat treatment?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> He shook his head. \u201cI don\u2019t know. They were referred to by code.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo is the key to the code in that hard drive you mentioned?\u201d I prodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know. Perhaps. I had wanted it largely as it had surveillance data for Am on it and password protected files on Pierce and Stein.\u201d He looked mildly frustrated. \u201cIt\u2019s still on Benson.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked fucking concerned. \u201cGiven all that, it really does seem like Am is bait.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cI\u2019m sure they\u2019d love to get some werewolf DNA. Then those bug-dogs wouldn\u2019t need human keepers to open doors.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey were already smart enough to know that the server closet plus shut door equals bad.\u201d Liz shuddered.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd to use tools. They started throwing the monitor at the door.\u201d Billy Mack said in response to our questioning looks.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut... back to Am.\u201d Liz looked to Billy Mack. \u201cI could maybe talk to her about the whole deal, see what she remembers, but if she\u2019s being surveilled...\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cSurely it\u2019s not like a goddamn wire or something. Just don\u2019t talk with her in her fucking room. Or in public.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t moment by moment, just things like her dorm room, roommate, year in school, class schedule, etc.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked relieved. \u201cAnd no ping or anything from when I fed on her?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot in those records.\u201d Billy Mack confirmed.<br /> <br /> \u201cLovely. More immediately, what are our plans for the goddamn facility?\u201d I checked the mirror, and started getting us closer to the agency.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked goddamn pensive. \u201cI was running the numbers. I could probably just barely make a powerful enough explosive to get through the security door in time to hit it tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell then.\u201d I went for a more direct route to the office. \u201cI do agree, if we\u2019re going in, it\u2019s gotta be fucking tonight or in a long goddamn while. But...\u201d I looked at Jack. \u201cKnow any grenade shops?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked back incredulously. \u201cThat turn around in...\u201d He checked his watch. \u201cFive hours? No.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t like this time table. How \u2018bout you cook up some goddamn sleeping gas or some shit for the dogs instead, and we just go for the fucking hard drive?\u201d I gave Billy Mack a look.<br /> <br /> The fucker sighed. \u201cThat does seem reasonable.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can produce tones pitched high enough to hurt the dogs and not affect us. That way we wouldn\u2019t even need to leave chemical traces.\u201d Liz offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cDone.\u201d I turned to head back to east Seattle.<br /> <br /> Jack got a fucking gleam in his goddamn eye. \u201cI could EMP the lab, since we won\u2019t get to go in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd let out the flesh eating kangaroo-walrus hybrids?\u201d Liz smiled at Jack to take the sting out of it. \u201cHave you never seen Jurassic Park?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> The rest of us had, so we kept it to the goddamn retrieval. It went off without a hitch. Jack opened the door, blocking it with his body, but Liz\u2019s throat and chest were already moving as if she were holding a long fucking note and the dogs cowered the hell away from her. They even went so far as to shoulder the fucking office door shut between them.<br /> <br /> The cameras were all trained on the insides of the individual rooms, so there was no fucking surveillance for the two of them to dodge. Jack handled the poor schlub\u2019s wallet carefully, with gloves and a goddamn face mask. After a glance at the bank cards and a quick pilfering of his cash, he put the wallet back and grabbed the hard drive.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, unless the dogs can talk to sketch artists, we\u2019re solidly out of the picture here, yeah?\u201d Jack started, looking around at us. I nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut there is clearly a third party.\u201d Liz pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cExactly!\u201d Jack smiled like a goddamn Cheshire cat. \u201cSo, what if, say, a large sum of money made its way into Benson\u2019s accounts? What if the money used to be in an account associated with one Michael White?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned back. \u201cLike a certain goddamn downtown laundromat, huh? I knew we kept you the fuck around for something.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful, then nodded. \u201cShould be doable, easy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI should -\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should -\u201d Liz turned to me and we spoke almost simultaneously. \u201c-call Jake and let him know?\u201d I nodded. \u201cThe Fools might be able to use the distraction.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I left Vivian to her hacking and dialed Jake\u2019s number. A woman\u2019s voice answered in Chinese. I responded in the same language. \u201cHello, ma\u2019am. I\u2019m looking for Jake. It\u2019s Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is indisposed, at the moment.\u201d She sounded somewhat apologetic.<br /> <br /> I switched to Inuit. Either this was another cover, or another Fool, and she\u2019d follow, or it was a member of his cover\u2019s circles of acquaintances and she\u2019d be very confused. \u201cCould you take a message? I have a couple of pieces of news that might interest him.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a hint of a smile in her voice, as she responded in Inuit as well. \u201cHe is in a stalking horse cover at the moment. This is Mrs. Clocks. Where would you like to meet to discuss your news?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKiki\u2019s work?\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> I could almost hear the inaudible sigh over the phone. She was fucking good. \u201cYes.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I checked if company would be acceptable and invited the others along. Me and Bobby McGee was playing over the speakers and the usual crowd of riff raff was scattered about the place, including some fucker in a goddamn bunny suit. I\u2019d seen him before, when Jack called me over to get an extra set of eyes on Vanessa. The bunny fucker stayed away then, and did now too, giving Jack a nervous look. I\u2019ll have to get the fixer a goddamn thank you card.<br /> <br /> Vivian winked at the waitress Shelley as we ordered our drinks and took them back to the table Mrs. Clocks had described. Seated at the table was a goddamn gorgeous Asian woman, legs crossed under the table and hands crossed above it.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello Gabe. I am Colleen Lung.\u201d She spoke in an obscure Chinese dialect. It was a good choice. Casual racism would have most people not batting an eye at the Asian woman speaking one of those Asian languages, and it\u2019d be a hell of a fucking coincidence if anyone could actually eavesdrop.<br /> <br /> I nodded and sat down, letting Liz, Jack and Vivian introduce themselves. \u201cTo lead in gracefully,\u201d I began, \u201cI figure the laundromat\u2019s rewiring job was you guys?\u201d She nodded gracefully. \u201cAs it turns out, it was goddamn fabulously insured.\u201d That wasn\u2019t even our doing. Vivian had discovered that while she was moving the money. Some of it was now safely tucked away in an offshore account. \u201cAnd it turns out that a chunk of that insurance money made its way into the bank account of a Team Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine security guard, who just tonight stole a hard drive before being viciously mauled by hive-minded guard bug dogs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know them. They\u2019ve stolen damaged Infrastructure from the Muck Works before. We\u2019d wondered what they were about.\u201d She looked fucking intrigued.<br /> <br /> Vivian did as well. \u201cWe\u2019re still trying to figure out ourselves. We\u2019ve found something of a connection to Sanderson but... Infrastructure, you said?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cSanderson has his fingers in many things. I wouldn\u2019t be surprised to find him associated with a company that is aware enough to have an idea that the Infrastructure in the Works is special. He or his wife - Gina is not just a pretty face.\u201d She said it like a warning.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s for fucking sure.\u201d I rubbed my collarbone. \u201cAnyway, we mostly just wanted to give you a heads-up that there might be heat on one of White\u2019s assets.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian smiled. \u201cIt seemed neighborly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do wish there were someway to connect this to the Tower.\u201d Colleen glanced aside, considering. \u201cI believe Jake told you some of out long term plan in generalities. As an example... after Puriel first showed up at the dam, White investigated. We hit his laundromat shortly thereafter, as if in retaliation for his interest. The idea has been to get him to be suspicious of the other God Machine forces in the area and...\u201d she smiled tightly, \u201cI like pissing him off.\u201d She took a sip. \u201cStalking Horse also made sure to have a cover be caught on camera, then we falsified the dam\u2019s personnel records, showing that cover was hired and then \u2018covered up\u2019 - the records was sloppily deleted, and easily recovered.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked to Vivian. \u201cMaybe you could unclean your tracks in a way that looks like the Tower did it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would need to be more than that, unfortunately. He is somewhat characterized by his vengefulness. We would need to make certain he doesn\u2019t merely extend an olive branch to Team Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine and ally with them against whoever did this. It is a standard tactic of his, to sweet talk people like TTCM and throw them at his enemies to see who they are.\u201d Colleen leaned back, her hands crossed in front of her again.<br /> <br /> Vivian shook her head pridefully. \u201cTTCM would have no reason, no evidence to back up White\u2019s play.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is a slimy motherfucker though.\u201d I tossed back the rest of my sour. Shelley brought me another, the fucking saint.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is a Messenger, don\u2019t forget.\u201d Colleen warned. Liz rolled her eyes. Colleen\u2019s response was goddamn stern. \u201cDo not underestimate him. If he\u2019s seemed bumbling, that\u2019s what he wants you to see. The best play is to work off his ego, his temper and his vengefulness, and keep him from thinking rationally. He\u2019s incredibly dangerous when he\u2019s acting rationally.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat if I leave traces of a message from the Tower, to TTCM, suggesting they frame the laundromat for their internal troubles?\u201d Vivian suggested.<br /> <br /> Colleen nodded. \u201cThat should work.\u201d<br /> <br /> Son of a Preacher Man come on the speakers. \u201cGreat! Now that that\u2019s settled, how about a dance?\u201d Jack asked Colleen. She raised an eyebrow, but smiled and accepted.<br /> <br /> After the dance Colleen took her leave and Jack rejoined Liz and I at our table. Vivian had fucked off to go flirt with Shelley. Poor goddamn bird. I think Vivian\u2019s taking her to see Langley aka Bernice tomorrow.<br /> <br /> After a drink or two, Liz stretched. \u201cWell, I have a pipe I need to suck on and then my beauty sleep to get to.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack opened his mouth to say something, then closed it again. I smirked at him. \u201cWell, I have another solid fucking two hours of drinking to get in before I hit the goddamn hay, so you take care of yourself doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou too sweetie. Remember what I said about every 6th word?\u201d She smiled at me.<br /> <br /> I smiled back and flipped her off.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday was intended to be devoted to personal projects, with a little business on the side. Jack and Vivian had talks to have with Crusher and Rosanna respectively, so they said they'd talk with them about Drake. Liz had a laundry list of fit birds to talk to and I had a library to visit.<br /> <br /> By the time I got to the library, we had a text from Naomi. That put it around two - White hadn\u2019t sent any more fucking night mares, so I was well rested, but I\u2019d spent more time than usual getting ready for the day. I even found that iron.<br /> <br /> The text from Naomi was about Am. She didn\u2019t remember a whole goddamn lot, which was unsurprising. She was seven, after all, when the procedures took place. But she did remember the doctor\u2019s name was Patterson, and that a woman conducted her opening interview. Also, she confirmed that TTCM wasn\u2019t getting their info straight from the source. It was possible they were getting it from her fucking parents however.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t find out a whole lot either, in my couple of avenues of research. I found Daniel Thompson's obituary. He\u2019d been a churchgoer and had \u2018died where he worked\u2019, survived by his mother. There was no mention of the school by name at all, or any other family.<br /> <br /> I also took a stab in the dark, looking up the dead couple from Mac\u2019s freaky fucking double homicide, to see if I could find any pieces to help him out, without breaking my promise. Not a goddamn thing. It wasn\u2019t surprising either. Not everyone makes the papers. It was just a hope. Fuck, I wish I could get eyes on the place. More correctly, I wish I could get Jack\u2019s eyes on the place a week ago. Ah well. If wishes were goddamn horses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Quietus\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> Leaving the Fed in the car seems simple enough. I\u2019m not looking for an occult tome, just a book. I\u2019ll make it more important later.<br /> <br /> \u201cWait here. I don\u2019t want you to find someone \u2018interesting\u2019 and disappear into the stock room.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Gman gives me the slightest side glance, which for him is a Go to Hell look. Before he can make some incredibly droll quip that I\u2019ll have to think about longer than I will ever admit, I jump out and head inside. We didn\u2019t have to time to go look for anything special so the first big box book store and overpriced coffee shop on the way would have to do. The vapid barista gives me a worried once over before finding something far more important to do away from the counter. Lucky for her, I\u2019m not interested in her burnt coffee. Looking down one of the aisles, I spot a white girl, 20something, shelving a cart of books. Her clothes say she isn\u2019t recently cut off from Daddy\u2019s money, but never had it to start with. She sighs when whatever the next lame pop song on the radio starts, and I think she might be a hipster with clothes from Goodwill. But then I notice that she handles the books like they are her children. She likely needs the money, but she definitely worked here because she loved books. Probably best not to tell her why I needed mine. As I walk up, she glances up from her shelving and gives me the same smile she gives everyone. That is a good start.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I help you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smile and wonder if she knows I\u2019m observing her entire being. \u201cYes I need to get a gift for a friend. Do you have a hardback of The Grapes of Wrath?\u201d<br /> <br /> It's only meaningful to me and Crusher and probably Rosanna. The book didn\u2019t make any different outside of that context. She stands up and nods for me to follow.<br /> <br /> \u201cI want it to be more than just an afterthought purchase, but honestly he isn\u2019t very careful with his things, so I don\u2019t want to spend too much.\u201d I look almost comically sheepish when she turns around to smile at me again. The smile hits her eyes this time. The fact that I\u2019ve put that much thought into a gift that I know won\u2019t be treated properly intrigues her.<br /> <br /> \u201cHere you go, sir. This one isn\u2019t very fancy, but honestly I think it might be more sturdy than some of the more elaborate copies we have.\u201d<br /> <br /> Before I can take the offered book, a rather annoyed little man shuffles around the shelf.<br /> <br /> \u201cJennifer, I ...,\u201d he stops short when he looks up at me then looks back as if trying to forget he sees me. \u201cOh. Yes there is an unattended cart left in fiction.\u201d He waits expectantly for Jennifer to scurry away, obviously from past experience. This apparent supervisor carries a clipboard, dresses in department store clothes without a speck of book dust on them, is notably older, has less concern for the books than the numbers, and doesn\u2019t like that I\u2019m in \u201chis\u201d store. Jennifer obviously has more to lose in this situation and that bothers me more than anything else. Maybe it\u2019s the Saboteur in me, or maybe I\u2019m not as big of an asshole as I think I am, but I feel something click. I\u2019ve found something that needs to be \u201cfixed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat would be because Jennifer was helping me, a paying customer, find a gift. Something that she was very helpful with, by the way.\u201d Turning back to Jennifer, who looks up at me with an expression somewhere between shock and amusement, I offer my card.<br /> <br /> \u201cNames Jack. I\u2019m a Private Investigator. If you ever need anything found out or proven, just let me know.\u201d The last I emphasize while I glare at Mr. Stick Up My Ass. The way his face turns paler suggests I might have some work to do. He runs back to wherever he came from. Jennifer quietly smiles and takes my card.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you. I appreciate that.\u201d She looks like she has more to say but neither of us have the time. I nod and tap the book. \u201cAnd I appreciate this.\u201d I start to walk away then look back. \u201cCall that number if you need anything?\u201d The question at the end makes her look up again. She\u2019s blushing but happy. She nods and I figure now would be a great time to get the hell out before I pull a Speed and say something sensitive.<br /> <br /> Back in the car, Billy Mack looks at me then his shiny retirement watch. \u201cShut up and drive old man.\u201d<br /> <br /> Yeah, I\u2019m still as big of an asshole as I thought.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XX</i><br /> <br /> Ah Team Tomorrow Contemporary Medicine. Nothing sinister going on there.<br /> <br /> There was talk about how the inside guard was clearly on Chatroulette, a website primarily used for stumbling over unexpected penises. In such a case his partner saw the guard wordlessly rise, walk back in the server closet, and then see several large dogs go look at the closet, bark, hurl themselves into the door then, in unison, look at the screen and rush the monitor.<br /> <br /> Finally Miranda, there is a mystery eh? What is Speed getting herself into? We will see you next time, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the