hack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T22:17:19-07:00","id":586808,"title":"","content":"Hee hee...Glad you got caught up. Also glad you are enjoying these. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T14:45:39-07:00","id":595024,"title":"","content":"It is time to return to Demon. Speed Demon\u2019s player had to miss, but all three players present stepped up and did journals, so while we won\u2019t have her excellent narration sadly, the session should be well covered. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXI</i><br /> <br /> <b><b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b></b><br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>T.G.I. Tuesday's</u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> Saturday was a day of divergent agendas. Clytemnestra spent the day with Robin Graves with plans to enlist her death-aspected senses to track down the materials we need to repair the reality damage the Abyssal has caused. Speed was planning to do some research before attempting to seduce and collect a blood sample from Miranda Asbury. Quietus wanted to meet with Crusher Creel and Rosanna to give the man his gift and cement them as allies. Vivian had plans to take Shelly to see the Bernice Burnheart and the Sisters of Chaos that evening but I decided to join him for the afternoon so I could speak to them about her entanglement with the gentry known properly as Mr Smiles, though I am still rather partial to Jack Slenderskellingtonman. I wonder, given the import of names in fairy, if it would be irksome to call him that directly? I shall have to find out when I get the opportunity, which seems likely as he did technically buy me dinner by sending me that meat and cheese basket. Though it does beg the question of how he knew to send it to the detective agency. It is possible that Michael White gave him the information if they are linked. Otherwise, it would be yet another unknown fae power. They are decidedly too unknown in their abilities and dangerously able to divine what should be secret information for my liking.<br /> <br /> The mass produced atmosphere was suitably unobtrusive to our purpose and the wait staff suitably scarce to give us adequate privacy. Rosanna provided us with some further information concerning the local Changeling political structure. The Autumn Court welds the lion's share of the power and numbers in this area, but not so much that it could stand against the other seasonal courts should it attempt to seize total control. Of course, their position does afford them great leeway in activities and a powerful voice in what I gather is supposed to be a council of equals. The Autumn King, known only as The Harvestman, is clearly a shrewd man who is content to be a stronger indirect power than to give into the temptations of tyranny. This bodes well, I do prefer to deal with reasonable individuals and our talents are certainly of greater impact when used with the sort of subtle and surgical precision that such a man would appreciate.<br /> <br /> Rosanna said that the Autumn Court was looking into the issue of Mr Smiles already, so it seems likely that we can collaborate. An excellent means to establish some mutual awareness and lay a groundwork for future dealings. She was concerned that they might wish to use me as bait to lure Mr Smiles in. I was mildly surprised at her concern, as such an approach is the rather obvious tack and dismissing such leverage without good cause would be foolhardy. Of course, she may well believe Vivian to be mortal or at the very least have no clear idea of power levels. Also, I do not believe the Changeling's fear of these gentry is entirely overblown or based on their misfortunes. Even at the reduced power that his exile causes, Mr Smiles is a formidable being. Also, these beings are apparently mystically difficult to kill, being fairy-tail monsters such as they are, they have only one, often obscure, manner of true death.<br /> <br /> In speaking of the Autumn Court, she did also explain that the courts operate under something akin to the medieval definition of hospitality. She advised being sure that we had such in place to keep our secrets safe from the Autumn Court when we met with them. She also explained that they do seem to have some rules of engagement that prevent their members from sowing fear too indiscriminately. The gist of it all was not pleasing. Our actions at the coffee shop seem likely to have been a violation of hospitality. Oneiromancy is a common fae talent. Given the very intensely personal content of the nightmares I experienced and the reactions of the others, I fear this Autumn Court knows entirely too much about us for comfort. For now, we must rebuild a state of hospitality to prevent further harassment. Then we must glean as much information as we can about them.<br /> <br /> Quietus made it clear that he was prepared to aid Rosanna and her Summer Court in reducing the power of the Autumn Court but she seemed disinclined as the current arrangement is mutually beneficial, even as unbalanced as it may be. Also, internal strife would only serve to weaken all of the Changeling courts and endanger the locals.<br /> <br /> I have some thoughts on repairing the breech of etiquette that we made. Hopefully, a gesture of good faith and a successful joint venture against one of their enemies will suffice. However, clearly the balance of power is delicate and could be tipped to create discord and strife which would make them all extremely vulnerable to the Gentry. As a precaution, I shall need to discover how one might go about making sure the Arcadians know of such a situation when it occurs. It seems likely they have spies of some sort watching, but relying on such could be disastrous.<br /> <br /> All told, it would be a difficult and dangerous undertaking and almost assuredly require the sacrifice of our current covers and the Night Train Detective Agency. Also, destroying what could otherwise be a large number of very potent allies would be a terrible waste even without the hefty expenditure of resources involved. I do hope it does not become necessary.<br /> <br /> Once we'd spoken about that, Quietus made his gift to Crusher. He offered the ogre a boost to his intelligence and education, with a focus on literature. It was quite well received. Mr Creel reiterated his willingness to use his powers to attempt to local Drake and once more cautioned us against entering the Hedge if it proved that he had become lost there.<br /> <br /> Once we departed, I shared my observations with Quietus concerning the fallout of our indiscretion toward the Autumn Court. He was not pleased but he could find no fault with my reasoning. I imagine Speed will be disappointed that it was not Micheal White's handiwork, but his list of crimes remains ample for whatever misfortunes we might see fit to visit upon him and his house.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Once More Into the Breech</u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> We had finished our luncheon when Clytemnestra called us about meeting her and Robin at the Asbury house. Mrs Graves was very interested in seeing Alice after hearing about her from Clytemnestra but our Tempter was not comfortable entering the house alone as she had not personally investigated it previously. Quietus and I joined them at the house and we all entered.<br /> <br /> As I had not been fully prepared last time, I took the occasion to bring my kit with me and collected some much more proper samples. In particular, I was able to get some intact grubs and insects from the downstairs room for study. Quietus remained hyper vigilant as I worked and Clytemnestra and Mrs Graves waited upstairs at his direction. The aberrations of the Asbury house were unchanged from before as we made our way up to the attic. Of note were some personal effects in a previously empty and unoccupied room. There was female clothing including some rather elaborate cowboy boots. Despite the unexpected choice of foot fashion, I concurred with Quietus that it was most likely Miranda returning to her familial home. This might complicate his plans to claim the house and the identities of the deceased once we've repaired the reality damage.<br /> <br /> Mrs Graves was unable to ascertain whether or not Alice was tainted by the corruption or not. Her overwhelming drive to return to life concerned Robin as did her ability to possess someone and warp them into a nightmarish monster. According to Mrs Graves, this was a taxing but not damaging power for Alice and so one she was only likely to use when angry or frightened. The effect is quite harmful to the victim as their body attempts to revert back to its proper shape afterward but without the benefit of ghostly magic to aid the movement of bones and flesh. This is not a power beyond the realm of ghostly ability, but one Mrs Graves has not previously encountered. It may have been triggered by abyssal exposure or it might simply be a power Alice manifested naturally. Either way, it makes her very dangerous and her single-minded determination to find a way back to life at any cost makes her unlikely to be laid quietly to rest.<br /> <br /> As Clytemnestra made her intention to reveal her own nature to Mrs Graves, Quietus was open about using some partial transformations in her presence as well as making reference to the ability to 'do things'. At this point, Robin Graves admitted that she had determined that we were not mundane humans, though her theory was that we were magi. Interesting, and possibly an angle worth considering as a means of laying a false explanation for our abilities in the future. More pertinent was that she and her 'crew' had encountered angels in the past. They are the group that we have heard of that killed a group of angels using bone spurs and bleeding smoke rather than blood. Mrs Graves is an ally of value and, especially with her connections to this group of others, a very clear threat especially now that she knows more about us. I trust Clytemnestra's ability to monitor and control her. I do know she is fond of Mrs Graves, but I do not believe she would put her safety or ours at risk for such attachments. Mrs Graves account of the incident with the angels made it clear there was an occult matrix involved. A death every four days of every fourth name alphabetically of the building's residents. I should perhaps see if the location itself bears any further significance. She also made particular mention of one of her fellows, named only as the Burning Man, who she said was very hostile to, as she termed it, robots. She seems to accept that our physical similarity does not equal a like-minded dark intent but she was skeptical that there could be a peaceful meeting with this Burning Man and thus he was to be avoided. Further comments paint him as very intense and humorless with a perpetual anger. This is a mindset I can certainly fathom and have seen not infrequently among my more combative and hostile fellow Unchained. Unfortunate that such a powerful fighter is so predisposed to be hostile to us. Perhaps, with proper introduction or great subtly his rage can be directed to the God Machine's minions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Shelly Shocked</u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> Having completed the investigations at the Asbury house, we went our separate ways. Quietus and I returned to the office while Clytemnestra and Mrs Graves headed back to Clytemnestra's house for further revelations and presumably sex, as there is usually sex when Clytemnestra is involved, before going out to seek the death-marked car parts we need to produce, as Speed dubbed it, Reality Spackle at the Peterson Chemical infrastructure.<br /> <br /> I made ready for my date with Shelly. Vivian's typical hacker geek wardrobe isn't entirely unsuitable for a cross-dressing punk show. I selected something more anarchist than otaku for the evening and set out. Shelly had also gone with a jeans and tee casual as this wasn't her usual venue either. I did remind her that she'd asked for different.<br /> <br /> We started with a meal, going to a nice little family run Japanese restaurant that favors authentic quality cuisine over kitsch. Shelly seemed to enjoy the food and I was able to steer the conversation to her past without too much difficulty. She took up waitressing to pay for college but soon fell into the trap of being unable to work enough to support herself and continue her studies. She harbors a strong desire to resume her degree while it is still a viable option, but is resigned that her current circumstances do not make this a likely event. Clearly, this would make for excellent leverage to gain nearly anything she might have of interest or value to me. Her area of study is chemistry, and thus our conversation was pleasingly advanced. She is a clever woman and I do enjoy her company. Perhaps, if she proves suitably trustworthy, she could assist me in the lab. It may prove to be worthwhile to gift her the means to finish her degree simply to have her as a valuable ally.<br /> <br /> After eating, we made our way to the venue. Bernice and her ladies where every bit the performers as before. Even having been to the previous show, I found their talent enjoyable and while it was not Shelly's genre of choice I think the novelty of it appealed to her. I continued to be witty and charming. As the evening went on, Shelly relaxed with a few drinks and I took advantage of the rather sexual nature of the show to grow steadily more flirtatious. I do not think she'd set out with intentions of bringing me back to her place afterward but as the evening unfolded she began to flirt back and our dancing took on considerable contact. By the end, we'd dropped any real pretenses and moved into kissing and light if mostly subtle petting. I briefly considered asking her if she wanted to stop for coffee, but as she seemed quite adequately warm and stimulated already we instead headed back to her place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> My day with Robin was fun and exciting yesterday.<br /> <br /> Oh don\u2019t give me that look! You could spend time with me you know. Why don\u2019t you do that, actually? My Agency won\u2019t bite.<br /> <br /> I do, but you know. It\u2019s not like that isn\u2019t going to happen anyway.<br /> <br /> So I was going to enlist Robin for acquiring the car parts we needed. You know for patching reality. She was keen on seeing Alice\u2019s ghost, though, so against my will and better judgment we met Kilroy and Quietus at the Asbury house.<br /> <br /> The bits I saw were as unpleasant as I had heard. I had told you about it before, I don\u2019t see much need to go into detail again.<br /> <br /> One change Speed Demon\u2019s girl had left some stuff there, it seems, and thankfully Robin did not need to actually interact with Alice to use her powers. Quietus picked up a vocal glitch, though, after admitting to Robin he had powers. Glowing eyes and all.<br /> <br /> Alice is an unusual ghost, but it is not impossible she is not tainted. She is driven to return to life whatever the cost, and can possess people and warp them into monstrosities for as long as they are possessed. It sounds unpleasant.<br /> <br /> Robin and I went back, and had dinner. I revealed my nature to her, which she took as well as one could. Well, without some details\u2026but enough that she knew Angels hunted us. It turned out they killed a couple Angels earlier who were killing people to further a matrix. It was interesting. She has a group, but has neglected to introduce me, based on suspecting some members might have issues with me.<br /> <br /> So we went to the junkyard and things got\u2026odd. Seems some Spirit there possessed a number of junked cars, turning them into some sort of ad hoc combat machine. It chased Robin and I off, so we called Quietus. He went back in with us, and we were attacked again. Quietus did what he does best and attacked it, which seemed futile till he began blowing cars up.<br /> <br /> Actually, first he blew up a car it had set to attack us, which seemed to hurt him somewhat from shrapnel. Actually, the shrapnel sucked all around. When he had serious trouble hurting it, he started blowing up its components This forced it to begin reconstituting itself from cars, which bought us time. Quietus created a gate to the Underworld since Robin had said she knew her way through. We easily made it through before the Spirit finished prepping its battle form. Hopefully it will take awhile to regain Essence.<br /> <br /> But we were in the Underworld now and\u2026hmmm\u2026sweetie, I need a new glass.<br /> <br /> Thanks so much. Where was I?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Quietus\u2019s Thoughts</b><br /> <br /> The old man changes in the car. We do have business to attend to after all. Vivian has a date with Dr. Smiles and needs some pointers before she takes an unwanted vacation. Ruby Friday\u2019s will do, just to have a meeting place without atmosphere. That\u2019s what Kiki\u2019s is for. Atmosphere.<br /> <br /> Rosanna waves us over to their table and Crusher genuinely smiles. I introduce everyone in Spanish and explain that Vivian is the friend Billy Mack mentioned previously. Dr. Smiles is considered one of the Banished. Since I have no idea what the fuck that means, I keep listening to Rosanna explain Changeling politics. The short version is that the dentist pissed off the wrong imaginary tyrant and got kicked out of Neverland. Now he looks for \u201csomething unique\u201d to convince \u201cthem\u201d to welcome him back. That \u201csomething\u201d about Vivian is \u201cunique\u201d is only mildly terrifying. Rosanna says she can talk with the Autumn Court to look into the problem, but they may need to use Vivian as bait. Viv is way too eager. I apparently missed it before as Rosanna talks about the \u201cother Monarchs\u201d in the area. So she\u2019s the Summer Queen. Good to know. I offer to help the Summer Court get a leg up as it sounds like the Autumn King has the other courts by the balls. Rosanna says they are all working well together since no one is trying to hold power all the time, so I won\u2019t get in the way right now. She also notes that the Autumn Court keeps a long list of people that earn their way onto a Shit List. So long as you don\u2019t do anything to get on it, they generally don\u2019t terrorize you.<br /> <br /> The time comes to give my gift to Crusher. He\u2019s pretty quiet as I explain that he\u2019s the only one at the table that thinks poorly of his mental abilities. Rosanna nods vigorously to drive the point home. To help fix that, I offer my gift of more intellect, a bit of scholarly learning, and a focus on literature. If anyone other than a Changeling asks me what\u2019s the catch, I will be insulted. Crusher has been burned too many times, so I know not to take it personally. No strings, this is a gift. I don\u2019t mention that I also know he\u2019s honorable enough that if I were to need help, he couldn\u2019t really turn me away. This just helps to remove his hangup about everyone being smarter than him. We finish lunch with our Cat Snake Queen and Hard as Granite Crusher without any bullshit. I do like having friends.<br /> <br /> Vivian looks at me when we get back in the car. I hate that look, it reminds me of Billy Mack\u2019s \u201cThinking\u201d face. She asks who didn\u2019t have terrible dreams the other night. Naomi and Jared. And who didn\u2019t go with us to the Autumn Court command center. Naomi and Jared. And who didn\u2019t have any involvement with fucking with the spiders. Damn it. Now we have to discreetly make up with the Autumn Court.<br /> _____<br /> <br /> It\u2019s still early evening, not even dark yet, when we get a call back at the office. Liz and Robin are at the Asbury House. Why the fuck this happened, I don\u2019t know at first. Eventually I hear Robin saying something about meeting Alice. Right, Ghost Hunters gonna Hunt. Billy Mack throws some of his science shit in the back seat and looks pleased. That\u2019s never a good sign. It takes much longer to get there when Gabe\u2019s not driving, but we pull up and Liz looks incredibly not pleased to be here. Robin looks like she would rather be somewhere else, but she has a sad determination to her expression. This is her job, not her life. Good to know. The girls are holding hands and I remember being told that Liz is not looking for any monogamous relationships. That\u2019s a shit load better to hear coming from an \u201cinvested third party\u201d than to see like this. Whatever, there\u2019s nothing between Liz and I, right now. I walk up on the front porch and open the creaky front door. Robin shivers at the sound and Liz follows suit. I\u2019ll have to tease her about missing a cue later. I walk in and close all the doors except the stairwell. Billy Mack wants to collect bugs from the anti-grav shit room. I give instructions of how to specifically get to the attic then stop the ladies before Robin and Liz go upstairs. I ask Liz how serious things will get with Robin tonight. I need to know if it will be worth the pain for me to not be discreet. Liz takes on a dull monotone about the whole monogamous thing again, but admits she will show Robin who she is tonight. Also that Robin believes we\u2019re mages. Fair enough. I send them up while I stay with the nut job of an old man. He puts on a headlamp while I turn on my night vision. I draw my gun before he goes in because I don\u2019t trust him to pay attention and I don\u2019t trust a hand or something worse to reach out of the shit when his back is turned. I stand right in the door so I have a full view of the room and Mr. Shaky as he flops around in silence. Billy stands on a fucked up piece of broken furniture and pulls some squirming nasty thing out of the shit on the ceiling. I breathe out thinking we\u2019re good before the Gman starts trying to pull one of the bugs off Mr. Shaky. I tense and ready my weapon. Fucking crazy old man. The mutant shrimp slug that goes into the bag thrashes around at its new environment. I give Billy a look without putting my gun away.<br /> <br /> I put my shades on so I can have a proper talk with Robin while my eyes are still blue and glowy. We walk upstairs to find them standing in the hallway looking shaken. The bedroom doors are open and I realize they looked inside. Damn it. I\u2019m not too growly when I fuss about following directions. I pull Robin over and lower my shades to explain that I can \u201cdo stuff.\u201d I know this could compromise me, but everything seems to go okay. Then I speak. Well hello Optimus Fucking Prime. Shit. I have glowing blue eyes, and a metallic voice so it\u2019s not a huge jump for Robin to ask if I\u2019m a robot. I\u2019m not a robot technically, so I say no. I\u2019m not worried about her suspecting me of lying but I tell her I broke a rule by telling her about me. She says that her group killed some robots that were murdering people a while back. The details are important. They are the ones that killed the angels with the bone spikes. The angels were killing people in a specific apartment building, every four rooms, every four days, etc. etc. etc. She explains that one of her people is called the Burning Man and that we shouldn\u2019t meet him. He doesn\u2019t like the robots at all. Fair enough. Robin goes up to look at Alice when Liz notices new stuff in the room that didn\u2019t look lived in for a while. Cowgirl boots, clothes, looks like Miranda moved home. Robin comes back down looking a little more pale than before. Alice apparently possesses people when she gets spooked and forces their bodies into horrific monsters to protect her. Ghosts don\u2019t normally do anything close to that according to Robin. I get the idea that Robin and her people try to help ghosts, not just make them go away. I offer that if they have some that need to be put down, I\u2019d like to help. I don\u2019t tell her how or why. Then we let them go on their date. Billy needs to get back so Vivian can get ready.<br /> _____<br /> <br /> Gabe has a date with Miranda, Vivian has a date with Shelley, the waitress from Kiki\u2019s, and Liz has a date/morbid shopping trip planned with Robin. Fuck if I know what or who Jared is doing, but given it\u2019s a Saturday night, I probably don\u2019t want to know. I finish up some of the paperwork Gabe makes me do for the random cases I work on and get up to head home when Liz calls.<br /> <br /> She and Robin are in the big junkyard the police use to scrape unwanted vehicles after they are used for evidence. There is a monster there and she asks me to come take care of it. I call a cab then hit the petty cash safe. Gabe will have to be pissed when she finds out how much I bribe the cabbie to drive like she does. Both women are waiting for me outside, no obvious sign of injuries. I\u2019m really glad I talked to Robin earlier. I make myself hard to hurt and hit the night vision again. Looking over the fence, I can\u2019t see anything but cars. They explain where it is and what it looks like. With my limited occult knowledge, it sounds like a spirit or cars or murder or something made a home in the junkyard. As we move back to the spot they were attacked, I spot a car shoved into a bus, holding another car that can easily fall on us when we walk into the corridor. I have just the thing for this. I tell both women what I see and how to move when I get the word. Making cars more likely to explode is a Saboteur\u2019s wet dream, so long as you can get away before the cops show up. I also ask Robin if she knows her way around the Underworld. She nods with a confused look on her face.<br /> <br /> Plans aren\u2019t always supposed to go to shit, but mine of have been known to. When Liz and Robin run past the trap, I shoot the doctored car. It blows chunks of animated car off and still has enough left to send a few bits of shrapnel my way. Not wanting to risk Liz or Robin, I try to reach out with my ephemeral attack for spirits. But, probably because it is manifested in the cars, there\u2019s nothing there for me to hit. I put the whammy on another car at the base of the beast, and run for the others. As I move, I yell to Robin to shoot the Volkswagen. She fires and I\u2019m hit by more shrapnel, notably more this time. Using my body as a shield had better earn me points for something. I turn with a new idea. Robin probably thinks I\u2019m nuts for punching that monster, but since the thing inside is not actually manifested, I just tag a Greyhound. Blowing up a piece of the body works better. Then I rip a gate into the Underworld and ask Robin if she will lead the way.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m in the Underworld. This is sure to be fun.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXI</i><br /> <br /> Well that\u2019s fun. Not too much to add.<br /> <br /> We are all aware of T.G.I. Tuesdays/Ruby Fridays discrepancy. It is deliberate. I don't think we ever sorted out which it was. It was a generic restaurant of the type.<br /> <br /> Of course, with most of the group in a <b>Changeling: The Lost</b> game (Speed, Kilroy, and Clytemnestra) and one not but playing one in a crossover game (Jack), there is always the excitement of having to play dumb a bit on Changeling politics.<br /> <br /> Much of the house stuff was just letting the Sin-Eater work. As a note, Jack\u2019s dice hate him, apparently, leaving him with a heck of a glitch.<br /> <br /> The battle was fun. Jack\u2019s player (whose dice still hate him) was innovative on blowing up the car parts, as the Spirit-possessed critter was pretty dangerous. It\u2019s a hybrid murder and car spirit, as this junkyard was picked because it is where the police drop off cars which are totaled in criminal actions. They can get what they need from other junkyards, it will just take a lot longer. Bringing Robin Graves (heh) in for that was a wise move on the PC\u2019s part.<br /> <br /> As a last note Kilroy, trying to move ahead on his Cipher, kept looking for stuff to Sabotage. It was pretty funny.<br /> <br /> Okay, well I think that covers it, but if you have comments or questions they are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-18-2015, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T15:00:32-07:00","id":611390,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check back on our infernal band. You will be glad to hear that Speed Demon is once again your narrator, though Kilroy and Clytemnestra have lent their voices as well. Let\u2019s see what happened last session.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXII</i><br /> <b><br /> Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> After finishing up my business, and taking another fucking shower, I called up Miranda. She picked up after only a couple of rings. \u201cHey there Princess.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe. Is it time?\u201d Her tone was serious.<br /> <br /> I cleared my throat. \u201cAh, no...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you in danger?\u201d There was a little worry in her voice. That was good, right?<br /> <br /> I answered quickly. \u201cNah, I\u2019m fine. I was just wondering if you were... I mean, if we could talk.\u201d My parents were clearly goddamn justified in not giving me the fucking middle name Smooth.<br /> <br /> There was a pause. \u201cAlright. I presume you do not wish to meet at my family\u2019s house?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI haven\u2019t been there yet, but from what the boys said, it doesn\u2019t have the greatest ambiance.\u201d I agreed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWould meeting at the Student Center do?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cJust fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I made goddamn good time to the school but found her waiting anyway. She was still in her old-style school uniform, sitting legs crossed at a bench just inside the Student Center. As I walked up, her reading of a digest of 2013 news stories was being interrupted by some college douchebag. \u201cSo, what was your name again?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGo away.\u201d She didn\u2019t look up from her book.<br /> <br /> He smiled good naturedly. \u201cAh, come on, you just look interesting. Can\u2019t I even know what year you are?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d She turned a page.<br /> <br /> He was moving to sit down next to her when I got in arms reach. I came up behind him, so the fucker was startled a little when I said. \u201cHey sweetheart, this guy bothering you?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked up and smiled. \u201cYes\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey now...\u201d He turned around and his eyes widened. I smirked. \u201cI was, I was just leaving.\u201d He held his hands up slightly and backed off, stumbling a little as he tried to move away without turning his back to me.<br /> <br /> She stood up, smoothing her skirt. \u201cHello Gabe. Would you like to talk here, or elsewhere?\u201d<br /> <br /> I glanced around at the food court in one direction, and the bookstore in another. Clusters of college students were crossing between the two. \u201cI was thinking some place more private.\u201d Sheer force of will kept me from making it an invitation right off.<br /> <br /> \u201cI could give us more privacy here.\u201d She considered, looking me over. \u201cFollow me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She led me outside, to a garden area, I guess. I dunno, I don\u2019t keep the goddamn things. It had a few flowers, some paths and benches and knee level bushed that \u2018walled\u2019 off the paths. She sat on one of the benches next to a small fountain. I lingered a few steps behind her, admiring the view. It was no less admirable when she sat, watching me with that slight smile and one raised eyebrow. She was almost luminous in the moonlight and the path illumination did interesting things with shadows. I ambled over, grinning broadly and sat beside her. \u201cNice choice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you. This is a nice place. And it is a pleasant diversion from work, to meet you here.\u201d She sat up straight and kept up the smile.<br /> <br /> I slouched, leaning back against the bench. \u201cIt is for me too. Lots of dead ends today.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d She looked interested. \u201cAre you working many cases?\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my shoulders back and started walking a coin across my knuckles. \u201cTwo officially. This stuff...\u201d I jerked my head in the vague direction of the Asbury room. \u201c...and a missing persons case. My dead ends were to help out a friend though. He\u2019s a bull, and they\u2019ve run across a hell of a murder case. Woman drowned, without a trace of liquid at the scene, except for the husband\u2019s blood.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is puzzling,\u201d she agreed.<br /> <br /> \u201cHopefully the boys are having better luck on doing favors for some of our supernatural contacts.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> She looked approving. \u201cHaving the local night children indebted to you is advantageous.\u201d I blinked. \u201cThe supernaturally gifted.\u201d I nodded. \u201cBut I would like to know more about you than just \u2018Gabe the investigator\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s not a whole lot that doesn\u2019t touch on that. It was my first job...\u201d I gave her a little of my history. Well, my cover\u2019s history. Still, as far as getting to know me, that history defines me as much as anyone\u2019s defines them, except maybe more explicitly. After all, I was adult enough to read the story as it was written. Still, I got to my Fall pretty quickly. \u201cIn the end it turns out my boss - the guy who got me setup up with this whole deal -\u201d I gestured to indicate the vague supernatural powers she had assuredly figured out I had, \u201cwas just using me to get some kind of emotional resonance from my clients and didn\u2019t give two shits about helping them.\u201d<br /> <br /> She listened intently, making all the appropriate noises. \u201cWho was it that treated you so shabbily?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned, somewhat bitterly. \u201cTo be fair, I had an idea about it from the start, but then he started getting pissy and picky about it. And, I guess I figured out that I gave at least two shits myself, so I blew him off.\u201d I sighed. \u201cAs to who... that\u2019s, well, complicated. It\u2019s definitely not an \u2018I could tell you but then I\u2019d have to kill you\u2019 situation, but... it is something of an \u2018if I tell you, someone might try to kill me. Not because you let on or anything, just the act of telling you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She raised both eyebrows. \u201cWell, we wouldn\u2019t want that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI certainly would prefer more opportunities to spend time with you.\u201d I gave her a lopsided grin.<br /> <br /> Her smile widened, just a little. \u201cFor my part, as you can probably guess, I am older than I look.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cProbably.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am a scion of an old magical tradition. I,\u201d she looked down briefly, \u201cworked with people ultimately on the wrong side for a time. I defected to a different organization, only to find I had traded one set of otherworldly masters for a second. So I defected again and have since been working...\u201d She considered her words. \u201c... freelance.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled, tracing the profile on my coin with my thumb. \u201cI can understand defecting from otherworldly masters.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI asked who because I wondered if that second group I mentioned might be related to your previous boss - the Seers of the Throne?\u201d<br /> <br /> I was already shaking my head before she said the name. \u201cNah. My boss, people working for him, they show signs of it, in their aura.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I don\u2019t have those signs?\u201d she asked. I shook my head. \u201cAh.\u201d I couldn\u2019t tell if she was pleased or disappointed that we didn\u2019t have that in common.<br /> <br /> We talked for awhile more, back and forth, staying a little shallower than all that by mutual, unspoken agreement. I did mention that our method for repairing reality would let us fix her house as well, which made her happy. In general, she seemed warmer than that first talk under the tree. I even felt like she was into me. Not that I was precisely fucking objective. Still, nothing ventured and all that shit.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s starting to get chilly in the evenings.\u201d I mentioned, stretching my arm behind her and resting a hand on her shoulder.<br /> <br /> She smiled at me and moved closer. The smell of honeysuckle got stronger. \u201cSomewhat.\u201d We sat in comfortable silence for a moment, until she spoke up again. \u201cI haven\u2019t been involved with anyone in a long time.\u201d She paused. \u201cOr a woman ever.\u201d Her smile faded and she looked thoughtful. \u201cI have spent much time watching and not much socializing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Now it was my turn to smile slightly. \u201cI can understand that.\u201d I didn't move my arm and she didn\u2019t move away.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe last time I was involved was with the head of the local Seers.\u201d She considered for a moment. \u201cHe won\u2019t be jealous. He\u2019s trying to kill me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was just about to ask. So, a problem, but not the kind I thought. I bet I could take him.\u201d I grinned over at her, winking to let her know I was kidding.<br /> <br /> She took it as the joke it was, and her slight smile was back, for a moment. \u201cThe last time he and I fought, I threw something awful at him.\u201d Her voice had lost some color. \u201cThey burned the building and salted the earth it had stood on.\u201d She sighed and held a finger to my fucking lips when I started to say something. \u201cI don\u2019t wish for you to get hurt. A romantic relationship should wait until after this is dealt with.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked at her. \u201cI\u2019ll have to light fires under the other\u2019s asses then, get this done.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked over at me, amusedly resigned and sighed. \u201cSpeaking of such things, I should return. It has been a pleasant evening, Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad to hear it.\u201d I kissed her on the cheek before we both stood.<br /> <br /> She kissed me back, on the cheek before moving away. I locked eyes with her as she did. She smiled slightly. I was still getting good vibes from her. At the same time, it was pretty clear she thought this was a bad idea, but what the hell, I\u2019m pretty good at bad ideas.<br /> <br /> I took her hand to pull her close enough to rest on hand on her hip while my other started on her shoulder and ran up her neck to cup her cheek. Her face clouded slightly as mine moved close, but she kissed me back. It was some soft romantic dip kiss, or a hard demanding kiss. It was what it was, and I wouldn\u2019t have traded it for the world.<br /> <br /> It might have been my imagination, or wishful thinking, but I thought I saw a little more color in her cheeks as we moved apart. Her facial expression didn\u2019t change to match though, just her usual slight smile. \u201cWe\u2019re taking that route then?\u201d There was definitely more warmth in her voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe only route I know.\u201d I glanced at her red lips and licked my own, smiling cockily back. \u201cI\u2019ve wanted to do that since we met.\u201d<br /> <br /> She laid a hand on my cheek. \u201cI should still go home alone tonight.\u201d She came in close for another kiss.<br /> <br /> I was grinning like a goddamn idiot. \u201cIf you insist.\u201d<br /> <br /> She pulled away slowly and left me standing at the garden bench. She looked back once. I winked at her. And when I couldn\u2019t watch her leave anymore, I walked back to my car, twirling my keys and whistling.<br /> <br /> <br /> From there, I headed over to Mavericks. Bobby wouldn\u2019t let me hear the fucking end of it if I missed another goddamn Saturday night. I felt like celebrating anyway. I was in a good mood, good enough that I started up the chant of \u2018one of these things is not like the others\u2019 whenever Bobby got up on stage with the ladies. It may also have been the whiskey sours. I was even still in a good mood after going home alone and waking up by myself. I was awake early enough to get Liz\u2019s noon thirty text asking about plans as soon as she sent it.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t have any, considering every next step depended on what the hell other people got done the night before. \u2018Anything come of shit yesterday?\u2019<br /> <br /> Liz responded with a series of texts. \u2018Delay in acquiring materials\u2019, \u2018Discuss over lunch or at office?\u2019, and \u2018If you say Kiki\u2019s, I will back hand you\u2019.<br /> <br /> I deleted the one word text I had almost fucking sent, responding instead with \u2018Promise? How bout Alfredo\u2019s Feast-ro?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018What kind of name is that? Nevermind, I don\u2019t want to know. That work for everyone?\u2019<br /> <br /> Billy Mack and Jack responded in the affirmative, so we set a time. Liz started knitting, and fucking bi