ndering to the kid again. \u201cI dunno. Maybe it considers the cars there like its children and doesn\u2019t want me to look at them.\u201d I held back a laugh and topped off her coffee with my flask. \u201cThanks darling.\u201d She turned to Billy Mack. \u201cWhy the last resort? Surely we could come up with some excuse for needing specific parts?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf we do things flawlessly at Peterson, the God Machine won\u2019t notice a thing.\u201d Liz noted the g-man\u2019s stress on the \u2018if' and a light came on. He continued his thought anyway. \u201cIf not, the materials used will be on record and the purchases could be traced. I would miss Liz greatly when you abandoned her. I\u2019d have to find a place to live too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeaking of where you live, have you thought about steam cleaning that Winnebago?\u201d Liz pointed at Billy Mack with her fork. \u201cGuys don\u2019t care what the clothes on their floor smell like, but if you\u2019re going to be spending time with girls...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow. \u201cI\u2019ll take it under advisement. Since that\u2019s settled, on to my and Jack\u2019s business from yesterday. We got quite a lesson on their politics and I believe it was not Michael White who sent our nightmares.\u201d I looked confusedly at them. Jack\u2019s mouth was set in a fucking line. \u201cTheir Autumn Court, currently in power, has powers based around fear. They also have a policy to only prey on \u2018douchebags\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put two and two together and glared at Jack while Billy Mack rambled on about hospitality or some fucking shit. \u201cThe goddamn motherfucking spider.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, yes.\u201d The g-man was nonplussed at my interruption. \u201cAnd while the dreams were disturbingly personal, I don\u2019t believe they know more than what we are afraid of and that we can write up supernatural contracts I have plans to repair our blunder, involving a tar