y Aura sensors and nudged Billy Mack to indicate she was a Changeling, and recognized us. I didn\u2019t have a signal to convey have much amusement she got at the idea of fucking with us. He walked the terrarium right up to the counter.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow can I help you fine young people today?\u201d the old woman asked sweetly, smiling impossibly fucking wide.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello ma\u2019am.\u201d The g-man was all politeness and smiles. \u201cWe were hoping to speak with a manager?\u201d<br /> <br /> She kept smiling. \u201cWell aren\u2019t you in luck? I am the acting manager until 2:30.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack cleared his throat. \u201cCan we talk in private?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease wait just a moment.\u201d She called to the back and an absolutely goddamn terrified human girl came out. \u201cI need you to watch the counter. Can you do that?\u201d The girl nodded. The Changeling smiled at us. \u201cWell behaved young people are so pleasant.\u201d<br /> <br /> I lingered behind a bit to give the girl a card and mouth \u2018in case you need help\u2019. I caught up easily as the old woman took a moment to open a door behind the desk that she then sat at. Once seated, she waited expectantly.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack began. \u201cI believe that you are aware that we may have made an error, last time we were here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNow, I don\u2019t know what you did to get on the douchebag list.\u201d She crinkled her nose. \u201cNot my choice of terms, you understand. But you did something rude, crude, or unnecessarily cruel...\u201d<br /> <br /> He cleared his throat. \u201cA spider got stepped on.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes fucking glinted. \u201cOh. You\u2019re those.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a rash overreaction to a reasonable security measure.\u201d Billy Mack spread his hands. \u201cHopefully you can understand bad reactions to authority. I can assure you, it will never happen again.\u201d He indicated the tarantula. \u201cThis is a peace offering, in hopes of a better future relationship.\u201d<br /> <br /> She considered the terrarium. \u201cit is not my place to remove anyone from the list. I can take your offering to the one who is, or arrange a meeting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am simply interested in putting this behind us in the most convenient way for you.\u201d The g-man emphasized the last two words, implying both her Court and her personally.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are very polite young people. I give you my word I will pass along your gift, and request he sends word of his decision, either way. He sometimes forgets such niceties.\u201d She clucked her tongue.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cI will certainly take you at your word. I do hope to avoid any unfortunate animosity. We are, truly, sorry.\u201d She returned his smile, a hair too goddamn wide. \u201cThe profuseness of your apology will be brought along as well. You should hear back shortly after nightfall.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs there anything we could do for you, specifically?\u201d Jack asked.<br /> <br /> Her smile widened. \u201cOh Sonny, I don\u2019t need anything, but you are quite kind.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIn that case, we\u2019ll stop taking up your time. I\u2019m William Mackenzie, but the way.\u201d Billy Mack stood as she did.<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJack.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded at each of us in turn. \u201cI am known as Little Grandmother. Any of my kind should know who that is.\u201d We followed her out and I nodded to the girl behind the counter. She only had terrified eyes for Little Grandmother though. As we were leaving, the last fucking thing we heard was \u201cWhy don\u2019t you go work in the back before you make me peckish?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> On the ride to the garage, it was obvious Jack was fucking chafing at the conversation. Billy Mack tried to talk him around. \u201cThink of what they could do against Michael White.\u201d<br /> <br /> The fixed sighed. \u201cSure. But we gotta have something to offer. I don\u2019t like not knowing what they want.\u201d He was about to elaborate when his phone rang.<br /> <br /> He picked it up and made noncommittal grunting noises at it for a few moments before passing it to me. \u201cSo I met your girlfriend,\u201d Naomi said brightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cJesus fuck what did you do?\u201d I sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing!\u201d She made kissing noises at me. It was a thing for today, apparently. \u201cI was *appropriately* polite, that\u2019s all. Just for you, cause I love you like a sister.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes. \u201cNot still in a snit then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah.\u201d She paused. \u201cI got over that by switching to Naomi and realizing I care about the house, not the previous occupant. Anyway, I was over at the campus cops power trip building - you know, where they keep their power wheels and sticks and dream about growing up and getting to use real guns? It\u2019s fucking adorable. But she ambushed me while I was getting Angela out...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAmbushed?\u201d I said warily.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, not really. She started talking to me and I was the only one that could see here, which would have been nice to know before I started talking to thin air in front of Cassandra and Am.\u201d She said something in English to someone over there. \u201cSo, she wasn\u2019t really happy with letting Angela out, since she\u2019s tainted and all. I talked her around though. Nothing compromising. I held back. For you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back in my seat. I was getting a goddamn headache. \u201cYou\u2019re a fucking peach, Naomi.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Breakfast at Shelly's</u></b><br /> <br /> Whatever initial reservations Shelly Waters might have had about being wooed by another woman have been laid quite firmly to rest. There was no real question of intentions as we drove back to her place and Vivian followed her inside. She seemed to exhibit that mixture of anxiety and excitement that humans typically do when they are aware that they are being incautious but choose not to alter their behavior. I believe that she was rightly nervous about allowing a relative stranger into her home with strong implications of intimacy following. However, Vivian is a woman, and a petite one at that. From both a societal and physical standpoint, she seems relatively harmless and fortunately for Miss Waters, my intentions do not run to any of the mundane depravities a woman must fear in such situations.<br /> <br /> There had been an awkward mixture of heavy flirting and innocent small talk during the ride, the manifestation of her lingering uncertainty. Once we were inside, I waited for her to secure the door and then as she turned to ask me if I'd like some coffee I acted decisively. In lieu of an answer, I pressed her back against the door with Vivian's fingers tangled in her hair and kissed her hard until I felt us both running short of breath. As expected, there was very little small talk until much later as we lay sweaty and lazily entangled in each other and her bedsheets in the dark.<br /> <br /> The next morning I slipped free of her and selected a suitable button down shift from the closet before making breakfast. Her kitchen was much better stocked than Speed's and the results were quite satisfactory. Miss Waters seemed rather surprised to wake to breakfast being brought to her in bed but was pleased well enough with the gesture that she reclaimed her shirt quite vigorously before we moved to the shower, ostensibly to wash up.<br /> <br /> While I did not have any objections to the way the day seemed to be developing, a text from Clytemnestra for a meeting of the agency arrived as we were toweling off. I told her I needed to go and see to some business and she asked if I was going to call her later. I gave her firm assurances and a firmer kiss before departing and changing to Billy Mack on the way to Alfredo's Feast-ro. It would appear Vivian has acquired a girlfriend.<br /> <br /> <u><b><br /> As Italian as Apple Pie</b></u><br /> <br /> Alfredo's Feast-ro was everything the name suggested. Apparently Alfredo himself is no longer among the living. I was not given the details, but I can only assume it was a tragic pasta related accident. And as a tribute to his departed friend, his partner kept the name. There is also the fact that Rafael's Feast-ro simply lacks the same je ne sais quoi.<br /> <br /> I was still quite sated from the breakfast Vivian had made for Shelly so I simply ordered a coffee and a slice of apple pie. It was, much like the Feast-ro itself, everything Speed promised.<br /> <br /> Far more important than the bitter coffee and questionable pastries was the news from the previous night's activities. Speed had made contact with and deepened her association with Miranda Asbury. Clytemnestra had successfully eased Robin Graves into the knowledge of what we are and taken her to seek the death-aspected car parts. Quietus had come to their aid and blown up several cars that a spirit of some sort was using as a makeshift body to defend the salvage yard.<br /> <br /> Without more information I cannot effectively calculate a plan to neutralize the spirit. If I can see it manifest I could employ Sum of All Fears, which is likely to give insight into what banes and bans it might have. As we do not count any werewolves among our allies, I did suggest that Speed use her new-found rapport with Miss Asbury to see if she is willing to help deal with the spirit tonight. Our alternatives are either to acquire the parts during the day, which would leave a potential paper trail back to Elizabeth Covington and thus the agency, or to shop out the search over other salvage yards. But our targeted one has the contract to dispose of vehicles from police evidence and thus the lion's share of the sort of death-tainted parts we require. Speed agreed to inquire about Miss Asbury's help as repairing the damage to reality is of interest to her. I cannot help but notice that Speed does seem to be growing attached to Miss Asbury. For the moment this does not appear to be an issue. I hope it remains that way.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra's fondness for Mrs Graves is more amusing. For one, as a Messenger and a sensualist she has a much healthier division of pleasure and emotional attachment. Despite what the others may feel, I rather suspect her snit over not being introduced to Mrs Graves' offspring was less about growing overly attached and more that the woman deigned to refuse her something she asked for. Had it been the former, I rather expect that rather than indulging in being upset over it she'd have used her powers to break the woman's will. As I find Mrs Graves pleasant enough company, I hope that she continues to be useful and entertaining in her free-willed state least she find herself worshiping her spider goddess to the exclusion of all else.<br /> <br /> By comparison, my own activities seemed rather frivolous. I shared them with the others anyway, as it is important to keep abreast of the details and potential complications of our various webs and cults and pawns. After all, I am most likely going to offer Shelly a pact that allows her to finish her degree, which would place her within the sphere of the university and Clytemnestra's pagan cult there. Quietus found it cold when I relayed my thoughts on that subject and felt the need to remind me that it is possible to offer a pact without a tangible reward. Without going into the power of obligation and gratitude over another, I did point out that Miss Waters could prove to be a competent lab assistant with such completed training. He did not seem overly pleased with that answer. He has certainly embraced the emotions of his new existence with gusto. Clytemnestra took the occasion to offer some suggestions regarding how best to approach same sex relationships with Vivian as she is more well-versed in the finer points of being a woman and especially seducing other women as one. Apparently the cleanliness of my dwelling is paramount. Vivian shall be making an appointment to have her Winnebago detailed next week.<br /> <br /> Once we had exchanged our information and discussed our options we broke for the afternoon. Quietus contacted Mr Creel about the timing of his search for Drake. Apparently the changeling had intended to do so in conjunction with the action against Jack Slenderskellingtonman but saw the wisdom in confirming if that is indeed Drake's captor ahead of time. We'll be using the power to attempt to locate Drake tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Speed contacted and secured Miranda Asbury's help with the spirit. I am looking forward to meeting her with great interest.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra needed to be seen on campus as Naomi and made arrangements while doing so to have Angela released into the custody of her religious leader. I believe this included a conversion by sword to Clytemnestra's cult on Angela's part. But she feels confident the girl will behave and she remains without the key to the Asbury Room.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Pet Shop Boy</u></b><br /> <br /> During lunch, I shared with Speed and Clytemnestra my realization as far as the source of our nightmares. Speed was less than pleased to say the least. However, things remained on track with a focus on corrective action over recriminations.<br /> <br /> While they were making their arrangements, I switched to Vivian and made my way back to the pet store where I'd acquired the feeder mice. Clytemnestra seemed mildly disappointed that I was toying with another so soon after leaving Shelly but I did not wish to pass up the opportunity. The boy that works there has such a painfully obvious and intense attraction to Vivian it is simply too tempting to ignore.<br /> <br /> I switched to Vivian and dressed her in something that showcased her without being quite immodest enough to risk being charged with public indecency. I waited outside the store a few minutes to insure that I would not run afoul of any later afternoon family shoppers. I was not looking to create that manner of scene and I wanted the lad to myself.<br /> <br /> Casey Rogers, as I learned his name was, proved to be quite helpful and adorably fixated while trying quite ineffectually to conduct himself otherwise. I gave him Vivian's name before I left with a new tarantula and all the supplies and such to go with its terrarium. If the boy receives a commission or at least has his sales monitored I imagine such a purchase will look favorable. And now that I have his name, I am sure I can find out more about him and find some suitable use for such a pliable and devoted admirer. If nothing else, one can only imagine he has a few noteworthy events he'd be happy to let someone else have endured.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Ganora might have some use for him? She is going to need a human to handle some of her cult's affairs. Though that would require him knowing about Billy Mack and convincing her not to make a snack out of the poor boy so perhaps not.<br /> <br /> <b><u><br /> My What Big Teeth You Have Grandmother</u></b><br /> <br /> I shifted back to Billy Mack as that is the form the Autumn Court is familiar with. In spite of the situation I was feeling rather pleased as I met my companions. I think Quietus was too focused on reigning in his temper to take notice but Speed shook her head and muttered about 'that poor fuck' under her breath as she assisted in gathering the supplies up.<br /> <br /> The coffee shop was quiet with a few customers sipping and chatting quietly or reading. The lone employee was an elderly woman who greeted us with a smile so wide and unsettling it would have made the Cheshire cat envious. Speed silently signaled that she was indeed a Changeling and we approached. I asked to speak to a manager and she informed me she was the one on duty. I said it was a matter of delicacy and asked if we could speak in private and she summoned a terrified girl from the back to watch the counter.<br /> <br /> The manager's office was small and plain. I presented the terrarium and explained that it was a peace offering. I offered profuse and sincere apologies and assured her I did not wish to be at odds with the Autumn Court. I explained that it had been a mistake to disrespect their hospitality and power and that we would most certainly never make it again. She did not miss the subtle implication. When you offer the hand of peace, it is important to keep the other hand ready to strike until it has been accepted. Also, as much as I dread the cost in resources that hostilities would mean, I am only prepared to offer so much contrition to these fear mongers.<br /> <br /> She explained that it was not her place to remove us from the douche list. She clearly found the term juvenile but it was not her place to change that either. She offered us her word that she would bring our offering and word of the sincerity of our apology to the proper individual. She also assured us that she would make sure that we received word of his decision either way. Apparently he is not always good about such things. I would imagine she was referring to the Havestman Rosanna spoke of but I cannot be certain. We thanked her and asked after her name, to which she told us that she was known simply as Little Grandmother.<br /> <br /> We departed as she set the human girl to task with threats of consumption. Fortunately, both of my companions held their tongues and let the creature's behavior go.<br /> <br /> Speed remained out of sorts over the whole affair and Quietus displayed a fair dose of contempt for having to come before these fae hat in hand and their attitude toward their position of power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Upgrade the Apparatus</u></b><br /> <br /> It was as yet early for investigating the salvage yard so the three of us decided to make productive use of the time while waiting for word from the Autumn Court. Speed made a call to secure a rental bay at the garage and we drove there.<br /> <br /> She and I set to work adding some of the other modifications she'd initially planned for the Mustang while Quietus busied himself with the gadget I had helped him sketch out ideas for. I offered, somewhat in jest, to change into Vivian but neither expressed an interest so I opted to save the Aether. It's better to not have her seen with Jack and Gabe anyway and I'll need to be Billy Mack later since that is the form Mrs Graves knows me in and the one Miss Asbury is most likely aware of from investigating her house and the campus. I do need to contact Miss Waters but I can text her from Vivian's phone once we're done here without changing.<br /> <br /> The work, both mundane and magical, went smoothly and quickly. The Mustang's capabilities are nearly optimal now with only a few tweaks before we reach the point where diminishing returns make further modification impractical. It has also gained the ability to rip open a portal to the Underworld to facilitate escape from extreme situations. Normally I would question the logic of driving a car into a realm composed entirely of rough terrain and caverns, but Speed is an excellent driver even by the high standards of her incarnation and that Mustang is an automotive enthusiast\u2019s wet dream. <br /> <br /> And with that done, it is time to gather Clytemnestra, Mrs Graves, and Miss Asbury and make our way to the salvage yard to see if we can find a way to subdue the spirit guardian.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Heya girlie! You doin\u2019 okay?<br /> <br /> Okay cool update on the current investigation.<br /> <br /> Okay, so I mentioned the whole mystery lady Miranda? Gabe had her date and apparently that worked out pretty well for her. In addition to the whole personal side of it (and I am hoping she can get some trim and calm the fuck down) she is now pretty sure Miranda is okay, but she is biased as hell.<br /> <br /> Yea, Mystery Lady Miranda does sound like an anime. <br /> <br /> I am not surprised you would watch it. You watch anything Japanese, which I think is weird, honestly. Anyway.<br /> <br /> I actually met Miranda, though I was trying to breath through on my work that night. Also, my stupid math teacher assigned homework over the weekend. Who does homework over the weekend? Seriously. Anyway, Miranda\u2026.I met her after we went to spring Angela.<br /> <br /> Oh, right. Angela was, according to Cassandra, finally getting a grip and no longer insane, though she still wanted to get in the fucking room, because of course she did, so I had to slap her around a bit. Since I was pretty sure she was not gonna gnaw any faces, I talked the glorified mall cops into letting her go and remanded her to the custody of her spiritual leader, that being Cassandra of course.<br /> <br /> So going back and forth and updating Gabe and stuff I ran across Miranda, standing under a tree. She began talking to me, and I cleverly noticed neither Am nor Cassandra could see or hear her. Which is kinda a dick move, honestly, since she did not clue me in. After getting all that sorted out, she wanted to know why I was releasing Angela. I noted Angela was less crazy, and that I did not care for cops. She never acknowledged sensing anything unusual about me, but as she was speaking invisibly to me I assume she did. Maybe inviso-stalking Gabe or something. Regardless, we parted ways amicably but she seemed pretty off. I mean, really attractive, but off. Not exactly sultry either\u2026not that that is a problem.<br /> <br /> Yea, Uniform and everything. Weird.<br /> <br /> Anyway I dunno. I\u2019ll keep you informed. For Gabe\u2019s sake I hope she is legit.<br /> <br /> Okay so Angela. She is still fixated on getting her key, but has been turned over to Cassandra and Am who are taking care of her. I really hope she stays calmed down, poor things. I noticed Miranda did not seem to care for Angela. Jealousy? I hope not that would be a bad sign.<br /> <br /> Oh, Miranda suggested looking into Dr. Kris-Kross. I should not let that sleeping dog lie. Nothing new, per se, just advising to look after her. I am thinking I will try to talk to her tomorrow, assuming she is not at her office. I am walking that way now.<br /> <br /> Nah Gabe is not with me, she and I think Vivian and Jack are working on her Mustang. Yea. It is, apparently, not fast enough. Well she is white so less likely to get pulled by the cops I guess.<br /> <br /> Oh lets see. Lady Covington and Jack and Lady Covington\u2019s Not! Girlfriend ran afoul some problems getting the materials to deal with the intrusions. I don\u2019t know the whole story, but Jack blew stuff up, as that is what the Jack do.<br /> <br /> Yea Dr. Kriss-Kross is not at her office.<br /> <br /> Okay so I think that covers it. More later and Deanna? My place tonight.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXII</i><br /> <br /> This session was mostly RP.<br /> <br /> I had a great deal of fun with Little Grandmother. Still looking for a good picture. Changeling, obviously.<br /> <br /> The breakfast at the, ahem, feast-ro was an extended and if I may say excellent role playing bit. Lots of IC banter, arguing, discussion and planning, all of which was very IC. Not that such is a surprise with my players, nay, it is an <i>expectation</i>, but that scene was especially good.<br /> <br /> Good session. More to come. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:12:13-07:00","id":613897,"title":"","content":"So, some of the players were talking, and we wondered if people had theories about who was playing which characters in the various WoD games I have up. So I figured we would offer a chance at discussion of it. In order to protect identities of players, I have not been in a habit of confirming links between players between games. But if you are curious and follow more than one game you can ask. Anything else you ask about will be up to the players if they want to answer. But I will confirm or deny common links between characters if you ask.<br /> <br /> Some facts<br /> <br /> In the four New WoD and one Classic WoD games there are 13 different players. 2 are/were in all five games. 1 is in four games, 4 are in three games, and 6 are only in one game each, at least of WoD games.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d rather you be nice\u2026I don\u2019t want to hear \u201cI think player A plays X and Y because they suck\u201d or anything, I am proud of my players. A number of them will be peering in to enjoy this too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you have any theories I would enjoy hearing them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T14:42:20-07:00","id":627962,"title":"","content":"Another Day, Another Possessed Auto Graveyard killing you by throwing cars. Just a typical day for (dramatic music) The Night Train Detective Agency! (Ba-Dum!)<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> All in all, the work on the car took about two fucking hours. Me and Billy Mack boosted the max speed and acceleration in an hour each. Jack\u2019s deal was more goddamn complicated, and took the whole two hours. He explained it again as we made our getaway from the garage. We really didn\u2019t want to have to fucking account for the localized thunderstorm. \u201cActivate it here, and the whole car will go through a portal to the Underworld. Just the car and what\u2019s in it, nothing on top or behind.\u201d I eyed the panel and its sucking black hole, raising an eyebrow at him. He shrugged. \u201cWanted to make sure you didn\u2019t mistake it for a lighter.\u201d<br /> <br /> My sneering response was interrupted by a call from Naomi. I put her on speaker. \u201cBadass fireworks hombre. I noticed they stopped, everything go well?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed. We are now spelunking-capable.\u201d Billy Mack said from the back, holding onto the oh shit handle.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I am right the fuck out of Aether.\u201d Jack did look pretty goddamn wiped.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked concerned. \u201cThe dam is too far, and we shouldn\u2019t hit Peterson before our operation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe really should hit the Works up soon, get bits for our own Infrastructure.\u201d I pointed out for the goddamn billionth fucking time.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe do, but we don\u2019t have time tonight.\u201d Jack pointed out. Hell, he did have a point. \u201cWe need to get a bunch and have stashes in various places - the agency, the Asbury House...\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cYou do remember that doesn\u2019t belong to us, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> He fucking waved me away. \u201cArrangements can be made.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not stealing my girlfriend\u2019s house either.\u201d I gave him a look.<br /> <br /> The look only grew more goddamn aggravated when he kept on. \u201cI meant more like adding to the family.\u201d<br /> <br /> Not being one to let a fucking opportunity by, Naomi piped up. \u201cSpeed can\u2019t do that without another cover.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then the goddamn g-man joined in. \u201cYou probably don\u2019t want to use your homeless cover for that. At least, Miranda probably doesn\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s bi, right?\u201d Naomi shrugged. \u201cOr Liz could sleep with some dude and zap it over.\u201d Her voice changed to Liz\u2019s. \u201cNo. Anyway, Jack dear, go to my house and use the hookah. Also, Gabe, feel free to give Jack my charged cell phone. He does look a bit peaked.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked taken aback. \u201cThanks. I hate to impose...\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi had her own fucking voice back. \u201cNo problem. Just sit there and look pretty and don\u2019t talk to strangers - I mean, people we don\u2019t know. Don\u2019t talk to them.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> We had plenty of time to all get out little boosts from the goddamn cell phones and for Jack to hit Liz\u2019s hookah. We even had time for him to come down off his fucking high. So it was a sober Jack and Billy Mack in the back seat when I pulled up to the drive Miranda had me pick her up at.<br /> <br /> She was wearing a pair of cowboy boots and dark jeans, topped off with a nice white button up. She looked good, and I guess she noticed me spending a little too much time appreciating the way she filled the outfit out, since she greeted me with \u201cI hope this will blend in sufficiently?\u201d after a kiss.<br /> <br /> All I said was \u201cPerfectly.\u201d as I held the door open for her. I introduced the guys once she was all buckled in and started towards the junkyard.<br /> <br /> Jack ignored Naomi\u2019s advice and started up right the fuck off. \u201cSo, I dunno much about mage stuff, but I heard something about Seers of the Throne...\u201d<br /> <br /> She interrupted him quickly. \u201cYou should not throw that name around lightly. They have rotes in place that alert them if people are paying attention.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, that\u2019s not fair.\u201d Jack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2018Fair\u2019 is not in their playbook. If someone IDs as a Seer of the Throne, shoot them in the back of the head as soon as they turn around.\u201d It was a detached sort of vehemence, but passionate nonetheless. Jack looked even more incredulous. \u201cThey believe you are aberrations in the hum of reality, pieces working out of order.\u201d That set Jack twitching. I\u2019d told him he\u2019d appreciate her current predicament. \u201cI joined them because I thought they served as guardians and caretakers of reality, to keep out that which must not be.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike the house?\u201d I asked quietly. She nodded.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack cleared his throat. \u201cWhat changed?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI came to realize they believed the word of gods who had every reason to lie to them, that they would come to inherit this reality, and this was the sum of their cares.\u201d Her face was impassive as she watched the two in the back.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, if you ever need any backup against these fuckers, I\u2019m there.\u201d Jack managed to unclench his jaw long enough to offer.<br /> <br /> She gave him something of a smile. \u201cAny other questions I have deeply uncomfortable answers for?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack leaned forward. \u201cI believe you\u2019re due for asking, if you have any for us.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cBest if I don\u2019t know too much I could reveal under torture.\u201d She sat back in the seat, looking over at me.<br /> <br /> The g-man chuckled. \u201cReasonable. I like you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes and smiled over at her. She smiled back, then glanced over at the Maserati as we pulled into the junkyard lot. Seeing Liz, she frowned slightly. \u201cIf that is your other member, where is the pink haired one with the smart mouth?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot with us for this mission.\u201d Billy Mack said quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe needed a break from her smart mouth.\u201d I muttered.<br /> <br /> Miranda looked a little confused. \u201cIs she not your friend?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack and I shrugged. He answered first. \u201cShe is. But still... breaks are nice sometimes. Doesn\u2019t mean we don\u2019t have her back.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda shrugged as well. \u201cShe mostly smart mouthed her friends. She was very civil to me, comparatively.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll have to remember to thank her a little more sincerely.\u201d I grinned.<br /> <br /> Liz raised an eyebrow at me as she moved into earshot of that last comment. She had hung back at her car, fucking whispering with Robin, who was eying Miranda. Once they got over here, Liz introduced herself to Miranda and Robin asked to speak with me privately.<br /> <br /> \u201cYour girlfriend needs serious medical attention. I - all her organs are damaged, seriously. She, I mean, by all rights, should be dead.\u201d She looked almost fucking green.<br /> <br /> I looked back over at Miranda. \u201cI, uh, thanks. I appreciate the heads up.\u201d<br /> <br /> She glanced over at her too, then away. \u201cShe\u2019d kinda hard to look at, like someone\u2019s bleeding out.\u201d She looked back at me. \u201cBut, I mean, she seems like she\u2019s fine, you know?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded and thanked her as we walked back to the group. Liz had already swapped to her goddamn beautiful spider form. Miranda was appreciating the view, but at our footsteps, she turned to look back at me and caught me watching her. \u201cYou\u2019ve been a bad influence on me,\u201d she said as she took my hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019ve got surveillance up.\u201d Jack jerked his head at the cameras. \u201cI could take them out, but I\u2019d need to hit the fuse box, so it would take the lights out too, for all the good they do.\u201d<br /> <br /> I glanced at Robin and Miranda and shrugged. \u201cI can handle it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could just hide our faces...\u201d Liz suggested.<br /> <br /> \u201cOooh! With Daft Punk helmets?\u201d Robin looked goddamn excited.<br /> <br /> Miranda looked at me for an explanation. \u201cA band with stupid looking helmets.\u201d<br /> <br /> She touched her hair. \u201cI don\u2019t want to wear stupid looking helmets.\u201d She sounded a little unsure.<br /> <br /> I winked at her. \u201cNah. Really, I got this.\u201d<br /> <br /> I went full demon form, swapping my Angel sensors for a fucking floodlight while Jack and Billy Mack found the goddamn fuse box and EMPed it. The place was pitch black for a moment before I lit up the yard. Then we started moving quickly.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d chosen a treaded truck this time, to haul our loot and get through the cluttered as hell junkyard without problems. Robin pointed gave directions and pointed out useful bits that Liz grabbed up using her goddamn long legs. Miranda and the boys kept an eye out for the fucking spirit.<br /> <br /> Miranda spotted it first, as it was manifesting. \u201cHe\u2019s a mean one.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked it over with my Aura sight, figuring at least I\u2019d be able to ID the fuckers in the future. My read agreed with Miranda\u2019s. \u201cYeah. It\u2019s not about protecting the place or anything, it only cares about fucking us up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks.\u201d Billy Mack had gotten armored up and was peering out the window. \u201cThose of us with a conscience are now OK with fighting it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen why are you the one thanking me?\u201d I raised a goddamn eyebrow.<br /> <br /> He almost fucking smirked at me. \u201cBecause now I won\u2019t be the only one fighting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt appears to be a murder spirit that\u2019s eaten many damaged car spirits.\u201d Miranda mused.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThat matches thematically with its ban and bane. It can best be hurt by a weapon that someone used to murder someone who hurt them. And it can\u2019t harm or even push past anyone who\u2019s never wanted to hurt someone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, fuck that.\u201d Robin said. \u201cThat\u2019s impossible. But for the first thing - could a keystone work? I don\u2019t have it on me, but I could get one.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack thought for a moment. \u201cIf it fits the other requirements, surely.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack stared at him like he\u2019d grown another goddamn head. \u201cThe hell you say? You trying to make it more powerful?\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man raised an eyebrow. I revved my engine. Close as I could get to fucking clearing my throat. \u201cEither way, it\u2019s not here, we are, that\u2019s for later.\u201d<br /> <br /> The fixer gave Billy Mack a look, but climbed out of the car, flanking the forming car conglomeration with him. I upped the speed a little, but it recognized Jack, and went for him first, tossing a goddamn compact car at him. It turned its attention to me next. Well, probably to Miranda, considering whatever she was doing had caused gravity to reverse inside the car. That\u2019s a weird fucking feeling when you\u2019re the car.<br /> <br /> I dodged the next thrown car, while Jack climbed out from under the last car, to set up the monster\u2019s center of mass to fucking explode when Billy Mack put a rivet into it. The shrapnel put a long scratch down my side and a deep gash in Liz\u2019s arm, even with evasive maneuvering. Jack managed to get away with just a souvenir courtesy of his calf and it only barely dented Billy Mack\u2019s armor.<br /> <br /> We kept up with the scavenging, keeping an eye out for it to reform. After a moment, Miranda sighed and relaxed some. \u201cIt\u2019s angry, and thinking about what to do. I siphoned much of its energy, so we have some time.\u201d<br /> <br /> I followed Robin\u2019s direction as we got the rest of the scrap in record fucking time and Billy Mack consulted with Miranda. \u201cSince you\u2019ve gotten a more detailed look, do you believe it is confined to the area?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI would guess so, for now. This place resonates with it strongly, but it might grow powerful enough to make its way elsewhere.\u201d She shrugged.<br /> <br /> They discussed the particulars on the way to the agency where I dropped off the boys and the parts. Billy Mack looked at me significantly as we got back in the car. \u201cGet a good night\u2019s sleep. You\u2019ll feel better in the morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure I will.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda and I were mostly silent on the short drive back to the school, and I walked her to her room, where she kissed me again and said good night. I held onto her hand. \u201cLook, Princess, I don\u2019t want to pry, so tell me to fuck off if you don\u2019t wanna talk about it but... Robin can tell how healthy someone is at a glance. And, well, she\u2019s pretty sure you\u2019re not doing too good in the having working organs department.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have them working well enough. They were damaged by abyssal exposure.\u201d She sighed. \u201cI told you not even the one got away. My physical form has been damaged by the things I\u2019ve done.\u201d<br /> <br /> I lifted her chin to look at me. \u201cBut... you are, well, alright, for lack of a better word?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked me in the eyes. \u201cHonest assessment - I\u2018m not well. Magic is what\u2019s keeping me alive and it has its side effects. But I\u2019m not dying.\u201d<br /> <br /> I managed a smile. \u201cI just wanted to make sure...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry I couldn't tell you anything more comforting.\u201d She squeezed my hand.<br /> <br /> I gave her a lopsided grin and went in for another kiss. \u201cIt\u2019s comforting enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I went for a drive. I needed to clear my fucking head and more importantly, not do something goddamn stupid like break into Dantaine\u2019s house to use his library. My flask started out full and the highway largely empty. It worked.<br /> <br /> I had something close to an idea when I got an email from Liz. It was titled \u2018Fwd: Um...\u2019 and Liz\u2019s preamble of \u2018WTF\u2019 led into the forwarded message \u2018So, is this your thing? Robin\u2019 Attached were a collection of pictures of the junkyard being fucking patrolled by a pair of people with a pair of dogs. I use both nouns goddamn loosely, as the \u2018dogs\u2019 had human eyes and overly wide grins and the \u2018people\u2019\u2019s skin was inhumanly jet black and they had no fucking facial features. It was time stamped about twenty minutes after we left the junkyard.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack responded first. \u2018Doesn\u2019t look like angels. Mages? Miranda did throw around some power there.\u2019<br /> <br /> I had the dialer open before the rest of the message even fucking registered. Miranda answered after only a couple of rings with a groggy \u201cHello sweetie.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey darling. Sorry to wake you but...\u201d I described the figures in the photo. \u201cThey\u2019re not people from my past, so I wanted to make sure they weren\u2019t going to be after you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUh, that doesn\u2019t ring any bells.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cIt sounds like it could be someone who keeps a pet murder spirit. Or they might be manifested spirits themselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let out a breath. \u201cAlright. Sorry, again, for waking you up, I just wanted to make sure.. So you know exactly what they look like, just in case they manage to track any of us down, do you have a way I can send you pictures?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike the email? I had one. Um... <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#de93b7acbf9f9eb6b1aab3bfb7b2f0bdb1b3\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"04496d766545446c6b7069656d682a676b69\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>, I think?\u201d I don't even know if I still have access to it.\u201d She sounded sheepish.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cNo worries. Maybe we\u2019ll get you set up with a new one. Or even a cell phone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAren\u2019t those really distracting?\u201d she said driftily.<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe in your willpower.\u201d<br /> <br /> She made a doubtful noise. \u201cIf I had any, I wouldn\u2019t be in this situation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe in your willpower regarding such frivolities?\u201d I offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re sweet Gabe,\u201d she muttered, a smile in her voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cGet back to sleep beautiful. I\u2019ll see you later.\u201d I smiled to myself.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cGood night Gabe. Love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled down at the phone and then another fucking notification came up. I responded with Miranda\u2019s lack of recognition. Before I sent it, something occurred to me. \u2018Who took the pics?\u2019<br /> <br /> Liz took a moment to respond. \u2018\u201cSkeevy Larry\u201d Who calls himself Skeevy Larry?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Someone named Larry, who is skeevy\u2019 was Billy Mack\u2019s quick response.<br /> <br /> The retort was quick as well. \u2018I truly am in awe of your genius\\Naomi\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Thank you.\u2019 Billy Mack responded, probably sincerely, the fuck. \u2018Had some luck with the hard drive. Sanderson was a patient too, with lots of procedure codes. Some stuff about a Goldwater incident we should look into. And Stein apparently likes long moonlit walks in the shadier parts of town.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018That\u2019s lovely but /\\o00o/\\ zZzZ\u2019 was Liz\u2019s final comment, and I sure as hell didn\u2019t bother responding.<br /> <br /> <br /> I nodded to Billy Mack as I poured a cup of coffee. The four or so hours of sleep were just fucking barely enough and the coffee helped some. The whiskey I poured into helped more. He handed me some goddamn letter. I took it, but wandered over to the window instead of reading it. If I had timed it right... there we go. Shorts short enough you couldn\u2019t see them below her fucking shirt, which read \u2018I\u2019m Here, You\u2019re Welcome\u2019 and boots touching the bottom of that shirt. She walked in the door and two seconds later another goddamn argument erupted in Portuguese. I waited, looking expectantly at the door until Naomi told Cecilia to \u201csit there and get old - it seems to be what you do best.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shared a look with the g-man and caught a glimpse of the research he\u2019d been doing overnight. The corner of the screen was a picture of a wide-eyed kid labeled Casey Rogers. From what I could see, it was the kid from the goddamn pet shop. \u201cThat poor fuck.\u201d Naomi walked in just then and looked inquisitively at me. I jerked my head towards the computer.<br /> <br /> She looked fucking disapprovingly at him. \u201cDon\u2019t you have a girlfriend?\u201d Billy Mack shrugged and brought up a different desktop, this one with Shelley\u2019s picture showcased.<br /> <br /> I remember the letter Billy Mack handed me and took the moment to read it over. \u2018Everything\u2019s fine dears. You just be good and respectful now (and wash behind your ears). Grandmama\u2019 I tossed it back at him. \u201cFucking great.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi sighed goddamn theatrically, standing next to the couch before kicking up her feet and falling out flat on it. \u201cSo, any questions for Dr. Cross or am I just sticking her in the ass and getting a blood sample? Also, where are the hypos?\u201d Billy Mack and I both pointed at their drawer. \u201cThat\u2019s what I meant of course. Any other ass sticking doesn\u2019t involve drawing blood.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMost don\u2019t enjoy bloodletting that much.\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> Naomi shrugged, as goddamn sheepish as I\u2019d ever fucking heard her. Not that that was very. \u201cUnless it\u2019s me. But I guess my saliva would taint the sample and I might get the clap of evil.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded and turned to me. \u201cI don't suppose a similar caution would help?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNope.\u201d I smirked at him.<br /> <br /> He fucking turned back to the computer. \u201cBesides, dealing with the tainted places might be enough to get any of us infected.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStill, no reason not to dental dam it up!\u201d Naomi pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks.\u201d I said goddamn sarcastically. She gestured at the \u2018You\u2019re welcome\u2019 on the shirt.<br /> <br /> \u201cCrusher is looking for Drake this afternoon, but doesn\u2019t need or expect our presence, correct? Jack nodded in response to the g-man\u2019s question. \u201cPerhaps we should pay Peterson a visit then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s the plan for that? Smash and grab? I mean, I\u2019m not the saboteur...\u201d Naomi leaned back on the couch, her eyes shut.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cNeither am I, and I\u2019d rather fucking not. For one, it would be nice to see if we could get, I dunno, medicine or some shit, since we know it\u2019s like a goddamn infection. For Angela and Dr. Cross.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd your girlfriend, right?\u201d Naomi opened one eye. \u201cMaybe. If she\u2019s infected.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. If she\u2019s infected.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> Naomi smiled and pointed at the cabinet. \u201cHypos are in there. Or maybe you want to give her a full physical.\u201d She raised an fucking eyebrow. \u201cOr did you give her one last night?\u201d She kept on about dental dams as I walked over to the arm of the couch she was resting her goddamn head on. \u201cHey, who -\u201d she sputtered as I got her in a headlock and put my hand over her mouth.<br /> <br /> I looked at Billy Mack, ignoring Naomi\u2019s tongue on my palm. \u201cSo we go in quiet, get the fucking spackle made and plan on hitting them up for the goddamn medicine later?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI should be able to determine what materials we need while the spackle is being created.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat.\u201d I let Naomi go and rubbed the hand she\u2019d fucking licked on her goddamn head.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, hey, hey! No rubbing the pink without permission!\u201d Naomi batted at my hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think that\u2019s more fuchsia.\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> Naomi looked at him goddamn blankly. \u201cI don\u2019t understand English.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked fucking amused. \u201cDon\u2019t you have class Naomi?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, that was this morning. Unless you mean that other class, that I\u2019m not burdened with. The Communism, you know. Or maybe it comes from being politically Canadian. Or are those the same thing?\u201d Naomi went back to stretching out on the goddamn couch.<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe politically Canadian would be more socialism.\u201d The g-man fucking played along.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever. I don't even know what that is, except rich white people don't like it, so I do.\u201d She rested her head on her hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about anchovies?\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at Billy Mack. \u201cThe fuck?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cRich white people don\u2019t like that either.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNobody likes anchovies.\u201d Naomi thought for a moment. \u201cAnd Liz is rich and white and she doesn\u2019t like anchovies, so I don\u2019t have to either.\u201d She waved the two of us off. \u201cAnyway, my class is not really in question. I\u2019ll come with to Peterson. Dr. Cross is not going anywhere, unless things get much worse. Maybe I\u2019ll set up a tiger trap outside Cass\u2019s. She falls in, I jump in after, kissy noises and I pop up with a full hypo.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen the hell did we get into a fucking cartoon?\u201d I asked the room, taking another drink.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack ignored both of us. \u201cIt will be good to have the medicine. Miranda is almost certainly tainted. At this point,\u201d the fucker looked right the hell at me, \u201cburning out that infection would be inadvisable, not only for Speed\u2019s sake, but having seen some of what she does, it would be an inefficient use of energy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhoa, whoa, whoa. How hard it would be to set her on fire is irrelevant.\u201d Naomi interrupted. I nodded, mouth set. \u201cI think we should have a no burning of significant others policy. Never again the Burning Times and all that shit.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cUnless they betray us to the God Machine. Then I\u2019ll have the marshmallows and long pork please.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack sighed. \u201cAlright. No burning them with fire. Cleansing, cleansing fire.\u201d We stared at him. \u201c...it was a joke.\u201d<br /> <br /> He got a text and read it impassively. \u201cYour girlfriend?\u201d Naomi asked. He nodded. \u201cYou really should do something nice for her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was thinking flowers.\u201d He shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cLike, delivered to her door? Not her work surely, unless you know she\u2019s out. Otherwise, people will ask who it\u2019s from and she\u2019ll have to say they\u2019re from her boyfriend, Staniel or Danley.\u201d Naomi looked goddamn defensively at me taking an exaggerated fucking drink. \u201cWhat? Humans are bad at lying on the spot.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked fucking bemused. \u201cI\u2019m not sure whether she\u2019s out or not, but I was going to bring them on my next date.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi rolled her eyes and laid an arm over her eyes. \u201cSure, if you wanna be predictable. At least you know to make your tools feel nice.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI find they work much more efficiently.\u201d He fucking stroked a microscope. \u201cWho\u2019s a good microscope? You are!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I can think about anything else but what just happened, Gabe, have you asked your girlfriend about Working as Intended?\u201d Naomi looked at me upside down, leaning over the armrest.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cDidn't really come up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWould you be terribly put out if I do?\u201d Billy Mack asked, leaving his fucking microscope alone.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs long as you don\u2019t ask her if you can keep it, you can ask her whatever the hell you want about what you saw when you broke into her house.\u201d I poured another cup of coffee and whiskey.<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cWe thought she was dead at the time, to be fair.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked the fuck up from his paperwork. \u201cHey, we didn\u2019t break into the place, it was unlocked.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi stretched. \u201cAh, the best part of college. If a door\u2019s unlocked, you can go right in. If you see weed, you can smoke it. Unless there\u2019s some previously established rule set up. Even then, if you\u2019re cute enough, it doesn\u2019t matter.\u201d She pointed up triumphantly. \u201cCollege!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe my next cover should be a college student...\u201d Billy Mack smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cEveryone should have a college cover. It\u2019s great except for the classes. The art ones are alright. I\u2019d recommend against English for Gabe though.\u201d I flipped her off. \u201cSee, it gives her the rage just thinking about it. But seriously, it\u2019s cool, you don\u2019t have to be well educated for me to respect you. Not saying I do, but it\u2019s not for that reason.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pushed my hair back from my eyes and rubbed my temples. \u201cJesus fuck. Let\u2019s just get going.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Hey cutie! Class go okay?<br /> <br /> Cool, cool. So apparently big shit went down last night with the Agency. They got the stuff requested and all and dealt with the big junkyard monster, but did not kill it. It is a spirit, apparently.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how big, I was not there.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s done, and we can take steps to get your case done! Grand, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Awww c\u2019mon, you can sound more excited than that. <br /> <br /> Fine, save your voice then.<br /> <br /> So they are having me along for the next step, which is why I am putting on a catsuit and\u2026<br /> <br /> There you go sweetie! Want one from the back?<br /> <br /> Oh yeah.<br /> <br /> Anyway, am getting ready\u2026we are just stepping out for a few for some minor stuff. Gabe put me in a damn headlock though. I dunno why. I don\u2019t think she wanted me to talk to Dr. Kriss-Kross. Everyone seemed pretty okay with it, which fucking blows. Even Jack.<br /> <br /> I know right? Where would they even be without me?<br /> <br /> Okay talk to ya later doll.<br /> <br /> o o o o<br /> <br /> Kayla? Liz. Hey.<br /> <br /> Did you get the email\u2026right.<br /> <br /> So we went back to that junkyard, and the spirit was still there. Miranda, Speed\u2019s lady, said it was a Murder Spirit who had absorbed a number of car spirits\u2026really nasty one too. It attacked us but was drained when Quietus detonated it\u2019s body\u2026Speed was actually driving around with Robin and Miranda\u2026.it was funny. Robin was showing me what to grab, and I was doing it.<br /> <br /> No, Speed was the car.<br /> <br /> Heh.<br /> <br /> Explosions suck, by the way. So, We got the stuff and got out. Quietus had wiped out the security stuff with his EMP, so nothing was recorded.<br /> <br /> Right, the pictures. Robin sent those to me. Someone she calls \u201cSkeevy Larry\u201d sent them. A member of the Krewe I assume, or a well equipped ghost. Do you have\u2026you know\u2026any idea what that could be?<br /> <br /> Hmmmm\u2026me either. Creepy as hell tho.<br /> <br /> Before we do anything else (or Kilroy gets distracted) we are hitting a local Infrastructure for some Aether\u2026even after ravaging my stores they are short. Also, hopefully going to get the, as Kilroy calls it, \u201cReality Spackle\u201d ready. I\u2019ll be \u201cwearing pink\u201d just because I am enjoying the hell of it. Did you know Speed broke her calm enough to actually put her in the headlock? I totally win.<br /> <br /> Take care. If I don\u2019t send a message saying we got out okay, get help. <br /> <br /> Nah, we will be fine. Take care you.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIII</i><br /> <br /> The Spirit was obviously a hybrid, Miranda pretty much had down what it was. As for her powers\u2026I am rusty as hell at Mage, but I think I got everything mostly right sorta. The battle was mostly between the creatures, Kilroy and Quietus, as Speed was evading and Clytemnestra was gathering. Otherwise the spirit was covered last entry.<br /> <br /> What were the things at the end? What indeed.<br /> <br /> If you read this and other game journals, note the comments above about guessing about common players. We are curious what you think. Though comments and questions of other sorts are welcome as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:41:59-07:00","id":644635,"title":"","content":"The trip to Peterson Chemical was not without incident. The Agency encounters it\u2019s guardian, and a familiar face from session one.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Billy Mack filled us in on the way there - the layout, the procedure and each of our bits in it. He was manning the computer, of course. Jack and I were on pickup and delivery, respectively, and Naomi was on overwatch. Despite her smart ass strong back comments, I somehow managed to not strangle the mouthy broad on the way to Peterson and once we were there, the need for stealth finally got her to shut the fuck up. We powered on our various form powers outside the place. I stuck with my radio suite and reflective plating, since in an ideal world, our plan amounted to a lot of hurry up and wait for fifteen minutes, while not being seen.<br /> <br /> Reality had apparently been taking goddamn lessons from one pink haired dame, and tried to give me some fucking lip, but I did manage to convince it that a back door was left open and in we went. I was almost to my position, and thought I was free and fucking clear for the wait portion of things, when from a door I\u2019d just passed came a singsong voice. \u201cCome out, come out, wherever you are! We have candy. And hugs.\u201d It paused. \u201cSo many hugs. The first ones free. The rest of them are free too.\u201d<br /> <br /> I was still processing what the hell I\u2019d just heard when the sound of metallic footsteps got to the door. I ducked around a corner, then another as quickly as possible. The Guardian (I presumed) noticed the movement, but missed my second turn, so I got a peek at the fucker as he moved past the doorway. It was a big bastard, with mirrored shades and goddamn heavy duty armor. The defined abs and angelic as shit codpiece made the too-young-to-be-gendered-without-a-fucking-bassinet-lining child\u2019s voice all the more goddamn creepy. The self assured way it held the fucking big ass cannon one handed didn\u2019t help.<br /> <br /> It paused, looking around, while I stood stock still, until an explosion went off outside the goddamn facility. \u201cMore hugs! I dunno if I brought enough,\u201d the fucking psycho babbled, not moving its mouth. It stalked off towards the noise, armored boots clinking on the metallic floor.<br /> <br /> I took the opportunity to make it over to the fucking loader and put in the materials we\u2019d gathered. The machine started running shortly after, and I took up my position to watch. So I had a primo view of the line of molten metal being carved into the door from the other side. I\u2019d have said it was a goddamn laser cutter. I\u2019d have been wrong. It was Puriel, her sword blazing as she stepped through the smoldering remains, as fucking hot as ever.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh bad word.\u201d The piping child\u2019s voice sounded fucking disappointed. \u201cDon\u2019t you know you\u2019re not supposed to be here? Now I\u2019ll have to cut off your skin with my gun.\u201d Its tone brightened with the thought.<br /> <br /> Puriel looked at the goddamn Guardian levelly. \u201cI\u2019m afraid I\u2019m going to have to cause one more explosion. It\u2019ll be a big one.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Guardian cocked its head. \u201cI\u2019m afraid I\u2019m going to have to keep your eyes.\u201d It paused and began firing its laser cannon at her. \u201cI\u2019m not afraid. I\u2019m just going to do it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Puriel saved her breath to dodge, staying a step ahead of the continuous laser beam it had trained on her. She made no attempt to fight back, reacting defensively, but it wasn\u2019t hard to see, if you weren\u2019t a goddamn psychotic Hugbot, that she was leading its beam to some of the more sensitive, explosion prone equipment in the facility. Not the lynch pin - Demons wouldn\u2019t be distracted by the place if she destroyed that - but just about as goddamn worrisome for our fucking needs.<br /> <br /> The same thought must have occurred to our Saboteurs, as the goddamn fire suppression system turned on, filling the place with steam and chemical extinguishing agents. It caught Puriel\u2019s attention, but Hugbot ignored it in favor of fucking target fixation. That wasn\u2019t broken until something exploded as soon as its laser hit it.<br /> <br /> Puriel got some distance on the other Guardian as it stopped and scanned the component that exploded. It frowned. \u201cMore friends. Need more hugs. Need more arms!\u201d<br /> My eyes widened as I just fucking barely managed to flood the channel Hugbot was using to send a distress signal with noise. Its eyes narrowed but I had enough forethought to cut off the intercom transmission ordering the goddamn cultists to use the control room Billy Mack was in to send a wired message.<br /> <br /> A moment\u2019s work decrypted the distress signal. The message was easy, if as fucking disturbing as everything else the fucker said - \u2018Puriel is here, with more friends. Need teddy bears for a picnic.\u2019 The target was the harder part, but I eventually extracted it from the code. It was about what I suspected - the Tower. Worse, a garbled header had arrived there. I sent my own message along Hugbot\u2019s channel, copying its packaging, to say \u2018Puriel was here. I gave her a hug, and she left to give the dam a hug. They need teddy bears for a picnic.\u2019 I was simultaneously proud of myself and feeling in need of a goddamn bath after picking up psychotic-ese so quickly.<br /> <br /> The situation pissed Hugbot the fuck off and it started stalking Puriel with a vengeance. It slithered into and out of pipes and ventilation shafts, using its mobility to attempt to terrorize and herd Puriel. \u201cI\u2019m gonna make a doll with your pretty skin. And give the doll your friend\u2019s eyes. And maybe, if your friend\u2019s skin is pretty, I\u2019ll make them into their own dolls...\u201d It did leave off using the goddamn laser, but its pistol shots were getting disturbingly close. It kept glancing up at the control room, but didn\u2019t seem willing to leave Puriel on her own.<br /> <br /> Naomi\u2019s voice whispered in my ear. \u201cWhat do you want me to do? I can talk with her this way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe need to maintain the fucking stalemate.\u201d I muttered in response.<br /> <br /> Jack reflected a brief flash of light at Naomi. \u201cJack\u2019s plan if that if she can hold out for ten minutes, we\u2019ll help her escape,\u201d Naomi passed on to me after a moment, \u201cand Puriel agrees.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded to her and moved slowly up to the command center. I stayed low, beneath the window and closed the door. \u201cNaomi\u2019s got the broad wrapped around her finger and I\u2019ve got the fucking psycho\u2019s channels locked down. We should be good.\u201d I explained the details of the plan to the g-man.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. She is an excellent distraction, but I was worried the fight would not last.\u201d Billy Mack was focused on the screen. He glanced at me quickly. \u201cPresumably, given the Infrastructure remains intact and security is not overly high, we should be able to make something to remove the taint from human tissue. I have the schematics.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat.\u201d I took up watch at the window, after jamming a chair under the goddamn door.<br /> <br /> With about four minutes left on the timer, Hugbot got in a fucking lucky shot, grazing Puriel\u2019s arm. Naomi shrieked, a rising tone that shattered every goddamn glass container in the area, before melting into a pile of spiders and scattering.<br /> <br /> Hugbot shook its head and peered through the growing clouds of greenish red gas. It didn\u2019t seem too fucking concerned with the collapsing cultists, except as obstacles. To be fair, the chemicals were designed to keep something asleep. Barring a fucking overdose or some shit, they were probably just knocked the hell out.<br /> <br /> It was enough to throw the psychotic fuck off its game though. It didn\u2019t even get close to Puriel again, and when the timer was up, Billy Mack motioned me out. The whole floor smelled like a sulfur pool with extra chlorine to compensate and the pools of water were warm to the touch. Clytemnestra noticed us leaving through the now orange clouds of gas and swarmed Hugbot. \u201cSome many spiders!\u201d So. Many. Spiderhugs!\u201d it screeched.<br /> <br /> \u201cRun!\u201d Jack yelled as he slung a wrench at an outer wall like he was a fucking Apple mascot, shattering it. Puriel was out and away by the time we got to the car and found Naomi passed out there.<br /> <br /> I started driving as the g-man revived her. He took her vitals, asking her \u201cAre you alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cConsidering I lost 96% of my body mass...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat would be why I was asking, yes.\u201d He looked at her sternly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be alright, just need a big juicy burger.\u201d She smiled at him.<br /> <br /> I gave an audible sniff. Jack and Naomi fucking stank of chlorine-laced sulfur. \u201cAh well. Kiki\u2019s won\u2019t notice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHuh?\u201d Naomi looked at me questioningly before catching a goddamn whiff of herself. \u201cOh!\u201d She flickered a moment and now her shirt read \u2018I don\u2019t speak Idiot\u2019 and she smelled shower fresh.<br /> <br /> I drove for Kiki\u2019s anyway. Jack still reeked. Billy Mack checked over the bag Jack had slung in the back. \u201cWell, we have what we need to cleanse locations, as well as a formula for cleansing biologicals. It requires the usual easily purchased things, in addition to baby tears...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI need some Aether... out of her neck...\u201d Naomi\u2019s fucking drifty musing interrupted him. She was staring off into space. \u201cOh, hey.\u201d She appeared to remember we were there.<br /> <br /> The g-man frowned. \u201cThere are far safer playthings. You are smart enough not to be sexually attracted to fire.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked. \u201cWhat if fire is sexually attracted to me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s still an angel,\u201d he pointed out.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cFor now.\u201d She looked out the goddamn window. \u201cI guess Jack is outvoted?\u201d<br /> <br /> He had been muttering some shit about showers, but I had ignored him. \u201cShoulda said something.\u201d I sped up. He glared at me. \u201cThey won\u2019t even notice.\u201d I waved him off.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry, they\u2019ll all be looking at me.\u201d Naomi patted Jack\u2019s arm.<br /> <br /> Jack crossed his arms. \u201cAnd you\u2019ll be right between me and Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave him a mock surprised look. \u201cYou say that like it\u2019s a bad thing...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot for us.\u201d The fucker leaned back in his seat, hands behind his head.<br /> <br /> <br /> Naomi was still complaining as we walked in to Kiki\u2019s. \u201cI figured we'd get some juice at Peterson. I went all in. Maybe I should visit Kayla. I\u2019m pretty sure she\u2019s fang curious...\u201d Her thoughts drifted, pleasantly, judging by her fucking smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe the rest of us are in a similar state.\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could hit the dam after this. I hear there\u2019s a party.\u201d Naomi made for an empty table near the stage.<br /> <br /> I pulled out a chair and sat in it backwards. I rolled my eyes at the pink-haired kid. \u201cThe Works.\u201d Jack and I said simultaneously. Jack continued, \u201cThere\u2019s not much safe to plug into, but we need to build our own sources. I\u2019m thinking three, at least. The office, the Mothman Theatre and...\u201d I waited, one goddamn eyebrow raised. \u201cAnd somewhere.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi looked interested in spite of her-fucking-self. \u201cWe do have a start at the Mothman Theatre.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned at her. \u201cTechnically, a middle.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t you know it\u2019s rude to correct an immigrant on their English like that? I mean, I\u2019m not one, technically.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cI guess I immigrated from my mom\u2019s uterus.\u201d She shrugged. \u201cFor the best really. Rio\u2019s got too much Jesus.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cIt does have a large Jesus.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smirked at him. \u201cYou own, personal Jesus?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMine is much smaller.\u201d Billy Mack looked down at Vivian\u2019s phone, typing something.<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess Naomi is the size queen of us.\u201d Jack fucking leered at her.<br /> <br /> She looked affronted. \u201cHey! The only sticking out things I like are boobs.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked up from the goddamn phone. \u201cBut you do like them bigger?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, but I\u2019m not, like, a guy about it.\u201d She made a point of ignoring us for a moment, flicking through her own fucking phone. \u201cOh! It was an old music reference. Depeche Mode? Ugh, and Marilyn Manson did it too...\u201d her obnoxious kid routine was interrupted by the waitress. \u201cA burger, a pina colada and ecstasy - pill or tongue form, your choice.\u201d She winked at the poor dame.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack took a stab without looking at the menu. \u201cShawarma?\u201d At her blank look, he shrugged. \u201cA gyro will be fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, fuck it. A gyro for me too.\u201d I said, mispronouncing it just for Herb. The waitress gave me a dirty look, and I winked at her too.<br /> <br /> Jack sighed. \u201cSomething substantial and easy to make.\u201d He looked beseechingly at her. \u201cWith no spit?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi smirked up at her. \u201cSpit\u2019s fine by me, we\u2019ll be trading more later anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> The waitress smiled at her and sashayed the hell off. I looked over to the g-man. \u201cSo, we got the shit. I don\u2019t think we wanna hit the goddamn Room before we fill up, but the House should be fucking easy enough. Unless... if we fix it, will the goddamn taint come back, from the bugs, or Alice or if Miranda is?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe will have to do something about the bugs. It does seem likely Miranda is tainted, even without a blood sample, but she also seems able to contain it. Alice is more troublesome.\u201d Billy Mack looked fucking thoughtful.<br /> <br /> \u201cRobin knows a ritual to trap ghosts.\u201d Naomi offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent.\u201d Billy Mack nodded. \u201cIt should be a temporary measure. We might also be able to make a cleansing agent for spiritual beings.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi gave me a significant look from behind her glass. \u201cThe medicine is priority, right? I mean, I have a perfectly good minion that\u2019s Abyss tainted.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack took a drink, considering. \u201cThinking of Angela - if someone refuses to be cleansed, would possessing them be risky?\u201d<br /> <br /> We were interrupted by the waitress with our food. Naomi smirked. \u201cSee? You just have to look pretty and tell people to do things.\u201d She showed us a pill with a goddamn smiley face.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt has some risks,\u201d Billy Mack said, ignoring Naomi. \u201cBut just that the possessor might acquire some taint. If we produce enough medicine, there will be no issue.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi stretched, watching the fucking waitress. \u201cLots of sad babies then.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a look. \u201cWe\u2019d probably have needed some for us anyway. We\u2019re going to be fighting the fucking thing, not just humping its goddamn furniture.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot unless Furniture has a rich dad and a dumb nickname.\u201d Naomi sipped her drink, smiling. The waitress walked by with another for her, as well as a slip of paper that Naomi smirked at and put in her pocket. \u201cSo what\u2019s the final call? I gots plans to make.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCrusher should get back to us fucking soon.\u201d I looked to Jack for confirmation. He nodded. \u201cIf we\u2019re not needed for that shit tonight, we cleanse the goddamn House.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi nodded approvingly. \u201cRobin has been holding her schedule open for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I knocked back my drink. \u201cThen definitely tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll let Miranda know I assume?\u201d Billy Mack looked at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. Just tell her \u2018We\u2019re coming to your house and bringing a Mexican!\u2019 You think?\u201d Jack smiled broadly at Naomi.<br /> <br /> She glared at him. \u201cI\u2019m Brazilian...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know.\u201d He interrupted her, shit-eating grin still on his face.<br /> <br /> \u201c<u>And</u>. Not there if Robin is,\u201d she continued.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow and ignored the two of them. \u201cParticularly about her sister. We can maybe clean the taint, given time. But we need to contain Alice now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack kept with the jokes. \u201cMaybe we could get her a restaurant.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi made a show of squinting at her phone. \u201cOh, another old person song reference?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is, and you already know it.\u201d Billy Mack\u2019s tone was stern.<br /> <br /> <br /> Shelley showed up for her shift not much later. Seeing her come in, Naomi grinned at us and ducked back into the goddamn ladies room. I glanced at Jack, who shrugged, then smirked and jerked his head towards our waitress, taking a bathroom break now that Shelley had arrived.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack followed the two of them into the ladies room and Vivian came out. She took a seat at the bar and chatted with Shelley. Jack went to chat up his bartender lug so I had the table to myself. I signaled for three drinks and sat back to fucking people watch.<br /> <br /> After a while, Naomi collapsed into the seat across from me, grinning broadly. \u201cCult recruitment is hard work. Be glad you\u2019re not doing anything like that.\u201d I rolled my eyes and threw my goddamn drink back. I finished a second drink in a single toss and started sipping the next again. \u201cYou OK Gabe?\u201d She looked honestly worried.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t want the poor girl to risk her cover on account of me. \u201cI was until someone sat down.\u201d I winked at her and she smiled back before sticking her tongue out at me.<br /> <br /> A serious fucking look came over her face. \u201cOK, I put up the no eavesdropping sign. What are we doing about the Miranda situation?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot telling the g-man. He promised no fire, not no experiments.\u201d I sighed. \u201cOnce this Abyssal shit is over with, I\u2019ve got a few fucking things to look into.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi waved a hand. \u201cNah, I\u2019m sure it\u2019s not worth... I\u2019m trying to think in asshole terms here... the cost of your trust, to do anything like that. Is there something else to protect her from?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThe leader of...\u201d I jerked my head significantly. She looked at me blankly. \u201cRight. You weren\u2019t in the car. Her old people. It\u2019s a fucking Beetlejuice thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded her understanding. \u201cShe can hide out in Liz\u2019s house, if that\u2019d be helpful.\u201d She looked up briefly and her tone changed from honest concern to mouthy little shit. \u201cI don\u2019t think you understand how hard it is when everyone falls in love with you. Oh hi Jack.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack sighed heavily as he sat down. \u201cSo Roadrash there -\u201d He looked sideways at the bartender. It was a fucking flattering name, considering. \u201c- has some unpleasant info for us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMost rashes tell you something unpleasant.\u201d Naomi nodded goddamn sagely.<br /> <br /> He glared at her. \u201cThe Tong have been poking around.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi wasn\u2019t expecting that. \u201cThat have anything to do with the Fools?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot the ones he described that I know of. A Respectable Ping and a Two Chin have been making nice, tipping well and shit. They\u2019re smugglers mostly, some drug running.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI bet they can get the good stuff.\u201d Jack gave her a look. \u201cWhat? We\u2019re Demons - you know, bad guys?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shook his head. \u201cI dunno. Being mafia types and all, I\u2019m sure they have life events they\u2019d be alright with giving away. But do I really wanna work with the Tong?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi gave him a goddamn dubious look. \u201cAnyone else? Sure. You... start running?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sneered at her, then shrugged. \u201cRoadrash is worried they\u2019re gonna start offering \u2018protection\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, they probably just want folks inclined to look the other way. Once they come in and start strong arming white people, it all goes down. I know. You know?\u201d she asked Jack, thumping her chest.<br /> <br /> <br /> We killed time at Kiki\u2019s until Jack got the fucking call from Crusher. After the initial pleasantries, he put it on speaker. \u201cYou found a town in the Hedge, you said?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUh, yeah. It\u2019s full of Hobs. Creepy looking smiley things.\u201d Crusher cleared his throat.<br /> <br /> Jack jumped right the hell on that. \u201cCreepy smiley things? Dogs, with large eyes and human smiles maybe?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a pause. \u201cNo. What the f- No, no, I don\u2019t think I want to know. Nothing like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cStay out of the police junkyard, by the way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. Sounds like a plan.\u201d There was another pause. \u201cSo the town. We\u2019re gonna have to put together a raiding party. It\u2019s gonna be a hell of a fight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCould a stealthy strike team work, you think?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> He thought a moment. \u201cMaybe... we had some sneaky folks with us, no ninja shit though. We\u2019ll be talking with the other Monarchs, the Harvestman included, so we might have some fear power bullshit to go along with ninja shit too. We did do a little, what\u2019s the word, skirmishing. They\u2019re not the most powerful Hobs I\u2019ve fought, there\u2019s just lots of \u2018em, and they have a town and all that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks for keeping us in the loop. And let us know if you get Drake, or if we can help out?\u201d Jack made our goodbyes and put the phone in his fucking pocket.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood enough.\u201d I pushed my hair back from my face. \u201cI suppose if we get fucking antsy or some shit, we could trade the wardrobe fucker to Mr. Smiles, maybe get him off Vivian\u2019s back and get Drake back all in one.\u201d I grimaced. \u201cThey\u2019ll probably eat each other, or become best of fucking friends.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack raised an eyebrow. \u201cI don\u2019t like those odds.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sent Vivian texts filling her in on the conversation with Crusher. \u2018Curious: Abyssal + Gentry = ?\u2019<br /> <br /> Vivian looked thoughtful. \u2018Not sure what would happen. Something interesting.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018So bad then\u2019 I sent, chuckling.<br /> <br /> \u2018For someone\u2019 was her only response, though she glanced over a couple of times.<br /> <br /> Naomi looked up from making faces at her goddamn phone to smile at the waitress bringing our checks. She put hers back down, the X over the price very fucking visible, smirking. Her phone buzzed again and she scrunched her face up before looking at us. \u201cPop quiz. You\u2019re with a girl. Do you think your loyalty will increase more if you put something in her, or if she puts something in you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2018I.. uh, wha?\u201d I managed.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes at the phone and waved me off. \u201cNevermind.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Well, that could have gone better.<br /> <br /> We got the materials\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026No we are not dealing with the breach yet.<br /> <br /> No you cannot come<br /> <br /> It\u2019s dangerous Kayla I don\u2019t want you\u2026<br /> <br /> Kayla\u2026<br /> <br /> KAYLA!<br /> <br /> MS LIQOUR!<br /> <br /> Better. Okay, Kayla, listen, we are not doing it yet, keep your shirt on\u2026never thought I would say that\u2026<br /> <br /> Mmm Hmmm<br /> <br /> Okay, so what I was trying to tell you Darling is that we had a bit of a scuffle at Peterson.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m fine, thanks.<br /> <br /> So anyway, we were getting the materials, when a certain person whose name rhymes with Bill-Roy was not quite stealthy enough and attracted the Guardian. The Guardian, who called itself \u201cHugbot\u201d was a reflective black skeleton in sunglasses teaming with guns. It spoke in an androgynous child\u2019s voice offering us \u201chugs\u201d and threatening to take our skin and eyes for teddy bears and dolls. If you plan to fix the God-Machine, your work is cut out.<br /> <br /> It was soon after that Puriel arrived. Since our first fateful night as an Agency we had not seen her, only heard reports, but there she was, blazing sword, blazing wings, a corona of fire, she was magnificent. She challenged that she needed to make a big explosion, having heralded her arrival by blowing up a tank outside. Hugbot challenged her in his singsong child\u2019s voice, and started firing a powerful stream from his cannon.<br /> <br /> I cannot really bring across how fucked up Hugbot is. First of all, it calls itself that on purpose, and answers to it. Second, if I had not stressed it, it looks like an armored black skeleton, and third, it talks in the damn sing song voice.<br /> <br /> They fought awhile, as Kilroy tried to get the material made. He and Quietus distracted it, he with sprinklers and Quietus with explosions, which convinced Hugbot to turn off his gun. Quietus informed me afterwards that Puriel, dodging attacks, was trying to lure him into blowing up a transformer itself, Hugbot switched to a less powerful but more accurate pistol, and got Puriel off guard.<br /> <br /> We kept hearing about Puriel mowing down teams of Demons, but Hugbot had her at bay, mocking her with that awful voice and virtually teleporting all over the facility. Creeping out of shadows and pipes to block her escape, it became apparent he was toying with her out of sadism.<br /> <br /> Yea, bad news. Even if it fell, I suspect it would not be our friend.<br /> <br /> So I, after consulting with Speed and Quietus, used my powers to talk to Puriel. I asked her to delay, not telling her it was for our materials but for reasons that suit both of our goals. I promised her support. She nodded.<br /> <br /> First I screamed, to shatter the glass and create a huge spill, which distracted everyone, I think. Then when the time came I turned into a mass of spiders and rushed Hugbot. While most of them died, we, and Puriel, escaped.<br /> <br /> Kayla pull yourself together! I said I was okay. Sure it was\u2026a lot\u2026of my body mass but I am fine.<br /> <br /> So anyway\u2026Kayla\u2026KAYLA.<br /> <br /> (Sigh) Okay just lay it on me.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> I see. I will be more careful. I promise.<br /> <br /> Okay, so we stopped by KiKi\u2019s and compared notes. Puriel was clearly raiding Peterson to get attention on it. That is bad, it is a fuel stop of choice and we need to go back to make some medicine to help tainted folks like Angela. Hugbot knew others were there but we were a huge distraction, and Speed\u2019s jamming radio we were not up to our armpits in Destroyers. Short term, we got the material we needed.<br /> <br /> While there, we passed some time on personal endeavors. I did a little light recruiting, Kilroy chatted up her girlfriend as Vivian, and Quietus spoke to the bartender and got info on Chinese criminal gangs in the area.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Crusher called, and reported his search\u2026they think they found Drake, but it will be a hard nut to crack.<br /> <br /> Tonight, though, we will fix the house. It will be an easier run than the room, and there should be little meaningful resistance. Miranda will be there in case something bad happens, and Robin will be there to trap the ghost.<br /> <br /> I will be careful, I promise Darling.<br /> <br /> For you.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIV</i><br /> <br /> Hugbot was popular. Not Michael White popular, but popular. I used the Thin Man robot from Rift\u2019s Mechanoids as a design, and threw in some deeply messed up personality. Initially, he managed to keep tying but never beating some PCs stealth pools, so was out of his box and prowling until Puriel showed up.<br /> <br /> Speed Demon happened to have radio suite up, which was good\u2026it made the difference between success and failure of the objective. Naomi used Across a Crowded Room extensively, and her Swarming form power. She also got 8 successes on a social roll to flirt with the waitress.<br /> <br /> Groundwork laid for other storylines. Hob Towns are a thing in the Hedge, there is more in<i> Dancers in the Dusk</i> on the subject.<br /> <br /> It looks like cleansing the house is next. It should be exciting. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T12:52:10-07:00","id":649222,"title":"","content":"Finally caught up! Very exciting adventures, and colorful characters; Clytemnestra is the scariest PC I've seen in years!<br /> <br /> Will Jared's player be back?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T15:22:37-07:00","id":649363,"title":"","content":"I am curious why Clytemnestra is scariest.<br /> <br /> To be completely frank, I hope so. He has dropped off the radar, and I am to be honest worried about him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T16:22:19-07:00","id":649509,"title":"","content":"It's her casual, playful predatory habits, the way she presents being eaten by her as being a desirable prize to the person she relates her story to. No predators are scarier than the ones you don't want to run from, even knowing what they'll do to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-02T21:12:11-07:00","id":649733,"title":"","content":"Okay that's fair, I will give you that. Her conc