br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T23:37:58-07:00","id":653539,"title":"","content":"Okay, here are the current Ciphers as discovered by the PCs. I will sblock them to avoid wall of text related issues. In each case the other players and I worked together on them, though each player is ignorant of their own character\u2019s. And yes, the names are themed.<br /> <br /> Speed Demon \u2013- Gabriella Norton \u2013- Gabe; Psychopomp Inquisitor<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Key 1: Soup Up<br /> <br /> Key 2: Like the Movies<br /> <br /> Interlock: Double Indemnity<br /> <br /> Your car is surprisingly durable when this power is used. From the time it is activated until the time it is turned off, the car never takes more than one level of durability damage from anything short of a direct attack. Falling, crashing, sideswiping only causes a single level of damage regardless of how much it should take, unless none would be taken at all. Direct attacks (shooting, punching, eating the car) are resolved normally.<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Resolve + Drive<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> <br /> Action: Instant<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The power fails. Worse, if it takes more damage than the Demon\u2019s Primum in a single hit it explodes, doing dice of damage equal to it\u2019s size to those inside.<br /> <br /> Failure: The power fails to work.<br /> <br /> Success: The power works while the car runs.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Not only is the car protected, anyone inside is as well. They only take one level of damage appropriate to the type at maximum. The car could go into the Grand Canyon and take one durability while everyone inside takes one Lethal from the fall.<br /> <br /> Key 3: Check Backdrop<br /> <br /> Interlock: The Woman in the Window<br /> <br /> Speed Demon is especially hard to hit when she takes cover. In addition to the usual effects of cover, Speed Demon can apply her Defense, including Dodge, to firearms. If this Interlock is used in a car, Speed Demon can elect to substitute her Drive for Athletics when calculating her Defense.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Dexterity + Firearms<br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Speed Demon cannot use the cover effectively. She gets no benefit at all from being behind cover<br /> <br /> Failure: The power fails to work.<br /> <br /> Success: The power works for the scene.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: In addition to the protection from firearms, if the attacker attempts to use Melee, Speed Demon enjoys a +3 to her Defense or Dodge so long as some cover remains between herself and her attacker.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Kilroy \u2013- William McKenzie \u2013- Billy Mac \u2013- Vivian Marley; Guardian Inquisitor/Saboteur<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Key 1: Cause and Effect<br /> <br /> Key 2: Sabotage<br /> <br /> Interlock: Somebody Set Us Up the Bomb<br /> <br /> Kilroy can cause an object to shatter as if exposed to extreme heart or an explosion. The Interlock produces no heat or fire itself; instead, any object shatters violently, potentially hitting anyone within Kilroy\u2019s Primum in yards around it. This damage does not distinguish friend from foe, but after touching the object and spending Aether on it Kilroy can activate it anytime that scene. He cannot set a trigger, however, only a time or as a Reflexive Action.<br /> <br /> The object does Lethal or Bashing depending on the materials involved. Most do Bashing, but a metal object, hot object, or something made with jagged parts may do Lethal. The object does half it\u2019s Size, rounded down, in levels. Kilroy can affect an object with a size up to twice his Primum.<br /> <br /> Cost 1 Aether per 5 Size, rounded up.<br /> <br /> Action: Instant to use, Reflexive to Activate<br /> <br /> Die Pool: Resolve + Crafts<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The object explodes immediately, doing it\u2019s Size in appropriate Damage to anything within feet equal to Kilroy\u2019s Primum. Since Kilroy must touch the object to activate the power, this always includes him.<br /> <br /> Failure: Nothing happens. \u20131 to subsequent attempts to affect the same object that scene.<br /> <br /> Success: The Object detonates when Kilroy wishes it to.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Instead of the Scene, Kilroy can have it \u201chold\u201d it\u2019s charge for hours equal to his Primum.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Fulgur -- Jared Evans; Destroyer/Saboteur<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Key 1: Data Retrieval<br /> </div></div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <br /> Quietus -- Jack Stone -- Mr. Ends Destroyer; Saboteur/Tempter<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Key 1: Authorized<br /> <br /> Key 2: Bystander Effect<br /> <br /> Interlock: In the Heat of the Night<br /> <br /> Quietus can turn a crowd of bystanders to his side. So long as he did not <i>obviously</i> initiate violence with the target (though he could ultimately be the instigator) any bystanders when someone assaults or attacks Quietus will step in and take his side. Most won\u2019t fight, though they may restrain his \u201cattacker\u201d and any who call the police relay that Quietus was attacked. Some violent sorts may well fight on his side if it breaks into serious violence, though this does not keep the crowd from dispersing if they are fired into or butchered.<br /> <br /> While a Hunter Angel may simply be delayed a few turns while he butchers anyone in his way, most attackers will be disinclined to face down Quietus with an angry mob at his back.<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Intimidation<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The crowd turns against Quietus. The power works in reverse.<br /> <br /> Failure: the crowd reacts normally<br /> <br /> Success: The crowd sides with Quietus and frowns upon his attacker\u2019s shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The crowd can get downright violent toward Quietus\u2019s harasser, with all but the meekest becoming violent unless Quietus chooses to calm them.<br /> <br /> Key 3: Cooler Heads Prevail<br /> <br /> Interlock: They Call Me <u>Mister</u> Tibbs!<br /> <br /> <br /> When something needs done, Quietus can make people fall in line. Rather than by standing, they calmly, rationally begin solving an immediate crisis. House on fire? They form a water line, strongest may seek survivors, anyone with basic medical skill will use it, etcetera. They might try to plug a leak, help survivors of a car wreck, or whatever non violent needs may arise. Supernatural beings can resist this, Demons and Angels are immune, but know a power was used. If there is no emergency, the power fails. Utterly self centered people will ignore it, but most people will step in to help.<br /> <br /> Cost: None<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Persuasion vs. Resolve + Composure + Primum (if supernatural)<br /> <br /> Roll Results<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The crowd turns against Quietus. They are not compelled to attack but may boo or mock him.<br /> <br /> Failure: the crowd reacts normally to the situation.<br /> <br /> Success: The crowd will move to help with whatever skills they have. They will not risk their life unless given to do so, but they will work to deal with whatever crisis has appeared.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: The crowd will risk their life to help defuse the crisis, though they will avoid suicidal situations.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Clytemnestra \u2013- Ms Weaver \u2013-Elizabeth Covington \u2013- Naomi Cruz; Messenger Tempter<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Key 1: Heart's Desire<br /> <br /> Key 2: Ambush<br /> <br /> Interlock: Kiss of Death<br /> <br /> The allure of the black widow is powerful and deadly, often causing her prey to watch in helpless fascination as she closes in for the kill.<br /> <br /> This Interlock effects a single target, which must be able to see Clytemnestra. If the target of this power is engaged in active combat Clytemnestra's roll is at -3.<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Intimidation \u2013 Composure + Power Stat<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The target's fear of Clytemnestra causes them to defend more vigorously. Their defense against Clytemnestra's attacks is +3 until the end of the scene and she cannot use this power against them again.<br /> <br /> Failure: The target is able to defend normally.<br /> <br /> Success: Target loses their defense against Clytemnestra's next attack as per a successful surprise attack.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Clytemnestra's next attack against the target is a killing blow.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Feedback welcome, of course. See you in a week.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T05:08:13-07:00","id":653750,"title":"","content":"Nice! I especially like Quietus' Interlocks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T12:44:17-07:00","id":662116,"title":"","content":"We heard from Fulgur's player! He is...well, he will be back hopefully in October.<br /> <br /> First site is repaired, but more to go. The team gets to work. Welcome back to Night Train<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Eventually Vivian wandered over to our table, and she and Naomi appeared to continue an argument about minions and the care of same. Apparently Naomi was worried Shelley would wind up castrating That Poor Fuck or something. Jack and I stayed the goddamn hell out of it. I agreed with Naomi in a general sense, but it\u2019s Kilroy\u2019s life. I\u2019m sure as hell not one to throw stones - I like my 360 view - and I do think she was a little off base describing Vivian\u2019s treatment of her minions as God Machine like, but the pink haired dame had her points. Unfortunately for Vivian, Jack seemed to agree with Naomi too. Fortunately for her, he also seemed like he would prefer to dance a goddamn polka in Kiki\u2019s kitchen\u2019s fucking fryer than say so out loud.<br /> <br /> After a check of her goddamn phone, Naomi changed the subject. \u201cOnce Liz is done helping with the cleansing of the house, I have to be seen on campus. No rush, since staggering in late with an I don\u2019t give enough of a fuck to tell you where I\u2019ve been is in character, but I can\u2019t go to the Works or anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe shouldn\u2019t go to the Works until we\u2019ve charged up anyway.\u201d Vivian pointed out.<br /> <br /> Naomi looked confused. \u201cBut I thought we wanted to go there to charge.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack snapped out of his meditations on not fucking agreeing with Naomi. \u201cThat\u2019s more long game, I think.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cThere is likely to be abandoned Infrastructure there, but the Angelic and cryptid presence is likely to be significant.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhere then?\u201d Naomi looked at each of us.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fucking dam should be safe tomorrow,\u201d I offered. \u201cHell, it should be safe now. As soon as I stopped fucking with the radio signals, 20 to 1 says the bastard phoned home.\u201d I leaned in. \u201cLook, if we\u2019ve got some time... I\u2019ve got an idea what the next step on my goddamn Cipher is. Just gotta get in a fucking firefight to check. So I was thinking, we could hit up a paintball field, blow off some steam, do team building exercises, all that bull shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi pointed at me, grinning. \u201cYes! We\u2019ll wipe the floor with them, especially when I lock in the next key on my Cipher.\u201d<br /> <br /> I saluted her with my goddamn drink. Jack looked back and forth between us. \u201cWell, now I have to try something.\u201d<br /> <br /> He wandered off to the fucking bar, leaving Naomi and I looking expectantly at Vivian. She shrugged. \u201cI got nothing.\u201d<br /> <br /> We watched Jack order a drink and linger at the bar near an incredibly goddamn drunk guy hitting on a regular. While we watched, her expression went from slight interest to active fucking disgust. Jack winced and after a sip or two, rejoined us.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo let me get this fucking straight,\u201d I smirked at him as he sat down. \u201cYou just tried to mystically cockblock some poor gee and reality bitchslapped you for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> He glared at me. \u201cI <u>succeeded</u> at mystically cockblocking some douchebag and reality gave me a black eye for thinking it was more significant than that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, sure.\u201d I finished my drink. \u201cWhatever helps you sleep.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Between my use of Check Backdrop and Naomi\u2019s use of Ambush, we were goddamn kings of the fucking paintball field we found just on the edge of town. Both of us unlocked our Interlock, so we were both fucking flush with Aether again. By the end, even Jack was feeling better, despite the swaths of dead vegetation in his path, since Naomi had popped Halo to get him moving towards healed.<br /> <br /> It was about 20 after 7 when I gave Miranda a call. \u201cHey sweetheart.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHello Gabe.\u201d She was smiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood news beautiful. We got the stuff we need to repair the tainted places. We, uh, we figured we\u2019d get your house first - it should be easier and we\u2019re a little tapped for resources, some of us. If you\u2019re cool with that.\u201d I started flipping a coin and catching it backhanded.<br /> <br /> She responded quickly. \u201cOf course, that\u2019s excellent.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s one thing. Robin\u2019s going to be helping out cause...\u201d I paused. \u201cMaybe I could come by before the others?\u201d \u2018Cause she needs to put your sister in a bottle\u2019 didn\u2019t fucking seem like the best thing to bring up over the phone all of the sudden.<br /> <br /> She was still smiling. \u201cI\u2019m at home now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMeet you there in... twenty?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Her house was a big fucking house. I took my time going up the drive admiring the view, especially once Miranda got to the door and stood there watching me watch her, smiling slightly. I stopped myself from glancing towards the attic as I leaned on the doorjamb. \u201cHey Princess. Gimme a tour of the grounds?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever you say, tough girl.\u201d Her smile grew warmer.<br /> <br /> She reached for my hand and I took hers as we walked down the slightly overgrown path. \u201cSo... Robin. She deals with, well, death energies, which is why she was at the junkyard, right? But mostly she deals with ghosts.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlice.\u201d It was almost a whisper and the warmth left her face.<br /> <br /> I stopped and turned to face her, keeping a hold of her hand. \u201cBest I understand it, something\u2019s gotta be done. If we cleanse the place, but she\u2019s still around, the infection will spread again?\u201d She nodded, biting her lip. \u201cIt\u2019s not a permanent sort of dealing with. It\u2019s a temporary containment kinda thing, until we have a plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA plan. To help her. So that it was all worth it.\u201d She looked up at me. \u201cI... I give my permission, so long as Robin promises she won\u2019t be hurt.\u201d Love and hate warred in her eyes and she looked away as she muttered. \u201cThe manipulative bitch.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s your call sweetheart. It gets your ok first. That\u2019s why I came early.\u201d<br /> <br /> She had a slight smile back on her face as she looked back at me. \u201cHere I thought it was to see me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned back. \u201cNah, that\u2019s my reward, for being the bearer of good/bad news.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c<u>That\u2019s</u> your reward?\u201d She ran a finger around my collar. \u201cHow long until your friends get here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs long as we need.\u201d I stepped closer and put a hand on her hip.<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t make promises you can\u2019t keep.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked at her. \u201cCross my heart.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked back and pulled me by the hand to the house and up the stairs. I sent Liz a quick text - \u2018Come later\u2019 -and turned the ringer off before I got a response. Miranda let go of my hand and put her hands on her hips, looking me up and down before saying \u201cThis is a bad idea\u201d and pushing me back on the bed.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do love bad ideas\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> My phone said 10 when a knock on the goddamn door woke us out of our afterglow. Miranda lifted her head from my chest to gaze dozily up at me. \u201cYou better go let them in. I\u2019ll need a moment to find my legs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMm.\u201d I smiled down at her and shifted off the bed.<br /> <br /> I smirked at her watching me get dressed. Another knock came before I finished tucking in my shirt, so one tail was out as I kissed Miranda on the forehead and winked at her. She chuckled. \u201cIf you\u2019d kissed any lower, your friends would have at least another fifteen minutes to wait.\u201d She shoved me out the door.<br /> <br /> I slung my jacket over my shoulder and fucking sauntered out the door. The other three members of the agency were there, along with Robin. Liz noticed me first and beamed at me briefly before reassuming her bored demeanor. \u201cPreparations have been made then?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack eyed me. \u201cShe looked pretty prepped.\u201d He was standing in the middle of the driveway, so only the edges of the greenery along the drive was fucking dead.<br /> <br /> I sneered at him but Miranda\u2019s arrival forestalled whatever the hell I was going to say. She moved to stand next to me. \u201cHello, everyone. There are two breaches. The primary breach is downstairs - the room with the flies?\u201d She raised an eyebrow. Billy Mack and Jack nodded. \u201cThe secondary breach is upstairs. I will show you where.\u201d<br /> <br /> She invited us inside and as we all got into the foyer, Robin spoke up. \u201cMa\u2019am, while they\u2019re doing that, we need to ensure your sister is safe from us and us from her. I\u2019m going to...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know what you\u2019re going to do.\u201d Miranda interrupted her coldly. \u201cLet\u2019s go speak while they deal with the bugs.\u201d Miranda put a hand on my shoulder and gave me a slight smile before starting upstairs.<br /> <br /> Liz moved to fucking follow them. \u201cI\u2019m going with if she is.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda stopped on the stairs and looked at Liz a few moments. \u201cI see you are not prepared to be argued with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Liz put her hands on her hips. Miranda shrugged and continued upstairs, the other two women following.<br /> <br /> Jack, Billy Mack and I went to the room covered in flies. \u201cWell shit.\u201d I grimaced at the smell. \u201cI know you\u2019re the goddamn brain Billy Mack, but you\u2019re our best craftsman too, with the fucking Download Knowledge. How about you take point there, with Jack\u2019s backup and I\u2019ll drag Liz the hell away from her lady to help me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well.\u201d Billy Mack nodded and began measuring the fucking room.<br /> <br /> I went upstairs to find Miranda standing with her arms crossed, facing Robin who had Liz behind her and a step away. They\u2019d stopped talking at my approach and looked at me. \u201cSorry to interrupt, ladies. I\u2019m afraid I gotta steal Liz. We need an extra pair of hands - eyes, really.\u201d<br /> <br /> She glanced at Robin. \u201cAlright.\u201d<br /> <br /> It took twenty five minutes to cleanse the fucking shithole of a room. Well, to cleanse it of the taint. The flies and maggots still covered the room and it was gonna take a hell of a something to get the stench out. But gravity as pointing in the right direction and the never ending font of shit found an end. Billy Mack spent a few minutes gathering the goddamn bugs. Jack made a gagging sound. \u201cKeep that tupperware out of the freezer, OK?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust don\u2019t get leftovers from the fucking Winnebago.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> Miranda was waiting for us at the top of the stairs. Robin had ducked out once Alice was dealt with, to avoid antagonizing her. She took us to the room with the wardrobe. The thing inside it was licking the inside of its door. Miranda\u2019s face drew tight. \u201cI didn\u2019t teach him to do that.\u201d She kicked the wardrobe.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack stepped forward eagerly. \u201cSo you know what\u2019s in there then? I\u2019m quite curious...\u201d<br /> <br /> She withdrew, looking at him wide eyed. \u201cI\u2019m not sure I like the way you said that.\u201d The thing was reacting to her voice, rubbing against the inside of the wardrobe like a creature wanting affection. Her voice dropped as she stared at it. \u201cYou disgust me,\u201d she muttered under her breath.<br /> <br /> I put a hand on her shoulder and tried to catch her eye. \u201cWe\u2019ll work it out Princess.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t mean to intrude, it\u2019s just an interesting creature,\u201d the g-man offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cGet to work and get out.\u201d She stepped back and away again, her face blank.<br /> <br /> The second breach only took fifteen minutes to patch up the same way. Miranda looked on coldly. After we finished, Billy Mack turned to Miranda. \u201cWould you like us to take this with us and dispose of it with the other items?\u201d He indicated the wardrobe.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo!\u201d Her nostrils flared and she swallowed hard. \u201cYou will leave him as he is.\u201d She took a deep, shuddering breath. \u201cThank you for cleansing my house. Now please go.\u201d She grabbed my hand.<br /> <br /> We stood quietly in the room until we heard the front door shut. Then Miranda collapsed into my arms, sobbing. \u201cMy baby... oh, my boy.\u201d<br /> <br /> That was as coherent as she got for the rest of the night. When I felt my back start to twinge, I gathered her up as gently as I could. She buried her face in my neck as I carried her down the hall to her room. I sat down on her bed and leaned back against the headboard, settling her beside me. She curled into a ball on my lap, nestling her head under my chin.<br /> <br /> She was more than half asleep before she\u2019d cried herself out. I sat with her in silence, stroking her hair until her breathing became more regular and her muscles relaxed. I tilted my head back to stare at the fucking ceiling. She sighed and shifted in her sleep, her hand falling to my waist.<br /> <br /> My eyes were heavy. I could have fallen asleep there with her. I had a feeling she wouldn\u2019t mind.<br /> <br /> I need a goddamn drink.<br /> <br /> I moved carefully out from under her, supporting her head to her pillow and stretching her out on the bed. Then I went to my car. The grandfather clock ticked fucking disapprovingly at me when I came back, flask in hand. I flipped it off and went back upstairs.<br /> <br /> Maybe it was creepy, spinning the chair around so I could sit in it backwards to watch her sleep. I didn\u2019t care. She made a small noise and brought her hand up to her pillow, smiling slightly. I don\u2019t know why I didn\u2019t climb back into her bed, where it was warm and soft. Then again, everywhere is warm enough with a few slugs of whiskey and they do a good job of softening the edges too. But there was something distressingly real about that bed, about falling asleep holding her, a kind of real I had never been. Not that I was having second thoughts. But, as sure as I was about my welcome, I needed her voice to make me real enough to fit.<br /> <br /> I tucked my empty flask into my jacket pocket and drug the chair closer to where the head of the bed met the wall. I fought to keep my fucking eyes open, but the last thing I remembered was reaching out to touch her hand with my outstretched fingers.<br /> <br /> <br /> I woke up to the smell of coffee nearby. I came to slowly, moving carefully so as not to knock it over before I found it. I opened my eyes to find Miranda smiling down at me, holding a mug out. \u201cGood morning Gabe. Coffee?\u201d I took it and smiled back at her. \u201cI thought so. Then, perhaps we might have time for a shower and breakfast.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a sip of the coffee. It was a decent blend at least. Maybe she\u2019d let me take a look at her coffee maker though. \u201cSounds like a plan to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood.\u201d She looked down, her smile fading. \u201cI want to apologize, Gabe, for my lapse in control yesterday. I just...\u201d She trailed off.<br /> <br /> I took another sip then sat the mug on the desk before standing up. \u201cBy yesterday, you mean last night, not earlier in the evening right?\u201d I grinned rakishly at her. She smiled at me slightly and nodded. \u201cNo need to apologize love. I\u2019m alright at being cried on. Anytime you need.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took a breath. \u201cI\u2019m not really ready to talk about the elephant in the room, as it were.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing sweetheart.\u201d I stepped in close and put a hand on her waist.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo... when do you have to meet your friends?\u201d She ran her knuckle down the line of my chin.<br /> <br /> I shrugged, smiling. \u201cYou know. Later.\u201d I pulled her to me and kissed her deeply. walking backwards towards the bed as I did.<br /> <br /> <br /> When I opened the door to the agency, there was a fucking flutter of motion as Liz and Cecilia broke apart quickly. They gave me breathy hellos before going upstairs. I wandered past Jack\u2019s office where he was asleep in his goddamn chair. \u201cI said, I\u2019m not letting the agency get fucked over by shit bugs.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stopped in my fucking tracks, and looked back over my shoulder slowly. His eyes were still closed and his chin was on his chest. \u201cJack?\u201d He didn\u2019t respond. I slammed a hand into his door and ducked. His gun was sitting close at hand. There was no need to be fucking careless about that shit.<br /> <br /> \u201cFoul smelling shit bugs!\u201d He sat bolt upright.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cHaving a bad dream there Jack?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are <u>fascinating</u> shit bugs.\u201d Billy Mack joined me at the door.<br /> <br /> Jack glared at the g-man. \u201cHe stayed up all night looking at shit bug parts. I stayed up all night making sure they didn\u2019t crawl through his eyes and eat his brain.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful. \u201cGiven their infection vector and what I learned last night, it seems more likely they would attempt to enter my system through my mouth. Or possibly my nose. Should they have been capable of any such thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack ignored him, speaking directly to me. \u201cI stayed up all night in a room with foul smelling shit bugs, making sure they didn\u2019t crawl in his eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou truly are a goddamn martyr.\u201d I deadpanned.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell!\u201d Liz said brightly. \u201cI recommend kissing Brazilians to anyone.\u201d She glanced at Jack over my shoulder.<br /> <br /> The g-man smiled. \u201cI'll take that under advisement. Speaking of kissing,\u201d he turned to me, \u201cyou look well Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, Gabe, is Miranda alright?\u201d Liz set a fucking gasper on her holder and held it out for me to light.<br /> <br /> I smirked as I fished out a goddamn lighter and held out a flame. \u201cBetter now. And, just in case, that permission I gave before? I\u2019m taking it back.\u201d I smiled at Billy Mack to take the sting out.<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cUnderstood.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo... the dam?\u201d Jack stood and stretched, popping his neck.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. In addition to restoring our Aether supplies, I was hoping to finalize my arrangement with Ganora.\u201d Billy Mack suggested.<br /> <br /> Jack thought a moment. \u201cRight. We still need a human contact for the contract, yeah?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue, so perhaps we shall simply scout for one. But I would also like to introduce Ganora to Langley, presuming she is ok with it.\u201d Billy Mack got his fucking phone out.<br /> <br /> Liz\u2019s smile was goddamn strained. \u201cI have faith in your glibness.\u201d<br /> <br /> Foreman Jameson answered Billy Mack, and transferred him to Langley\u2019s office, making no effort to hide his derision of his fucking boss. Langley\u2019s response was a reminder why. \u201cWhaaaa...t\u2019s up dog?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is a pleasure to speak with you again. It is William Mackenzie and I had some business to speak with you about.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh yes. Over the phone or where we can murrrder each other?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack cleared his throat. \u201cFace to face, but a lack of murdering would be preferable.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell then. The dam is not best, certainly. My house? Your house? A building I say is my house? The woods surrounded by lumberjacks?\u201d Langley was on a goddamn roll.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly if they are evenly split in loyalty.\u201d Billy Mack fucking played along.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can\u2019t buy lumberjacks! Have you ever been to Canada?\u201d Langley sounded goddamn scandalized.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack\u2019s response was serious. \u201cYou\u2019ll find American lumberjacks are much less tied to honor.\u201d<br /> <br /> Langley chuckled. \u201cMore seriously, the commissary? There\u2019s an Orange Julius.\u201d He paused. \u201cI should warn you, I will no longer respect you if you order there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYour place would be best, I think.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo not the commissary or the woods surrounded by imported Canadian lumberjacks.\u201d Langley seemed mildly disappointed. \u201cVery well. Will 8:30 work? And how many should I expect? I might need more strychnine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere will be 5 of us and 8:30 is fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. Toodles!\u201d The smarmy fucker hung up first.<br /> <br /> Liz had a goddamn pained look on her face. \u201cToodles? I\u2019m not one to eavesdrop but... toodles?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou met him, right?\u201d Jack and I asked, fucking simultaneously.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes at us. \u201cThis may come as a shock, but I find him somewhat aggravating.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful. \u201cA Foreman Jameson answered the phone. If he\u2019s clean he might make a good contact for Ganora.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWonderful. You go look into that while I drink the double bourbon I\u2019ll need to deal with Langley.\u201d Liz patted him on the shoulder.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> By the time Billy Mack had uncovered all he could on fucking Lester Jameson and found no red flags, Liz had had her double bourbon and done a goddamn line of coke. She gave Cecilia one last set of instructions as we left: \u2018Wait in the basement next to the hookah. Wear the outfit.\u2019 We made good fucking time to the dam and met Ganora by the lake.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey.\u201d She only had eyes for the g-man.<br /> <br /> He greeted her warmly. \u201cIt is good to see you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah... Snuggles?\u201d She smiled widely.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot quite yet. I do have news though. We believe we have found a good candidate to be your contact in the dam. He is a foreman and so in a position to be of assistance. Also, since you are representing our interests here at the dam, and Langley represents the vampire, I would like to introduce you.\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> Every pause for breath was punctuated by a goddamn breathy \u201cYeah...\u201d from Ganora. Her eyes widened at Langley\u2019s name. \u201cHe will obey?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cHe belongs to another group.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe will not obey...\u201d Her eyes narrowed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have agreed to cooperate. They are dangerous - they have proved capable of fighting and killing the God Machine's minions. It is a worthwhile alliance,\u201d he assured her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes...\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz gave me a long suffering look. \u201cSince there\u2019s going to be a meeting, I brought you some pants. I hope you enjoy them. And wear them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ganora looked back and fucking forth between Liz and Billy Mack. \u201cYes...?\u201d The question was aimed at Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou might as well. It won\u2019t throw him off for you to arrive pantsless, so there is nothing to be gained.\u201d Billy Mack nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cPants...\u201d She still looked uncertain.<br /> <br /> Liz smiled tightly. \u201cThey will be in the car, with the pullover.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow has the Rattus problem been?\u201d Jack asked Ganora.<br /> <br /> She blinked at him. \u201cMs. Crimson killed all the Rattus. She doesn\u2019t like anyone down there.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked fucking concerned. \u201cHas she kept you away?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJob\u2019s not to go down there, so... yeah.\u201d Ganora nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat bitch!\u201d Liz\u2019s brow furrowed. \u201cDo you need Aether?\u201d<br /> <br /> Ganora shook her head. \u201cThere\u2019s still the arrangement. We just don\u2019t go... there.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cWasn't gonna be a free fucking lunch forever. We wanna give it a goddamn try anyway?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think we kinda have to.\u201d Jack looked at Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> <br /> Once we got the hell down there, I snuck ahead. There were no signs of the fucking Rattus, or as far as I could fucking tell, Ms. Crimson. In my defense, she was on the goddamn ceiling and didn't see me either. Thankfully, Billy Mack spotted her before any of us fucking jacked in.<br /> <br /> She was patrolling on a regular fucking route, so we were able to time it so we had a few seconds to recharge before concealing ourselves again. Since I was full, I charged the goddamn phones myself and did the dance with the rest of them. That way, we were all able to leave full, with 8 Aether waiting in my bolthole for a goddamn rainy day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <b><u>Better Living Through Chemistry</u></b><br /> <br /> While the events at Peterson Chemical cannot be described as a failure, I cannot say that I am pleased. The timing of Puriel's attack on the infrastructure was decidedly inconvenient. We did manage to acquire the materials we needed to repair the Abyssal damage at the Ashbury House and the University. Also, I was able to discern what we would need to make a similar compound for treating living beings. However, the running battle between Puriel and Hugbot did a fair amount of damage to the structure and our interference left no question that we were present. The investigation will doubtlessly show that we hijacked the Infrastructure before aiding Puriel in escaping from Hugbot. There is no telling how long the facility will be on high alert and what measures will be taken to improve its security. We shall have to completely re-evaluate it when we return and there is a strong likelihood that the increased security will make it far less useful to us.<br /> <br /> Hugbot 9000 is clearly insane and I dare say is as close or closer to falling than Puriel. However, I cannot say that this will make a difference in the need to destroy that abomination. If anything, being free to roam would make the thing even more dangerous. Thankfully, none of my companions seem to have misguided priorities where that Angel is concerned.<br /> <br /> Sadly, the same cannot be said for Puriel. Her unorthodox plan to protect her Infrastructure by drawing attention to other God Machine installations is useful for the most part, though her randomness is frustrating. And while I cannot say that I do not find her physical form alluring, the rest of the agency seems entirely too partial to her. That she acts against the God Machine is no reason to think of her as any sort of ally or to expect that she will not try to kill us given a chance. Even more concerning, Clytemnestra seems dead set on bedding this thermophilic guardian angel and steadfastly refuses to see the extreme danger in this course of action. I sincerely hope that she simply lusts to draw Puriel into her clutches and devour her. But I cannot discount the possibility that she may be allowing other even more misguided desires to cloud her judgment. As I cannot seem to dissuade her from this course of action, I shall simply have to do what I can to insure that she survives her infatuation.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Afterparty at Kiki's</u></b><br /> <br /> After our escape from Peterson Chemicals, we traveled to Kiki's. Clytemnestra needed food to replenish herself after losing such a large percentage of her swarm. Apparently she was also in need of publicly laying claim to our waitress. I do hope it was a side effect of her hunger or simply a desire to show off her ability to manipulate humans. I fear, however, that it was the encounter with Puriel that prompted her actions.<br /> <br /> For my part, I was pleased enough to wait for news from Mr. Creel and discuss our next move at that establishment. Around the time that Clytemnestra was enjoying her dessert in the ladies room, I changed into Vivian to greet Shelly. She was surprised but pleased to see me. It was not difficult to ascertain that her coworkers are unaware of her leanings and so I refrained from any over displays of affection. I shall also be sure to send any flowers or other tokens to her home and not her place of employment.<br /> <br /> While we were there, I also took a few moments to send Casey Rogers an e-mail. Apparently Clytemnestra finds my behavior toward him and Miss Waters quite inappropriate. She was clearly agitated that Vivian had two interests who were unaware of each other. She did not bring Ganora into the discussion, I believe because as she sees it affairs conducted by another cover are separate and permissible by her overly complicated standards. It might also be that she discounts that relationship due to Ganora being cryptid rather than human. At any rate, she saw fit to lecture me on proper treatment of humans and both Speed and Quietus seemed inclined to agree with her view of the situation. They did, at least, refrain from commenting about it.<br /> <br /> From: Spiders N Snakes<br /> To: Casey Rodgers<br /> <br /> Subject: Guess Who?<br /> <br /> Just wanted to let you know that the lovely little darling you helped me pick out did absolute wonders for my poor friend. He's quite taken with the wee dear and has completely forgotten about the whole tragic death that was bringing him down. He can be a real nightmare when he's in a sour mood so it's a serious relief to see him moving past it. I'm sure your corporate masters are way to stingy to give you a commission or anything but I hope you at least got some brownie points with your manager for that sale. Either way, I owe you a big one for helping me out such a perfect gift and I know JUST how to repay a sweetie like you.<br /> <br /> Anyway, good luck on that big English test tomorrow. Not that you need it, since you're such a clever boy and all.<br /> <br /> See you soon,<br /> V<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>This Old Abyssal Breech</u></b><br /> <br /> Test running the repairs on the Ashbury House before attempting them with active resistance seemed wise. Also, Puriel's interference had prevented gathering Aether and lead to spending it instead. It was necessary to contain Alice to prevent her from recontaminating the house. Fortunately, Mrs Graves was up to the task. Unfortunately, we had not had a chance to brooch such a topic with Miranda. Speed was the obvious choice to go and speak to her about it so we sent her ahead. This lead to a rather hasty text to delay and a somewhat disarrayed state of both women when we did arrive.<br /> <br /> I took point on the repairs while Miranda and Robin went to speak about what exactly the containment would entail. Miranda does not seen fond of her sister, but she is loyal to her. Such a trait does bode well, given that Speed has clearly lost any semblance of objectivity where that woman is concerned. I hope we are able to access the logistical Infrastructure at Peterson Chemical soon or that we can locate a suitable alternative. I am going to need to be sure we have enough material to cleanse them both.<br /> <br /> The main point of infection was the room with the insects. Speed and Clytemnestra guided while Quietus assisted me in the hands on work. It was a good practice run for our confrontation with the entity.<br /> <br /> The lesser site was upstairs, in the room with the mysterious wardrobe. The being contained within became even more active when Miranda was present. I expressed my interest in knowing more about it and asked if we should remove it as we did with the insect host from downstairs. This was clearly a mistake, as Miranda became quite upset, though she contained it well. We did as she asked and worked quickly to finish and depart except, of course, for Speed. She remained behind and spent the night.<br /> <br /> I brought the insect host and the samples back to the lab. Without abyssal energies, they were likely to degrade rapidly and I wanted to glean as much as I could from them. Quietus insisted on remaining and quite unhelpfully standing guard over me as I worked. Despite my assurances that I had everything contained and was using all reasonable safety precautions he stayed at hand with his weapon ready while muttering about the \u201cshit bugs\u201d and ranting about them overrunning the agency and eating my eyes or some other such nonsense. After a while, I simply ignored his rambling and complete lack of confidence in my abilities and focused on the specimens.<br /> <br /> It proved to be a late night but I was unwilling to destroy the abyssal remains before I had thoroughly analyzed them and I was not willing to let them remain unattended while I slept in the vicinity. I kept a few small and well contained samples and a couple of sealed experiments but I feel confident that I learned as much as I am likely to from these manifestations. I sent Quietus to sleep in his office as I destroyed the bulk of the abyssal materials.<br /> <br /> As I was waiting for the incineration to complete so I could verify the complete eradication of the tainted specimens, I ordered some flowers to be delivered to Shelly's home address. I also had time to compose an e-mail for her. Once that was finished, I checked to confirm that the lab was safe and uncontaminated and then took to my cot for some much needed rest.<br /> <br /> From: Vivian Marley<br /> To: Shelly Waters<br /> <br /> Subject: Sweet Dreams<br /> <br /> So, I am here pulling an all nighter trying to make some order of this client's code and I was thinking about sending you a text or maybe calling you when I realized it had gotten late enough to be early and that you were undoubtedly asleep like any sane person would be at this hour. So I am instead contenting myself with remembering just how adorable you were all snug and sound asleep the other morning.<br /> <br /> I hope you didn't mind me dropping by the bar to see you unannounced earlier. I really don't want to make things awkward for you at work. As much of a pain as this whole freelance thing can be sometimes, I do occasionally forget just how nice it is to not have co-workers or a boss looking over my shoulder and being judgmental. I promise though, I'll play it cool.<br /> <br /> I mean, assuming things keep going and all. Damn, I hope this isn't all sounding weird and stalkery. But, I really enjoyed spending time with you and I would very much like to continue seeing you and follow this thing between us to wherever it winds up.<br /> <br /> Alright, this code isn't going to write itself (which is good, else I'd be out of a job) so I had best get back to it. Hope this finds you well dearheart.<br /> <br /> Thinking of you,<br /> Vivian<br /> <br /> PS: I'd like to see you on your night off this weekend. We could do something less adventurous like dinner and movie if you'd like. Your pick since I hauled you off to the see the Sisters of Chaos last time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Teddy Bear Picnic at Diablo Dam</u></b><br /> <br /> Both Clytemnestra and Speed where in good cheer the next morning, while Quietus was grumpy from the late hour and sleeping at his desk. After the usual banter and such, we set out for the Diablo Dam to replenish our Aether stores. It seemed a good opportunity to finalize my pact with Ganora and to aquatint her with the vampire's lackey in the area since we are working in cooperation with them. I called Langley Fitzgerald's office and set a meeting at his home in the evening. His eccentricity was as strong as ever. I confess, I am looking forward to seeing him and Ganora in the same room. However, I do not believe the others, Clytemnestra in particular, find them quite as endearing.<br /> <br /> The call provided the final piece in the pact in the form of Foreman Jameson. The man is in a position of some authority and seems free of entanglements. He is not particularly fond of or amused by Mr Fitzgerald's antics. The pact will instill him with loyalty to Ganora and her cult. Quietus intends to further bargain directly with him to bolster his effectiveness, which seems a prudent and useful move.<br /> <br /> Upon our arrival my dear Ganora greeted me quite warmly. She seemed quite happy that all was ready to complete the pact, clearly eager for the power it would bestow upon her. It brought a very aesthetically pleasing gleam to her dark eyes that I know full well will translate into a most delightful increase in her already impressive ardor for carnality.<br /> <br /> She shared news with us concerning the angel that we encountered on our previous visit. Miss Crimson does not like anyone to enter the area around the actual Infrastructure. Fortunately, she has continued the arrangement put into place by her human predecessor so Ganora and her people do have the Aether they need. Also she has eradicated the Rattus completely. While this is a good thing, it is also a clear indication of the risk she presents in physical confrontation. We shall need to be cautious in gathering Aether at the dam.<br /> <br /> Given our need, we did opt to risk a gathering run. We had the advantages of a secret entrance and forewarning of the Angelic guardian on our side. Also, perhaps unsurprisingly given Miss Crimson's appearance and demeanor, none of my fellow unchained seem inclined to be reckless where she is concerned. I spotted her moving along the ceiling in a fairly regular patrol route, so we were able to reach the Infrastructure and recharge in quick shifts without being detected. It extended the overall time required to fully charge ourselves and the collection of spare cellphones we've been keeping in Speed's bolthole but we completed the operation without incident and withdrew the way we'd come without compromising our backdoor into the Diablo Dam's power center.<br /> <br /> We are now waiting for nightfall to take Ganora to the meeting with Mr Fitzgerald. I believe Quietus is working on his plans to strike a bargain with Jameson. I am not sure about Clytemnestra and Speed, but I took advantage of the afternoon to spend time with Ganora and visit the egg that contains our child. In addition to sealing the contract to bring her material and human resources I have made it clear to her that I will do all in power to see her and our spawn prosper.<br /> <br /> The child should concern me more than it does. They will have some measure of my power. Also, they will be know me truly despite any cover I may wear to conceal myself. To this son or daughter I will be Kilroy first and foremost. This could make them the single most dangerous weapon against me. It could also make them a powerful ally. Someone I can be honest with. I know full well my intentions are skewed by emotion but I am powerless to change how I feel. If I am to allow this child to survive and be born, I must see that they are raised carefully. They must be nurtured and taught to understand the deeper truths of the world. They must learn to fear the God Machine and it's Angels and agents.<br /> <br /> I will raise this child to be a strong and clever soldier in the fight. There is no choice. Nothing aware of the truth underlying existence remains free of the God Machine's gaze. Weakness and ignorance will only lead to them falling prey to the lies and manipulations of the God Machine. I must not allow that. I will not allow that.<br /> <br /> It is better to die free than live as a slave. My child will be as I am, free of chains.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Okay Kayla, I promised if you were good I would tell you what all happened the past couple days.<br /> <br /> Bourbon is being good.<br /> <br /> We went to the house. Speed had\u2026well\u2026I believe Speed had a tender moment with Miranda, or two\u2026Quietus had hurt himself during paintball and\u2026<br /> <br /> Hee hee. I know right?<br /> <br /> Oh you are terrible. Please keep going.<br /> <br /> Okay that is enough I feel bad now. I\u2019m crying a little. Actually Speed and I worked out part of our interlock and he was trying. He was not actually doing anything dumb. He\u2026<br /> <br /> Oh you will have to do something unspeakable to learn that about me.<br /> <br /> Mmm hmmm.<br /> <br /> MMMM HMMM.<br /> <br /> That is not, by definition, unspeakable since you spoke it.<br /> <br /> Oh don\u2019t give me that look. I\u2026<br /> <br /> Jack is not your favorite person, is he?<br /> <br /> Oh Ms. Liquor, do you really think you have rivals? You silly thing.<br /> <br /> Where was I? Right. Anyway, I used the excuse I needed to finish healing him with my Halo to give Speed extra \u201cQuality Time.\u201d I think it went well.<br /> <br /> Because I want Speed to be happy Dear.<br /> <br /> Darling, I want everyone to be happy. Even you. Sometimes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we moved in and began a cooperative system to try to get the breach repaired. Kilroy did the heavy lifting on repairs aided by Quietus, and Speed did the lead on giving instructions with I helping. I used my Embeds so I could stay away from the toxin zone. The lower one was by far the largest and hardest, and the upper was pretty easy. I, <i>like I said</i>, stayed away from the dangerous bit both times. Robin took care of the ghost, for now. Kilroy accidentally upset Miranda\u2026that is usually Quietus\u2019s job but not being Quietus only made her really upset rather than hate us.<br /> <br /> Mmmm Hmmm.<br /> <br /> So see, first job done and I am fine. It is the easier one, but eh, I will be\u2026<br /> <br /> No, No you will not be there for the next\u2026KAYLA.<br /> <br /> KAYLA.<br /> <br /> MS. LIQUOR. Stop. STOP.<br /> <br /> Okay.<br /> <br /> The others decided to take a break from all the danger to recharge, so we hit he dam. Looking to kill two birds with one stone, Kilroy began preparing a meeting with the Goober and Ganora, which sounds like a sitcom when I say it out loud.<br /> <br /> Maybe it should be Ganora and the Goober.<br /> <br /> ~Ganora and the Goober~ okay when we sing it at the same time that sounds\u2026way too\u2026Okay let me catch my breath.<br /> <br /> You\u2019re awesome Kayla.<br /> <br /> Regardless, we had to slip in first to recharge, made more dangerous by the Angel, Ms. Crimson, hanging around there.<br /> <br /> Yes, found her name from Ganora. You remember me talking about her, right?<br /> <br /> Yea drills and shit. She never saw me. Of course.<br /> <br /> So we slipped in and out easily to meet the Goober at his house with our fine fishy friend with time to spare and\u2026<br /> <br /> You\u2019re\u2026you\u2019re not wearing anything at all under that shirt are you? Losing all self-preservation instinct are you?<br /> <br /> Right.<br /> <br /> I am going to need more bourbon.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXV</i><br /> <br /> It does sound like something may come to a head with Clytemnestra and Ms. Liquor.<br /> <br /> Note the above post on the Ciphers for our Agency so far.<br /> <br /> Speed locked on her second Interlock by guessing the Key. Clytemnestra finally got her first Interlock down but she knew the key. Quietus guessed incorrectly. Speed\u2019s player did a good job of working two OOC turned IC conversations (Minions and Ciphers) into her IC dialogue.<br /> <br /> So the repair system involved up to four characters, one rolling Strength + Crafts (with an helper) and the other rolling Intelligence + Occult (with a helper). The former could not add more successes to a given roll than the latter rolled. Every two full rounds they had to remain was a Stamina + Resolve check to fight the taint. Clytemnestra could use her \u201cAcross a Crowded Room\u201d to be the assist on the Occult and avoid making the rolls, and that was what she did, with Speed being helped by Clytemnestra and Kilroy being helped by Quietus. The first roll required a larger number of successes, second smaller. They did pretty well, all told. Each roll was five minutes.<br /> <br /> Robin used the Sin-Eater Ceremony Spectral Captivity to capture Alice. With Miranda as a distraction she got the drop on her and got a large number of successes right off and quickly trapped Alice in the bottle. That was one roll per turn, so she obviously finished quicker.<br /> <br /> Ganora\u2019s pic involves her in a thong, hence the pants thing. I was on a serious roll with Langley. He is such a schmuck and fun to play.<br /> <br /> Things with Ms. Crimson was tight. First they all failed to see each other, but then Kilroy saw her and she tied Speed, so she was suspicious but could not find them. They had to carefully take turns but got their Aether.<br /> <br /> That is all for now. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-12-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T23:38:00-07:00","id":663975,"title":"","content":"Good that you heard aout Fulgur's player!<br /> I like Speed and Miranda's relationship more and more.<br /> I also liked the conflict between Kiljoy's and Clytemnestra's approach to relatonships.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T11:33:00-07:00","id":664564,"title":"","content":"It is sort of funny to see the giant spider lecturing the robot on how to treat people.<br /> <br /> Yea the Speed/Miranda relationship is interesting. I can't really just say Gabe/Miranda because it really is Speed not just the cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T01:54:54-07:00","id":666624,"title":"","content":"I think part of the Kilroy/Clytemnestra issue stems from the fact that it seems to me that Demons have a less uniform notion of covers and identity Kilroy views the covers as basically masks or costumes to hide behind. Kilroy also does not identify as human, so sees no real difference in romancing Ganora or Shelly. Also, the last human Kilroy actually opened up to about the full truth of being a demon did not handle it well (Vivian was more or less suicide by soul pact) So yeah, they don't view relationships in the same manner. It was a fun scene to play. *smiles*<br /> <br /> And yeah, Speed and Miranda are kinda of adorable, even Kilroy can't completely deny it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-26T12:56:23-07:00","id":679277,"title":"","content":"Back to Washington. The Night Train Detective Agency is at the Diablo Dam, waiting to meet a certain ghoul. Conversations are happening, and plans being put in place. Also, romantic advice.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d gotten out of the fucking dam, Billy Mack allowed himself to be led aside by Ganora. The rest of us wandered towards the visitor\u2019s entrance to the dam. Liz and I made for the goddamn food court. Jack gave us a nod, rolled his shoulders back and strode cockily towards the Employee\u2019s Only entrance.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Gabe, you are in love with Miranda, right?\u201d Liz asked as we made our way through the fucking crowded open air atrium.<br /> <br /> I blinked at her a few times. She looked back at me goddamn seriously. \u201cI...\u201d I closed my mouth and my brow knit. \u201cFuck, I guess I am more than a bit dizzy.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded intently. \u201cHow do you know? That it\u2019s love and not just fondness or physical attraction?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShit, doll, you do ask the fucking hard questions.\u201d There was a pause as I got to the front of the fucking Orange Julius line and ordered.<br /> <br /> She looked frustrated. \u201cDo you believe that it\u2019s that you\u2019d die for her? I am quite fond of you in the agency and Robin, but I wouldn\u2019t throw my life away.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. She was on a goddamn tear for sure. \u201cI don\u2019t think it\u2019s that simple. You could love someone and life enough that you\u2019re not willing to die. And you can sure as hell be willing to die for someone you\u2019re not in fucking love with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen how? How can it be measured?\u201d She found a seat under a No Smoking sign and lit up. I looked at her sympathetically, keeping my own fucking feelings off my face. This talk of \u2018measuring\u2019 love sounded too goddamn much like 3 fucking petabytes of despair. I was pretty sure she didn\u2019t mean it that way, so I was glad to be a Demon right then. \u201cI will fall in love.\u201d<br /> <br /> I made a loud noise getting the last bit of my Orange Julius through the goddamn straw. \u201cI don\u2019t think it works like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you mean? If I have free will, I can be in love. Right?\u201d She sat back in her chair, cigarette holder up in the air.<br /> <br /> I held my hands out in fucking surrender. \u201cSure, sure, sweetheart. I just... shit, I\u2019m trying really hard not to say \u2018you\u2019ll know it when you see it\u2019. But I don\u2019t fucking know if I would have known before I met Miranda. And I don\u2019t know how much of a sheer goddamn force of will it can be.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cSorry, I don\u2019t mean to attack you. I appreciate you not brushing it off.\u201d She glanced in the direction of the lake. I would like to figure it out and soon. You\u2019re really the only one I feel like I could talk to about it either. As cold as he is, if Kilroy falls in love before me, I don\u2019t know if I could handle it.\u201d She took a drag on her cigarette. \u201cI\u2019ve used powers to make people fall in love with me, but I\u2019m too smart to have someone use them on me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned at her. \u201cOf course you are, doll.\u201d I sighed. \u201cLook, this is the kinda shit that is probably personalized, but, as far as the dying for thing, that puts the wrong... I don\u2019t fucking know, spin on things, I think. It\u2019s more about wanting to protect her, to keep her safe, as much as I do myself. Hell, probably more.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d She nodded, still fucking serious. \u201cI appreciate the data you\u2019ve given me. I have much to consider.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Jack rolled his shoulders back and strode cockily for the Employee\u2019s Only door. A security guard moved to stop him. Jack flipped his fucking badge out. \u201cS\u2019cool man. I\u2019m authorized. Need to have a word with Foreman Lester Jameson.\u201d<br /> <br /> The guard nodded. \u201cKnow your way in?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGive me a hint?\u201d Jack smiled.<br /> <br /> The security guard smiled back and gave him directions. Jack nodded genially to the other people in the hall and knocked on the fucker\u2019s door.<br /> <br /> \u201cForeman Jameson?\u201d He looked in the door.<br /> <br /> Jameson looked up. \u201cCan I help you with something?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack stepped in. \u201cAn associate of mine called earlier, I need to speak with you privately.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAbout Mr. Dorkgerald? What\u2019s he done? You the Feds?\u201d Jameson seemed fucking pleased as shit at the prospect.<br /> <br /> \u201cLester, right? I am aware of your distaste for Langley. It\u2019s part of why I wanted to talk to you...\u201d Jack began as he sat down on the other chair in the office.<br /> <br /> The foreman interrupted him. \u201cI wanna be clear about that. It\u2019s cause he\u2019s a dick, not cause he\u2019s a queer. I\u2019m not a homophobe. If that\u2019s what this is about, I\u2019ve got a fist with your name on it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, that\u2019s endearing.\u201d Jack smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy son\u2019s gay,\u201d he said by way of explanation.<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cWhat I got has got nothing to do with that. I\u2019ve got a proposition for you. \u201c Jameson crossed his arms and made considering noises. \u201cMr. Fitzgerald is well positioned with certain groups.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe does look like a Mason.\u201d He thought for a moment. \u201cOr not. Shooter looks way more like a Mason.\u201d He looked sharply at Jack. \u201cYou\u2019re not a Mason, right? I always say, if they\u2019ve got nothing to hide, there\u2019s no need to keep that shit secret. Who then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, man, I\u2019m not throwing names around. But there are other groups that wanna keep an eye on them. And we\u2019re offering a bit of a bonus for it.\u201d Jack leaned back in his fucking chair.<br /> <br /> Jameson eyed him goddamn suspiciously. \u201cAlright. Two things first. What are the goals of your organization?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged. \u201cJust want to keep the dam running properly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is the entirety of your goals?\u201d He looked dubious as hell. \u201cLook, I\u2019ve seen X-Files, you might leave and take your face off and be an alien. I don\u2019t wanna work for the bad guys.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not a bad guy.\u201d Jack gestured expansively. \u201cAll it is is that you work for the dam and report anything weird to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jameson sighed. \u201cBut your people, the ones you work for... what\u2019s the bigger picture? Overthrowing the government? Renaming Seattle to something more authentically native? I really don\u2019t want to help the bad guys.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack crossed his arms. \u201cWork with me here. Define bad guys.\u201d<br /> <br /> He started counting on his fucking fingers. \u201cAliens enslaving the earth. Replacing our leaders with lizard people. Eradicating the... a race.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can swear to you and sign it in my own blood, I am not about enslaving or eradicating.\u201d He shook his finger at the foreman.<br /> <br /> He raised his hands. \u201cWhoa man, I\u2019m not Astaroth.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack leaned closer. \u201cLook. I am what some people call a fixer.\u201d Jameson\u2019s eyes got wide. \u201cI don\u2019t kill people - that\u2019s a cleaner.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought that was a hit man.\u201d Jameson looked confused. <br /> <br /> Jack looked goddamn perturbed at the interruption. \u201cSometimes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh!\u201d The foreman smiled widely. \u201cCleaner is an inside word.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c...right. Something weird\u2019s going on here. We - I - wanna know if it needs fixing. You see, if the dam stops working, things more important than losing power will happen. You\u2019ve watched X-Files?\u201d The fixed looked significantly at Jameson.<br /> <br /> He nodded vigorously. \u201cYeah, all of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack glanced in the direction of the fucking mountains. \u201cYou familiar with the rocks? You know what they say?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo...\u201d The foreman answered goddamn nervously.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey say someone\u2019s watching. And we need to watch the watchers.\u201d Jack pointed two fingers at his eyes, then Jameson\u2019s, then at the mountains.<br /> <br /> Jameson nodded determinedly. \u201cOK.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack reached into his bag and pulled out some of his fucking papers. \u201cI have a contract here, it\u2019s more fair this way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe second thing -\u201d Jameson pointed at Jack. \u201cI want it to say that you won\u2019t come after my family. You know, in case. I\u2019m not planning on screwing up, but they need to be safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack was writing as he spoke. \u201cIn black and white, there you go.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> We met up by the car. Billy Mack had a fucking satisfied look on his face and an arm around Ganora as he greeted us. \u201cThings go well?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d Jack shrugged. \u201cLester\u2019s gonna be seeing some shit here in a few days. Gave a pad for Countdown Lion too. The orange one.\u201d He chuckled. \u201cThe guy would have been yours if you\u2019d gotten there first. He\u2019s a big X-Files dork.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor our part,\u201d Liz said archly, \u201cbased on my recent experience with Gabe, I fear - and it pains me to say - I most agree with Langley with respect to the Orange Julius. Not that I don\u2019t respect Gabe now, but if she, or I, went back...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cSpeaking of Langley, are we ready to meet him? It is approaching time.\u201d He squeezed Ganora\u2019s shoulder. \u201cI think it is important to have our contacts familiar with each other. I believe you brought Ganora some clothes?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz pulled a pair of jeans and a goddamn baggy sweater from the car. \u201cI hope you can handle denim, dear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah...\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Langley answered the door in a Little Bo Peep costume, goddamn bonnet and fucking staff included. \u201cWhy, hello!\u201d He invited us in and as he turned to get the refreshments, it became clear it was <u>half</u> of a Little Bo Peep costume. Only the belt went all the fucking way around. Tea and coffee were laid out on three trays, labeled \u2018poisoned\u2019, \u2018not poisoned\u2019, and \u2018poisoned (not to a lethal degree)\u2019. Langley called out from the kitchen, \u201cCream?\u201d<br /> <br /> We all answered in the negative and Billy Mack smiled as Langley came back in and sat down. \u201cI figured you would greet us interestingly. You didn\u2019t disappoint.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI disappointed someone once. It was terrible.\u201d Langley sighed fucking theatrically.<br /> <br /> The g-man made introductions, eying Langley for his response. \u201cI felt that, since you represented the vampires...\u201d<br /> <br /> Langley interrupted him. \u201cThey prefer sanguine impaired.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c...and Ganora represents us, you two should meet,\u201d Billy Mack continued without reacting.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, so if there are any issues, I would come to you?\u201d Langley addressed Ganora.<br /> <br /> She looked at him intently. \u201cYeah...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought it might help deal with any issues in a civil manner, not in the middle of the night.\u201d Billy Mack offered.<br /> <br /> Langley raised an eyebrow. \u201cThat is more my people\u2019s deal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd uncivilized of us.\u201d The g-man shrugged.<br /> <br /> Langley and Ganora traded phone numbers. \u201cI\u2019ll ring you if I have any particular issues. And if you need crazy blood suckers, give me a call. I don\u2019t do any sucking...\u201d Jack gave the fucker a look. \u201c...blood. But I know people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah...\u201d Ganora breathed.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou certainly are enthusiastic.\u201d The dam manager wiggled his fucking eyebrows at Ganora.<br /> <br /> My phone beeped and I glanced down at it. A message from Liz floated across it. \u2018If he keeps this up, I\u2019m going to make a dive for the poison\u2019. Out loud, she said \u201cSo, what kind of poison is in there?\u201d<br /> <br /> He fucking winked at her. \u201cAh, darling, only your undertaker will know for sure. That reminds me.\u201d He got up and walked to the kitchen, ass waving the whole fucking way. He returned with a tray of muffins. \u201cI don\u2019t usually have muffins, But I\u2019ll make an exception, this once. For you.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was no label on the goddamn muffins, and after watching Langley eat his, Jack took one. Billy Mack and therefore Ganora fucking followed suit. After a few minutes of idle gum flapping, Billy Mack glanced at the rest of us and stood to go. \u201cThank you for meeting with us. I believe we\u2019ve both moved agendas forward.\u201d He extended his hand. \u201cI am sorry I missed your show.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, we\u2019ll ride again. Once Henry\u2019s less sore.\u201d Langley waved his apology aside.<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps I will catch you next time then. Good evening.\u201d<br /> <br /> Langley threw his arms forward. \u201cTa!\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> On the ride back to the dam, Billy Mack sat in the back with a fucking arm around Ganora, warning her not to underestimate Langley just because he appears goddamn cuckoo. Once we dropped her off and started home, he sighed contentedly. \u201cThat was certainly productive.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was. And on the topic of productivity, what are our plans for tomorrow? Other than Naomi bothering her math teacher, I have no demands on my time.\u201d Liz looked sideways at Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re still waiting on Creel to follow up on the Cannon case.\u201d I frowned.<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cAnd we should wait until we have the medicine to cleanse the Room.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack sighed. \u201cRight. And who knows what state Peterson is in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI could check,\u201d Billy Mack offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly if you thought it was safe.\u201d Liz put a hand on his shoulder and smiled. \u201cAnd here I thought you\u2019d want to be the baby tear collector.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked at her with all fucking white eyes. \u201cI can check now, from here, in complete safety.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell then. While you do that, on the topic of the Room, my friend Kayla might visit soon. She wants to come here to make sure I\u2019m not doing the things I\u2019m doing. I don\u2019t really want her here - contrary to her belief, she doesn\u2019t need to risk herself that way. I\u2019m going to have to do something to make sure she stays behind when we deal with the Room...\u201d She trailed off, looking out the window, missing my significant look. Anyway, I\u2019m not asking you to trust her, necessarily. I mean, she\u2019s not the type of Integrator to sell us to the God Machine.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack turned to her. \u201cJust think it\u2019s broken and also fixable?\u201d Liz nodded. \u201cAn intriguing notion. Peterson is still functional and repairing itself. There is a second Angel, with wings, dark eyes and cracked skin. I am quite willing to bet that she is well equipped to notice stealthy intruders and serves as a spotter for the now patrolling Hugbot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could potentially negotiate with other Demons for their knowledge of any nearby Logistical Infrastructure of the right type.\u201d Liz pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is mandatory to have, and soon.\u201d Billy Mack agreed.<br /> <br /> Liz looked at the time and took out Naomi\u2019s phone. In the pink haired girl\u2019s voice, she said \u201cBitch\u201d and hung up. She looked goddamn thoughtful. \u201cWe could even offer to let them make it and not have to tell us where it is, or have to be afraid that we\u2019ll screw up their system.\u201d She considered for a fucking moment. \u201cThe Fools first, I think, with Valefar as a last resort. He is a mastermind, I would rather not be in debt to him for any reason.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Fools might even be willing cut us a good deal, considering what it\u2019s for.\u201d Jack looked back and forth between the two of them.<br /> <br /> Liz smiled craftily. \u201cNot to mention that I would like to speak with Ms. Clocks again. We could also ask about Respectable Ping, before Jack goes pissing in their Cheerios.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack sneered at her. Billy Mack smiled and responded, \u201cTrue, we don\u2019t want to step on any toes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr spiders.\u201d I sneered back at Jack for Liz.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhore.\u201d I looked at her with one fucking eyebrow raised. Liz hung up Naomi\u2019s phone and switched back to her own goddamn voice. \u201cI believe this is the proper response from a petulant artist to the person who spread rumors about her. It definitely seems like what Naomi would do.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack had a vacant expression for a moment, but raised an eyebrow of his fucking own at that. \u201cBy the way, Puriel\u2019s Infrastructure appears to be some sort of foundry type location. There is not much light where she is, but a lot of heat. I suppose it is not truly surprising.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat she\u2019s dark, hot and intense? No, not really,\u201d Liz responded. She glanced at Naomi\u2019s phone. \u201cOne more time.\u201d She dialed the number and paused a goddamn moment, tuning on Naomi\u2019s voice. \u201cOh, are you her boyfriend? How long does it take to wash the stink off?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> After I dropped the others off at the fucking office, I took off for the Asbury House. Miranda had implied that I would be welcome to come back there. I just hoped the goddamn late hour wasn\u2019t a problem. I finished my flask driving down her road and rifled through the glovebox as I went up the drive. I had finished the rye that was usually there last night and hadn\u2019t restocked it.<br /> <br /> I got the last few drops from my flask and got out of the car. I leaned against the pillar outside the door, jacket over my shoulder, after knocking. She gave me a sleepy half smile as she opened the door. \u201cHello Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey there beautiful.\u201d She was wearing an old fashioned night gown that was soft under my hands as I stepped in close. \u201cHope I didn\u2019t wake you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re fine.\u201d She gave me a kiss. \u201cThough I do believe it is time for sleeping.\u201d<br /> <br /> I brushed a stray strand of blond hair behind her ear. \u201cSounds like a plan to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> The next morning I debated having the talk with Miranda, about what I am and what we could possibly do. The peace of the morning was too much to break though and until we had a usable Logistical Infrastructure, not particularly time dependent. So after a late breakfast, I kissed her goodbye and headed into the office.<br /> <br /> \u201cOK, piece of shit, call Jake22.\u201d My phone dialed Stalking Horse and put the fucker on speaker for me.<br /> <br /> Jake answered after a fucking ring or two. \u201cHey, what\u2019s up?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHad a business proposition for you. You free to meet on the soon?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cDinner soon enough? At Kiki\u2019s?\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a wrong turn, different from the goddamn wrong turn I made yesterday, circling around the city to get to the fucking office. \u201cSure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. Now, should it be me, me and Ms. Clocks, or just Ms. Clocks?\u201d He smiled.<br /> <br /> I thought for a moment. \u201cBoth, if it\u2019s feasible.\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled. \u201cWell, she\u2019s deigned to show up once, that\u2019s the hard part. It shouldn\u2019t be a problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Jack met me at the door with a goddamn coffee mug. \u201cYou need to go by Liz\u2019s office.\u201d His cryptic warning, or whatever the hell it was, given, he fucked off.<br /> <br /> I passed by Billy Mack looking at a fucking map of the area with a handful of pushpins in it, muttering to himself. Leaning on Liz\u2019s door, I saw her talking goddamn animatedly to a green haired woman with a sweet smile and a pretty face. The new girl looked up at me and smiled cheerfully. \u201cOne moment!\u201d She went over to Liz\u2019s bar setup and came back with a cloudy yellow drink. \u201cYou must be Gabe. I\u2019m Kayla.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded and took a sip from the best goddamn whiskey sour I\u2019d ever had. Liz laughed at the look on my face. \u201cKayla does use her god-asterick given talents, yes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can mix other chemicals too, but it\u2019s not as much fun.\u201d Kayla shrugged modestly.<br /> <br /> \u201cKayla came early to help out,\u201d Liz explained. \u201cThough all we have planned is speaking with the Fools and you shouldn\u2019t come with us there.\u201d<br /> <br /> I kept sipping my sour as Kayla got a goddamn grumpy look on her face. \u201cSo long as \u2018speaking with the Fools\u2019 is not a euphemism for dealing with the Abyssal breach.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked in, fucking dubious. \u201cYou want to be involved in that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf she\u2019s involved, I\u2019m involved. I\u2019m a Psychopomp, we fix things. Don\u2019t let her leave me behind.\u201d Kayla\u2019s mouth was goddamn set.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing doll.\u201d I smirked at Liz, who was mouthing \u2018We\u2019re going to leave her behind, tied up if necessary\u2019 behind the green haired woman\u2019s back.<br /> <br /> Liz sighed. \u201cIt wasn\u2019t a euphemism. We just don\u2019t know these Demons that well, is all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s fine then.\u201d Kayla smiled, just for Liz. \u201cI don\u2019t <u>think</u> I\u2019ll get lost in your house.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack raised an eyebrow at the goddamn emphasis on think. \u201cThat is a tough job.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kayla laughed. \u201cTell me about it. I was trying to find the bathroom this morning...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, the meeting\u2019s for dinner at Kiki\u2019s...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack interrupted me, muttering. \u201cJust not enough detail.\u201d I glanced back at the fucking map. It looked like he had Puriel\u2019s hits marked on it. He was right - there weren\u2019t enough goddamn data points.<br /> <br /> Liz waited for an explanation for a moment. With none suck fucking thing forthcoming, she went back to our conversation. \u201cSo, we have a few hours then. Anything I can be of help with?\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow at the goddamn unusual offer, then glanced at Kayla and smiled. \u201cThe Works?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is dangerous but...\u201d Liz looked at Kayla.<br /> <br /> Kaya sighed exasperatedly. \u201cI know what the Works are, I can come. I\u2019m not useless, I have a machine gun and can reach in my pocket and pull out explosives.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not Private Vasquez. You need to be careful. A bulletproof vest maybe?\u201d I gave Liz an amused look. She fucking ignored me.<br /> <br /> Kayla, for her own goddamn part, ignored her. \u201cI can also transform entirely into liquid, and by liquid I do mean booze.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smirked. \u201cStay away from Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m the only one that is going to drink her dry.\u201d Liz had a wicked gleam in her eye and Kayla smiled back at her. It was like something from a goddamn romance movie. Or maybe a porn I saw once.<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me specify - stay away from Gabe, or Liz will be mad.\u201d Jack moved fucking quickly to catch the mug I lobbed at him.<br /> <br /> Liz smiled goddamn cheerfully. \u201cAbout that bulletproof vest - I can think of two reasons she can\u2019t get one off the rack.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack coughed. \u201cI was going to say, I think we could pick one up, easy enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I still have that one from the cute Asian bodyguard. It might fit. Still have her book too.\u201d Billy Mack gestured at the paperback on his fucking desk.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t tell all our secrets,\u201d Jack stage whispered at him.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack spread his arms and shrugged. \u201cWell, I wasn\u2019t prepared to have her believe I <u>purchased</u> Cocklords of Mars.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Okay now that you have gotten a hold of yourself I can continue. Do you have a death wish Darling?<br /> <br /> You do make it sound tempting, yes.<br /> <br /> So where was I\u2026oh the dam. Kilroy went off to be disturbing with Ganora, and Quietus apparently successfully met with the Foreman and got us an agent for our group. I hung around with Speed and gave her more romantic advice. I want to see things go well with her and Miranda after all.<br /> <br /> Mmmm Hmmm.<br /> <br /> Then we met with the Goober. He was wearing the front half of a Little Bo Peep outfit, and was bare on the back, short the belt that held it all together. He had muffins, and three options for tea \u201cpoisoned\u201d, \u201cnot poisoned,\u201d and \u201cOnly a little poisoned not lethally.\u201d <br /> <br /> Yes, yes I know.<br /> <br /> But the meeting went smoothly, overall. If we were human, I think we would have been off guard, and I think Ganora was confused the entire time, poor dear. But, well, they know of each other, and they can communicate as needed.<br /> <br /> Having the Goober halfway between town and the dam is usually a good thing for getting home. However, we had to drop Ganora off at the dam then turn around and go home, so it was half again the time. She had clothes on, fortunately. Also fortunately, Speed is not called Speed Demon for nothing; it is no empty boast.<br /> <br /> I asked about seeing you, which is why I called. I did not expect you to rush over. Our short visits and calls you have been worried about me and the Abyssal stuff, so it seemed good to have you here a bit.<br /> <br /> Listen, I need to lay down rules.<br /> <br /> Mmmm Hmmm.<br /> <br /> If I tell you we are going to deal with the Abyssal stuff, you will stay behind where it is safe, you will not risk corruption or death. You will do this even if I have to handcuff you to something.<br /> <br /> Okay, true, you can slip out. It the.<br /> <br /> Oh.<br /> <br /> No handcuffs. But you will stay behind Kayla I am serious.<br /> <br /> Next, no preaching to the Agency with your Integrator stuff. I am serious. Quietus will fucking end you.<br /> <br /> Regardless of if you want to see him try I don\u2019t. I don\u2019t want either of you harmed, Kayla.<br /> <br /> Last, but not least\u2026you should put on some pants, lest you get consumed right now.<br /> <br /> Mmmm Hmmm.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVI</i><br /> <br /> Largely roleplaying. Kilroy \u201cpicked up\u201d his new Clairvoyant Demon Form power when his Primum went up due to his Interlock. He traded one out for it.<br /> <br /> As always, Speed\u2019s player fairly faithfully recorded the conversations. All the banter you are reading actually happened.<br /> <br /> So next is the Works. How exciting! They have been talking about going since the game started!<br /> <br /> That will be next time, though. In the meantime comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T14:04:55-07:00","id":696476,"title":"","content":"Exploring the works, having a meeting with the Fools, and meeting Clytemnestra\u2019s SO. The session was full of exploration, physical and for one member of the Agency, emotional.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s journal does not recap the session, but takes place after events described in Speed\u2019s. The conversation did not happen in game.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> The Works covered a large area, filled with pipes and machinery and abandoned buildings. Three of those latter, to be fucking exact, a large one that had held the Infrastructure and two smaller ones that had, once upon a goddamn time, served a fucking offices and storage for the main facility. The Agency Symphonic Metal had set off an explosion in the storage areas that had caved in a goddamn underground complex. Nobody fucking knows how extensive that shit is, or was, or at least they are not fucking saying. Enough so that the third floor of the Infrastructure building is now sitting at ground level.<br /> <br /> A high fence circled the place. Regular patrols and rumors of goddamn radiation served to keep most motherfuckers away. The patrols weren\u2019t in the habit of making trouble disappear - enough Fortean douchebags tramped around the fucking place that it would get hairy if they all disappeared, even for the goddamn God Machine. Things that for past the obvious security got into trouble of their own. Robin told us about a pack of werewolves that got run off the damn place by whatever the goddamn hell called it home. Just as disturbing is the fact that fucking werewolves felt the need to go poking around.<br /> <br /> We approached it along a small dirt access road. It was public fucking property, but the only place it led to was private, so I planned on pulling aside before we got too fucking close. While I was looking for a good spot, Billy Mack jerked his head towards a goddamn muddy turn off. I raised an eyebrow at him, but turned down it.<br /> <br /> Following it led to a small service building outside the campus on the east side. It was abandoned, for its original goddamn purpose at least. Now it was apparently every fumbling Fortean fuckwit\u2019s wet dream, to judge by the beer can, condoms and goddamn \u2018occult\u2019 imagery scattered about the fucking place. The lock on the outer door was broken and the lingering pieces of furniture had been shoved to the edges of the room, out of the way of what used to be a hidden trapdoor.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack indicated the trapdoor. \u201cThat leads to a tunnel that used to connect to the underground complex. After about a ten minute easy walk, it\u2019s caved in. I thought we could either tunnel up to get past the wall and patrols, or we could break through the cave in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI like breaking through myself. Shatter and a hit or two from your rivet guns should make short work of it,\u201d Jack said, rolling his shoulders back.<br /> <br /> I shrugged, looking between the others. Liz had already transformed into her goddamn transfixing spidery form and sat suspended above her long golden mechanical legs. Kayla followed soon after, becoming a warm golden liquid humanoid shape, filling the service outpost with the sweet and goddamn tempting scent of bourbon. Billy Mack fucking ruined it, the dick, adding a hint of sulfur with his glitchy transformation. I forgave him, comparatively, as soon as Jack glitched his own transformation and overwhelmed every other smell in the area with the hot scent of burnt metal. It receded after a moment. Not too far though, we weren\u2019t that fucking lucky.<br /> <br /> I managed to transform without fucking glitching myself. I didn\u2019t figure on needing to drill mygoddamnself, but I still styled myself after the old scifi standby mole machine, cylindrical and compact. I bulked the hell up, affixing a set of resistors on a thick outer plating. I preferred my rod to the fucking cutter, but I brought it out anyway - it might help get through a rough patch. Lastly, I boosted my goddamn sonic receivers. We were worried about what might be set up waiting at the end of the tunnel and every bit counted.<br /> <br /> We made our way down the tunnel. The collection of beer cans, condoms and conspiratorial markings didn\u2019t let up and the stubs of candles and a burnt out LED flashlight or two joined the rest of the trash. The sound of steady goddamn thumping machinery was all I could hear from beyond the cave in. Kilroy phased through while Jack and I found an appropriate \u2018cap\u2019 to our tunnel, that we could leave intact to cover our fucking traces.<br /> <br /> We\u2019d found a good goddamn solid slab of rock and moved it aside by the time Kilroy got back. \u201cThis tunnel, straight ahead, will lead to the former ground floor. The machinery you hear,\u201d he nodded towards me, \u201cis on the second floor. The place smells strongly of mothmen, but there were no active signs of them. There was a small, 6-wheeled drone patrolling the hallway. Breathing sounds indicate a roughly rhino-sized animal is asleep in one of the other rooms off the hallway.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised my eyebrows. \u201cYou didn\u2019t want to fucking lead with the sleeping goddamn rhino?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, because then you would have stopped listening.\u201d He looked at me levelly. \u201cIt is not truly a concern of the moment. It is probably not small enough to fit through the door, based on the sound.\u201d<br /> <br /> Giggling sounds came from Ms. Liquor and Clytemnestra. \u201cDid it have to be the boobs?\u201d Kayla chided Clytemnestra, who looked over at her with a fucking gleam in her eye.<br /> <br /> Kilroy looked over with a goddamn smile. \u201cYes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI dated girls to get away from this shit.\u201d Ms. Liquor rolled her eyes at him while she dodged Clytemnestra going in for another sip.<br /> <br /> I raised a finger. \u201cYou still dated girls who liked fucking girls.\u201d I made circular motion in front of my chest.<br /> <br /> She stuck her tongue out at me as I leered at her and we got to work. Kilroy and I took turns clearing the fucking rubble and shooting the larger pieces that Quietus had prepped with Shatter. Clytemnestra followed up behind using her adhesive to maintain structural integrity.<br /> <br /> When Kilroy let me know we were close to breaking through, I was able to pick out the breathing sounds he had mentioned. I kept an ear out for changes that would give up the fact the thing had woken up, whatever the goddamn hell it was, but the breathing never changed. With the last rocks moved out of the way, I got eyes on the drone. It bathed the area before it in red light, but didn\u2019t appear to have any other sensors. It was transmitting on a short range radio frequency, nothing that could possibly leave the complex, without a relay setup. It wasn\u2019t sophisticated, just a constant check in signal and transmission of the general shape of things inside the red light.<br /> <br /> We shut the door to avoid having to dance around the fucking thing. \u201cSo, we wanna get at that fucking shit, right?\u201d I jerked my head upwards, towards the sound of thumping machinery.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is most likely where a good portion of the Infrastructure was located.\u201d Kilroy nodded.<br /> <br /> My treads rolled over the table, gaining me a few feet of height. I was able to extend my laser cutter just enough to put its full fucking power to use, cutting a hole in the ceiling. Eddies of essence wafted through the hole.<br /> <br /> The air up there was goddamn thick with it. Heat came with it as well, the dull hear of moving parts. Light was provided by red emergency lighting that was all a backup generator could provide. The room the hole let to was a large central room, flanked by three slightly smaller rooms. Each, along with the central room, held a fucking big Aether releasing generator. Only one was in working order and not the one here, of goddamn course.<br /> <br /> Kilroy looked thoughtful. \u201cThe place Puriel was meditating was like this but... more. Perhaps her Infrastructure was built to replace this one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat would explain why Puriel goes to such lengths and is given such leeway to defend it.\u201d Clytemnestra nodded.<br /> <br /> The room with the working, thumping generator also had four creatures in it that we could see, with the vague sounds of movement betraying the presence of several others. They looked like fucking scorpions, with goddamn gray alien heads and no-shit rocket launchers for tails. They chattered in First Tongue, arguing over who was going to check on the noises they heard.<br /> <br /> We dropped back down through the hole. Jack spoke in a low tone. \u201cSo do we adhesive the door, or explore down here? I could sneak around, get eyes on the big guy?\u201d<br /> <br /> Kilroy\u2019s brow knit. \u201cFor what purpose?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis place supposedly either made or repaired Angels. If we could find these facilities, we could potentially repair glitches. Or even find an alternate solution to the Abyssal taint.\u201d Clytemnestra shrugged. \u201cI\u2019m happy to seal anything you want though. Presuming I don\u2019t get my head cut off,\u201d Ms. Liquor objected quietly, \u201cI can undo it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps it would have been better put, \u2018Why now?\u2019. We have particular goals for this foray. Dealing with large cryptids is not...\u201d Kilroy was interrupted by a series of fucking rocket blasts landing in the room above us. I moved quickly, grabbing the cut out portion of the ceiling and holding it in place. Clytemnestra got my goddamn drift, and glued it in place as soon as it was there. I could hear eight voices now, searching that central room now that they\u2019d peppered it with rockets.<br /> <br /> Quietus smirked, jerking his head upwards. \u201cI like these people. \u2018We don\u2019t know what\u2019s there, let\u2019s fill the room full of rockets then go out and check\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes at him. \u201cYou fucking would.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d ride those motherfuckers like mounts...\u201d He had a far off look in his eyes.<br /> <br /> I ignored him. \u201cWith that shit... we got an idea of the fucking layout, have our very goddamn own back door. Wanna call it a successful scouting mission?\u201d I looked to Kilroy. \u201cUnless we wanna deal with some of these fuckers while we\u2019re all powered up?\u201d<br /> <br /> Kilroy listened to the upper floor carefully. \u201cThat generator is unstable. If it is not repaired, it will explode. Ten minutes or ten years from now, I couldn\u2019t say.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo do we wanna negotiate with them?\u201d I offered.<b