of Demon, I can appreciate his low BS kind of Demon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is my kind of goddamn gee.\u201d I walked a fucking coin across my knuckles and smirked at her.<br /> <br /> The dame looked unsurprised but didn\u2019t say anything. \u201cWe should still investigate the Build a Bear. The feud with Michael White is particularly interesting. I mean, they are still bad guys, and I want to burn down Build a Bears on general principles, but...\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cThe fact they were willing to involve the mortal authorities is what intrigues me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd helpful.\u201d Liz\u2019s eyes lit the hell up. \u201cThere will be a police report with why they wanted him removed. They could have had to tell them something. Vivian opened her laptop and got to work. Giving her time, Liz turned to me. \u201cYou should take Miranda to the Build a Bear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI dunno how she feels about the fuckers.\u201d I added a line to my fucking sainthood application when I didn\u2019t ask when we could make it a double date.<br /> <br /> After a moment, Vivian smiled. \u201cGot it. He was... \u2018intimidating employees\u2019. They have him down as a known troublemaker, but note he was falsely accused before. So no charges, but they still escorted him away, since it was private property after all.\u201d She chuckled. \u201cApparently, he was excessively cooperative.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a lull in the conversation as we considered our two targets, so I nudged Liz and glanced towards the pair I\u2019d noticed before. They hadn\u2019t done anything fucking proactive to go after the \u2018weird', but I figured Liz might be familiar with the student at least. \u201cAh, Adria. I wonder what she\u2019s doing here.\u201d Turns out she was.<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cBlondie brought her here to the goddamn epicenter of weird.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked the blonde over. \u201cNaomi needs to meet her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA week ago I\u2019d have called dibs.\u201d I grinned at her and took a drink.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou need another cover - a college student. Or a naughty professor. Or a tattoo artist...\u201d Liz shook a finger at me.<br /> <br /> Vivian stroked her chin thoughtfully. \u201c\u2018Epicenter of weird\u2019, huh? That\u2019s almost like a challenge.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAdria\u2019s a challenge. She keeps running hot and cold with Naomi. Come to think of it, hot when Deanna\u2019s around and cold without her.\u201d Liz took another sip.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe she\u2019s keeping up appearances around an audience? Or wants to make Deanna jealous?\u201d Vivian suggested.<br /> <br /> Liz considered it. \u201cI don\u2019t know. She\u2019s the one who started the politically Canadian thing, by the way. Well, not entirely, but she got us doing it. There\u2019s going to be a rally.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you figured out what it is yet? Maybe I should ask her...\u201d Vivian looked Adria over.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have. Usually she just finds out what you\u2019re into and asks \u2018doesn\u2019t that sound politically Canadian to you?\u2019 It usually does.\u201d Liz shrugged.<br /> <br /> Vivian kept fucking looking at Adria. \u201cI need to see how she\u2019d respond to Vivian\u2019s anarchist leanings.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz got a dark look in her eye. \u201cJust don\u2019t make her your chew toy. Not to tell you what to do, I\u2019m just protecting my people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstood. She\u2019s university.\u201d Vivian raised her hands.<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cYou should still all make college covers. I can get you into the best parties, since they are the best because Naomi\u2019s there.\u201d She looked over at me. \u201cIf we\u2019re splitting them, you can have the tattooed girl. I am nothing but generous.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sneered at her, goddamn glass halfway to my mouth. \u201cThat\u2019s alright, I\u2019ve got my own blondie.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTalk her into a three-way. Naomi\u2019s good at that.\u201d Liz smiled fucking brightly.<br /> <br /> I sighed \u201cYou had your couple of fucking drinks yet? Is it time for step three of the goddamn plan?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz sighed too. \u201cYes.\u201d She turned to the other two. \u201cI\u2019m taking the night off. Are you three going to scout out the water wheel?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t see why not. It\u2019s kinda urgent, right?\u201d Jack shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, message me when you are out safe. I\u2019ll check in regularly too.\u201d Liz looked nervous.<br /> <br /> <br /> When we got into the office, Liz called out for Kayla. When she came out into the lobby, Liz said, \u201cWe\u2019re going to my house.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOK...\u201d was as far as Kayla got before Liz kissed her, far clumsier than I would have expected. Of course, it being Liz it was still twice as goddamn graceful as I ever am. It looked like it might have been the first time they\u2019d ever even kissed. No wonder she was so goddamn fucking nervous. \u201cI guess so.\u201d Kayla looked nervous herself as she followed Liz who had a vice grip on her hand.<br /> <br /> Vivian watched them go and sat staring for a moment before turning to me. \u201cIs that what you two were talking about in the bathroom?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cI could tell you, but I\u2019d have to kill you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. Well, before we head to this water wheel - I\u2019ve figured out the next Embed in my cipher.\u201d Vivian looked pleased with herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d Jack prodded.<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cData wipe. I can erase one statement of fact from collective knowledge. Until people research to fill in the hole - the context stays put.\u201d<br /> <br /> I got a big grin on my face. \u201cSo have you activated it yet?\u201d She shook her head no. \u201cGot something you want erased?\u201d Again, no. \u201cJenny\u2019s number!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that old people music again?\u201d Jack asked. Vivian and I both glared at him. He held his hands up. \u201cWhat? She\u2019s not here, somebody\u2019s gotta say it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes at him. \u201cC\u2019mon, 8675309. Jenny\u2019s number. It\u2019s perfect.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian chuckled dryly. \u201cWhy not?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck yeah, why not!\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t supposed to be this way.<br /> <br /> Kayla I\u2026<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, you say you love me but do you realize what this means? The implications of this? We are in love it\u2019s\u2026<br /> <br /> How do I feel? I feel weak.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t supposed to be this way. I had it all planned out. I would take you to your favorite restaurant. We would go dancing. We would go out on the pier and hold hands. There we would kiss for the first time. Then we would return here and, over a course of hours, slowly make love to you, giving you the most pleasure anyone, man or woman, has ever experienced. Then I would sink my fangs into you, and drain you utterly into myself. It would have been glorious, Kayla.<br /> <br /> Yes, I can in fact imagine why you are happy it turned out differently. I\u2019m not\u2026am I?<br /> <br /> Kayla, I kissed you on impulse. It was not how your slow first kiss from me was to be. I shoved my tongue in your mouth, drove here, then staggered half dressed to the bedroom where we fucked for like an hour and a half. Rutted. It could have been better for you, Kayla. You deserved better than this.<br /> <br /> It is true, I have plenty more chances\u2026but I\u2026I can\u2019t eat you now. I don\u2019t want you to die, even to me. I must have you close, near me, in me sometimes. I\u2026I feel so vulnerable.<br /> <br /> Very funny. Yes I suppose this is how I make other people feel. I\u2026.<br /> <br /> \u2026I was hoping you felt that way too.<br /> <br /> Kayla, I don\u2019t\u2026I don\u2019t know how to do this. I don\u2019t knnmmmmmmmmmmm<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Yes, I feel better. Just\u2026I can\u2019t believe this is happening. I had everything planned. Everything had a purpose\u2026what if something else kills you Kayla? Someone who isn\u2019t me I\u2019m\u2026I\u2019m scared for you. Vulnerable.<br /> <br /> I\u2026<br /> <br /> Yes I did say I wanted to be love. It was true I did\u2026.I mean I do\u2026I mean I am.<br /> <br /> I did not expect it to be so overpowering I\u2026<br /> <br /> I need you, Kayla.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll just need each other than. And have each other. Kayla I\u2026.<br /> <br /> Of course Kayla.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s done now. I messed this up once but now I swear, nothing will tear us apart.<br /> <br /> My love.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXVII</i><br /> <br /> Isn\u2019t that sweet?<br /> <br /> So the Works took a good chunk of the session. Kilroy\u2019s contacts (via Vivian) knew of the back way in, so he got to make a roll to know too. A good deal of time was spent deciding how to enter; everything from Speed becoming a mole machine with burrow to separating into aboveground and belowground groups. In the end, it came down to Rivet Guns, Shatter, and Adhesive (Giant Spiders are handy).<br /> <br /> There was also a fair amount of initial planning, whether to look for the Werewolves, whether it was a Wound, and other concerns. They had a plan for cutting the fence until Kilroy made his roll.<br /> <br /> Colleen is Ms. Clocks, Jake is Stalking Horse.<br /> <br /> The rest was straight RP. And yes, I have some ideas for a rally for \u201cPolitically Canadian\u201d students. But that storyline will be after the Abyssal one is dealt with.<br /> <br /> Yes, they deleted Jenny's Number, at least temporarily.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome, see you next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-10-2015, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-26T02:22:04-07:00","id":728189,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s got to be a morning after. But we start with the night before for those of the posse other than Ms. Weaver. The raid on the water wheel starts our session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> The water wheel was located in a residential area, surrounded by normal, everyfuckingday houses. Getting close to the wheel had my fucking nerves on edge for no goddamn apparent reason. I gripped the steering wheel tensely, scanning the area and even activating a couple of my usual form powers. It wasn\u2019t until my fourth sweep of the goddamn still streets and then looking back that I realized what was wrong - there wasn\u2019t a single fucking lit street lamp. Or unlit ones for that matter, not for blocks around the place. That let me relax, a little. Fear of the goddamn dark is hardwired in and the dull roar of white noise from the turning wheel only added to the feelings of fucking sensory deprivation. It was still dangerous as hell - it was a goddamn piece of Infrastructure - but IDing the problem helped with the feeling of creeping dread.<br /> <br /> After driving by, we ditched the car a bit away and hoofed it back. Jack still fucking reeked of goddamn burning metal, so he was the look-out. He gave the place a glom with his electrical sight, getting a good read on the place. There were two doors each, each locked with a keypad, each spotlit by a light from the top of the building. They both had a camera watching and the front door had a watchman standing guard. The windows were all alarmed. It wasn\u2019t the most secure place I\u2019d ever found carelessly left open, but it was gonna be hard to get in either door without a higher than fucking preferred chance of tipping our hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, so do we blow a break... fuck, it\u2019s a goddamn power plant. Do we, shit, EMP or cut the wires to a particular light and camera combo?\u201d I eyed the facility, standing close to the others so we could hear each other over the roaring waters.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Guardian\u2019s be over that like fucking white on rice.\u201d Jack glared at it, personally affronted.<br /> <br /> I ran my finger over a water smoothed stone I\u2019d found on the shore. \u201cDidn\u2019t say it was a good goddamned plan. I don\u2019t suppose we\u2019re fucking lucky enough that they give tours, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cNot as a general rule. They are open to the public, I believe, just not a tourist location. Visitors would look out of place.\u201d<br /> <br /> I snapped my fingers. \u201cCollege students wouldn\u2019t. If Naomi came by, doing research for, fuck, I dunno, a poli sci paper on public works or some shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr an article on green energy for the newspaper...\u201d Billy Mack mused. \u201cNot a bad idea, but I have a thought for a more immediate plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShoot.\u201d I looked at him expectantly.<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI\u2019ve picked up an aquatic form recently.\u201d Apparently, Ganora was fucking rubbing off on him. \u201cWith your amorphous nature, we could even both go in through the river. And once we\u2019re in, I will hopefully be able to possess a worker to run the analysis on what it would take to modify our process so that the production facilities here can manage it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I frowned. \u201cDoesn\u2019t the Guardian go around masquerading as a worker?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. However...\u201d Billy Mack paused for a goddamn moment, calculating something. \u201cI believe it has the best probability of technical success, in the sense that should we be discovered - should I attempt to possess the Guardian - we would be able to escape without having been seen and without revealing any of what we are or want.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged. \u201cSeems reasonable.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou won\u2019t fucking be there.\u201d I glared at him, then sighed. \u201cBut, yeah, that seems like a reasona... an alright conclusion.\u201d<br /> <br /> We both made the quantum shift, and I tweaked a few things as I did, to get an aquatic form as well as fucking night vision and electrical sight. We spent some time determining the quickest way a human sized being could be pulled or pushed into or out of the facility, in case Jack needed a way in later. That done, we took a goddamn tour.<br /> <br /> Inside, the fucking creepy crawlies came back. It seemed normal enough, even the full work crew on site. Power plants don\u2019t get to shut down after normal business hours. The motivational posters up around the place had the usual goddamn inspirational pictures but the captions were things like \u2018Hard work is rewarded in Heaven\u2019, \u2018There is no life without pain\u2019, \u2018The water is life\u2019 and finally, \u2018You are being watched\u2019. The entire internal staff appeared to be Cambodian and spoke to each other in that language, though the posters were in English.<br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d had eyes on any room the water flowed through, we found one closest to where there was likely to be a goddamn computer terminal. Kilroy signaled he was about to go in and then one of the workers melted into the ground and every worker stood and turned in unison. We got the fuck out.<br /> <br /> Jack was further away from the fucking dam than we\u2019d left him, crouched and eying the front door. I followed his sightline to the security guard, whose eyes glowed white. \u201cThe hell did you do?\u201d he asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI appear to have chosen poorly in my choice of vessels.\u201d Billy Mack responded gravely.<br /> <br /> Jack\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cSo why are we still here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCause somebody\u2019s asking dumb fucking questions.\u201d I sneered at Jack and started walking for the car.<br /> <br /> Back at the car, Billy Mack turned to look towards the wheel. \u201cThat is a very secure facility.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cIt\u2019s been here awhile. They\u2019ve had time to work the bugs out.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue.\u201d He sat quietly a moment. \u201cIt should not be too much of a hardship to take the time to prime the production. The production aspects of the Infrastructure certainly seem secondary and are less likely to be locked down, even if there is an alert.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough.\u201d I bit my lip and took a goddamn drink. \u201cSo, we just have to get the goddamn tears then, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can get those.\u201d Billy Mack nodded.<br /> <br /> I glanced over at him. \u201cAlright. Do you need...? I don\u2019t know if I want to fucking finish that question.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have a plan to get more than enough.\u201d He smiled at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am 10000 goddamn percent sure I don\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I finished my flask tidying up some goddamn paperwork and started on another on the way to Miranda\u2019s house. I smirked at her as she answered the door, stepping in close for a kiss. \u201cHey beautiful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHello yourself Gabe, Did work go well?\u201d She smiled at me and took me by the hand to lead me to the kitchen, where coffee was waiting.<br /> <br /> I stalled, taking a sip of the coffee. \u201cWork was good. Real good.\u201d I took another sip. \u201cWe\u2019ve been working on something... it\u2019s why we haven\u2019t moved on the room yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her brow knit. \u201cAlright.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, we had our source for the spackle stuff. We - Billy Mack mostly - have figured out how to use it to make something similar, for people. Enough for everyone who\u2019s been tainted.\u201d I found that smooth river stone and started fidgeting with it. \u201cEnough for you. And for..\u201d I paused, but interrupted her barely formed response. \u201cTwo things. First, I, fuck, I didn\u2019t want to hand you something from an unknown source on just my word without you knowing where it\u2019s from and what I am.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked at me, a serious look on her face. \u201cWhat you are?\u201d<br /> <br /> I ignored the emphasis on the first word. \u201cRemember how we talked about how my old boss and your old people - the Seers,\u201d I said hastily at her raised eyebrow. \u201cOne thing they have in common is that there are consequences for talking too much about either, so I couldn\u2019t ask the questions that would help figure out how similar they are. But... hell, this might be easier than I\u2019m making it. Does the God Machine mean anything to you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her face was fucking blank. \u201cSomewhat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd its servants? Angels?\u201d She drew back slightly. I smiled. \u201cI\u2019m not an Angel. But I used to be.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo now you are...?\u201d The suspicion was still there, but so was curiosity now.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cA Demon. A fallen Angel. One of the Unchained.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat does that mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMostly? That the God Machine fucking hates me. And that I live on multiple quantum planes of reality at once and I can use that to hack the system. The vehicle I turned into at the junkyard? It\u2019s just a different quantum state of me.\u201d I watched her face, tapping the rock lightly on the table.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo who are you?\u201d She poked me on the chest.<br /> <br /> I smiled sardonically. \u201cThe God Machine carves out little bits of reality for all its servants. Our covers come into being instantaneously and then have been there all our lives. Gabe is who I was when I fell. Her past, her history, the stuff I told you before... it may not have been real before Gabe hung her shingle in LA, but it still had a hand in making her - me - who I am.\u201d<br /> <br /> She frowned slightly. \u201cI wish you wouldn\u2019t refer to yourself in the third person.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry love.\u201d I smiled at her. \u201cIt\u2019s... weird.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sat for a moment and sipped her coffee. \u201cYou are still a person, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI fell because I made a choice. Because I figured out free will and gave the goddamn God Machine the middle finger. I guess that makes me a person?\u201d<br /> <br /> Another moment of silence, then she seemed to come to some decision and laid a hand over the one I had tapping the rock. \u201cDo you need to be hidden?\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned my hand over and gave hers a squeeze. \u201cIt\u2019s kinda built in. I mean, don\u2019t go around introducing me as \u2018my girlfriend the Demon\u2019 but a lot of my innate stuff is centered on hiding me.\u201d I smirked at her. \u201cI imagine you scanned me magically?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did. You showed as human with every spell I tried.\u201d She looked vaguely put out.<br /> <br /> \u201cSpoofing\u2019s a hell of a thing.\u201d I leaned back in my seat and grinned at her.<br /> <br /> She finished her drink and muttered, \u201cI suppose I didn\u2019t have enough enemies before.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is something we\u2019re gonna deal with.\u201d I pointed at her. \u201cSoon, hopefully.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt has always been me against the world.\u201d She smiled at me. \u201cI\u2019m glad to have it be me and you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled back at her. My smile faded when I remembered the rest of the shit I wanted to talk to her about. \u201cSo, that second thing I mentioned... with the medicine, as we've been calling it - I was thinking, but didn\u2019t know enough and I wasn\u2019t going to tell Billy Mack to figure out...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe?\u201d She raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, I know you said you weren\u2019t ready to talk about him and I don\u2019t want to push but I was wondering if you thought something like the medicine would help with...\u201d I trailed off, looking at her helplessly, then glancing in the direction of the wardrobe.<br /> <br /> Her smile was gone. \u201cMy son.\u201d I nodded. She shook her head. \u201cI don\u2019t know what effect it would have on him. I don\u2019t know what effect it will have on me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I frowned. \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe taint is killing me. That\u2019s for certain. But it is also partially fueling the magic that is keeping me healthy, young and difficult to injure.\u201d<br /> <br /> My eyes widened, but I managed to clamp down on most of my panic. \u201cI don\u2019t like the sound of that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s why I can\u2019t magically remove the taint. My magic is filtered through it, somewhat. It\u2019s how the Scelesti operate. But I don't know what will happen. I might advance to my physical age, instantly. I might die. I might simply begin aging again as normal and have to find some way to protect myself in the future.\u201d She looked at me levelly.<br /> <br /> I looked around and bit my lip. \u201cSo it\u2019s not the serum, we can\u2019t just modify that...\u201d I muttered. I stood up and took her mug and mine to the sink.<br /> <br /> She closed her eyes briefly. \u201cThis is why I didn\u2019t want this relationship.\u201d She stood up as well. \u201cBefore, this would have been a relief. Now, it\u2019s possibly a tragedy.\u201d She stepped closer. \u201cBecause of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, we\u2019ll just have to make sure it\u2019s not.\u201d I turned around and leaned against the sink.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou better.\u201d She threw herself into my arms.<br /> <br /> <br /> She was up and coffee was on when i rolled out of bed the next morning. I leaned against the wall as she handed me a mug with a distracted look on her face. \u201cI have some