rolonged exposure. I wonder if the amount of power also increases in keeping with it, to offset the increased cost of sustaining the flesh or if it is a slow but inevitable decline? Perhaps, once this is over I will be able to speak to Miss Asbury about it and gain some insights from her own first hand experiences.<br /> <br /> Of course, that does require her to survive the cleansing of her taint. The key seems to be the timing, if the spells are ended first, then the taint is suddenly unchecked. If the taint is cleansed first, the spells are left without a source of power. Quietus suggested that Speed's pocket space could be useful, as it is not subject to time and entropy. Given the limits of my knowledge of magic, it seems the best option. Miss Asbury is also sequestered to research and prepare herself for the process. Given the way she has presented this to Speed and what I know of her mannerisms and personality, I believe that she does actually expect that she may be able to survive intact. If she did not, I think she would have either told Speed directly or kept it entirely to herself. I hope, for Speed's sake, that her abilities are up to the task. Sadly, this falls beyond my own expertise and as far as I know there is naught I can do to help Speed's paramour. <br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Fair Trade</u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> I suspect it was an effort to distract herself from the chance of losing Miss Asbury that put Speed on reviewing other matters. But she brought up Mr Paulson's situation. At present, we are awaiting word from the Changelings as to their preparations to assault Mr Smiles' stronghold. A less than ideal position.<br /> <br /> Speed was frustrated with the wait and brought up the possibility that we might have alternative solutions. We discussed the matter and decided to at least investigate the option of, as Speed put it, negotiating with terrorists.<br /> <br /> As Vivian, I contacted Dr Samuel Miles and reached him directly. We discussed the situation guardedly and in the end reached some agreement. We shall bring Overseer to pledged neutral parley for him to inspect and judge whether or not the angel is a viable replacement for myself. I have attempted to impress upon him the absolute finality of my intention to avoid being taken. I am afraid, however, that he does not grasp just how absolute my will to remain unchained is or, more likely, appreciate the powers at my disposal. Pity, he could prove a powerful and useful ally and I could certainly offer him much as well if he could be trusted but it seems most likely that his inability to rise above his base desires shall make any such arrangements impossible.<br /> <br /> While speaking, we did reach an arrangement concerning Drake Paulson. Mr Smiles will relinquish him in exchange for us delivering a simulacrum of his own body to the local Changelings and claiming to have killed him. That he clearly does fear their impending attack is worth noting. As is the fact that he is aware of it. In the end, the others seemed unconcerned with the deception since the True Fae are difficult to kill permanently and thus the Changelings will expect his return. Also, whether or not Overseer is sufficiently 'unique' to convince his fellow Gentry to allow him back into Arcadia, he will be occupied for some time with the attempt.<br /> <br /> The only real issue at stake here is that this does mean we'll be going hot at the Water Wheel by design, and thus damaging a known Infrastructure given to us by the Fools. Also, Clytemnestra shall need to exercise the self restraint to subdue without killing Overseer. She will be displeased.<br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>The Water Wheel</u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> Clytemnestra returned from the university where she, as Naomi, had seduced Dr Cross and acquired a blood sample. As expected, it was contaminated. However, it was a higher degree of contagion than I expected. Her taint exceeded Angela's which led to some speculation on what her involvement with the Asbury room was. Theories were put forth, but we have nothing beyond conjecture. Apparently, Dr Cross' mental state is troubled. She apparently has self loathing issues which seem to at least in part stem from a difficulty in accepting her own sexuality. Clytemnestra is concerned and has her cultists keeping watch over the woman. Once she is free of the Abyssal taint, it should help some, but the underlying issues will remain. I am fairly certain that Clytemnestra intends to delve into her history and attempt to fix her. She should make a useful addition to the University cult.<br /> <br /> As expected, Clytemnestra did not take the news of my arrangements with Mr Smiles well. Honestly, I find her behavior overly emotional. She chooses to embrace of the concept of being a predator as self identity very deeply, even to the point of it being a detriment to her. But then, she is hardly alone in her emotionalism. Most newly fallen demons I have encountered seem to revel in the sensations of emotion that are part and parcel of our expanded consciousness as Unchained. Not that emotion is absent in older and more established angels, and is often a precursor to if not part of the cause of the epiphany of free will.<br /> <br /> I am not devoid of emotion but of the Unchained I know I seem to be the only one that tries to rule it rather than allow it to rule me. The same is largely true of all emotional beings in my experience, human and otherwise. I cannot truly blame those that were born seeped in such animal instinct and irrational drives to find it difficult to rise above such. But why those that have been without self direction find it so appealing to surrender themselves to this flow of impulsive and illogical behavior is beyond me. I have only just now opened my eyes to making my own decisions, why would I turn that over to some reptile brain chemical-driven Id? And why is it that my stance on this is the outlier? Is it that I myself am abnormal? If so, I must confess that I prefer it to those that seem ruled so by one base desire or another.<br /> <br /> Hmm. Perhaps the answer lies in the intensity of the emotional experience. Positive emotions are a source of great comfort and pleasure. Even pain and loss are intense experiences. It is the case that an addict will pursue their fix with reckless abandon, even with the full awareness of the consequences of their actions. With that in mind, perhaps I should be more mindful of my own actions. I have certainly made choices driven by purely emotional rewards. Some of these have very clearly been mistakes. Fleeting satisfaction spurred by an overly strong reaction to a show of authority was a poor payoff for offending the Autumn Court. That brief high cost me a measure of security that cannot be recovered. It resulted in a much stronger degree of emotional distress. It necessitated the expenditure of time and resources to making reparations. It placed the Agency in a vastly inferior position with a very powerful group that could have been (and admittedly may still become with sufficient diplomacy and management) extremely useful allies. <br /> <br /> At any rate, she was indeed displeased but did agree to capture Overseer without killing him.<br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Round and Round She Goes</u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> We arrived at the Water Wheel without incident. Our plan was fairly straightforward. Through Vivian's contacts with various hacktivist collectives, I had secured a blackout of the local call towers, promising them something big. I had the virus tailored to disable Overseer's known abilities and a few of the likely and highly inconvenient possibilities. Quietus had a small radio, so that Speed could stay in contact with him.<br /> <br /> Speed and I entered via aquatic form as before. Clytemnestra entered as a spider swarm. Quietus waited outside, both as lookout and to disable the external guard once we moved into the second phase of the operation.<br /> <br /> Infiltration went smoothly. There was a powerful and very obvious stigmatic patrolling that had not been present before. I accessed the systems and initiated the serum production. While Speed discreetly feed the materials to the Infrastructure, I explored the system. I determined that the main purpose of this Logistical was to jointly provide power to a Command and Control with another Logistical. It had been briefly and hastily converted to do some light production work, seemingly as part of the aftermath of the destruction of the Muckworks. Digging slightly deeper, I was able to identify the stigmatic as the Deacon of Agony, a ranked member of the pain-centric God Machine cult that made up the workforce. I was also able to determine that there was a much higher power output than the hydro-electrics alone could account for. The remainder came from a torture facility located beneath the main structure.<br /> <br /> Once the serum was finished and safely stored inside me, we moved to initiate the attack. Clytemnestra reformed near the terminal that would dump Overseer once the virus disabled his ability to possess the facility. Quietus was given the green light to neutralize the external guard. Speed and I moved to attack the Deacon of Agony. The rank and file cultists quickly joined in, taking up tools as improvised weapons. The Deacon of Agony's ability to hurl lightning was impressive and quite effective at bypassing even my own normally high levels of armor. However, within a few moments, we were able to secure the facility. Overseer was cocooned and the rest were dead.<br /> <br /> Speed and Quietus searched out the hidden torture chamber while Clytemnestra and I removed a fair amount of the secondary apparatus to build our Aether generation resources up. When we joined them, they had killed the two stigmatic cultists and Speed was experimenting with the essence gathering equipment. She has an interest in emotionally charged essence. I was surprised to find both interested in the equipment. I would have assumed that it's pain oriented function would have been more distasteful to them. They did ask about converting it to some less negative emotion, and I explained that the main issue would be the need to acquire the actual gathering equipment. The theater was mentioned. The use of the battery simply to store Aether gathered elsewhere was also brought up. In the end, we dismantled the converter and some of the gathering apparatus and loaded them, along with our captive angel, into Speed's hyperspace.<br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Where She Stops, No One Knows</u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> As we moved to depart, Clytemnestra stopped us and alerted us to helicopters. She then swarmed and slipped out. Speed and I carried Quietus with us as we flowed out, depositing him on the shore when he was at his limit for air. Unfortunately, the scent of burning metal that he had been emanating due to previous transformation drew the attention to a pair of angels in dog covers that seemed to have been optimized for detection and tracking. They closed and engaged. Clytemnestra swarmed one while Quietus used an embed to open a portal to the underworld. Both slipped into it and the angels did not attempt to pursue them.<br /> <br /> Speed and I were able to flow with the river to her car, which she possessed before the angels in the air cover could identify it clearly. Their attempts to track us as we peeled away were valiant but entirely fruitless. Even in it's currently unfinished state, that car is a masterpiece and there is no one that can match Speed's skills in driving.<br /> <br /> <u><b><b><u>Home Again, Home Again</u></b></b></u><br /> <br /> Speed took extra precautions to insure that we were not being tailed before returning to the office. Once there, we sent out a general warning and then made a couple of specific calls. I contacted Jimmy Marsh, who seemed a bit distracted by the hour to give the matter his full attention but did eventually seem to grasp the level of scrutiny that was likely starting up. Speed alerted the Fools through a voice mail drop.<br /> <br /> We then tried to contact our missing agents but had no luck. We left messages with the various drops set up and settled in to wait. Or at least I did. Speed grabbed her coat, hat, and gun and headed out with a cryptic comment about needing to run an errand. I was not really in condition to provide backup and Clytemnestra and Quietus were incommunicado, which seemed to make going out ill advised but I was also not in a position to stop her. I would guess from the emotional intensity in her that she was off to see Miss Asbury, whom she said had told her she needed time and solitude to work out her means of surviving being cleansed of Abyssal taint. But such is the irrational behavior of one in love. Hopefully I will continue to remain blissfully free of such madness.<br /> <br /> I took the quiet to mend my wounds and rest while waiting for any word from our missing comrades. Speed returned, still agitated, and settled into her office to drink and then sleep until the meeting with Mr Smiles.<br /> <br /> I left her be and returned to my own rest.<br /> <br /> On our way to our meeting Clytemnestra contacted Speed. Both she and Quietus are alive but he is apparently injured after their escape through the underworld. Her tone suggested that all was not entirely well but she assured us the situation was stable for the moment. We'll retrieve them once this business with Mr Smiles is done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:25:43-08:00","id":760266,"title":"","content":"<b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> Kayla, sweetheart, I am safe.<br /> <br /> Yes, yes, I\u2026wait\u2026.no, no we did not do the room! I promised, Kayla!<br /> <br /> Anyway, yea, the Water Wheel. While I had originally been promised the Angel, Overseer, to make up for the unsated hunger from not utterly consuming you, they decided to provoke the tiger by making a deal with Mr. Smiles without asking me involving them giving Overseer to him. I was quite pissed off, and made that clear.<br /> <br /> Still I am a good team player, better than them, and went along with it. Speed and Kilroy went in via the water in aquatic form while Quietus, who was still having odor problems, waited to ambush. I went in as a spider. There was a power stigmatic walking around, who my powers revealed to be a major leader keeping an eye out.<br /> <br /> We decided to have Speed and Kilroy ambush him while I pounced on Overseer, who would be forced into his angelic form by Kilroy\u2019s virus. Quietus would take out the Stigmatic in the front, much weaker, and we would clean up the workers.<br /> <br /> Overall, it went smooth. I caught Overseer easily. The leader stigmatic, the Deacon of Agony, proved difficult to put down. He managed to hit Kilroy and hurt him with a lightning stream, but Speed and Kilroy took him down. Meanwhile Quietus easily got in. The cultists tried to stop us but we easily\u2026<br /> <br /> Fuck, hang on I have another call I need to take.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yo Deanna, you know what time it is?<br /> <br /> No, I did not say I would see you tonight. I said I would try to get out of my plans. I couldn\u2019t sweetie.<br /> <br /> Sweetie\u2026<br /> <br /> Look, I am many things, but I am not your girlfriend, compreende?<br /> <br /> Deanna\u2026Deanna\u2026 Aten\u00e7\u00e3o!<br /> <br /> I\u2019m sorry I did not see you. I could not get out of it. I will spend time with you when I can. You are pissing me off.<br /> <br /> Go to sleep, Deanna.<br /> <br /> Boa Noite<br /> <br /> <br /> Back Kayla.<br /> <br /> Where was I? After we busted up the angelic stuff, Kilroy and I uprooted some of the equipment...<br /> <br /> Right yea, the the medicine. We did that first. Sorry.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Kilroy and I were grabbing stuff and Speed and Quietus found a small pain factory below. They took down a couple cultists and found equipment. Quietus was a bit too enthused about a charging station we found, and Kilroy about the pain machines, so that delayed us as well as the uprooting stuff for parts.<br /> <br /> We spent long enough that we relized as we hit the top the area was swaming with angels, including choppers with them.<br /> <br /> Helicoptors, not motercycles.<br /> <br /> Speed and Kilroy got away easy. They used acquatic form, fled to the water, and sped off. Even helicoptors can\u2019t keep up with Speed Demon.<br /> <br /> I was sneaking off as spiders, when I saw Quietus being set upon by dogs. Angel dogs. I distracted one, while he made an Underworld gate, and we fled in.<br /> <br /> Yes, I know, too daring. I did not want anything to happen to Quietus. Anyway...<br /> <br /> ANYWAY....<br /> <br /> So...Quietus and I were escaping through the underworld, and he was holding on, and he grabbed my breasts by accident, and, uh...<br /> <br /> No, I didn\u2019t slap him.<br /> <br /> Yea...<br /> <br /> Sweetheart...sweetheart, Kayla, calm down<br /> <br /> Please?<br /> <br /> No I love you Kayla<br /> <br /> There is no need to have \u201cA word\u201d with him Kayla...I don\u2019t feel the same about...<br /> <br /> Kayla, I am fucking telling you about it.<br /> <br /> I wanted you to know what happened.<br /> <br /> Kayla...<br /> <br /> KAYLA I GOT ATTACKED BY ANGELS AND STUCK IN THE UNDERWORLD AND I WANT SYMPATHY GOD FUCKING DAMNIT!<br /> <br /> That\u2019s sweet. Thank you.<br /> <br /> We are safe now. Soon and Speed and Kilroy are done with their giving away my dinner, I am going to go home, and get some sleep.<br /> <br /> I wish you were there.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXIX</i><br /> <br /> <br /> So this was the first major test of Kilroy\u2019s Virus making ability from his Cipher. I think it went well, and the spread has been interesting: he infected the computer, Overseer tried to possess it and was infected, Clytemnestra was infected by biting Overseer, but this was anticipated. Clytemnestra\u2019s Demon Form powers were well suited to capturing Overseer. Her extra, extended legs, adhesive, and Essence Drain make escape from her difficult.<br /> <br /> Not unrelated, when she was dashing through the underworld and made the comment about not groping her, I asked Quietus\u2019s player if Quietus groped her. Quietus\u2019s player made a random roll and determined yes, so Clytemnestra turned him into spider chow. Well, he survived the sexing and draining\u2026. Clytemnestra passed a Resolve + Composure roll not to kill him, same roll she made with Overseer and Ms. Liquor. It was still hilarious\u2026she was now trapped in the Underworld and the guy who could get her out was unconscious. She used Halo to heal him enough to get them out, but hand to turn it off given the Hunter Angels had gone active.<br /> <br /> They do still have to pay group XP for the Suborned Infrastructure. They (like my other games) get 1 XP per game in the group pot, 2 if everyone present does a journal (which only happens in Changeling).<br /> <br /> Instead of Glitching as has become usual, Speed and Clytemnestra, who passed their transformation Cover checks without an Exceptional Success, took \u201cSpooked\u201d (Speed) and \u201cShaken\u201d (Clytemnestra). Speeds resolved in her going and annoying/distracting her girlfriend, while Clytemnestra failed the ambush attempt at grappling Overseer.<br /> <br /> Quietus is always immune to electricity in Demon form, and before going to the torture room Speed used Amorphous to become that way as well. Thus the lesser lightning did nothing to them. The big guy had souped up lightning that did hurt Kilroy (ignoring metal armor) but nothing too lethal. Still, the damage roll was high.<br /> <br /> That covers everything, I think, and I am out of time. Still, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T14:48:56-08:00","id":770967,"title":"","content":"With a major Infrastructure hit, it is time for the Agency to go quiet for awhile. Just kidding, you did not think I would let them do that did you?<br /> <br /> As a note, today\u2019s scenario involves student groups with a religious or explicitly irreligious slant. This is not a statement of the group\u2019s beliefs. Any religious or irreligious folks of any bent in my games are presented as people, with good and bad. My extended group has Agnostics, Atheists, Christians, Diests, Jews, and Pagans in it and faith (or lack thereof) is not a factor when having friends game with us. We are not assholes. But we also acknowledge some people are. So\u2026<br /> <br /> Also as always every conversation in Speed Demon\u2019s Journal happened in game. I am terribly proud of my repartee. However, Clytemnestra\u2019s journal is a short fiction which did not happen in game, but the fallout from it will be first thing they deal with next time. It takes place at the same time as the events at the very end of Speed\u2019s Journal.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> I went to put my goddamn phone in my jacket pocket and realized I didn\u2019t fucking have one on. It was back in my office where I\u2019d clung it over my chair. I shrugged it back on, making a half hearted attempt to straighten out the wrinkles and ran my fingers through my hair as I joined Vivian in the lobby. She looked at me, a concerned eyebrow raised.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe only time it\u2019s fucking acceptable to see dawn is at the goddamn end of a long, relaxing couple handles of whiskey or because your goddamn lay was so fucking good you didn\u2019t get to sneaking out until then. Neither of those things happened last night, so don\u2019t fucking give me that look.\u201d I grimaced.<br /> <br /> She chuckled and patted my arm as we got in the Mustang. The meetup was in an alley near Kiki\u2019s, but my paranoia got tripped before we\u2019d gone a goddamn block. Unmarked black cars were out in force and moved with a purpose, gumming up traffic with intent. Moments after that became clear, I caught a glimpse of another one of the fucker\u2019s helicopters. I immediately fired up my Radio Suite and fucking Aura Sight while I was at it. It\u2019d be nice to know what the hell fuckers like Mr. Smiles looked like using that bit of machinery.<br /> <br /> It took a moment of scanning to find their frequency. It sure as shit wasn\u2019t in the first place I looked. When I did, I gripped the goddamn steering wheel tighter and sped the hell up. \u201cFuck.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe?\u201d Vivian looked around alertly.<br /> <br /> \u201cFifteen units of God Machine fuckers sweeping the area,\u201d I said distractedly. \u201cThey can track the fucking Guardian.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cIt\u2019s a good thing we told those we care about to lay low.\u201d<br /> <br /> I relaxed some. \u201cAlright, the goddamn unit closest to us is distracted - found some poor fuck they thought was us who\u2019s giving them a hard time.\u201d I paused to catch the details. \u201cHuh. That\u2019s the alley we cornered Gina in.\u201d<br /> <br /> I caught sight of Vivian\u2019s eyes going pure fucking white before she slipped on a pair of sunglasses. \u201cThe unit appears to be five low Rank Angels, the MBI types. They\u2019re fighting...\u201d She chuckled. \u201cYour, what is it, mustard gas breathing motherfuckers? Plus a friend, who to all appearances, seems to be causing the Angels to spontaneously combust. And to be damn impossible to hit, despite standing in the open against five opponents with SMGs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s not anybody we know then?\u201d I kept an eye on the fucking unusual traffic and an ear on the goddamn radio.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think so. He\u2019s definitely into the whole vampire thing - brooding, creepy eyes, dark leathers, those clawed finger armor pieces.\u201d She glanced around, her focus on the immediate again.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cSo, nobody I give two shits about involved. Check.\u201d I checked the mirrors. \u201cLook, we should negotiate in my bolthole.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat does sound like a good plan. We are mystically responsible for security at the meeting.\u201d She nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut you tell him about it. I\u2019m not talking.\u201d I drew my hand flat across my throat.<br /> <br /> Vivian smirked. \u201cGood. Otherwise, you\u2019ll probably wind up fucking something you don\u2019t want to.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pointed at her. \u201cAnd fuck that. Shit. Definitely not at the same time. Goddamn it - I am not talking.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> We\u2019d gotten to the alley and been parked for a few minutes when Mr Smiles sauntered up from around the corner. He was dressed like he was going to the goddamn theatre with a proper fucking \u2018re\u2019, holding a long garment bag. \u201cI apologize that I am not quite on time. Traffic was hellish.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s quite alright.\u201d Vivian nodded. \u201cIn light of the potential implications of said traffic, and in the interests of security, might I offer a change in venue? My associate,\u201d she indicated me, \u201ccan open a door to a safe place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was going to offer a hidey hole myself, but I am willing to go as a gesture of good faith.\u201d The tall motherfucker smiled broadly. I opened the nearest door and went in, holding it open for the two of them. He looked around with interest at the random shit there. \u201cInteresting place. Call it... barbeque boutique.\u201d I looked him over as he passed. Not too different from a Changeling, but I should be able to tell them apart with some inspection.<br /> <br /> I smiled. Vivian gave me a look. \u201cThanks.\u201d She indicated the webbed up Angel on the desk.<br /> <b