 the approaching sirens.<br /> <br /> <br /> I got to the office fucking early the next day. Shit, I\u2019d gone to bed a fucking four PM, and with Miranda still holed up at home, I didn\u2019t have a hell of a lot else to do. Billy Mack was already there and greeted me with \u201cSomeone\u2019s been in my lab.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about eating your fucking porridge?\u201d I took the cup of coffee he poured for me.<br /> <br /> A concerned look came over his face and he glanced in the side room. \u201cWell, there\u2019s no one sleeping on my bed.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked and brought up the news on the computer. \u201cShit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHmm?\u201d Billy Mack glanced up from cataloging whatever the fuck it was that had been touched.<br /> <br /> \u201cA van exploded at the Mothman Theatre. And a body was found nearby - not many details there, but a cop got hurt.\u201d I brought up the video clip. \u201cShitfuck. It\u2019s fucking crawling with people.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful. \u201cI hope the mothmen are ok. We didn\u2019t give them anything that would allow them to do that, did we?\u201d<br /> <br /> I set my coffee down and took a shot from my flask. \u201cI don\u2019t fucking know. If we\u2019re going to salvage anything, I need that cover... maybe Jack could get me a gambling addiction.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is both unfortunate and fortunate timing. Had I not needed to sleep, I likely would have been there with Casey when the altercation took place,\u201d Billy Mack mused.<br /> <br /> \u201cHell of a goddamn date night.\u201d I tried a few other news sites without getting any more details.<br /> <br /> .Billy Mack looked at me disapprovingly. \u201cI was hoping to use the mothmen and the Infrastructure to awaken the boy.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cUse Ganora?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a little out of the way...\u201d Billy Mack was interrupted by Jack\u2019s arrival.<br /> <br /> \u201cJack. Just the fixer I was fucking hoping to see. I need a gambling addiction.\u201d I smiled widely at him.<br /> <br /> He stared at me blankly. Billy Mack handed him a coffee. \u201cHave you seen the news today Jack?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked away. \u201cNo.\u201d<br /> <br /> I spun the monitor towards him. \u201cTrouble at the goddamn theatre.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFuckheads,\u201d he muttered under his breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cExploding vehicles and the like.\u201d Billy Mack was back to straightening up the cabinets. \u201cWere you in the lab last night?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cI made some colored amylase...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBroke any chairs?\u201d I interrupted him.<br /> <br /> He gave me a confused and pissed off look. \u201cI was trying to make a distraction.\u201d He paused and answered the unspoken question we both had. \u201cBumfuck Northwest Paranormal.\u201d Billy Mack and I looked at each other. \u201cThey don\u2019t have any footage, at least.\u201d He sighed. \u201cLook, there was a dead body.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThe news mentioned.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIts spine was ripped out, by something big, 2-3 days ago.\u201d He downed half his coffee. I offered my flask.<br /> <br /> My phone rang, with Naomi\u2019s ringtone. \u201cHello Naomi.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey there Gabe. I was just calling to see if I need to come in today?\u201d She smirked. \u201cI dunno about you, but I had an awesome night. Deanna is definitely sure I\u2019m me, and I don\u2019t wanna leave.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNewsworthy shit\u2019s gone down at the theatre. Nothing to rush in on now though.\u201d I topped off Jack\u2019s mug from my flask.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, well, the TV\u2019s not what\u2019s gotten turned on here.\u201d She sounded surprised.<br /> <br /> My phone beeped. \u201cHey doll, Jake\u2019s on the other line. Be right back.\u201d I hit the button. \u201cJake. You alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled. \u201cWas gonna ask the same of you. You mentioned the old theatre, down on Lindow Street. You\u2019re not near there right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot now.\u201d I leaned back in my chair.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. Angels are coming in hot, about eight or so. You didn\u2019t leave anything behind, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cNah. Thanks for the heads up though. You been doing ok with the extra fuckers around?\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled. \u201cYeah. I\u2019ve been catching up on Netflix. Clocks has been doing what she does.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBest not to ask?\u201d I offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cProbably Korean soap operas. That shit melts your brain, Ms. Clocks loves \u2018em.\u201d He rolled his eyes. \u201cTake care of yourself Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSame to you buddy.\u201d I swapped back to Naomi. \u201cHey doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi took a moment to get back to the phone. \u201cHey, right, so... what\u2019s the plan?\u201d<br /> <br /> I ran my fingers through my hair. \u201cLaying low. Chilling out. Fucking your girlfriend.\u201d I paused. \u201coh. We need to get up with Crusher. He can make it so we can see Changeling shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. Two hours?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> A quick phone call arranged for Crusher and Rosanna to come by the office in a couple of hours. I\u2019d just started moving towards my own goddamn office when Cecilia let us know Cannon was here. We went down to talk to him.<br /> <br /> He shook all our hands fucking enthusiastically. \u201cI\u2019ve talked to Drake. He told me you did what was necessary and I\u2019m here to settle up.\u201d I took the offered check and filled out a receipt. \u201cHe said you were right and respectful. You did good. Thanks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re quite welcome Mr. Cannon, it was our pleasure.\u201d I leaned against the wall.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou three be careful - there\u2019s anarchists in the city. The press is under attack.\u201d He shook a finger at us.<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cI heard it was a shitty cable show.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shook his head. \u201cThey gotta start somewhere.\u201d He nodded to all of us. \u201cAny of you get locked up, you give me a call. It\u2019s a dangerous business.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll keep that in mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> <b><b>Demon of the Morning</b></b><br /> <br /> The Spider opened her eyes.<br /> <br /> The girl lying beside her filled the Spider\u2019s nose with the smell of hair products. Deanna Lee had a particular smell that was a particular combination unique to her. The Spider\u2019s human form moved a little closer, letting it overwhelm her senses. She liked the smell, now.<br /> <br /> Still, she was troubled. Deanna realized she was a lesbian halfway through <i><i>Mean Girls</i></i> when she realized she liked the wrong people for the wrong reasons and accepted it three-fourths of the way through. She liked sassy, snarky women, and as the Spider was spinning Naomi, they seemed a perfect combination. Naomi would be the cute girl she had a crush on. They would have the same Math class, and Naomi would need help. They would talk, and Deanna\u2019s being annoyed at Naomi\u2019s rudeness to their teacher would be overwhelmed by how much she liked it, and she would do battle within herself before yielding to the irresistible force that was her desire for Naomi. They would have a fiery relationship, and her tendency to stay and study in while Naomi went out would be perfect. Naomi would never get in trouble at parties she was not actually there for.<br /> <br /> Deanna wasn\u2019t Pagan, but she did not believe in her parent\u2019s religion, and their general (but not fierce) distaste for lesbians had left her further disaffected. The LBTQIA friendly campus had drawn her, and the Pagan student group and it\u2019s charismatic leader would, with Naomi\u2019s help, draw he there.<br /> <br /> And everything went according to plan. Deanna fell in love with her. They started dating quickly. Deanna did not try for commitment; Deanna\u2019s nervousness about admitting she had a girlfriend stemmed in part in it\u2019s ability to keep her from having to directly lie to her parents and partially from low self esteem, but the end result was she did not push too hard on Naomi\u2019s freedom. It was very nearly perfect.<br /> <br /> But was the manipulated love love at all? Would Deanna have fallen for her without the dominoes being placed just right? The spider was uncomfortable. Was this a natural love? Had Deanna given her heart to someone indirectly because of what the God-Machine did? Only silence answered the Spider, and it left her unsettled.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey Pretty\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna stirred and had turned to face her lover. The Spider broke her reverie.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s the face I wanted to wake up to. Feeling better sweetie?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider pushed Naomi to the fore. \u201cOf course I am sweetheart. I feel great anytime we are naked together.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlways the Romantic.\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna got up and put on a robe. Naomi\u2019s robe. Of course, Naomi left it handy on purpose.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen are you going to teach me magic?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider twitched.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen I get better at it. And after I bully Cassandra into giving me permission. It\u2019s a special thing in her tradition,\u201d Naomi lied to her intimate lover.<br /> <br /> \u201cGardnerian?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi rolled her eyes. The Spider would have rather kept the bonhomie up. \u201cShe isn\u2019t Gardnerian in either her magical practice or traditions. She is mostly not even Wiccan.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, not my faith. I am certainly not Gardnerian.\u201d Naomi stretched. The Spider wanted to smell Deanna\u2019s hair again. \u201cWanna get a shower, grab some breakfast, and jump in bed again?\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna wrinkled her nose. Damnit. \u201cLike, after we change the sheets, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh right. Sheets don\u2019t wash themselves. Apparently she did not know Naomi hadn\u2019t changed the sheets since last time. Did Naomi even have clean sheets?<br /> <br /> \u201cHow about we shower, go get food, and go to your room and kick your roommate out. I am too tired to change sheets today.\u201d Domestic Bliss.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll think about it. I\u2019m getting first shower. I know you won\u2019t behave, so wait your turn.\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna disappeared into the bathroom. Naomi watched her go. The Spider considered. Speed would not need her, would she? This is a period where her Agency was to maintain a low profile.<br /> <br /> The Spider weighed her options. There wasn\u2019t really all that great a chance of having sex in her dorm. Naomi craved more sex, but the spider was fine with cuddling. Smelling her hair again. It smelled like humanity. People. There was a greater chance of sex if she stayed here. She could lie and pass off old sheets she never got around to washing as clean. But\u2026she had already lied too much to Deanna today. And she had only seen her for five minutes.<br /> <br /> The shower started.<br /> <br /> Naomi picked up Deanna\u2019s phone and furtively checked for messages. Two from Adria.<br /> <br /> \u201dI can\u2019t believe you went home with that bitch!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi smiled, but the Spider did not. Naomi put down the phone.<br /> <br /> The Adria situation would need to be dealt with. She was getting more hostile to Naomi. Why? They had been friends. Adria was flirtier with Deanna than Naomi, but that was okay. They got along. Adria now seemed to be actively trying to sabotage her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy is that?\u201d Naomi murmured aloud.<br /> <br /> No reply from the shower. Naomi checked her phone. Something went wrong with the theater. But it was low profile time, too risky to investigate. An all clear from Cassandra. Am checking in to ask about Angela. Oh yea, Angela. She would need food, and best not to have the servants do that. Shit. Naomi walked to the shower, and shouted over the loud noise of the water.<br /> <br /> \u201cLady Covington needs a quick errand. I will meet you at your Dorm and we can grab breakfast, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a pause.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, um, you are okay with me being here alone?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider thought about this. Naomi had gotten mad before when she found Deanna asleep inside, though honestly that had more to do with the whole blackout and getting through the locked door.<br /> <br /> \u201cYea, babe. If I am running out on you like this least I can do. Key on the cabinet near the door, just give it back when we meet. This way you know I have to show up, eh amada?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026Okay. I love you Naomi.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh what the hell why not?<br /> <br /> \u201cLove you too Deanna\u201d<br /> <br /> As Naomi headed out the door, her form rippled a moment as her clothes and body became completely clean. She locked the door from the inside and stepped out, hearing it latch behind her.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere must be an easier way to do this,\u201d she opined aloud, as she stepped into the pale light of an October morning sun.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXI</i><br /> <br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s story was to be titled \u201cDeceptions II\u201d but the title it wound up with was irresistible when it came up. Her somewhat obsessive behavior resulted from her getting a version of Guilty for passing her Cover check without exceptional success.<br /> <br /> I think everyone wanted to kill Andrew at the table, if less than Michael White. Also, Heather was generally deemed creepy\u2026the picture for her is kinda awesome. As a note on Anti-Psi, we use a slightly pumped up version, same as in Balance of Shadows\u2026Psychic Powers a chance die, -5 to Low Magic or Ghostly use of Numina or Manifestation, (Spirits are unaffected) and \u20131 to Sin-Eater Ceremonies. But they are easily enraged by talk of supernatural, and cannot perform Exorcism or Warding.<br /> <br /> Heather\u2019s having never a met a Demon was not an error\u2026the previous meetings they were always in Cover.<br /> <br /> I have no explanation for the Quietus thing. The challenge was he could use social skills, raw intimidation, or he could be clever and use his powers to spook them, or try to lure Andrew over to go off on the crew. Success means they leave and all is well, failure means Fortean investigators take an interest. Things got a bit more serious, though, and they won\u2019t be able to safely use the theater for some time.<br /> <br /> And more next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-19T02:39:24-08:00","id":789172,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to the Night Train Detective Agency. A new case, a new client\u2026if they can find her.<br /> <br /> Also, if the university characters are running together good news! Clytmnestra recaps who they are.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> The Changelings showed up right the hell on time. Crusher was his usual collected, genial self. Rosanna glared at Drake with slightly less fucking heat and only snarled at him every other goddamn time he spoke. The poor fucker himself only looked a little shell shocked. He returned my nod with a slight smile.<br /> <br /> The whole deal worked a lot like one of our Contracts, with more \u2018my word is my bond\u2019 bullshit and less legalese. It was a goddamn strange feeling, a reality twist with a hint of something else to it. I\u2019m sure Kilroy was fucking entranced.<br /> <br /> Once it was done, we got eyes on what the dame and the lugs 