n eyebrow and she looked away, then back. \u201cThey paid for hookers and sent them over last night. My husband didn\u2019t want to be \u2018inhospitable\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> I made a fucking sympathetic face, and glanced at my goddamn watch. \u201cWell, Esha, work calls, but... after your meeting, you wanna grab a drink? Unwind a little?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI...\u201d She paused for a moment in thought. \u201cYeah. Yeah, I do.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Billy Mack took a deep breath and dialed Langley\u2019s number at the dam. \u201cYeees...\u201d Langley channeled fucking Miss Goddamn Prissy.<br /> <br /> \u201cI hope the day is treating you well.\u201d Billy Mack acted like it was goddamn normal.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, the dam is...\u201d Langley started a drum roll on his desk. \u201c...still here.\u201d He burst into applause.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack chuckled. \u201cThat is good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d think so - I\u2019m on it!\u201d He sat back in his chair.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Langley. Did you know Cleveland Shooter has a connection to Roxanne Steele?\u201d the g-man asked.<br /> <br /> Langley put a hand to his goddamn mouth. \u201cOooh. Are they fucking? Tell me they\u2019re... no, don\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cNo fucking. Attempted murder.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh ho. Who tried to kill who?\u201d Langley pointed back and forth between two different sides of the room. \u201cC\u2019mon. Dish.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe tried to kill her. I was actually hoping you would know more. We\u2019ve been trying to track her down and ran into his cigar ash.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I know he\u2019s not the hitman type. If he were...\u201d He paused for fucking dramatic effect. \u201cI\u2019d be dead. He does work with the robots, you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cYes. He was there with one. The robot was the one who actually got shot, which is how we know something is fishy.\u201