m the tower, I believe. I got a few documents, including his calendar. Nothing out of the ordinary there, except for an off-site meeting with an employee scheduled for termination. A data extraction specialist went with him. This was the twelfth of this month.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man looked fucking thoughtful. \u201cThat is the correct date. Did it have an identifying information for the employee?\u201d<br /> <br /> Langley began typing. \u201cAn ID number. I\u2019ll send it along to you.\u201d He narrowed his eyes at the goddamn screen. \u201cI\u2019ve blocked the remote IP - they\u2019ll probably be able to get around it in 10, 15 minutes. They\u2019ve also probably called security.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps. I can try to access it remotely.\u201d Billy Mack looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s Unit 1564. The admin password is assslapper69.\u201d Billy Mack set things in motion and paused as he heard a conversation begin on Langley\u2019s side. \u201cTen minutes ago? Why, talking to my good friend Rod Hugeous.\u201d Langley was back to his fucking chucklehead vocal tone. \u201cNo, that\u2019s not the name his momma gave him, but someone did.\u201d Langley wriggled his eyebrows. He spoke into the phone. \u201cRod, tell Raymond I was talking with you, not... doing what? But the sweetums isn\u2019t there, why would I be there alone?\u201d Another pause. \u201cOh, good answer.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack waited as the phone changed hands. Another man spoke over it. \u201cYou been talking to this fuckhead?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWh - forget I asked.\u201d Raymond handed the phone back to Langley.<br /> <br /> Langley waggled his fingers at Raymond. \u201cWell I hate to break up the bonhomie, but Rod and I are having a moment.\u201d The security guard rolled his fucking eyes and left. \u201cHe\u2019s poking around still.\u201d Langley dropped the act. \u201cIf you still want to, move quick. Kisses!\u201d<br /> 