brass, flirts with everyone. Well, except creepy folks. Louise and I have gotten along, but I have not even spoken with her about Adria. She has asked me about Angela.<br /> <br /> Angela is dealing with stuff. She is inclined to do anything Naomi tells her to, but I can only keep her happy with binge watching and video games so long. I\u2019ve gone by a few times to talk to her. I\u2019d like to drop Am off awhile, but Am is a terrible liar and will give everything away. My inclination is to sneak her back into the base in the dead of night, not announcing she is back but letting her, you know, talk to more people<br /> <br /> No, I have not fucked her in the Web. Pervert.<br /> <br /> Am is not dealing great with her friend being gone. She is a natural follower, and is a bit lost without the more cocksure Angela. She has hung out with Deanna, but Deanna is also a natural follower, and one to stay in doing homework with a Korean soap opera on rather than go out. So Am has been my minion a lot past few days. She hung out while I was talking to Callie, but not with Heather, because she is afraid of her.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also been going over stuff with Cassandra. Cassandra does not know the truth about \u201cLady Covington\u201d but I am sure she suspects something. She is no fool. But she does not ask, and I do not tell. We\u2019ve taken steps to protect anyone in the Pagan group from such invasion of privacy, enough that hopefully we can sneak Angela back soon, as I say. We are discussing trying to recruit Heather. She has spies on Dr. Stein and Dr. Cross again and we have had Adria watched some but we have to be careful.<br /> <br /> After spending a few days being a bad influence to these beautiful young women, though, I needed to come back here and see a bad influence. My favorite bad influence.<br /> <br /> Mmmm hmmm<br /> <br /> I hope you have been well my love. I have very much missed you.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s good to hear. I suppose\u2026<br /> <br /> No the beds would not be as soft in Olympia as mine, would they? Lets talk about you, and these eight arms to hold you\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXII</i><br /> <br /> Jack\u2019s presence is\u2026spotty. His player had to Skype in, and the signal where he was was terrible. So he could listen and pitch in some but his connection was not stable enough to really handle a scene focusing on him. Still, points for trying.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll Have The Most Wonderful Time In My Rear\u201d and insanely dirty Oompa Loompa songs were part of my college experience. Don\u2019t you judge me.<br /> <br /> I am aware the chances of an Indian \u201csheik\u201d are remote. That\u2019s casual racism for you<br /> <br /> As always, I am terribly pleased with how I pulled off Langley. As always, that is direct dialogue from in game off the top of my head. Langley is a special boy.<br /> <br /> Langley\u2019s scene had 3 video game references. Did you notice?<br /> <br /> We should have Quietus back this session. Hope you enjoyed, as always comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-02T14:34:21-08:00","id":798399,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check back in on our Agency, as they work on various projects through the day. No Clytemnestra this time, but Speed does an excellent job of covering the session, so it is all good.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Naomi was already at the Roost, wearing a shirt that read \u2018Tell your girlfriend to stop staring, she already has my number\u2019, when Billy Mack, Jack and I arrived. I kept my hat low and my sunglasses on, since I\u2019d already activated my fucking Aura Sight and Mindreading. I took a long, mundane look around first. It wasn\u2019t crowded - the only familiar faces were Cleo, the long haired hippy chick that was a frequent diner at Kiki\u2019s, and Dr. Dawson, a creepy balding motherfucker we\u2019d seen around campus. History, or some shit.<br /> <br /> Our pink haired bitch was sitting with someone, a hell of a dame with long dark tousled hair, a well worn leather jacket and a nervous tic like she was fiddling with a gasper. When Naomi saw us walking in, she turned to her friend. \u201cWelp, my friends are here, Callie. I\u2019ll see you later.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut your friends look so interesting.\u201d Callie mock pouted and looked around goddamn conspiratorially, offering Naomi something from inside her jacket. \u201cI got Pocky...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can stay.\u201d Naomi took a stick of Pocky.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow at her as I slid into the booth. The others made conversation while I scanned the room less mundanely. I started with our new friend. There were no supernatural indicators in her aura, but her nervous tic took on more fucking significance, paired with the constant nibbling on her Pocky, lighting up as an indication of an addictive personality.<br /> <br /> Louise and the professor were both supernatural, nothing I\u2019d gotten a slant on before. They were awfully fucking similar though, both lighting up as hybrids of something, with a malleable look to it. Certainly stuck some kind of goddamn chord with me. The others kept jawing, going back and forth between English and Portuguese, while I tried for Louise\u2019s thoughts, to get a better angle on her deal.<br /> <br /> Her surface thoughts were focused on Naomi, as Louise tried to gauge what kind of person the other girl was. I started out digging for how the hell she was tied to Adria, since that was a big part of how she was tied to us. Apparently it was the fucking Politically Canadian meetings that caught her eye, as well as the brunette\u2019s good looks. The same thread of gauging what kind of person Adria was ran through her memories.<br /> <br /> It made more sense after I looked into her memories of when she first came into her supernatural heritage. She was pretty sure everything started when she was attacked by what she thought was a goddamn puma out along the river. I raised an eyebrow and said, in Portuguese, excluding Callie, \u201cEither Louise is crazier than a fucking feather duster, or she\u2019s a werecat.\u201d<br /> <br /> The others paused, briefly. Jack smiled at Callie, and glanced sideways at me. \u201cI\u2019m gonna need more details than that.\u201d I gave them to him. \u201cWerecat would make sense. They do spread via infection.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded .\u201dThey are infected themselves by a car spirit, to put it very roughly. They are, as a type of supernatural entity, inclined to protect humanity. In fact, they will go insane if they don\u2019t kill a \u2018bad person\u2019 with some regularity.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was with you until the going insane part.\u201d Jack took a sip of his beer.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe cat spirit begins to degrade the human psyche if it is not satisfied with a suitable morally degenerate kill. I imagine she is always on the lookout for someone who will satisfy her need.\u201d Billy Mack nodded, fucking approvingly.<br /> <br /> Naomi sighed, accepting Callie\u2019s offer of another goddamn Pocky stick. \u201cThere are far too many punishment oriented creatures on campus. As a bad girl, I don\u2019t like it. They don\u2019t even punish with spankings.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled at her. \u201cPerhaps you should be careful what you get up to...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m a good person!\u201d Naomi interrupted him.<br /> <br /> Jack raised an eyebrow and I chuckled. \u201cFucking listen to yourself much?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled slightly. \u201cBefore we get too far off subject, werecats are very difficult to take down. Nine lives and all. We should avoid getting on her bad side.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOK, I won\u2019t talk.\u201d Jack held his goddamn hands up. \u201cI can take a hint.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a fucking awkward pause until Naomi sighed. \u201cAm really took the edge off.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack leaned back and looked at her goddamn dubiously. \u201cIs she OK?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHaloed.\u201d Naomi shrugged. \u201cAnd she gets better quick.\u201d<br /> <br /> Louise came by to take our orders. I got a burger, Billy Mack his goddamn apple pie. Jack played up asking for the special. When she got to Naomi, she had a resigned look on her face. \u201cWhat about you, Naomi?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked back. \u201cThe usual. You\u2019re looking good.\u201d<br /> <br /> The blonde girl rolled her eyes and didn\u2019t respond. \u201cCallie?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGot Pocky.\u201d Callie grinned and held up her fucking box of the shit. Louise smiled and headed off. Callie leaned in. \u201cDo you think Louise is a giant flirt?\u201d She looked between us. \u201cI mean, you are detectives, unless Naomi\u2019s been lying about what she does for a living.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI...\u201d Naomi lifted a goddamn finger, \u201cdo this to make extra money. I don\u2019t do anything for a living - I\u2019m an artist.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cAnd I think Louise is acting like a fucking waitress.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cThat knows how to get tips.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAdria\u2019s been spending a lot less time with Callie and more with Louise,\u201d Naomi explained in Portuguese. \u201cThey\u2019re both pretty sure Adria is straight, they just enjoy spending time with her.\u201d She rolled her eyes. \u201cThey\u2019ve both promised me Deanna hadn\u2019t possibly slept with Adria.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let them go back to chinning and scanned Dr. Dawson. I chuckled at the shit I heard in his surface thoughts, and waved the others off. He pegged Naomi for a damn troublemaker and didn\u2019t approve of her bringing adult friends to a fucking college hangout. Thankfully, it was mild annoyance and only vague recognition, so I let it lie.<br /> <br /> Louise came back fairly quickly with our food and passed it out. She smirked at Naomi. \u201cYour shirt doesn\u2019t apply to me, I don\u2019t have one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA pretty girl like you should find one,\u201d Naomi shot right the hell back.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re making assumptions.\u201d Louise put a hand on her hip.<br /> <br /> Naomi shrugged. \u201cI\u2019m usually right.\u201d<br /> <br /> Louise smiled and left with our empty glasses. Callie gave Naomi a goddman look. \u201cSome girls might like it better if you weren\u2019t so cocky.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I find one like that, I\u2019ll let you know.\u201d Naomi pointed at her with a fry, then ate it. Jack sighed heavily.<br /> <br /> Callie rolled her eyes. \u201cSo what are you doing tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi smiled at her. \u201cYou maybe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah.\u201d Callie finished off her fucking Pocky.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll hang out with Heather maybe then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Callie crinkled her nose. \u201cWhy? Even Adria doesn\u2019t like her, there must be something wrong with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi made a face back. \u201cAdria doesn\u2019t like me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCase in point! For one, you just assume I want to have sex with you.\u201d Callie crossed her arms<br /> <br /> \u201cYou do!\u201d<br /> <br /> The brunette rolled her eyes and left, flipping Naomi off. At the door she paused and yelled back. \u201cLove ya, Naomi.\u201d<br /> <br /> Louise came by the table to take up our checks. \u201cSo, you, me, some quality time?\u201d Naomi leaned back in her fucking seat.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have plans.\u201d Louise smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not a no.\u201d Naomi grinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s never a no.\u201d The blonde waitress winked at her and smiled at the rest of us.<br /> <br /> I glanced at my watch and tossed a couple of bills down for a tip. \u201cI\u2019ve got a goddamn thing. You three, don\u2019t do anything I wouldn\u2019t fucking do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not.\u201d Billy Mack nodded. \u201cJack, I could use your assistance on my Cipher. I believe you know what to do to unlock yours, as well. I could assist in turn if you needed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d Jack shrugged and the three of them headed out as well.<br /> <br /> Naomi glanced back as Jack held the door. She winked at him and nudged Billy Mack. \u201cYou seem to have piqued our catgirl\u2019s interest. She was keeping an eye on you.\u201d<br /> <br /> He raised a goddamn eyebrow. \u201cIt\u2019s too bad we can\u2019t let her know it couldn\u2019t help stave off the madness to kill us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would be nice if we could point her at bad people, you know, a guilt free way of doing a Michael White.\u201d Jack scanned the streets.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am not doing Michael White,\u201d Naomi deliberately fucking misheard.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cYou\u2019d never be able to wash the scent of bridge building off. It might be contagious.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I got to the bar a little early and ordered a goddamn whiskey sour. I popped my Aura Sight and leaned back, elbows against the bar. I didn\u2019t get much on Esha as she walked into the fucking place, but I was able to confirm she wasn\u2019t supernatural. I switched off my Sight and looked at her over my sunglasses. \u201cHey you,\u201d she greeted me, smiling. She sat on the stool next to me and ordered a beer.<br /> <br /> I turned on my stool to face her and stashed my goddamn glasses in my fucking jacket. \u201cHey doll.\u201d I sipped my drink and she followed suit. \u201cHow was the Thai?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was delicious.\u201d She smiled shyly.<br /> <br /> \u201cGlad to hear it.\u201d I smirked at her. \u201cYour, uh, business meeting go well too?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded absently, taking a goddamn long fortifying sip. \u201cYes. Apparently these investors had a hand in starting Blue Sun to begin with. They are hoping to expand into this area, calling it Phase 2.\u201d She put a hand on the back of my fucking chair.<br /> <br /> I leaned towards her slightly. \u201cIs that right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt means I\u2019ll probably be in town a few more times.\u201d She paused and bit her lip before reaching to stroke my cheek. \u201cIt will be nice to have... friends in the area.\u201d<br /> <br /> Things moved goddamn quickly once she got her nerve up. After another drink or two she was grabbing my fucking hand and pulling me out the door. We stumbled and laughed our way to a different hotel, my arm around her waist.<br /> <br /> When we got into our room, I pushed her against the wall and kissed her, hard. She pushed me away, laughing, and put a hand on my goddamn collar and a finger against my lips. \u201cWait.\u201d She grinned and slipped out from under my arms, pulling out her fucking cell phone. \u201cHello Girik. I\u2019m afraid I can\u2019t come home tonight.\u201d She giggled. \u201cI\u2019m a little drunk.\u201d She paused a moment. \u201cNo, I\u2019m staying with a friend.\u201d<br /> <br /> I came up behind her and put my arms around her waist. I was close enough to hear his fucking disbelieving \u201cWhat friend?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA friend I\u2019m going to fuck.\u201d She hung up and turned around in my arms, linking hers behind my head.<br /> <br /> <br /> Once she fell asleep, I stood up to stretch while I turned on my Mind Reading. I sat at the goddamn table and poured myself a fucking drink, walking a coin over my knuckles as I rummaged through her memories.<br /> <br /> The pertinent one was fuzzy, and in goddamn layers. The opening of the meeting was easy enough to find as she and a dozen other VIPs were led into a room at the conference center, decorated in blue, with the Blue Sun logo on the carpet and ceiling. That memory was followed by an innocuous, boring as shit meeting. Another layer down, hidden beneath some kind of supernatural repression, I saw the real fucking meeting.<br /> <br /> The thirteen Blue Sun VIPs were introduced to the five investors, a white woman and man on each side of an Indian man with fucking glowing blue eyes and blue circuitry tattoos. He spoke with a goddamn reverberating voice. \u201cPhase 1 has progressed well. You have been chosen, and will be scanned to determine whether your psyche is sufficiently strong to weather the difficulties of Phase 2.\u201d<br /> <br /> A blue laser came from the glowing eyes and hit each one in turn. Each one screamed in a hell of a lot of pain as they were hit and only four, including Esha, managed to stay conscious. \u201cYour strength and expertise will be very valuable. You will return to the US for portions of your training as preparations are made. You are not to tell anyone of Phase 2.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe will not tell anyone of Phase 2.\u201d Their response was creepy as shit, monotone and in unison.<br /> <br /> The rest of the meeting matched in both memories. Dr. Manhattan\u2019s eyes stopped glowing and his voice took on a more normal tone. \u201cWe\u2019ll meet again tomorrow. Enjoy your evenings.\u201d<br /> <br /> I ran my finger over my coin in circles, tracing the lines in the wallpaper with my eyes. This was some messed up shit, and not small fucking potatoes either. I smirked at the sleeping woman on the bed. So much for my plans to sneak the hell away before morning.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Naomi had left Billy Mack and Jack to their own goddamn devices. \u201cSo... what\u2019s the project you need my \u2018assistance\u2019 with?\u201d Jack asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy next Interlock is tied to the Embed identity Theft. It leaves my target listless, but possibly wandering and if they come to harm, there are serious consequences. I thought backup would be useful.\u201d Billy Mack began walking towards campus.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing. You have a target in mind?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cI can\u2019t use it on Mr Morris, thanks to his supernatural abilities. But I have a plan, and more information about him would be useful. The kind of information a faculty member would have access to.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI gotcha.\u201d They pair looked for a classroom building with its fucking lights on. Billy Mack walked brazenly down the sidewalk, peering at each building. Jack scanned the area, giving the g-man annoyed and disbelieving looks. \u201cWould -\u201d Billy Mack turned to look at him. \u201cWould you be less goddamn conspicuous?\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> The biology department was the first they found that had a fucking light on in an office, one belonging to a grad student. A handshake got Billy Mack the poor bastard\u2019s identity and he immediately sat down at the computer. He closed the Google Image Search of \u2018alligator attacks\u2019 and brought up the school intranet. He managed to get Andrew\u2019s dorm and room number, his roommate\u2019s name - Levi - as well as both of their class schedules. After a moment\u2019s thought, he got Nathan\u2019s information as well.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked towards Jack and indicated the exit with a jerk of his goddamn head. As soon as they\u2019d left the office and shut the door on the fucking drooling grad student, Billy Mack let go of the identity. \u201cSo, is there anything I can do to help you? If not, I believe I will pay Ms Waters a visit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smirked at him. \u201cI\u2019m starting to feel left out. I should find someone to bang.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cGirlfriends are good stress relief. I\u2019m thinking about setting Ms Waters up with a chemistry degree.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that what they\u2019re calling it these days?\u201d The fixer smiled.<br /> <br /> The g-man raised an eyebrow. \u201cI\u2019m just looking for the best way to approach her, as I don\u2019t want to scare her off. But it won\u2019t be tonight, so if you need anything...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, I\u2019m just gonna help a bum get a trash fire started.\u201d He clapped Billy Mack on the shoulder. Neither of them noticed the goddamn large cat lurking in the fucking shadows behind them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Esha was smiling at me the next morning when I woke up. I smirked at her and pushed myself up to a sitting position to watch her get dressed. She did so fucking briskly and efficiently, pausing occasionally to smile over at me. \u201cWell, I believe I have some damage control to do.\u201d She pulled her hair back. \u201cI\u2019d like to see you again, before I go. I had a great time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing doll.\u201d I stood and stretched, then shrugged into my goddamn shirt.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think it could be best if I called you. My husband...\u201d She trailed off, watching me.<br /> <br /> I pulled her close. \u201cOh. Yeah. The fucking pig.\u201d<br /> <br /> She laughed and gave me a quick goddamn kiss. \u201cI have to go. There\u2019s a meeting this afternoon, and the pig. I had a great time Gabe. I\u2019ll be in touch.\u201d<br /> <br /> I winked at her and grabbed my hat. \u201cYou better.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> When I got to the office, only Jack was there. I stole one of Cecelia\u2019s pens as I walked by her fucking desk and spun it in my fingers. \u201cSo where\u2019s the g-\u201d I stopped when my phone started ringing. I answered it. \u201cHey Naomi.\u201d I pulled out Jack\u2019s spare chair and put the phone on speaker.<br /> <br /> \u201cGot Vivian on the phone too. Anything exciting going on?\u201d Naomi leaned against her kitchen counter.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have both Mr Morris and Mr Klein\u2019s room assignment and class schedule.\u201d Vivian spoke in Japanese. \u201cOtherwise, my evening was relatively uneventful.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi finished off her goddamn coffee. \u201cLouise canceled plans with Callie and Adria, abruptly. That\u2019s the only thing that went on here, other than Am being too good for her own good.\u201d<br /> <br /> I snorted. \u201cNo shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes. \u201cSo stop eating her?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t last night. Not in a bad way.\u201d Naomi smirked. Jack sighed. \u201cHey, she deserved it after being such a good aperitif.\u201d<br /> <br /> I ran my fingers through my hair. \u201cSo, the good fucking news is Esha passed the goddamn pop quiz. The bad news is it was a fucking Angel who gave it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi tapped her fingers on the counter. \u201cThat doesn\u2019t sound good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt certainly sounds disconcerting.\u201d Vivian agreed. I filled them in on the goddamn details of the meeting at the conference center. \u201cVery disconcerting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you think the God Machine is planning on opening a new facility here?\u201d Naomi mused.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cOr Phase 3 is back the hell in India and this is just fucking training or some shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked over at me. \u201cWere they checking if Esha and the others were stigmatics?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSeeing if they had the grit to become stigmatics most likely.\u201d I started tossing and catching the goddamn pen.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is all assuming it\u2019s as God Machine as it sounds like,\u201d Naomi pointed out.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cIf it\u2019s not, I\u2019ll eat my goddamn hat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe need to keep tabs on this.\u201d Vivian smiled over at Shelley and mouthed \u2018family\u2019 before rolling her eyes.<br /> <br /> I rolled my shoulders. \u201cI\u2019ll see her sometime in the next few goddamn days, and the next meeting is this fucking afternoon.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi frowned briefly. \u201cWe could check out the meeting room. The Convention Center is a public area, shouldn\u2019t be hard to get into.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s some weird fucking decorating for a Convention Center meeting room.\u201d I stood up and leaned against the wall.<br /> <br /> Vivian tapped her lips. \u201cInfrastructure?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi nodded. \u201cEither there, or they set up some kind of temporary portal. The Infrastructure wouldn\u2019t be public, but we could detect it, or the portal.\u201d She sighed. \u201cWe don\u2019t want to forget Steele though. We gonna check out Brand Corporation?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIn unlocking my Cipher, I have acquired new abilities to fit in and bypass security, though not human or sentient elements,\u201d Vivian offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can deal with those \u2018elements\u2019.\u201d Jack put his fucking feet on his desk. \u201cIt won\u2019t be quiet.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my goddamn eyes at him. \u201cI think we need fucking quiet with this shit.\u201d He shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe, I would like to know what Mr Paulson might know about the security there.\u201d Vivian smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing doll. I\u2019ll give him a fucking call. Lunch?\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi shrugged. \u201cI can come along as Liz.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cThat would be nice, for the purposes of speaking freely. Kiki\u2019s?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKiki\u2019s it is.\u201d I picked up my phone. \u201cLet\u2019s say one, unless I call again to change it.\u201d I smirked at Jack and headed to my goddamn office.<br /> <br /> <br /> Drake was free and happy to help. He chuckled when I suggested Kiki\u2019s but agreed to meet at one. I killed time cleaning my goddamn gun, until my phone rang. I smiled to hear Miranda\u2019s ringtone, but after just a moment, my smile fucking disappeared.<br /> <br /> Fuck. Shit. I fucked up. And I\u2019d fucked up bad. No excuse either, I\u2019d just fallen into old habits, from times before I got dizzy, before I had someone that meant something. It was an old tactic, one I\u2019d used before I had partners to guide the conversation while I picked through someone\u2019s memories. But fuck, that didn\u2019t make it OK.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t let on anything then. She was cheerful, and tired, but wrapping up the few last loose ends. I listened, teased her about getting some sun and told her I loved her. If I told her - when I told her - it would be after we dealt with the Asbury Room. It would distract her and she needed everything she had for whatever she needed to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> I paused just inside the door at Kiki\u2019s, scanning the room and letting my eyes get used to the dim light. My first sweep caught Carla Pierce and Erwin Holt, speaking quietly at a fucking table in the corner. I got myself lost in the goddamn crowd before she saw me and started getting paranoid again.<br /> <br /> Adria and Louise were there again. I passed by their table on the way to the one Drake sat at and heard them discussing Billy Mack. It sounded like they were comparing notes on where they\u2019d seen him and how he was connected to campus.<br /> <br /> When we got to the table, I activated my Aura Sight and looked Adria over. She wasn\u2019t supernatural, but there were subtle signs of a fucking supernatural influence on her. Ironic, considering how goddamn focused she was on having control. But her vague desire to harm Naomi made it more disturbing.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave her a goddamn hard look too, but quickly focused on Drake as he said \u201cHey guys, how are you doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man sat down. \u201cFairly well. You?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, the other Changelings decided not to Old Yeller me. Gabe said you needed something to do with Brand?\u201d Drake smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. Are you familiar with Roxanne Steele?\u201d Billy Mack asked after accepting his goddamn usual from the waitress.<br /> <br /> Drake looked fucking confused at the apparent change in topic. \u201cYeah, jumped a big bail. She has info the Harvestman wants.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cWe received information that she had a meeting with an unknown subjects, and afterwards was trailed by NSA agents. Those agents were trailed by a woman you\u2019ve had the pleasure of meeting, courtesy of White.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake sighed. \u201cSo White wants the thumb drive too. Or she does, independently. Either way, Roxanne is in danger.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re also considered the possibility that Ms Steele was meeting with Mr White\u2019s associate. We would like to try to find out what his angle is.\u201d Billy Mack scanned the goddamn room.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Brand is the best place for that, their employee records specifically. Each of their front companies have listed \u2018representatives\u2019 - that is, the people working directly for White. You\u2019ll need to look for a representative not associated with any other companies. That\u2019s gonna take time. You can\u2019t make any copies to search at your leisure either - it requires a password and probably sends a signal back.\u201d Drake looked between us. He began to sketch out the layout on the fucking table. \u201cIt\u2019s a closed system, but the front door is not super well secured - I just hung around until someone held the door open for me. Inside, there\u2019s a 50/50 chance that any given office will have a computer logged in already. You might need tier 2 level access though, for her. That won\u2019t be left logged in.\u201d He took a goddamn deep breath. \u201cI might know more, be able to find what you need quicker.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cI had no intention of asking you, since you are not involved.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Changeling shrugged. \u201cI owe you a lot. It does make things more risky for you, but it\u2019s your call. If I\u2019m seen, we\u2019ll likely have to shoot our way out - you could probably get away disguising yourselves as temps. They\u2019ll only notice you if you\u2019ve got an AK-47 or if you\u2019re on a list. I\u2019m on a list.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is also more risky for you. We didn\u2019t get you back in order to involve you in unnecessary risk. And we do want to keep a low profile - you and us.\u201d The g-man clapped him on the shoulder.<br /> <br /> Drake smiled wryly. \u201cTrue. White doesn\u2019t know I\u2019m back, or he would be taunting me. Too bad they can\u2019t see me the way I am now, they wouldn\u2019t recognize me then. They might ask me if I\u2019ve lost Wallace.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked at him. \u201cYou\u2019ve helped fucking plenty already.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am glad to see you are taking you change of circumstance well.\u201d Billy Mack nodded approvingly.<br /> <br /> \u201cLife is all about how you take it.\u201d The bounty hunter shrugged. \u201cLook, the Harvestman said the supernatural was involved here, and not our type. Is it White\u2019s \u2018type\u2019? Is Roxanne the same deal? Not that I\u2019ve asked the Harvestman what that is.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe do think it is tied to what Mr White is, yes. But she is a case of someone who saw a little too much, which put her in the position she\u2019s in. He is a dangerous man, a manipulator. We don\u2019t know whose side he\u2019s taking, or what he\u2019s getting out of it.\u201d Billy Mack frowned. \u201cAt some point, Mr White will need to be dealt with.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake made a fist. \u201cI\u2019m gonna go all Cujo on his ass.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a fucking drink. \u201cI\u2019ll hold him the hell down.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry we haven\u2019t been more forthcoming.\u201d Billy Mack watched Adria and Louise leave. \u201cIf we\u2019d told you about Mr Creel and Ms Rosanna, you wouldn\u2019t have believed us.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake shrugged. \u201cThere are people who don\u2019t tell you things that you wish you\u2019d shot and people who have their reasons.\u201d He smiled. \u201cAnd if you told me I\u2019d be Clifford\u2019s smaller, more bipedal cousin, there\u2019s no way in hell I would have listened.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled back. \u201cIf you become more involved in this kind of thing, we\u2019ll tell you what you need to know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d Drake took a sip of his beer. \u201cOne thing - if it turns out to be fucking chemtrails, don\u2019t tell me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cIf it\u2019s goddamn chemtrails, you\u2019ll hear all the fuck about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake rolled his eyes. \u201cOh I have.\u201d He looked around. \u201cAnything else I can help with?\u201d We shook our heads. He stood to go. \u201cThanks for the drink.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack watched him leave. \u201cThat is a remarkably noble and heroic man.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m goddamn shocked he hasn\u2019t gotten himself fucking killed yet.\u201d I signaled the waitress for another drink.<br /> <br /> \u201cHopefully we\u2019ll be able to keep him from doing that in the future, at least in this matter. No force will convince him to leave this alone, we will need to tell him.\u201d Billy Mack looked goddamn thoughtful.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot everything, I hope.\u201d Liz raised an eyebrow. \u201cHe has seen things, but...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cHe has handled what he has seen well so far. Hopefully he can handle the truth.\u201d<br /> <br /> I glanced around. \u201cSpeaking of handling - you\u2019re gonna wanna be fucking careful handling Adria.\u201d I explained what I had picked up from Adria\u2019s goddamn aura.<br /> <br /> \u201cI see. The avenues of leverage I was able to pick up on mesh interestingly. She fears being ignored, and losing her place on the Dean\u2019s list. Also a man from her past, Alvin Lang - he assaulted her, I believe. She wants Naomi to fall in love with her and in the long term, to become a power broker in national and eventually international politics.\u201d Billy Mack chuckled. \u201cNo small dreams. She is also both intrigued by and afraid of Ms Davidson. I believe Ms Watson is somewhat aware of her supernatural nature.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m shocked she\u2019s not supernatural, considering everyone\u2019s in love with her and no one\u2019s jealous.\u201d Liz smirked.<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded seriously. \u201cI\u2019m impressed she\u2019s smart enough to realize where the real power in politics lies.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz nodded back. \u201cIf she\u2019s being controlled, it might be time to move more proactively.\u201d She held out her fucking cigarette holder for me to light. \u201cI don\u2019t think Louise is the one controlling her, but she might have an idea who is. And the controller may or may not have been the one to sic her on the Pagan Club. I was thinking that was Louise.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would be nice to ascertain her intentions with confidence.\u201d Billy Mack finished his goddamn drink.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s put up way more resistance to Naomi than most. Naomi might have to make the first move this time. Or maybe start a shouting match, get emotions running high...\u201d She trailed off in thought.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shrugged. \u201cThe problem might be that she wants Naomi for a minion.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz sighed. \u201cOption B is to pretend to fall for her, like she wants.\u201d She made a hell of a face. \u201cI don\u2019t like even pretending to be beholden to anyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou could go for the other leverage, support her Politically Canadian thing more actively. Maybe even pact her a cult?\u201d Jack suggested.<br /> <br /> \u201cI plan on making a pact with her eventually, though I was hoping to Spider God it.\u201d Liz blew out a fucking cloud of smoke.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow. \u201cI recommend waiting on the reveal until we know who is controlling her. It could be the same person who sent Mr Morris, even if it were Ms Davidson who sent Ms Watson.\u201d<br /> <br /> The dame shrugged. \u201cUltimately, the addictive nature of my personality will mean she does what I want.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf the softer touch fails, certainly.\u201d Billy Mack inclined his head. \u201cI have a plan, speaking of Mr Morris. It requires Ms Bale\u2019s assistance. I will possess Mr Klein and have him call his friend, informing him that I had eyes on Ms Bale and her cult about to perform a ritual. When he arrived, presumably having acquired adult assistance, they would find Mr Klein and Ms Bale making out. He is a problem that need dealing with. His death would draw too much attention...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut crying wolf... good plan.\u201d Jack leaned back.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhile we\u2019re on the topic - I need to let Angela out, to get her some human contact. I\u2019ve brought Am by, but... I was thinking we could smuggle her out.\u201d Liz looked concerned.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked at me. \u201cThe God Machine\u2019s presence is down, we should be able to deal with the Room soon. If Ms Asbury is ready?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cAs ready as she\u2019ll ever be. Tomorrow night? Since tonight we\u2019re dealing with the Brand fuckers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat works. I was gonna ask for a 24 hour warning, and that\u2019s about 36. Plenty of time to let the Pagan Club handle some preparations.\u201d Liz let out a deep breath. \u201cAnd I'm obligated to tell Kayla.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat sounds like a good plan,\u201d Billy Mack agreed. \u201cThe thing with Brand will probably take more than one night. I\u2019ll work on a back door.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure fucking thing pal. You work on that goddamn back door.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIII</i><br /> <br /> If you forgot who Louise is, she was with Adria in Kiki\u2019s talking about supernatural stuff, and showed up in the whole Angela madness.<br /> <br /> By Werecat, we are talking about The Colony, from <u>War Against the Pure</u>. The Colony are really awesome and I can\u2019t wait to see them in 2e. If you follow <i>Balance of Shadows</i>, Noriko is a member of the Colony. She is not the only weird thing in <i>Balance of Shadows</i> also running around Seattle, either. Billy Mack\u2019s description is sorta right, sorta wrong, but hits the major points, assuming you consider Uratha to have a wolf spirit. Same deal. She has to kill one bad person per month or she begins going mad.<br /> <br /> Before any artists start getting upset about the \u201cdon\u2019t do anything for a living\u201d remark remember Naomi is a jerk.<br /> <br /> During the scene with Jack and Billy Mack, they were being stalked by Louise. They knew this Out of Character, but were not near the requirements to actually beat her stealth roll. I let them know this OOC for a couple reasons, but mostly with an ambush she could easily one shot either of them, and it seemed a bit unfair to haven someone lose a character like that if they were feeling capricious IC. Not that I expected anything on that level, but I\u2019ve given up predicting anything about what Quietus would do. Louise has also stalked Naomi in the past.<br /> <br /> Erwin Holt was the man representing Erasmus, who the PCs suspect is a recently awoken Vampire or a Mummy. He is also from Carla\u2019s past, and Carla is the personal assistant for Sanderson, who was getting the statues session one. Clear?<br /> <br /> Anything else you need reminders on? NPCs who would help if they were pictured?<br /> <br /> Let me know. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T19:39:07-08:00","id":800047,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the recap on the names - they are starting to get confusing. I almost wish each was hyper-linked to a character sheet or note page just for keeping track of who is who and where they've been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T23:19:00-08:00","id":800304,"title":"","content":"I am trying to think of the best way to get the names across in these APs.<br /> <br /> In game, they are not an issue because there are pictures set out on the table with names on it every time they come up. So whether you are good with names or faces, it is easy to link the characters. Now sometimes NPCs one has not seen in some time take some reminding, Erwin Holt for example, but in general this works VERY well for keeping even long lists of names straight.<br /> <br /> Online, there are issues. Some pictures are used with permission of the subject or photographer. But most of the time, it is that uploading, naming, and linking the picture is a LOT of work, and when they fall 10 pages back anyway, not as much use. And constant linking seems a lot of work.<br /> <br /> I am open to suggestions. I want to make these APs as enjoyable for my audience as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T05:31:37-08:00","id":800527,"title":"","content":"Yeah, linking would definitely be a post-write-up treatment (Find and Replace might be enough, if editing the markup directly). No idea what they'd link <i>to</i>, though (bio page? on going NPC notes? &lt;shrug&gt;).<br /> <br /> Maybe if you were turning these into annotated PDFs once they are wrapped up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T23:50:36-08:00","id":801192,"title":"","content":"Yea a big resource with all the NPCs would be awesome, but a lot of work to build and some work to maintain. Writing journals and formatting/commenting on sessions eats a lot of time as is. That's the big problem :-/<br /> <br /> Short term people asking for clarification is what I rely on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T13:52:22-08:00","id":810346,"title":"","content":"Time to investigate the Brand Corporation. Kick over a rock, and plotlines come running out. Clytemnestra\u2019s info basically covers two sessions.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> There were still a few hours in the work day, so we decided to use Drake\u2019s ploy to get our peepers on the place. Liz had changed out of drop fucking dead sexy into business casual and when she stopped at the door and started ruffling through her purse with the slightest frown, the security guard only needed a few goddamn seconds of a \u2018help me\u2019 look to open the door for us. She paused to thank him, giving Jack and Billy Mack time to walk up casually.<br /> <br /> We scattered once we were inside. Liz looked at her wristwatch as she walked. She paused briefly at the elevators, then moved on to the stairs, as if it was taking too fucking long. Billy Mack glanced at the floor key, then he and Jack moved to the east elevators to wait.<br /> <br /> I lingered, my eye on a new opportunity. Erwin Holt was standing at the front desk. \u201cTell Mrs. Scoggins I am here to see her.\u201d The secretary\u2019s voice was quiet, just that side of too goddamn low to hear. \u201cI do not have an appointment, but she will see me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I moved closer to hear the secretary. \u201cThat\u2019s not how...\u201d He paused, looking at his computer then back at the arrogant fuck. \u201cVery well sir. Her office is on the 38th floor, as I believe you know.\u201d<br /> <br /> Holt smiled smugly and moved to the west elevators. I glanced at the key as I followed, but it didn't have a goddamn entry for the 38th floor. I let him take the first fucking elevator alone and took the next.<br /> <br /> There were no raised eyebrows among my fellow passengers when I asked for 38. I was the only one who got off there and the hallway was empty. It was a goddamn classy fucking hallway though. A fucking aquarium ran down the entire length of the hallway, full of lion fish or some shit like that. Quiet classical music played gently in the background.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t see any sign of Holt, so I shrugged and went right. I found an office for an M. Fagin and an L. Dulcimer but then the hallway ended at a fucking water cooler. Left from the elevator was more fruitful. I passed by a W. Wilkinson but then managed to find T. Scoggins\u2019 office. I risked a look in the window and saw Holt putting on airs like a fucking billionaire\u2019s favorite daughter, berating another secretary. She looked less than goddamn amused, but eventually the inner door opened and Holt went in.<br /> <br /> I waited until the door shut again and went in myself. \u201cHello Ms...\u201d I checked the nameplate. \u201cCox. I\u2019m from security. I understand a Mr. Holt was here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUh, yeah.\u201d She looked at me goddamn dubiously. \u201cYou don\u2019t look familiar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m new. Plainclothes, you know.\u201d I smiled hopefully. \u201cI wasn\u2019t told to confront him, and if he\u2019s in a meeting... I\u2019ll stay and make sure you don\u2019t have any problems though. Who is this fucking guy?\u201d I tweaked reality to get her fucking talking.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cErwin Holt is a dick who\u2019s going to catch a bullet someday. He works for a Mr. Erasmus. Well, I think it\u2019s Mr. Erasmus. He just calls him Erasmus.\u201d<br /> <br /> I crossed my arms. \u201cWhat\u2019s he bothering Mrs. Scoggins about?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s an import, one of Mrs. Scoggins\u2019 special imports, that she\u2019s acquired for Mr. Sanderson. Mr. Holt says Erasmus wants it. Not that he\u2019s willing to pay more, or anything.\u201d She sneered at the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s ballsy. Gotta be a special doohickey, huh? I mean, Mr. Sanderson\u2019s kinda a big shot, right?\u201d What the goddamn fuck had I wandered into?<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cI don\u2019t know anything about the, um, doohickey, other than it\u2019s from Nepal, cause that jackass said so. Mr. Sanderson is a regular client.\u201d She paused. \u201cHe\u2019s had shipments go astray before - he had a shipment hijacked at a train station, back in late September. Come to think of it, that\u2019s when Mr. Holt first started showing up.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled to myself, but knit my brow at her. \u201cWhy does he think he can get away with this?\u201d<br /> <br /> She frowned. \u201cWhen we don\u2019t do what Mr. Holt asks, seconds after he leaves the building we lose contact with one of our elite teams. The next time he shows up, he gloats about it.\u201d She glared goddamn daggers at the inner door. \u201cHe\u2019s gonna get himself killed one of these days.\u201d She looked back at me. \u201cHe spent his entire time waiting in here last visit deciding whether I was worth having sex with. He decided I wasn\u2019t but Mrs. Scoggins had his permission to ask.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHell, I\u2019ll go toss him a slug right now.\u201d Shit, I\u2019d wanted to help him get Carla away from Sanderson. But now... fuck that guy sideways and hard.<br /> <br /> She smiled. \u201cNo, I think you\u2019ll have to get in line. But Mr. Erasmus is almost certainly the real power. If he kills a whole team because we told Mr. Holt no, we don\u2019t know what Mr. Erasmus will do if we kill him.\u201d<br /> <br /> I blew my hair out of my eyes. \u201cAlright...\u201d<br /> <br /> I was interrupted by Holt\u2019s raised voice, speaking right the fuck over Mrs. Scoggins. \u201cHow is Dakota enjoying Wayside Elementary?\u201d There was a pause. \u201cThat wasn\u2019t a threat. I\u2019ve never threatened any of you, I was just offering condolences.\u201d Another pause. Mrs. Scoggins kept her voice lower. He still kept speaking loudly over her. \u201cI was on your security cameras, I will remind you. I am personally offended...\u201d She managed to convince him to quiet down.<br /> <br /> Ms. Cox sighed and opened a drawer. She pulled out a fucking Glock, checked it over and put it back. I raised an eyebrow. \u201cSo, other than the douchebags... how is this place to work at?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s good. Well, here in Imports. The bosses are great. More shootouts than I expected though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShootouts? Like, in here?\u201d I looked around.<br /> <br /> She jerked her chin towards the outside door. \u201cIn the hallway. We had a problem with the shipment of one of our clients, a cult leader called Frater Pietr. He brought in a pair of bruisers in black robes with black daggers, so the Uzis surprised us.\u201d She shook her head. \u201cHe managed to disappear and calls us up occasionally, trying to get us to honor his contract. Apparently there was nothing in it about bringing holy thugs to the building.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled at her. This was way more goddamn exciting than I figured \u2018Imports\u2019 would be. I guess if you are importing for fucking supervillains... \u201cExciting customers then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t know the half of it. Most of them are less unpleasant - I\u2019m not sure Frater Pietr is so good at bathing. Mrs. X is the worst though.\u201d She shuddered.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t fucking wait. \u201cOh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. She doesn\u2019t talk, just writes stuff on a little chalkboard tablet thing. Her face never moves. Her last shipment moaned. Like, a person. But the box was roughly toaster sized.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked over at the inner door as Holt raised his voice again. \u201c...I\u2019m reconsidering giving you the option to have sex with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes and shook her head. \u201cMrs. X was agitated last time she was here. By which I mean her skin was, like something was crawling underneath it. Mrs. Scoggins left right after her meeting and said I could go home too. It was 10 AM. You know, when I was a kid, worried about something in my closet, I didn\u2019t picture her, but I bet that\u2019s what was there.\u201d I had a nervous look on my face. She smiled encouragingly. \u201cDon\u2019t let me scare you, other than the weirdos, it\u2019s a nice place to work.\u201d<br /> <br /> We stopped talking as the inner door opened. Holt came through, speaking back over his fucking shoulder. \u201cTalk to your bosses, see how they feel about things. You\u2019re pretty, I\u2019m sure you can work something out.\u201d My left hand wandered towards my wrist where my goddamn rivet gun usually manifests. He nodded at the secretary. \u201cWoman.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mrs. Scoggins followed him to the door and watched him leave, glaring. When he was gone, she sighed. \u201cNo calls or meetings for a few minutes please, Ms. Cox. I need to drink something.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course Mrs. Scoggins.\u201d Ms. Cox smiled apologetically at me and started typing something into her computer.<br /> <br /> I smiled understandingly and nodded. A glance out the door showed that the fucker was long gone, so I left too. Liz was fixing her makeup in the lobby, lit cigarette resting against her compact. She found a bench under the No Smoking sign, of fucking course. I sauntered over. \u201cHey doll. You ready to go?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled serenely up at me. \u201cI am. It doesn\u2019t do to keep our boys waiting.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Billy Mack and Jack had gone straight to the 11th floor. Jack took a seat in the lobby, keeping an eye on the other patrons. A lot of suits, with one guy in a polo, fucking reeking of pot, playing Plants versus Goddamn Zombies on his phone. Jack\u2019s eyes kept straying that way, but he didn\u2019t do shit about it.<br /> <br /> The g-man made a bee-line for the cubicles labelled \u2018New Investors\u2019. He found a computer setup there to take the new clients\u2019 information. The UI was goddamn basic, just a form, but Billy Mack managed to hack the hell around it and get to a terminal. An ASCII banner read \u2018Brand Corporation: Making a Better Future Inevitable\u2019. Underneath it was an alert: \u2018Security is not to approach Erwin Holt. The emergency buttons should be used if he proves to be a serious nuisance.\u2019<br /> <br /> The file system was basic. The upper level had five folders: \u2018Banking - Mrs Everway\u2019, \u2018Loans - Mr Tate\u2019, \u2018Imports - Mrs Winters\u2019, \u2018Security - Mr Holiday\u2019 and \u2018???? - Mr Innis\u2019. Billy Mack\u2019s eyes narrowed as he read the first initials and mentally rearranged them to WHITE. That did prove to be the only direct connection to the bridge building motherfucker he found.<br /> <br /> He started with Mr. Innis\u2019 folder. The only file in it was a text document named Contacts. Opening it, he found a list of names and phone numbers. Billy Mack scanned the list, committing it to memory, and two names stood out. C. S. Shooter and J. H. Sanderson. Shooter\u2019s listed number was the one we had for him.<br /> <br /> Just as Billy Mack came to the end of the list, a message began typing itself at the goddamn prompt. \u201cWhat are you looking for?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack typed back. \u201cRoxanne Steele.\u201d<br /> <br /> A series of commands were typed and executed fucking quickly. The unknown user opened the \u2018Security - Mr Holiday\u2019 folder and then one particular text document there, too quickly to catch the file name. It was another list. One entry was highlighted - \u2018RFSTEELE\u2019. The prompt flashed again. \u201cIs that what you are looking for?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d Billy Mack looked over the list.<br /> <br /> The unknown user wasn\u2019t done. \u201cExcellent. Who are you again?\u201d The g-man fucking smiled and gave the username attached to the password he\u2019d used to log in. \u201cJust checking.\u201d<br /> <br /> He got back to the list. It only had eighteen entries, which were nothing but names in a similar format to Roxanne Steele\u2019s. There were a few more familiar names there. Billy Mack found DMPAULSON, GASANDERSON and SMMILES listed along with hers. A goddamn watchlist, then, it seemed.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack went up a level and scanned the fucking lengthy file list. Jack checked their surroundings as he noticed the g-man look to the side, but relaxed as Billy Mack went back to typing. \u201cAre there any other references to Roxanne Steele?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me check.\u201d The response was quick but there was a pause after. \u201cNot that you have access to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u201d Billy Mack began looking over the files again. \u201cI could get you access. If you wanted to make a deal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat kind of deal?\u201d<br /> <br /> The cursor blinked. \u201cEvery Tuesday Team Tomorrow Medical sends vans to Northwest Hospital, sometimes to pick up equipment, sometimes to donate the same. It is the only way they get their equipment, they never order it themselves. I want to know what it is they are receiving. Put a thumb drive in the laptop you\u2019ll find there, run the program on it, then return it to any computer in this building. Oh, and don\u2019t plug it into any computer you care about.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack narrowed his eyes consideringly. \u201cI can do that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. If you don\u2019t, I\u2019ll murder your family.\u201d<br /> <br /> Another series of commands too goddamn quick to follow were executed and the text of an email from Mr. Innis was displayed. \u201cMs. Roxanne Steele has information and/or technology of interest to the firm. You are authorized to offer her large amounts of money or take it off her dead body.\u201d<br /> <br /> The lady behind the front desk came over to Billy Mack\u2019s cubicle. \u201cI was told this is for you?\u201d She offered him a fucking thumb drive.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, thank you.\u201d He took it and smiled at her. She smiled back and returned to her desk.<br /> <br /> As he cleaned up his tracks and began to restore the proper fucking GUI, one last message flashed on the screen. \u201cRemember.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Back at the office, I leaned back in one of the lab chairs. \u201cSo, Billy Mack, why the fuck do you have a brand new thumb drive?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cA computer gave it to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, sure, a computer - the fuck did you just say?\u201d I looked up at the ceiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat does sound like something Billy Mack would say, you must admit?\u201d Liz smiled at me. I rolled my eyes.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack told us about his deal. I eyed the goddamn thumb drive suspiciously. \u201cGonna put one of your viruses on it, just in case it gets back to the fucking bridge builder?\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked thoughtful. \u201cPerhaps. It did say that if I failed, my family would be murdered. Well, the family of FDarrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> I just looked at him for a fucking moment. \u201cDid you get anything useful?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhite\u2019s watchlist.\u201d Billy Mack recited the 18 usernames. He raised an eyebrow at me. \u201cI imagine at least two of them are Jake.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI, for one, will be goddamn fucking disappointed if not.\u201d I started tossing a stress ball against the wall.<br /> <br /> Liz cleared her throat. \u201cI managed to find a name for our mystery woman. Only one, Kim, and I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s the first or last name.\u201d She smiled like a cat with a fucking canary. \u201cI made a friend who complimented my eyes. She told me about how Ms. Kim has a blue clearance card that lets her in anywhere. If she shows it to anyone, they are to do exactly as she says.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s a swanky fucking deal. Can I get me one of those?\u201d I smirked at her. I filled the rest of them in on Holt and the Imports division.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, two bullets in the feet, drop him off at the right corner and he\u2019ll be dealt with.\u201d Jack held up the wall, his hand straying to his goddamn gun.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cVivian has the contacts to make him miserable.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz grinned. \u201cIf you have not mean girled someone to a pile of tears, you have not lived.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz and Billy Mack began swapping stories. Jack and I looked at each other goddamn longsufferingly. \u201cYou think if we just leave, they\u2019ll notice?\u201d he asked me.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe most certainly would.\u201d Billy Mack looked at me goddamn disapprovingly. \u201cI believe this was quite successful. We have an idea how to get in and we have confirmed White\u2019s interest in Mrs. Steele.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. It was not particularly difficult, though we might have been watched the whole time.\u201d Liz pointed at him with her cigarette. \u201cAnd we\u2019re no closer to knowing where she is.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack sighed. \u201cAnd we can\u2019t blow the place up. Too many innocents.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cMost of them, I believe. My new friend Amy Price thinks that Brand Corporation is a villain because they are a large corporation that buys other corporations, but has no idea of the scale.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe believes they are regular villains, not supervillains?\u201d Billy Mack smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe clearly doesn\u2019t work in fucking Imports,\u201d I muttered.<br /> <br /> \u201cOn that topic,\u201d Billy Mack began, \u201cI would hypothesize Mrs. X is some sort of spirit, something not from earth that is simply trying to look like they belong. Frater Pietr\u2019s cult is an interesting one. It is approximately a century old. They have in their possession a large crystal that has inside it what they believe is a being of pure evil, analogous to the Christian Satan. Their dogma says that a pure child will be born and that they must stab their crystal into its forehead. Satan will take over the child, and the world, for 1000 years, after which Jesus will manifest in the purity of the child and eat Satan from the inside out and ascend.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh fuck.\u201d I ran my fingers through my hair.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded, \u201cWe should go through their records, and see what they are importing, and for whom.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack made a strangled noise. \u201cSteal it and seal it in concrete, is what we need to do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps. But that is for another time, and not tonight. I believe we should relax in preparation for tomorrow night.\u201d Billy Mack looked at each of us.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I have things to do, and not all of it involves my legs being