u201cIf you <u>need</u> me,\u201d she emphasized.<br /> <br /> Jack watched them leave. Once the door was shut, he turned to Billy Mack. \u201cSo, there\u2019s this vampire...\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really have a master plan, Kayla.<br /> <br /> Okay, so, the Adria situation. You remember it all from last time, I guess. I decided to have Naomi home in on Callie, Louise, and Adria, but kinda sidestepping Adria as I could. We had met at the Roost, and hung out with Callie was Louise was waiting tables. Speed and Kilroy figured out Louise is a werecat. They hunt for, um, bad people? Threats in humanity\u2019s midst. She was seeing if Kilroy or I were, and I bet if Cassandra was. It\u2019s my theory she sent Adria to the Pagan clubhouse. Callie seems okay, but as Adria hangs out more with Louise an odd dynamic has started where Callie is getting weird about Louise. I understand, I guess.<br /> <br /> However, despite Callie and Louise flirting, I owed Am some attention. Sweet Am. Drama free Am. If you want to hook up with one of these girls, I recommend Am. She tries hard to please, and says the most adorable things while cuddling. I had used her to take the edge off my hunger, so she missed our dinner, so when I came out of the meeting I took her out to somewhere classy. We spent the night together. It was sweet. Am isn\u2019t turned on by Naomi\u2019s biting side, so I try to be gentler with her.<br /> <br /> We met Drake for brunch the next day, and dealt more with the Michael White stuff. We did a run in the Brand Corporation headquarters\u2026I\u2019ll explain that later weird shit. Anyway we\u2026<br /> <br /> Hang on. It\u2019s Deanna.<br /> <br /> Hey Sweetie?<br /> <br /> Yea I got the call from Cassandra. We are being mobilized, finally. How are you?<br /> <br /> Good. Listen you be sure there are no heroics here. Stay back. Help the Pagans away from the action. I am making sure I am some distance myself. I may see you, but not sure, Cassandra has me intercepting people who go near.<br /> <br /> Yea, I will see if I can have us together.<br /> <br /> Take care Sweetie.<br /> <br /> Okay, so when we got out I went to see Heather a bit, help her with some writing. Was remarkably hinjinx-free. We also argued about our ships for<i> Legend of Korra</i>. It\u2019s started the fourth season, just online, and it is probably the last. So the shipping arguments are hot and heavy. I am kind of glad I made friends with Heather. Obsessing on a show like that is a human thing, and fun to do.<br /> <br /> Okay, so, my target after that was Callie. She was less dangerous than Louise, and less worldly. I was also pretty sure she has a serious thing for Naomi. Contrary to Naomi\u2019s protests, one probably that would be more intense without Naomi\u2019s smart-ass attitude. With the understanding Naomi would not seduce her, she came to hang out with her and watch Netflix. I am trying to get her into <i>Korra</i>. Anyway, So we talked about what might be affecting Adria. Naomi\u2019s charm and I think her slight jealousy of Adria\u2019s attention away had her naming names, and I have narrowed to a few. Dr. Cox is not impossible, but unlikely. I think they only spoke once. Louise is probably not directing her too much. She has, however, spoken several times to Dr. Hargrove. He is supposed to be a Vampire. I suspect he is. However, she has not shown a lust for vampire blood, so I don\u2019t think she is a ghoul.<br /> <br /> No no, hold my hand. Please.<br /> <br /> My bet is he thinks I am a Vampire or Ghoul, probably ghoul. Not sure. I plan to negotiate. If he is pulling Adria\u2019s strings, he needs to know I am not opposing him. And if there is trouble, Quietus can deal with him.<br /> <br /> Yea, I know. Given Quietus is trying to impress me so much, he sure spends a lot of time directly defying me and talking about doing things he knows will piss me off, doesn\u2019t he? If I could not read him, I would think he was just trying to piss me off on purpose.<br /> <br /> So after that, Naomi seduced Callie, because she is a bitch. It was a good night though. Callie actually proposed, though to be fair it was in the heat of passion. As lovers go, Callie has been one of Naomi\u2019s better ones, just behind Cassandra and not by much. It\u2019s hard to replace the bond with Am, though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as Naomi is a bitch, she had Speed pick her up and see Callie spent the night. She enjoyed the gloating.<br /> <br /> Speed has\u2026a dilemma. I\u2019ve advised her on it but unsure if I did right. She seduced this girl Esha, an Indian girl connected to the Blue Sun stuff. However, Miranda is her girlfriend, and she feels dissonant sleeping with Esha. I suggested Miranda was Speed Demon\u2019s girlfriend so what Gabe does is about Gabe, not Speed, but it did not help. I was also torn by things because Speed\u2019s relationship with Esha is, well, valuable. Blue Sun sounds frightening, and we need that in. I don\u2019t want to damage things with Miranda though. I don\u2019t know, what do you think?<br /> <br /> Well that\u2019s true.<br /> <br /> Regardless, in the end Speed and Miranda must decide, not us.<br /> <br /> Speaking of us, let\u2019s enjoy this moment my Sweet. May sundown never come and end it.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Oh what fun!<br /> <br /> I was proud of the Brand Corporation scene. There was nothing at all sinister happening there.<br /> <br /> Gabe had a very good use of \u201cYou can tell me\u201d on the secretary for Ms. Scoggins. The reason Gabe found the delivery going awry funny is it harkens back to Session 1. Holt has been seen twice having lunch with Carla at Kiki\u2019s\u2026the first time was when Fulgur temporarily hacked his phone.<br /> <br /> A reminder, in case it was unclear, Billy Mack\u2019s entire conversation with the computer was typed.<br /> <br /> Speed\u2019s player did add some nuance to the conversations at the bar. A lot of that was handled OOC, with options worked out as to what might interest them. Speed\u2019s player did rather an expert job of giving us some IC stuff for it. Naomi\u2019s chat with and seduction of Callista was not handled IC either. The brand stuff was totally IC, as was the Esha conversation, and the office stuff always is.<br /> <br /> The Room tonight, unless we get sidetracked. Wish our villains luck; they might just need it. See you next time; Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-30T13:54:33-08:00","id":819965,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time. Let\u2019s deal with the Abyssal breach. Our villains go down to face the void and end this evil once and for all.<br /> <br /> As sometimes happens, Clytemnestra is a vignette which takes place after Speed. Speed covers the session. Clytemnestra just shows her interacting with some cultists, and talking about the future.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon's Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Once Jack fucked off to stalk around campus looking for a goddamn vampire lair, Billy Mack got down to Shooter\u2019s emails. His program had managed to decrypt them over the night. Cataloged them too. He started off with the obvious connection: Steele.<br /> <br /> The oldest email that search got him was from Seattle City Lights. It informed Shooter that there was a problem with Roxanne Steele. He was to meet with her, along with some kind of special fucking operative named Jose, to retrieve whatever the fuck she had stolen and evaluate whether she should be killed, have her mind altered, or simply be allowed to rot in prison.<br /> <br /> He reported back quickly after the goddamn shootout at her house. That went down just like we'd fucking figured, with a few extra details. She managed to manipulate Jose into making the first move - when he tried to grab her, she telekinetically threw him into the table. Then when Shooter threw lead at her, she managed to move Jose to block the shot. She made a break for it towards the back of the house, where there was no door out. Still, she managed to escape somefuckinghow. Shooter didn\u2019t catch sight of her again.<br /> <br /> The managerial fuck had a high opinion of the dame - dangerous, cunning, resourceful, manipulative, smart, not to mention powers to go along with her telekinesis. His conclusion was that she needed to be killed and fucking quick. He recommended a team of multiple special operatives and that she be shot on sight if at all possible. He worried both that her powers would be difficult to deal with, especially in public, and that she knew more than she let on and may have already been compromised by disgruntled employees. Such a goddamn boring name for the Unchained.<br /> <br /> The poor sap ended his email with an almost goddamn routine sounding request to eliminate Fitz-y boy. He even acknowledged they probably thought it was funny but he was sure that the goober needed to be dealt with. Their response thanked him for his report, with an almost fucking routine sounding ending - there was no evidence Fitzgerald had ever taken out a special operative and they weren\u2019t going to kill a man because Shooter couldn\u2019t get along with him at work.<br /> <br /> It was a running theme - he reported to HR that Langley had sent numerous photos of dicks with STDs. They volunteered to file a complaint with Seattle City Lights about the employee account that sent them. His insistence that Fitz-y boy had spoofed the from address was met with another request for proof.<br /> <br /> Fitzgerald\u2019s goddamn ongoing gas-lighting campaign was not the only side project Billy Mack looked into. He ran a couple of searches getting the skinny on the situation at the dam. Looking for Ms. Crimson didn\u2019t get any emails directly from her, but he did seems to meet with her regularly and would pass on her reports when needed. The gee was fucking scared of her, that was for goddamn certain, but appreciated the security boost since she\u2019d arrived. And the fact that she did a better job than \u2018the Old Man\u2019 at keeping the \u2018operatives at the lake\u2019 in line.<br /> <br /> That was the only reference to Ganora and her people. Shooter was worried about Tsagogla\u2019lal though, worried that she was active at the dam and that some of the workers were worshiping her. Didn\u2019t mention the operatives at the lake worshiping her, so that\u2019s probably fucking good. Her symbol had shown up as graffiti in the bathrooms and dirtfall on the dam. Again, he didn\u2019t have any proof but he reminded Seattle City Lights that those symbols \u2018started showing up in the Works, and we saw what happened there\u2019. His superiors were more inclined to believe him on that front though they claimed there was nothing they could do at this point.<br /> <br /> He mentioned the Works in one other context, his concern that \u2018the entity\u2019 in the Works might escape. Not much follow-up to it, no indication whether that was the rhino-sized motherfucker Billy Mack heard breathing, the alleged goddamn crocodile Cryptid (if that\u2019s not the rhino sized motherfucker), the shit Symphonic Metal left behind or some other bullshit we haven\u2019t heard rumors about yet. It was interesting that Shooter had been in this shit going that far back.<br /> <br /> Nothing else on our radar came up in a big way. Shooter was considering having work done at Team Tomorrow. His employees had orders to avoid White if at all possible and if they let Fitz-y boy talk to him, they\u2019d be fired and he\u2019d see to it they never worked again. Nothing else we\u2019d connected to White came up, or any of the shit we\u2019d tied to Sanderson.<br /> <br /> <br /> I, meanwhile, had a goddamn appointment. Esha met me downtown at the high end shopping district. She led me to one of a couple of fancy fucking boutiques. \u201cPick out something nice.\u201d Her gaze wandered over to the lingerie section. \u201cSomething you wouldn\u2019t usually be able to afford, something you really want.\u201d<br /> <br /> I winked and then went wandering around a bit, avoiding the lingerie. They had some damn nice suits but I kept my eyes from lingering too long. Nothing I\u2019d worn since I finished unlocking my Cipher looked too good for long. It all got rumpled and creased like I\u2019d slept in it for days as soon as I put it on. That wasn\u2019t precisely gonna fucking fly when I tried on a new suit here.<br /> <br /> After a few minutes, she pulled me along to another shop. I was eying a silk tie - that couldn\u2019t rumple too bad right? - when she called me over. She held up a translucent purple negligee. I raised an eyebrow. She smiled. \u201cI\u2019ll have to let you see it sometime.\u201d She looked at me thoughtfully, then down at the negligee. \u201cYou know, I never wanted anything like this before. It made me feel like a sex object. Now...\u201d She grinned at me. \u201cI kinda like it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked at her and something over her shoulder caught my eye. It was a hell of an overcoat - full length, single breasted, fully canvassed and 100% goddamn wool. I usually made do with my heavier suit coat in the cold and rain of Seattle \u2013 a good coat was expensive. The one on the store dummy there probably cost twice as much as my so fucking called good suit. Plus, it was way too goddamn heavy to get creased for at least 10 minutes. Esha wouldn\u2019t let me see the price tag, but whisked it away as soon as she saw that it fit.<br /> <br /> I shrugged into it as we left. Esha looked me up and down appreciatively. \u201cNow you look like a proper gumshoe. Are you prepared for your femme fatale?\u201d She gave me a fucking significant look.<br /> <br /> I can thank the God Machine for small goddamn favors without being a fucking Integrator, right? I don\u2019t think Esha would have appreciated the dismissive look that would have come over my face if I was human. Instead I gave her a rakish grin. \u201cAlways.\u201d<br /> <br /> We went to a couple of other places before she treated me to a late lunch. She looked at me over her glass of water. \u201cYou know, in a few days, I\u2019ll have my own office. Maybe I could get some advice on decorating - I\u2019ve always had to share before.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh ho, and you get your own now huh?\u201d I leaned back in my chair, running my fingers along the inset carving along the seat of the goddamn chair.<br /> <br /> She arched an eyebrow. \u201cI\u2019m going to be one of the leaders in this project.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded appreciatively. \u201cGrats, doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m going to be getting a townhouse here. I\u2019ll have to let you see that sometime too.\u201d She put a hand over mine.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are moving up in the world.\u201d I winked at her.<br /> <br /> It was a fucking nice lunch. Sometimes being a goddamn shithead had its fucking perks. The conversation was light and comfortable, though I made sure to let her know I had work tonight and wouldn\u2019t be answering my phone. She took it in stride, probably imagining all sorts of PI business that had nothing to do with fucking Abyssal taint.<br /> <br /> As we left the cafe, she stopped, putting a hand on my collarbone. \u201cCan I kiss you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I made a show of looking around, scanning for \u2018tails\u2019. Sure, that was not the kinda place where I expected to run into Miranda, but that\u2019d be just my goddamn luck. I winked at Esha and kissed her. \u201cWe\u2019ll talk, about that office thing.\u201d I glanced down at her bags and smirked. \u201cAnd maybe those other things too.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> When it was time, I went to pick up Miranda. She was waiting for me. She came out the front door as soon as I pulled up, locking it behind her. I didn\u2019t say anything, just opened the passenger door for her. She smiled at me, slightly, and laid her arm, palm up on the console armrest. I laid my hand on hers and laced our fingers together.<br /> <br /> I let go when we got there but my gaze lingered on her over the car. She walked close to me as we headed towards the Room. We didn\u2019t touch, but I caught her glancing over at me about as much as she caught me glancing over at her.<br /> <br /> We met Cassandra and the boys outside the alumni building. Cassandra began to fill us in. \u201cMaster is already inside and had given us the order to help. The other pagans are around the place to try and socially slow down people trying to get in. There\u2019s 15 of them, and they\u2019re wandering in twos and threes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey have eyes on Stein and Cox?\u201d I kept a goddamn eye out, shifting to get the best view.<br /> <br /> \u201cDr. Cox is off campus, we didn\u2019t follow her, but people know to keep an eye out for her.\u201d Cassandra checked her phone. \u201cAnd Dr. Stein is in his office with the lights on. A few of the girls are watching him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re coordinating things, right?\u201d Jack watched her check her fucking phone again. She nodded. \u201cStay nearby then, but do not go into the Asbury Room under any circumstances.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cassandra nodded again and we went inside. As we walked into the courtyard, Ms. Liquor was teasing Clytemnestra. \u201cAbout time you ended up on the other side of long limbs, huh Clytemnestra?\u201d<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra gave her a goddamn flat look. \u201cNo.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe I should get spinnerets too...\u201d Ms. Liquor tapped her chin thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am the spider in this relationship.\u201d Clytemnestra crossed her arms.<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes and looked over to Jack. His eyes flashed with goddamn static in his pupils. He moved purposefully and carefully towards the other side of the courtyard where Cox had put up her fucking surveillance cameras, tracing their hidden locations with his electrical sight. He found all five of them without being caught.<br /> <br /> That done, the rest of us Demons shifted quantum states. I followed Ms. Liquor\u2019s lead, since she and I were the hands on team - Clytemnestra and Kilroy would be handling the esoteric shit and Quietus got lookout duty. So I picked up some long... well, limbs technically. I wound up in something like a miniaturized construction vehicle. Admittedly one with an insane amount of manual dexterity and a mastery of craftsmanship.<br /> <br /> Cassandra looked up from her phone towards Clytemnestra. \u201cMaster, Stein got a phone call, he\u2019s left his office. Am is on the alert, watching the door in the back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDoor in the... what? There\u2019s no other fucking door, just that one.\u201d I jerked my hydraulic arm towards the door off the courtyard.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s what she said...\u201d Cassandra typed into her phone. \u201cYeah, she says...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCome with me,\u201d Quietus interrupted her.<br /> <br /> Cassandra looked at Clytemnestra. \u201cI\u2019m supposed to stay here. Sir.\u201d Quietus ground his goddamn teeth.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra waved her on. \u201cGo on. Figure this out. We need to get started.\u201d<br /> <br /> Quietus put an arm around Cassandra and unfurled his wings, shooting the hell up into the air. Cassandra held on tight with one arm but extended the other with her phone. Quietus looked at her disapprovingly when he heard the fucking click of its camera. \u201cDon\u2019t worry God-man, you\u2019re not in frame.\u201d She smiled at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat did you say?\u201d he growled.<br /> <br /> \u201cUm. God-man? You... you\u2019re a god, right, sir?\u201d She shrunk away a little, as best she goddamn could.<br /> <br /> Quietus made himself relax. \u201cOh. Right. Yeah, sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled tentatively. \u201cWhen someone asks you if you\u2019re a god, you say yes, right?\u201d She glanced at her phone. \u201cDr. Stein walked right by Deanna and Gavin loudly having sex and didn\u2019t stop.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat.\u201d Quietus landed gently, near the tree Am was sitting in. He looked over the empty fucking wall. \u201cWhere\u2019s this back door you\u2019re talking about?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat door?\u201d Am asked, hopping down.<br /> <br /> Quietus narrowed his eyes at her. \u201cWhat door?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat door, sir.\u201d She pointed at a blank stretch of wall.<br /> <br /> \u201cI -\u201d Quietus cut himself off as she walked up to and through the wall. He looked over at Cassandra, then tried walking through himself. He felt reality fucking glitch as he moved into the back room cleanly. The rest of us stared at the two of them.<br /> <br /> Miranda looked at me. \u201cThat is not magic like I have seen before.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cIf Am and Stein are the common link, it\u2019s something to do with Team Tomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought they were a medical facility.\u201d Miranda raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019ve got some weird shit going on though - dogs with hive minds for one.\u201d Quietus looked around, then ducked back out the invisible door.<br /> <br /> Miranda narrowed her eyes at the wall. \u201cThat\u2019s still biological...\u201d she muttered. I put an arm around her waist.<br /> <br /> Quietus came back quickly with Cassandra. She looked up from her phone. \u201cDr. Stein\u2019s pushed past Amy and Beverly.\u201d Quietus started moving the furniture in front of the door and nudged Am into picking up reams of paper for the goddamn barricade.<br /> <br /> Miranda, Kilroy and I started down to the boiler room. It was strange swinging myself down the ladder using an articulated hydraulic arm. Clytemnestra lingered at the ladder. \u201cAm, if there\u2019s a confrontation, leave.\u201d<br /> <br /> Am glanced at the ream of paper in her hand. \u201cWell, the door\u2019s barricaded, so I guess I'm fucked?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHide then.\u201d Clytemnestra sighed. Am saluted fucking cheerfully and Clytemnestra and Ms. Liquor joined us downstairs.<br /> <br /> Am turned to Quietus. \u201cUh, sir, what kind of gun is that?\u201d He looked at her. \u201cWhat? I\u2019ve never seen one in person before. My parents don\u2019t like guns.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cIt\u2019s a standard-issue cop weapon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t see many cops...\u201d She trailed off.<br /> <br /> <br /> We got set up quickly and in short order the progress we made got some pushback. From the back corner of that goddamn boiler room came the fucking scraping noise of metal on concrete. Miranda began preparing a spell. Clytemnestra scattered, a carpet of spiders spreading out over the walls.<br /> <br /> A blackish blob of darkness, filled with fucking morphing faces, scraped its way into the red light. Kilroy, Ms. Liquor and I kept working, though I kept an eye on Miranda and called back towards the stairs. \u201cQuietus! Could use some goddamn help down here!\u201d<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t hear over the clamor of Stein trying to shoulder open the goddamn back door. Clytemnestra ambushed the thing, tying it up in webs. Miranda\u2019s spell made it writhe and howl, but it couldn\u2019t break free from Clytemnestra\u2019s web. A long, low and loud growling moan came from the shadows in the room and the wound in reality began undulating - summoning something.<br /> <br /> Quietus heard the moan but had fucking problems of his goddamn own to deal with. Stein wasn\u2019t able to get past his barricade, but a humanoid thing had wandered in from the Asbury Room. He got a good look at it as it wandered past where he sat still and invisible. He recognized it as one of the people whose portrait was in the Room, if that man had been fucking underwater for a couple of weeks.<br /> <br /> The fixer pounced on it after it passed, blade hand sinking deep past a thick skin. It swung fucking wildly at him, trying to grab onto him, but missed and he finished it off with one more hit.<br /> <br /> We had a chance to patch up the wound enough to delay its goddamn summoning, but I wasn\u2019t fucking fast enough. A thing that looked like a goddamn gorilla crossed with a fiddler crab with a fucking skull face. It moved quickly, swiping its jacking arm at Kilroy and hitting hard, breaking bones and bruising deep. Miranda made a tearing motion, and pain flew over her face as she braced herself against the wall. But the creature also stumbled back, its arm dangling by a thread of what passed for flesh.<br /> <br /> It turned to Miranda, dull rage on its immobile face. I stepped between her and it and took a shot, staggering it. Then it collapsed in front of me. From behind its bulky corpse, I saw Kilroy wince as he breathed deeply and lowered his weapon.<br /> <br /> I stared my gratitude at him. The wound began undulating again so we got right the hell back to work. We managed to dampen its pulsing and get a little more fixed before it flared into life again. I almost had the edges stabilized when there was a ripping noise.<br /> <br /> Quietus called up to us as he finished of a drowned version of the woman whose portrait hung also in the goddamn Asbury Room. \u201cThere\u2019s shit coming from the paintings up here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s shit coming from portals down here. No bugs though.\u201d Kilroy called back. When a bipedal roach tumbled from the tear in reality, crooning noises like a fucking child\u2019s mobile or a simple goddamn music box he sighed. \u201cMaybe I spoke too soon.\u201d<br /> <br /> The creature swiped at Kilroy but missed. Clytemnestra wrapped her limbs around it, beginning to cover it with webbing. I braced myself between the fucking thing and Miranda, turning when I heard her call my name. She made a tearing motion again and fell. A quick motion of my long hydraulic arm caught her and brought her close to lean on my chassis. Ms. Liquor sprayed it with a liquid that fizzled and steamed as it hit, and Kilroy finished that one off as well.<br /> <br /> After finishing off a third zombie who did not have a portrait in the room, Quietus fucking stormed into the Asbury Room. He slashed across the first portrait, cutting through the painted man\u2019s neck. He froze after, taking advantage of his goddamn mirrored skin to hide in plain sight from the zombie climbing from the other portrait. His surprise attack almost took its head off but the zombie collapsed onto him, grabbing fucking tight. Throwing his arms out, Quietus electrified the air around him. The zombie twitched once as it collapsed.<br /> <br /> Am ran in, breathing hard, holding a dagger in front of her. Quietus turned to her after he slashed the second portrait. \u201cGet back...\u201d His barked order was interrupted by Cassandra fucking flying past him.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m afraid you\u2019re trespassing.\u201d Stein stood in the doorway to the courtyard.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m following orders.\u201d Am crossed her arms and stood in his way. Quietus rolled his eyes and held Stein\u2019s gaze over Am\u2019s head.<br /> <br /> Steam raised a fucking eyebrow at Quietus but addressed Am. \u201cFollow mine, go home and go to bed.\u201d A goddamn gunshot rang out from Quietus\u2019 left. Stein raised a hand to his face and looked at the blood on his fingers. He looked at Cassandra. \u201cWould you stop that? You are really upsetting me.\u201d He was unfuckingfazed.<br /> <br /> Jack glared at Cassandra. \u201cDr. Stein. My friends are fixing the Abyssal intrusion. I\u2019m not going to let you stop them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStop them? Do you even know what you are doing? Have you studied the occult formulae?\u201d Stein looked goddamn dismissively at Quietus.<br /> <br /> \u201cMe? No. That\u2019s why I\u2019m up here.\u201d Quietus shrugged, vaguely in the direction of the goddamn zombies.<br /> <br /> Stein sighed. \u201cVery well.\u201d<br /> <br /> He moved towards the back room. Quietus rolled his eyes again and moved to intercept him but Cassandra and Am got there first. Cassandra raised her fucking gun. \u201cYou\u2019re not going any further!\u201d<br /> <br /> The large professor stomped, creating a goddamn shockwave that knocked Cassandra and Am off their feet. He glared at them a moment before turning to Quietus. \u201cI hope you know what you\u2019re doing.\u201d He turned and went out to the courtyard, sitting on the bench.<br /> <br /> Quietus looked at the two girls. \u201cDo not antagonize Stein, do not touch the paintings and do not let anyone in, understand?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes sir!\u201d He gritted his teeth at their chorus as he moved quickly to join us downstairs.<br /> <br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t get to have any more fun. I wasn\u2019t about to let Miranda hurt herself again, and the others put their goddamn backs into it too. We managed to stabilize the portal every fucking time it began undulating. It slowed our progress, but after thirty five minutes we\u2019d closed the portal completely and after forty, the hole in reality was patched completely.<br /> <br /> As soon as the last bit of Abyssal presence disappeared, Miranda\u2019s legs gave out. I shifted back into Gabe and caught her before she hit the ground, but she was out like a light.<br /> <br /> I held her close. Quietus looked at her fucking confusedly, not seeing any injuries. \u201cWhat happened?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe magic she was doing hurt her too, somehow. I think.\u201d I looked over at Kilroy.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat should we do? Would the medicine help?\u201d Quietus looked at Kilroy too.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI don\u2019t know. But not that. She needs to be conscious for that, for whatever countermeasures... I think.\u201d I held her, helplessly.<br /> <br /> Ms. Liquor put a hand on my shoulder and looked at Kilroy. \u201cLet Kilroy accelerate her healing and put her in your bolthole. Without time passing, she\u2019ll be fine until we can watch over her somewhere safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded my thanks and disappeared through the nearest doorway as Clytemnestra turned to Quietus, after Kilroy indicated he\u2019d done his bit. I kicked things away from the wall and sat her up in the corner so I could shrug out of my jacket. Not the softest pillow in the world, but better than the hard floor. I folded it inside out and settled her down on it.<br /> <br /> I brushed her hair away from her face. A small trail of blood came from the corner of her mouth. I wiped it away with my thumb. \u201cWe\u2019re gonna get through this Miranda. You\u2019ll be OK, right?\u201d I watched for a few moments, syncing my breathing with the soft rise and fall of her chest. Then I kissed her on the forehead and went back out.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow did things go upstairs?\u201d Clytemnestra asked Quietus.<br /> <br /> \u201cA few zombies.\u201d He looked at me, then back at her. \u201cAnd I think Cassandra took offense at being thrown across the room.\u201d Clytemnestra stared at him in horror before running right the hell upstairs. Quietus looked fucking bemused. \u201cShe\u2019s fine though?\u201d he told her rapidly disappearing back.<br /> <br /> I smiled slightly at him as we followed along. Cassandra was explaining something to Clytemnestra when we caught up. \u201c... a flash of fire in the Asbury Room, where Dr. Stein was. He said, uh, that was that, and he\u2019s going to see a doctor.\u201d<br /> <br /> The room did look more than a little fucking singed. No sign of any zombies - then again, the goddamn creatures downstairs had disappeared in the heartbeat I was in my bolthole. I paced, looking around, while the others flapped their gums about some shit.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong with Team Tomorrow?\u201d Am asked.<br /> <br /> Quietus was about to go into it when I threw a goddamn hand up. \u201cFor fuck\u2019s sake. Cassandra, can you get Dr. Cox to campus? To the pagan club house?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI can get her anywhere.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFucking great. Take Am the hell with you. We\u2019ll meet you there after we catch Dr. Stein.\u201d I started walking in the direction Cassandra had said he went.<br /> <br /> The students left. Ms. Liquor shifted into Kayla. \u201cI\u2019ll get Angela and bring her to the pagan club house as well.\u201d I nodded and she smiled at me sympathetically as she left.<br /> <br /> Quietus took off into the goddamn air while the rest of them shifted to human form, Kilroy into Billy Mack and Clytemnestra into Naomi. The silver skinned robot caught sight of Stein fucking quickly and landed in front of him. \u201cStop please.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stein eyed him. \u201cI need a doctor.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, we can help with that too, but you\u2019re tainted by the Room. My friends have something to fix that.\u201d He pointed the direction we were coming from with his goddamn blade hand. \u201cAh, sorry about that.\u201d He shifted into Jack, shrugging.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. It\u2019s you.\u201d Stein did a double take at the three of us crossing the lawn.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded to him. \u201cDr. Stein, I have something here to correct the Abyssal taint. And I might be able to help with your injuries as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes. \u201cWell, you can go to a goddamn doctor, they just can\u2019t help with the fucking taint so let\u2019s get that fucking dealt with.\u201d I scanned the area, but no one was around this part of campus at this hour.<br /> <br /> He raised his hands. \u201cI\u2019m not going to struggle, I appear to have hurt myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack administered a dose of the medicine, laying a hand on the tall professor\u2019s fucking shoulder. \u201cRest for an hour and you\u2019ll be fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d He checked his watch. \u201cI could go use the couch in my office, I suppose.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBored now,\u201d Naomi announced and started moving towards the pagan club house. I followed, head down, hands in my pockets. The other fuckers trailed along after, I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> Once we got to the pagan club house, we all got our shots. I tossed the place \u2013 fucking gently, for Clytemnestra\u2019s sake - and found a full bottle of cheap whiskey in one of the bedroom cabinets. I tossed a goddamn sawbuck at Cassandra and took a long pull.<br /> <br /> Cox wasn\u2019t slow getting here, which was good for my goddamn psyche. Just before she got there, Jack looked at me and jerked his head towards a side room. I gave up pacing with another swig and followed him. \u201cListen Gabe - the zombies I dealt with started out looking like the portraits but they didn\u2019t all look like them. They were all clearly Asburys though. I don\u2019t know if I rekilled some of Miranda\u2019s ancestors or what, but I wanted to let you know...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, sure. We\u2019ll fucking figure it out.\u201d I took a drink. \u201cWhen she gets better.\u201d<br /> <br /> I walked back into the room with the others, pacing around the edges to check the windows. Cox saw Cassandra first. \u201cIf this is a booty call...\u201d She fucking trailed off when she saw the rest of us.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Room\u2019s been dealt with,\u201d Naomi said in a matter of fact way.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you trying to convince me, Naomi Cruz, that you\u2019ve done anything good for anyone ever?\u201d Cox looked goddamn unconvinced. Naomi smirked.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cUnbelievable as that may be, Dr. Cox, we have. And we have medicine that will deal with the lingering taint you still suffer from.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cox looked to Cassandra who smiled widely at her. \u201cWe know what we\u2019re doing - we\u2019re pagans!\u201d<br /> <br /> I got back to pacing as Billy Mack administered the medicine. Cox watched me fucking nervously. \u201cWhat\u2019s going to happen with the Room?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shrugged. \u201cThere is no longer an evil occult resonance to it. More mundanely, I imagine the University will chalk it up to... vandalism.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> <b>Colloquy </b><br /> <br /> A strange pattern of footfalls could be heard entering the darkened building. Four long golden legs extended from the form of a luminous golden woman, her human feet never touching the ground. Two more humanoid women flanked her. While she resembled a human otherwise, the resplendent form had hair of spun gold, golden fangs and long golden nails that combined with her extra pairs of long legs gave her an arachnid look. The two women who followed, both completely human especially in contrast to the golden form before them, walked a bit more quickly to keep up with the shining being before them, flipping on the light to the sitting room, which had been lit with gold. The golden woman had a dreamy look on her face as the legs carefully stepped around the furniture until they gently lowered her onto the couch.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid we save the world, Master?\u201d<br /> <br /> The redhead walked down, regarding her golden master. Her friend moved and sat next to her master, smiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cFrankly Cassandra? Yes and no.\u201d The Spider regarded her lieutenant. \u201cDid we ultimately stop a threat to the world as we know it? Yes. Would it have all ended had we not heroically interviewed?\u201d A gold talon tapped the Spider\u2019s chin, her human arms resting in her lap, \u201c\u2026No. We caught it before it got too horrifically bad, and no doubt we saved lives, but\u2026eventually forces would have moved to correct it.\u201d A perfect head cocked and regarded her Priestess, \u201cThe Mad God of the Middle East is evil, but He jealously guards the world He sees as His. He would have, with a half dozen slave angels, stopped this, and not cared who was hurt.\u201d<br /> <br /> The girl sitting beside the Spider lay her head on her arm, \u201cWe did well?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou did, Amsterdam. You all did.\u201d<br /> <br /> Am giggled happily. \u201cWhat\u2019s next then?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider put her human arm around the girl, \u201cNow we get to the bottom of what is going on with Adria. Get her off our backs.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot violently I hope?\u201d Cassandra looked over at Am, who kept her eyes on her Master.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t hurt humans if I can help it. Hurting, killing, that\u2019s what Angels do. You know I feed, I have overfed before but I don\u2019t deliberately hurt humans if I can help it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am honored to give of myself for you,\u201d Am smiled fondly at the beautiful woman beside her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, I am glad you are so happy to do that,\u201d Cassandra said, giving Am a sideways glance. She shivered slightly.<br /> <br /> The Spider pointed a golden leg in her direction, \u201cYou feed me too, when called upon. And it is also appreciated.\u201d<br /> <br /> Am looked at her Master, \u201cIf I am good for you, why is Team Tomorrow bad? They helped me. I would likely be dead without them.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider sighed, \u201cThe problem is we don\u2019t know, Amsterdam. We don\u2019t know what they are trying to do. Just that they work closely with some very bad people. You were made into near perfect prey, Am. I would like to know why.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe they knew you would come.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen why not contact me? Naomi really just happened to meet you. And I liked you enough to, well, sample. That part was coincidence.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat if it wasn\u2019t?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider gave the girl a look. \u201cYou have no idea how disturbing that concept is to me, Amsterdam.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cassandra looked from Am to Clytemnestra, \u201cSo you gonna be seducing an evangelical? Can it be Mariah Lawson? Please?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider considered. \u201cNaomi\u2019s swagger aside, the whole homophobes are secretly gay thing is less a sure thing with women. I\u2019ll check her out and weigh her heart. If she might work out then sure. Just for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Am grinned. \u201cOur goddess takes requests!\u201d<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra shifted. \u201cJust be sure they are within my idiom. I don\u2019t have my paradise again\u2026yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou will have it,\u201d Am looked serious.<br /> <br /> Cassandra looked at her phone, \u201cWell the others are almost here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Almost immediately three more women came in the door. One, a Korean girl, smiled at another, a pale woman with long pink hair. The paler of the two was distracted.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to lie down Deanna. Deal with this headache. I will rejoin you later,\u201d Naomi said and headed upstairs. As Am\u2019s friend Angela sat on the other side of her friend, Deanna turned to Cassandra.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t believe you had me in the bushes with Gavin,\u201d her voice was whiny. \u201cI don\u2019t like kissing boys.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere was no need to kiss him, you could have just made noise,\u201d Cassandra regarded the Korean girl coolly. \u201cI did make noise,\u201d Deanna sighed. \u201cI hope Naomi is not mad.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am pretty sure at least forty percent of the spit in her mouth belonged to other people originally anyway,\u201d Cassandra smiled impishly. Deanna wrinkled her nose.<br /> <br /> Am leaned against her master and whispered \u201cIt must be hard, being like Superman.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider laughed.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXV</i><br /> <br /> Naomi\u2019s appearance simultaneous with Clytemnestra was a use of Alibi.<br /> <br /> Once again, the rolls were Intelligence + Occult to determine max successes per roll, and Dexterity + Crafts for how many actual successes were achieved, with two primaries and two assists. The drama kept things exciting, as every so often they had to roll to keep a thing out, with a starting base of seven successes, then if it got out the number needed to keep the next thing went up, if it didn\u2019t it went down. Keeping something out meant getting a \u201cfree\u201d shot at just repairing, and successes ABOVE the threshold to stop an intruder counted as well. As you see, a couple things got through. Every so many turns anything close had to roll Stamina + Resolve to resist Abyssal taint, though the long arms sidestepped the need for a roll, hence Clytemnestra being assigned there, and Speed and Kayla using their amorphous-sens to mimic it.<br /> <br /> I think you could really see the core of who Clytemnestra, Speed Demon, Kilroy and Quietus were in flashes here. I feel like people really got a chance to shine. It was a good session.<br /> <br /> The world goes on. Lets see what happens as other plots must be dealt with. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-13T01:36:17-08:00","id":829174,"title":"","content":"Follow the clues, find the dame. But then what do you do?<br /> <br /> Just Speed this time, as the sort downtime between end of this and start of next session does not involve much to say, Kayla is right there, and Clytemnestra won\u2019t be Naomi for\u2026awhile.<br /> <i><br /> Session XXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues </b><br /> <br /> After we\u2019d gotten everybody squared the fuck away, I looked around quickly and shouldered my way out the door. Billy Mack took a few steps after me. \u201cGabe?\u201d<br /> <br /> I turned to look at him impatiently. \u201cI got the goddamn medicine.\u201d I showed it to him. \u201cI even got an empty one to practice with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPractice will be more effective with an experienced teacher.\u201d He held my fucking gaze. \u201cAnd if I can be of any assistance, I would be more than willing to stay so that I can be at hand when she wakes.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head to clear it. \u201cSure. I don\u2019t... sure. Let\u2019s just fucking go.\u201d I jerked my head towards the goddamn door and started walking quickly again. Billy Mack followed, just as quickly.<br /> <br /> <br /> At Miranda\u2019s house, I shrugged Billy Mack towards the living room and went upstairs. I opened the door of her bedroom into my bolthole. She was still out, unsurprisingly. Her stillness had me worried, but I gathered her up and held her close, ignoring my racing heart.<br /> <br /> Her head lolled against my neck and I felt her warm but shallow breath. I took a deep shuddering one of my own and walked back out the door. She looked better, lying on her own bed. She even shifted and moved on her own, settling into her usual sleeping position. I brushed her cheek, smoothing the lines left by my goddamn jacket.<br /> <br /> After a few moments, I pulled myself away. I got her shoes off before changing into night clothes. I crawled into bed, carefully curling around her. I buried my face in her neck and let myself drift off to sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cGood morning Gabe.\u201d Miranda had shifted so she could look at me. She ran her fingers through my hair as I slowly woke up.<br /> <br /> I smiled over at her and pulled myself up to a sitting position. \u201cGood morning beautiful. How are you feeling?\u201d<br /> <br /> She leaned against me. \u201cLike something big is over. Like it\u2019s time to start planning everything after that.\u201d I smiled and put my arm around her. \u201cYou want to go anywhere?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnywhere with you.\u201d I chuckled. \u201cI think I could swing a vacation.\u201d We cuddled contentedly for a few minutes before I broke the silence again. \u201cWe still need to do something about the taint, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yes. I haven\u2019t survived yet.\u201d She sighed.<br /> <br /> I put my fingers under her chin. \u201cBut you will.\u201d She nodded. I got up and found the syringe Billy Mack had given me. \u201cIs there anything an extra pair of hands would help with?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cI\u2019ve done as much preparation as I can. Now it is just a matter of timing, which your pocket dimension can help with, I believe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing love.\u201d I held the door open to my bolthole and followed her inside.<br /> <br /> As I let the door close, she turned to me and let out a deep breath. \u201cAlright, I\u2019m going to stop the magic maintaining things so that your medicine will work. Are you ready?\u201d I nodded. \u201cThen go.\u201d She shut her eyes.<br /> <br /> I lined the syringe up like Billy Mack showed me and bit my lip. All of the sudden I wished I\u2019d brought him along - it was harder to find her veins than mine. Her eyes fluttered open, looking at me questioningly. I smiled up at her and shook my head, getting the hair out of my eyes. I ran my finger down her arm, tracing her vein and feeling her heartbeat. I held her gaze as my fingers guided the needle in.<br /> <br /> Her hand clenched and I saw her eyes roll back before she shut them again. I removed the needle and stood quickly, ready to catch her if she fell. She steadied after a moment though, with a hand on my shoulder. I put an arm around her waist as I opened the door for her.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo...\u201d I began. She still looked a little like death warmed the hell over.<br /> <br /> She sat on her bed. \u201cNothing is eating me alive anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow, a half smile on my face. \u201cThat\u2019s good. Right?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled up at me. \u201cYes. I will just need to rest for a few days.\u201d I looked down and back quickly, hiding my disappointment. \u201cI could come rest at the office. If I wouldn\u2019t be underfoot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou could never be underfoot.\u201d I pulled her up and kissed her.<br /> <br /> She smirked at me and moved to get dressed. If she changed slower than was absolutely necessary, well, I sure as hell wasn\u2019t complaining. I changed into my own clothes and came up behind her, resting my chin on her shoulder. \u201cAs a warning, Billy Mack is downstairs. He wanted to be on hand in case there was something he could help with.\u201d I cocked my head towards the door. \u201cAnd it smells like he found the coffee machine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMmm.\u201d She kissed me again before leading me out by the hand.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked up from Vivian\u2019s computer. \u2018Happy Birthday\u2019 was playing from the speakers, but he muted it as we came in. \u201cFeeling better?\u201d he asked Miranda.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI am recovering.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs there anything I can do?\u201d He looked concerned.<br /> <br /> \u201cI smell coffee.\u201d She smiled slightly at him.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack passed out mugs, then went back to his computer, muttering at the screen. \u201cWe\u2019ll see who is, in fact, a noob.\u201d I paused in reaching for my flask to raise an eyebrow at him. He shrugged. \u201cAaron here had some not so nice things to say about Vivian. So I found a rather embarrassing birthday video on his mother\u2019s Facebook page that...\u201d He hit a button. \u201c...everyone in that forum will have the pleasure of seeing. I\u2019ve also taken the liberty of shipping some exotic fetish items to him at his parent\u2019s house.\u201d<br /> <br /> I wound up leaving the fucking flask where it was after sharing a glance with Miranda. She held back a chuckle. \u201cI\u2019m going to be haunting the office for a little bit, to be near Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat sounds like an excellent plan.\u201d Billy Mack nodded.<br /> <br /> Once we finished our coffee, Miranda frowned. \u201cWe should get going.\u201d She sat her mug by the sink and walked out the door.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack and I followed behind. \u201cWe should get donuts on the way to the office,\u201d he suggested.<br /> <br /> \u201cWait a minute, actual goddamn food for breakfast?\u201d I looked at him mock-dubiously.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe did save the world last night.\u201d He shrugged, smiling.<br /> <br /> Miranda was buckled into the passenger seat by the time we got there. I looked questioningly at her as I hopped in and started the car. \u201cWhat do you think, donuts?\u201d<br /> <br /> She glanced around. \u201cThat\u2019s fine.\u201d She kept glancing around as we peeled off and once we left the neighborhood, she focused on a particular car. \u201cGabrielle, we need to lose the car following us.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked in the mirror to see a goddamn nondescript Corolla. A pair of men in aviators and heavy coats were in the front seat, and an older man sat in the back, staring at us between the bucket seats. My eyes were pulled back to the road when the car in front of me blew a fucking tire. I swerved to miss it and put on speed, weaving in and out of traffic. \u201cThose are Seers.\u201d Miranda bit her lip and started muttering something.<br /> <br /> I smirked at the stubby car and shot forward. Just before a break in the dividing wall, I made a quick reversal and spun the wheel 180 degrees. I kept my eyes on the oncoming traffic, stopping my spin with a quick gear shift and gun. Miranda winced a bit as the car took the median, but it handled it a damn sight better than the Corolla did.<br /> <br /> I pulled all the way over, weaving between the shoulder and the right lane. They managed to take the median with a wide U-turn, but lost a lot of ground, swerving to avoid another car that was fucking fishtailing towards them.<br /> <br /> I swept back into traffic, threading the needle between the guard rail and a utility van. I\u2019d almost lost them when a goddamn light pole fell onto the roof of the car, rolling off behind us. With my cipher, it dealt minimal damage to the car, but the shock knocked my jaw shut. A moment later my vision blurred and pain shot through my head.<br /> <br /> A delivery truck shifted lanes next to us and I used the opportunity to floor it and slide in front of the van. I squinted and blinked to clear my vision. I jumped up a few places, in and out of the scattered cars before taking a right turn from the left lane. I left horns blaring and the mages vainly trying to merge over in time.<br /> <br /> I took my next few turns quickly, circling the city. I shook my head after we\u2019d put some distance between us and Miranda took my hand. \u201cI\u2019m sorry Gabe. They were coming after me. They probably noticed what went on at the Room, figured I had something to do with it and were checking it out. I didn\u2019t sense them until we were leaving.\u201d She leaned back in the seat, taking a few deep breaths. \u201cNice driving, by the way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe is an excellent driver.\u201d Billy Mack smiled.<br /> <br /> <br /> At the office, Miranda hopped out of the car quickly and circled around the front of the car. I raised an eyebrow, pausing after I shut my door. She pinned me against the car, kissing me hard. \u201cI like you protecting me, hero.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood, cause I\u2019m not gonna stop.\u201d I smirked at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I were feeling any better, you might not be available for a while.\u201d She swayed, a little. \u201cI\u2019ll have to take a rain check.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPayable whenever the hell you want sweetheart.\u201d I put an arm around her waist as we headed inside.<br /> <br /> Jack got an odd look on his face, looking at Miranda. \u201cSomething go wrong?\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda sat down on one of our couches. \u201cNo, I\u2019m no longer in danger as dying, at least from anything beyond the usual. I just need rest.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou look like you have the flu,\u201d Jack kept fucking prodding.<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps. I am better however.\u201d She settled in comfortably.<br /> <br /> Kayla and Liz breezed in. \u201cNaomi,\u201d Kayla said with a sigh, \u201cis a bitch.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cSure, and water is goddamn wet -\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think she knows that,\u201d Jack interrupted.<br /> <br /> \u201c- the sun is fucking hot and booze tastes good.\u201d I glared at him.<br /> <br /> He smirked back. \u201cI know she knows that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, you met Naomi, huh Kayla?\u201d I grinned at the green haired dame.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe slapped me!\u201d Liz looked hurt. I gave Kayla a high five. Liz narrowed her eyes.<br /> <br /> Kayla grinned at Liz. \u201cWhat can I mix for folks?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz sat fucking carefully and put her head down. \u201cCodeine. Bourbon.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kayla raised an eyebrow and went to fill a pitcher with water. As she poured it, it turned into booze, to each our usual. \u201cWhat about you Miranda?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cScotch please. Thank you.\u201d She took the glass carefully.<br /> <br /> Jack looked over at me as he sipped his goddamn rum. \u201cIt\u2019s a good thing Gabe can\u2019t do that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tossed mine back. \u201cHey!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe do like you to be able to walk occasionally.\u201d Jack shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cWalking is fucking overrated - driving now...\u201d I took another slug. \u201cSpeaking of which, we may have gotten in a car chase on the way here. The car\u2019s a little banged up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack slammed his glass down. \u201cWhat? How?!\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow. \u201cWell, a telephone pole fell on it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA telephone pole?\u201d Jack stared at him.<br /> <br /> I fucking shrugged. \u201cMages.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda took a sip. \u201cThe Seers. They were after me. They probably felt what happened at the college.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Seers... you mentioned them. They\u2019re the Abyssal ones?\u201d Jack looked between us.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I\u2019m the Abyssal one.\u201d Miranda smiled slightly. I gave her a look. \u201cI\u2019m the trying not to be an Abyssal one.\u201d She smiled, just for me. \u201cThe Seers are strong here. I... my ex is there leader. It was a bad breakup.\u201d She paused. \u201cI like to stay here because I annoy them and I only recently developed a self-preservation instinct.\u201d She looked over at me through her eyelashes, that smile still playing around her face like a kid on a fucking snow day. Clytemnestra beamed at us from behind Liz\u2019s aloof facade. \u201cWe don\u2019t want to provoke them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cBetcha Jack does.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked at me, goddamn annoyed, then at Liz as she nodded. \u201cWell, it is something of a trend.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWho... what?\u201d He glared at us both.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fucking Autumn Court?\u201d I suggested, glancing at Liz.<br /> <br /> \u201cHeather?\u201d Liz looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> I pointed at her. \u201cParanormal TV show crews.\u201d<br /> <br /> She laid a finger on her chin. \u201cVampires, definitely.\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cLook, I\u2019m not going to mess up your situation on campus. I think shaking him down might do you good, but I promise...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDear.\u201d Liz stopped him with a smile. Kayla frowned at him. \u201cI said you wanted to, not that you always do. You are aggressive, not stupid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t bring it up to suggest a goddamn raid anyway. I just wanted people to know in case they had the presence of fucking mind to get my plate down.\u201d I started tapping a pen against the table.<br /> <br /> Kayla looked over at Billy Mack. \u201cYou could make the license plate number disappear, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cThey don\u2019t have anything to research for it either.\u201d He glanced at Jack. \u201cI think it\u2019s been enough time to erase the race of the man who confronted the TV crew as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks man.\u201d Jack nodded at him and turned to Miranda. \u201cSo, since this will probably come up, whether we do provoking,\u201d he shot me a glare, \u201cor not, maybe give us Seers 101?\u201d<br /> <br /> Kayla brought me another whiskey sour. Miranda took a sip of her scotch. \u201cThey specialize in coming in force and shutting off people\u2019s powers.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rubbed my forehead. \u201cThese ones made that telephone pole fall and did something to my head that hurt like a motherfucker and made my vision blur.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA mild stroke, perhaps?\u201d Billy Mack looked at me carefully. \u201cYou should be better with an hour or so of rest.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d Jack leaned back in his seat. \u201cHow about 201? They sound kinda like Angels to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda shook her head. \u201cThey\u2019re rather stridently atheists and don\u2019t have allegiance to any \u2018God\u2019, machine or not.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked fucking dubious. \u201cWell, I assume talking won\u2019t work, so fuck \u2018em anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt probably will not. There\u2019s the bad break up I mentioned, plus I\u2019m an illegal mage.\u201d Jack made a strangled noise and Miranda looked over at him. He waved her the hell on. \u201cThere is good news - they can no longer track me via the magic I had to use to keep myself alive. Also, it is likely they just thought to catch me while I was weak - I\u2019m not public enemy number one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWho is?\u201d Jack perked up.<br /> <br /> \u201cAny of the organized mages in town.\u201d Miranda set her scotch down.<br /> <br /> I looked over at Jack. \u201cDone with the lesson?\u201d He shrugged. I rolled my fucking eyes. \u201cWe don\u2019t have a lot going on. There\u2019s the car - it got a little beat up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kayla smiled at me and refilled my glass. \u201cI could help with that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t have to do that.\u201d Liz put a hand on Kayla\u2019s arm.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat, refill my drink? What did I ever do to you?\u201d I gave Liz a shit eating who waved me aside.<br /> <br /> Kayla put a hand on her hips. \u201cOf course I don\u2019t have to. But I want to. I\u2019m a Psychopomp, it\u2019s what I do.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged at them. \u201cWhatever you like, doll.\u201d Cecilia left the room to answer the goddamn door. \u201cThere\u2019s also the Steele case.\u201d<br /> <br /> As if on fucking cue, Jimmy walked in. Cecilia escorted him in, then went back to her desk after frowning at his back. Jimmy looked around. \u201cThere\u2019s... more of you.\u201d He shrugged. So did I. \u201cI was instructed to give you more information about your case.\u201d His eyes flicked to Miranda, then Kayla, then back to Billy Mack. \u201cShould we go talk privately?\u201d He glanced at the rest of us. \u201cYour call.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t see any reason to get up. My chair\u2019s comfy.\u201d I spun my chair around.<br /> <br /> \u201cYour call, like I said.\u201d He sat down. \u201cRoxanne Steele\u2019s safety deposit box was stolen from the bank, last night at about 4 AM. Also, one of the three Angels is unaccounted for.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cScully, Mulder or the other fuck?\u201d<br /> <br /> He frowned. \u201cFox. I mean, Mulder is missing, Fox is... the other fuck?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf they\u2019re the ones who stole it, Mulder might be guarding whatever the hell was in the box.\u201d I looked at the others. \u201cSince they\u2019ve already been fucking tossed once.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019ve been seen all three together since their room was broken into, but I guess if there\u2019s something new...\u201d Jimmy trailed off.<br /> <br /> Jack looked thoughtful. \u201cWhere and when were they seen as a pair?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jimmy flipped through his papers. \u201cAt a play called Rogue Diver, last night. I have the address of the theatre here.\u201d He passed us a post-it note, after scribbling on it quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cBased on what we\u2019ve discovered about the altercation at her house, Ms. Steele quite possibly has some kind of phasing powers. She might have stolen it herself.\u201d Billy Mack brought it back to the theft.<br /> <br /> The lizard man shrugged. \u201cYou\u2019re the investigators. Look, not to put too much on your plate, but there\u2019s a big group leaving the hotel the Angels are staying at. They\u2019re pretty suspicious.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned forwards, running my tongue over my teeth. \u201cWe\u2019ve got that shit under control. It\u2019s to do with the fucking Blue Sun, who are on Phase 2 of a big project. I\u2019ve got eyes on it, and there\u2019s definite Angel involvement.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are possibly part of the creation of a new bit of Infrastructure,\u201d Billy Mack put in.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are on top of this.\u201d Jimmy put his papers back in his briefcase. \u201cWell, unless there\u2019s anything else?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack held up a hand. \u201cYes, actually.\u201d He retrieved a thumb drive and handed it to the cryptid. \u201cThis has all of Cleveland Shooter\u2019s work emails on it. I\u2019ve gotten the highlights, but I\u2019m sure a more thorough search, and more eyes, will be useful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll get it to him. It will mean I\u2019m not in town tonight.\u201d He looked around and nodded to all of us before he left, whistling the goddamn opening theme to