e Aetheric resonance of a goddamn trio of Angels. After a moment, a knock came at the door and Vivian heard weapons being cocked. Casey got up to answer the knock. \u201cDon\u2019t open that door Casey.\u201d<br /> <br /> They knocked again, more firmly. He looked fucking uncertainly at her. \u201cOK...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis way.\u201d Vivian led him to a window and they were just about out when a shotgun blast took out the goddamn door. They booked it for the parking lot, but the two policeman and dog caught up with them quickly.<br /> <br /> Vivian shifted parts of her Demon form into reality - her armor, shield, data form and phasing - while nudging Casey gently towards the RV. She veered the hell off, drawing the three Angels after her. The two coppers took their shots, but they either missed or got deflected by her armor. She wasn\u2019t so lucky with the goddamn dog - it tackled her and pinned her to the ground not far away.<br /> <br /> Casey got to the RV and Vivian broke out of the pin at about the same time. As soon as she saw he was safe, Vivian transformed into a stream of data and jumped into the burner phone she\u2019d dropped on the ground nearby.<br /> <br /> The Angels turned their attention to Casey and the RV when she disappeared. After the first shot, Roxanne peeled out. She glanced back at Casey. \u201cHow do you feel about Portland?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPortland\u2019ll do,\u201d Vivian said from the back of the RV, shifted back into fully human form.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh good.\u201d Roxanne smiled at her. \u201cI felt bad about leaving you behind. I was going to, like you said, but...\u201d<br /> <br /> Casey looked at Roxanne, eyes fucking wide, \u201cWho are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked. \u201cI\u2019m the person every cop in the Pacific Northwest is looking for. Hold on to your seat.\u201d Casey gulped.<br /> <br /> Vivian sighed. \u201cI still need that book of fairy tales. I can\u2019t sell Speed out to the fairy legbr