Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T02:05:01-07:00","id":858232,"title":"","content":"It's the off week for Demon, but this was asked on this thread...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=855067#post855067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I missed it, but how exactly did Gabe meet Mac?</div> </div> </div> </div>Speed's player has answered.<br /> <br /> <b>Four Detective Walk Into a Bar</b><br /> <br /> Gabe settled back into her chair, taking another sip of her drink. The cheap whiskey burned its way down as kept an eye on the pair of dirty cops in the corner and a tab on their surface thoughts. She was so focused on what they were thinking she almost missed the short Irish man approach her table from the bar, beer in hand.<br /> <br /> He sat down next to her. \u201cI haven\u2019t seen you around here before, and...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, Mac, I\u2019m not interested.\u201d His wide eyed look of surprise stalled her suggestive obscene gesture in its inception.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow... how did you know my name?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged and, turning off her Mind Reading sensor, looked over her sunglasses at him. \u201cCasual racism. With hair that red, it seemed a 50/50 chance minimum.\u201d<br /> <br /> He took it well, grinning and sticking his hand out. \u201cCorman Nolan.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe. Gabe Norton. And I\u2019m still not interested.\u201d She shifted to have a better sight line on her targets, hoping this human would take the hint so she could get back to real surveillance.<br /> <br /> He ignored the implication, turning to look over his shoulder at the dirty cops. \u201cYou\u2019re paying an awful lot of attention to them.\u201d<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow. This was a shitty bar with a shifty clientele. If he was gonna interfere in someone else\u2019s business, either he was in it with these guys, or he had a thought that I didn\u2019t belong. He didn\u2019t look like their kind of scumbag, so... \u201cDon\u2019t you worry Mac, I\u2019m no copper.\u201d<br /> <br /> He raised an eyebrow right back. \u201cReally? Cause if you are, you have to tell me. It\u2019s the law.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cReally really.\u201d She kept her smile to herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou sure look like a detective though.\u201d He took a sip of his beer.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ve got a good eye Mack. But I am a strictly <u>private</u> dick. The public variety give me hives.\u201d From what Gabe had been able to piece together, some of the regulars here knew those two were cops, some didn\u2019t. No one talked about it though, not here. From the way Mac glanced back over his shoulder at her comment, she figured he was one of the ones who knew.<br /> <br /> \u201cHives, huh?\u201d Gabe stopped paying attention to Mac as her target\u2019s auras shifted, their plans and intentions changing. She cut him off, hoping to get moving before they did, to ease the short human\u2019s suspicions.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry, pal, gotta jet.\u201d She threw back her drink. \u201cBreak time\u2019s over.\u201d She left over his protestations, lurking in the shadows outside. Her marks left shortly after, and she took the trail back up.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Apparently Mac shared a regular with the two dirty cops, judging by how often Gabe ran into him there. He almost always struck up a conversation with her, and eventually she managed to work out how to keep Mind Reading up despite the distraction, at least enough to get the cues she needed.<br /> <br /> She didn\u2019t mind, really. It was a slow job - a little slower than necessary, thanks to her calculations as to how to maximize the despair harvesting. But only a little. It was a delicate job regardless. And Mac seemed like a decent guy, even if she couldn\u2019t get a handle on his angle.<br /> <br /> So maybe it was because of him that she went back that last time, after the job was done. Maybe it was the fact that the case getting thrown out of court had gotten her the single biggest download of despair yet and she felt like celebrating and habit did the rest. Maybe the drinks were to forget the look on her client\u2019s face as he thanked her for doing everything she could, even though it wasn\u2019t enough. Or maybe she had an inkling of what was going to happen.<br /> <br /> Habit certainly had her tuned into the taller one\u2019s surface thoughts as Mac told another story of how adorably insane his pregnant wife was. Her eyes widened at what she heard in his thoughts. Mac frowned at her. \u201c... and then she grew wings and jumped off the bridge.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUh huh.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you even paying attention to me Gabe?\u201d He crossed his arms.<br /> <br /> She made sure she wasn\u2019t staring at the dirty cops, but mostly focused on their thoughts. \u201cSomething\u2019s wrong Mac.\u201d She found their plan, right as they finished settling their tab. Payback. She grabbed her hat and got up to follow.<br /> <br /> Mac grabbed her arm. \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong Gabe? What\u2019s between you and them?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gabe pulled away and moved fast. \u201cIt\u2019s not your business Mac.\u201d Ideal despair gathering would be to arrive just moments too late, but that didn\u2019t mean she could dawdle. Mac scrambled after her, throwing some money on the table to cover his own tab.<br /> <br /> He caught up with her outside, grabbing her again, with a better grip this time. \u201cI\u2019m not going to just let you go chase after those two like that, not without an explanation!\u201d<br /> <br /> Gabe blew her hair out of her eyes. On one hand, he might give the game away, and get her shot as well as Richie. On the other, he could definitely delay her long enough for everything to go to hell. And... he seemed like a decent guy. \u201cLook - those two fuckers are the dirtiest cops I\u2019ve ever had the opposite of pleasure knowing about. They got fingered in an extortion deal last week. I got sources that say they\u2019re looking for payback on the poor kid they were extorting.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac narrowed his eyes at her \u2018sources\u2019 but didn\u2019t seem shocked by the rest. \u201cSo how did you get involved?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s a long story.\u201d Gabe sighed. \u201cCan I at least tell you in the car?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe car? Gabe, you\u2019ve been drinking. You can in the taxi.\u201d Gabe opened her mouth to protest, but Mac had already flagged down a taxi. He looked to her for an address, and once she gave it, showed the cabbie a double sawbuck. \u201cIf we get there quick.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gabe sat in the seat with Mac, an unhappy look on her face. \u201cSo, there\u2019s this kid, Richie. He\u2019s... a sweet kid, you know what I mean? Sweet. But... not all there. He owns a food cart, his uncle set it up for him. Felt bad for the shit his sister did to the kid, I guess.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis the kid they were extorting?\u201d Mac asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou do pay attention. He\u2019s one of \u2018em. The one that\u2019s got neighbors looking out for him. Like I said, the boy\u2019s not all there. He thinks it\u2019s legit, that he\u2019s \u2018paying their salaries\u2019.\u201d Gabe shook her head. \u201cHe picked that up from his neighbor, that us regular citizens pay cops\u2019 salaries. Those two fuckheads took advantage of that to get him to pay every week.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac\u2019s eyes were hard. \u201cWho\u2019s the client then, if he thinks it\u2019s legit?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe neighbors. They look after him on the day to day sorta stuff, more like family than any of his blood. They wanted to sue these guys and got a lawyer and everything. He took one look at Richie and refused to put him on the stand. The stuffed shirt had a point - any lawyer worth half his salt could have Richie confessing to being the one extorting the cops with a few seconds cross.\u201d Gabe looked out the window. The cabbie was making decent time at least. She willed the car to go a little faster anyway.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo they needed evidence.\u201d Mac put the pieces together himself.<br /> <br /> Gabe nodded. \u201cThe lawyer thought it was enough, but a judge threw it out. She\u2019s probably dirty too. The whole damn precinct seems to be. But those two got a few days suspension without pay and didn\u2019t appreciate that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac gave her a wry smile. \u201cWhile we\u2019re being so open, I don\u2019t suppose you wanna tell me your source?\u201d Gabe just looked at him. \u201cDidn\u2019t think so.\u201d<br /> <br /> When they got there, Mac gave the driver the twenty and a decent tip besides. Richie wasn\u2019t at him food stand and the street was empty. Too empty. The rain that had been threatening all afternoon started, a few drops at first but quickly picking up steam.<br /> <br /> Mac and Gabe both heard the voices in the alley, and they both moved to the edge of it, Mac fiddling with something in his pocket as the peered around the corner. Richie was on the ground, his paper \u2018cook\u2019s hat\u2019 next to him, disintegrating in the rain. He looked up at the cops, his lip quivering. \u201cI... I paid your salary. I did, I remember, I counted. I\u2019m good at counting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou fucking idiot.\u201d The taller one brandished his piece. \u201cYou paid alright. Then you went and told you fucking busybody friend, and he got us suspended. They took my gun and my badge. I don\u2019t like it when people take my gun or my badge.\u201d<br /> <br /> Richie sniffled, smearing mud on his face as he tried to wipe it. \u201cBut you have your gun. It\u2019s right there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s right.\u201d The other feinted towards him, causing Richie to start backwards and hit his head. \u201cWe\u2019ve got your guns and we\u2019re gonna blow your simpleton head off with them and leave enough drugs to make sure everyone knows about what you and your food truck were selling.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe we\u2019ll even show up at your funeral, just to let your nosy fucking neighbor know that now he\u2019s paying our salary.\u201d The tall one cocked his gun.<br /> <br /> Richie rubbed his head. \u201cNo. I don\u2019t do drugs. They\u2019re bad for you. And I don\u2019t have guns either.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I\u2019ve heard enough Rogers.\u201d Gabe\u2019s eyes widened as Mac stepped into the alley. He had a gun out, leveled on the taller one. \u201cYou are under arrest. You and Valentine both.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNolan.\u201d Rogers narrowed his eyes at him. \u201cEven better. I had to shoot the moron, he shot my good pal Nolan. Reads even better for the press. They hate cop killers here.\u201d He gave Valentine a nod and Mac looked nervous, moving his gun between the two.<br /> <br /> Gabe stepped into the alley beside him, covering Valentine. Mac smiled, not taking his eyes off Rogers. \u201cAre we good pals? I sure hope not. I\u2019ll feel bad when I forget to send you a birthday card in prison.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re new in town, Nolan. It\u2019s my word against yours. And I\u2019ve got lots of friends. So I\u2019ll tell you what...\u201d Rogers sneered at the two of them. \u201cWalk away. Forget you ever saw this, you and the bitch with the gun.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2018We\u2019ve got your guns and we\u2019re gonna blow your simpleton head off with them and leave enough drugs to make sure everyone knows about what you and your food truck were selling.\u2019 The somewhat tinny recording was just loud enough to hear over the now-pounding rain. Mac put the pen-recorder back in his pocket. \u201cActually, it\u2019s your word against yours.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou little bitch...\u201d Valentine ground his teeth.<br /> <br /> Rogers held a hand out to stop him. \u201cYou got the upper hand this time Nolan. But this isn\u2019t anyway to make friends. And if you think I\u2019m gonna be in a cell for long... you\u2019re as soft in the head as Richie there.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac handcuffed both of them as Gabe helped Richie up, encouraging him to pack up and go home for the day. The kid smiled happily at her and agreed.<br /> <br /> Mac watched him go, smiling at Gabe. \u201cThanks for the assist. I\u2019ll be sure to talk you up...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, no, nonono.\u201d Gabe waved her hands. \u201cFlatfoot or not, <u>you</u> are a decent guy. But I\u2019m a PI - me and the bulls don\u2019t always get along anyway. Sometimes I\u2019ll run into a public dick that\u2019s not you, and there\u2019s no way I wanna be that bitch that collars dirty cops when that happens. No way, no how.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThose two are just some bad eggs, Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gabe grinned at him. \u201cYou\u2019re just adorable Mac. But no. If I\u2019m your friend, leave me out of that shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDone and done.\u201d Mac returned her grin. \u201cPal.\u201d<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Next week we get our next journal, see you then.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:33:39-07:00","id":860333,"title":"","content":"Thanks. &quot;You\u2019re just adorable Mac.&quot; Truth, as is this story.<br /> <br /> Question: Is Fulgar still semi-active? How do you handle characters in between large player gaps? Are they up to background stuff, or do they just exist in limbo?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T12:32:10-07:00","id":860484,"title":"","content":"Fulger is semi-active, just living his cover. His player is two hours away and his car is not reliable enough to get down here. When that changes, hopefully Fulger will get more active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T00:01:47-07:00","id":862486,"title":"","content":"Bonus Gabe story above. Check it.<br /> <br /> There is a new case to investigate, but also an alligator murder. Wait\u2026alligator murder?<br /> <br /> <i>Session XXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Jack got to Terry\u2019s place quickly. He made his way up to the room number Terry had given him and walked in on some fuck rummaging through the living room. He could hear 2 people bickering in the bedroom. After ducking his head in to make sure neither were Terry, he drew his goddamn gun and banged on the door frame. \u201cEverybody - get the fuck out!\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry fucking ambled out of the bathroom and looked at him reproachfully. \u201cYou know I have to live here, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes, but otherwise ignored him, gesturing the other fuckers towards the door. They left, with a pile of shirts and a pretty goddamn nice looking wristwatch between them. Once they were gone, the fixer put his gun up, but left it visible. \u201cHow long ago did he die?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat one, or that one?\u201d Terry shrugged towards the bed and the living room.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe one with the bullets.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry looked up at the ceiling like he was doing fucking math in his goddman head. \u201cTwenty minutes ago.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOK, we have about ten, then.\u201d Jack nodded, satisfied.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I pee in here?\u201d A man stood in the doorway.<br /> <br /> Jack moved so the gun in his belt was visible from the door. \u201cNo.\u201d The guy at the door fucked off.<br /> <br /> The fixer moved back into the bedroom, using Synthesis to get an idea of what the goddamn hell had gone on. Most of the place was a fucking wreck to that sense as well, but the looters had left the bed and its morbid contents relatively untouched, so Jack was able to pick out the movements of the alligator as it slipped between the sheets and ambushed the sleeping man. He focused a little more, reaching further back, and was able to pinpoint the first thing taken from the room - a briefcase, at about the same time as the goddamn alligator attack.<br /> <br /> \u201cUh... the alligator\u2019s in there,\u201d Terry pointed out, his eyes flickering back and forth between Jack and the goddamn bathroom. The other man waved him away as he picked through the shambles, finding an empty envelope addressed to one H. Crumb, but nothing else with potentially identifying information on it.<br /> <br /> He was dialing Vivian\u2019s number when another couple of fucks showed up at the door. They waved slightly, catching Terry\u2019s attention, then pointed at the dead body in the living room. \u201cYou using that?\u201d He shrugged and they nodded their thanks.<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes and greeted Vivian. \u201cHey. So, what kinda jolt am I looking for to knock out a...\u201d He trailed off as he moved to the bathroom door and peeked in. The alligator hissed at him. \u201c... a 600 pound alligator without killing it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat does provide an interesting word problem for a human child with the knowledge of the conductive capacity of reptile flesh, but why not simply punch it? I believe, given your abilities, that is more likely to achieve your stated goal.\u201d Vivian sounded fucking distracted.<br /> <br /> Jack explained the situation. \u201cIt does look like it was a premeditated murder/theft kinda deal.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cAlligators are rarely weapons of opportunity, I\u2019ve found. I can help out with whatever data collection and analysis you might need, but not for a bit. I have a lunch date.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. I\u2019ll knock it out until tomorrow. It seems safest,\u201d Jack considered out loud.<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue.\u201d Vivian smiled. \u201cIf it wakes up too early, Ms. Pombal will be quite unhappy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks Kilroy.\u201d Jack hung up and turned to Terry. \u201cWe need duct tape.\u201d Terry patted around his pants for a second before pulling a squashed roll from his goddamn cargo pocket. \u201cAlright, here\u2019s the plan - you hold it, and I\u2019ll punch.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry\u2019s eyes went wider. \u201cI knew I woke up this morning for a reason. I need to start drinking.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack led the way into the fucking bathroom. \u201cYou should talk to Speed about that. It\u2019s always best to learn from a master.\u201d<br /> <br /> As the two men moved closer, the alligator took a snap at Terry, catching nothing but air. The mechanic fucking pounced on it, flailing around like a goddamn maniac and grabbing ahold of a few scaly patches, but he wasn\u2019t able to pin it the hell down. Still, he distracted it enough that Jack was able to catch it on the chin and the alligator went limp.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, duct tape!\u201d Terry\u2019s eyes lit up as he caught onto Jack\u2019s intentions. He started wrapping the alligator\u2019s snout in the stuff, saying \u201cAll of its head\u201d over and over in a goddamn sing-song voice. Jack gave a sideways look as the fixer made sure there were airholes. Terry smiled at him and pulled a marker out of his pocket to put a fucking smiley face mouth on the tape.<br /> <br /> Then Jack called me. \u201cHey Gabe. Are you sober? Cause you\u2019re about to not be...\u201d<br /> <br /> I missed his last sentence as I almost spit out my whiskey. \u201cHow the goddamn hell did you get Jack\u2019s phone? He fucking knows better than that shit. He\u2019s met me!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe need a ride.\u201d He paused. \u201cMe, Terry and an alligator.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSince when does sober enter into...\u201d My brain took a moment to catch up to what he said. \u201cAn alligator? Is that a fucking euphemism?\u201d<br /> <br /> From the background, I could hear Terry talking. \u201cIt\u2019s oddly cute when it\u2019s sleeping.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGo get a rug Terry,\u201d Jack sent the mechanic off. \u201cNo euphemisms. There\u2019s been an alligator murder and we need transport for our key witness.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor fuck\u2019s sake. Where the hell are you?\u201d I finished off my goddamn whiskey.<br /> <br /> He gave me an address in the bad part of town. \u201cIt\u2019s Terry\u2019s building.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took a moment to plot out the fucking route. \u201cBe there in ten.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry had a rug thrown over his shoulder and was about to open the door when his doorbell rang. Outside the door when he opened it were two people of indeterminate gender, wearing loose robes and goddamn plague doctor masks. \u201cHello brother. It seems you are not worshiping the false gods today. Would you like to hear about entropy and the end of all things?\u201d Terry blinked at them. \u201cSurely, brother, you have seen what humanity is like, living here.\u201d The cultist gestured down the hallway. \u201cDo you not long to see it end?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis? I mean, this is just a little urban blight. It\u2019s not that bad. The ceilings don\u2019t leak much. And I kinda like the alligator, despite everything.\u201d Terry gave their proposition serious fucking thought.<br /> <br /> The other one spoke up. \u201cDo you have an alligator problem, brother?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry nodded, looking like he\u2019d come to a goddamn epiphany. \u201cYeah, now that you mention it.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two cultists looked at one another. \u201cIf you had a tank, or some way to store it, we could take it off your hands?\u201d the first one offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll consider it. Do you have a card? Or a pamphlet?\u201d Terry looked back and forth between the two of them.<br /> <br /> The second one dug around for a card, finding one just as Jack came up. \u201cGabe\u2019s on the... what the fuck?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry put a fucking finger to his lips. \u201cShh... I\u2019m learning about the false gods, shh...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat false god?\u201d Jack narrowed his eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cZ. False gods. The ones we\u2019re not supposed to worship. Now shh, they\u2019re just getting to the good part.\u201d<br /> <br /> The cultists looked somewhat nervously at Jack as the one handed over the fucking card. \u201cHave a good day brother, until there are no more.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry looked over the card as they left. \u201cTemple of the Endless Void.\u201d He showed it to Jack. \u201cSee that font on there? And it\u2019s got texture.\u201d He shook it at the fixer. \u201cThere weren\u2019t $9.99 for 100. These people are going places. I\u2019m new, I need contacts.\u201d Jack shot a goddamn dubious look down the hallway. \u201cHey, Dude McHalfy just got chomped. By an alligator! I need all the friends I can get.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> When I showed up a few minutes later, I caught the robes coming downstairs, discussing a pair of fucking Madonna tickets. Their hop-skip step at the landing warned me about the goddman puddle of vomit, so I suppose I owed them a thank you or some shit. I opened the door to Terry\u2019s floor carefully, trying not to lose them another set of hinges. Thankfully, I didn\u2019t run into any goddamn trouble. \u201cJesus fuck Terry. I know cardboard boxes better than this shit.\u201d I took in the blood smear that started at the center of the living room and petered out at the doorway. Jack was stuffing hair clippings from the dead body in the bedroom into a blood soaked pillowcase, and Terry was dragging a rolled up carpet through another blood smear. \u201cSafer too.\u201d<br /> <br /> A knock on the door interrupted us. We closed the door to the bedroom and let Terry answer. An older looking man smiled pleasantly at him. \u201cI\u2019m moving into the building and I\u2019m legally obligated to inform you that I am a sex offender.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry nodded and the man nodded back and moved to go, but Jack stopped him. \u201cWhat number?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. 314. Have a good day.\u201d The old man left to knock on more doors.<br /> <br /> \u201c...let\u2019s get the goddamn fuck out of here.\u201d I looked to Jack.<br /> <br /> \u201cGator. Pillowcases. Car. Lab.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow at him. \u201cComplete sentences?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cIt\u2019s been a day. Let\u2019s go.\u201d<br /> <br /> By this point the police had finally fucking showed up. They weren\u2019t in any goddamn rush to come inside though. As we got to the door, we could hear one of the bulls talking to dispatch while the other watched YouTube videos on his laptop. \u201cAre you sure you\u2019re sure the call was for this place? Certain sure?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI got this.\u201d Terry shouldered the rug over onto Jack and I and we staggered a bit until we managed to balance it between us. \u201cLeave it to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhoa whoa whoa.\u201d I grabbed his goddamn sleeve. \u201cWhat are you going to do?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cIf they care...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re gonna care.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThen I\u2019ll tell them it\u2019s my dog and we\u2019re taking it to the vet!\u201d He beamed, proud as a fucking four year old that had just shit in the toilet for the first time.<br /> <br /> I rested my head on the rug. \u201cWrapped in a carpet?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded, then put his hand to his mouth like he was telling a goddamn secret. \u201cHe has the mange. Just horrible.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cLook, man, you live here. Go give a report like a good fucking citizen. Embellish is you need to. Just stand on the other goddamn side of them from my car. For fuck\u2019s sake.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do need to meet the police. They\u2019ll probably be here a lot.\u201d He nodded resolutely and walked over there, sticking his hand out. \u201cName\u2019s Terry McTavert. I live here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. I\u2019m sorry.\u201d The cop looked genuinely sympathetic. \u201cDid you call in the gunshots, alligator attack or the possible cannibalism?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shook his head. \u201cNo but I did see the alligator.\u201d<br /> <br /> The cop rubbed his head. \u201cIt\u2019d been comparatively quiet since we caught the toilet rapist - that\u2019s a guy who rapes toilets.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry sketched a goddamn salute. \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019re here to help people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRumor was it was built on an Indian burial ground. The original building burned down in \u201868 after a whole big human sacrifice scandal.\u201d The flatfoot looked fucking concernedly at him. \u201cHow many locks do you have?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAll of them.\u201d Terry nodded. \u201cI\u2019m out most of the time and don\u2019t keep any valuables in here either.\u201d<br /> <br /> The bull clapped him on the shoulder. \u201cThat\u2019s a good plan. D\u2019you know, there was a group here who rented rooms to homeless people, for free, so long as they brought them a person a month.\u201d He shook his head. \u201cWas there really an alligator?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry looked around fucking nervously. \u201cI heard hissing...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow far could it have gotten?\u201d The cop turned to his partner.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh they move fast. Make sure not to run in zig zags. Just run faster than your friend,\u201d Terry advised.<br /> <br /> By that time, we\u2019d managed to get the goddamn alligator into the back seat. Jack sat in the back with it as I pulled around the corner. Terry took his leave and hopped in the front as I gunned it the hell home.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vivian held the door open for Shelley, a fucking hopeful smile in her face. Shelley returned the smile. It was clear she was trying to keep some distance there. They made small talk waiting for their food, a little awkwardly, and after a while, Shelley sighed. \u201cI like you Vivian, but... I\u2019m not looking to be Bonnie and Betty here. I need long term stability, or at least the possibility of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes it help that it usually doesn\u2019t work like that? Mostly I do work with computers, you know.\u201d Vivian asked hopefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, what happened this time?\u201d Shelley looked down, not meeting Vivian\u2019s eyes.<br /> <br /> Vivian looked goddamn regretfully at her girlfriend. \u201cWe got some serious heat and... an ally was in serious danger. We had to skip town to cover for her, really.\u201d<br /> <br /> Things went quiet for a moment. Vivian kept the hopeful look on her face while Shelley focused on her food, eventually glancing up. \u201cI still... we can still be together. We\u2019ll just need time to get to where we were again.\u201d She smiled, more warmly. \u201cDinner tomorrow?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI understand.\u201d Vivian nodded, beaming. \u201cI can change. I already have, by coming back. Usually... well, I\u2019ve changed. You\u2019re special.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want to be the bad guy here...\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian reached for Shelley\u2019s hand. \u201cYou\u2019re not. I am. That\u2019s the problem. But I am willing to change.\u201d They shared a warm smile and finished off their lunch, keeping the conversation light and cheerful.<br /> <br /> <br /> Terry slung the alligator over his shoulder, swaying a little to get his fucking balance. As we walked through the door, Naomi jumped out, grabbing me into a big hug from behind. \u201cLook out, there\u2019s a spider on your back!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHello Naomi.\u201d I rolled my goddamn shoulders.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, the stuff with Penelope\u2019s sister Marjorie is done. I removed all the cancer and it\u2019s going in a box. She\u2019s called Nikka to renegotiate tonight.\u201d She slid off my back. \u201cYou know, helping people feels good.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put my hand to her forehead. \u201cYou feeling feverish?\u201d<br /> <br /> She stuck her fucking tongue out at me as she followed us up to the lab. \u201cSo what\u2019s with the rug?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged and leaned against the goddamn wall. \u201cIt was the best thing in Terry\u2019s shithole apartment to carry an alligator in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll have you know, everything about my house is structurally sound,\u201d Terry ob