mply have to make do with whatever they bring to the lab.<br /> <br /> Shelly does not appear to arrived yet. This is not cause for concern. I am twenty-three minutes early and her thoughts last night were concerned with how we would resolve things, not if.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W46-7T12:41-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> While women are not Shelly's primary romantic or sexual interest, she is not approaching her relationship with Vivian as an experiment or fling. She has made it clear that while she remains strongly attracted to Vivian, she is unwilling to proceed without at least the possibility of a long term commitment.<br /> <br /> She seemed conflicted and some of her statements seemed almost as much for herself as for Vivian. It seems logical to conclude that Vivian is not the first individual with an air of danger and mystery to draw her interest. And given the general incompatibility of such traits with the sort of stable future Shelly also desires, Vivian would not be the first to drag her into an emotional roller-coaster until either abandoning her or the toll in heartache forces her to.<br /> <br /> As Vivian, I offered her assurances. I explained without going into enough detail to compromise her about what had happened. It was a little difficult to justify certain aspects without explaining the Clairvoyance or making it seem unsafe, but I believe that my version satisfied her. She seemed accepting of me leaving details intentionally vague but not completely comfortable. It seems likely if she did even a cursory search that she is aware of Vivian's past but if so she was not prepared to address it yet. My suspicion is that she desires the truth, but also fears that it will make things untenable.<br /> <br /> However, if there is to be anything resembling the happy ever after she wishes for, there must be at least the appearance of honest communication between her and Vivian. To that end, at some point when we are in a sufficiently controlled and private setting, I shall explain the truth to her and judge her ability to handle and accept it. I will most likely need to edit her memories to a version of it that she can mentally and emotionally accept. However, once I have established the version of the truth she can deal with, I will then maintain that with her.<br /> <br /> It is a bit more involved and complex than I might otherwise desire for a cover life, but I find that I rather enjoy the intimacy and the idea of Vivian Marley finding someone that she could let inside her emotional defenses and settle down with happily pleases me better than the ending her life actually came to. It is still nothing but a pleasant fiction, of course, but then all of reality is for humans.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W46-7T18:43-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> I really do not believe Markizel understands how serious Clytemnestra is about consuming him. It seems to be related to his overall difficulty in grasping the nuances of human interaction. I believe the root of this is that his purpose as an angel was apparently focused entirely on dealing with mechanical entities which are considerably more logical in their behaviors. Also, he has not had a great deal of time since his fall to adjust and learn. However, I feel confident that he will be able to as he is possessed of a refreshingly strong intellect. Provided, of course, that Clytemnestra does not devour him first. I should take action to insure that is prevented. <br /> <br /> His skills in the lab are quite respectable. Together, we were able to run a DNA analysis on the victim as well as run a broad spectrum chemical panel on the blood and tissue samples. The samples were positive for recent cocaine use, consistent with there being a quantity of it in the apartment.<br /> <br /> Once we had completed the basic tests, I settled in to secure access to some of the more likely DNA databases to see if I could find a match. As luck would have it, I did get a hit. The victim is one Harold V Crumb, listed as Virgil Crumb on all but the most inflexible records. <br /> <br /> Mr Crumb was a criminal defense attorney who'd made a name for himself and leveraged it into a position in corporate law with Smittz and Horowitz. This raised further questions concerning the location of the crime, though the most logical conclusion is that the hole in the wall apartment was a place of anonymity.<br /> <br /> My search did reveal a potential suspect. Mr Crumb had recently divorced his supermodel wife on the grounds that he believed she was trying to kill him. While it seems too straightforward (even with an alligator as a murder weapon) Rhoda Crumb is most likely worth investigating.<br /> <br /> There was also some discussion and speculation as to the unusual method. As my compatriots discovered, transporting an alligator is not easy, even in such a strange location. Why would someone go to such trouble? Where did they manage to acquire a full grown alligator in Seattle? Theories were put forth. Speed suggested it might be a forensic countermeasure. It's not an unreasonable possibility, but it returns to the fact that none of us could put forth a reason that some far less complicated method would have been equally effective at accomplishing.<br /> <br /> In any event, the alligator himself seems likely to be the best route to follow. I believe Quietus intends to attempt to use an embed to communicate with it. If successful, this could provide excellent insight into the situation.<br /> <br /> However, further efforts will have to wait until tomorrow. Our client Nikka is going to be at Kiki's tonight. She is concerned about Naomi's friend 'Penalope' backing out of a deal to acquire a lung for her sister. And we cannot allay her suspicions without revealing that Clytemnestra took the girl's cancer as part of a pact.<br /> <br /> Also, even if we know the meeting is not actually suspect, there is a chance her stalker may put in an appearance. So we shall need to be prepared. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W46-7T21:29-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> Speed did not join the surveillance at Kiki's. I believe she and Miranda went to attempt to retrieve the Infrastructure from the Mothman theater. I know Quietus maintained contact with her so I believe it went uneventfully.<br /> <br /> So far it has been an interesting evening for people watching and familiarizing Markizel with some of the local players.<br /> <br /> The mysterious vampire that was setting angels on fire after the Waterwheel was there with the 'Mustard Gas Breathing Motherfuckers' as Speed has so eloquently dubbed them. He was meeting with Dieter who had brought Langley Fitzgerald along. Langley was in a Willy Wonka outfit (classic Gene Wilder, of course) and as seems to be something of a pattern for him he'd modified it to be ass-less. Langley does have a fetching posterior and as they say, when one has it one should flaunt it.<br /> <br /> Also present was Carla Pierce with a previously unknown man in leathers. Kiki took an interest in them, crawling across the ceiling with her hair obscuring her face and settling above them. I do not believe anyone beside us noticed her. And shortly after she'd taken up her perch, Respectable Ping's man Two Chin and a woman who's no doubt colorful nom de guerre is currently unknown to us came in to join Mrs Pierce.<br /> <br /> So far I have put out some feelers among Vivian's more criminal connections hinting that she has information that could prove useful to whoever holds Kiki's. We shall see what it brings. At some point, I really should speak to Kiki and insure that certain ground rules are established before she begins to exact her vengeance. I cannot see where she would have cause to harm Shelley, but I rather suspect that she may not see a need to avoid doing so in the pursuit of her goals. I need to make sure she is aware that Shelley and Vivian are under Billy Mack's protection. Of course, I shall need to be Billy Mack for such a conversation, so it must wait.<br /> <br /> Nikka's stalker is not present, though we will remain until she has finished holding court. Also, it seems Robin Graves will be joining us so she can meet Markizel. He's rather determined to do something about the unfavorable manner that the Rain City Mafia views us. While they would make strong allies and our aims do seem quite compatible, I am not sure they are terribly receptive. But Ms Graves is the best disposed toward us and thus the best place to begin building relations.<br /> <br /> The Fogmen are clearly very knowledgeable about the Underworld and matters of the soul. I do wonder if they might have some insights into Mr Ox. Also, that matter has raised some doubts about Vivian Marley's soul. I have believed that the soul pact destroyed her, but if not then do I now possess her soul, or whatever remains of it? It is a mostly academic question, it will not alter the pact. But I cannot help but wish to understand the deeper ramifications and questions of the soul's disposition after such a pact. Tonight may not be the best time for an in depth discussion. That is likely also a task better suited to Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> What Vivian Marley has been quite well suited for is a bit of light flirting with Shelley, who has made sure to swing by even though we are not in her area. She seems more relaxed after our conversation this afternoon, and I have enjoyed our banter so far. I am very much looking forward to tomorrow night's date. Even as perfect as my memories of our previous encounters are, I am looking forward to exploring the textures of her skin and hair and the unique scent and taste of her body chemistry once more.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Creepy, Kilroy.<br /> <br /> You can more or less assume Markizel has the old \u201cWierdness Magnet\u201d flaw, at the players request. Strange, random things seem to happen to him, and some are frankly bizarre. The overall tone of the game is not shifting, but sometimes, well, sometimes odd things happen with him.<br /> <br /> Like an alligator murder, apparently.<br /> <br /> OOC, there is very little danger of Clytemnestra eating Markizel. IC, she absolutely is planning to when she thinks she can get away with it. He will probably grow on her first. She has a soft spot for Psychopomps\u2026Speed being her closest friend and Kayla being the lover of the actual Unchained not Cover.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s all that comes to mind, Speed\u2019s player tends to be thorough. But comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-23T13:59:54-07:00","id":872630,"title":"","content":"Damnit Terry, you are not allowed to make any more friends. Damnit Liz now is not the time. While nothing explicit happens, the language is unusually explicit due to that one guy. You\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XL</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> \u2018The End\u2019 started playing over the speakers as Robin walked in. Liz waved her over. Jack fixated on the man who came in after her, wearing a \u2018Pussy Inspector\u2019 shirt and a long raincoat with no pants showing below his coat. The fucker didn\u2019t come anywhere near our client or their table, so Jack focused on Robin again.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s great to see you.\u201d Liz smiled intimately at Robin as she moved over to give the Sin-eater room.<br /> <br /> Robin returned the smile fucking hesitantly. \u201cWe, uh, need to talk, Liz.\u201d She looked around the table. \u201cLater.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked between the two of them. \u201cHey, Robin. Thanks for not letting Sharon do whatever she does with a shotgun.\u201d He nodded at Terry. \u201cThis is the new guy, Terry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think you\u2019re new too?\u201d Robin asked Vivian.<br /> <br /> \u201cVivian. I\u2019m just a contractor, I work with the Night Train agency sometimes.\u201d Vivian looked up from her computer briefly.<br /> <br /> Robin glanced to Liz and got a nod. Then she took Liz\u2019s hand off her knee, putting it on the goddamn table. \u201cSo what do you guys need to know?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry looked from side to fucking side, then leaned in. \u201cI wanted to formally, cordially offer the services of us... robot folks, to make an alliance.\u201d Jack groaned, putting his head in his hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t call you that, I understand you don\u2019t like it.\u201d Robin eyed Jack.<br /> <br /> Terry nodded, eyes goddamn wide. \u201cI understand you\u2019ve met some of the misguided others, the broken ones. I want to make amends for them, to try and help you guys out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin bit her lip. \u201cThe Burning Man really doesn\u2019t like your kind.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know! That\u2019s what I want to fix.\u201d Terry grinned, wild eyed.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve been trying to keep you guys separate because I don\u2019t want you at risk. He already thinks I spend too much times with you...\u201d Robin began.<br /> <br /> Liz\u2019s face was fucking stormy. \u201cHow the fuck is it his business?\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin looked warily at her. \u201cLiz...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe want to show we\u2019re different.\u201d Vivian broke in.<br /> <br /> Robin looked away from Liz. \u201cI have been telling him that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz frowned. \u201cSo how close are you two?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot right now, Liz, please.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think we do need to talk about this right now.\u201d Liz crossed her arms, a goddamn set look on her face.<br /> <br /> Terry snapped his fingers over the table. \u201cMore business, less relationship.\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin focused on him, a fucking thankful look in her eye. \u201cI can suggest a sit down. We don\u2019t compete or anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight! I\u2019ve never even met a ghost. Well, only one.\u201d Terry looked up at Kiki who was still focused on the pair of Tong fucks.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh fuck.\u201d Robin sighed heavily.<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged. \u201cShe\u2019s friendly to us.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head, eying the ghost. \u201cThis is bigger than \u2018to us\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe just wants vengeance on the people who killed her. It seems fair,\u201d Jack argued.<br /> <br /> \u201cGhosts sometimes have a liberal interpretation of things. Are those the ones who did it? Cause she seems pretty focused on them.\u201d Robin kept looking at the ghost, trying like hell to ignore Liz\u2019s stare.<br /> <br /> Jack leaned back in his seat. \u201cWe\u2019ll keep an eye out. Look, what do I have to do to get my passport stamped or something so I don\u2019t get shot whenever I go into the Underworld?\u201d<br /> <br /> That brought Robin\u2019s attention back to him. \u201cWhy do you need to go into the Underworld?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack started to list things out, counting on his fucking fingers. \u201cTo escape Angels, or the police or evil car/murder hybrid spirits. Mostly to escape, I guess.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t forget \u2018just cause we can\u2019,\u201d Terry offered goddamn helpfully. Jack flipped him off.<br /> <br /> Robin glanced at Liz, then away quickly. \u201cIt is our job to keep the living and the dead apart.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack frowned. \u201cWe\u2019re not messing with any ghosts.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. But when a heavily armed someone walks through a playground...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstood.\u201d Vivian nodded. \u201cWhat can we do to smooth that out, and let out peaceful intentions known?\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin thought for a moment. \u201cWell, I don\u2019t mind. Sharon hates everyone equally, but I can probably bring her around. I\u2019ll... I\u2019ll talk to the Burning Man.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz made a fucking disbelieving noise. \u201cYou\u2019ll talk to him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan you not make this harder?\u201d Robin shook her head, looking away. \u201cI am willing to be an advocate here, and I really do think I can bring Sharon around. Unfortunately, she did figure out you guys can feel pain, so...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked confused. \u201cHuh?\u201d<br /> <br /> They went back and forth for a bit, with Robin dancing around it. Finally she sighed, throwing her goddamn hands up. \u201cShe likes causing pain, OK?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood, you are capable of saying things outright.\u201d Liz raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cLiz!\u201d Robin looked unhappily at her.<br /> <br /> She looked away. \u201cI\u2019m waiting my turn.\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin\u2019s eyes dropped to the table. \u201cCan we not do this tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, we\u2019re talking tonight.\u201d Liz\u2019s tone was goddamn definite.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo.\u201d Terry put his hand down on the table sharply. \u201cBusiness?\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll do what I can to arrange a sit down talk in a neutral location. For what it\u2019s worth, I\u2019m certain he won\u2019t betray you. He\u2019ll might not agree, but he\u2019ll say so outright.\u201d She sighed. \u201cWe certainly don\u2019t want any enemies we don\u2019t need.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry pointed at her significantly. \u201cRight! And we don\u2019t need any. Any enemy can be a friend!\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rubbed his fucking forehead. \u201cI\u2019m gonna put you in a box when we get home.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd fix him?\u201d Vivian smiled playfully up at them over her laptop.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou? Come.\u201d Liz grabbed Robin\u2019s hand and pulled her to another fucking booth before making their conversation unable to be overheard. They argued for a short while before Liz began seducing the Sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Vivian looked back over at them, then closed her laptop slightly, looking at the scrawny fuck. \u201cYou do realize that Clytemnestra is truly intending to consume you? As in, kill you.\u201d He shrugged. \u201cYou need to tell her no, explicitly. You are a useful lab assistant, I would hate to lose your services.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMe too,\u201d Terry nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou contain two concepts of humanity, can you not talk like a human?\u201d Jack looked goddamn dubiously at Vivian.<br /> <br /> She looked confused. \u201cWhy?\u201d<br /> <br /> He opened his mouth to respond a few times, finally saying \u201cCause it\u2019s weird.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian was about to respond when Liz\u2019s table caught her fucking eye. Robin\u2019s clear resistance to Liz\u2019s advances had crumbled somewhat. Even still, the Sin-eater didn\u2019t look like she felt this was a goddamn good idea. \u201cI don\u2019t believe that is a positive development in our alliance efforts, given that it seemed fairly clear Robin and the Burning Man are involved.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShit.\u201d Jack looked over and tried texting Liz. She ignored it.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have an idea.\u201d Vivian sorted through the phones in front of her, finding her own and dialing Kayla.<br /> <br /> \u201cMoshi moshi,\u201d Kayla answered brightly.<br /> <br /> Vivian smiled, matching her Japanese. \u201cHello Ms. Liquor. We need to distract Clytemnestra.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kayla frowned. \u201cI\u2019m not in the habit of colluding against my girlfriend.\u201d Vivian explained the fucking situation. \u201cOh. I see. I can call, but... I\u2019m in Olympia.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA call will distract her, perhaps enough for Robin to escape,\u201d Vivian pointed out. She grimaced at the other table. \u201cLiz doesn\u2019t deal well with rejection.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHas she ever experienced it before?\u201d Kayla smiled.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, Liz\u2019s phone rang. She answered it, pressing Robin\u2019s face into her goddamn neck. After a moment, she hopped up and Robin took the hell out of