ales. And he handled being chased by Angels quite well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kayla kept staring. \u201cIt doesn\u2019t sound like he owes you anything.\u201d She shook her head. \u201cAre you more normal when you\u2019re a Japanese girl?\u201d<br /> <br /> We headed straight for the shore of the lake nearest our goddamn entrance point. Before we jumped in, we shifted forms, comfortably just far enough from the God Machine\u2019s direct eye. Jack and I just picked up a few modifications. The rest transformed completely into their demonic form, leaving Kilroy a little twitchy and Markizel reeking of goddamn chicken wings.<br /> <br /> Once we got out of the water, my phone started ringing. I raised an eyebrow at Esha\u2019s name on my caller ID. I answered as Clytemnestra scattered to get the lay of the fucking land. \u201cHey there doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe. It\u2019s been awhile,\u201d she purred.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt has. You get back alright?\u201d Jack gave me a look.<br /> <br /> She smiled. \u201cI have. The office here is all set up. I\u2019d like to show you around. Get dinner perhaps?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d like that.\u201d I smiled cockily. \u201cI\u2019m in the middle of a job right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTomorrow? 3 PM? That should be time to show your around the office, get dinner, then... see where things go.\u201d She paused. \u201cIt will be good to see you again - things have changed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled again. \u201cYou\u2019ll see.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess I will. You take care of yourself doll. I gotta jet.\u201d<br /> <br /> I ignored Jack\u2019s amused goddamn glances until Clytemnestra got back and reformed. \u201cI don\u2019t want to exaggerate, understand, but there is a very large bee hovering above the honeycomb. Roughly the size of two human heads.\u201d She looked at Jack. \u201cIt\u2019s letting out a low hum. I can recreate it, if you can knock it out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack nodded and we snuck carefully in. We were helped out again by the fact that Ms. Crimson followed a pretty set patrol, and by the fact that many of us had the mirrored skin modification. In the end we all got filled the hell up, and a few filled cell phones besides.<br /> <br /> Once we were out of Ms. Crimson\u2019s fucking patrol path, Clytemnestra reformed and took a quick sip of Ms. Liquor. The woman made of bourbon yipped and dodged the hell away. \u201cYou\u2019re so cute when you dodge.\u201d Clytemnestra looked at me. \u201cAre we waiting around while Billy Mack has his booty call? I have bourbon to drink.\u201d Clytemnestra shifted back into Liz while Ms. Liquor shifted back into Kayla. As she did so, Liz pounced again, biting her goddamn neck. Kayla looked at her reproachfully when she let go. \u201cWhat? Everyone else was full...\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked to Kilroy. \u201cDo you really need a ride?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll find my own way home.\u201d Kilroy nodded,<br /> <br /> Terry looked goddamn grateful. \u201cI do have some cash to deal with.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kilroy turned to him. \u201cWe know a laundromat that might could use some attention.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was thinking some less literal laundering...\u201d Jack raised a fucking eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs was I - such places frequently have change machines.\u201d Billy Mack returned.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra nodded. \u201cThe 20s might cause a problem with those.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry looked goddamn inspired. \u201c20s! An ATM?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe cameras might cause a problem. Plus, you\u2019ll have trouble finding an ATM that doesn\u2019t associate an account with the physical deposit.\u201d Jack shrugged, thinking fucking hard.<br /> <br /> \u201cCameras can be broken, right?\u201d Terry suggested. \u201cI mean, without breaking the ATM.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack gave him a long suffering look. \u201cWhen I break thing, they\u2019re broke.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W47-1T01:47-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> I do wish Clytemnestra was better at reigning in her emotional insecurities. Jealousy is most unflattering and it would vex me to find myself at odds with this 'Rain City Mafia' over what I believe could be well described as High School drama. Apparently her hold over Mrs Graves was insufficient as a month of no contact was enough for Mrs Graves to form a relationship with her fellow Fogman and the head of their group, known only to us as The Burning Man. Unfortunate, but given that Mrs Graves is (or at least was before Clytemnestra's behavior tonight) still an ally, and our only one within this collection of Fogmen, it seems counterproductive and childish to react in such a manner. I was able to enlist Kayla's assistance in preventing Clytemnestra from taking things too far tonight but I fear that her irrational behavior will ultimately poison this Burning Man against us and ruin Quietus' desire to use the Underworld freely and Markizel's hopes for an alliance. It will also make it impossible for me to gather any information about Mr Ox and the actual state of Vivian's soul from them.<br /> <br /> And in the same vein, I further reiterated and explained in careful detail to Markizel that Clytemnestra's intention to consume him is deadly serious and that if he does not wish to be ended, he needs to make such perfectly clear to Clytemnestra. I believe he had been operating under the false (and very dangerous) belief that her behavior was playful. I believe I have cleared up this misconception.<br /> <br /> I am quite fond of Clytemnestra but I find her lack of emotional restraint frustrating. Not that the others do not have their own moments of irrational behavior. I simply do not understand why they all try so hard to be human when we are so much more than those we emulate and impersonate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W47-1T02:13-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> Markizel appears to have befriended a chaos spirit. More specifically, a human claimed by one. Phil (possibly also known as Chester) followed Nikka out of Kiki's and instituted a vigorous pursuit and somewhat surreal confrontation. In the end, Phil's intentions toward Nikka appear to have been relatively harmless and completely unrelated to the matter she hired us about. He desired sexual congress but showed no indications of hostility at being rejected. More importantly (as far as a chaos spirit can prioritize things) he seems to believe that she can help him locate the vortis that he came from. It seems likely that he wishes to bring more of his kind into the world.<br /> <br /> It was rather amusing to watch Markizel and Phil interact. Markizel truly fits all the stereotypes for a psychopomp and especially in this instance was driving Quietus to distraction. I really think it would do him a great deal of good to find an outlet for this tension. Perhaps I should take him out for a few rounds of racquetball or offer to engage in intercourse with him. He did seem quite comfortable making out with Vivian during our foray into the dorms. I need to see about proper precautionary supplies until I can make arrangements for a reliable and long term solution for insuring there is no undesired issue form my dalliances with Casey anyway. Also, I should see to making sure I have the requisite precautionary supplies for my new cover while I am at it.<br /> <br /> I must say, lesbian sex is refreshingly less complicated. I am starting to understand more clearly why Clytemnestra chose to limit Naomi's sexual preferences.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W47-1T09:53-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> Hugo the alligator has helpfully provided us with more information about the murder. The city is apparently home to a wild eyed man who walked Hugo in on a leash (oddly without raising any alarms?) and set him to his meal. It was not Hugo's first human victim. This would seem to beg the question of why our mystery alligator wrangler left him behind. Also, the possibility of this man returning to seek his missing pet (tool?) remains. At any rate, it appears that Quietus intends to keep the creature, though the lab is not particularly well-suited as a reptile habitat and Ms Pombal is decidedly not fond of Hugo. I suppose we shall have to find him a home.<br /> <br /> Mrs Liqueur has joined us today, both she and Clytemnestra are in good spirits though she is, not unexpectedly, low on aether and wishes to join our refueling run to the Diablo Dam Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W47-1T10:49-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> The trip to Diablo Lake was illegally swift and thanks to Speed's proficiency with driving uneventful. We took the opportunity to give both Mrs Liqueur and Markizel an explanation of the key players in the region and a security breakdown on Miss Crimson. The two began discussing fixing her, which while I am dubious of the means or success of such an endeavor I would not be at all opposed to having some sort of working arrangement with her. And I do suppose it is not entirely beyond the realm of possibility since it could be framed as being positive for the Infrastructure's integrity to allow us to collect what is nothing more than a waste byproduct to the God-Machine while avoiding a conflict that could result in damage to it.<br /> <br /> We entered through the lake as usual. Clytemnestra used her swarm form to scout and discovered that in addition to Miss Crimson patrolling the ceiling as usual, there was also a bee of exceptional size. Quietus knocked the bee out without harm and Clytemnestra used Vox to recreate it's droning while we charged our fill of the aether.<br /> <br /> Upon withdrawing, Speed asked if I could see to returning to the city on my own as the others were not inclined to wait while I caught up with Ganora and our cult. I assured her that I would be fine to see to it and they departed.<br /> <br /> It has been some time since I was able to safely visit my aquatic paramour I am most curious to see how the cult has progressed and to offer whatever assistance I can. I am also eager to visit my unborn child and, of course, to spend some intimate time with the mother of my spawn. There should be ample time for Ganora and I to satisfy our carnal appetites and still be back in the city proper for my date with Shelly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XL</i><br /> <br /> Quietus knocked the bee out with Knockout Punch, and Clytemnestra used Vox to mimic the buzz so there would not be a break in the white noise. I think everyone plans to pick Vox up at this point if they haven\u2019t already.<br /> <br /> Other than that, not much requires explanation. Speed shadowed Phil, and did so easily. He barely had a fraction of her successes. Phil is a Claimed, you can see some on them in the <b>Demon</b> rulebook and more in <i>Book of Spirits</i>. Purified are in <i>Chronicles of Darkness: Immortals</i>.<br /> <br /> It was a fun session. Phil\u2019s picture looks rather unbalanced without being over the top, and he certainly\u2026amused the group. As did Clytemnestra and Robin\u2019s interplay.<br /> <br /> On the journals, the phrase \u201cI must say, lesbian sex is refreshingly less complicated,\u2019 makes my eyebrow twitch. I know they were talking about birth control and pregnancy, but still.<br /> <br /> Well I think that is everyone, but Comments and Questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T15:40:45-07:00","id":884957,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for a return to the mean streets with the Night Train Detective Agency. In the interest of my readers, I need to make a couple notes before we start.<br /> <br /> \u201cPhil\u201d is a bad person. He says some bad things, including racist and scatological stuff this time. This is staying true to his nature as a Claimed of Madness or Chaos or whatever he actually is, but if that offends you I recommend skipping a lot of the conversation between he and Terry. The banter is not really required to understand what is going on, and little of what \u201cPhil\u201d says really makes much sense. This is restricted to him being an abject pottymouth, not doing much bad beyond grand theft auto and property damage, but still. Wanted to warn.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s journal story (which takes place that first night) draws on tropes of vampire fiction, and comes from the perspective of a predator actually able to read her partner\u2019s desires. Still, while there is not force, there is assuring that she knows what her partner wants, even if her partner denies it, and a very predatory/vampiric scene, though no rape (or even date rape) occurs. If this bothers you, again, it can be easily skipped. It is NOT intended to portray anything darker than a nod to something like Carmilla, but that is still coersive, so there is a disclaimer.<br /> <br /> Disclaimers done? Disclaimers done. Let\u2019s do this.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> When we got back to the office, Kayla stepped in close. She tugged on the points of my collar, straightening it out. \u201cSo, what are your plans for the afternoon?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked at her. \u201cWork, doll. I am one of the working stiffs here and we do have a goddamn agency to run.\u201d I quirked my head at her, raising a fucking eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cShame.\u201d She grinned back up at me.<br /> <br /> Liz shook her head, an amused smile playing over her lips. \u201cGabe, a word? In private?\u201d I shrugged and followed her back to the conference room. I spun a chair around to sit in it backwards, looking up at her expectantly. \u201cI don\u2019t want you to think I\u2019d be mad at you, or that it\u2019d be \u2018betraying\u2019 me somehow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI... sure. Thanks.\u201d I bit my lip, avoiding her eyes. Fucking timing. Dames would wait until I had a girlfriend to throw themselves at me. Then again, Miranda did make that comment about inviting Kayla to Ireland... \u201cI don\u2019t suppose she likes blondes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy dear Psychopomp friend.\u201d Liz raised an eyebrow, and sighed. \u201cWell, part of her attraction to you is her Thanatos impulse, since you\u2019re an alcoholic and she\u2019s made of booze. I don\u2019t know if Miranda will trip that trigger...\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cShame.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked at me goddamn seriously. \u201cI can ask her to stop, if it\u2019s upsetting you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head, grinning up at her. \u201cI\u2019m not about to ask a dame like that to stop fucking flirting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs you wish.\u201d She smiled back at me and inclined her head towards the main room.<br /> <br /> We wandered back out and Kayla looked between us quickly. \u201cShe didn\u2019t chew you out, did she?\u201d<br /> <br /> I winked at her. \u201cI am completely unchewed.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack and Terry came from the back with sodas. \u201cLook, Jack, you can\u2019t shoot all my friends.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWanna bet?\u201d Jack chugged the rest of his soda goddamn belligerently.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll save money not shooting everyone...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll start with you, so you don\u2019t have to worry about it.\u201d He glared at the scrawny fucker.<br /> <br /> Terry looked around wide eyed. \u201cGot anymore of that rich Corinthian leather?\u201d<br /> <br /> Kayla looked at Liz playfully. \u201cIs your leather Corinthian? In that outfit?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know. Maybe I should wear it again so you can get a better look.\u201d The look they shared was full of heat and Jack forgot what the hell he was about to yell next. Liz rolled her fucking eyes at him. \u201cSo what are people\u2019s plans? I have a personal project this evening.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smiled at her. \u201cI need to pick up a case of homelessness and unemployment.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you tried calling Speed a cunt?\u201d Liz asked archly. Jack and I stared at her. \u201cIt might help with the unemployment.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Terry looked down at the nicely printed business card, then up at the abandoned strip club, All signage had been removed at some point in the past, but the bleached out shadow behind the former sign stood out against the goddamn grimy walls, revealing that this used to be Ben Dover\u2019s House of Ass. The door was slightly ajar, bullet holes peppering the fucking door knob.<br /> <br /> Terry pushed it open tentatively, peering inside. The room just beyond was fucking bare. There was another, sturdier door across from the one he slipped in. On his left was a large bloodstained window with bulletproof glass. Terry eyed the scattered teeth underneath it, looking up slowly until he was looking at the face of a hooded figure in a gas mask.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you enlightened brother?\u201d The hooded figure spoke.<br /> <br /> \u201cI, uh, want to be?\u201d Terry looked between him and the door.<br /> <br /> The figure nodded. \u201cDo you have a card?\u201d Terry nodded and showed it to him. \u201cAre you a member of the police?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry shook his head quickly. \u201cNope. And I\u2019d have to tell you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can go in.\u201d The figure pointed at the inner door.<br /> <br /> The door opened creakily as Terry turned the handle. Just inside were two more hooded figures, these carrying goddamn rifles. Several more were sitting at tables around the stage. One of them, a short fuck, came up to Terry. \u201cCan I help you?\u201d she asked in a soft voice.<br /> <br /> Terry scratched his head. \u201cTwo brothers came by and told me about enlightenment, so I came seeking it.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and gestured towards the stage. He followed her and sat with her next to the blood-crusted stripped pole, avoiding the fucking bullet grooves. \u201cSo, the core of our beliefs - we, humans, have clearly had a negative impact on the planet. Mostly we\u2019re actively destroying it.\u201d She was on a fucking roll. \u201cIt\u2019s become all about Kardashians and not about caring. We don\u2019t know if it\u2019s possible to save th - the human race, but we\u2019re not so sure it\u2019s worth it. Better to start over.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, like a reboot?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes! The Master was playing Civilizations once, and he realized that when a polluted square was left alone long enough, the square returns to its pristine state. We want to let the whole earth return to the peaceful state until it is absorbed by the sun when it becomes a red dwarf.\u201d The hooded woman sighed goddamn happily. \u201cWe have plans to hasten the end, plans beyond a neonate, you understand. What skill set do you have to offer?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry looked around and shrugged. \u201cI went to school to become and engineer.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d She looked intrigued. \u201cWhat was your specialty?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cChemistry. Some physics.\u201d Terry looked ready to wax goddamn poetic about his studies.<br /> <br /> She cut him off. \u201cIf you were given access to a reactor, would you be able to start a meltdown? How long would it take?\u201d She held a finger up. \u201cThis isn\u2019t a current project, mind, we\u2019re just doing some thinking.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry thought for a moment. \u201cThat is a good way to start a reboot. 20, 30 minutes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSee, the thought is, if one was to hypothetically fire a missile in such a way that the American government thought it was from a foreign power, then one hypothetically timed a nuclear meltdown to coincide with when the missile should hit, we\u2019re thinking the reaction would, hypothetically, be quite significant. But one would have to have the skills, the manpower...\u201d The woman eyed him.<br /> <br /> \u201cI totally get it.\u201d Terry winked.<br /> <br /> She tilted her head. \u201cHave you had any thoughts as how to best quickly and as painlessly as possible eradicate humanity? It is appropriate for humans, who created the problem, to end it - we are always looking for ideas.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry tapped his chin, thinking. \u201cGMOs... poisonous bees?\u201d<br /> <br /> She pointed at him, nodding fucking approvingly. \u201cWe have something along those lines in the works, though I can\u2019t give any details. I do have a possible loyalty mission idea. Do you know what ricin is?\u201d Terry nodded. \u201cWe have a Russian brother, who\u2019s gotten ahold of a walking stick dart gun. It\u2019s not how ricin is commonly used, but we have the equipment for it and it\u2019s nearly untraceable. We can provide a picture and where we expect them to be. If you succeed, we\u2019ll know you\u2019re interested and willing to take risks.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry nodded. \u201cAlright...\u201d He trailed off, distracted by another hooded figure leading a fucking big dog from the champagne room. The mutt looked at Terry, narrowing its human eyes. The mechanic tried not to stare, but kept looking at it from the corner of his eye until the dog moved along, following its master.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you want us to call you?\u201d The woman asked, continuing quickly. \u201cPlease don\u2019t tell me your real name.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSammy. Your dog is pretty. I like dogs.\u201d Terry looked back to her, wide eyed.<br /> <br /> The dog\u2019s master looked over at him. \u201cUmm...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot like that.\u201d Terry nodded. \u201cThey\u2019ll inherit the earth, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Another robed, masked figure walked in carrying a stack of pizza boxes. The woman looked over to him. \u201cPapa John\u2019s?\u201d<br /> <br /> The new figure shifted the b