e\u2026don\u2019t\u2026\u201d Robin could no longer look away. She knew the Spider had her. Liz stepped into the doorway as well, looking deeply into Robin\u2019s eyes before pulling her into a kiss. Their union had an electricity Robin hungered for and desperately feared. Her knees buckled, and Liz caught her even as her other hand slipped up the back of her shirt. Robin felt tightness release from around her chest. Her head was spinning. Then, a small voice broke the reverie<br /> <br /> \u201cMom?\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLI</i><br /> <br /> So, what happened when the story ended?<br /> <br /> Short version: Liz and Robin had a long conversation. They are seeing each other but not in anything formal. Liz did not spend the night with Robin.<br /> Long version: Kaylee ended the seduction with her abrupt appearance. Robin introduced the two and put her daughter to bed. Liz waited in the kitchen, and Robin came back and they talked. Liz expressed frustration that Robin had not even contacted her, and that she believed right up until Robin admitted involvement with the Burning Man that they were in love. She was less concerned with Robin's involvement with the Burning Man than she was about Robin ending their relationship without a call, though the Burning Man being prone to anger sort of raised red flags. Robin admitted she had gotten caught up in things. She did not think The Burning Man was trying to break up she and Liz, but she was sure he suspected involvement.<br /> <br /> They decided, essentially, that they would see each other again. Nothing happened that night beyond that. The promise of rekindled romantic involvement is there. Robin promised to show if they set a date to meet, and Liz promised no seduction unless Robin invited her back to her place or accepts an invitation to Liz's place.<br /> <br /> Not much else to discuss. The cult plot is custom made for Terry, and it proved a good segue into some Mage business. The \u201cJunkyard Dogs\u201d