path.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T13:00:07-07:00","id":895647,"title":"","content":"Just Speed this time. But she pretty much covers things. Terry\u2019s player had to miss, and will miss the next one, because apparently when I start closing in on making your Cipher you have to miss, but good fun. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Terry got called away, so Naomi met Billy Mack at the Brand Corporation building, seeing as she was the only fucking other one of us lugs that Kim hadn\u2019t laid her peepers on. She gave me a cheeky goddamn grin as she changed and left to head over there. I rolled my eyes at her ensemble - an open hoodie over a shirt that read \u2018I didn\u2019t mean to turn you o\u0336n\u0336 gay\u2019, a pair of baggy pants and a toboggan.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack didn\u2019t raise an eyebrow when she showed up. \u201cAlways a pleasure, Ms. Cruz.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, yeah.\u201d Naomi followed him in, fucking slouching with her hands in her pockets.<br /> <br /> They went up to the fourth floor. It was a mirror of the 38th floor I had been on before, except the goddamn bulletproof aquarium that served as a wall was inhabited by angelfish instead of lionfish. At the end of the hallway was a heavy door, the camera above it trained on the approach. It was unlocked when they reached it and as it shut behind them, a collection of bolts slid home. Naomi gave Billy Mack a rueful look.<br /> <br /> Mr. Gone approached them, coming out of the office. \u201cYou would be associates of Ms. Norton?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWilliam McKenzie.\u201d The g-man showed him his PI license. Naomi smirked and waggled her fingers in a wave.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh yes. Adam Gone, esquire.\u201d The arrogant douchebag took out his phone and, with the push of a button, slid back the four bolts in three clusters, 1-2-1, that secured Crumb\u2019s office. Gone stood near the computer and the other two followed him in.<br /> <br /> Naomi perked up as she walked in, looking around alertly. Billy Mack frowned slightly, recognizing something fucking off in the room. It reminded him of the Abyssal intrusion, just less goddamn malicious. The g-man turned to the schmuck. \u201cWhat have you found so far?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone looked at him consideringly. \u201cNot much here. One interesting thing that we discovered was that a number of Crumb\u2019s passwords were changed within 48 hours. Particular files - personal, mundane seeming ones - are locked.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnfortunate.\u201d Billy Mack\u2019s brow furrowed. \u201cThese changes were made before his death, yes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is unfortunate, and quite unexpected. I can only imagine he did change them before his death. They would either have had to be made from here, or it would have required significant coordination. Only I and one other have been in here since.\u201d Gone glanced over at Naomi.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cWas he frequently this cautious?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone thought for a fucking moment. \u201cSomewhat. Not to this extent however. Some of these files were even on a shared drive, and no changes made it to the log. It is highly unusual.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHas anything unusual happened here recently?\u201d Billy Mack looked around.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot to my knowledge,\u201d Gone smiled, \u201cbut I was on vacation.\u201d His smile faded somewhat. \u201cI heard about Mr. Crumb\u2019s passing on the news my first day back.\u201d He cleared his throat, turning to the computer. \u201cLet us check his mail first. Is there anything specific you would like to search for? I am merely here to screen things, to make sure you don\u2019t find anything we would have to kill you for.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled slightly. \u201cI am partial to not being killed.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone\u2019s smile in response seemed fucking genuine. \u201cIndeed. Also, it would be detrimental to our bonhomie with Ms. Norton.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs he pagan?\u201d Naomi snapped a picture of the contents of a desk drawer.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo...\u201d Gone looked over at her, a note of goddamn confusion in his voice. \u201cJewish, I believe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi let the camera settle around her neck. \u201cThen what kind of shrine is this?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t...\u201d He looked over at Naomi who held his gaze. He sighed and walked over and looked in the fucking drawer. \u201cOh. Oh! That\u2019s ghastly.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack took the opportunity to slink the hell into the office chair and bring up the croaker\u2019s emails. One particular email chain caught his eye, labeled \u2018Classified Data Breach\u2019. Several people were involved in tracking down some kinda fucking \u2018data leak\u2019. Reasonable enough on the surface, but you rarely warn people to avoid confronting a data leak alone before it left the floor. Gone was supposed to deal with that kind of shit, but in his absence, Crumb and a few others had been put on the task.<br /> <br /> Before Gone turned back to the computer, Billy Mack switched over to the access logs. Contradicting what Gone had fucking said, three people including him had accessed that computer: Aloyisius DeBerry, Velma von Neuyes and Adam Gone. One, Velma von Neuyes, had only logged in once, the night Crumb had died.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou will not tell anyone where that picture was taken. If you do, you will disappear and all will forget both you and that picture.\u201d Gone pinned Naomi with a goddamn stern look. His frown deepened as he turned and saw Billy Mack at the computer.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re scary old man. Don\u2019t cough up your Geritol.\u201d Naomi rolled his eyes at his back.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack didn\u2019t balk at the stare, pointing at the logs. \u201cYou said two had accessed this machine?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone narrowed his eyes at him. \u201cYes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis says a Mr. DeBerry and a Ms. von Neuyes, as well as yourself, accessed it.\u201d That got his fucking attention.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. She\u2019s just clerical, nothing important.\u201d He took the g-man\u2019s place at the goddamn computer and peered at the logs. \u201cShe was checking his datebook, it appears.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cThat does explain that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone raised an eyebrow. \u201cLet\u2019s see. Back to the emails... we\u2019ve already isolated emails from his ex-wife. She does threaten his life - she even promises to acquire his skull, but that was likely figurative language. I have met her and she is smart, too smart to publicly threaten someone, then murder them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLuring someone to such a location and killing them with an alligator speaks to premeditation, not a crime of passion,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> Gone nodded and pointed at a particular email. \u201cThere. It appears to just be a response to his provocation. I\u2019ve personally found it best not to respond to such things.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi smirked. \u201cNo shame in having difficulties responding, at your age.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNow, now. He\u2019s a paying client,\u201d Billy Mack chided. She rolled her eyes again and went back to taking pictures of every goddamn thing.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs she qualified for this sort of thing?\u201d Gone eyed her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI assure you, I would not have brought her if I didn\u2019t have every confidence in her abilities.\u201d Billy Mack smiled and nodded.<br /> <br /> Gone raised an eyebrow and went back to the emails. \u201cMore threatening language was from Rhonda. The only other red flag was from a \u2018mwgriffith\u2019. One email, reading \u2018Be a pal\u2019 in the subject and repeated in the body text. Crumb received it the day he died and responded with \u2018Motherfucker\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned fucking thoughtfully. \u201cIt clearly had some meaning to him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe was quick to use that metaphor.\u201d Gone made a face. \u201cHe doesn\u2019t need much provocation for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs there anything references Harold?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone shook his head. \u201cNo, nothing in the three years since the last archive. Neither is there anything referencing the establishment, street name or room number he was found at. Nor crocodile or alligator - wait, there is one... oh, he made a comment that a crocodile is the appropriate size to eat small children.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack agreed. \u201cIt is.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone nodded abstractedly. \u201cThat was sent two years ago and not part of a threat. He brought it up in fact.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey boss.\u201d Naomi looked over from her goddamn picture taking. \u201cWhat about the girl who owned the room? Wanna check that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGirl who owned the room?\u201d Gone looked at the g-man fucking questioningly.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled at Naomi. \u201cYes, a Zelda Ridley was renting the room Mr. Crumb was found in.\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone searched for the name and found an email chain between her and Crumb. The language was goddamn evasive: he was trying to deal with \u2018an irritant\u2019 and needed \u2018particular expertise\u2019. Ridley promised to establish a meeting place, claiming to need time. At first, Crumb seemed patient, but his patience ran out fucking quickly. The last email in the chain, from Ridley, warned him that she would try to move quicker but nothing was certain. That was sent the day Crumb died.<br /> <br /> The mage\u2019s brow knit and he picked up the desk phone. \u201cVelma. Oh yes, yes, you\u2019re a dear. I need everything you can on one Zelda Ridley... immediately... yes.\u201d He paused. \u201cYes, thank you.\u201d He hung up the phone. \u201cWe\u2019ll have the information for you before you leave.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhile we\u2019re waiting - Naomi, do you have that sketch?\u201d She nodded and handed the sketch of the fucker who brought the crocodile in to Billy Mack who showed it Gone.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my, that\u2019s an unpleasant looking individual.\u201d Gone raised a goddamn eyebrow. \u201cHe looks like a gentleman of the road.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m guessing Crumb wasn\u2019t expecting trouble, or he\u2019d have taken his gun...\u201d Naomi peered curiously into another drawer, after taking a picture of the shit in it.<br /> <br /> Gone went to the drawer. \u201cA gun? Here? Oh, it\u2019s one of mine. That\u2019s odd.\u201d He picked it up It was fucking odd looking, a goddamn modular pistol. It had a tubular contraption hung beneath it and some kind of side extension.<br /> <br /> Naomi raised an eyebrow. \u201cYou said you searched the office?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t personally...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wouldn\u2019t admit it either.\u201d Naomi winked conspiratorially. Billy Mack frowned at her.<br /> <br /> Gone\u2019s phone beeped. \u201cWe have an address for Ms. Ridley. Well, isn\u2019t she well to do?\u201d He gave the address. It was in Liz\u2019s neighborhood. \u201cAn eccentric heiress, apparently. There is a remarkable lack of information on her.\u201d He sighed and sat back in the fucking chair. \u201cI am very impressed with both what you have done here and what you had done already. Is there anything else I can help with?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cI don\u2019t believe so. I hope you get that password deal worked out.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen we do, I will pass along what I can. There is likely to be something I can, some of those files have a very low clearance. Not so Vera, Velma, whatever could access it, but still...\u201d Gone gave him a smug smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cBefore we leave, Ms. Norton would like to investigate Crumb\u2019s house. I assume this is acceptable?\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> Gone nodded, unsurprised. \u201cI can give proof that Ms. Norton has been hired to look into his death, to give to the police, should they object.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack inclined his head. \u201cThank you. Out of curiosity, would he usually have had anything worth stealing?\u201d<br /> <br /> Gone thought for a moment. \u201cMonetarily... his suit would have been quite expensive. Dressing well is part and parcel of working here. Well, when one is an associate.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was thinking more company secrets.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Gone was goddamn certain. \u201cHe would have been terminated for that. The exit interview would be unfortunate.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned, thinking. \u201cThey obviously went to a fair amount of trouble For what? What was he working on, insofar as you can tell me?\u201d<br /> <br /> The lawyer stood up. \u201cHe was dealing with some things related to the Roxanne Steele debacle.\u201d He grinned at Billy Mack\u2019s spike of interest. \u201cSome individuals we represent got mixed up in that situation. In fact, it\u2019s how Ms. Norton\u2019s name came up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh. Well. It is regrettable we were unable to retrieve her.\u201d Billy Mack looked fucking disappointed.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut it is admirable that you worked so hard to deny her even the respite of an out of country sanctuary. And to know when to cut your losses.\u201d The mage\u2019s goddamn smug grin deepened.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled back. \u201cThank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway, while Crumb was somewhat distracted by internal issues, the large part of his duties was dealing with the damaging effects of the information released by Ms. Steele.\u201d Gone opened the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt does seem, as you said, to not be pertinent, the day already having been done in this situation.\u201d The g-man followed him out, Naomi just behind.<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed.\u201d He hit a button on his phone to relock Crumb\u2019s office and unlock the outer door. \u201cI wish you a productive day.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi waited until they were out the door, its bolt shoving home behind them, and almost to the goddamn elevator before letting out a big sigh. \u201cLet\u2019s blow this taco stand - another hour here and I won\u2019t be able to shit properly. The old is strong here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head, pushing the button for a different floor. \u201cI need to find an open terminal.\u201d Naomi sighed again.<br /> <br /> The g-man found one quickly and Naomi took up a bored post nearby. After he plugged in the thumb drive the cursor blinked and a message typed itself. \u2018Ah, you\u2019re a sport. No hard feelings, right?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Pleasure doing business with you,\u2019 the fucker typed back.<br /> <br /> As they left, Naomi pulled out her phone. \u201cHey. I am finally done, we can get in some work on the fanfic. I won\u2019t have all day - Deanna\u2019s pretty much done ragging, so I\u2019m going to be going over there tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I spent the afternoon looking into Rhonda Crumb\u2019s financials. If she wasn\u2019t in town, she still might have paid for a fucking hit. But there were no big payments made. In fact, she was getting paid regularly by the asshole, Crumb himself - possibly alimony, possibly a payoff, possibly some other fucking arrangements. But a few angles didn't fucking check out.<br /> <br /> The weirdest shit was the sequence of small payments made to multiple parties only identified by goddamn number strings. Always upper hundreds, and only to one number string at a time. A few payments to one, then to another, and another, never going back to the previous ones. There were 8 payments, totaling approximately six thousand smackers worth. I figured them for account numbers and printed them out, leaving them and a goddamn explanatory note for Kilroy.<br /> <br /> The other odd entries were a trio of $500 payments to a fucking Whacko Bob\u2019s Lemonade and Watermelon Stand. That I could look into without Kilroy\u2019s goddamn wizardry. A little bit of digging showed that Whacko Bob\u2019s Lemonade and Watermelon Stand was a shop in Seattle, something of a catch all for unusual imports. \u2018Unusual things the likes of which you\u2019ve never seen. Plus lemonade and watermelon.\u2019 I frowned at the logo. It looked fucking familiar, some sort of castle shit in a lightning storm. I ran through a bank of similar images I\u2019d seen, eventually recognizing the Tower tarot card. Definitely something to look into.<br /> <br /> <br /> I met Esha at her office. The address she\u2019d given led me to a white stone building with no goddamn signs or labeling. I sauntered into the well-fucking-appointed reception area. The dame behind the counter gave me a polite smile. \u201cCan I help you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned on the counter, quirking an eyebrow. \u201cI\u2019m here to see Mrs. Karnik.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, yes, she did have an appointment.\u201d She looked towards the elevators. \u201cShe\u2019s on the second floor.\u201d<br /> <br /> I winked at her and headed towards the stairs. I was hit by a wave of blue as soon as I left the fucking stairwell. The walls, the floor, the ceiling, even the goddamn light was blue. There was a slight humming that pervaded the place. I sent out my senses in a quick pulse, checking the Resonance of the place. It was definitely a bit of Infrastructure, and heavily guarded - two Angels and a fuckton of Stigmatics.<br /> <br /> I knocked on Esha\u2019s door, leaning against the door frame. \u201cHey doll,\u201d I said as she opened the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cCome on in!\u201d She took my hand, pulling me inside. The office was large and airy with a fucking great view. The lighting was back to the usual white and a large Blue Sun logo spread out over the carpet. As the door shut she moved in close for a kiss. \u201cI\u2019ve wanted to do that again for awhile. Things are... they\u2019re going well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLooks like.\u201d I looked around, smirking.<br /> <br /> She looked away demurely. \u201cI\u2019m on the leadership council here. There\u2019s the chair and us, no CEO, so we have a lot of influence in decisions.\u201d She laid a hand on my collar. \u201cBut what about you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned. \u201cA few things here or there. I missed my own bit break, but did get to spend a month abroad. Got a big name client though, so things are up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s excellent Gabe!\u201d She gestured towards a seat and sat down next to me. \u201cIt reminds me - I had an offer to make you. Independent of any other connections between us.\u201d She laid a hand on my knee. \u201cThe things we do here... it\u2019s basically technological enhancement of human subjects. We\u2019re picky about who we involve but... I feel a certain sense of loyalty to you.\u201d She smiled. \u201cI assure you, it\u2019s nothing I haven\u2019t done.\u201d Her goddamn eyes glowed blue for a brief moment. My thigh was pleasantly fucking warm under her hand. The glowing faded and I realized her eyes were blue and had been even before the glowing. They were brown when I first met her. \u201cI\u2019m very interested in seeing you. And I want you to reap the benefits of seeing me.\u201d She ran her other hand down my cheek.<br /> <br /> Wasn\u2019t that some shit? I could have my very goddamn own superpowers. Of course, any Angel supervising would know right the hell off that something had gone wrong. Even if they didn\u2019t, it was a serious investment, to run that scam. And fucking dangerous for my cover structure. Still, that in could be useful when-slash-if we moved to take down Blue Sun. \u201cSerious? Wow, that\u2019s... wow. I, uh, I\u2019m flattered, really, but I\u2019m gonna have to think about that.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded goddamn excitedly. \u201cYou know, I was just thinking, one option is a light mind reading ability. Surface thoughts, you know? It seems like it might be useful for your work.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt really would be.\u201d I smirked over at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can touch a car and direct it, just by touch. I have a number of abilities, more than some because... well, they said very kind things. I have a high capacity for such things.\u201d She smiled up at me. \u201cI think you could too.\u201d<br /> <br /> I bit my lip thoughtfully and she dropped the subject, showing me around the office. She babbled a little, filling the silence with chatter. She talked about her ongoing divorce, a fucking sparkle in her eyes as she looked over at me and recounted his description of our fight. I smiled, keeping my eyes more on her than her office. At a pause, I did pump her for information about her work. \u201cTell me more about your swanky job here. I like hearing good news and, well, the more I know about what you do here, the more comfortable I\u2019d be with your... offer.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cLong term, we\u2019re hoping to contract out to other companies, provide enhancements to order. Short term... we\u2019re refining the process. We can\u2019t do animal testing, not really, so it\u2019s not fast going.\u201d At my inquisitive look, she elaborated. \u201cThe most successful attempt at animal testing by Dr. Radim, the whole bonobo thing, led to the flesh melting off of four people.\u201d I raised a goddamn eyebrow. \u201cHe gave them powers that would allow one to discharge electricity, to power electronics.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat seems unwise on Dr. Radim\u2019s part.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe was happy it worked at all.\u201d She shrugged. \u201cThey experimented with a different monkey. I\u2019m not sure precisely what happened, they won\u2019t talk about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> A thought crossed my mind and I smirked internally. We\u2019d already kicked the hell out of this beehive, why not take one more shot. Shit. Fucking saboteurs. I think they\u2019re fucking rubbing off on me. \u201cYou do anything with Team Tomorrow? Sounds like they do similar things, but with biological, not technological enhancement.\u201d<br /> <br /> She frowned slightly. \u201cSounds like a competitor. That\u2019s not really my area - I\u2019m largely overseeing internal things, keeping the boys on track, approving subjects...\u201d She ran a hand down the curve of my neck.<br /> <br /> I shrugged, putting an arm around her waist. \u201cSomething to look into.\u201d I swung around so that she sat down on the desk sharply and I moved in close. \u201cMaybe we oughta have that dinner before we skip it.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> We made it to dinner, at Marcilla\u2019s, the fucking fancy joint Vivian had taken Shelley to the other night. We swapped stories of our past month. She\u2019d been back to India for a short visit but had been back in the US for awhile. She sympathized over our wild goose chase. I shrugged. \u201cWe\u2019ve had a surge since though. Two cases right now. One\u2019s hush-hush, but big names. The other\u2019s a security case. Not so high profile, but it\u2019s good for our rep.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI hope these cases won\u2019t miss you before tomorrow.\u201d She laid a hand on mine.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t rush - the food was too goddamn good for that - but we didn\u2019t dally either. At her townhouse, I teased her, sauntering down the tenth floor hallway, admiring the artwork on the walls. She tugged me inside, kissing me fiercely.<br /> <br /> She backed up for air, pulling me by the fucking tie to her dark bedroom. She looked at me with an anticipatory gleam glinting in her cat-like blue eyes. \u201cI was thinking of you when I got this one particular power.\u201d She ran one hand down my cheek, the other hand tugging out my shirt so she could lay bare skin on my waist.<br /> <br /> Lightning followed her touch, suffusing my body with a fucking pleasant warmth. The electricity coursed through me, surging in power. It was never painful, just the goddamn opposite. The feelings of pleasure grew in intensity and combined with her clever fingers, it was all I could do to stay awake longer than she did.<br /> <br /> Once she was asleep, I brushed Esha\u2019s hair away from the nape of her neck and traced the goddamn intricate glowing blue circuitry spreading like the skeleton of a pair of wings across her shoulders. Her surface thoughts gave me glimpses of some kind of fucking anxiety dream. I didn\u2019t dwell on the Venus flytrap or protestations of heterosexuality. I went deeper, looking first for a memory of a council meeting. There were four other members on the council, all Indian men, one of which was clearly an fucking Angel. That one was the chairman. Her apparent job was what she\u2019d said, clearing people into the program and other inward facing duties.<br /> <br /> Secondly I looked for a memory describing Esha\u2019s powers. One I\u2019d seen - the fucking hot lightning she\u2019d used on me earlier. It could also be used to cause extreme goddamn pain, if she wanted. She had the ability to control machines with a touch, like she\u2019d said, and did have that mind-reading power she\u2019d mentioned. Lastly, she had a specific scrying power, the ability to, with eye contact, see whatever the hell those eyes had seen.<br /> <br /> The third memory I looked up was of when she got the goddamn implant that I knew she had to have. I got a memory of a surgery prep, where they explained that the implant was designed to \u2018unlock\u2019 the fucking apocryphal unused 90 percent of the brain. Then she went under. That made it easier, in a way. She didn't know she was a goddamn ticking time bomb. Of course, I\u2019d hoped so, considering she offered it to me. Still, it might give us the leverage to pull her away.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cAh, my friends left me presents.\u201d Billy Mack regarded the handful of teeth and stack of printouts with a fucking pleased smile.<br /> <br /> He started with the printouts, reading over my note and the financial records goddamn carefully. His initial forays revealed fairly quickly that the mystery numbers listed in the debits\u2019 descriptions weren\u2019t account numbers to any bank. He was able to determine they were electronic payments and presumed they were some sort of fucking internal code - the first few digits were the same for all the numbers. He started looking into her bank accounts more closely, but getting into a bank\u2019s system is serious goddamn business, even for him. But he got started.<br /> <br /> After a few hours he stretched and set it aside, letting a few scripts run in the background. He moved onto the fucking teeth, carefully scooping them up with a gloved hand and putting them in a Petri dish. Testing and observation showed they were definitely human teeth. Some chips were missing and Billy Mack ran a model or some shit to determine that the teeth were knocked out when their owner\u2019s face was rammed into something flat.<br /> <br /> He filed the teeth away and tidied up the lab. Cecilia had left by the time he was finished, so he locked up behind himself, whistling off key as he pocketed the keys.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next morning I woke up to the shifting of the bed next to me. I turned to see Esha smiling at me. I rolled over and propped myself up. \u201cHey doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHungry?\u201d<br /> <br /> I could fucking smell something cooking somewhere else in the town house. I pushed myself up to give her a kiss before rolling off the bed. \u201cFamished.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled on my goddamn undershirt and she shrugged on a blue robe with a prominent Blue Sun logo. The chipper Latina cook served us a fucking delicious breakfast while Esha tentatively prodded at my relationship status. \u201cI\u2019m sure you have women throwing themselves at you...\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged, deflecting each time, not denying anything but not letting anything slip either. She seemed satisfied. And only a little disappointed when I slipped out right after breakfast, giving me just enough leeway to stop by my apartment for a quick shower and still get to work on time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Liz was the last to breeze in, after Naomi\u2019s class was over. We gathered in the lab to share fucking notes. Once I was done, Liz raised an eyebrow. \u201cI\u2019m glad you had a good evening. I had an excellent one - well, Naomi did. She spent it with her girlfriend, watching Korean drama on Netflix.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cThose will rot your brain I hear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wouldn\u2019t know.\u201d She sat on a desk under the No Smoking sign, folding one leg over the other. \u201cShe couldn\u2019t hear it over her girlfriend screaming.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA good precaution.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz lit her cigarette and put the goddamn holder to her lips. \u201cSo, what is our plan for today?\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back in my seat, swinging the chair back and forth. \u201cWe\u2019ve got a few leads - the fucker on the sketch, Whacko Bob...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCould they be the same guy?\u201d Liz had a fucking thoughtful frown on her face.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shrugged. \u201cMight be a good place to start looking for him at least. We also have an address for Zelda Ridley.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tapped a pen on my chin. \u201cWith that goddamn address we should definitely send Liz.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can handle that. I don\u2019t suppose we know whether it\u2019s Miss or Mrs.?\u201d Liz gave me a wicked grin.<br /> <br /> I shrugged, smiling back. \u201cYou wanna go it alone, or to have backup?\u201d<br /> <br /> She blew out a cloud of smoke. \u201cAlone, most likely. I\u2019ll check with the neighbors first. If she shows signs of excessive straightness, I might as well take friends\u201d She looked thoughtful. \u201cZelda is probably a pseudonym. Rhonda, do you think?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should be so goddamn lucky.\u201d I smirked at her. \u201cIt seems unlikely. It\u2019s an odd fucking play for someone in her position.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe was receiving money from Mr. Crumb,\u201d Billy Mack put in.<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cI was just thinking, he was killed in the bed. Why would he be in that bed, sleeping in that room, unless there was something romantic?\u201d I mimed a punch. \u201cOK, it could have been that. But why put him in the bed?\u201d<br /> <br /> I stretched and stood. \u201cTo set the stage? It\u2019s a weird fucking tableau, no matter where he was killed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s the cocaine as well.\u201d Billy Mack checked something on the goddamn computer.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat does not explain the bed - I\u2019ve taken enough to be put away for life and when I\u2019m on it, I don\u2019t go anywhere near a bed unless I\u2019m fucking someone.\u201d Liz glanced at me. \u201cWas Crumb supernatural?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cNo fucking clue. Corpses don\u2019t have auras.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked thoughtful. \u201cWell, Gone - who\u2019s a prick and a half, you\u2019re right - seems to think the only other people who are important are mages, so...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cMr. Crumb was tapped to deal with that \u2018data breach\u2019. It seems unlikely that a job usually handled by Mr. Gone would be given to a non-mage.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. A mage.\u201d Liz sighed. \u201cI wish I\u2019d taken the gun. I had no idea he didn\u2019t know it was there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe might still have been aware of it being stolen.\u201d Billy Mack smiled sympathetically at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou said you had pictures, right? Of the gun and the shrine?\u201d I looked over at Liz.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d She pulled out the pictures. The gun was fucking weird, but the \u2018shrine\u2019 seemed to have some real significance.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack\u2019s eyebrows raised. \u201cWell, this certainly might explain the odd feeling in the office. Something of a mystical aftertaste.\u201d I waited. Eventually he cottoned the hell on to the fact we hadn\u2019t yet. \u201cIt\u2019s a channel to some other realm. Another realm like the Abyss is another realm, but more incomprehensibly alien, less focusedly malevolent. You were warned about the Men in Black, yes, when you were first sent out by the God Machine?\u201d We nodded. \u201cThey\u2019re from one of these \u2018stranger shores\u2019, I believe they\u2019re called.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned against the wall. \u201cFucking great.\u201d I paused. It was as good an excuse as any. I held up a finger to the others and dialed Miranda. \u201cHey sweetheart.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe...\u201d She had a teasing smile in her voice. \u201cI didn\u2019t sleep as well last night - it was a little chilly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMmm, well, I can\u2019t let that happen again tonight. And, more immediately, it\u2019d be nice to see you now, and, completely honestly... I need a consult. For work.\u201d I started walking a coin over my knuckles.<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow. \u201cOh?\u201d<br /> <br /> I explained about the shrine and the gun and where we\u2019d found it, along with Billy Mack\u2019s conclusions. \u201cOf course, we didn\u2019t take these pictures there, and I never said we did.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey really gave you the spiel, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah. I\u2019m shaking in my boots.\u201d I rolled my fucking eyes.<br /> <br /> She pressed her lips together. \u201cDon\u2019t trifle with him Gabe. He\u2019s dangerous.\u201d She paused. \u201cEven still, I didn\u2019t think they\u2019d have the balls to go poking around stranger shores.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cSo, you have time to stop by? Look at some weird pictures, maybe get lunch before I go toss a dead man\u2019s place?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like a date. I\u2019ll see you soon Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pocketed my phone and returned to the conversation in the lab. \u201cI\u2019m just saying, whoever searched that room did a shit job.\u201d Liz looked at Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> The g-man shrugged. \u201cThey likely thought Mr. Gone was aware of the gun. Would you take something like that from him, without asking?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTo piss him off,\u201d Liz shot back quickly.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack sighed. \u201cIf you were Mr. Crumb, would you? I rather don\u2019t think so, but I suppose when he was asked to do Mr. Gone\u2019s job.\u201d He nodded to me as I sat down. \u201cDo be careful Liz.\u201d<br /> <br /> She waved a fucking hand at him. \u201cI\u2019ll be very cautious. There was some social Ms. Ridley was supposed to attend, and when she didn\u2019t and I realized I didn't know her, I figured I'd looked into. My neighbors won\u2019t bat an eye.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust keep in mind the potential for magely aptitude,\u201d he warned.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be the soul of discretion.\u201d She hopped off the desk and stretched. \u201cWell, I should get to it. Though... I suppose I could grab lunch first.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cNo reason not to.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked at me. \u201cThat depends on where Gabe decides to go.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sneered at her. It wasn\u2019t too long before the doorbell jingled and I could hear Miranda speaking to Cecilia. Miranda came up be herself a few moments later. I beckoned her over to my desk and took her hand. Billy Mack smiled at her. \u201cA pleasure as always.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you, it\u2019s nice to see you.\u201d Miranda smiled at me.<br /> <br /> I smiled back and showed her the photos. \u201cThat gun - it definitely could be something made by a technologically oriented mage. Those kinds of things allow someone to cast a spell in very controlled circumstances, safe from paradox. Then when it is used, there is no personal backlash.\u201d She set the picture aside and looked more interestedly at the shrine. \u201cHrm. I could probably find you something on this. I\u2019ll have to look it up, but I have an idea where.\u201d<br /> <br /> I beamed at her. \u201cThanks love.\u201d I stood up, resting my hands on her waist. \u201cSo, ready for lunch? This is a hell of a way to come, just to look at a couple of pictures.\u201d Miranda nodded, smiling slightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Gabe, where to?\u201d Liz raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> I decided on a nearby Thai pizza place, Bangkok Pies. Liz did decide to come with us and we made a fucking party, that\u2019s for damn sure. Billy Mack looked around as we were seated. \u201cPerhaps it is good Terry is not here. Certain things were said when he first arrived, I\u2019m not sure he\u2019s gotten over it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike what?\u201d Miranda looked curiously at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe hadn\u2019t quite settled into being human yet. He\u2019s learning,\u201d Billy Mack deflected.<br /> <br /> He was saved as the owner came over to greet us, introducing herself as Kat. \u201cHello everyone. I don\u2019t believe I\u2019ve seen you guys around here, you seem like nice people.\u201d She flirted some, with me and Liz, though she backed off me when Miranda gave her the eye.<br /> <br /> Liz flirted back and watched her leave as Kat returned to her rounds. \u201cI believe I\u2019ve developed an increased hunger for Thai-seasoned pizza pie.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda frowned at the owner\u2019s back before schooling her features and turning back to the table. \u201cWhat are you doing after this?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLiz is checking into the woman who rented the room the dead guy was found in. Turns out she lives in Liz\u2019s neighborhood.\u201d I smirked at the dark haired woman, whose eyes were still fucking tracking Kat as she spoke to other tables.<br /> <br /> Liz turned to Miranda and smiled. \u201cIt\u2019s good to know your neighbors.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe rest of us are hitting up the dead guy\u2019s house, then a trip to Whacko Bob\u2019s.\u201d I glanced around, surreptitiously spiking my drink and winking at Miranda.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhacko Bob\u2019s? The lemonade and watermelon stand?\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow at her. \u201cYou know it?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cYes. They deal in occult items. I\u2019ve never done business there myself, but I know of them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHuh.\u201d I took a slug of my drink. \u201cThe victim\u2019s ex-wife made a few purchases there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey do sell non-occult items. The proprietor is rather pretty.\u201d I smirked, hiding my face in my glass. \u201cNot Whacko Bob! I haven\u2019t seen her either, I\u2019m just going by what I\u2019m told.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kat came by again, placing a hand on the back of Liz\u2019s chair. She chatted briefly before looking conspiratorially at Liz. \u201cSo how many of them are your girlfriend or boyfriend?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz grinned playfully. \u201cAny of them that I want to be.\u201d I rolled my fucking eyes at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI would figure you wouldn\u2019t have trouble.\u201d Kat quirked her lip.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I do seem to stumble upon the prettiest people.\u201d The two kept flirting until Kat had to wander off again.<br /> <br /> We discussed the case in between visits from Kat and when the check came, Liz took it. \u201cYou are all welcome for the sacrifice I\u2019m making. Especially since,\u201d she glanced at the bill, \u201cit seems like the bill has been discounted.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda glanced over at me. \u201cI\u2019m trying to figure out which one thinks the other is meat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure the feeling is mutual.\u201d Liz smiled predatorily at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am trying to decide whether to bring Vivian here. Perhaps with Shelley.\u201d Billy Mack looked thoughtfully at Kat.<br /> <br /> Liz made a fucking moue at him. \u201cI saw her first.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow. \u201cDefinitely with Shelley?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t let her flirt too much.\u201d Liz looked sternly at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe seems to know her place.\u201d Miranda smirked at me.<br /> <br /> Liz sighed. \u201cWell, I have bored housewives to talk to. Don\u2019t have too much fun.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave her a look. \u201cBe careful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will keep you updated.\u201d She gave him a wry look back. \u201cI will call you before I speak to Zelda.\u201d She waved at Kat as she left.<br /> <br /> Miranda watched her leave. \u201cI\u2019ve never seen a non-smoking establishment bring someone an ashtray.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled, also watching the dame leave. \u201cShe is special.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> Speed leaves out one part, where Quietus test drives his new Cover to try to get some janitorial jobs for just recently not homeless folks, unfortunately his skills and the dice were uncooperative so not much came of it. This was the first day while stuff was going on after the diaspora from the office.<br /> <br /> The \u201cStranger Shores\u201d referenced discussing Mr. Gone was referring that chapter of <i>Summoners</i> for <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, namely the weird shit chapter. My personal favorite. Gone and his fellow Mages are messing with some odd shit.<br /> <br /> Okay that seems to cover it. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-04T20:29:09-07:00","id":907407,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to accidentally pepper your vocabulary with Noir-speak by reading our newest Night Train Detective Agency journals! Clytemnestra\u2019s story takes place late session, and as has been the case recently is a short fiction. Speed has an insanely faithful breakdown of the session. It\u2019s time to meet the Tick-Tock Men. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Miranda joined us on our trip to Crumb\u2019s place. We picked Jack up on the way. There was a black car in the driveway when we got there, about halfway up. I picked up the thin piece of metal I keep in case it was locked and approached it casually, sauntering the rest of the way up the drive. A quick glance down, however, showed me it had one of those fancy fucking keypads so I waved Billy Mack over.<br /> <br /> He put the key code in, first try. Once he\u2019d unlocked the rest of the doors, I slid in the passenger side, checking the glove box and shuffling through the assorted shit while Billy Mack poked around on the GPS. First thing I noticed was that this jackass had a hell of a goddamn thing for clocks - analog, digital, wrist, alarm, all kinds of fucking clocks. He was also a smoker, or someone who\u2019d ridden in the car was, so I grabbed a few butts and put them in an evidence bag.<br /> <br /> The first sign that anything was wrong was when I noticed that two people had been in here very recently. I was just about to say something when Miranda narrowed her eyes and looked towards the house and Billy Mack frowned. \u201cThe GPS says this car arrived thirty minutes ago, from Portland.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd belongs to one John fucking Smith.\u201d I leafed through the registration papers.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe should be careful. I have a suspicion that I hope is not accurate.\u201d Miranda\u2019s eyes were locked on the house.<br /> <br /> Jack looked at her over the car. \u201cAggressively careful?\u201d Miranda nodded. Jack cocked his gun.<br /> <br /> I got out of the car, moving next to her. \u201cWhat\u2019s up sweetheart?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Tick Tock Men.\u201d She looked over at me. \u201cThey\u2019re Abyssal tainted mages who like clocks,\u201d she glanced inside the car, \u201cand time magic. They have grenades that look like clocks that will destroy the fact that whoever or whatever was caught in the explosion ever existed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway to know for sure it\u2019s them, if I get eyes on them?\u201d I took in the place - a nice house, pretty big, and a couple of decent windows.<br /> <br /> She shook her head. Billy Mack elaborated. \u201cThey\u2019re simply mages. Spawned from a very significant Paradox storm, if I understand correctly.\u201d Miranda nodded. \u201cThey actively work against the God-Machine, as most knowledgeable, sentient things that wish to destroy reality do. They can rewind time and reset what they\u2019ve done, in addition to their destructive powers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat.\u201d I started flipping on combat powers, noting that the others were doing the same. \u201cI\u2019m gonna get eyes on them anyway, see what they\u2019re after. I\u2019ll be careful.\u201d I caught Miranda\u2019s eyes and gave her a grin. She gave me a slight smile.<br /> <br /> Looking in the window I found two Men in Black looking fuckers - well, one Man in Black, one Woman in Black. Heavy watch chains were attached to their shoulders and went down into their chest pockets. I looked them over with my Aura Sight - they were definitely mages and definitely Abyssally tainted. They were looking for a briefcase in particular, some information in general. Something about this shit was going to give them an angle on some Infrastructure.<br /> <br /> I risked a quick peek at the dame\u2019s thoughts also. \u2018If I were a Free Council mage, where the fuck would I leave a briefcase?\u2019 I smirked and snuck back to the others.<br /> <br /> Miranda sighed as I relayed what I\u2019d seen. \u201cAt least I wanted vast amounts of personal power, not just to end the world. I suppose they do believe all people will becomes mages and ascend to the Supernal realms, but still...\u201d She moved to stand next to me. \u201cI did figure the lawyers were Free Council. As little as I think of Gone, at least he\u2019s not trying to destroy reality.\u201d<br /> <br /> My phone buzzed with a text from Liz. \u2018Zelda is a snake woman.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018You in trouble?\u2019 I sent back fucking quickly, mentioning it to the others.<br /> <br /> She sent three texts in quick succession. \u2018No.\u2019 \u2018Probably.\u2019 \u2018Probably not in trouble.\u2019<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u2018Peachy. We\u2019re about to be. Will contact when done. If not we\u2019ll be erased from history. Cheers.\u2019<br /> <br /> While I was responding, Jack and Billy Mack set up a collection of surprises in case the fuckers ran for it in their car. Miranda looked at me seriously. \u201cI can give them something to think about.\u201d I started to object, but she put a finger to my lips. \u201cI\u2019m not going to run in and do something stupid, I\u2019m going to do something stupid and give them something to attack other than me. Or you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I bit my lip. \u201cI\u2019m not sure...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am. Perhaps as a last ditch effort.\u201d Billy Mack looked up from the car at us. Miranda nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo. Am I setting up an ambush?\u201d Jack turned away from the goddamn clock he\u2019d placed on the dash.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cThey\u2019d just rewind time and replay it knowing we were coming.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFront door it is.\u201d Jack strode towards the door, with the rest of us fucking following close behind.<br /> <br /> He kicked in the door with a quick solid blow. They looked up, unfuckingsurprised, and Jack\u2019s gun disintegrated in his hand. Billy Mack\u2019s rivet gun barked once, putting a serious hole in the dame. After that, things got goddamn weird.<br /> <br /> They zipped out, breaking for the back door. Everything but us seemed to be moving at an inhuman speed - it was a little hard to reconcile it with the fact that I knew it was us who were fucking slowed down. They were long gone by the time we could react. Still, we kept after them. Miranda and I moved to cover the back door they appeared to have left through. Jack checked the front door while Billy Mack took up position at the window to keep an eye on the car.<br /> <br /> After a few moments, time returned to its normal pace. The two Tick Tock fucks were long gone and had left nothing behind, so I turned back to go over the house. Jack decided to go a little further. His eyes widened and he turned back inside and ran for it. \u201cGet down!\u201d<br /> <br /> I dived behind cover, pulling Miranda along with me. The back yard fucking exploded, taking out a chunk of the back wall as well. We stood up carefully, taking stock, but no one was seriously hurt.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, that\u2019s our cue to leave.\u201d Jack looked around, a goddamn paranoid expression in his eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe were here for a reason.\u201d I started going through the office they had been tossing.<br /> <br /> Jack glared at me. \u201cThe cops have a reason now too.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cRight. And if we smooth that over, Gone\u2019ll be particularly, monetarily, pleased. It was, uh, a gas leak.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA gas leak?\u201d Billy Mack raised a fucking eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck it, not a leak. That was the kitchen wall - he left his stove on, or some shit, and you lit that cigar of yours... boom!\u201d I kept looking.<br /> <br /> My phone buzzed again. \u2018Correction, not a snake woman - has snake people.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Not been erased.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Kay\u2019<br /> <br /> Jack decided against dragging me out bodily and started conferring with Billy Mack. Miranda looked over my shoulder as I started flipping through Crumb\u2019s notes. At first, I figured he was talking about the \u2018data leak\u2019 - he mentioned needing to start carrying a gun, since the Visitor was tired of being tracked down and was beginning to stalk back. The powers that be, apparently, didn\u2019t want her killed. There was a picture, a porcelain looking woman in heavy clothes. It reminded me of Madame X, so I showed it to Miranda.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe look familiar at all?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d She looked at me bemusedly.<br /> <br /> I shrugged and gave her a lopsided grin. \u201cTell you about it later.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe!\u201d Mac\u2019s voice came from the fucking doorway. \u201cDidja do it?\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes at him. Billy Mack joined us, smiling at Mac. \u201cNo, just unfortunate timing. We\u2019ve been hired to look into Mr. Crumb\u2019s death.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac gave him a smile back. \u201cHello government man. Tell me about how this isn\u2019t my problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt certainly isn\u2019t. A gas leak.\u201d Jack held up the goddamn wall.<br /> <br /> \u201cSwamp gas?\u201d Mac smirked.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head fucking seriously. \u201cNo, oven gas. Believe me, I know my gas leaks.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac hid a smile. \u201cDangerous things, gas stoves.\u201d He looked around. \u201cThis doesn\u2019t look like a gas stove house. I\u2019m just gonna walk away now, a government agent assures me there\u2019s no problem. Right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded to me. \u201cTake care of yourself Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked up from the papers. \u201cYou too Mac.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mac called the other flatfeet off and they headed the hell out. Once they were out, I called Gone. \u201cMs. Norton?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMr. Gone.\u201d I leaned back in Crumb\u2019s chair. \u201cWe\u2019re at Crumb\u2019s house. There were some suits here when we got here - had some kind of fucking fetish for clocks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cClocks?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned at Miranda. \u201cYeah. All over their car. They even left a bomb behind that looked like one.\u201d<br /> <br /> He paused. \u201cIn your opinion, do you think these people killed him?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t say. I think they\u2019re some kind of terrorists, I overheard them talking about taking down infrastructure. They were looking for some documents, a briefcase.\u201d Billy Mack nodded approvingly at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI see. Well, Ms. Norton, don\u2019t take unnecessary risks. Avoid these characters, should you encounter them again.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cSure, sure. Don\u2019t worry about the bulls, by the way. We talked them around. They won\u2019t be looking into the explosion.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent! That will be reflected in your recompense.\u201d He sounded fucking distracted. \u201cI need to speak with my fellows on this, they may know who those fellows are. Any relevant information will be passed on. Be careful.\u201d He hung up.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought that was pretty fucking good, with the goddamn terrorism angle and everything.\u201d I smirked over at Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> He shook his head amusedly. \u201cBravo.\u201d He paused. \u201cDid you say something about snakes earlier?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. Zelda\u2019s not a snake woman, as it turns out, but keeps snake women, or some shit.\u201d I stood and stretched.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know...\u201d Billy Mack looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes. \u201cYou already have an egg.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked fucking sternly at him. \u201cSnakes are reptiles, as are crocodiles. Power over one might give someone influence over the other.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d I texted Liz. \u2018Have a moment to talk?\u2019<br /> <br /> My phone rang a few minutes later. \u201cHey doll.\u201d I explained what had happened on our end, condensing for time. \u201cHow about you? Can you discuss things vis-a-vis snake women?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re working for Zelda. Snake people, really.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gestured the others in the car, and put the phone on speaker as I started out for Whacko Bob\u2019s Watermelon and Lemonade Stand. \u201cHave you met Zelda herself?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz made an affirmative noise. \u201cShe herself is something like Erasmus, but of a different faction. She said he would call her one of the Deceived. I said uh-huh.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh. Most Mummies work for the gods of the underworld. The Deceived, or Akham-Urtu, don\u2019t.\u201d Billy Mack nodded goddamn thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is the word she used for herself. She\u2019s in town looking for Mr. Erasmus, they are not friends. And what a coincidence - we aren\u2019t either.\u201d Liz smiled. \u201cShe\u2019s gathering \u2018pawns\u2019 to move against him, as he\u2019s far too powerful to move against directly. It seems she was working with a particular agent when he was assassinated. She presumes he was killed by Erasmus, but as she said \u2018it is the vanity of immortals to assume all players are pieces in her game\u2019. She\u2019s hot when she talks like that.\u201d She sighed. \u201cShe\u2019s not responded to my innuendo however, so she\u2019s either straight, boring or both.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack chuckled. \u201cOr dead.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack leaned back in his seat. \u201cYou haven\u2019t rolled her over and checked?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fuck?\u201d I gave him a look.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe doesn\u2019t have much experience dear, he thinks you can roll someone over and check their sexuality. Could you move him away from the phone?\u201d Liz\u2019s tone was light. \u201cShe has expressed that she won\u2019t make me into a pawn. We\u2019re having tea.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes. \u201cDid she say what the fucker wanted from her in return?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. I can ask.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019d be good. Even without, this does give us an idea on a potential motive. Though... the \u2018gentleman of the road\u2019 shit doesn\u2019t seem like Holt\u2019s deal.\u201d I tapped my fingers on the steering wheel.<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cI do believe she\u2019s trustworthy - she keeps referring to him as a pawn, and never me. I think it mean she wants me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cOf course it fucking does.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s just doing the aloof thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave fun at your tea.\u201d I smirked over at Miranda.<br /> <br /> Liz sighed. \u201cI\u2019ll report after.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd we\u2019ll give you a call is we run into anymore Tick Tock men.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a shame that portal to the Hedge isn\u2019t larger,\u201d Billy Mack mused as we pulled into the parking lot in the fucking artsy neighborhood we found ourselves in.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Hedge doesn\u2019t need their goddamn car. Or their clocks.\u201d I got out of the car and looked the small shop over. Its glass door and large windows were barred and it looked fucking cozy inside.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shrugged. \u201cIt would be amusing. Particularly if they went looking for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda shook her head. \u201cI\u2019ve never been there and based on what I\u2019ve heard, I don\u2019t think I want to.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled over at her and put an arm around her waist as we walked up. A bell rang as the door opened. We\u2019d just barely been able to take in the shelf closest to the door, with its array of watermelons, fresh tomatoes and Venus flytraps, when a sharp looking dame in a flowing kimono, with long dark hair and dark eyes. She looked to be about four foot eight - her hair was long enough to sweep the goddamn ground. The smell of lilacs followed the swing of her hips as she walked to greet us.<br /> <br /> \u201cHello! My name is Mary.\u201d She looked at each of us as we gave our names. \u201cWould you like some of our award winning lemonade? We offer free samples.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat sounds excellent.\u201d Billy Mack smiled at her and we each took a small sample cup. I took a small sip. It definitely deserved those goddamn awards.<br /> <br /> She smiled broadly. \u201cWe have alcohol to spike it with, if that\u2019s what you would like.\u201d<br /> <br /> I followed her over to a particular shelf, doing my best to keep my eyes off the sway of her hips as Miranda walked next to me, sticking close in the narrow aisles. There was a whiskey or two, nothing special, but it made a nice mix. Most of the options were fancy fucking wines and champagnes and vodkas from goddamn Uzbekistan. The next shelf over was filled with taxidermied monkeys and kukris.<br /> <br /> As I wandered off to look at them, Mary looked around at us. \u201cAnything else I can help you find?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs Whacko Bob available?\u201d Billy Mack asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d Mary smiled. \u201cLast I heard, he was in the Congo. He has me to look after this place.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked around. \u201cIt is a nice place. We came across the name in the course of our work. It sounded intriguing and you do have many curiosities.\u201d<br /> <br /> She followed his gaze. \u201cI can\u2019t take all the credit. But there is something in my store for everyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve heard that before...\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d She tilted her head. \u201cAnd who has been stealing my phrase.?\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man smiled slightly. \u201cDo you know a Mr. Ox?\u201d<br /> <br /> She was fucking taken aback. \u201cI wouldn\u2019t have expected you to. You are... not his usual clientele.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe are private investigators. We run into all kinds of people.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes grew goddamn large. \u201cI - has something happened to a customer? We are a close knit group, all of our advertising is word of mouth...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cNo, a customer\u2019s ex-husband.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Well, I hope he deserves what happened.\u201d Mary sighed in relief. \u201cFeel free to look around.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you.\u201d Billy Mack nodded.<br /> <br /> She went back to the counter and we started walking the aisles. Miranda took my arm and spoke softly in my ear. \u201cShe\u2019s not human. I think she\u2019s a spirit of some kind.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked to Billy Mack. \u201cWant we should...?\u201d I tapped beside my eye. He nodded.<br /> <br /> I put on my sunglasses and popped Aura Sight. She was definitely some kind of supernatural fuck and her aura had a familiar feel. It was kinda like a spirit\u2019s, in the same kind of way that an Angel was, but she was no goddamn Angel. I couldn\u2019t see any outside control or any red flags, she just seemed to honestly want to make a sale.<br /> <br /> I looked away and killed Aura Sight as my phone fucking buzzed. It was Liz again. \u2018Out safe.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018The spirit proprietor of Whacko Bob\u2019s is goddamn hot.\u2019<br /> <br /> I was about to fill the others in on what I saw when Billy Mack beat me the hell to it. \u201cShe could be an ice giant, I suppose.\u201d<br /> <br /> I blinked, then looked slowly over at the four foot eight dame behind the counter, then even more goddamn slowly back to him. \u201cRight.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. Miranda waited for him to elaborate and when he didn\u2019t, she looked to me. \u201cYou seem to trip over hot women all the time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, she stumbles before she gets to them.\u201d I flipped Jack the fuck off.<br /> <br /> \u201cNow, Jack, Gabe is very physically adept. She rarely stumbles.\u201d Billy Mack chided him, a twinkle in his eyes.<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes at them and moved over to the next shelf, where there was an eclectic collection of books - \u2018Are You There God, It\u2019s me, Margaret\u2019 was next to the writings of De Sade, with \u2018The Lesser Key of Solomon\u2019 on the other side. She also had a goddamn full set of the 1976 World Book Encyclopedia. I poked around there a little more and found a biography of Macho Man Randy Savage next to a collection of maps of the underground city of Seattle. I flipped through the latter, getting a good look at each map in case I needed it later.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Billy Mack approached Mary at the counter. \u201cOne other thing, Ms. Mary. I would like to rule out your customer, Ms. Rhonda Crumb, as a suspect - I don\u2019t believe it is her, but we need to check all the angles.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor one thing, I recommend being careful looking into Rhonda Crumb.\u201d She shifted to the side. \u201cI had heard Virgil died, but I don\u2019t know how I could rule her out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded seriously. \u201cI am aware that some of the items you have here are somewhat... outside of the box. Now, I am not asking what she purchased-\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head fucking quickly, interrupting him. \u201cOh, I never disclose procurements.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut in general...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are you asking?\u201d She raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> The g-man met her gaze goddamn seriously. \u201cAnything that would control an alligator.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head again. \u201cNo, or any other sauroid. Are you working for his employers?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack sidestepped the question. \u201cWe\u2019re looking into his death. It does appear that many had reasons to kill him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, if I\u2019d decided to kill him, it would have been spectacular.\u201d Mary grinned brightly at him.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow, a smile creeping up on his goddamn face. \u201cBecause it always should be, or do you have a reason for him in particular?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, I never met him.\u201d She shrugged, her hair swishing like a tail. \u201cBut I don\u2019t do things halfway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shared a look with Miranda as the two began fucking flirting, and went back to the book of maps. Once I was done, I looked back over at them and sighed. I cleared my throat. \u201cYour ride\u2019s leaving.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man smiled at Mary, her hair still swishing. \u201cI shall have to return when I\u2019m not on duty. I would like one of those watermelons, before I go.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWonderful! I believe you\u2019ll find it more flavorful than you are used to - more intense, less water filled.\u201d She rang him up and smiled as she waved goodbye.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re gonna run goddamn DNA tests on that watermelon, aren\u2019t you?\u201d I grimaced at Billy Mack as we got into the car.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course.\u201d He smiled at me.<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes as the engine roared to life. \u201cI guess it\u2019s better than just snacking on a cheese and sausage tray because the secretary of the person who sent it was fucking terrified.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned at me. \u201cI\u2019m reasonably certain Mary is not a Gentry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cReasonably...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ve seen a Gentry, correct?\u201d He raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cFair. She is some kind of fucking spirit, but different. Kinda like an Angel is.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful. \u201cI found out she was afraid of pollution and global warming. Also, someone stealing her hoard, being bound to service and a sword called Hawk\u2019s Talon.\u201d The name was in goddamn Icelandic.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou got fucking giant from that? Sounds more like a dragon.\u201d I glanced in my rear view.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere are dragons that are spiritual creatures who can take human form,\u201d Miranda put in.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat also occurred to me. Giant is merely what I said first. I thought it best to not elaborate in her shop.\u201d Billy Mack smiled fucking fondly. \u201cShe is a charming and intriguing individual.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda looked at me. \u201cYou have a horny group.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled and Billy Mack looked sternly at us. \u201cShe is a vivacious young woman is all...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLemme stop you right the fuck there.\u201d I shook my head. \u201cWhen a man your age says \u2018vivacious young woman\u2019, they sound like a goddamn creeper.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA creeper would use clairvoyance... actually, I probably should.\u201d Billy Mack\u2019s eyes went white, as he shrugged. \u201cAs one supernatural that can take human form to another, she is a sharp dresser.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda frowned. \u201cA robe and titties hanging out?\u201d I glanced over at her, mouth quirking.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked into the distance. \u201cI was referring to the particular titties themselves, her human suit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSee? Fucking creepy.\u201d I nodded to Miranda. She gave me a slight smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cMhm. Such precision.\u201d Billy Mack blinked a few times and his eyes returned to goddamn normal. He noticed Jack staring at him. \u201cShe was moving around the shop at an inhuman pace, precisely realigning everything that had shifted to a fraction of an inch.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pulled into the parking lot. \u201cGreat. An OCD Icelandic dragon spirit who knows Mr. Ox. No wonder you want to fuck her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Going inside at the agency, Cecilia wasn\u2019t at her desk. After a moment she came out from the back. \u201cOh. Hello. Ms Covington is back here.\u201d<br /> <br /> We followed her back. \u201cSo, success?\u201d Liz smiled at us as Cecilia sat in her lap.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t fucking like Tick Tock men.\u201d I leaned back, holding up the wall.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo they taste good?\u201d Liz perked up.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cSure.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cThey are Abyssally tainted, so I would advise not. It wouldn\u2019t agree with your digestion. Plus, the danger of being erased from past existence is great.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I don\u2019t want to be part of any weird reverse It\u2019s a Wonderful Life scenario.\u201d Liz shuddered.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe God-Machine shares your feelings Speed. And things high on its hit list are often bad.\u201d I raised a goddamn eyebrow at him. \u201cOften. Not always.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz smiled at him. \u201cThat\u2019s why I spend less time fighting the God-Machine and more getting ass.\u201d She looked at each of us. \u201cSo what\u2019s on the docket tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> I stretched. \u201cI have an actor to talk to and...\u201d I turned to Billy Mack, \u201cI could use your help.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d He cocked an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need someone who owns a building in a rough part of town that could be renovated into a theatre and also has lost a sister. Plus someone else with a conviction for drag racing.\u201d I walked a coin across my knuckles.<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cCertainly.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave Shelley a call using Vivian\u2019s phone and voice. \u201cHey! You working tonight? If not, you up for a date?\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley smiled. \u201cI\u2019m not. Are you thinking dinner, or Netflix?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was thinking dinner first. There\u2019s an interesting pizza place I\u2019ve heard of.\u201d Billy Mack sat down at the computer.<br /> <br /> \u201cPizza, huh? I can try it.\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled. \u201cIt seems a litt