tient.\u201d<br /> <br /> She stepped closer to me. I looked sympathetically at her. \u201cDo you have a place to stay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can stay at my sister\u2019s.\u201d She took another step closer. \u201cYou... you can\u2019t put me up?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry doll.\u201d I shook my head, biting my lip. \u201cWhy don\u2019t you get together some thing for an overnight stay. I\u2019ll make sure you get there safe and that they don\u2019t fucking follow you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack jerked his head towards the hallway and I followed him out while she packed, staying where she could fucking see me, my back to the door. \u201cI was thinking a pact - we could make her sister\u2019s place safer, and leave some surprises here, in case they try again.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cA good plan. Draw one up, I\u2019ll get her to sign it.\u201d He started drawing one up and I went the hell back inside. \u201cHey doll. Jack\u2019s drawing up a contract - I wanna get you all the goddamn security I can, and an official contract looks good for the records.\u201d She nodded, nervously. \u201cAnd, Ginny? Don\u2019t come back here, for the day. We\u2019re going to leave some shit here for whoever it was.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked pleadingly over at me. \u201cThanks Gabe.\u201d Thanks hadn\u2019t sounded so much like please in awhile, but she didn\u2019t ask again.<br /> <br /> She signed the contract, barely fucking reading it. The ride to her sister\u2019s was uneventful, if a little longer than necessary - I went the long way round, keeping an eye out for tails. Her sister was happy to put her up for the night, smiling somewhat confusedly back at me.<br /> <br /> I looked over at Jack, smiling wryly. \u201cWhen it rains, it fucking pours, I guess.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> <b>Trust in Me</b><br /> <br /> It had been, Adria Watson decided, the most surreal week of her life.<br /> <br /> Dr. Hargrove had been an excellent advisor for the Political Canadian Society the past few weeks. He was a history professor, sure, but he knew a lot about youth movements, socialism, and that sort of thing, and with his guidance the Political Canadian Society had been expanding it\u2019s membership, and was even looking at maybe having a convention on campus. When she went for a late night meeting with Dr. Hargrove the other night, she as proud of how things were going.<br /> <br /> So was he, as it turned out. Enough to feed her some of his blood, making her feel stronger and more confident than ever before. She was not sure what all of it meant, but a growing feeling she had was that the notoriously nocturnal professor may be a vampire. Which would make her something more like Renfield, maybe, but she was not much of a fly eater.<br /> <br /> But it did put an almost humorous take on this evening.<br /> <br /> Adria had gone to Kiki\u2019s to hang out a bit with Callie and possibly meet Louise or something. Then in came Naomi Cruz, who was certainly a\u2026complicating factor in her life. Since meeting the Latina, Adria had both sometimes disliked and frequently desired her intently. Naomi was involved in many of the same cliques, and while she never argued against the Politically Canadian Movement, she never identified with it per se. She often danced around it, and their debates sometimes bordered into flirting. Then Naomi all but disappeared for a week, leaving her feeling bereft\u2026and frustrated, feelings that were similar, as it would turn out, to Deanna Lee, the girl Naomi was stringing along. The result was, in retrospect, perhaps Adria\u2019s biggest mistake, hard though it was to regret the encounter.<br /> <br /> Tonight, Naomi was all smiles and charm, and moving in for the kill faster than Adria was prepared for. Then Callie and Penelope were there, one thing lead to another, and now Adria was mummified to her neck and hanging suspended horizontally seven feet