 little anger.<br /> <br /> Adria nonetheless looked defiant, despite being suspended in the air. \u201cSo am I a meal? Do you want me to beg? Because I will not. Even if I end up like her, \u201c as she glanced at the mummy on the bed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2026?\u201d The Spider glanced over and smiled, \u201cOh, that\u2019s just Am. She likes it when I do that. Can you breathe okay Am?\u201d The mummy wriggled happily.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra looked back. \u201cListen, Adria, you are not here for me to torture. Your business with Naomi is your business, and you two can work it out between you. I am looking to expand my influence beyond my worshippers, and you have a large social clique, and are well respected, so I had been planning to talk to you even before the vampire grabbed you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHargrove. It figures.\u201d Adria sighed, \u201cHe is your enemy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA god does not have a mere Vampire as an arch enemy. We just have competing spheres of influence. And I am not one to kill a vampire out of hand for hunting in my territory. I am going to have a word with him. In the meantime, though. No seeing him alone, no drinking his blood.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what do I get out of it? Aside from not being eaten?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh you are going to be my dinner. It happens to all my inner circle. But you will survive the experience with no ill effects.\u201d The Spider smiled. \u201cBut I want to give you more of what you want, in exchange for your influence.\u201d The Spiders\u2019 legs shifted, almost like she was pacing, one leg onto the bed one onto a table, as Clytemnestra\u2019s body was moved slightly forward. \u201cYou want power. Power over people. To no longer be the outsider, like in High School. Serve me, I can give you power. Stan will only make you his tightly controlled servant. I won\u2019t control you, like you even now feel the pull of his blood. Serve me, and do so with your mind all your own.\u201d<br /> <br /> Adria suspected the offer was not going to get any better for her.<br /> <br /> \u201cFine, we have a deal. Can you\u2026.put me down now?\u201d Her voice was hopeful.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra smiled. \u201cWhen you wake, you will be quite free to move.\u201d She leaned in and bit the bound girl\u2019s neck, sucking greedily on her. Adria\u2019s head began to spin, as her extremities numbed. She was not sure if she screamed or not. She tried to keep conscious as she felt herself within the fluid swirling and tumbling down the Spider\u2019s gullet, but soon blacked out.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> When she woke, she was warm, and unbound. The bedroom was empty of webbing and almost so of people, and while both were fully clothed, she was slightly horrified to find herself waking beside a sleeping Naomi.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, being bound and eaten by a giant Spider wasn\u2019t a dream.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIII</i><br /> <br /> The Tick-Tock Men are a left handed Path of Mages, and can be found in <i>Legacies: The Sublime</i> for <b>Mage: The Awakening</b>. The Free Council are one of the core groups for Player Character Mages. Mummies, Deceived and otherwise, are part of <b>Mummy: The Curse</b> and more can be found there. Man, this story is getting complicated, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Ginny Right is Bobby Right\u2019s ex-wife, and co-owner of Mavericks. The two sort of just torment each other, as Bobby uses the place to hook up with younger women and Ginny gets as much money from it as she can. Both are friends of Gabe. Ginny has had a thing for Gabe for awhile, but tends to be a bit repelled by Gabe\u2019s language. Bobby brings her in to help judge wet T-shirt contests.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time, where I traumatize my players with a haunted hospital, and we discover just what Madame X is up to. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:58:19-07:00","id":907854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=907407#post907407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Man, this story is getting complicated, isn\u2019t it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You aren't kidding - I practically need a plot map to keep track of who is linked to what.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T18:10:45-07:00","id":908018,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel better there is overlap. For example, Crumb's death (in the weird apartments) touches on Madame X (from the investigation of the Brand Corporation) and Holt, who they saw at Kiki's meeting with Carla who is working for Sanderson whose wife attacked Gabe with a razor. There is a lot interconnected in the city","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T01:01:49-07:00","id":916712,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to the Night Train Detective Agency. A lead in the case leads to our villains finding themselves in a horror story. There are stories for both Kilroy and Clytemnestra after, which reflect offspring dealings with NPCs referred to on screen.<br /> <br /> You should be sure to read it alone in the dark. Cuz it\u2019s so, uh, unbearably cheerful. Yeah.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> The next morning we all gathered at the Agency, except for Jack, who texted to let us know he had fucking cover business. I sat down in one of the chairs in the conference room, swinging it from side to side slightly. \u201cOK, leads. Whacko Bob\u2019s was a bust but it was a goddamn long shot anyway. We could do a little B&amp;E, if we wanted to really rule Rhonda out, but my gut says that shit\u2019s not a priority.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cI agree. I can do dragon hunting on my own time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d I tapped a pencil on the table. \u201cThe Zelda angle is probably a better one. It sounds like he was having her track down the Visitor.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. The Visitor, or at least the otherworldly being she was after, can sense mages and other reality hackers. Zelda is good at that sort of thing - she was able to peg me as a Demon right off. It\u2019s why she came to speak to me in person.\u201d Liz smiled. \u201cThat and my charm.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe w... shit.\u201d I shook my head. \u201cI forgot to ask. Did she actually meet with him that day?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cShe did. He asked her if it was alright if he spent the night there - she got the impression he was meeting someone else.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked off to the side, considering. \u201cThat does have two angles looking at the goddamn Visitor.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could use Madame X.\u201d Billy Mack refilled his coffee cup. I blocked him from refilling mine and topped it off from my flask. \u201cThe import/export business has some sort of records surely. Even if the Visitor isn\u2019t Madame X, she might know something of the other.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeed does have an in with the receptionist.\u201d Liz gave me a shit-eating grin.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cIndeed. I was thinking Speed could distract her while I remotely accessed her terminal. There would be an indication if I did so, but I\u2019m sure you could be distracting enough without endangering your relationship.\u201d He raised an eyebrow at me.<br /> <br /> I sneered at him. \u201cSo that\u2019s that. I got nothing to look into the fucking \u2018data leak\u2019.\u201d I looked around but the others didn\u2019t offer anything. \u201cWhat about \u2018BE A PAL\u2019? I\u2019d lay goddamn money MWGriffin is Michael Fucking White.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wouldn\u2019t, but I wouldn\u2019t lay money that it isn\u2019t either.\u201d Liz looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can look into that fairly easily.\u201d Billy Mack shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like a first step then.\u201d I nodded. \u201cOnly other things I can think of are canvassing with the sketch of the goddamn gentleman of the road, but Jack and Terry\u2019d do it better. And... Erasmus.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz raised an eyebrow. \u201cI could talk to Zelda again to get leads on him.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grimaced. \u201cI\u2019m not sure I trust the shit she\u2019d give us, given it\u2019d be pointing us at her enemy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cConfidentially, I\u2019m not positive she\u2019s the good guy,\u201d she said from behind her hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut... that Erwin fucker is on the other side.\u201d I grinned at her.<br /> <br /> She chuckled. \u201cWell, he\u2019s certainly a bad guy, regardless.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cIt is absolutely possible that neither is the \u2018good guy\u2019, from our perspectives.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz shrugged, waving fucking airily. \u201cTwo millennia spanning immortal creatures are having a shadow war in our city, and one is hot.\u201d She inclined her head towards me. \u201cAnd the other has Holt.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTo be fair,\u201d I mused, tapping my chin, \u201cshe did have Crumb. Clearly mummies have goddamn bad taste in pawns.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd she didn\u2019t want me to be one. She clearly wants me.\u201d Liz smiled. \u201cI can still go speak with her and imply I\u2019m interested in working with her, without signing on, and see what she has to say. We can always take her information with as much salt as necessary.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cSounds good. That gives us a solid fucking line up for a day\u2019s worth of work.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. And after that day\u2019s worth of work, I need to confront Dr. Hargrove about ghouling Adria. I have control now, but he does still have pull. She has been told not to go near him, and I want to make sure she is not endangered. Particularly after my pleasant morning.\u201d Liz had a smile like the goddamn proverbial canary-catching cat.<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes at her. \u201cWant back up?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded thoughtfully. \u201cObvious muscle would be nice. If he makes a move against me, I intend to web him and flee, but it would be nice for that to prove unnecessary. I do hope to incite cooperation, not rivalry, he simply needs to understand that I like Adria and she belongs to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I opened my mouth to say something and thought fucking better of it. \u201cRight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs charming as Jack\u2019s idea of waking him up in his haven is,\u201d she smiled goddamn fondly, \u201cI do believe it would get us off on the wrong foot. I believe I will have Adria ask him to meet her in his office, and go in her stead. I would like to make a display of power that is less... insulting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d I nodded and finished off my spiked coffee. \u201cNo way our work takes us til nightfall. I\u2019m up for whatever you need.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack stood. \u201cAs am I.\u201d He nodded to us as he went back to his computer in the lab.<br /> <br /> About ten minutes later, the g-man called me over. \u201cWhat am I looking at?\u201d I asked him.<br /> <br /> \u201cI found a dynamic IP associated with the account MWGriffin and no name, however...\u201d I sighed goddamn impatiently at him. He fucking frowned at me. \u201cHowever the username is also used on an urban exploring website. He\u2019s never written anything, but he has posted a number of photos.\u201d<br /> <br /> He moved out of the way to give me a better look. At first glance, they were all of an abandoned hospital, but some shit was off. For one, any of the pictures with more than one goddamn room in frame, when compared to the pictures of each room itself, made it clear the rooms were bigger on the fucking inside. A fleeting afterimage of a female silhouette that looked a hell of a lot like the Visitor showed up in a couple as well.<br /> <br /> More importantly, a couple of the pictures showed pieces of an old, inactive bit of Infrastructure. It seemed fucking familiar to me and after a moment\u2019s study, I realized it was designed to process my gathered despair. I pointed the Infrastructure out to Billy Mack. \u201cWe\u2019re finding this goddamn hospital.\u201d I scrolled down and indicated the silhouette. \u201cAnd we\u2019re charging Mr. Gone for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I read the posts following MWGriffin\u2019s, where the community brainstormed about the location. One fucking troll posted an address that led to a rough and tumble Latino bar. There were a couple of accusations of \u2018shopping, specifically of the pictures with the Space Needle in them, one poster insisting they\u2019d heard legends about the hospital, and another poster, a JSSteele, who claimed they had a good idea and were going to check it out. That was about two goddamn weeks ago and they hadn\u2019t posted anywhere in the forums since.<br /> <br /> MWGriffin had a few other posts, all of them just fucking picture posts. Most of his posts, however were nothing but red x\u2019s. The only pictures still showing were of the goddamn water wheel. I backed off to let Billy Mack start to fucking fiddle with maps and texted Jake. \u2018MWGriffin?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018No. Demon?\u2019<br /> <br /> I was disappointed. I\u2019d hoped it was another known Demon sharing Infrastructure, or at least Michael Goddamn White. \u2018Puts up pics of... interesting places.\u2019 I sent him the address to the forums. \u2018MW maybe?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Unsure. Maybe either way.\u2019<br /> <br /> Billy Mack cleared his throat. \u201cI\u2019ve used the views from the windows in those pictures to narrow it down to a neighborhood - the area with the theatre in it. I could narrow it down further with more time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr we could just fucking beat feet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUrban exploring it is then.\u201d He smiled at me.<br /> <br /> We found Cecilia in Liz\u2019s goddamn lap again. At a look, Liz peeled Cecilia off and sent her away. \u201cMWGriffin posted pictures of my goddamn Infrastructure that had the fucking Visitor in them to an urban exploring forum.\u201d I leaned on the door frame.<br /> <br /> Liz blinked. \u201cI should probably change. Naomi will come around back, so she can avoid Cecilia.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded and head out to the car as Liz used Alibi to split Liz off. Naomi came around the back as we got to the parking lot. She was wearing sturdy jeans and boots and a shirt that read \u2018I got laid today, what about you LOSER\u2019. She waved and held up a fucking backpack. \u201cI got my pack - water and spray paint!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd your camera.\u201d Billy Mack looked at her goddamn sternly. \u201cWe are PIs and this is relevant to a case.\u201d He paused. \u201cAnd twice, actually.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi rolled her eyes and shouldered the pack. \u201cYeah, yeah. Let\u2019s go before I\u2019m as old as you two. Shotgun!\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at Billy Mack. \u201cYou brought the duct tape, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I believe Terry still has it in his pockets.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> We found the hospital after only a little driving around. It was a tall imposing building that looked long abandoned. It had another of Terry\u2019s goddamned doomsday cult\u2019s symbols tagged on it. We need to ask him what the fuck that means. Billy Mack got a weak ping back from the building using Resonance, so there were no Angels, Demons or active sources of Aether inside.<br /> <br /> The lock on the front door had been forced long fucking time ago. Naomi smirked at us as we walked up. \u201cThis place was a hospital right? At your age, it should all be familiar to you.\u201d I rolled my eyes.<br /> <br /> The lobby was covered in graffiti. An elevator was centered on the far wall, flanked by two doorways. The one on the left was completely splattered with blood, looking all the world like some fucker had exploded.<br /> <br /> \u201cBlood first?\u201d I looked at the other two. They shrugged, so we went left.<br /> <br /> That door led is to a hallway with three numbered doors on each side. Glancing in the first door on the left showed a graffitied examining room, complete with fucking tongue depressors and paper covered beds. That was as far as our artist friend had gotten, seeing as the other five examining rooms lacked any kind of spray paint decoration.<br /> <br /> One was decorated in blood though. The trail from the doorway led into one of the rooms, whose furniture looked like it had lost a goddamn fight. The bed had even lost its clothes, the paper covering torn and jagged at the head. The blood petered out there, but the body it came from was nowhere to be seen.<br /> <br /> The room across from that one had no fucking furniture at all, just a goddamn gaping hole leading to what was apparently a basement from the look of it. The shaft went between rooms, but we could just barely make out a hole carved in the side at the bottom, that led into deeper darkness than we could see though. I could see Billy Mack shifting as he peered curiously down. \u201cOne level at a time seems best. Besides, my Infrastructure is up, not down.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. I still think this place warrants... preparations.\u201d He gestured with his shield.<br /> <br /> I shrugged and shifted myself into a jittery tri-wheeled vehicle with extendable and detachable extension. I moved jerkily, teleporting in small jumps at a time and reading the vibrations I got back to get an idea of movement in the dark.<br /> <br /> We\u2019d just finished transforming when a loud shriek fucking split the air, followed by the sound of running feet ending in a goddamn smack of flesh on metal, then something started pounding on the door at the end of the hallway. When we took a step towards it, it stopped. <br /> <br /> Once we got close, Clytemnestra stopped us with a long golden leg. \u201cThere are two voices whispering on the other side of the door, wondering if they\u2019ve been seen. There\u2019s no smell though, so it\u2019s probably ghosts.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s no movement. Goddamn this place is fucking creepy.\u201d I looked over the door. It was pretty standard for a hospital, though the bolt was placed to keep people in, not out. It wasn\u2019t bolted at the moment though.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey think they\u2019re on their way out.\u201d Clytemnestra looked to me and I shrugged and opened the door.<br /> <br /> The hallway continued on, curving to the right, We could see three small surgical theaters before the curve blocked out line of sight, and no goddamn graffiti. We were peering into the first theater when a golden leg tapped my shoulder. \u201cThree things, moving jerkily on two legs, are coming this way.\u201d<br /> <br /> By that point, I could sense the fucking movement as well. Kilroy made a gesture to be still and I nodded before freezing in place. Clytemnestra scattered into a pack of spiders. It wasn\u2019t long before the three humanoid figures rounded the corner. They were dressed as orderlies, masks covering their faces, and moved like a goddamn movie Frankenstein. Surgical implements of various kinds sprouted from their wrists.<br /> <br /> Kilroy and I had the same idea and we both aimed carefully and shot the lead construct in the head, putting him down fucking instantly. Clytemnestra dropped onto the third one in line, webbing it up quickly, plastering it to the wall. The free one took a swing at me, missing by a mile as I jerked behind it. Two more quick shots later and that one was also missing a head. With all the threats down, I executed the last one, finishing off what Clytemnestra\u2019s spike to the eye had begun.<br /> <br /> I nudged one with an extended arm. \u201cWell they\u2019re not cryptids...\u201d I looked unsurely at Kilroy.<br /> <br /> He nodded, kneeling next to the pile of them, looking them over carefully. \u201cThey appear to have been constructed within the last five years, which is since the hospital was abandoned. I can tell at least... eight people were used for parts, between the three of them here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t like this fucking place.\u201d I jumped back, keeping an eye out for any more surprises as Kilroy finished his examination.<br /> <br /> Continuing down the corridor there were two more of the smaller surgical theaters before the hallway ended in a T intersection. A sign read \u2018Operating Theater\u2019 to the left and \u2018Offices\u2019 to the right.<br /> <br /> I looked at the others. \u201cLeft hand rule?\u201d They shrugged again and we headed left. As soon as we rounded the corner, a terrified person ran through me. \u201cFucking. Creepy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere certainly are a lot of ghosts here.\u201d Kilroy looked ungoddamnperturbed.<br /> <br /> The window to the large operating theater was covered in what looked like a splash of fresh fucking blood on the inner side. Kilroy peered through the window as I got out my lock picks, blistering the air when they didn\u2019t work.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can hear movement on the other side.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kilroy nodded at Clytemnestra. \u201cAs can I, but I don\u2019t see anything moving.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo... do we want it open?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe might be attacked by inanimate objects, but the sound of it.\u201d Kilroy looked goddamn thoughtful.<br /> <br /> I looked around and jerked my head at the window. \u201cBut is it worth it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Kilroy shrugged. \u201cI can\u2019t see much. The blood might indicate a new victim.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe might could help them,\u201d Clytemnestra offered.<br /> <br /> I tried the door and found it open. \u201cNo wonder I couldn\u2019t fucking pick it.\u201d I smirked at the other two.<br /> <br /> Kilroy\u2019s brow raised as he looked around the inside. \u201cThat\u2019s disconcerting. The operating theater I saw was pristine, and fairly standard, if old fashioned.\u201d He looked up. \u201cWhat sort of thing would those restraints contain?\u201d<br /> <br /> He was looking at the restraints hanging from the theater's goddamn ceiling. There were restraints everywhere - along the walls, on the beds, in the floor, as well as the ceiling ones. They, the instruments, and the table were rattling in place and everything was covered in old bloodstains. From the look of things, there had been a serious fucking fight in there about a year ago, though much of the blood was older than that. None was fresher.<br /> <br /> After we backed out and shut the door, I looked at Clytemnestra. \u201cI wonder if Robin knows about this goddamn place.\u201d She and her friends were my first thought as to who might come and fuck up the day of whoever used to run this s