ights were on. Then I went to wait.<br /> <br /> He had a confused look on his face as he rounded the goddamn corner. His eyes widened when he saw me. \u201cI didn\u2019t do it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot this time.\u201d I smirked. \u201cYou have a record.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d he sighed.<br /> <br /> I started flipping a coin. \u201cI thought you might want to not.\u201d<br /> <br /> His look turned suspicious, but I could see a hint of interest. \u201cWhat are we talking about?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m in the business of fresh starts.\u201d I snatched the coin from the air, and started walking it over my fucking knuckles.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should talk to Chad next.\u201d He smirked. \u201cUnless you only talk to good people.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cI do try to work with people that will make the best use of a fresh start.\u201d<br /> <br /> He rubbed the back of his neck. \u201cDefinitely me over Chad then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike all creatures of the modern world, I run on paperwork.\u201d I offered him the contract.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis\u2019ll really wipe my record clean?\u201d He eyed it.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt really will.\u201d He signed it.<br /> <br /> <br /> The next morning, I watched Miranda walk over to refill her coffee cup. Maybe there was something to this moving in business. Not that I had yet, but a few of my things may have migrated over. Why it\u2019s so hot when a woman wears your shirt, I\u2019ll let Billy Mack quantify. I\u2019m happy just to fucking enjoy it.<br /> <br /> Miranda gave me an amused look when she caught me staring. I smirked. \u201cSo, beautiful, mind coming into work with me again? Billy Mack wants to pick your brain about this Madame X.\u201d I explained, as best I could, what had gone down at the goddamn hospital.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know how much I can tell you, but I\u2019ll be happy to come along.\u201d She smiled and tilted her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess we better get dressed then.\u201d<br /> <br /> The others were there and gathered in the conference room when we showed up. I pulled out a seat for Miranda and spun the one next to her around to sit in it backwards. Liz smiled at us. \u201cI have good news. Robin is firmly on our side. She\u2019s not talked to the Burning Man yet though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHopefully that will go well.\u201d Billy Mack passed me a half full cup of coffee. I topped it off from the bottle in the nearest filing cabinet.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s deciding what\u2019s best. If it comes down to me versus the krewe, her choice is me, but we\u2019re hoping it won\u2019t - we\u2019d rather an alliance, as Dinner wants.\u201d Liz smirked. \u201cWe\u2019re trying to get the others on our side. Comestible will be so pleased.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded and smiled at Miranda. \u201cIt\u2019s good to see you Ms. Asbury.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda smiled slightly back. \u201cYou as well. Gabe was telling me about the hospital.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRobin was to me as well. It seems there\u2019s an amorphous, light absorbing things with many legs, arms, and mouths in the basement. They went down first and after their weapons didn\u2019t work, they left.\u201d Liz shifted slightly. \u201cThe ghosts were protecting the thing. Well, torn between protecting it and warning the living to leave. There\u2019s no records of that hospital anymore, by the way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was former Infrastructure. It might have been the God Machine's doing,\u201d the g-man pointed out.<br /> <br /> Liz looked fucking thoughtful. \u201cBut it wasn\u2019t dismantled... I suppose something might have gone deeply wrong and they washed their hands of it. The Sin-Eaters didn\u2019t run into anything like the Visitor.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sipped my coffee. \u201cWhen did they hit the place?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSix months ago, I believe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cShe may not have set up shop yet. Those pictures were from two months ago and they had no fucking sign of her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked at Miranda. \u201cYou said Gabe told you about the Visitor?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. I don\u2019t know what she is or what she can do - I know about the spirit world, and the Abyss, but not wherever she\u2019s from. It sounds like she can manipulate reality enough to know Infrastructure can modify things. It might even be painful for her to be here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI transcribed the formulae written on the walls. They shouldn\u2019t cause you the harm they did me.\u201d Billy Mack slid the paper over.<br /> <br /> Cecilia arrived and went to sit on Liz\u2019s lap. \u201cGentle, gentle!\u201d Liz fucking yelped.<br /> <br /> Miranda knitted her brow at them and took the paper. \u201cI\u2019ve gazed into the abyss and it winked. I can handle it.\u201d She frowned, slightly. \u201cThe void didn\u2019t give me vertigo... they do resemble magical formulae, perhaps a parody...? The Free Council mages might understand more of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed heavily. \u201cI\u2019d be happy to shove it onto the jackasses, but they wouldn\u2019t give me my Infrastructure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey would probably attempt to tinker with it, to make it work in their idiom.\u201d Miranda nodded thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, and it\u2019s mine.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave me a look. \u201cBased on what we saw, it took the hospital Infrastructure and modified it with other Infrastructure pieces, human bits, etc. It looked like a portal.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda thought for a moment. \u201cIf so, it\u2019s unlikely to destroy reality, though you probably wouldn\u2019t want to be near. After all, they opened in the law offices, and while there were lingering effects, they do still work there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, localized at worst...\u201d Billy Mack began.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut -\u201d I interrupted him. \u201cMy Infrastructure is local.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda hid a smile. \u201cMy guess is that it will remain intact, but... I really can\u2019t know for sure sweetheart. Most of what I\u2019m going on is that it didn\u2019t bring the Brand Corporation building down.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned, a thought occurring to him. \u201cThe power magnitudes involved... all those ghosts were not enough power.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cThey weren\u2019t the right kind of power, that\u2019s all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe she simply inherited them when she killed the necromancers.\u201d Liz nodded at me. \u201cShe seems more... benign. She might be willing to make a deal, she was smart enough to contact the import/export company after all.\u201d She paused thoughtfully. \u201cThough she may simply have a power to know who could get what she needed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOur knowledge of the Infrastructure involved might make it more efficient,\u201d Billy Mack mused.<br /> <br /> Liz continued. \u201cAt least, she didn\u2019t want to face us on her own. She probably won\u2019t simply tear off our faces.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cecilia fucking shuddered. \u201cThis all sounds really unpleasant. I\u2019m glad I wasn\u2019t there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe might have thought you were mages.\u201d Miranda looked at Liz. \u201cShe is quite cunning if she evaded Gone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah.\u201d I leaned back in my goddamn seat. \u201cCrumb was after her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz smirked. \u201cIf it was Crumb, not Gone, the company apparently didn\u2019t rate her a high threat.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cecilia looked between us. \u201cIf Crumb let it out, maybe it was a \u2018you break it, you fix it\u2019 situation... I mean, my cousin did find that altar in his office.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda looked at me and mouthed \u201cCousin?\u201d I shrugged. She looked back over at Liz and Cecilia, a measuring look in her eyes. Then she sat in my lap.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a shame Jack\u2019s not here to sit in Billy Mack\u2019s lap,\u201d Cecilia said under her goddamn breath, smiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. While there are multiple suitable candidates, Jack is not one. He\u2019s more Vivian\u2019s speed.\u201d Billy Mack\u2019s smiled quirked.<br /> <br /> I was distracted from that image by my fucking phone beeping. I checked the message from Ginny. \u2018I\u2019m told there\u2019s lots of blood at my house.\u2019<br /> <br /> I answered quickly. \u2018On it.\u2019 I looked at the others. \u201cWe need to go by Ginny\u2019s.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s lots of blood there.\u201d I brushed my hair out of my face.<br /> <br /> He sat up straighter. \u201cOh?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cI believe Jack\u2019s Home Alone trap caught a burglar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz patted Cecelia\u2019s leg. \u201cWe\u2019ll deal with Naomi\u2019s vampire problem tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cecilia smiled at her. \u201cI\u2019m glad you put up with her shit. She must give good head.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u201cNot as good as you.\u201d Cecilia kissed the top of Liz\u2019s head and got up to go back to the front desk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T01:03:02-07:00","id":916716,"title":"","content":"<b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> Shelly Waters yawned and rolled over to reach out and pull her lover back into her arms. But her blindly seeking hands came up empty and her eyes fluttered open to see that she was indeed alone. Her lips quirked down but as she turned and sat up she could hear the muffled clink and rattle of dishes from the apartment's tidy little kitchen. She smiled and shook her head. Before Vivian she'd never had anyone bring her breakfast in bed. It had been endearing and sweet and totally unexpected to wake up to after their first night together. Since that point, it had become a ritual for the petite woman to slip away from her bed and return with almost lavish fare that always looked like something Shelly had only seen while watching one of those food porn cooking shows.<br /> <br /> She stretched and slipped out of the bed, deciding that since she was awake that perhaps she'd surprise Vivian for a change. She reached for the robe out of habit but paused, considering returning it to its hook. There was a little thrill of naughtiness at the thought but she instead slipped it on and tied it as she moved to the door that separated her bedroom from the greatroom/kitchen that made up most of the limited space she could afford. She opened the door carefully and peeked out.<br /> <br /> Sure enough, across the room in the micro kitchen Vivian was moving about in just a frilly little apron that she'd apparently brought with her in her bag. Shelly started to step forward but something made her pause. Vivian was moving about with a quick almost mechanical efficiency, juggling all of the various elements with an uncanny precision. Shelly's smile soured as she watched, unable to put her finger on just what was wrong with the scene but feeling quite suddenly uncomfortable. Then Vivian turned from one task to another seamlessly and Shelly saw her expression, or rather, lack of one. The woman was utterly calm and focused, there was no sign of that twinkle of mischief in her eyes that both thrilled and worried Shelly. There was no humming or grin or anything. <br /> <br /> Shelly withdrew and closed the door as softly as she'd opened it. All she could think of was how Vivian looked more like she was at task in a lab than whipping up breakfast for her lover. It was all too easy to picture her making bombs with that exact same detached air. She moved back to the bed and sat, pulling her legs up to hug them close and rest her chin on her knees. She wished she'd never read those news stories. She just wanted to forget what they'd said. What the woman in her kitchen had done. Allegedly done... She tried to correct herself but it felt weak. They hadn't found her innocent, they'd dropped the case because all of the evidence had evaporated. In that way it was worse than if she'd been convicted. She'd gotten away with it. The images of Vivian looking neither repentant in her guilt or horrified in her innocence flickered unbidden to her mind's eye. How could she love someone who was capable of such a terrible thing? How could that madwoman be the same person she'd fallen into bed with last night, the same woman who'd laughed and cuddled with her? She wished she'd truly been joking when she'd asked Viv about that explosion last night. She was going to have to talk to her about this at some point. But then what? If the woman denied it she'd never be able to really believe her. But what if she didn't? <br /> <br /> \u201cWake up sleepyhe- Oh! You're awake.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelly jerked up with a start to see Vivian standing there in her cute pink frills and lace apron that looked like it had escaped from some perverted anime and holding a tray so artfully arraigned that only the fact that the aroma was so delicious gave one the will to touch it. Her eyes were bright and adoring the way they only were when they were alone together and she caught her lower lip in her teeth as she looked down shyly to perfectly strike that weird mix of innocent and sultry. <br /> <br /> \u201cIs something wrong Shelly-chan?\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelly shook her head and moved to stretch her legs out and scoot back to sit against the headboard. \u201cNo,\u201d she answered just a little too quickly, \u201cNothing. I was just... thinking.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian moved to settle the tray over Shelly's lap and then to carefully straddle the woman's legs and settle in facing her across the tray with a bright smile. \u201cIt is entirely too early for thinking darling.\u201d She plucked a strawberry from the tray and whisked it through a tiny bowl of cream before offering it to Shelly's lips.<br /> <br /> Shelly smiled. \u201cYou really don't have to do this every morning you know.\u201d She parted her lips and took a bite, chewing slowly as she watched Vivian bring the remaining half to her own mouth and claim it before licking the drops of juice and cream from her fingertips. \u201cIt's very nice, but I would be happy just to wake up with you next to me sometimes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded as she leaned forward far more than required to feed Shelly another bite. \u201cYou know how much I like making you happy Shelly-chan,\u201d she purred wickedly as she fed her lover the next bite.<br /> <br /> Shelly chewed and tried not to squirm. \u201cWe're not going to finish eating if you keep that up...\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian kissed Shelly lightly and then grinned wickedly as she eased back. \u201cOh you're going to eat every. Single. Bite. Before anything else happens.\u201d Her left hand drifted down to brush the woman's knee lightly. \u201cAnd I haven't even begun to tease you...\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelly groaned and couldn't help but squirm again at the brush of those fingertips along her leg. It was so easy to let everything else slip away when Viv was being playful like this. Shelly closed her eyes and sighed, she didn't want to have that conversation right now. Hell, she didn't want to have it at all. She'd had it too many times already. Vivian might be the first woman she'd fallen for, but she was the same sort of mysterious and dangerous type that always swept her off her feet but never, ever, stayed for the long haul. And she believed her when Viv claimed she wanted to, because they always wanted to but it was like that awful story about the scorpion and the turtle her mother had told her when she was little. Sooner or later she was going to end up getting stung again but today, she decided, wasn't going to be the day. So she pushed her doubts down and opened her eyes as she leaned forward for the next bite with a smile. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra's Yarns</b><br /> <b><br /> Questions and Answers</b><br /> <br /> Elizabeth Covington knocked on the door to Robin Graves\u2019 house. It had only been a couple days since last time, but the circumstances were very different. This time, Robin told her to come here. She ran her fingers through her hair and adjusted her sky blue blazer, which matched her slacks. Was she nervous?<br /> <br /> The doll-like woman answered the door, and pulled the Spider inside and into an embrace.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my beloved, sweet stupid girl. Why did you go to that hospital?\u201d<br /> <br /> After a moment, Liz pulled back and straightened herself up, regaining her dignity.<br /> <br /> \u201cInvestigating Infrastructure. In retrospect, it is clear it was a trap set by Michael White.\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin led her inside to the living room, where just a few days ago she had tried to escape her magnetism. \u201cHave a seat I\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you knew about the hospital and said nothing to us of it?\u201d The Spider sat on the loveseat and looked expectantly at her.<br /> <br /> Rationally, Robin knew Liz was being unfair. But her fears of losing her made the words feel like a punch in the gut.<br /> <br /> \u201cListen, sweetheart, I\u2026first, some Krewe information is on a need to know basis\u2026second, I could not imagine why, on earth, you or your agency could possibly want to go into an abandoned hospital in a bad part of town we had seen no ro- angels in.\u201d Robin quickly corrected herself as she sat next to Liz. \u201cAnd I did not want Kilroy to find out and want to investigate.<br /> <br /> The Tempter\u2019s stern expression shifted to a wry smile. \u201cThat makes sense.\u201d<br /> <br /> Abruptly, Robin pulled Liz to her. \u201cDamnit I could have lost you\u2026\u201d She kissed the Unchained deeply on the lips for several moments, then on her neck. And again.<br /> <br /> Liz snapped out of her reverie and glanced around as she felt her shirt being unbuttoned. \u201cIs Kaylee here?\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin straddled the Spider on the loveseat, finishing unbuttoning her lover\u2019s top. \u201cHer Nana picked her up before you got here. You say you want to be mine? Prove it now!\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider smiled. And she did.<br /> <br /> <br /> Liz sat her phone down next to the bed and stretched. She had spent an excellent couple of hours with her lover, and the nap afterwards had done much to recharge her physical and emotional batteries. Night had fallen, and Robin was clearly awake next to her, lying on her side looking away. Liz ran a hand over the Bound\u2019s pale shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay, dear?\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin turned to Liz, \u201cWell, I guess that settles that, then.\u201d She shifted so she was facing the Spider. \u201cThis isn\u2019t casual.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor me, it never was,\u201d the sad-eyed woman propped her head up with her elbow. \u201cI am glad you are coming around.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happened in the hospital?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz frowned. \u201cIf I answer that, can we please actually talk about this relationship? Not doing so is what caused the problem in the first place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFine,\u201d Robin laid on her back, and turned her head to look at the Tempter.<br /> <br /> \u201cGhosts, mostly\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are mad, \u201c Robin looked sadly at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cA passage to the basement\u2026.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you fight the Beast?\u201d Robin sat up. Liz shook her head. <br /> <br /> \u201cHeard, never saw. At that point, we were taking it one floor at a time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat thing killed two of us. We could make it afraid with fire, but bullets and weapons did not hurt it. It seemed to spawn a lot of human and some animal limbs and features, like from different people,\u201d Robin looked down, then up. \u201cFrom either people or souls it absorbed, we were not sure. Those it killed came back though.\u201d Robin leaned forward. \u201cBut you wouldn\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz kissed her nose.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am serious here, stop!\u201d Robin giggled. Liz giggled back. \u201cI am trying to have a serious conversation with you and you are kissing my nose!\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz kissed her nose again. <br /> <br /> \u201cDamnit Lizzie, stop that,\u201d Robin was laughing fairly hard now. Elizabeth nuzzled her face then leaned back again.<br /> <br /> After a few moments, Liz continued.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe were looking for a thing from outside our universe as part of a murdered Mage case\u2026not like with the house, but just a\u2026\u201d She paused. \u201cAn outsider. Visitor. She is in there trying to jury rig an abandoned Infrastructure to try to go home. We think she killed some sort of Necromancer\u2026we killed a few of their pets.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d Robin was back to lying on her back again. \u201cThey were there when we were. They hid from us, wisely, but we were in no shape to pursue after fighting the Beast.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow long ago was this?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSix months\u2026ish.\u201d Robin began doing math in her head. She yelped when her lover moved to lay on top of her, facing her again. She felt Liz\u2019s hot breath on her face, her dangling hair touching her ears, her breasts pressed on her own.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo more distractions. We. Talk. About. Us.\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin looked in the deep, dark eyes. Her late husband flickered there, as did the Burning Man, but in the end, there was only the deep pools that were the eyes of Elizabeth Covington.<br /> <br /> Robin swallowed heavily, and gave her answer.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIV</i><br /> <br /> Kilroy got many successes to analyze the altered Infrastructure, and paid the price. Speed did not get enough to seriously damage herself; the successes to understand it were compared to Resolve, the differences taken as Lethal. <br /> <br /> Oh man I love running haunted houses. Give me a haunted house over a dungeon any day. And this place has a complicated history, and it has changed since the Visitor/Madame X arrived and killed the mad Moros Mage that had been there. And of course, Michael White was here.<br /> <br /> Jack\u2019s player had to miss, but rolled out some work as his new cover Miguel on his business, and Cover hunting.<br /> <br /> Okay well I think that covers things. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:18:15-07:00","id":917126,"title":"","content":"What, precisely, does Speed mean by &quot;her Infrastructure&quot;. I <i>think</i> it is the despair processing one, but as possessive as she is of it, I get the feel it is something like Infrastructure maintaining something about her now, rather than historical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T00:28:55-07:00","id":920235,"title":"","content":"Nah, it's the despair processing one. She has a deep interest in figuring out what the GM used her for, and was planning on trying to kludge something together with the theatre Infrastructure, since it was, well, similar? But having found something that resonates more directly with her former job, she's not about to let some weird spirit dame to ruin it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1471-levinserra","name":"LevinSerra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1471_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T02:34:56-07:00","id":924828,"title":"","content":"After the fiasco in the hospital, it is back to dealing with the Rights\u2019 investigation. Jack pops up again and the team gets moving.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> I called the number Jack had left, sitting on my desk and resting my chin on Miranda\u2019s shoulder, an arm around her waist. \u201cHey, Miguel, right? Can you get a message to Jack? His Home Alone trap caught somebody.\u201d<br /> <br /> He made an affirmative noise. \u201cWhere would you need him to be?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can pick him up wherever - I dunno where the fuck he is, and I know I\u2019m more mobile than him.\u201d<br /> <br /> He gave me a pair of streets. \u201cI think you will find him there at that corner.\u201d<br /> <br /> Miranda kissed my cheek as I hung up. \u201cI think I\u2019ll leave the bloody crime scene investigation to you. I have some projects to work on anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright beautiful.\u201d I stole another kiss after I hopped off my desk. I left her chatting with Cecilia.<br /> <br /> Jack was waiting at the fucking corner Miguel had told me and hopped in quickly. He waved away the cloud of smoke Liz blew at him and asked, \u201cSo, we find a body or what?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe haven't found shit - Ginny was just told there was blood.\u201d I rolled my eyes at Liz who raised an eyebrow at me over her cigarette.<br /> <br /> \u201cBy who?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz shrugged. \u201cHer sister, I presume. It\u2019s just a guess, but she is staying with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> The door was still locked, and not forced in. Most of the blood was on the stairs - it looked like a goddamn group of them had filed up, the lead one had gotten the brunt of Jack\u2019s trap and fallen on the rest. Two others had hit their fucking heads hard enough to leave bloodstains of Billy Mack to analyze.<br /> <br /> Jack used Synthesis to confirm that, and also learn that a fourth fucker had been far enough back to avoid a fall, instead running panickedly through the house. He was able to trace their entry and exit to a particular window, which was unlocked.<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck.\u201d I used gloved hands to flick it locked again. Billy Mack looked at me, eyebrow raised. \u201cThat window was locked. And there\u2019s no sign of tampering.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat has your friend done to attract Demonic or Angelic attention?\u201d Billy Mack flexed his hands, activating his sensors.<br /> <br /> I sighed and shook my head. \u201cNo goddamn clue. Which is fucking worst case, since Angels are the ones that don\u2019t fucking need motives.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged and moved over to the stairs, running his hands over the bloodstains. Liz watched him idly, dropping ash in a houseplant. After a moment he frowned. \u201cTwo of them were reptoids, both in human guise.\u201d He looked at me. \u201cOne set of fascimilated DNA was of a human female and matches the predominant DNA found in trace samples elsewhere in the house. The third is fully human.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr a goddamn Demon.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded at me. \u201cI believe their intention was to replace her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz sighed heavily. \u201cJust what I needed to worry about.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy her, is what I continue to return to.\u201d Billy Mack frowned thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is one of the two owners of Mavericks. It is a popular place,\u201d Liz offered.<br /> <br /> A fucking light came on in Billy Mack\u2019s eyes. \u201cThere was the other reptoid. Their fascimilated identity was male.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz dropped ash on the goddamn plant again. \u201cWe could try and figure out a way to test Bobby. If the reptoid was copying him, that makes it more clear what their plan is. If he\u2019s currently a reptoid, we have someone to question.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat should be easy enough. We simply need to discreetly obtain a DNA sample,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out matter of factly.<br /> <br /> Liz screwed up her face. \u201cNot. It.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged. \u201cSpeed can pull him away from people, and I can pull him away from consciousness.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhoa, whoa, fucking whoa. You\u2019re not gonna punch Bobby because he may be a goddamn reptoid.\u201d I glared at the fixer.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy not?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCause he\u2019s my friend, for fuck\u2019s sake.\u201d I rolled my eyes at him.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled, looking between us. \u201cWell, Speed did give him a name, figuratively speaking, so I can\u2019t sleep with him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLook - I\u2019ll go talk to the fucker, let him know someone\u2019s after his ex-wife and maybe him. He finished his drink, I get him to goddamn refill and the old glass goes to Billy Mack, before hitting the dishwasher.\u201d I gave Jack a dirty look. \u201cNo muss, no fuss.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about his mistress?\u201d Jack asked.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cWhich one?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed, rolled his eyes and changed the subject. \u201cYou want I should take care of arrangements for Ginny? She\u2019s throwing herself at you and your dance card seems pretty full.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNever underestimate how small one can write.\u201d Liz gestured airily with her goddamn cigarette holder.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d I shrugged, ignoring Liz. \u201cI was thinking of offering my place. I\u2019m... not using it so much, these days.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cI should go with you. I need to see Ginny, so that I can keep tabs on her via clairvoyance.\u201d His phone beeped. We waited as he read. Mostly patiently. He glanced over at us after just about five fucking years, and jerked his head. \u201cYou were recently memorizing maps of the undercity of Seattle, correct? It appears MWGriffin...\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz interrupted him. \u201cOh hell no. No. We need to deal with this before we go somewhere to die. No.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes at her and took Billy Mack\u2019s phone. MWGriffin had made another post to the urban explorers forum, this time with a collection of pictures of the undercity. Most of the pictures showed various patches of goddamn glowing mushrooms. The green white glow was echoed in the big fucking moths.<br /> <br /> I focused on the signs, to see if I could get an angle on where it was - the undercity was a goddamn big place. I found a sign warning people away from the river and was able to get a fix. \u201cBased on some of these angles... there\u2019s about a twelve mile stretch of the river in the northwest section of the city that this could be in.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat!\u201d Liz blew out a cloud of smoke. \u201cNow that we have pinpointed the area we\u2019re not going to because we're tied up helping Gabe\u2019s friend who wants to bang her, then maybe we can move onto the other very important things we are in the middle of.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeaking of important stuff, when we go to the college, we should look up Hargrave\u2019s address. It\u2019s not likely to be real, but it may be a place to look into, if things go south.\u201d Jack brushed his jacket back from his goddamn gun, distractedly.<br /> <br /> Liz sighed. \u201cIf things go south, I\u2019ll just eat him.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack made a fucking frustrated noise. \u201cI didn\u2019t just mean tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked sternly at them. \u201cAs for this case, given there were three reptoids and a human, I agree with Speed, the human was likely a Demon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow do we get reptoid minions?\u201d Jack grinned at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have one.\u201d Liz dropped ash in the plant. She looked around at our fucking confused faces. \u201cJimmy?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack waved her aside. \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure he\u2019s not our minion.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, if Cecilia asks, he\u2019d do whatever.\u201d Liz smiled goddamn predatorily.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019d hate us for it.\u201d Jack met her smile, more ruefully.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful. \u201cI could see about acquiring one, if needed.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged. \u201cNeed is a strong word. I was just thinking.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, with that settled... Liz, why don\u2019t you head to see Ginny with Billy Mack - he needs to see her and you can talk fucking anyone into feeling safe. Jack and I will do more canvassing. We\u2019ll meet up at Mavericks in a few hours, when Bobby\u2019s likely to be there.\u201d I looked around the room, making one last sweep.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. And as far as Ms. Right\u2019s arrangements?\u201d Billy Mack looked at me.<br /> <br /> I let out a long breath, thinking. \u201cA hotel\u2019ll be safer, more goddamn public. If she doesn\u2019t agree, my place is still any option. Just make sure she knows I won\u2019t be around much.\u201d I ignored whatever the hell expression was on Liz\u2019s face and tossed Billy Mack my key.<br /> <br /> <br /> Liz knocked twice on the door at the address I\u2019d dropped Ginny off at the evening before. The voice that answered was colored with suspicion. \u201cWho is it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe are friends of Gabe Norton. We\u2019ve checked out Ms. Right\u2019s house, and we thought she would appreciate an update.\u201d Liz smiled fucking brightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs Gabe there?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz shook her head. \u201cWe have another case going on at the moment, we had to split our forces.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ginny\u2019s sister opened the door, a goddamn disappointed look on her face. \u201cOh well, come on it. I\u2019m Phyllis by the way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m Elizabeth Covington.\u201d She pressed a hand to her chest, then indicated Billy Mack. \u201cAnd this is William Mackenzie.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ginny stuck her head into the living room Phyllis had led the others to. \u201cIs Gabe here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHer particular skills were needed on another case, unfortunately.\u201d Billy Mack smiled gently at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh.\u201d She took a seat on the couch next to her sister. \u201cDo you know what happened at my house? It sounded bad.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThe perpetrators returned to your house.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked horrified. \u201cThe traps that... Jack mentioned?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey hurt themselves on the stairs,\u201d Billy Mack sidestepped.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs - will Ginny be liable?\u201d Phyllis looked concernedly at the two investigators.<br /> <br /> Liz quickly moved to reassure her. \u201cNo, no. The individuals involved are the sort who don\u2019t want any kind of attention.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded in agreement. \u201cI do recommend not returning home until things are resolved. There may possibly be some danger still.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI, um, can I get some things, at least?\u201d Ginny looked between the two.<br /> <br /> \u201cCertainly...\u201d<br /> <br /> Phyllis jumped the hell in. \u201cIs Bobby involved?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked over at her. \u201cWe don\u2019t know as of yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe thinks it\u2019s unlikely.\u201d Liz shot him a glance.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, they don\u2019t get along.\u201d Phyllis gave them a significant look.<br /> <br /> Liz smiled gently. \u201cAnd if Ginny were gunned down on a busy street by an international criminal, the police would still regard him as a prime suspect. Don\u2019t worry.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised a goddamn eyebrow. \u201cHe might also be a target. It\u2019s possible whoever this is has an interest in Mavericks.\u201d<br /> <br /> Phyllis sighed heavily. \u201cWell why don\u2019t they go after him instead...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPhyllis... he\u2019s a sleazeball, but I don\u2019t want him dead.\u201d Ginny looked goddamn chidingly at her sister.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cYou said they don\u2019t want you dead either, they just want to kidnap you. Kidnapping might do him good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe will be speaking with him as well.\u201d Billy Mack tried to steer things back to their fucking purpose. \u201cWe should make arrangements for you now, Ms. Right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can stay here. Phyllis and Richard don\u2019t mind.\u201d Ginny looked at Phyllis, who nodded encouragingly.<br /> <br /> Liz laid a hand on her shoulder. \u201cThis is likely to be the first place they look for you, dear.\u201d<br /> <br /> Phyllis looked goddamn affronted. \u201cMy husband has a gun. She\u2019ll be safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you know where it is? Can you fire it?\u201d Liz raised an eyebrow at her. \u201cHe won\u2019t always be here to use it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know where it is...\u201d<br /> <br /> Ginny looked nervously at her sister. \u201cWill they be in trouble? Do they need to leave for somewhere safe too?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cIf they don\u2019t find you here, it is highly unlikely they will make trouble.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo where can I go?\u201d Ginny bit her lip.<br /> <br /> \u201cA hotel would be...\u201d Billy Mack began.<br /> <br /> Phyllis rolled her eyes. \u201cYou should get Gabe to put you up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ginny looked away. \u201cIt wouldn\u2019t be right to push her. If she offered...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack cleared his fucking throat. \u201cA hotel has security and the public nature of those accommodations only adds to that, in this instance.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFor how long?\u201d She had a resigned look on her face. \u201cIf I don't go and crunch the numbers, who know what Bobby will do? I\u2019ll wind up coming back and finding he\u2019s installed a giant pair of fake tits on the outside of the building, and a barker like from Dusk til Dawn.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack chuckled. \u201cYou should be safe in public, at the bar. We believe they intend on kidnapping and replacing you. I know it sounds farfetched, but it does mean you are likely to be safe in public.\u201d<br /> <br /> Phyllis pointed at him, then at Ginny. \u201cThey probably want to kidnap you to make you pop out babies in Juarez.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t start up on Juarez again.\u201d Ginny rested her head in her hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s no link to Juarez...\u201d Billy Mack began.<br /> <br /> \u201cHalf a dozen child soldiers, with your eyes...\u201d Phyllis shook her fucking finger at Ginny, ignoring Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> Ginny looked goddamn pleadingly at the g-man. He smiled at her. \u201cYou should be OK to go to and from the bar.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI do know a hotel near the bar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you really think it\u2019ll be safe? Ginny doesn\u2019t speak Spanish.\u201d Liz hid a smile as Billy Mack nodded gravely at Phyllis.<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe knows what she\u2019s doing.\u201d Ginny frowned at Phyllis. \u201cIf these people are working for her...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf?!\u201d Phyllis interrupted her.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack got out his PI license and a card for the agency. \u201cI understand it\u2019s strange to be speaking of this without Gabe, but as I said, we needed her specific skills in another matter.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ginny smiled ruefully. \u201cOf course. I don\u2019t want to ask too much.\u201d Phyllis rolled her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cMs. Right, if you will sign here,\u201d Billy Mack offered her a contract, \u201cofficial documentation will be helpful when I speak with the staff. And I will, so do not be startled when they are particularly attentive. We\u2019ll escort you to get your things first, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, OK! Thanks.\u201d She signed. \u201cPhyllis, I\u2019ll - we\u2019ll - step back by after the house...\u201d She looked at Billy Mack, who nodded. \u201cAnd let you know how it\u2019s gone.\u201d<br /> <br /> Phyllis hugged her sister. \u201cOK. You be safe, alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Ginny crinkled her nose as she gathered up a few things, studiously ignoring the fucking bloodstains. \u201cIt smells like one of them was smoking.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re... looking into that.\u201d Liz glanced at the goddamn houseplant.<br /> <br /> <br /> I let Jack take the lead in the canvassing - this was his sort of thing way more than mine. We lucked out after not too long.<br /> <br /> \u201cUgh. It looks like a pedophile and a serial killer had sex.\u201d One of the guys we showed the sketch to made a hell of a face.<br /> <br /> Another fucker looked over the first\u2019s shoulder. \u201cYeah, like the product of some kind of hobo anti-eugenics.\u201d<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t even have time to marvel over the guy\u2019s fucking ten cent words before someone called out from a food truck nearby. \u201cIs Skeevy Larry back around then?\u201d<br /> <br /> That got the attention of a muscled woman lugging around a trashcan. \u201cSure. He\u2019s been working over at El Carnicero.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat can you tell me about this Skeevy Larry guy?\u201d Jack slipped the trash lady a twenty.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot much, other than he looks like if Marilyn Manson had sex with what Gary Glitter looks like on the inside. He shows up every once in awhile, does odd jobs.\u201d She shrugged.<br /> <br /> Jack looked thoughtful. \u201cEl Carnicero, you said?\u201d The dame didn\u2019t look like a fucking native Spanish speaker, so I presumed it was a proper noun.<br /> <br /> She gave us an address not too far away. I stopped Jack as we got close, making sure he saw Heather before we moved right the hell on. She was loitering on a corner, eyes locked on a laundromat across the street. She felt our eyes and glanced back, clearly recognizing us. When we moved on past, she went back to playing with her lighter, her goddamn creepy stare back on the laundromat.<br /> <br /> El Carnicero was a butcher store, as you might have fucking guessed, attached to a small market. The neighborhood was more Latino than not, but it wasn\u2019t exclusively so by any goddamn means. Still, when the guy behind the counter greeted us in not-great English, it wasn\u2019t a leap for Jack to respond in Spanish. \u201cHey man. We\u2019re looking for someone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou police?\u201d He looked between us suspiciously.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, private. You\u2019ve got nothing to worry about from us.\u201d Jack leaned on the counter.<br /> <br /> He nodded slowly. \u201cAlright...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack leaned in even closer, taking on a fucking conspiratorial tone. \u201cI don\u2019t know if you heard, but there\u2019s been some weird shit going on.\u201d<br /> <br /> As soon as he mentioned the address of Terry\u2019s apartment building, the butcher shook his head. \u201cGod has turned his eyes from that place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan\u2019t argue with that.\u201d He showed the guy the sketch. \u201cHave you seen this guy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot in... 4, 5 days. He makes deliveries for me.\u201d The butcher shrugged. \u201cIt is unusual for him, but he kinda drifts. I pay in cash, anyway.\u201d He looked significantly at Jack.<br /> <br /> Jack made a face. \u201cThat guy? Deliveries?\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugg