ound the goddamn tool closet. It was locked, but he happened to have a set of particularly nice lockpicks in his pocket and he had it open in a jiffy. The tools inside were decent, but he has a way with the fucking things, and they did him fine.<br /> <br /> Once he got the pipes loosened, he was able to remove the clog. He pulled out piles of gnawed on cat and dog corpses, wrinkling his nose. After the pipes were clear, he wiped his hands off and looked up.<br /> <br /> A fucking swarm of rats were looking at him with irritation. His eyes widened, but he held their gaze. After a moment, he pointed two fingers at his eyes, then at them. The largest one narrowed his eyes as the swarm fell back, looking at him as it faded into the shadows.<br /> <br /> While he was down in the basement, Terry decided to have a look around. The first thing he checked on was the supposed to be secret door leading to the Seattle Undercity that was right where he expected. More strange was the second furnace that didn\u2019t map to anything he expected.<br /> <br /> So he got into the head of whoever built the strange furnace. Once he did, he blinked a few times. The goddamn thing was made to draw in the souls of people who died in the building and refine them into some sort of power source. The problem was it was rusted and leaking. He could fix it, he thought. It certainly hadn\u2019t been maintained in a while. He could even siphon some energy off. He winced away from that thought.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe I need to sleep first, feel a little better about myself...\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> <b>Real Friends</b><br /> <br /> The door to the house used by the Pagan student group came open as four women carried a vaguely human shaped bag inside. Callista Carson, Callie to the women in the room, moved a coffee table over to set it on. \u201cCareful with her. Easy does it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe need a place to hide Bernice here\u2026\u201d Clytemnestra looked around thoughtfully, and then realized all three girls were staring at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cHer name is Bernice?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo like Weekend at\u2026\u201d Glassy stares. Clytemnestra shrugged. \u201cNever mind. Before your time.\u201d<br /> <br /> The other three set the body on the coffee table while Callie scratched her head looking around. \u201cI had not thought about needing to hide her. I guess we can\u2019t just say our God told us to keep her here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s only for a day or two.\u201c Clytemnestra walked across the room. \u201cWhere is Cassandra? She did not answer her phone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSleeping. Probably not alone.\u201d deadpanned Angela Wilcox.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, this can get us arrested\u2026\u201d Penelope, pronounced like the Greek name, or sounding like an ungulate to people who liked annoying her, was getting worried. Callie gave her a look.<br /> <br /> \u201cWansome Pocky?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cK\u201d<br /> <br /> The Pocky seemed to calm her; so Clytemnestra directed her attention to the Psychic Witch.<br /> <br /> \u201c Maybe we should put her in a back room and I can web the door shut? If school officials come just say that is a spider problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am sure that will neither arouse suspicion nor begin a panic.\u201d Angela nodded sarcastically.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra shook her head. College students were not the best-behaved cultists. \u201cWhat if I webbed her to the ceiling; people don\u2019t usually look up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere is an ice chest.\u201d Angela grinned. The spider nodded, and Penelope went to fetch it.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy does the pagan club have an ice chest big enough for a person even before I showed up?\u201d<br /> <br /> Angela shrugged as Penelope set it down. \u201cCassandra is always thinking ahead.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGoes with the name I guess. Let\u2019s get her in here.\u201d The other three girls moved around the body while Clytemnestra moved the ice around.<br /> <br /> The front door opened, causing all four women to turn and look. China Garcetti, Amsterdam to her friends, strode in.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood, we need help here.\u201d Callie gave Penelope another piece of Pocky.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho is that?\u201d asked Am, staring at the body.<br /> <br /> The Spider continued dealing with the ice chest. \u201cI don\u2019t know\u2026a member of the tong,\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre we gonna eat her?\u201d She was still staring at the body.<br /> <br /> The room went silent as all four women stared at Amsterdam.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I am going to resurrect her for answers and to put her in our debt.\u201d Clytemnestra was talking slowly staring at Am. \u201cThat will work out better without embarrassing teeth marks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCreepy.\u201d Mumbled Angela.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah faces are a sometimes food.\u201d Callie grinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, people who aid reality destroying extradimensional entities don\u2019t get to complain about a little cannibalism right Master?\u201d Am looked from Angela to Clytemnestra and smiled.<br /> <br /> The spider opened her mouth, but Penelope was already talking. \u201cCallie have you actually eaten a face? I knew you had an oral fixation but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes kissing count? And what do you mean oral fixation?\u201d Callie took the Pocky stick out of her mouth a moment.<br /> <br /> A second dead silence across the room.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, if we are not going to eat her we get to name her, right? That is the rule, like, from farms?\u201d Amsterdam sounded hopeful.<br /> <br /> Penelope just mouthed something at her, but Clytemnestra spoke up. \u201cSo like I said I am going to raise her from the dead so we can get information and a favor owed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOoooooh. You could make a lot of money doing that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Penelope looked at Am. \u201cDid not choose you for your brains, did she?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo\u2026do concubines normally get picked for intelligence?\u201d Amsterdam looked confused.<br /> <br /> Callie glanced at Penelope, who held out her hand for more Pocky. \u201cDon\u2019t pick on Hamster here. \u201c She got out another piece for herself, too.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I mean I am food, I have to be higher on the food chain than SOMEBODY\u201d Amsterdam sighed.<br /> <br /> Penelope chose her words carefully. \u201cYou are not\u2026exactly\u2026a vegetarian Am. You are higher than most things on the food chain. And I have never seen a girl crave meat like you do. Actually\u2026\u201d She glanced at Clytemnestra.<br /> <br /> \u201cEventually we will investigate that.\u201d The spider was webbing the ice chest into a cocoon.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2026are gonna undo that before she wakes up right? I mean it would be unpleasant otherwise. \u201c Callie chewed her Pocky nervously.<br /> <br /> \u201cClawing your way from your grave is part of the rite. I say we bury her first.\u201d Angela sounded serious.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo we are not burying her at all.\u201d Clytemnestra sighed and walked down the hall, keeping line of sight to the ice chest. Outside a door to a side room, she fired a web pulling it to her, then dragged it in the room. Am looked over to Callie \u201cWhat where did you find her, anyway?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe got killed by a Japanese Grudge-ghost. A transgender one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t know there were transgender Japanese Grudge-ghosts.\u201d Am blinked.<br /> <br /> Penelope rolled her eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s the twenty-first Century, of course there are. Get with it.\u201d She looked down the hall as Clytemnestra called the girls down.<br /> <br /> \u201cGirls, two guards, all times. Makes sure Cassandra knows as soon as you can. Am join me in here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTime for a bowl first?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlways time for a bowl.\u201d Angela grinned at Am.<br /> <br /> The Spider sighed. \u201cOkay fine. But then come in here. I am going to get started.\u201d<br /> <br /> As they left, Penelope looked at Callie. \u201cYou are not gonna give her her wallet back when she wakes up, are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMust have fallen on the floor in the confusion,\u201d she said with a wink.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLVIII</i><br /> <br /> Reminder Louis/Valefor is the most powerful local Demon, roughly an equal of Scarecrow who helps the PCs from time to time. His image is based on Orson Wells in <u>The Third Man.</u><br /> <br /> Playing Kyle, I was pronouncing Celts like the Boston team. The taint hasn\u2019t washed off yet. I feel dirty. In a bad way, I mean. Okay, that\u2019s not the only reason running Kyle made me feel dirty.<br /> <br /> Markizel used several Embeds while fixing up the situation at the apartment building. Speed\u2019s player did a good job of telegraphing it. If it looks like she implied he did, he did.<br /> <br /> I was hoping to get Louis out and involved in things. Louis is a complicated character. He is doing a lot, and the PCs have nudged up on stuff involving him a few times. But this was a chance to go head to head with him a bit, flush him out of the shadows. Suffice to say, this new plot is not the only time the PCs have run afoul Valefar\u2019s schemes, but not wanting a shadow war with Scarecrow and his general distaste for killing Unchained has been staying his hand.<br /> <br /> So onward to a new session\u2026maybe with less Kyle this time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-13-2016, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:53:37-07:00","id":958929,"title":"","content":"Time to come back to the case. The fight is over, the ghost has struck, and now it is time to investigate these leads. While Clytemnestra raises the dead and Kilroy strengthens his cover, Speed takes point.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s story takes place after the end of the session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon's Monologues</b><br /> <br /> When Vivian woke up, Shelley was sitting in bed next to her, her arms wrapped around her legs. The light by the bed was on, and the one in the hall. The clock read 3AM. \u201cHey Shelley. Are you...?\u201d Shelley shook her head, fucking unsteadily. Vivian sat up next to her and put an arm around her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m OK. It\u2019s just... last night...\u201d Shelley took a deep breath. \u201cI don\u2019t even really remember what happened. Something with Kiki? I knew the place was haunted, but I\u2019d never seen her before.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure that\u2019s the first time she\u2019s gone on a killing spree.\u201d Vivian started rubbing her shoulders.<br /> <br /> Shelley leaned into her. \u201cI really couldn\u2019t tell what was going on. The crowd... I know there was a lot of screaming. And shooting...\u201d She took another goddamn deep breath. \u201cI think I\u2019m gonna take tonight off. Assuming it\u2019s even open.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t imagine they\u2019re open.\u201d Vivian chuckled darkly. \u201cAnd if they are, and somebody has something to say about you not being there, I will have words with them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know what, fair enough.\u201d Shelley managed a weak smile for her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou need a night off, after what you went through.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley\u2019s smile strengthened. \u201cI do.\u201d She paused, hesitant. \u201cCan you hang around?\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian\u2019s brow kit. \u201cI\u2019ve got a thing, later, that I have to take care of. But I\u2019ll come back right after.\u201d She pulled the shaky girl close. \u201cBut I don\u2019t have to leave for awhile.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Morning came a little fucking earlier than usual, if not particularly brighter. Still, I woke up with Miranda in my arms, so it wasn\u2019t all bad. Not even the shadowy tentacle monster in her front yard could chill my smile for too long. It didn\u2019t seem to be singing anymore, at least. She did catch me glancing out the window. \u201cWe need to keep them gem somewhere that is not here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing love.\u201d I shrugged, not completely hiding the concern on my face. \u201cIt can go back in the bolthole.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Tick Tock men are trying to get it.\u201d She sat down at the table, frowning. \u201cFighting them out of time sync is... weird.\u201d<br /> <br /> I drummed my fingers on the table. \u201cCan they track it? I mean, they won\u2019t be able to get to it in my bolthole, but will they at least know it\u2019s not here?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI assume so, but I really have no idea. I don\u2019t know how they knew it was here. All I know I was negotiating with Gone, who brought more thugs than was necessary to make sure I was thoroughly intimidated, when a car pulled up and they just started pouring out.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever I can do to make sure you\u2019re safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI certainly won\u2019t be less safe - I don\u2019t dare use it.\u201d She made a face. \u201cThe good news, if you don\u2019t like the Free Council, is that they\u2019ve had casualties. Not Mr. Gone of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cGood. The fucker hasn\u2019t paid us yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a small smile, which faded with concern. \u201cHave I mentioned recently that you absolutely don\u2019t want to fight Mr. Gone?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wasn\u2019t looking forward to it, so I\u2019ll keep trying to avoid that.\u201d I took a sip of my coffee.<br /> <br /> \u201cI watched at least two of the Tick Tock men kill themselves trying to shoot him. I don\u2019t even know how he did that exactly, just that they fired their guns and the bullet hit them in the head.\u201d She looked intrigued. \u201cWhen they used time dilation powers to shoot multiple bullets, it looked like the Tick Tock men\u2019s heads exploded. So if you have to fight him, don\u2019t attack him. With weapons - powers might work - they didn\u2019t get reflected that I saw.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back in my chair. \u201cI\u2019ll keep that in mind. Really, I like the future where he pays me and we don\u2019t fight a lot better than any others.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cOf course. I just wanted to give you a warning. He\u2019s, well, not happy with me. Because of...\u201d she trailed off, looking out the window.<br /> <br /> \u201cFido?\u201d I grinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, we\u2019ll call it Fido.\u201d She smiled at me. \u201cMr. Gone and his Free Council men are pursuing the Tick Tock men.\u201d She looked at me with a raised eyebrow. \u201cNow, you\u2019re not an Abyssal creature nor do you intend to destroy the crystal, right? I\u2019d really rather the pact I made with Mr. Gone to not backlash. If that was ever secretly the case, now\u2019s the time to tell me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cNah, neither of those. You\u2019re in the clear.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cThe Free Council will be back to talk with me about it, once the immediate emergency is dealt with. There\u2019s more of a Tick Tock man problem here than we thought.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe they just happened to be in town, for the Crumb situation.\u201d I started fiddling with a fork.<br /> <br /> \u201cPossibly. It\u2019s hard to get an idea of their numbers. They pulled reinforcements from alternate timelines, so we fought the same guy multiple times. We shot a lot of people.\u201d She frowned.<br /> <br /> I cocked my head and grinned at her. \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019re alright.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged self-deprecatingly. \u201cI sat in the back and threw monsters at them. And made their magic foul up