9re not.\u201d Jack scowled fucking menacingly at her.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled calmly. \u201cWe have prevented you from kidnapping Mr. Right. We have no intention of harming you. Do you like coffee?\u201d She nodded. \u201cGabe, I think we can release the cuffs...\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked at him fucking dubiously. Jack rolled his eyes. \u201cShe can\u2019t overpower us - and I will shoot her if she tries to run.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was more for her goddamn protection.\u201d I shrugged and got her a coffee before unlocking the cuffs. I settled back on one of the tables and put on my sunglasses before activating Mind Reading.<br /> <br /> \u2018JesusshitfuckI\u2019mgonnadiefuckdamnshit...\u2019 I winced, only barely able to maintain my concentration. I kept it running though, letting the boys drive the questioning.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack kept up the calm, soothing monotone. \u201cObviously we have you at a disadvantage, but we are prepared to be reasonable. Mr. Right is an associate of ours...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry,\u201d she interrupted him with genuine feeling, then winced away.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is our associate, so we are disinclined to let someone kidnap him and take over his business.\u201d Billy Mack continued unperturbed.<br /> <br /> Her eyes widened and she talked fucking fast. \u201cI won\u2019t, if you keep him away. Getting close to him was the hardest job I\u2019ve ever had. D\u2019you know the first thing he said to me? \u2018You know I gotta motorboat, but I\u2019ll wait a few seconds.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack sighed. \u201cThe problem with that deal is you were not working alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose I probably wasn\u2019t.\u201d Her eyes darted around the goddamn room.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe did dissuade them from trying to follow up on your mission.\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> She looked quickly down at the cup she held in two hands. \u201cThey\u2019re not... in th