r replacements foul up at specific times. Times calculated to cause the most feedback.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOur contact with the Rights makes it so we could likely convince them to make similar alterations,\u201d Billy Mack suggested.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are only human.\u201d His tone was fucking dismissive. Then again, he sounded like Billy Mack, so how the fuck can you tell? \u201cTheir ability to resist is practically non-existent. My reptoids also have counter programming that would be dangerous to implant in the Rights.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned. \u201cWe are somewhat fond of the Rights.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow. \u201cOur primary interest in this is in their protection. Do you have a time frame for the activation of the matrix?\u201d<br /> <br /> Mr. Ludwig answered quickly. \u201cIt\u2019s hard to say. Five days to six weeks. Most likely within two weeks.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat long term impact do you expect this to have?\u201d Billy Mack asked. \u201cIf we could arrange for the Rights to be away.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTo Mavericks? Minimal, provided things go right. The reptoids have precise instructions as to what to do when the operation begins to go down. And the reprogramming I mentioned will kick in. The ones chosen are fairly even tempered, as reptoids go. And Drak has guaranteed they will \u2018keep their shit together\u2019.\u201d Mr. Ludwig smiled thinly.<br /> <br /> \u201cMs. Sleet does seem to be remarkably composed, convinced though she is that she won\u2019t see the end of the day.\u201d Billy Mack smiled as well.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ludwig gave a goddamn derisive chuckle. \u201cThey normally think they\u2019re not going to see the end of the day whenever they find themselves in a strange situation. Like cats that way.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cI do believe we can come to an arrangement that will allow your original plan to proceed as you intended, without kidnapping the Rights.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well. Five days. That\u2019s the time limit.\u201d He shrugged. \u201cYou have my number now, if we need to discuss this again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed. Things are better when we work in concert. I\u2019ll be in touch.\u201d Billy Mack hung up and looked to the rest of us. He frowned at the monitor where Clytemnestra kept fucking pointing between Sleet and her stomach.<br /> <br /> I turned the goddamn monitor to face the tower. Clytemnestra protested. \u201cI\u2019m just giving her the option. It\u2019s prime real estate in there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes that mean I get to be Ginny? The last woman on earth Bobby will hit on?\u201d Sleet looked hopefully at Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> \u201cTry telling him you\u2019re a dyke next time.\u201d I took a drink. \u201cIt works. Usually.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack cleared his throat. \u201cIndeed. Let\u2019s give Drak a call and arrange a meeting. Over lunch perhaps.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOoh. What about Bangkok Pies?\u201d Sleet perked up.<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well.\u201d He called the reptoid leader. \u201cHello again Drak. I would like to discuss arrangements to return your wayward Ms. Sleet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow many Slim Jims do you want for her?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cI thought that was off the table. I was thinking a hand off, at Bangkok Pies.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drak winced. \u201cAh, that\u2019s gonna hurt. OK, 30 minutes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c30 minutes.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> We took the long way round and she was blindfolded until we got to the parking lot. She stood up a little goddamn woozily, holding fucking tight to the car frame. Billy Mack nodded to her, and we walked in separately. <br /> <br /> Once we\u2019d gotten a table and ordered drinks, Billy Mack got up and walked over to the group of five reptoids, clapping a hand on Drak\u2019s shoulder. \u201cA good night\u2019s sleep should take care of your health issue. Are any of the others hurt?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot six times through the large intestine.\u201d Drak grimaced.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s a good night...\u201d one of the other reptoids muttered. They all shook their heads though, when Billy Mack glanced at them.<br /> <br /> He nodded a goodbye and rejoined us just as Kat dropped by. \u201cThe detectives... you\u2019re back!\u201d She ran a hand across the back of my chair. \u201cAny interesting cases?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled up at her. \u201cA couple.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnything with that museum theft that\u2019s been on the news? It seems interesting.\u201d She looked around at each of us.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cNah. The public dicks are all over that shit. There\u2019s no reward out yet either. Or did I miss one?\u201d I looked questioningly around the table.<br /> <br /> She looked at me like I just told her to expect goddamn cats with her morning thunderstorm. \u201cPublic\u2019s... dicks...?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPublic detectives.\u201d Billy Mack hid a smile. \u201cThe police. Our jobs are a little lower profile than that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, of course.\u201d She smiled. \u201cI didn\u2019t mean to imply... it\u2019s just what\u2019s in the news.\u201d<br /> <br /> We ordered our pizzas and Billy Mack placed an extra order to go. Apparently Vivian had a stay-in date with Shelley since Kiki\u2019s was closed. Our food came out quick, Kat laying it down with a wink for me. \u201cFuel for your brain!\u201d I grinned back and saluted her with my beer.<br /> <br /> As we ate, Billy Mack filled us in on Ludwig\u2019s plan. I nodded approvingly. \u201cI should be able to swing it. With the attacks and all, it\u2019s too fucking hot and they need to get the hell out of town. I know a couple of con artist fuckers who would swing being them, can definitely handle a few goddamn terrorists, and even run a bar in a pinch. For a few weeks.\u201d I tossed back my drink. \u201cBesides, they deserve a vacation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure you can sell it to them. They do not seem entirely unreasonable.\u201d Billy Mack smiled. \u201cExcellent.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe six week thing will be the hardest to sell.\u201d I looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cHe said mostly likely in two. We can start at 3-4 weeks and reevaluate when the time comes. As long as they are gone within five days. The voice that was my own on the phone was quite insistent. That was a neat trick, I must say.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cIt does sound like your kind of creepy shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is very effective at both disorienting some people and giving away nothing of one\u2019s own identity.\u201d He shrugged.<br /> <br /> I sent texts out as we finished our pizza. Nikka responded to my \u2018Free later? Have case news.\u2019 quickly.<br /> <br /> \u2018Yes. Here? Say, 9?\u2019 I sent out a confirmation just as quickly.<br /> <br /> Esha was slower to respond to my \u2018You wanted to talk?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Hey.\u2019 There was another pause. \u2018I wanted to ask you about Team Tomorrow. Somewhere we can\u2019t be eavesdropped on.\u2019<br /> <br /> We worked out to meet at my office in a half hour just as the check came. My check had an extra, a card for the joint, with a handwritten message on the back, \u2018Case?\u2019 with a phone number. Once we got out to the car I showed it to the others. \u201cI\u2019ll call it after dinner. If we wanna take the case?\u201d<br /> <br /> They nodded, and after assuring them, for the ninth time, I could handle a goddamn phone call on my lonesome, so they could console their girlfriends, raise the dead and troll for homeless cultist fodder all they wanted.<br /> <br /> <br /> I made it back to the office in time, if only just. I let her in with a half smile. \u201cHey doll. What\u2019s up?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled and gave me a kiss. It wasn\u2019t precisely a nun\u2019s kiss, but she was clearly distracted. I led her back to the office. \u201cNot too much.\u201d She sat down. \u201cWe... talked about Team Tomorrow last time we spoke.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. They do enhancement type stuff.\u201d I snapped like I remembered something and pointed at her. \u201cThat guy you were talking to, at Kiki\u2019s, he had a tie tack with their logo.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve been in contact with them. I.. that is... my abilities... I think I\u2019m in danger.\u201d She took a deep breath. \u201cI\u2019ve gotten his attention and they want me to come by and see what Blue Sun, and me specifically, can do. Plus there are three new people in my hall. I can read minds, I mentioned, and they are supposed to \u2018acquire the specimen in a way that can\u2019t be linked to Team Tomorrow\u2019. They can secrete some kind of non-lethal knockout drug.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked fucking horrified. \u201cI - Esha, I didn\u2019t think that shit would get you in trouble, doll. Really.\u201d<br /> <br /> She patted my arm. \u201cOf course. I don\u2019t think you did. I can take precautions - I have electricity thing - but I\u2019d like options. I was hoping you could break in and get evidence that they were from Team Tomorrow and up to something. If I get that to the building manager, it could get them removed.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cYeah, I guess Mind Reading doesn\u2019t hold up in court.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr for my superiors.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave they followed you?\u201d I spun side to side in my chair. <br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cNot that I\u2019ve noticed. I\u2019ve spoken with the only other person I know that is connected to them, a friend of yours.\u201d She smirked at me. \u201cShe claims innocence.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked back. \u201cOh, Nikka?\u201d She nodded. \u201cSome of the other detectives mentioned she was talking to someone as beautiful as you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFlattery will get you everywhere.\u201d Her eyes sparkled. \u201cShe works with Team Tomorrow on occasion. She wasn\u2019t lying about being innocent, though that\u2019s about all I could tell - she\u2019s very resistant to Mind Reading.\u201d<br /> <br /> I moved to sit at the edge of my desk. \u201cI should be able to get any shit they have. Do you know anything about their habits, when they\u2019re in, when they\u2019re out? Party all night, live like a fucking cloistered monk, throw orgies?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cThey just moved in, I don\u2019t know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo worries, I\u2019ll just need to case the joint a bit. Will you be alright?\u201d I frowned in concern.<br /> <br /> \u201cI should be. I mean, I\u2019m not a super spy, they could get the drop on me and I\u2019m not immune to their drug. But they don\u2019t know that I know - I didn\u2019t tell Team Tomorrow I could read minds. It\u2019s a certain ace in the hole that I... well, you\u2019re special.\u201d I grinned at her. \u201cI do appreciate you telling us about a competitor under our nose, one I think is somewhat more morally suspect than Blue Sun. I found Dr. Gist very detached and curious about our subjects. Which, since I\u2019m the only subject whose name I gave out, means he\u2019s curious about me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my neck. \u201cAs long as he doesn\u2019t get too fucking curious...\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked up at me from under her goddamn lashes. \u201cI\u2019m sure I\u2019d be safe if you stayed the night...\u201d<br /> <br /> I sighed internally, and gave her a regretful look. \u201cIt\u2019s that security case, doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI understand.\u201d She looked down, then back up, a smile on her face. \u201cI assure you this isn\u2019t just a complex effort to get you back in my bed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou wouldn't have to go to that much effort.\u201d I smirked.<br /> <br /> She smiled. \u201cI will be paying you for this, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned wider and hopped up to rifle through a drawer. \u201cI can\u2019t say no to that, doll. You wanna make it fucking legit, paper trail and all, right?\u201d I wrote out a quick contract, glossing over the sticky bits like \u2018B&amp;E\u2019<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you Gabe.\u201d Her hand lingered on mine as she took the contract.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo problem doll.\u201d I filed our copy away. \u201cHey - the woman who was there when you talked to, what was it, Dr. Gist. I keep seeing her around but I don\u2019t know shit about her.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked down to the side, remembering. \u201cMs. Liu? She\u2019s one of the Tong, a bodyguard or assassin or something - a very serious sort of person. I\u2019m not sure she\u2019s still alive though... something happened last night. She was there.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a concerned look. \u201cRight. The others mentioned a ghost?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah... it\u2019s weird. I don\u2019t really remember leaving, just being out in the parking lots. I guess I panicked.\u201d That or Nikka pulled something out of a sleeve. <br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019re alright then.\u201d I cocked my head. <br /> <br /> \u201cI was talking to Nikka at the time. She was being... flirtatious. To get information, surely, but still... I wish I could be that good.\u201d She gave me a fucking significant look. \u201cShe asked me if we knew each other. Come to think of it, she asked that before she got flirtatious. It was incredibly difficult to read her mind. It was like a fog and the memories were at a distance.\u201d<br /> <br /> I frowned. \u201cThat\u2019s a hell of a thing.\u201d And it probably meant one of two things, considering I\u2019d never gotten any kinda fucking fog: either Esha\u2019s Mind Reading wasn\u2019t as powerful as mine or Nikka had a particular defense that she hadn\u2019t realized she needed against me. After a moment, I smiled at her. \u201cWell, anyway, I\u2019m pretty damn good at finding hidden things, so we can definitely handle this.\u201d I winked at her and moved to stand close to her chair. \u201cYou watch yourself, alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> She grabbed my tie and pulled me down for a kiss. \u201cAlright.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Esha had to go home eventually and I gave the business card number a call. Kat answered. \u201cHello?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHello Kat. This is Gabe Norton, the PI. You left me a card?\u201d i propped my flask up and used the distorted mirror to straighten my goddamn collar.<br /> <br /> \u201cI would like to schedule a meeting at some point, in the next day or two, perhaps.\u201d She sounded goddamn hesitant.<br /> <br /> I pulled up a calendar. \u201cAlright...\u201d<br /> <br /> She took a breath. \u201cI\u2019d rather not go into much detail over the phone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course.\u201d I tapped my desk. \u201cHow\u2019s Monday at 3 work?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> I ran my fingers through my hair. \u201cSo you know, we generally work cases as a team. Is that an issue?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh no, that is fine, as long as you trust them. Whatever you think is best,\u201d she answered quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright then. See you tomorrow.\u201d I stood up and shrugged into my jacket.<br /> <br /> She smiled. \u201cYes. Thank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I got a late dinner at fucking Johnny\u2019s before heading to my appointment with Nikka. She answered the door quickly, with a smile, and pulled me in for a kiss. I shut the door behind me with my foot.<br /> <br /> Eventually she pulled away and went to pour me a whiskey sour and herself a whiskey. I took a sip and smiled. \u201cSo, I had a talk with Cornelius.\u201d She looked at me blankly. \u201cSmarmy fuck, wears a bowtie...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, him!\u201d She frowned. \u201cAnd what did he have to say?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMostly that he was a douchebag. I mean, not in so many words but... you know how it is.\u201d I smirked at her. \u201cHe claimed the attack was made by an erstwhile apprentice.\u201d<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow. \u201cDo you think he was telling the truth?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cHe made a decent point, that he knows enough about you to know if one person can\u2019t kill you outright, a group is useless. With the Twilight thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat man knows entirely too much about me.\u201d She took a drink.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a little fucking uncomfortable.\u201d I cracked my neck. \u201cHe can look like other people - he knew where I the fuck was last night cause I made plans where a forty year old woman could hear.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyes widened. \u201cCould he look like you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I glanced up at her. \u201cProbably? I didn\u2019t go for the third degree about what the hell he could do exactly - I didn\u2019t figure it would get me anywhere.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course.\u201d She smiled worriedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe did seem disinclined to pull shit around me.\u201d I took a drink. \u201cBut that\u2019s not a tong term solution.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked at me. \u201cWhat do you advise as a course of action then?\u201d<br /> <br /> I swirled my glass. \u201cIf we can provoke a confrontation, make him realize we mean business and turn the heat up...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou do not think he realizes you mean business? He can come back from the dead, he is not a man to be startled off easily.\u201d She raised an eyebrow. \u201cYou think it will not merely make it more engaging for him?\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought back to his comments from last night, particularly \u2018That little bit of Aboriginal American Eurotrash has been one of the most interesting people for me to track in some time\u2019 and sighed. \u201cFuck, you\u2019re right. Well, like you said before, you didn\u2019t hire an assassin but between the obvious lethal intent and my conversation with him last night... we could go for his knife.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, leaning towards me. \u201cAlright.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs for how to find him, if he\u2019s telling the truth, his apprentice might be a source of information.\u201d I tapped my glass. \u201cPlus we have a first name.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou stole the body, yes?\u201d She ran her fingers down my arm. \u201cThere is evidence, leads, there surely. I do not know what else you may be able to do - all I know is that the abilities I have seen have been impressive..\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked at her. \u201cWe do have the equipment and access to run DNA.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cPerhaps I can go with you to your office tomorrow, if you think I would be of any help.\u201d<br /> <br /> I thought quickly. Kilroy could do what he needed to do fairly fucking discretely and she might have some insights. \u201cSure doll. Getting you and Billy Mack talking about those fucks could be useful and might help us not miss things. I\u2019ll let the kids know we\u2019ll have company in the morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI would be happy to talk to Billy Mack about the Harvesters.\u201d She smiled at me. \u201cTomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T15:54:25-07:00","id":958930,"title":"","content":"<b>Kilroy\u2019s transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W47-7T09:47-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> Shelly's slumber this morning seems more restful. I do hope so, she is a resilient woman but the shock of witnessing Kiki's murderous rampage was quite traumatic for her. The fatigue from improper rest cannot be helpful to her mental state and nightmares would most certainly exasperate it. She has asked Vivian to stay with her again tonight and I have promised to return after the interrogation of our captive reptiod.<br /> <br /> She is in an extremely vulnerable state presently and I am loathe to chance something misfortunate happening. Also, if her insistence on turning on all of the lights in her apartment are an indication the coming of night will be a more trying time than the midday. Nocturnal dread is a deeply ingrained human instinct. Fortunately, I should be back well before the waning of the sun's light to distract and comfort her.<br /> <br /> I have felt the strain that showing such a degree of care and concern is putting on my cover. Vivian Marley was not a selfless woman nor was she prone to such deep attachments. Too many emotional scars I believe. As much as she did crave intimacy she was simultaneously terrified of allowing someone to be in a position to inflict emotional harm upon her. However, an incident of mortal peril seems like the sort of catalyst that would bring an epiphany concerning her feelings toward Shelly Waters. Perhaps tonight or tomorrow (provided Shelly has recovered sufficiently of course) it would be the appropriate time for her to make a somewhat hesitant declaration of her feelings and open the option of possible future commitment. A touch of emotional vulnerability should help quell any doubts Shelly may be harboring. Also, given the volatile state of Kiki's, it would be an opportune time to broach a contract to secure her financially and allow her to return to her studies.<br /> <br /> I should confer with Clytemnestra once her resurrection is complete. The subtle shifting of a cover's paradigm from selfish to loving is an artful one and she has been working on a very similar adjustment with Naomi and her paramour. She likely has some useful insights on making the transition without damaging the cover.<br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W47-7T14:07-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> The interview has proven remarkably productive. Speed monitored the subject's thoughts and thus took a minor role in the actual questioning. Quietus, despite being directly cautioned against any displays of intimidation, found it necessary to threaten her both indirectly and directly. I suppose I really should not have expected a destroyer to grasp the concept of subtle manipulation. It did, I suppose, distract the subject from Clytemnestra's suggestions of devouring her. Despite having Amsterdam present and having already taken the subject's Aether, she seemed rather unaccountably peckish. Her appetite seems to grown of late and been less easily dismissed. Perhaps when we have a quiet moment I should speak to her about it. At least Markizel wasn't present. Given his fixation with fingernail removal and his lack of self censoring he might well have sent the subject into cardiac arrest. At the very least, he would have undoubtedly caused her to soil herself and I already have one too many defecating reptiles in my lab to clean up after. And, speaking of our apparent mascot, Quietus decided to ask the subject about the care and feeding of alligators on top of his menacing behavior.<br /> <br /> It was clearly a mistake to allow him to be present. I should attempt to limit Quietus' involvement in things outside of the purview of his role as a destroyer moving forward. One does not attempt brain surgery with a monkey wrench after all.<br /> <br /> Despite all of this, our subject, who goes by the name of Sleet, did give us a number to contact the leader of her team. She and the other reptoids were apparently recruited by an Unchained who later met with an unfortunate fate. They have been working freelance since that point and seem to be a reasonably competent group. Their leader, Drak, was agreeable enough to deal with.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, it would seem the interest in Maverick's is transitory. It is going to be instrumental in an occult matrix to bring the God Machine's newest Infrastructure online. The reptoids' employer, known to them as Mr Black, wishes to disrupt this.<br /> <br /> The reptoids have never seen or heard this Mr Black. All of their dealings have been through an intermediary who goes by the name of Mr Ludwig. Drak was willing to pass word to him of my desire to speak in exchange for the life and return of his wayward Sleet.<br /> <br /> While waiting for him to contact me, I called Jimmy Marsh. He was able to give me some information concerning the mercenary reptoids and Mr Ludwig. The actual Unchained was believed to have died at Puriel's hands some months ago. It seems likely, given the lack of certain disturbing and highly ingrained behaviors, that the Unchained in question is using the name to conceal their own identity.<br /> <br /> The most likely candidate seems to be a Ms Velvet. She was the partner of Mr Stripe, who formed the reptoid team before overextending himself and falling victim to hunter-killers. She would have known of them and had a powerset that seems suitable to what we know of Mr Ludwig. Also, apparently her file has gone missing from Marsh's records. A troublesome detail and he is going to inventory his files to see what other files may have also gone missing.<br /> <br /> While it is at present just a theory, I believe Valefar is behind the whole affair. It seems to match his usual modus operandi. In particular, I found the use of Vox to call me in my own voice to be a clever touch.<br /> <br /> That conversation did prove to be refreshingly civil. He wants the occult matrix disrupted. His reptoids need to be in place as the Rights to safely sabotage it. He was indifferent to our desire to remove them harmlessly so long as the replacements were in place within five days. Speed will be convincing them that we need them to go on vacation and allow a pair of stand ins to lure the 'terrorists' that have been targeting them out. If the occult matrix completes within the two to three weeks most likely, all will be well. If it runs late, there may be some complications with the Rights not wanting to be away from their business so long. But we shall deal with that if it becomes an issue.<br /> <br /> Now it is time to arrange the return of Sleet.<br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W47-7T15:13-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> At Sleet's suggestion, we set the exchange for Bangkok Pies. A simple blindfold and circuitous route seemed sufficient to obfuscate the office's location in her memory given that we seem to have resolved the affair on reasonably good terms with the reptoids. I took a moment to speak to them and to use my mending embed on Drak. He had lingering injuries from the traps Quietus set at Mrs Right's. I feel confident at this point that should we have need, we can make use of their services in the future.<br /> <br /> The meal has proved enjoyable. The owner, Kat, was present and again took time to greet and chat with us. She is a striking woman and rather pleasant company. She recalled us as detectives and asked if we were involved in the theft at the museum. We lied and assured her that we had nothing to do with that case.<br /> <br /> I ordered a second pizza to go and once we finish our meal and discussion shall take it back to Shelly. She did enjoy the food when Vivian brought her here before and I am sure she will have little desire to venture out tonight. I think a nice quiet evening of watching Netflix with pizza to nibble is in order.<br /> <br /> It is unfortunate that Clytemnestra remains occupied with resurrecting the Tong woman she collected from Kiki's. I had hoped to confer with her before having Vivian discuss strengthening the commitment between her and Shelly and setting things in motion for a contract to secure her return to school and keep her safely away from Kiki's. It is possible that Shelly will not be ready for that talk, but unless something has transpired during my absence I expect that her mental state with have normalized sufficiently tomorrow morning before Vivian departs for work, making it the ideal time for her emotional revelation. And I will still have an opportunity to speak to her before accompanying Shelly to Thanksgiving dinner to meet her parents. As a side note, Vivian has never done such a thing before, it will be important to remember to display the correct level nervousness about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> <b>Lost in the Chaos</b><br /> <br /> Kwan Jinghua woke up with a sharp gasp. Her eyes opened, and she noted several things in rapid succession. One, she was alive again. Her last memory was of the frightening Y\u016brei grabbing her face, and agonizing cold and wetness, as well as her throat tightening. Second, she was stuck to what seemed chillingly like a spider web. Third, a resplendent golden woman, the most beautiful she had ever seen, was crawling down the wall with a set of four golden mechanical looking legs. Finally, a white girl standing near part of the web was messing with her phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cWelcome to my Parlor\u201d the golden woman said, in perfect Cantonese. As she got closer, Jinghua was surprised how human, and beautiful she looked. The gold was a soft glow or haze, and golden hair. Her face was captivating\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happened to me?\u201d Jinghua pulled herself from her reverie. \u201cWhere am I and who are you?\u201d The white girl, Amsterdam she would later be told, in the corner of her vision seemed to realize her sleeve was stuck to part of the web.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra folded her human arms, her four spider limbs lifting her so she was eye to eye with the trapped gangster. \u201cI am now called Clytemnestra, a Goddess of Central America, trapped for many years. I have resurrected you to be my servant. Not my slave, but to serve me within the Tong.\u201d<br /> <br /> Amsterdam attempted to hide an attempt to pull her arm free with a vaguely casual looking stretch. It didn\u2019t work very well.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do I get out of this?\u201d Jinghua was having even less luck than Amsterdam at getting free.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you want?\u201d The Spider moved several steps back, then forward, on her long legs. \u201cI am willing to negotiate. I am even willing to give you time to think. But if I don\u2019t accept your terms, I will eat you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou drive a hard bargain\u2026\u201d Jinghua\u2019s eyes were drawn to the movement of where Amsterdam was attempting to walk away from her caught arm. She barely managed to avoid falling when she went too far forward. The gangster looked back.<br /> <br /> \u201cFine. My name is Kwan Jinghua. I work for a man locally known as Two-Chin. Not his name, but how you will find him. He likes female employees, says men underestimate us. I deal with some of his less acceptable imports. If I skim them, I will be dead and worthless to you.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider smiled. \u201cSee, from here we can see about getting you rewards, for information. Perhaps once people see your star rise, you can get recruits. But I do not intend to sacrifice you. I do not like sacrificing my-\u201c<br /> <br /> Amsterdam had been gathering her strength and attempted a run, pulling hard as she could. She did a flip in the air, landing on her back, arm and stuck sleeve in the air. Clytemnestra sighed, the long golden legs took her body over, and she wordlessly touched the strand Amsterdam had gotten herself stuck to, dissolving it. She then returned to Jinghua.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs I was saying, I do not intend to sacrifice you unless I must, even then I will give you an out. But betray me and you will be a desiccated husk. Work with me and you will be prosperous. Whatever happens to Two-Chin, even if I have to deal with him summarily, I will not make you directly betray him.\u201d A raised eyebrow. \u201cDeal?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a start, I am back from the dead.\u201d The Spider dissolved the webs holding her. Am helped catch her and get her to her feet.<br /> <br /> \u201cReport in, tell them what you like, except that a goddess resurrected you. If someone wants you punished for disobedience, I will deal with them. But we will work together.\u201d The Spider gave a winning smile. For some reason, Jinghua could not help but be uplifted by it. But then she frowned. \u201cWait\u2026where is my phone\u2026or wallet?\u201d<br /> <br /> Amsterdam gave a sympathetic look. \u201cMust have been lost in the chaos.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> Mainly role playing. Terry had to miss, but will be there tonight. Clytemnestra was using Raise Dead, which takes a long time to do.<br /> <br /> More soon, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-28-2016, 04:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T08:26:22-07:00","id":959831,"title":"","content":"So, Valefar it being brought more into the fore? I'd pegged him as behind the reptoids too as soon as the irregularity concerning Mr. Ludwig's identity was brought up. If so, it seems like his disdain for non-Unchained might be a personal signifier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T19:03:00-07:00","id":960164,"title":"","content":"Valefar has been a hidden hand since the beginning. It would be a bit unfair or misleading to say that the PCs failed to see his hidden hand in things, as he tends to keep a layer between him and whatever he is up to and the players would have to get specific enough with enquiries it would be strange to see some of the strings. Some things he is involved in semi-openly, such as Terry's plot, but non-Unchained rarely know they are dealing with him. So it is more a matter of this scheme, or more correctly this aspect of this scheme, we are aware of. He keeps more proxy's between than, say, Michael White.<br /> <br /> Presuming they are different people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:38:40-07:00","id":966898,"title":"","content":"Session 50. Wooooooooooooooooooooooo!<br /> <br /> Ahem. Just Speed this time.<br /> <i><br /> Session L</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Most people\u2019d think having the ability to fucking read minds would make it a lot easier to deal with the age-old questions every detective is trying to answer, especially that old chestnut \u2018why?\u2019. Unfortunately, it really just makes it more clear how goddamn complicated the question is. <br /> <br /> Take Nikka. I was still pretty damn sure her sleeping with me was in part the human instinct that the person you\u2019re fucking will have more of an inclination to protect you from violence. But my Mind Reading made it clear it wasn\u2019t just that, at least. Still, as far as her background went, all I\u2019d gotten was that it was definitely interesting.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s why I was up just before dawn, poking around the apartment of the girl I was fucking while she was still passed out in her bed. I wanted to trust her - I sure as shit liked her more than Douchebag McBowtie - but there was too much I didn\u2019t know and Last Place You Look was an easier hack that raking her brain for the answers.<br /> <br /> Two places lit up, the closet in the living room and the table in the spare room, the one that didn\u2019t have the shrine to an old photograph in it. I checked out the closet first. It had the usual shit, jackets and coats, as well as two mini-fridges. They weren\u2019t hard to find - the standard fucking electric buzz was evident as soon as I stuck my head in the door. Not a goddamn second sooner though.<br /> <br /> The hard part of that little foray was the high tech digital locks the fucking things had on them. Apparently though, some shit interfered with the seal last time she\u2019d shut them, so I was able to get them open with a little focus.<br /> <br /> The first one had organs in it, all packed in plastic bags labeled Team Tomorrow. No lungs though, so it seems like she was on the level with Penelope. The other was fucking full of drugs. More pharmaceutical than recreational, from what I could tell, but some of the hypos were unlabeled and I didn\u2019t really feel like testing them out. I kinda felt like testing the bottle of 1986 Chablis though, but I stuck to my flask.<br /> <br /> The table took some fiddling. It was one of those complicated fold out deals and once I got it open - treading goddamn carefully - I found a drawer full of surgical equipment. My first thought, that she occasionally took out or stuffed in clients\u2019 organs personally, was quickly discarded. These instruments were very fine tools. Even I, knowing close to jack-all about medicine and whatever is less than jack-all about surgery, could tell that those tools weren\u2019t designed to be used at any stage of the organ transplant process.<br /> <br /> None of what I found seemed particularly fucking useful to the case, but nothing else was hidden in the place so, well, I didn\u2019t bother looking. Even if it\u2019s not perfect, taking your cues from reality itself can still be handy...<br /> <br /> <br /> Shelley smiled at Vivian over a cup of coffee. \u201cI\u2019m really glad I don\u2019t have to go to work tonight. I was thinking of giving into the siren call of the mighty Netflix, but a few of my girl friends are going out, I was thinking I\u2019d join them. Something... normal would be nice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you need me to come back after work?\u201d There was a hopeful fucking note in Vivian\u2019s voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat would be nice, though you don\u2019t have to.\u201d Shelley took a sip. \u201cI can call you when I\u2019m heading home? It shouldn\u2019t be too late.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian looked goddamn hesitant. \u201cI\u2019d like to. Things are a little crazy, at the office, something might come up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley laid a hand on hers. \u201cJust let me know. I understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll keep in touch.\u201d They sat in silence for a moment. \u201cHey - I\u2019m really looking forward to Thanksgiving with your parents.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019ll be fun.\u201d Shelley smiled. \u201cI\u2019ve told them, so it won\u2019t be a surprise.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian reached to hold both of Shelley\u2019s hands and leaned in for a quick kiss. \u201cSomething happened, Saturday night, that I\u2019ve never dealt with before - when something started going crazy, I was more worried about someone who wasn\u2019t me than... I\u2019m... I\u2019m not good at that sort of thing. And I really do want to make this work.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley squeezed her hands. \u201cSo far so good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not just saying that. Which means I\u2019ve been thinking of ways to go about doing it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley brushed her hair out of her eyes. \u201cYeah... I can be looking into things with the place here as far as options...\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian took a deep goddamn breath. \u201cAlso, I know you really want to get back to school. And I know I... don\u2019t really want you going back to Kiki\u2019s. It\u2019s not safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve gotta get money...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo this whole thing I do...\u201d Shelley pulled back a little from the hacker. \u201cHold on - this thing I do, that I don\u2019t tell you about cause it\u2019s safer for you not to know? It does have its perks sometimes. I can make some things happen.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley bit her lip. \u201cListen, I do trust you. But I don\u2019t want to be supported by someone else right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cThat\u2019s not what I\u2019m talking about. There are grants, scholarships...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d be happy to have you look into that.\u201d Shelley smiled. \u201cI\u2019d be happy to look into it myself if you got me the resources to do so.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can talk to some people, make something happen for you,\u201d Vivian encouraged.<br /> <br /> Shelley kept up the smile. \u201cWe\u2019ll see how Thursday goes. Quite possibly.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian took a sip of her coffee, brow knit. \u201cI am really worried about you going back there. Not just because of the ghost - there\u2019s a reason that I end up there a lot and it\u2019s because it\u2019s a place people like me meet up at a lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut there\u2019s a code, that you don\u2019t do violence in that place, and I\u2019m pretty sure the last couple of incidents - well, they haven\u2019t been organized crime.\u201d Shelley shrugged. \u201cBut ultimately, it\u2019s neutral and normally more safe there than a lot of places.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, I know, I just worry about you.\u201d Vivian gave her a sideways look. \u201cAnd I know it\u2019s not what you want, ultimately.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley shrugged. \u201cI\u2019d rather see you burn down the service industry and I\u2019ll escape it altogether.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian grinned a moment before the serious fucking look returned. \u201cJust think about it, alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will! I\u2019ll think about the grant thing.\u201d Shelley looked at her goddamn sternly. \u201cBut I\u2019m still getting a job, even if I get a grant, and a lot of places my skill set would pay me less than Kiki\u2019s. And not have the theoretical protection it has.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m just saying... I can make some things happen. And... I care about you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley laid her hands out on the table. \u201cIf you can help me get a grant, I\u2019m definitely interested.\u201d She looked away. \u201cIt\u2019s not that I don\u2019t trust you, it\u2019s really not, it\u2019s just... I haven\u2019t known you long enough to make myself financially dependent on you. Anything more than the grant isn\u2019t fair to either of us. If things change, your options would be throw me out on the street or put up with me. I don\u2019t think it\u2019ll come to that, but I\u2019m looking out for both of us here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian chuckled. \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure if anyone\u2019s going to be throwing anyone out here, it\u2019d be you getting tired of putting up with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut we both have jobs right now, so if that happens, I haven\u2019t ruined your life. I can know that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo matter what happens, you can never ruin my life.\u201d The implicit \u2018because you\u2019re not significant enough\u2019 that I might have fucking assumed followed it in Kilroy\u2019s head was nowhere near Vivian\u2019s face. Vivian sighed. \u201cI do have to go. Just... I\u2019m not talking about supporting you myself, you know. Just making things happen so you\u2019re financially secure, independent from me, without having to work through college.\u201d Vivian stood.<br /> <br /> Shelley stood too. \u201cI\u2019ll look at information. But I think one of the things you like about me is that I do look a gift horse in the mouth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know coming like this, from is probably not the way you wanted to do this...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do want to go back to school.\u201d Shelley\u2019s eyes asked for some distance. \u201cBut I just want to read all the fine print.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian smiled and went in for a quick kiss before grabbing a jacket. \u201cI\u2019ll let you know when I\u2019ll be home.\u201d<b