back. \u2018nlm\u2019<br /> <br /> He loitered around for a moment, but not very long considering the fucking scene. So he got back to trolling for homeless folks to join his cult.<br /> <br /> <br /> After their first errand, Terry talked Billy Mack into taking him by the fucking management office for his apartment building. When they walked into the place, the large, somewhat irritated looking gee behind the desk was talking to Harvey Cannon. \u201cI\u2019m just saying, I know you know where he is. I\u2019ve got a bounty hunter or two I could call, or we could all make this easier. I don\u2019t wanna have to bring the kid in - he\u2019s got exams. But I\u2019ll do what I gotta do if you won\u2019t tell me who the guy is.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have no idea what you\u2019re talking about.\u201d The guy behind the desk had a goddamn deep voice and sounded tired. \u201cAnd I\u2019ll remind you you don\u2019t have to tell me you\u2019re carrying a concealed weapon. It\u2019s really not necessary.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, well, I\u2019ll let the kid know. I\u2019m just trying to be reasonable.\u201d He turned to go and saw Billy Mack. \u201cHow have you been?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his offered hand. \u201cGetting work done. Obviously you\u2019re doing the same.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cYeah, I\u2019m doing a little extra to help my new bounty hunter out, since he\u2019s got exams.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, a new one, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. Drake\u2019s got a lot of other things going on.\u201d Cannon looked fucking disappointed. \u201cHey, I\u2019ve gotta get going - it was good to see ya.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded to him and Terry continued up to the desk. The large man looked at him. \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry stuck a hand out. \u201cI\u2019m Terry McTavert. I live at Rapture Pines. I\u2019m very handy with tools and whatnot - I fixed a pretty horrible plumbing situation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did hear Mr. Stevens had his daily constitutional.\u201d The big man nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it was just come chewed up animal parts.\u201d Terry looked at him wide eyed.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat does sound like Mr. Stevens.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry blinked. \u201cAt least I have a name. Anyway, if you all need a superintendent for that place, I can do it.\u201d<br /> <br /> The man frowned thoughtfully. \u201cWell the last maintenance man did kill his entire family, so we\u2019ve been using temps since then. If you wanna put your application in, someone\u2019ll look at it.\u201d Terry took the offered application and filled it out quickly. The gee took it and set it to the side after a quick fucking glance. \u201cSure, why not? Don\u2019t eat any of the fungus, we\u2019re pretty sure that\u2019s what happened to the other guy. If you have the urge to begin face collecting, just go ahead and end it all, it\u2019s how it will stop.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks for the heads up. I\u2019m pretty sure I can handle anything that\u2019ll come up in that place. Plumbing wise. Maintenance wise.\u201d Terry smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou haven't lived there very long, have you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry shrugged. \u201cIt has been magical. So, lower rent? No rent?\u201d<br /> <br /> The lug cleared his fucking throat. \u201cYou\u2019ll have to work that our with the owner of your room. The rooms are privately leased.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Right.\u201d Terry thought for a moment. \u201cSite access, at least? Keys?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, that\u2019s gonna happen.\u201d He shuffled through a drawer and came out with a key ring and a folder, handing them over. Terry flipped through the goddamn thing. The word \u2018faces\u2019 was written many times, covering up a lot of the printed material. First thing on top was a not that \u2018anyone who still has their foreskin might be the enemy. CHECK.' The word \u2018check\u2019 was underlined 4 times. \u201cIf any of that makes you nervous, remember he is very, very dead.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks again. I\u2019ll keep the place running as best I can.\u201d Terry saluted him with the folder.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you\u2019re still alive at the end of next month, you\u2019ll be paid, plus you\u2019ll be paid for the time you work this month. If you murder anyone, you will not be paid for that month. If you do, please don\u2019t murder anyone who lives there - you have a much better chance at job retention that way.\u201d He stuffed Terry\u2019s application in a drawer. \u201cJust keep the water running and the shitters good. If we\u2019re lucky, the place won't explode or fall into a sinkhole or anything.\u201d He paused. \u201cNot that I think it would do that of course. I\u2019d be legally obligated to tell you.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> When everyone gathered back up at the office, Billy Mack had us swap out burner phones. The g-man explained, \u201cThe person who had Terry\u2019s phone is dangerous. She goes by Heroin and sometimes Ghost. The FBI\u2019s never been able to pin anything on her, but she\u2019s been a person of interest in numerous serious, violent cases. Standing orders are to not engage her without backup. She used to work at Whacko Bob\u2019s apparently.\u201d He smiled. \u201cShe\u2019s associated with a garden variety goon named Tar, who has also sloughed off his evidence of guilt since meeting up with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Getting all that switched over kept us occupied - I also had to reprogram the number forwarding to the number I gave Nikka - until Cecilia sent the message back that Kat was here. She brought her up to the conference room, speaking goddamn animatedly with her. I took the seat right across from her, with Billy Mack, Terry and Jack to my right. Liz was a couple of seats to my left, so that she was in the corner of Kat\u2019s eye whenever she looked at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI would like help with a case,\u201d she began nervously. \u201cThere is someone... investigating me? Going through my things? My townhouse - someone has broken in twice and not taken anything. I was at work, both times. The first time the door was forced - the second, I only know because things were moved. I think some of them have come into my restaurant to observe me but... many people watch me move around the room, so I do not know who.\u201d She looked down. \u201cI don\u2019t have much money...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you spoken to the authorities?\u201d Billy Mack asked kindly.<br /> <br /> She looked sad. \u201cNothing was taken, so... there is a lot of crime in the city, apparently? So they did not look into it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked fucking thoughtful. \u201cWhen was the last time? And the first time?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe day before last, Saturday. And the Saturday before that.\u201d She took a deep goddamn breath. \u201cI don\u2019t have much, so I can wait until I know more? I just have a feeling that it\u2019s bad.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure we can work something out.\u201d I smiled at her.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cIt is good to trust your instincts.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey do say that some of my customers are... watching-watching?\u201d She looked unsatisfied with the phrase.<br /> <br /> \u201cSurveilling?\u201d Liz suggested.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cBut I am watched a lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cYou are a striking woman.\u201d He thought for a moment. \u201cIs Saturday a busy day at work?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is either very busy or very dead, one or the other. But I never eat at home regardless.\u201d Kat shrugged. \u201cI wished to ask about rates, whether there is anything I can tell you, so I can afford to hire you.\u201d I quoted her a number. It was maybe a little lower then usual but fuck you that\u2019s why. The others didn\u2019t comment. \u201cI could afford a few days at that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo