t the pistol I\u2019d seen, handling it knowledgeably.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou seem to have had some training with it as well.\u201d Billy Mack looked fucking approving.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI had to, for the permit. I do things legally.<br /> <br /> He smiled. \u201cThat does make things easier.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYour government makes it easy to do. They don\u2019t arbitrarily change things for a king who isn\u2019t in control anyway.\u201d She frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed.\u201d Billy Mack gestured at the gun. \u201cIf you are confronted, simply indicating you have a weapon is occasionally enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded abstractedly. \u201cI have never felt as if I was followed, just watched at my store, and that began before the break ins.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned over at her, fiddling with a goddamn pencil. \u201cWe might suddenly develop cravings for spicy pizza and just... be in the area a little more frequently.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cAnd after some preliminary research, we might come by, say between lunch and dinner, to speak with your staff?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you come soon after lunch, I will only have to pay them for an extra hour, that would be perfect.\u201d She smiled at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd if you give signal that you feel eyes on you, we\u2019ll peg them.\u201d I ran my fingers through my hair.<br /> <br /> She gave us the Thai word for danger. \u201cI will recommend that to you if I do so.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes the holiday interfere with your usual hours?\u201d Billy Mack asked.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cWe will be closed for turkey day and the day after turkey day.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled. \u201cWe will plan on being by Wednesday to speak with your workers.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled back. \u201cThe last day before turkey day. Alright.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll stop by tonight after work, to see if we can get anything?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan it be 10? I have to do closing things, you understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz shifted closer, smiling. \u201cThat will be fine. Keep your wits about you in the meantime, stay where people are around and can see you.\u201d Billy Mack seconded the precaution.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI will do my best, but unfortunately I do live alone. I haven\u2019t had time to find a husband.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHusbands are overrated.\u201d I smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure you\u2019ll find... someone.\u201d Liz raised a goddamn eyebrow.<br /> <br /> Kat smiled slightly. \u201cI... thank you. I should be getting back. They don\u2019t work as hard when I\u2019m not there.\u201d<br /> <br /> We all stood. Billy Mack shook her hand and got the door. \u201cThat is how it goes.\u201d<br /> <br /> When she\u2019d gone, I sat back down, spinning my chair slightly from side to side. \u201cSo, she\u2019s a fucking penanggalan. Object reading didn\u2019t work out for her. The whole ex-husband thing - he tried to kill her when she woke up at her funeral, shot her a couple of times.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI hate it when that happens.\u201d Liz sighed goddamn knowingly.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe does seem to be making the best of her new life, regardless.\u201d Billy Mack chuckled. \u201cHer store is close to a Women\u2019s Center, I imagine a number of women with pregnancy cravings stop by.\u201d He shrugged. \u201cHer fears do seem to be focused on maintaining and growing her business.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz smirked. \u201cAh yes, one of those ruthless corporate vampires Anne Rice warned us about.\u201d She frowned after a moment. \u201cIf she has vampire hunters after her, they are almost certainly know what she is specifically for certain somehow - she is there every day. I don\u2019t know of any magical vampire-dar.\u201d She paused. \u201cThe Sin-Eaters eat there... I\u2019ll call Robin. They\u2019re not vampire hunters per se...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThey might have branched out and regardless, it would only be in the spirit of the sense of cooperation we\u2019ve been trying to build with them to consult them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know Comestible,\u201d Liz grinned goddamn predatorily at Terry, \u201cIf you stick around you might be able to get that meeting to happen. And I promise, if it looks like that will happen, I\u2019ll hold off eating you til after.\u201d He rolled his eyes. \u201cI\u2019m a giver!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt will be good to confirm their interests.\u201d Billy Mack tried to steer things back to the goddamn case.<br /> <br /> Liz looked thoughtful. \u201cThey might simply be trying to figure out her deal. She would show up as dead but not by exsanguination, right?\u201d Billy Mack nodded. \u201cShe might be something on their \u2018weird shit\u2019 list. Though they usually don\u2019t molest the phenomena unless something related to it is having problems.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back. \u201cMaybe the \u2018undead\u2019 bit means they\u2019ll look into it without related problems. That is their fucking schtick, yeah?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. I\u2019ll call her when she gets off work.\u201d Liz looked at her watch. \u201cSo about an hour and a half.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGot her schedule down pat?\u201d I smirked at her.<br /> <br /> She looked at me goddamn archly. \u201cI know when she\u2019s at work. I don\u2019t know, say, when they go to their Sin-Eating restaurants.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan you get sin at a restaurant?\u201d Terry scratched his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can get sin anywhere,\u201d Liz retorted, smirking.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cI suppose you can.\u201d He frowned. \u201cI should get to manually checking those DNA results. It will likely take all night and I was hoping to spend the evening with Shelley.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo start now and finish tomorrow,\u201d Liz suggested.<br /> <br /> I nodded along. \u201cAnd however you do, I\u2019ll see you later. I\u2019ve gotta convince two poor fuckers to skip town so we can replace them with doubles or the terrorists will win.\u201d I stood and grabbed my hat.<br /> <br /> Liz looked up at me. \u201cI could bring Naomi and provide color commentary...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you must.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t must.\u201d Liz smiled. \u201cBut I\u2019m not bringing Liz within a mile of that man. No offense.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cNone taken. Jesus fuck, I wouldn\u2019t take any cover that liked dick near Mr. Right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know...\u201d Billy Mack mused. <br /> <br /> \u201cWell you should,\u201d Liz interrupted him. \u201cI\u2019m literally 3 years old and I know.\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled. \u201cI believe Vivian could handle herself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not the fucking question.\u201d I threw my hands up. \u201cThe question is whether the goddamn fuck can handle himself around Vivian.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLet me put it this way: if you have stabbed, shot, set him on fire or broken his fingers, the situation was not handled.\u201d Liz pointed at him with her cigarette holder. I nodded as I got to the door. \u201cI mean, I could slit his throat and drink his neck juice, but it doesn\u2019t mean I handled the situation well.\u201d I thought about stopping. I didn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> \u201cDepends on whether you made a mess,\u201d Billy Mack suggested. I sighed and shut the door behind me. <br /> <br /> Liz sighed. \u201cNo, because Gabe is out a friend at that point.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T13:40:20-07:00","id":966899,"title":"","content":"After he began to search, Billy Mack looked in on Liz. \u201cThat discussion I mentioned earlier... do you have a moment?\u201d Liz nodded, folding her hands and giving him her full goddamn attention. \u201cI am interested in evolving my Vivian persona to be more capable of human attachment. I felt my cover twinge yesterday, and I know you have had a project along those lines with Naomi.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz nodded thoughtfully. \u201cThe trick is to move slowly. Those twinges will happen, but humans themselves evolve. If you move slow enough, it shouldn\u2019t be a big risk. You intend to strengthen Vivian\u2019s relationship with Shelley?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe seems fairly self sufficient, which is good. Deanna and Naomi only work because Deanna is a homeworkaphile and a workaholic. They spend time together, but Deanna doesn\u2019t need Naomi there all the time.\u201d Liz smiled fucking fondly. \u201cAm is not, but she knows I\u2019m a very busy god who has many things to accomplish. But I don\u2019t have a human relationship with her - she is Clytemnestra\u2019s concubine.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThis is part of why I\u2019m trying to get her back into school, which I will point out is very high on her own priority list.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz took a drag of her cigarette. \u201cYou should also consider your purpose. Deanna and Naomi relationship is a completely human one, on purpose, as it helps me build my connection to humans. I\u2019ve given up trying to understand how you relate to humans.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was fond of Vivian, and it seems a much better ending to her story, to have actually managed to find someone to fall in love with, than to have orchestrated the end of her own life,\u201d Billy Mack said, blank faced.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat I would really like to do, in the end, is to be able to give Naomi a soul, so that I can retire her and let her have a life with Deanna, or whoever, once I no longer need the cover specifically.\u201d Liz sighed.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked fucking intrigued,. \u201cWhat a fascinating notion. Alibi does show it is possible for our covers to exists outside of us.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cI wouldn\u2019t cast her off lightly, but I would like to let her have her happily ever after.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI shall have to look into this.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Both the Rights\u2019 cars were there when I got to Mavericks. Bobby greeted me loudly as I walked in, ordering the bartender to get me a drink with his usual fucking class. I took it, of course, but then jerked my head towards the back. \u201cCan we talk?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can clear the office out sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cActually, I need to talk to both of you.\u201d I tossed my drink back and picked up the second that was already waiting.<br /> <br /> Bobby paused. \u201cCan I check for traps?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cI\u2019ll make sure you\u2019re safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Ginny greeted me with a hug, ignoring Bobby. \u201cI appreciate you looking out for me. There haven\u2019t been any more problems.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAbout that - we managed to track down one of the fuckers that broke into your house, Ginny, who had ties to the young woman who told you, Bobby, she had tickets...\u201d I began.<br /> <br /> \u201cWho stood me up!\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave him a goddamn look. \u201c... in an effort to lure you to a place they could grab you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Bobby smirked. \u201cThey musta run off when they saw me. I bet it was the black belt.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I just threw up in my mouth,\u201d Ginny muttered.<br /> <br /> \u201cI remember when you took it off me...\u201d He waggled his eyebrows at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you have to bring that up in front of her of all people, and now of all times?! For the love of god, shut up.\u201d She shuddered.<br /> <br /> I gave her a sympathetic smile and gave them the anti-terrorist con men plan. Honestly, it was pretty close to the truth, as close as I could get and not mention \u2018occult matrix\u2019. \u201cThese guys, the ones that will replace you if you\u2019re OK with it, are fucking good - I trust \u2018em to run things for a couple of weeks - and it gets you out of the line of fire.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you think it\u2019s best Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUm...\u201d Bobby looked torn.<br /> <br /> I winked at Ginny. \u201cYou guys deserve a break. I\u2019m sure there\u2019s islands and beaches and boat drinks a-goddamn-plenty calling your name.\u201d When Bobby kept waffling, I continued. \u201cAnd what about Cindy and Rachel? Don\u2019t you think they might like going somewhere just the 2-slash-3 of you and however fucking many busty women you can find?\u201d<br /> <br /> Ginny winced but Bobby nodded thoughtfully. \u201cYeah...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know it\u2019s late notice, but four days is our window for leaving - discretely, remember people will be taking your fucking places.\u201d I looked between them.<br /> <br /> \u201cI doubt any of them are as attractive...\u201d Bobby straightened his Hawaiian shirt. \u201cI\u2019ll have to tell the girls to pack fast. You know how girls are, but I\u2019ll tell them they don\u2019t have to bother with underwear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sure that\u2019ll help.\u201d I managed to keep a straight face, only because I\u2019m a Demon. Bobby stretched and wandered off. I turned to Ginny. \u201cSorry doll. It\u2019s important though.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled, looking me straight in the eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s OK. I appreciate all you\u2019ve been doing for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t deserve to get caught up in that shit.\u201d I gave her a half smile. \u201cYou take care of yourself.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and let me go. As I walked out, I heard Bobby ordering the bartender to sweep for bugs so she \u2018can\u2019t run this place remotely\u2019. I sighed. Subtle with a capital B. Ah well. At least the fucker was known to be crazy enough to pull that sorta shit and ignore it the next day. I kept on walking.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session L</i><br /> <br /> So Penanggalan. This was OOC knowledge from before Kat even showed up, I just wanted to see how they work with it. This is my second Penanggalan in a CoD game, my first is in <i>Balance of Shadows</i> as Chandra, the wife of Alexia a PC. That was fun too. Penanggalan are in <b>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</b>.<br /> <br /> I had been waiting to introduce Heroin and Tar.<br /> <br /> That covers I think. Small cast for the game tonight, just Clytemnestra, Kilroy and Quietus. Will see what they get up to. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T01:50:40-07:00","id":975428,"title":"","content":"Speed\u2019s player was unable to make so\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026aw heck Speed\u2019s player did one anyway. Now that, ladies and gentleman, is dedication. It is accurate of course, down to the conversations. Kudos to Quiet\u2019s player for recording it.<br /> <i><br /> Session LI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> \u201cWe need to break into a hospital.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack stared at Liz blankly. \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI need someone to help break into a hospital,\u201d she elaborated.<br /> <br /> \u201cUh, what?\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked at him fucking stiflingly. \u201cWe are stealing a ricin victim.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a beat until his perfect goddamn recall kicked in. \u201cOh yeah, that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can get in, but getting him out is something I will have more trouble with. Between spiders and cellphones, I can even get Kilroy in.\u201d She nodded to the g-man. \u201cBut then we\u2019ll need to shut things down enough so that we can get him out. So, we need a plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe wanna make me up like a fed? I don\u2019t think a clipboard and a name badge will cut it in this case. But if I look the part, Authorize gets me in.\u201d Jack shrugged.<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cWe could go in legitimately as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack agreed. \u201cI could hack in some transfer papers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019d need someone masquerading as a doctor as well, I\u2019d think, considering his critical condition. I can handle that most likely. I have a nurse\u2019s outfit for reasons I don\u2019t care to disclose.\u201d Liz smiled goddamn enigmatically.<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed, that should do nicely.\u201d Billy Mack nodded approvingly.<br /> <br /> Jack snapped his fingers. \u201cHey man - what if you had the g-man come with me as an alibi, and you-as-Vivian provided overwatch, handling the surveillance cleanup, countering any traces or suspicion that might pop up?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful. \u201cExcellent point. My ID shouldn\u2019t be challenged and doesn\u2019t need Authorize, so that should be safe, with the added advantage of being able to support our cover story should it be challenged as a whole.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnother consideration - it would be perfectly reasonable Liz here to help, but she is quite recognizable. Naomi is much less likely to be recognized, but it would be a strain on the cover.\u201d Liz looked between the two fuckers for advice.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThat shouldn\u2019t be an issue. Download Knowledge should allow me to construct a disguise for Liz that will alleviate that concern.\u201d<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow. \u201cIf you say so.\u201d<br /> <br /> They got to work, and left Liz looking, fucking frankly, nothing like herself. With a quick tweak of reality, she even had on her nurse\u2019s outfit, completing the disguise. As they headed out, Billy Mack swapped to Vivian and split off a copy of Billy Mack to go with the other two.<br /> <br /> Vivian had the records in place by the time the other two got there. She let them know over their ear curls - the most goddamn convenient part of masquerading as g-men. So when they arrived, they walked right in.<br /> <br /> After they stated their business, introducing themselves as Agents Smith and McKenzie with Dr. Brown, the man on duty behind the desk nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll have to call Dr. Carson and get this cleared.\u201d The two \u2018government agents\u2019 flashed their IDs, one real, the other Authorized. \u201cAh, yes. If you\u2019ll just wait over here?\u201d<br /> <br /> After a moment, the doctor came back. \u201cYes, everything should be fine. I presume this means that Mr. Fitzgerald is not going to be here in the morning?\u201d <br /> <br /> Vivian\u2019s eyes widened as she heard that over the ear curls. \u201cFitzgerald\u2019s with the CDC.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack put his finger to his ear, listening goddamn intently. \u201cThe CDC has been notified.\u201d <br /> <br /> The doctor nodded and escorted them up to the appropriate floor. Liz got to work helping prepare the poor fuck for transfer and they left without any further trouble.<br /> <br /> Vivian started going through the computer system, wanting to know what kind of shit had been disseminated to get the CDC involved. From the looks of it, the symptoms that had been logged for Martin had gotten flagged as a potential for, well, fucking ricin poisoning, as well as a few other things, which had caught the government\u2019s attention. She smiled to herself, noting those \u2018few other things\u2019.<br /> <br /> She typed up a quick but formal email addressed to the CDC informing them that further testing had ruled out ricin, and that the patient had begun to recover. She spoofed the to: address to be from the appropriate official in the hospital email system and grabbed a Mountain Dew, a self-satisfied look on her face. As a last step, she cyber-walked into the goddamn security system, obfuscating her Agency members presence in the hospital.<br /> <br /> Once they got out to the car, Jack tapped his ear bud. \u201cWell, since I\u2019m all spiffied up, I think I\u2019ll go prowling.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian smirked. \u201cFair enough. I believe I have a date with my girlfriend. I\u2019m sure she\u2019s over the scare with the ghost, and me talking to her about moving in, and is not at all nervous about taking me to meet her parents.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot at all.\u201d Jack snorted.<br /> <br /> \u201cApparently she has already told them that she\u2019s bringing her girlfriend.\u201d Vivian shrugged.<br /> <br /> Jack cracked his neck to the side. \u201cSo when should we see about that U-Haul?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI live in an RV,\u201d Vivian said goddamn archly. \u201cIt\u2019s basically a U-Haul already.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNaomi\u2019s going to be eating and eating and eating at Cecilia\u2019s house for Thanksgiving.\u201d Liz grinned. \u201cI looked forward to tormenting her all day. The expressions of rage when I talk about certain things on Naomi...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes. \u201cI can\u2019t imagine.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian chuckled. \u201cShe is delightfully expressive.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about you Jack?\u201d Liz asked fucking sweetly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I dunno...\u201d he trailed the hell off.<br /> <br /> Vivian shrugged. \u201cSince Speed\u2019s off getting the Rights to leave town, I\u2019ll say it: We could always use someone manning the office in case anyone comes by on Thanksgiving to get a private detective to look in on their cheating spouse.\u201d She tried for my voice. She has Vox, so she got it in one. \u201cThat just seems tacky though. Thanksgiving? I mean, if you\u2019re going to ruin your marriage, you should do it on a real holiday.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack scratched his head. \u201cWhat the hell is wrong with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I\u2019ve been wearing Vivian too much, she\u2019s wearing off on me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz smiled. \u201cThis is your stop, I believe, Jack. I will see you folks later.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack chucked his chin towards the sick man. \u201cHow long you want him out for?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThree hours should be more than enough.\u201d She smiled thankfully as Jack knocked the man out.<br /> <br /> \u201cHave fun with your cabana boy.\u201d Jack gave her a mock salute.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, I will.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz headed back home with the unconscious man. Once she got there, she killed the poor fuck quickly, before the ricin could, and stored him away while she called Robin, then got herself a proper goddamn night\u2019s sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Jack was feeling restless and cast around for something to do. He decided to stick his head in Johnny\u2019s, see who the hell was there and whether it was worth his time to stick around. Sharon Needles was there, scowling at the world and so was Dmitri, talking to an attractive black woman, and scowling way goddamn less. Vivian\u2019s contact and his date were both speaking in Russian. The Last Starfighter motherfucker, not that Jack knew him from Adam, had grabbed a stool and was trying to tell any woman who\u2019d listen to him, as seductively as possible, how he saved the world from alien invasion.<br /> <br /> Jack walked up to the bar and ordered a drink to be sent over to Sharon, leaving off the fucking stupid lines. When the bartender looked back to see if he wanted anything for himself, he jerked his chin in greeting. \u201cAlright night? Nothing crazy going on?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d The bartender nodded. \u201cThere\u2019s been a little more business than usual, with Kiki\u2019s closed, but it won\u2019t last. So, things are alright.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack nodded, and sat back, looking over the crowd. He nodded when he caught a glance from Sharon and saluted her with the rum he\u2019d ordered to match her. Thinking a moment, he ordered a basket of fucking cheese fries and grabbed the nearest table to Dmitri, listening unobtrusively. It helped that he didn\u2019t look like the kind of fucker who might speak Russian.<br /> <br /> From what he could tell, Ms. Benoit was ordering a number of tracking microchips, satellite enabled. There was the small type, implantable if needed. It was a big order too, a few hundred. When she spoke, calling the man by the name Vivian knew him by, there was a slight accent to it, but Jack couldn\u2019t place it at a thought. The major topic of conversation was the bank account dance, as she was paying with several different account sources, to add up to the required amounts.<br /> <br /> Jack finished his fries and headed off, sending Vivian a text. \u2018The Russians are moving some heavy tech, to an unknown player.\u2019 He figured that might get her attention at some goddamn point, when she wasn\u2019t busy.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cAbout this morning...\u201d Vivian began, goddamn apologetically. Shelley raised an eyebrow as her girlfriend flopped down onto the couch next to her. \u201cI probably came across a little pushy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou did,\u201d Shelley said matter of factly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry about that. I really am just worried about you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley nodded. \u201cI know. You understand why we need to have independence, though...?\u201d She looked hopefully over at her.<br /> <br /> Vivian answered fucking quickly. \u201cI do, I do. And I don\u2019t, I mean, I think, it\u2019s just... I think I can help, without, you know, interfering with you being your own person.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d Shelley nodded. \u201cI will look over grant information and stuff, I promise, and I\u2019ll see what comes up, on the job front. Based on my skill set, waitressing is an easy thing, and if you can get in at Kiki\u2019s, it pays really well, remarkably well for the level of establishment, and...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, really.\u201d Vivian sighed. \u201cI just worry.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley shrugged. \u201cTwo Chin buys for everybody and I\u2019ve gotten over $100 tips from him before.\u201d<br /> <br