\u2019m blindfolded, with an IV in my arm and a chip in my head, I\u2019m not in any position to bargain, so... I accept.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are alive. Don\u2019t think you\u2019ve gotten nothing out of the deal,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> Liz clapped. \u201cThe experiment was a success. You should be pleased by that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded goddamn enthusiastically. \u201cThere may be unexpected side effect. An ability to see ghosts, perhaps? Read thoughts... You should be prepared for something unexpected. You have come back from the dead after all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry. We\u2019ll be watching.\u201d Jack stepped back, the voice sounding like it came from a ways away.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd it is our interests to keep you intact.\u201d Billy Mack smiled.<br /> <br /> He smiled. It was a fucking weak smile. \u201cWell that\u2019s good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe may have varying definitions of intact, you and I.\u201d Liz moved closer to Martin again.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s... goodish?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack sighed. \u201cYou will find a number in your phone. It will, periodically, update. If you need to contact us. I assure you that number cannot be traced to us directly. It is of no use to anyone trying to harm us. And we will contact you, as needed. For now, we will return you to your home. I suggest you not inform anyone of your brush with ricin poisoning. They will find it difficult to understand. You should also not tell them about this conversation. For one thing, I don\u2019t think they\u2019d believe you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack spoke up. \u201cFor another, your wife would never recover.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI, on the other hand, would love it if you did. I have <u>so</u> many surprises.\u201d Liz\u2019s voice was still bright.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf the terms are acceptable?\u201d The scared man nodded at Billy Mack. \u201cI\u2019m going to turn the sedatives back on. You\u2019ll sleep, and when you wake up, you\u2019ll be in a cab, on your way home.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz patted the IV. \u201cDo try to avoid any crushing addictions. This is quite expensive.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Once they\u2019d squared him away, the three returned to Liz\u2019s sitting room. Billy Mack nodded to the other two fuckers. \u201cI do believe that went well. We may have to use these voices again sometime.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI usually just use my GLaDOS voice when Dommeing. It\u2019s always a nice surprise when they get tied up and hear it.\u201d Liz shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cI imagine it is not what they are expecting.\u201d Billy Mack smiled. \u201cWell, where shall we embark him in a cab from?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz thought for a moment. \u201cIt is late, so we have a lot of options. Kiki\u2019s would be kinda hilarious, but there may be people poking around there. Plus, it has a connection to us.\u201d She glanced at a box of medical supplies. \u201cWe have 45 minutes. I\u2019m not giving him any more of this, it\u2019s some good shit. I thought Demerol was good, but this stuff...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack cracked his neck. \u201cIf we need more than that, I can handle it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Works?\u201d Billy Mack suggested. \u201cThere are not many people there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut if we just leave him, there\u2019s no assurances we won\u2019t get kidnapped and/or murdered, all the way out there.\u201d Liz frowned.<br /> <br /> Jack snapped his fingers. \u201cThe coffeehouse, the Changeling one. Not connected to us, fairly low key, but not off the beaten path enough to be dangerous.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThat works.\u201d<br /> <i><br /> End Session LI</i><br /> <br /> Yeah, things got a little out of hand there with Edward Martin (GERTY is from Moon, HAL obviously 2001, and GLaDOS from the Portal games.)<br /> <br /> They had some good work at the hospital. A good mix of skills and powers. I did not expect it to go so smoothly. <br /> <br /> I think that covers it. Comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T13:26:36-07:00","id":984034,"title":"","content":"Gabe is back! It time to poke around the restaurant and work on Esha\u2019s problem<br /> <br /> <i>Session LII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> \u201cHey doll.\u201d Greg Solomon greeted Esha with a smile, using my voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cGabe! Hello,\u201d she responded happily.<br /> <br /> Greg leaned back in his chair. \u201cI had a thought. My people and I need a few minutes alone in those fuckers' houses. I was gonna case the joint and see when they commonly were out, it occurred to me that we could force the issue.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Greg flipped a coin, wincing when the piece of shit landed tails twice in a row. \u201cThey just moved in right? I was thinking you could be neighborly, invite them over for coffee and pie - I\u2019d suggest not pumpkin, considering. My associate, Elizabeth Covington, is willing to be there also, which should do goddamn wonders for keeping them for going for you right then and there. And while they\u2019re all three there, we can look over their places, and you two can give us a heads up if they suddenly make for home.\u201d<br /> <br /> She made a considering noise. \u201cIf you think it\u2019s best. I...\u201d She paused. \u201cI worry - if something happens, and I need to defend us... I don\u2019t want to have to enact secrecy protocols.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah. I really doubt they\u2019ll try to go for you - they\u2019re playing a fucking long game. Liz - Ms. Covington is... prominent, in certain circles. It would be a hell of a lot more trouble than it\u2019s worth to go for both of you. Especially if you drop a hint that about some better time.\u201d Greg\u2019s eyes drifted towards the online racing report he had up.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, I can do that. I just don\u2019t want to put your friend at risk.\u201d Esha smiled.<br /> <br /> Greg put a smile in my voice. \u201cThanks doll. I think this is the best way. I\u2019ll see you tomorrow then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> After dropping the poor fucking sap off, Vivian called up Roxanne. She answered in Bulgarian, and Vivian responded in the same. \u201cWell hello there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, what do you need?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps I just want to call and talk to my friend.\u201d Vivian sounded mock-hurt.<br /> <br /> She gave a small chuckle. \u201cIt\u2019s a possibility, yes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian smiled. \u201cOr maybe I\u2019m curious as to what you might know about Edward Martin?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMartin...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe definitely seemed to remember you.\u201d Vivian smirked like she'd eaten the goddamn canary. \u201cOr at least, to be fair, he asked us more than once if you were behind what was happening to him.\u201d<br /> <br /> She thought for a brief moment. \u201cMartin is a corrupt financier. Some of the information I dug up was about him. I don\u2019t know if he works for your greater enemy directly, but agents of them do work through him, knowingly or unknowingly. They will pay him for services, and that money is turned around and put into things for the people they\u2019re backing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cAlright. That is pretty much what we thought - a useful, but possibly unwitting piece in the game.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not positive he\u2019s unwitting, but the conversations we had didn\u2019t imply full knowledge of what was going on, to me. I didn\u2019t really have my powers very long before they were on to me, so I can\u2019t say for certain. I can definitely say he\u2019s corrupt though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTo explain somewhat - someone got it in their head that killing him would be a great disruption to the financial sector,\u201d Vivian began.<br /> <br /> Roxanne chuckled fucking sharply. \u201cOh yes. Yes it would. He has several greedy and less intelligent people that are kept in check. If he died, there would be sort of an unofficial war between them. One would win, the others would lose their jobs, creating a domino effect of repercussions. And none of them are as good at what they are doing as he is. When, not if, they screw up, the irregularities would begin to be seen, stocks would begin to drop and while it wouldn\u2019t cause a world shattering cataclysm... on a good stock day, it would cause a dip for a while and job losses. On a bad stock day, it would cause a crash that would cause things to suck for a couple of months. On a day when the banks have been caught misbehaving again, there could be a recession.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian raised an eyebrow. \u201cWell. It seems someone definitely knew what they were doing then, targeting him. More than I would have expected, honestly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCould they have gotten ahold of the information I had?\u201d Roxanne asked. \u201cWhoever Kim worked for, perhaps, gave it to them? Or someone might have found it out independently. I\u2019m not so vain as to think I\u2019m the only one who could have gotten those records.\u201d She shrugged. \u201cI mean, it\u2019s also possible that everyone would have put the good of the conspiracy and the corporations first, and not gotten into a civil war over their big, stupid egos, but... it\u2019s also possible that an entire swim team is gonna come in here and need a place to stay tonight and to deal with their excessive horniness. I don\u2019t hear a knock at the door, is what I\u2019m saying.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian sighed goddamn happily. \u201cYou know, that was a good month. Anyway... we prevented him from being murdered so, probably for the best.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf they were trying to murder him, it is possible it was someone working under him,\u201d Roxanne pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe people in question were definitely trying to cause a disruption. A group of cultists, the Temple of the Endless Void?\u201d Vivian waited for recognition.<br /> <br /> Roxanne shook her fucking head. \u201cNot something I\u2019m familiar with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA doomsday cult. They are trying to bring about the end of the world.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cYou were asking about my connection - at one point in time, Mr. Martin was interested in making me Mistress #2. I am not Mistress #2 for anybody.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian smirked. \u201cOh, you are definitely Mistress #1, all the way. No second fiddle for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cListen. Someone his age is gonna need to have a whole lot of money and making me wife number all of them, or I don\u2019t have time for his shit.\u201d Roxanne crossed her fucking arms.<br /> <br /> \u201cHis wife is rather cute though,\u201d Vivian pointed out. \u201cAnd appears to be doing well for herself.\u201d<br /> <br /> Roxanne grimaced. \u201cApart from the likely perpetual disappointment, sure. Maybe she has some jumper cables...\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian chuckled. \u201cI am sure his bank account gives her all the satisfaction she needs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s fair,\u201d Roxanne allowed. \u201cSo, I dunno how deep in the shit he is, cause I only found out about the shit, but he\u2019s in it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCertainly. I was mostly asking as he seemed quite convinced you were the one behind what was happening to him.\u201d<br /> <br /> Roxanne frowned. \u201cI didn't think he was that on to me. Someone might have tipped him off, Kim\u2019s employer perhaps? Because as far as I knew, he wanted to get in my pants and that\u2019s all. For him to think I was behind some move against him... I don\u2019t know. I don\u2019t think he thought of me that way - he certainly was willing to show up creepily alone with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cTo be fair, there has been a bit about you floating around in the news. He might have drawn some conclusions. We did take precautions to conceal our identities, as we did know he worked closely with people who would be willing to backhoe his mind to figure out who he was working for, if/when they find out he\u2019s been compromised. We were saving his life from ricin poisoning...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRicin poisoning?\u201d She sounded goddamn impressed. \u201cThat\u2019s subtle, as doomsday cults go.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey were trying to have him assassinated for the chaos, so clearly not just run of the mill cultists, if they were aware of the effect his death would have,\u201d Vivian pointed out. \u201cThey are a sharper bunch of tacks than we thought they were, I believe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Roxanne nodded thoughtfully. \u201cOr they have some ability to know what would cause the most chaos, without necessarily the information to know why.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cQuite possibly,\u201d Vivian allowed, \u201cI\u2019m not even sure they are human.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWonderful...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway, he brought your name up a couple of times, asking if you were behind this, thus, my call.\u201d Vivian smiled.<br /> <br /> Roxanne shook her head. \u201cIt is strange. Something must have changed, maybe he was told something. It seems unlikely he would have offered me the \u2018honor\u2019 of becoming his other mistress, if he thought that was the kind of thing I did. If you find out what he secretly thinks I\u2019m up to, let me know. Maybe I can take advantage of it.\u201d She smiled. \u201cOr perhaps if someone is doing something in my name.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will, certainly.\u201d Vivian smiled in return. \u201cI trust everything is going well for you still?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. I shall have to make time to come see you, next time I have some vacation.\u201d Vivian grinned.<br /> <br /> Roxanne chuckled. \u201cI\u2019ll tell the boys.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday was a fucking busy day. We had a package to intercept, a crew full of restaurant workers to interrogate and a couple of houses to toss. And four people to do it with. Thankfully, we all got in early. I had motivation - my goddamn Infrastructure was on the line. Billy Mack and Jack are overeager any day of the week, and Liz and her Demerol had gotten a fucking early night. Once we all arrived, we got to planning.<br /> <br /> The fact that we didn\u2019t know when Mrs. X\u2019d be by the post office, other than \u2018before it closed\u2019, was the real goddamn concern. It wouldn\u2019t take all of us to interview the working stiffs at Bangkok Pies, but it would have been nice to have all hands on deck for whatever the hell confrontation came from Clytemnestra pulling the crazy spirit dame up onto the roof. In the end, we compromised on that bit. Billy Mack and I covered the interviews, since I had Mind Reading and Aura Sight, and he\u2019d done that shit before, and sent our Alibis to give the group on the roof a show of force.<br /> <br /> As the two Demons and the Alibi pair left, I saw Cecilia bustling around, putting an umbrella and a fucking small picnic basket in the back of Liz\u2019s car. Jack raised an eyebrow at Liz. \u201cI thought we\u2019d make a lunch of it. I don\u2019t want to have to make a cover check,\u201d she said primly.<br /> <br /> He raised his hands. \u201cOK. Food on a stakeout isn\u2019t that weird.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cThat is not a box of stale donuts and random cheap coffee that came from wherever the donuts came from.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCucumber finger sandwiches?\u201d I asked Liz, smirking.<br /> <br /> She nodded happily. \u201cWith lemonade and chardonnay.\u201d Jack had begun to groan at my question, but his expression changed and he shrugged at that. \u201cIt certainly ain\u2019t your momma\u2019s cheese and crackers.\u201d Jack frowned again.<br /> <br /> <br /> When they left, I swung back and forth in my seat, thinking. Liz and Jack were on the Infrastructure business. Billy Mack and I would be handling Kat\u2019s case after lunch and we\u2019d all be working on Esha\u2019s case after dinner. Gone\u2019s case was all but wrapped up - I think Billy Mack wanted a crack at finding Skeevy Larry himself, but we\u2019d fulfilled our fucking end of the bargain, as best I could tell.<br /> <br /> The only case that wasn\u2019t moving forward from fuck-all was Nikka\u2019s case. We\u2019d struck out with the DNA and all we had from Mr. Not-A-Goddamn-Farmer was a first name, Cornelius. Not precisely enough to go by, though that plus a sketch might get us something. After a few minutes thought though, it occurred to me I had the fucker\u2019s license plate.<br /> <br /> I ran the numbers and got back results fairly quickly. The plate belonged to one Adam Sandoval, living in suburban Seattle. Not precisely the fucking neighborhood I expected Bighead McGee to live in. The photo I got back certainly wasn\u2019t him, a blonde 20-something.<br /> <br /> I wandered over to Billy Mack\u2019s office. \u201cI need you to work your magic.\u201d I gave him what I had. \u201cThat\u2019s the owner of the car Cornelius was driving at the fight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d He nodded and got to work. \u201cNothing out of the ordinary. Married, a small child, 6 years old. He sells insurance, his wife is a speech teacher at the elementary school their son is in.\u201d He scanned through. \u201cOh.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood oh, or bad oh?\u201d I raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> He smiled abstractly up at me. \u201cGood oh.\u201d He waved me the hell around. \u201cHis wife, Amy Sandoval.\u201d<br /> <br /> I whistled. \u201cGood oh.\u201d He\u2019d found a picture posted online with just the right kind of lighting, making it clear that Amy Sandoval was one of the fucking Harvesters that attacked Nikka outside of Kiki\u2019s. Jackpot.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe seems to have experienced a quite recent rise in popularity among her students and peers,\u201d Billy Mack noted.<br /> <br /> I read over his shoulder. He was right - after 8 years of working there, she\u2019d suddenly begun winning all the goddamn popularity awards this past year. \u201cTricks from her mentor, the \u2018I have special bullshit powers\u2019 Harvester? That doesn\u2019t sound like anything you or Nikka said Harvesters could do.\u201d He nodded agreement.<br /> <br /> We both looked up as Cecilia came in. \u201cA Pham Min is here to see you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat. Send her up.\u201d I nodded to Cecilia.<br /> <br /> After a few moments we met her at the table. \u201cHey! You guys wanted to talk to me?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cYeah. We are looking into someone who has been breaking into Kat Vit\u2019s place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI dunno who this Kat is.\u201d She frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cProprietor of Bangkok Pies.\u201d I walked a coin over my knuckles.<br /> <br /> She had a look of recognition. \u201cThe weird disease monster thing? They working for the CDC maybe?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled fucking thinly. \u201cI believe the word you are looking for is Penanggalan. And the CDC is unlikely, based on the M.O.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFucking shit.\u201d She sighed. \u201cAre you her friend?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s our client.\u201d I held her gaze.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey eat babies.\u201d She made odd crying noises as she mimed rocking a baby, then made like she was taking a large bite. \u201cBabies.\u201d<br /> <br /> I ran a hand over my face, hiding a fucking smile. Billy Mack looked at us goddamn sternly. \u201cThat is not completely outside of the realm of a Penanggalan. But...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI haven\u2019t been in her house.\u201d The Sin-Eater crossed her arms. \u201cPenanggalan was on the list of things I thought she might be.\u201d She paused for a moment. \u201cIs it a problem, someone breaking into her house? I mean, she eats babies.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have seen no proof that she eats babies,\u201d Billy Mack reassured her.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s what Penanggalan do!\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack put on his lecturing voice. \u201cThey are drawn primarily towards the blood of infants and pregnant women.\u201d<br /> <br /> She interrupted. \u201cWhich is bad...\u201d She looked the g-man over. \u201cI feel like I\u2019m talking to aliens here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is a predilection that is directed more towards helpless victims than other vampires, it is true...\u201d Billy Mack continued. \u201cHow do you feel about other vampires, and their need for human blood?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDepends on how hot they are.\u201d She smirked.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cAnd you have a problem with Kat?\u201d She shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt does seem that eating babies crosses a line,\u201d Billy Mack informed me fucking solemnly.<br /> <br /> \u201cThing is, you don\u2019t have any proof she eats babies. Or else you\u2019d have known she was a Penanggalan.\u201d I leaned back in my seat.<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cThis is true.\u201d She sighed. \u201cSo what you\u2019re saying is, don\u2019t go and kill the baby eater or <i><i>you</i></i> will be angry?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cUnless you have some goddamn proof that she eats babies, sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want, like, a picture, or a baby with a bite out of it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat we\u2019re saying is, someone broke into her house, much more subtly the second time than the first, and has apparently been watching her,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out calmly.<br /> <br /> She turned back to him. \u201cMaybe they\u2019re seeing if she eats babies, cause someone wants proof.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps they are,\u201d he allowed. \u201cHowever, because we are aware that you and your associates generally investigate such things, we wanted to make sure it wasn't you, as we are endeavoring to maintain amicable relations.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked thoughtful. \u201cRobin does like to get involved with people who lead to disaster. Maybe she\u2019d involved in it somehow.\u201d I smirked. \u201cI\u2019m just saying, I don\u2019t know whether her girlfriend or her boyfriend are gonna cause more trouble. Even I think Liz is hot, but...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded goddamn seriously. \u201cThat is because you have eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cI\u2019m usually only so into women. When I\u2019m drunk.\u201d She paused. \u201cWhich is, to be fair, a lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnce we have determined who is stalking her, now that we know it isn\u2019t you,\u201d Billy Mack began.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah. Honestly, I\u2019ve been fooling around with this big paisano I\u2019ve gotten ahold of.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack paused, then continued. \u201cWell, we certainly hadn\u2019t wanted to be working at cross purposes. But, perhaps, once we have settled this matter...\u201d<br /> <br /> Pham interrupted. \u201cYou want the baby eating monster to pay you for taking care of the problem, and then we can talk about whether she and her lunch bunch are a particular problem?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, yes, that is a logical course of action.\u201d Billy Mack nodded happily. I rubbed my goddamn temples. \u201cAlso, there is the matter of professional ethics involved in working against her while she is our client.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know what, I respect that.\u201d Pham looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> I rolled my fucking eyes. \u201cGlad we have your approval.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled at me. \u201cVery few people do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is possibly she is feeding on infants. It is also possible she is not, keep that in mind,\u201d Billy Mack said.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat, you think she\u2019s chowing down on \u2018I Can\u2019t Believe It\u2019s Not Baby\u2019 so she doesn\u2019t have to eat them? Is she a vegan Penanggalan?\u201d Pham looked goddamn dubious.<br /> <br /> I tapped a pencil on the table. \u201cI believe Billy Mack also brought up pregnant women.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did. And, as I understand it, flawed though my knowledge of vampires might be, it is a preference, not a mandate.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut if you\u2019re a baby-eating vampire, you may as well go with it.\u201d She crossed her arms again.<br /> <br /> I sighed. \u201cUnless you don\u2019t want to eat babies.\u201d<br /> <br /> She made a face. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t become a baby-eating vampire then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not really sure she had a choice,\u201d I pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cAs I understand it, she was the victim of a Penanggalan, she caught the Penanggalan disease from this vampire...\u201d Billy Mack began.<br /> <br /> She interrupted. \u201cAnd that\u2019s why you use a rubber.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man gave her a look and continued, \u201cand had a rather unfortunate incident where she woke up at her own funeral and was shot several times by her husband. I do believe she is attempting to live as normal a life as she can after these events.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe the technical term for that is a bitch.\u201d She shrugged. \u201cThai pizza\u2019s aren't normal. They\u2019re delicious and I might, you know, spare her just so I can keep eating them, but that\u2019s cause I\u2019m a selfish little prick. Ask Robin, she tells me that all the time. Then she calls me slutty, and I point out she\u2019s been eating more box than a cardboard recycling plant. And then it all goes to hell. Sometimes she hits me actually.\u201d She pointed at her bicep. \u201cI have a bruise.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do believe we can certainly agree that the pizza is delicious.\u201d Billy Mack smiled. \u201cAnd it would be a shame if anything were to happen to her.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cThanks for coming by Pham. I appreciate you taking the time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo problem!\u201d She smiled brightly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Over near the post office, Jack was glaring at the wall as he carried the goddamn picnic basket and umbrella up the ladder while Liz sang to herself as she climbed below. \u201cThis is not a stakeout...\u201d he grumbled to himself. Raising his voice, he continued, \u201cand it\u2019s also not a fucking musical number.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz pouted. \u201cAw, you\u2019re no fun.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m lots of fun when you\u2019re not eating me.\u201d Jack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not eating you now.\u201d Liz looked at him slyly as she spread out the picnic blanket.<br /> <br /> Jack smirked. \u201cWe\u2019re busy, or I\u2019d ask you if you want to make out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked fucking perplexed. \u201cThat just seems rude to me. If I were watching through the binoculars, I mean...\u201d Jack gave her a look. \u201cThat\u2019s not making out.\u201d He kept up the look. \u201cYou have sandwiches! What more do you want to put in your mouth?\u201d Jack took the goddamn binoculars.<br /> <br /> After a while, we called them to catch them up on our conversation. Liz smiled. \u201cIsn\u2019t Pham Min the most charming?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is certainly a delightful young woman. Reminds me of someone else I know.\u201d Jack made a fucking disgruntled noise as Billy Mack\u2019s lips quirked. \u201cHas Naomi met her?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot yet. Robin only knows me as Liz and doesn\u2019t know Naomi exists. I could talk to her as Naomi and just not let on I\u2019m also Liz, but I am trying not to have Robin know I can be other people.\u201d Liz shrugged.<br /> <br /> Jack smirked. \u201cIt does harm that trust thing a bit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cFair. It is simply scientific curiosity as to what would happen if she and Naomi got together. I imagine there would either a significant attraction, or a spontaneous explosion destroying most of the city.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think they would become besties.\u201d Liz poured herself another glass of whatever the hell was in the lemonade bottle.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do lean more towards the immediate friendship, yes.\u201d Billy Mack smiled.<br /> <br /> Liz looked off into the distance. \u201cThere\u2019ll probably be many racial epithets for Latinos and the Vietnamese when they\u2019re talking to each other.\u201d Jack sighed goddamn heavily.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlmost certainly,\u201d Billy Mack agreed. \u201cI imagine it would be something of a competition.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> A short time later, Jack spotted Mrs. X, with her usual fucking mask, approaching the post office. \u201cLook alive, people.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz got into position and looked to him. \u201cReady?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded, and she shot web at the spirit, pulling her up onto the roof. Jack immediately moved to calm the fucking situation, try to enforce the reality to allow cool heads to prevail, but it didn\u2019t quite snap into place around her. Mrs. X reached for Liz, sucking the goddamn skin from her upper body off in an unwinding motion and wrapping it around herself.<br /> <br /> Jack growled out, \u201cWait!\u201d and tried again, this time forcing his will upon reality and locking Mrs. X into a non-hostile tension. At the same time, Liz wrapped her fully up in webbing. \u201cWe\u2019re not actually here to hurt you.\u201d He took a deep breath. \u201cWe want to help you get home.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHome?\u201d The spirit\u2019s voice was wavery and uncertain.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. Wherever you came from.\u201d Jack nodded goddamn encouragingly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need the crystal.\u201d Her voice broke slightly.<br /> <br /> Liz put a hand out. \u201cListen. We are willing to work with you, but we want to negotiate a way that might not damage the Infrastructure - the reality reinforcing things. We think there might be a different one, that would be more successful. And not have the side effects that one might. We want to help you get home.\u201d She smiled winningly at her. \u201cIf you can leave it be for a little bit, and let us figure out a better place to send you home through, we\u2019ll come and get you and help. You just need to promise us that you won\u2019t do anything <i><i>yet</i></i>. If you don\u2019t do anything <i><i>yet</i></i>, we won\u2019t interfere with you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut the crystal... is... there.\u201d The spirit pointed.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, but...\u201d Liz began hesitantly, speaking fucking slowly and clearly. \u201cWe think that there will be side effects you are not anticipating that will affect us and will likely affect you. It may be dangerous.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well.\u201d Mrs. X cocked her head towards Liz. \u201cYou have... four days. To get me my access point. To use.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz smiled brightly. \u201cThat is acceptable.\u201d She gestured towards the edge of the roof. \u201cThat fire escape will get you down. I need to go somewhere and scream. A lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstandable. That\u2019s usually what people do.\u201d The spirit turned to leave.<br /> <br /> Liz moved to sit under the umbrella and began quickly stripping the hell out of her shirt and bra, holding back winces as the clothes brushed against exposed muscles and goddamn nerve endings. She activated Halo and sat gently on the blanket. Jack sat with her, careful not to brush her with any of his clothes, and serenaded her with Spanish guitar using Vox.<br /> <br /> <br /> Kat introduced Billy Mack and I to the group of employees that had been able to stay a little bit longer than usual. There were 7 of them, 3 guys and 4 dames. Billy Mack got right the hell into questioning them, once Kat went back to deal with the customers such as there were. He was good at it, playing up the \u2018of course you\u2019re not involved\u2019 angle, specifying we just wanted to see if they\u2019d seen anything that was fucking significant, even though they might not have recognized it as such. They didn\u2019t seem to have though, except for noticing that Kat had been on edge recently.<br /> <br /> I sat back with my sunglasses on, scanning the lot of them with Aura Sight before Kat left. None of the fuckers were supernatural or hiding anything from somebody in the shop just then. A couple of the girls, a pair of Laotians about 18 or 19, were feeling a bit pissy at Kat, but there were no serious red flags in anyone\u2019s body language towards her or the shop. Another of the girls, a Vietnamese girl in her early twenties, did look like she\u2019d started a new relationship recently, which was worth looking into. It didn\u2019t seem like any of them were the one tailing her, but a new boyfriend or girlfriend might be.<br /> <br /> Once Billy Mack started up the interviews, I kept a tap on their surface thoughts, for the most part. We started with the Laotians girls with chips on their shoulders. When Billy Mack asked about Kat, the first\u2019s surface thoughts were full of \u2018Bitch is trying to steal my friend\u2019s boyfriend\u2019, though she didn\u2019t say anything of the sort out loud. The other\u2019s surface thoughts backed that up, grumbling about having found Kat and her boyfriend, another of the employees we were interviewing, talking in Kat\u2019s office, with not a hell of a lot in the way of personal space between them.<br /> <br /> We moved onto the boyfriend next, with Billy Mack confirming that the two had been on a date this last Saturday night. Nothing in his surface thoughts implied anything about a relationship between him and Kat, so I went searching for a memory of the incident in Kat\u2019s office. She had been trying to convince him to walk her home, since it was the night after the first break in and he was a goddamn second degree black belt. Now, she didn\u2019t cross any lines, but she\u2019s got a manipulative streak that runs about as long as Liz\u2019s and she made full use of it. He wound up turning her down, especially after the girlfriend had walked in on them.<br /> <br /> The Vietnamese girl with a new relationship, Laura, was next. Going digging for something on her new guy or girl, I found out Laura lived in the same general area as Naomi, near the college. She has a boyfriend, and that wasn\u2019t the new one - another Vietnamese girl had shown up recently at her apartment and asked to crash there, and holy fuck, Laura had a thing for this girl she thought of as Amy. I recognized her as Heroin, and she was a hell of a lot hotter dismounting from her motorcycle, shaking her hair out as she smoothly took off her helmet than Billy Mack or Terry gave her credit for.<br /> <br /> Heroin had played on the \u2018us versus the others\u2019 factor of the both of them being Vietnamese, and was quick on the seducing step of the plan once she\u2019d gotten in. She was still mostly a goddamn mystery to Laura, coming and going on an unknown schedule, but Heroin had told her that she was dangerous and couldn\u2019t tell her too much about her life right now, which just inflamed the curiosity. Laura had even let Heroin leave some stuff there that she knew was highly illegal - Laura left it alone.<br /> <br /> We talked it out with the rest of them, but none of them had any interesting shit to say, or in their surface thoughts. I decided to stick around, have a late lunch - Kat recommended the Dragon\u2019s Breath, and brought me plenty of water after I ordered it and an order of seasoned fries - and keep an eye on things. Billy Mack also ordered a pizza, heading out to check on the rest of the agency, up on the rooftop.<br /> <br /> <br /> I kept my wits sharp while I slowly finished my fries, not that I noticed anything particularly goddamn relevant. At least, not until I saw Laura go out to meet Heroin on her bike. I managed to get eyes on her license plate and sent that shit over to Vivian quickly. I figured she\u2019d have her laptop with her, and the request for plate info is hell on a mobile screen. Plus, then she could do her magic and come up with a life story for the dame. It was more efficient.<br /> <br /> She got answers back quickly. The license plate was registered to a Paula Toc, who lived, according to the DMV, at a shithole apartment. Unfortunately, the life story wasn\u2019t forthcoming, probably because it was likely a fake name and a fabricated identity.<br /> <br /> I still had Aura Sight up, so I looked her over. Anything to save myself a trip to the fucking Bowling Alley of Sex. I blinked a few times when I gave it my first good look. Changeling was not what I was expecting. Especially not a Winter-aspected one. At least not from the description Billy Mack and Terry gave. Her aura was strong anyway, so I got pretty much most of what I needed.<br /> <br /> Her drive to survive was less surprising, and her rebellious side even less so. For all that she seemed to fit our stalker, she wasn\u2019t really hostile towards Kat, more just distrustful. She was protective towards Laura, in an I-like-her-but-am-not-overly-attached way, definitely not in a well-I\u2019ll-stop-fucking-running-guns-through-her-house kinda way, which got me thinking. I might have the order wrong. I went looking for a new relationship, figuring someone digging into Kat might get a foot in the door by starting to date an employee. But if it was Heroin, it looked like it might be the other way around - she started using Laura, got to feeling goddamn protective, and started looking into her boss.<br /> <br /> What would have prompted that was another matter. She didn\u2019t have a look like there was someone outside pulling the fucking strings, and I didn\u2019t know of any way Changelings had of telling if someone was a vampire. I did know they could tell if someone or something was supernatural, which might have been enough to get her paranoid. With Winter, I was pretty sure she could tell what made people sad, and if Kat having her goddamn husband shoot her after she woke up at her fucking funeral came up for that, it\u2019d have thrown a red flag for me, at least. I also knew that the Autumn Court, the big men in town, were occultish types. So if she\u2019d asked around what any of her Changeling contacts knew, she might have gotten ahold of an Autumn-aspected gee who knew about odd things like Kat.<br /> <br /> I thought about asking Rosanna or Crusher whether they knew if this shit lined up, but they were more Jack\u2019s contacts and I hadn\u2019t heard from Drake in a bit. So I sent the bounty hunter a quick text, giving him the situation without any fucking identifying details. I did mention that a Winter-aspected Changeling might be the one involved, cause I knew that different aspects have different powers sometimes.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t take him too long to get back to me. \u201cThere\u2019s a power that all Changelings can learn that leaves no trace of your passing, not even to object reading. As far as telling if someone is supernatural, there\u2019s Kenning, but it\u2019s pretty taxing. I dunno anything about getting in without using the door though. To be fair, there are so many, I couldn\u2019t begin to tell you what all the different types of fairies can do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks pal, that does help.\u201d<br /> <br /> His reply was quick enough I\u2019d lay odds he was typing it as soon as he sent the other. \u201cYou mentioned the Winter court. There\u2019s not a bunch - their King is this really scary dude, and there\u2019s two or three others. What you\u2019re talking about... Heroin\u2019s the name of one of them, she\u2019s basically a criminal. Not a drug dealer, despite her name, though an occasional user. She\u2019s a Darkling, and has a friend that\u2019s an Ogre. She generally doesn\u2019t try to start trouble but she won\u2019t hesitate to end it. And if you do deal with her? Don\u2019t let her touch you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. The others had mentioned a \u2018Tar\u2019. Ogre sounded like serious business. As did someone who it was dangerous to let fucking touch you. \u201cGood to know. Thanks again man. You doing alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah. Opened up the business to Changelings in particular. It\u2019s done wonders for my education, that\u2019s for sure. I have done my best to stick with a strict \u2018no politics\u2019 rule.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned. \u201cThat sounds like a good rule. Keep in touch, alright? Let me know if there\u2019s anything I can help out with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing. Take care of yourself.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Liz knocked on Esha\u2019s door, smiling brightly when she answered. Esha was taken aback somewhat. \u201cOh. So <i><i>you\u2019re</i></i> Gabe\u2019s friend then.\u201d She gestured Liz inside.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yes. Gabe and I have a long history - we go back a ways together.\u201d Liz took an offered seat.<br /> <br /> \u201cReally?\u201d Esha began laying out shit for the get-together. \u201cYou\u2019ll have to tell me how you two met.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz grinned fucking coquettishly. \u201cOh but I just met you. I can\u2019t tell that story yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> They chatted for awhile, until the neighbors showed up. Liz sent us a signal and we moved quickly. We managed to get inside without being spotted, and stopped short at the nice sticker advising us what goddamn brand of alarm they had set up. Those things work better if you don\u2019t leave your door open, as I find people do with regularity, like they did here. We got in just fine.<br /> <br /> The first townhouse we went into belonged to the couple. The place was sparse, covered in Target brand art and just enough to knick-knacks to believe someone lived here at a cursory glance. Still, the lack of dishes and the fucking pristine appliances said otherwise. I went looking for hidden things specifically, and that got me a little more - a big sturdy sound resistant suitcase, just big enough for one Esha-sized person in the fetal position. It had restraints to match. I took pictures and made sure it got back to exactly where the hell it had been.<br /> <br /> Vivian focused on the computer with its goddamn adorable cat pictures screensaver. The adorable cat pictures were no match for her, but still, she found it just as fucking boring and made up as the rest of the place. The couple had a Facebook account, pre-logged in, full of cat pictures and meal selfies. Their email was full of procedurally generated emails to \u2018Mom\u2019 with absolutely no spam in the spam folder. Just enough activity to make a case that someone used that computer, not enough that anyone real did. Even Synthesis didn\u2019t find anything but move-in day.<br /> <br /> We checked the other fucker's place, just for completionism, keeping an eye on our phones for word from Liz. She did keep a steady stream of idle chatter, just in fucking case. There wasn\u2019t anything new in the other place. A restraining suitcase in the same place, a slightly different theme for the goddamn Target brand art, and a Facebook full of weightlifting records and a set of dumbbells. Synthesis didn\u2019t come up with anything different.<br /> <br /> We let Liz know we were out, and waited for them to wrap up their coffee and pie. Once the stalkers had gotten back to their townhouses, Liz and Esha met us out by my car. Esha greeted me with a hug and a kiss on the cheek. \u201cDid... things go well?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThese fuckers are thorough. But I did get some pictures of a restraint device that might be proof enough for your bosses. Let me know quick - if it\u2019s not, plan B is to glom their phone and see if they\u2019re more goddamn lax about security on the device they carry on their person.\u201d Plan C was to lure them into a trap, but I wasn\u2019t going to worry her with that, not when plan A or B might get us there fine.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll try to contact them. I might not be able to get it to them before Friday.\u201d She bit her lip.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. Shit.\u201d I tapped my fingers on my fucking car door.<br /> <br /> She looked up at me worriedly. \u201cDo you have anything specific I should do or not do tomorrow? Should I be away from my room? They all claimed they\u2019d be away for the holiday, but I\u2019m pretty sure neither has the intentions to be.\u201d<br /> <br /> I ran my fingers through my hair. \u201cFuck. Yeah. Yeah, you should definitely not be where they expect you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can get a hotel?\u201d she offered. \u201cI\u2019m worried they might follow me though. And with the holiday... people might not suspect anything until Monday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. They lucked the hell out with timing here. If they don\u2019t try and take advantage of it, they are not as good as the seem.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cThey weren\u2019t actively planning to grab me tomorrow, but I think that\u2019s just cause they were waiting to see what I would be doing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked intent. \u201cI think we should both go back in, you pack as quickly as possible what you need for a day or two, then we go off together. They\u2019re unlikely to follow, since you\u2019ll be with me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd the three of us can stick around for a few minutes and make sure they don\u2019t follow quickly even if they do.\u201d I looked at the boys. They nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll pick you up from... let's say, Kiki's, and we\u2019ll get you a hotel, maybe something a bit out of town even.\u201d<br /> <br /> As they were walking off, Liz said to Esha, \u201cI hope you don\u2019t mind riding in a Maserati.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add here. For The Stranger, I used the Power/Finesse/Resistance thing and some suped up Numina, but she is a creature from Stranger Shores, so it\u2019s just trying to model that.<br /> <br /> Lot going on here so leaving the commentary there, but comments and questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T22:41:46-07:00","id":984753,"title":"","content":"Initially, I wasn't really grabbed by this game. The language was a bit confusing, both in the game's terminology and how the characters were speaking (though to be fair, I did hit this wall with the other games). Then I got involved in making my own Demon character, and it was like I had learned a new language, and fell in love with the story. The players are great to read from, the APs are on top form (Speed Demon's in particular are amazingly thorough, not to mention consistent), the solutions, methods and mistakes the team makes are grand, the locations are varied...it's all wonderful to read, almost addictive.<br /> <br /> You're darn good at what you do Baroness, to consistently get this level of quality back for so many games. :-p<br /> <br /> Also, props to Speed's player for the constant and consistent content APs. I can say from experience they are not easy to keep up to date with, much less with the actual dialogue being kept intact and taking OOC things to IC. Are the sessions recorded by Speed's player (I remember that the session they couldn't come in was), or do they just have <i>that</i> good a memory?<br /> <br /> ...are we entirely sure that Speed's player isn't a Demon themself? It would make only too much sense...<br /> <br /> Also, on another note, what kind of permanent glitches have those in the Agency accrued, and what Primum are they at? We were given stats for a number of the characters, but that was a bit ago, and aside from sometimes naming the Embeds and Exploits the characters use there aren't a lot of uses for the terms the gamebook uses.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, that's something all the players have been doing great with too, thumbs up. It really makes the story smooth and immersive to read, even when going from the differing styles.<br /> <br /> Can't wait to read more~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:58:27-07:00","id":985132,"title":"","content":"(Speed's player) Thanks! I used to do it 'from memory' by which I mean I took, just, all the notes. Since the session I couldn't come to, where I saw how much easier having a recording made things, I've been recording them.<br /> <br /> We're at Primum 6, all but Terry. Speed's permanent glitch (that she got for her high Primum) is that she always looks rumpled/like she slept in her office/probably after more than a few glasses of whiskey. Even when trying on brand new clothes. I believe it has driven Esha to distraction on occasion. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1471-levinserra","name":"LevinSerra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1471_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:34:01-07:00","id":986648,"title":"","content":"And Kilroy's glitch is that he shows up faintly as a network to wireless devices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T03:17:33-07:00","id":987168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amberghylles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=986648#post986648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Kilroy's glitch is that he shows up faintly as a network to wireless devices.</div> </div> </div> </div>Secured or unsecured, I'm wondering?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T08:19:24-07:00","id":987263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=987168#post987168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Secured or unsecured, I'm wondering?</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I imagine it as being listed similarly to one of the odd wifi networks in the Doctor Who episode &quot;The Bells of Saint John&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T16:49:06-07:00","id":988513,"title":"","content":"Vent0 - We've never actually specified that detail. Though he does have electromagnetic linguistics...<br /> <br /> Taidragon - Oh, that would fit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4217-amberghylles","name":"Amberghylles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4217_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:42:56-07:00","id":991511,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: Thanks so much for the kind words. I thought I had replied but apparently not. Apologies. Yeah Speed's player does excellent work on their journals, it is kinda amazing. I am especially pleased because it brings my wit for dialogue across, and and my wit for dialogue is part of what I have going for me. I especially enjoy playing some of the mouthy characters, (including but by no means limited to Pham Min and Langley Fitzgerald.) And getting to have some noir is fun too. Thanks again.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Kiki\u2019s was busy when we got there, unofficially celebrating its grand reopening, since it was the first night it had been open since the goddamn ghost attack. Even fucking Terry was there, pulling up in dark blue Range Rover shortly after we did. I guess one of the others let him know we'd be there. Vivian raised an eyebrow as he walked over. \u201cNew car?\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry nodded. \u201cI thought it was perfect. Space for the alligator and everything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd how are the repairs going?\u201d she asked. \u201cNeed any help with it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGoing well, going well.\u201d He shrugged. \u201cI\u2019ve been doing the more mundane stuff for starters.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cI see. Well, I\u2019ll be busy tomorrow - Shelley\u2019s taking me home to meet her parents - but at some point we should look into the actual heart of the problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry looked at her wide-eyed. \u201cYeah, the hell stove thing. I put a sign on it: \u2018Don\u2019t fucking touch this.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe may need your assistance as well. We are going to be moving on getting Madame X home through another Infrastructure. Your expertise might be quite useful in that endeavor. I believe she has given us four days, so we will likely be tackling that soon.\u201d<br /> <br /> He scratched his head. \u201cDo we have another one sitting around to give to her?\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian chuckled. \u201cWe were thinking the Waterworks. We have already trashed it once.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo are we just gonna not mention the Bee-Angel-Sharp-Edges thing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is the Dam. We will *not* be endangering the dam.\u201d Vivian\u2019s face turned goddamn serious fucking quickly. \u201cThe Waterworks is the city\u2019s other source of power, south of town.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cThere is also Peterson\u2019s. The thought of what Madame X and Hugbot would do when confronted with one another is... amusing.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cThat\u2019s gonna endanger your dam there, doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cYou are correct. Ah well. The Waterworks it shall have to be.\u201d She shrugged and looked back over at Terry\u2019s new car. \u201cYou get a good deal on that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a steal almost.\u201d I rolled my eyes at Terry. \u201cIt fell off the back of a truck. Kyle sold it to me for cheap. I\u2019m not 100% sure who the license plate belongs to though. It belongs to me at the moment at least.\u201d<br /> <br /> Around that time, Liz and Esha pulled up in the Tempter's Maserati. \u201cThank fuck.\u201d I muttered under my breath and moved to meet them. I smiled as I walked up to Esha. \u201cAll good, they didn\u2019t even move.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz ducked in to get the lay of the land as Esha and I dawdled and I reassured her about getting her through the weekend safely. Liz came back out fairly fucking quickly, letting us know she was going to work out some details for Esha\u2019s security. I held back a frown and nodded like I knew what she meant. Inside it was more clear. Not only was Liz\u2019s girlfriend and most of the rest of her Sin-Eater crew here, but Naomi\u2019s goddamn clique had their own table as well. Just after we sat down, Naomi joined them.<br /> <br /> The boys and Vivian came inside eventually. Jack and Terry got their own seat, and Terry got his usual order of \u2018more fucking wings than one human could possibly eat\u2019. Vivian got her usual - a seat in Shelley\u2019s section and a kiss on the cheek. \u201cHey there - how you holding up?\u201d Vivian smiled up at Shelley.<br /> <br /> \u201cPretty good.\u201d Shelley laid a hand on her shoulder and smiled back.<br /> <br /> \u201cThings been... quiet so far?\u201d Vivian sounded concerned.<br /> <br /> Shelley nodded reassuringly. \u201cBusy, so far. A good night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcellent. I am so glad.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shortly after I sat down, I got a text from Robin. \u2018When you get a chance - can we talk about the stuff you talked to Pham about?\u2019 I checked my phone quickly and looked apologetically at Esha. \u201cThat group over there has some information on a case. I\u2019ll be right back, alright doll?\u201d She nodded and smiled.<br /> <br /> I tossed my goddamn drink back and walked over to the Sin-Eaters\u2019 table. \u201cEverything alright?\u201d I sat in the chair Robin indicated.<br /> <br /> \u201cPham was talking to us about the meeting she had with you, but since about 70% of the things she says are bullshit, I wanted to know what actually happened.\u201d Robin looked tentatively concerned.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey! You offend me.\u201d Pham rolled her eyes and took a sip of her drink.<br /> <br /> I sat back in my seat. \u201cKat is a penanggalan, if that\u2019s what she\u2019s told you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin frowned. \u201cOK. I don\u2019t know a lot about what that means. Pham told me some things, but again, 70%...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, let\u2019s see what I can remember from Billy Mack\u2019s lectures...\u201d I made a show of dredging up boring fucking memories. \u201cThey do, as a general sort of rule, prefer feeding from pregnant women and children...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow old?\u201d Her frown deepened quickly.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow and took a drink. \u201cBabies.\u201d She relaxed slightly. \u201cIt\u2019s not a dietary restriction or any of that kind of bullshit, just a craving or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> Pham smiled brightly. \u201cSee, not bad people, they just have a craving for the flesh and blood of children.\u201d<br /> <br /> I ignored her. \u201cBilly Mack\u2019s really the one to talk to, I just know about shit he\u2019s said. I know they are a little bit different from vampires in that you can get sick from them - that\u2019s what happened to Kat.\u201d Pham started gesticulating \u2018I-told-you-sos\u2019 at Robin. I shrugged. \u201cI figured that wasn\u2019t a fucking shock, since you called her a disease monster.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow dangerous do you think that she is?\u201d Robin tapped the table thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot anymore dangerous than any other vampire, and I like her better than any of those I\u2019ve met.\u201d I shrugged. \u201cCertainly full of less bullshit. And prettier. She hasn\u2019t mind-controlled anyone, breathed mustard gas at them, or quoted fucking poetry at me, that I know of, so she\u2019s got three marks in the good column as far as I\u2019m concerned.\u201d<br /> <br /> Pham chuckled. \u201cSounds better than most of the people I\u2019ve dated.\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin looked over at her, brow furrowed. \u201cDo you ever take anything seriously?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cLook, I\u2019ve not seen any evidence in any of the investigating we\u2019ve done that she\u2019s up to any bad shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d She smiled at me. \u201cLike I said, I just wanted to talk to someone who wasn\u2019t Pham about this.\u201d<br /> <br /> Pham looked fucking incredulously at her. \u201cYou are crabby. You should call Liz and get laid.\u201d<br /> <br /> Robin scowled at her. \u201cI don\u2019t need to get laid. That has nothing to do with how crabby I am.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t get laid and I\u2019m not crabby.\u201d Sharon shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cStop helping, Sharon.\u201d Robin shook her head. \u201cThank you very much Gabe.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. A thought hit me and I snapped my fingers. \u201cI was wondering, have you seen anyone lurking around Kat\u2019s recently?\u201d I described Heroin. \u201cAnyone like that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy do you want to know about her?\u201d Pham eyed me goddamn warily.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve seen her lurking around, and you guys are there occasionally and perceptive to boot.\u201d<br /> <br /> Pham eyed me. \u201cMaybe... but I don\u2019t think she has anything specific with Kat.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged and raised my hands. \u201cAlright. Not looking to bring the hammer down or anything. Remember, <i>private</i> eye.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOK. You should probably leave her alone.\u201d Her usual cockiness wasn\u2019t really there.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat so?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cAnd I\u2019m not just saying that cause she\u2019s my friendly acquaintance.\u201d I raised an eyebrow. \u201cShe has very few compunctions about killing people. And I don\u2019t actually hate you. Which puts you ahead of most people.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cAw. I like you too Pham.\u201d I tapped the table as I stood up. \u201cYou three take care.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou too.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grabbed another drink and slid back into the booth across from Esha. \u201cThings go OK?\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cPeachy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s something off about the blond one.\u201d She frowned slightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cMild sociopathy.\u201d I nodded sagely. \u201cBilly Mack likes her, feels she\u2019s a fucking kindred spirit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Esha looked thoughtful. \u201cHave I met Billy Mack?\u201d<br /> <br /> I tapped my glass, thinking. \u201cNo, I guess not.\u201d I shrugged. \u201cMild sociopath. Another PI in the agency.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo where do you think I need to go?\u201d she asked me worriedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cA hotel, on the outskirts of town sounds like the best bet. Some place, some direction they have no reason to look for you in.\u201d I smiled reassuringly.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cOK.\u201d She paused for a moment. \u201cSo, are you and Elizabeth a couple?\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cNo. We work together - she\u2019s our butter and egg man and plays with being a PI. Pretty goddamn good at it too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe wouldn\u2019t give me a straight answer on how she met you, so I was just curious.\u201d Esha smiled at me.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cThat does sound like Liz. If you ever do manage a straight answer, lemme know. We\u2019ll have to celebrate.\u201d<br /> <br /> I took stock of the place. Terry and Jack were diving into a bucket of chicken wings, Kiki\u2019s Super Bowl special, with Terry gesticulating fucking wildly. Naomi was sitting in Cassandra\u2019s lap, eating off her plate. Vivian had all her electronics spread out on her table and looked deep into something hacker-y.<br /> <br /> The hacker was looking into Terry\u2019s stolen car and license plate, seeing what she could do to help the crazy fucker out. The plate was supposed to be on a pickup registered to a Peter Ross, who had a rap sheet a few pages long. Most of the charges were for trafficking baby exotic animals, but a too-fucking-big number of them were for trespassing - in pursuit, he claimed, of evangelizing about Calvinism. He was, it seemed, the only evangelical Calvinist the arresting officers had ever come across. They weren\u2019t fond of him.<br /> <br /> She shook her head, chuckling and got onto the process of getting Terry a proper tag, one that didn\u2019t come with a load of charges piled on it or with such a memorable former owner. She sent a quick text to let Terry know, about the problems with his current plate and the fact he\u2019d be getting a new one soon. \u2018You are gonna switch it out now, right?\u2019 Terry gave her a thumbs up and heading out to the parking lot. She sent another text out fucking quickly. \u2018Don\u2019t get near the blue Toyota.\u2019<br /> <br /> He shrugged and whistled as he ambled around the parking lot. He made the swap fairly quickly and as he stood up from putting on his new one, a bit of movement in a car a few spaces over caught his eye. He looked up to see a goddamn snake looking at him through the window. Even better, he heard talking coming from inside the car, in a language he didn\u2019t fucking recognize.<br /> <br /> As he got closer, he thought it sounded something like Egyptian, though nothing he could put a finger on. Before he got too close though, Zelda stepped out. \u201cWell hello miss,\u201d Terry greeted her fucking cheerily, \u201cI couldn\u2019t help but notice your snake.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI put it back in its basket.\u201d She smiled reassuringly at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Good. I just... wanted to make sure nobody was gonna lose... a snake. Out the window of their car. In the parking lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> She raised an eyebrow at him. He raised one back. \u201cI\u2019ll expect my snake to be in the van when I get back.\u201d She walked past him towards the door.<br /> <br /> \u201cSome nerve,\u201d Terry muttered to himself. \u201cI mean, it\u2019s not like I was stealing someone\u2019s tag just before I started that conversation.\u201d He moved closer to Zelda\u2019s car and peered inside. A goddamn large snake looked back at him. He couldn\u2019t recognize what kind of snake it was, though as he looked closer he realized he could see shoulders for a moment. \u201cI don\u2019t know much about animals, but I don\u2019t think snakes have shoulders.\u201d<br /> <br /> Back inside, I noticed Zelda walk in, and glanced around to make sure the others did as well. I sent a quick text to the agency. \u2018The dame who just walked in is Zelda, the mummy.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Who\u2019s at war with Erasmus, the one who has Skeevy Larry, the one whose alligator ate someone in your building, Terr