/> \u2018Are you joyriding in his Range Rover? It is clunky.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018No! Not joyriding! Dodging fucking lightning monsters!\u2019<br /> <br /> I held in a snort. \u2018Yeah, Range Rover\u2019s a poor choice for that.\u2019<br /> <br /> <br /> Before I got that text from Jack, I\u2019d been texting Miranda. \u2018Hey beautiful. I gotta brace a suspect, and catch them off guard to do it. Might be a long night. Look - I forgot to ask, cause it\u2019s been a hell of a long time since I\u2019ve had someone to spend it with, but you got anything going tomorrow?\u2019<br /> <br /> After a little bit, I got a response. \u2018No. But I would be very happy to spend it with you.\u2019<br /> <br /> The thought kept me warm over a long fucking night. It wasn\u2019t til a little after sunrise that Heroin left Laura\u2019s apartment, shrugging into her black leather jacket. I got out and leaned against my car, catching her attention and her eye. She sauntered over. \u201cWhatcha want?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u201cI\u2019m having a bit of a problem.\u201d I crossed my arms. \u201cWell... name's Gabe. PI. I have a client who\u2019s been having a bit of a problem with someone looking in on them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWho\u2019s your client?\u201d Her face wasgoddamn guarded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI dunno. You looking in on anyone?\u201d I held her gaze.<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cYeah.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cAny particular reason?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDifferent reasons, depending on the person.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI was kinda figuring it might have been because you really fucking like Thai pizza or maybe cause your, uh, girlfriend? works there.\u201d<br /> <br /> She peered into my eyes. \u201cShe does.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cSo you wanna know why I\u2019m looking into Kat?\u201d I nodded. \u201cI probably don\u2019t plan to hurt Kat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat \u2018probably\u2019 doesn\u2019t really ease my troubled heart.\u201d I smirked at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I don\u2019t know what her deal is.\u201d She shifted her hips, leaning a little closer. \u201cAnd so I don\u2019t know if that puts people I may care about in danger.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled, enjoying the goddamn view. \u201cThat does a little more to ease it, honestly, it being a looking after Laura thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave me a lopsided grin. \u201cWell yeah. The poor thing\u2019s not gonna look after herself. I mean, she\u2019s letting a dangerous gun toting criminal live with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is not a good sign for her self-preservation, I\u2019ll admit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe does get some great ass out of it.\u201d She raised an eyebrow at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhich does lay out some priorities, I guess.\u201d I grinned back. \u201cIs there anything I could do to ease your own troubled heart on the subject?\u201d<br /> <br /> She tapped her lip, thinking. \u201cIf I knew for certain she posed no threat to Laura...\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cThat\u2019s a tall order on its own. What can I maybe do to reassure on that front?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou could tell me what her deal is.\u201d She leaned on my car, slightly flexing her arm to rest her hand on her chin.<br /> <br /> I gave her Kat\u2019s bio as I knew it, leaving out the whole \u2018coming back from the dead\u2019 thing. \u201cI think it was problems with the family that had her moving here.\u201d<br /> <br /> She gave a short laugh. \u201cBig problems with her family.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEither they tried to bury her alive, or bury her dead.\u201d She shrugged.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow and made a considering noise. \u201cI think it was the latter, at least at the time. She got better.\u201d<br /> <br /> She frowned. \u201cShe doesn\u2019t feel like people who got better. I have a friend who got better.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVarying levels of \u2018better\u2019. She\u2019s not a Sin-Eater, not 'fully healed' better. But she did stand the hell up again.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heroin smirked. \u201cI wouldn\u2019t say Sin-Eaters are fully healed. My friend\u2019s a little broken.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cI\u2019ll have to give you that one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s a hell of a lot of fun for it though.\u201d She had a fond smile on her face. \u201cSome people say if you\u2019ve never died, how can you really live?\u201d She paused. \u201cI haven\u2019t died, but I\u2019ve come pretty close to the edge.\u201d She cocked her head at me. \u201cI\u2019m glad you and I both like to live close to the edge.\u201d<br /> <br /> Man, she was hot. \u201cS\u2019fair. Can\u2019t say I\u2019ve got any desire to go ahead and jump the fuck off it though.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her smile widened. \u201cThat\u2019s what makes the edge exciting. You can see how far down it goes.\u201d<br /> <br /> A moment passed, and I cleared my throat. \u201cIt does occur to me. Pham knows what her deal is, so it might as well come from me, so I can get brownie points in a deal. Odds are if you poked long enough, you\u2019d get it anyway.\u201d I grinned at her. \u201cShe\u2019s a penanggalan.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy would Pham not tell me that, I wonder...\u201d she mused.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe just learned it recently.\u201d I shrugged. \u201cThat make you feel any better?\u201d<br /> <br /> She frowned. \u201cWhat the hell is one of those doing over here... well, yeah, that would be what one of those is doing over here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHiding from the family, I\u2019d imagine.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, a goddamn sad look passing over her face. \u201cI know how that is.\u201d She shook it off and looked determined. \u201cI\u2019ll just have to have a conversation and let her know Laura is off the menu.\u201d She glanced up at me. \u201cYou can be there for that if you want to. Or I can have it by myself. It won\u2019t be the kind of conversation that involves knives.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded slowly. \u201cI would prefer to be there - she is a client.\u201d I raised an eyebrow. \u201cSpeaking of brownie points... could we keep between us fuckers how you found out about the whole vampire thing? She hasn\u2019t told me, you see. But it doesn\u2019t do to not go looking into your clients.\u201d<br /> <br /> She took a step closer and sniffed the air near me. \u201cSo you\u2019re not a Sin-Eater... and you\u2019re not one of the Kind... what\u2019s your deal?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA lady - even one as fucking disreputable as me - has gotta have her secrets.\u201d I smirked at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI hope you\u2019re not saying that to dissuade me.\u201d She raised an eyebrow. I just smiled. She got out a business card to a body shop and wrote something on the back of it before slipping it into my pocket. \u201cContact me, sometime after Thanksgiving. Thanksgiving\u2019s my day to get drunk.\u201d Her tone was bitter. \u201cSeeing your family today?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSuch as I have.\u201d My lips quirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cLucky, lucky you.\u201d She pushed herself off my car and sauntered back over to her motorcycle.<br /> <br /> I watched her over there, and watched her get up on her bike. Then I watched her drive off. After a moment I shook my head and hopped into my car. I glanced at the card before I drove off. I knew the shop, but not anything special about it. On the back she\u2019d written a phone number and \u2018You can\u2019t feel the heat if you don\u2019t dance near the fire.\u2019<br /> <br /> I made one stop on my way to Miranda\u2019s - by my place to get a quick change of clothes. I left the business card on my dresser.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-22-2016, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T13:43:29-07:00","id":991512,"title":"","content":"Miranda made a hell of a Thanksgiving dinner, and I was in a good mood when I came back into the office Friday. I made arrangements to have Nikka stop by the office a little after lunch to get her approval for the next step, so I headed in a little early to let the others know about it.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack was already there and Liz got in shortly after. \u201cWell, I do still apparently fit into my Billy Mack suit. How was your holiday?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned and shrugged. Liz smiled goddamn widely. \u201cOh, lovely. Very lovely. I had a wonderful time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Right then Cecilia came stomping in and sat sulkily down at her desk, Jack just behind her. After a moment she glanced up to see Liz. \u201cOh hello Master.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz smiled at her and kissed her on the head. \u201cI\u2019m so sorry your cousin has been making you suffer. I\u2019ll have a word with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think she\u2019s good enough for you.\u201d Cecilia frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh...\u201d Liz sounded excited. \u201cOutright plotting against her now. Dangerous territory.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack looked between them. \u201cDo I want to know what happened?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t want to talk about it right now.\u201d Cecilia looked away.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid you at least hit her for it?\u201d Jack grinned.<br /> <br /> Cecilia looked fucking guilty. \u201cI slapped her. She started laughing at me when I did...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack leaned over and kissed her on the cheek. Cecilia looked past him at Liz, looking like she expected reprisal. \u201cIt\u2019s OK,\u201d Liz reassured her.<br /> <br /> Terry showed up right as Billy Mack let us know coffee was ready. We went upstairs to talk business. I spiked my coffee and turned my chair around to sit in it backwards, frowning at Terry as he poked his shoulder. Jack rolled his eyes at him. \u201cStop poking it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s fine. It just wouldn\u2019t go back together.\u201d He shrugged, and winced slightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust what wouldn\u2019t go back together?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> He thought for a goddamn moment. \u201cProbably a clavicle?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack glared at me. \u201cThe bits that got cut open by the \u2018clunky\u2019 things Wednesday night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe fuck? When you were drag racing lightning monsters?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked between us. \u201cWhat was all that about?\u201d He touched Terry on the shoulder. \u201cYou should be better once you sleep, Terry.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack started gesturing, \u201cThose automaton things you were talking about, the pieced together people things...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou went to the hospital!\u201d Liz interrupted. Liz\u2019s cigarette dropped out of its holder.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, we went so Terry could get a read on what the fuck the God Machine thought about that place,\u201d Jack started to explain.<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow. \u201cWhich doesn\u2019t require going inside.\u201d<br /> <br /> He crossed his arms. \u201cWell, yes. But whatever the hell Kilroy was looking at, that one,\u201d he pointed at Terry, \u201cgot interested in, and I had to cover him, cause I didn\u2019t feel like pulling him out was gonna work. We didn\u2019t touch anything, we were just looking.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomething clearly touched you.\u201d Billy Mack said with a straight face.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, when we opened the doors to the Infrastructure, three of those fucking things jumped us, and Jesus Christ, I thought they were clunky.\u201d He yelled the last phrase.<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes. \u201cFor goddamn fuck\u2019s sake, get over it. They were, when we fought them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Terry shrugged. \u201cThey had some kinda power over them, like a kind of blur.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey hit Terry twice before I could pull the trigger.\u201d Jack glared at us.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo Madame X can fuck with zombie monsters. Good job. You learned something.\u201d I tossed back my laced coffee, now that it was just cool enough to do so.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cShe clearly relocated them, and she likely did improve them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz relit her cigarette. \u201cObviously security was lax, since we got up there the first time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019d missed him with a gurney already, and a monitor.\u201d Jack slumped back in his seat.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, a monitor. They tried a typewriter with me. Those two things were more likely the ghosts than the automatons,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> Terry nodded, wide eyed. \u201cSome of them seemed right helpful. And others... were not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGlass was shattering out of doors, slicing me up.\u201d Jack frowned. \u201cAnd there were weird flies. Terry said they had human eyes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was thinking - my idea was - to get an idea how to fix the place.\u201d Terry shrugged.<br /> <br /> Liz gave a quick laugh. \u201cYour idea was to go into the place the rest of your Agency fled screaming. Maybe we won\u2019t flee screaming. I understand how horror movie logic works now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave her a quieting look. \u201cYour ability to read the God-Machine\u2019s intents could have certainly been useful in determining how much interest it had in the place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe signal to noise ratio in that place was hard.\u201d Terry rubbed his fucking head. \u201cI got pieces of maybe what was going on, but then it would get futzed up something weird.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe compromised Infrastructure is clearly making it difficult to get a read on the place.\u201d Billy Mack nodded thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cSo, while some people were fucking traipsing through death traps, that they were told were death traps, I was talking to Heroin.\u201d I flipped the card out onto the table. \u201cWe\u2019re going to arrange a meetup, so Heroin can ask her nicely to not eat Laura, and everything will be hunky-fucking-dory.\u201d I leaned back. \u201cI may have let it slip she was a penanggalan, figuring her close relationship with Pham\u2019d have it out eventually anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow close?\u201d Liz frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cSounded pretty close. She may have been trying to make me jealous though.\u201d I shrugged. \u201cPham also knew that Kat had come back from the dead, or at least that her family had tried to bury her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz eyed me. \u201cWas she trying to seduce you?\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked and took a sip of laced coffee. \u201cMaybe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s a hot girl in Gabe\u2019s presence. Of course she was trying to seduce her.\u201d Jack rolled his fucking eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not trying to seduce Gabe, and I\u2019m the hottest girl she\u2019s ever been around.\u201d Liz gave him a prim look.<br /> <br /> Jack chuckled. \u201cYou flirt with Gabe constantly. That\u2019s close enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I seduce Gabe, I\u2019ll eat her, you silly person.\u201d Liz took a drag on her cigarette. \u201cI don\u2019t want Gabe to die.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway...\u201d I tried steering things back the hell to business. \u201cI also invited Nikka to stop by so we can work out our next move, now that we know who the apprentice is. I\u2019ll probably call Heroin after that, to work out the arrangements.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds good.\u201d Jack crossed his arms. \u201cAre we organizing this meetup, or just being somewhere nearby?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cWe\u2019re the middleman. At a guess, Kat\u2019s gonna prefer to have someone on her side there when she talks to her stalker. On the other hand, she might want privacy, since she doesn\u2019t know we know, and I wanna keep it that way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe does seem slightly paranoid, not that I wouldn\u2019t be paranoid myself, in her shoes,\u201d Liz offered.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cOther business - do we have any leads on Skeevy Larry? We\u2019ve got everything Mr. Gone asked for. If we give him what we\u2019ve got so far, that\u2019s our fucking job done. We\u2019ve been holding off to see if we can\u2019t get somewhere with Skeevy Larry and this Mummy business ourselves. But I\u2019m all for coughing up a report and getting paid and not having mage business hanging over our heads. Especially given the risk he finds some of this shit out on his own.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked thoughtful. \u201cI could interview Zelda again. I was... distracted, Wednesday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI could look for someone who\u2019s missing an alligator,\u201d Jack offered.<br /> <br /> Liz hid a smile behind her hand. \u201cYou\u2019re going to be missing an alligator, I think, if you keep him up there.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack sighed. \u201cI know she\u2019s tired of it. We need to go look in the Undercity and see what we can set up, but we\u2019re a little busy. I\u2019d explain it, but I don\u2019t want to have her head explode from the details I\u2019d have to explain.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe don\u2019t want to upset her.\u201d Liz smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe Naomi seems to have done a fine job of that,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> Liz\u2019s smile widened. \u201cWhat a little bitch.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled back. \u201cVivian was much better... what am I saying, she was not actually much better behaved than that yesterday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d have been disappointed if so.\u201d Jack smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo would Shelley, oddly enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz shrugged. \u201cSome people like a bad girl.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cAnd some people want their families to know it.\u201d He nodded towards me. \u201cDo we have anything to gain from finding Skeevy Larry?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe may have some stake in the conflict between the Mummies, but I dunno if Skeevy Larry\u2019s the best fucking way in.\u201d I walked a coin over my knuckles.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd we might get a bonus if we give extra info to Gone,\u201d Jack pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not a hardship to talk to Zelda anyway. Angela has something she wants to talk to me about Special Collections over at the library, so I can get two birds with one trip and be back in time for Nikka?\u201d She looked to me. I nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. Esha\u2019s been checking in regularly and her office doesn\u2019t open up until Monday, so that\u2019s all of our cases moving forward. Otherwise, we got Madame X\u2019s deal, the monster in the hospital basement and Terry\u2019s cults.\u201d I started counting off on my fingers.<br /> <br /> That was apparently a trigger to start Billy Mack and Terry discussing... some fucking thing furiously. After a moment my eyes glazed over, and when I tried to pay better attention, I started getting a headache. So I went back to my office and sent messages off to Kat, letting her know we had a solid lead.<br /> <br /> The boys fully traumatized by what the g-man had to share, Billy Mack started going over the recorded writings and planning out how to use the Waterwheel to send Madame X home. After a little bit, he gave Kayla a call. \u201cHey! What did she do?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cActually, I was calling because I need some of your expertise on a delicate matter of engineering.\u201d Billy Mack smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cOK...\u201d she said hesitantly.<br /> <br /> He explained the situation - the state we left the water wheel in, the overall goals we had in mind, and a little bit about what the hell he figured we need to do. \u201cI need to make sure I have a good idea of the state it\u2019s in now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll be able to tell you in... tomorrow?\u201d she suggested.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019ll do.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Just before Nikka got there, Billy Mack gathered us together. \u201cWe\u2019re going to need a human element to make this work.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tapped the table with a pen. \u201cI don\u2019t like the fucking way you said that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019ll need to incorporate a certain amount of physical suffering, as that is what the Waterwheel runs on,\u201d he elaborated.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course we will.\u201d I ran my fingers through my hair. \u201cWater just isn\u2019t enough for a goddamn water wheel to run off of?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes. \u201cSo do I need to look for a special someone who enjoys pain?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shrugged. \u201cOr we could use one of the stigmatics I am sure we will run across as we endeavor to gain access. We don\u2019t necessarily have to do them permanent harm.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPenelope only likes pain so much. I think she would stop being willing very quickly.\u201d Liz frowned. \u201cAnd I don\u2019t share Am with anyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt had also crossed my mind that I am sure we could get a member of Ganora\u2019s cult to agree to this,\u201d Billy Mack threw out there.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cHaving someone loyal or making the best out of having to rough up the stigmatics there sounds like the best plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz looked goddamn unhappy, but nodded. \u201cI did get to talk to Zelda. She thinks Skeevy Larry is working from the Undercity. Not under your house, probably - that bit of the Undercity is very dangerous, apparently.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh. So whatever has infected that building has spilled beneath it?\u201d Billy Mack looked intrigued.<br /> <br /> \u201cOr the reverse,\u201d Liz pointed out.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cWe really should take a look, when we have a few spare moments.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d Liz took a drag on her cigarette. \u201cSecond thing - Angela works in Special Collections in the university. There\u2019s an attic room where they keep a lot of stuff. It was broken into Thanksgiving night and while she was checking to see if anything was missing, she found a partially open hidden room, that, judging by the disturbed dust, have 5 books stolen from it. The bits of the catalog she could access say that only a handful of tenured professors on campus were cleared to know what was in that room. When they were told, one of them skipped the state to Iowa and the rest are really agitated.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo they seem to think something very bad is about to happen,\u201d Billy Mack mused.<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cAngela is worried and wants us to look into it.\u201d<br /> <br /> I swung around in my chair. \u201cIs the school concerned about the loss?\u201d They\u2019d actually pay, for one. We\u2019d have to spin whatever we got, but that\u2019s the cost of doing business sometimes.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey say they don\u2019t have any books on the record as missing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack chuckled. \u201cSo they\u2019re covering it up.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stretched. \u201cSounds like it. I could talk with one of the professors. I know a few tricks to get them talking, in a couple of manners of speaking. That should be easy enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll get the names from Angela.\u201d She started messing with her fucking phone. \u201cI\u2019ll get Am to ask Angela, that way I don\u2019t have to switch personas. Am is utterly loyal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat.\u201d I looked around. \u201cSo, we wanna go looking for Skeevy Larry, or report in to Gone?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack started shaking his head. \u201cThe Undercity is a large place.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy thought exactly. If Gone wants us to scour the Undercity for him, we can write up a new contract and get paid for that.\u201d The others nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll call him after Nikka.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow do we want to proceed with that?\u201d Billy Mack asked.<br /> <br /> I leaned back. \u201cI\u2019m all for the plan where we turn the apprentice group against Not-a-Farmer. I wanna get her go-ahead though, to avoid any paranoia about why we\u2019re meeting clandestinely with the people who jumped her with knives. I don\u2019t wanna be part of any goddamn movie-level misunderstanding.\u201d<br /> <br /> The others were in agreement as Cecilia walked in. \u201cMy crush is here.\u201d<br /> <br /> I gave her a lopsided grin. \u201cSend her on up.\u201d After a moment, Nikka joined us. \u201cHey doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHello.\u201d She settled into a chair.<br /> <br /> \u201cTo get right to the point - we found his apprentice. Or at least, one of the fuckers who attacked you outside of Kiki\u2019s.\u201d I raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cAha.\u201d She nodded thoughtfully. \u201cWe are going to see what information they have on Cornelius?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack leaned forward. \u201cA little more than that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I jerked my head in his direction. \u201cWe were also hoping to try and push them towards making a play against him themselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDivide and conquer...\u201d she muttered.<br /> <br /> \u201cYep. No matter who comes out ahead, we\u2019ve got less motherfuckers out to kill you. We wanted to run it by you, get your OK, and make sure there were no misunderstandings about our intentions.\u201d<br /> <br /> She pulled out a cigarette and Liz lit it with her own. She raised an eyebrow at Liz. \u201cI am OK with it. You are doing this because I hired you. You have little reason to betray me. I like to believe that we have a rapport.\u201d She smiled at me.<br /> <br /> I smirked back. \u201cSomething like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKeep me as appraised as best you can, without... compromise.\u201d She waved a hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course.\u201d I fiddled with a pen. \u201cAnd you\u2019ve been alright? No weird shit?\u201d<br /> <br /> She scrunched her face a little bit. \u201cI don\u2019t think so.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned. \u201cGiven what we know, it seems important to err on the side of caution in these matters.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI left like I might be being followed at the grocery store. I have not returned and took a circuitous route home.\u201d She crossed her arms. \u201cIt could have been nothing but... I do not think he knows where I live.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd it would be for the best to keep it that way.\u201d Billy Mack nodded encouragingly.<br /> <br /> Jack glanced at me, then back to Nikka. \u201cWe do have the additional security package, if we wanna got that route.\u201d<br /> <br /> Nikka also glanced at me. \u201cI have placed with Gabe my safety. Whatever she thinks is best.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is an extra cost, and the results can be... dramatic.\u201d Jack shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you say, Gabe?\u201d Nikka asked.<br /> <br /> I nodded approvingly at Jack. \u201cIt\u2019s not a bad deal. He\u2019s a bit of a whiz with home security systems.\u201d<br /> <br /> She inclined her head decisively. \u201cAlright. It will be done. Cash will still be acceptable?\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned at her. \u201cOf course.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smiled and got out one of his contracts, setting it up for a week. \u201dWhen will be a good time to go by your place where I won\u2019t be in the way?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot toni - oh. To not be in my way, tonight would be fine. I will not be there, tonight is business.\u201d She looked over the contract, and signed it. \u201cIf you come by Kiki\u2019s, I will have my extra key on me.\u201d She looked around at us as she stood up. \u201cThank you very much. I will see some of you tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s the plan.\u201d I smiled at her and stood to shake her hand.<br /> <br /> Cecilia was at the door as Nikka reached it. \u201cWalk you out ma\u2019am?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cCertainly.\u201d<br /> <br /> After Nikka left, Jack stood and stretched. \u201cIf he does find her house, that\u2019ll be a bad day for him. It might not kill him, but it\u2019ll hurt like hell.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThey do feel pain. In fact, if one really looks at it from a certain perspective, it could actually be a disadvantage to them, to be unkillable.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJesus Christ.\u201d I stood up and moved towards my office to call a fucking mage lawyer, who at least probably wouldn\u2019t muse about torturing people in front of me.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s my cue!\u201d Liz exclaimed, standing up herself. \u201cBourbon and codeine are calling from my office.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LIII</i><br /> <br /> I think Vivian meant Water Wheel<br /> <br /> So, what Terry\u2019s player actually said was \u201cI don\u2019t have any Animal Ken, but I don\u2019t think snakes have shoulders.\u201d Which lead to us preceding obvious statements with \u201cI don\u2019t have any Animal Ken but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> Man, I had fun doing the haunted hospital. They should go there like all the time. Terry healed about as fast as he took damage, till he took agg. Jack is less of a healer but never piled on the damage Terry did.<br /> <br /> Okay, comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T17:24:08-07:00","id":991613,"title":"","content":"I do have a question regarding the Hookah that Clytemnestra has; it's suborned infrastructure, but was it part of the home she has, was it found and moved there, and or was it always the form of a hookah? I ask because I am having a hard time finding how infrastructure gets to how it is in its Suborned Infrastructure merit state, and I'm curious as to how it was handled here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T11:19:59-07:00","id":991921,"title":"","content":"Back story is it was stolen from an existing Infrastructure and Ms. Liquor altered it into a self perpetuating state and added the hookah as interface. In game terms it is just what it says on the tin. Does that answer your question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 10-23-2016, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T13:17:52-07:00","id":991980,"title":"","content":"Very much so, thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:10:04-07:00","id":998897,"title":"","content":"<br /> Back to rain city to check on our favorite reality deviants and divine rebels.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Billy Mack ducked his head into Jack\u2019s office. \u201cI am going by the hospital to speak with Madame X. There should be no issues...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack interrupted him, shaking his head. \u201cYou really shouldn\u2019t go in by yourself though. Asked around?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. Well, Gabe was on the phone at the time, and Liz is high on codeine and would prefer to not have her skin removed again. Apparently, she is a little \u2018once flesh unwound like a spaghetti noodle from her face, twice shy\u2019.\u201d Billy Mack shrugged. \u201cHopefully, everything will be civil. I do plan on discussing the specifics of the transfer we\u2019ll be assisting with, so it may be advantageous to not have too many of us listen closely to those details.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack grabbed his jacket, intent on the fucking buddy system. \u201cTo the hospital then.\u201d<br /> <br /> As they made their way to the hospital, Jack split off an Alibi of Miguel to go about his daily business of being seen.<br /> <br /> Once they got there, the pair moved goddamn carefully into the hospital. Billy Mack noted the new blood stain in a detached sort of way before calling out to the hospital in general. \u201cHello?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re here to see Madame X,\u201d Jack said gruffly.<br /> <br /> \u201cTo discuss the details of sending you home,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> After a moment, the elevator doors slid open. The two Demons noted with interest that the none of the lights were on, though there was a soft yellowish-green glow from beyond the doors. Once they opened a little wider, the two could see the fucking pulsating viscera that coated the elevator shaft and Madame X stepped out. An undulating intestine, connecting the door to the walls beyond it, moved out of her way. She took a few more steps forward, towards the two fuckers.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack stepped forward to meet her. \u201cHello there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHello.\u201d The silence after that greeting stretched goddamn uncomfortably.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have located an more suitable, undamaged piece of Infrastructure that we believe will have less detrimental effect, based on what I have been able to understand about the process.\u201d Billy Mack nodded to her.<br /> <br /> Her voice was thready and rusty with disuse. \u201cI shall have to modify it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded, more eagerly. \u201cYes, I understand that.\u201d He gave the specs for the Water Wheel. She nodded frequently, appearing to make note of the details he went over. \u201cAt this point, our estimate for the best time would be Sunday morning?\u201d He said it as a question, and waited for her approval before continuing. \u201cWe have someone who is taking care of some last minute reconnaissance. Unless something comes up with that, we will meet then. If it does, I will come speak with you again tomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe constructs you have upstairs - do they feel pain?\u201d Her goddamn wide-eyed stare turned on Jack as he spoke up.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack put a reassuring tone in his voice. \u201cAs I mentioned, the Water Wheel runs on pain, as opposed to misery. We should be able to make arrangements to have a suitable subject.\u201d<br /> <br /> She stared at him. \u201cThat will make the conversion easier. I\u2019ll just need to bring a few things from here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you have any knowledge of the thing in the basement?\u201d Jack asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is excessively dangerous.\u201d She thought for a fucking moment. \u201cIt was here when I arrived. It is atavistic. I was unable to harm it - when I attempted to take a sample, it did not work.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack frowned. \u201cSo not yours. And the constructs - will you be leaving them here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPresumably. They are simply animated corpses with some necrosurgery.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan you make them not attack us?\u201d Jack asked, rubbing his shoulder. \u201cThey were more than a little hostile last time I was here.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPresumably.\u201d She stared at him. \u201cThey do not allow people to touch the machine. They are not hostile to you if you do not approach the machine.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded his understanding. \u201cIt is our intention to repair the machine here once you are gone, as in its damaged state it is harmful to our reality.\u201d<br /> <br /> She paused for a moment. \u201cWhen I leave, they will return to their previous condition. I can put them back where they were.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery well.\u201d Billy Mack smiled. \u201cWe appreciate it. Will you require any assistance in bringing supplies along Sunday?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do not anticipate it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack took a moment to phrase things fucking carefully. \u201cAnd this will not require any dismantling of the Infrastructure here?\u201d<br /> <br /> She stared at him. \u201cNot presuming I have here what I have there. I will have to dismantle the things I have placed in the Infrastructure to modify it to work properly. The human organs and some of the other things will be taken out of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCertainly. No need to duplicate such efforts there when they have been done once. How long do you expect to need?\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cForty five minutes, if what you have described is correct.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded goddamn thoughtfully. \u201cAs it is a functional Infrastructure, as opposed to one that is abandoned, there will be some amount of security. We will certainly be able to take care of it, but it is good to know how long we shall need to do so.\u201d<br /> <br /> She cocked her head. \u201cI can help deal with them but it will be time I am not working.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHopefully we can get everything taken care of.\u201d Billy Mack smiled. \u201cOut of curiosity... there was an individual responsible for bringing you here, a Virgil Crumb?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, not familiar with him by name?\u201d Billy Mack described the pinked mage. She nodded. \u201cWhat can you tell me about him?\u201d<br /> <br /> She paused. \u201cLittle. It tried to bind me and was not able to. I was not able to remove its flesh effectively. It could use this reality against me as a weapon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, they do that.\u201d Billy Mack nodded thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt makes me upset.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe has met with a bad end,\u201d Billy Mack informed her.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack chuckled. \u201cAnd presumably it was because of an attempt to marshal resources to attempt to bring you to heel.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cGood. I need to get back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI agree. This is not where you belong. And returning you to your home is the most efficient way of taking care of that problem.\u201d Billy Mack smiled at the fucking weird dame. He made sure to give her proper directions for reaching the Water Wheel, as well as describing the bit of trees on the riverbank we planned to meet up at. \u201cWe will meet you there at 11 AM on Sunday.\u201d She nodded. \u201cI am looking forward to assisting you. I am glad we were able to come to an agreeable solution to our mutual problems.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and the corners of her mouth turned up in a goddamn horrifying approximation of a smile. \u201cI have preparations to make.\u201d She turned to leave, the elevator doors opening up in front of her. She walked in, and as the doors shut on her, the two Demons could see fucking intestines with teeth descend from the ceiling and wrap around her arms. They were beginning to pull her up as the doors closed.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cIt will be fascinating to go over this place once she is gone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWith a flamethrower? Sure.\u201d Jack frowned at the elevator.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cMs. Norton, this is a most anticipated phone call.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned back in my seat, ignoring the fucking g-man at my door. \u201cGlad to hear it. So, Mr. Gone, we tracked down your guy - the one who did the deed and the one who probably hired him for it. The gee who owns the alligator goes by Skeevy Larry.\u201d<br /> <br /> The mage made a considering noise. \u201cAlright... I believe I\u2019ve seen that name written down.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe got a sketch drawn up from a witness at the apartment complex - I\u2019ll be sending a followup email with a summary of everything, and it will include the sketch and other similar documents. No direct evidence that he owns that alligator, but we have statements that he has brought more than one strange reptile to his day job, and that he bragged about having an alligator.\u201d I brought up the report on my computer to check all our shit out one last time. \u201cAs to why... he\u2019s connected to a guy who goes by Erasmus? Not sure whether it\u2019s a first or last name, as best I can tell it\u2019s his only one.\u201d<br /> <br /> He grunted. \u201cI see.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou recall from Crumb\u2019s office, Zelda was the name of the dame who was renting the room and someone he was meeting with for assistance. She\u2019s something of an enemy of this Erasmus fucker. Our thought was that he figured Crumb was working for Zelda and offed him for that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d He mused a bit. \u201cSo a Skeevy Larry killed Virgil because he was working for his employer\u2019s rival. That does make sense.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cYeah. It\u2019s not the 'gonna hold up in court' kinda evidence, but there are some strong ties there and... not anywhere else.\u201d I tapped my desk. \u201cHe\u2019s got himself a squat in the Undercity. We hadn\u2019t narrowed it down past that - as I understood, you wanted a name and a motive and to deal with whoever it was yourselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mr. Gone sighed. \u201cThat would be ideal. We do, however, have some more immediate irons in the fire, not that that is yo