e immediately to mind, but I can keep you informed.\u201d He nodded agreeably, then something occurred to him. \u201cActually, Dr. Hazard might be good for that. He was the next person I was going to speak to. He\u2019s not on campus today, but he should be back Monday.\u201d He frowned. \u201cDr. Richardson wasn\u2019t supposed to be on campus today either.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded and fished around for a card and handed it to him. \u201cI would like to keep in contact about this. I think we do have the same goals, of keeping the students here safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> He took it and slid it into his own pocket. \u201cI regret I do not carry my own cards. I believe you can find me on the school directory however.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing.\u201d I smiled and turned to look the fucking place over.<br /> <br /> I checked for hidden things first and was able to find two - one above the ceiling of this top floor room and one behind a particular wall inside the hidden room. How the hell to get to them wasn\u2019t clear, so I got to looking over the place with a fine toothed comb. The room that had been stolen from was still open, but it was clear that whoever had broken into had actually had to break in. They\u2019d had no clue how to open the secret door, or else went to a fuckton of trouble to make it look that way, with at least 30 books tugged a little out from the shelf looking for the switch. Stein confirmed that as far as he knew, the professors who had access knew how to get to the door.<br /> <br /> Inside the room was nothing much. The books stolen were only the obvious ones, from a locked cabinet that they\u2019d apparently had the key to. They hadn\u2019t gone to any lengths to steal some and cover up the fact that those in particular were stolen. I was able to find shoe prints in there, some kind of smooth soled boot. No heels, but aside from that they were pretty generic. One thing was for sure though - they got Stein off the hook. His gunboats