<br /> <br /> I settled on Louise, just to keep tabs on what she was planning as far as Vivian and Naomi went. Her thoughts were focused on organizing her target ranking. Naomi was actually kinda low, since to Louise\u2019s estimation, she was \u2018just a slut\u2019. Vivian was a goddamn terrorist, so she ranked pretty high. She wasn\u2019t sure what Nikka was dealing, but her place on the chart was rising. The vampires were kinda up there, but interestingly, she knew they were vampires and so didn\u2019t know if they would count for her one bad person kill per month.<br /> <br /> The only deviation was her constant reminder to herself to stop checking Am out. She was mildly confused as to why she was so fucking obsessed with Am, but she was trying really hard to stay focused. And failing, quite frequently. It was starting to fluster her.<br /> <br /> I let the others know what I\u2019d found, including to Vivian via text. The hacker started looking into it, but found herself with pretty much the same goddamn question Louise had. The question of whether a vampire had a soul, or whether killing a dead thing counted for their fucking weird geas thing was up in the air, as far as Vivian knew. It wasn\u2019t really something the God-Machine frequently dealt with directly.<br /> <br /> Vivian\u2019s research was interrupted somewhat by Shelley swinging by. \u201cHey, how are you doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBetter now.\u201d Vivian smiled up at her.<br /> <br /> Shelley returned her smile. \u201cYou wanna crash over tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian leaned back. \u201cI would like that a lot. I wasn't sure if you were getting tired of me leaving a divot in the bed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, but it\u2019s not the same when you\u2019re not there.\u201d Shelley put a hand on the back of her chair. She looked around the room and sighed. \u201cThe place is full of college students tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot great tippers, I bet?\u201d Vivian grimaced.<br 