 They\u2019re calling her Nick.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know her, actually.\u201d Vivian smiled. \u201cThe cute guy apparently makes all the college kids fall for him somehow.\u201d She glanced up at Shelley. \u201cI know more things about what\u2019s going on on campus than I really should, don\u2019t I?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSuspiciously so.\u201d She smiled back down at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cKnowing things is what I do. It\u2019s the half I\u2019m good at.\u201d She glanced over at us. \u201cIt\u2019s a work thing, really. It\u2019s a hotbed for weird stuff, we keep getting clients over there that I have to dig into.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley looked a little worried. \u201cI have heard it\u2019s a good college though, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded goddamn quickly. \u201cYeah, it\u2019s got a great reputation as a college.\u201d She squeezed Shelley\u2019s hand. \u201cI don\u2019t mean to worry you. I\u2019m willing to bet you can\u2019t find a university that doesn\u2019t have weirdness going on. Where else can you hang around, hide your creepy books...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t have any creepy books...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s cause you\u2019re not an evil occultist.\u201d Vivian grinned. \u201cI could get you a creepy book though, if you wanted.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cAre there evil occultists there? Is there an evil occult class? Is it like Hogwarts?\u201d She looked thoughtful. \u201cThat would explain pink-haired girl.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian shrugged exaggeratedly. \u201cThere was an evil room. But I think that\u2019s all been taken care of.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright...\u201d Shelley glanced back to the back. \u201cWell, I\u2019ll be around. And will see you at closing time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDefinitely.\u201d Vivian smiled back at her. \u201cReal quick - you know anything about Lazer boy over there? At Shelley\u2019s fucking confused expression, Vivian pointed at Bobby.<br /> <br /> Shelley chuckled. \u201cOh, him. I think he tried drugs once, and no one was ever nice enough to explain it to him?\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian glanced down at her laptop. \u201cI\u2019ve read his story on the internet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBored were we? God, you could have called and talked to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know I keep track of all that kind of weirdness.\u201d Shelley made a begrudging gesture. \u201cThere\u2019s the sifting for the grain of truth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid he save us all?\u201d she asked goddamn sarcastically.<br /> <br /> Vivian spread her hands. \u201cI dunno if his story has that grain of truth or not, but I won\u2019t know if I don\u2019t read.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley made a face. \u201cIs it really in debate?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomething may have happened. Something he didn\u2019t remember properly. That wasn\u2019t just drugs. They are the most likely, but not the only possibility.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe possibility that he got taken up by aliens and saved us all in a starship battle?\u201d Shelley shook her head. \u201cI\u2019m thinking the mushrooms.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian chuckled. \u201cOf those two, mushrooms are more likely. But something weird might have happened, and the whole starfighting story is just his brain\u2019s way of processing it. You know, people don\u2019t always deal well with finding out about certain things. Like ghosts. They remember it differently.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley looked down. \u201cYeah, the ghost thing. Are you saying there actually was a for real ghost here that night?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes...\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley patted her on the shoulder. \u201cI gotta keep moving or I\u2019ll get yelled at.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian smiled. \u201cWe wouldn\u2019t want that.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> It was almost closing time when Naomi sent a text out to all of us. \u2018You guys need me for anything else? Cause I gotta do something involving these two lovely ladies here.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Not unless Nikka gets attacked.\u2019 Vivian shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u2018I can stay until she leaves. Poor Am will just have to hold out. I\u2019ll just tell her to smoke something, she\u2019ll be alright.\u2019<br /> <br /> I smirked. \u2018That\u2019ll give Louise more time to obsess over her.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Say what?\u2019 I grinned at Naomi, who was suddenly staring at me. She got up and walked over, making it so we couldn\u2019t be overheard. Penelope started making out with Am as soon as she left. Just before she got to our table, she turned back. \u201cHey!\u201d She sighed and stared at me. \u201cWhat\u2019s going on with Louise and Am?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe keeps getting distracted by her.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, time for us to go!\u201d She started to turn.<br /> <br /> I laughed. \u201cYou gonna deny the poor werecat?\u201d<br /> <br /> She upgraded to a glare. \u201cFuck yeah. Am is mine. Someone touches her they pull back a stump.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf it makes you feel better, she feels bad about being distracted by her.\u201d I took a sip of my sour.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t fucking care. She\u2019s mine,\u201d Naomi growled.<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cI had heard that. It\u2019s going around.\u201d<br /> <br /> She huffed. \u201cWell, I\u2019m gonna take her out of here.\u201d She stomped over. \u201cPenalope, I can\u2019t take you anywhere.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do not graze in Africa...\u201d Penelope began.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, you graze on my crotch. It\u2019s time to leave.\u201d Naomi pulled the two of them up.<br /> <br /> Louise watched them leave, closely, taking a fucking long drink of whatever she had in front of her.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t too long before Nikka headed out. Louise followed her, and I followed Louise, Alibi\u2019d Billy Mack in tow. When I got out to the parking lot, Louise appeared to be looking around for Nikka, having lost fucking track of her. When she turned back towards the bar, Nikka appeared in front of her. \u201cWhy are you watching me? Why are you following me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI... who are you?\u201d Louise took a step back.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou didn\u2019t even buy me a drink.\u201d Nikka crossed her goddamn arms.<br /> <br /> Louise frowned. \u201cI was looking at a lot of people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut you\u2019re following me. Why?\u201d Nikka countered. \u201cI\u2019m not interested in banter.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t have to explain myself to you.\u201d Louise straightened up. \u201cSo you back off.\u201d She moved away from Nikka. As she moved past me, I heard her mutter, \u201cAnd don\u2019t make me kill you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Nikka watched her go. I walked up behind her, careful to make noise so I didn\u2019t startle her. I leaned on a car beside her as she turned to notice me. \u201cHello gorgeous.\u201d She smiled at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s a werecat.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh.\u201d Nikka nodded. \u201cI had heard of them, but never met them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cApparently they have to kill someone, someone bad, every once in a while. Or they go fucking crazy.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack walked up to join us. \u201cYes. They are required to exterminate an evil person once every lunar cycle, or they suffer madness.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cInteresting.\u201d She looked back over at me. \u201cWill you be coming back with me, to make sure I am safe?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is what I\u2019m here for.\u201d I smirked at her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T15:10:49-07:00","id":998899,"title":"","content":"<br /> Jack was at the apartment building the next day at the crack of ten. Kyle was outside waiting in front of a freshly painted Sentra. \u201cHey! Sup?\u201d Kyle grinned over at him. \u201cLast night wasn\u2019t the best for the kid, but I have a feeling I\u2019m just saving up the luck for tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeaking of luck...\u201d Jack pulled out a contract. \u201cThis is how you\u2019re going to get paid. You sign this, go and buy a scratch off and it should more than cover it. Trust me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI...\u201d Kyle drew out the goddamn syllable way too fucking long. \u201c...can\u2019t really do that. I just met you. All I know is I handed you a sleeping child and never saw it again, and you have a rock that talks. And I need money or it\u2019s gonna break my legs through my anus. I\u2019m selling this *for* somebody.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes. \u201cJust sign the damn thing, go get your scratch off and its payout. You can give me the keys after you have the money from the scratch off.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kyle looked at him suspiciously. \u201cWhy don\u2019t you go buy the ticket, cash it, and give me the money?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt doesn\u2019t work that way.\u201d Jack sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m suspicious. I mean, I\u2019m pretty dumb, but...\u201d Kyle looked between him and the contract.<br /> <br /> Jack ran a hand over his face. \u201cLook, I\u2019m not asking where you got the car from. So pay me in kind and just roll with it. That\u2019s worth more than what you were asking.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd if the ticket doesn\u2019t win, you don\u2019t get the car?\u201d Kyle asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s the idea.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eventually, Jack talked Kyle into it, and the squirrelly fucker looked shocked when the ticket paid out exactly as much as the contract said it would. He traded the keys over to Jack after he counted the money, smiling broadly. \u201cEnjoy man! And wish me luck for tonight. Oh, and I\u2019m gonna go inside, so if a license plate goes missing, I won\u2019t know anything about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes and rummaged around for his forged temporary tag. \u201cThanks for this man. I hope your... business goes well.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cOh yeah. The trucks giveth, the trucks taketh away.\u201d Kyle waved jauntily at him as he wandered inside.<br /> <br /> <br /> Billy Mack made his own way up to the dam to visit his \u2018broodmother\u2019, driving the Crown Vic, since he couldn\u2019t just Dataform back with whatever poor fuck the cult had found for him.<br /> <br /> Ganora was waiting eagerly for him. Billy Mack smiled. \u201cIt has been far too long since I was able to visit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah...\u201d Ganora grinned toothily. \u201cAll\u2019s well here. Tsagogla\u2019lal\u2019s been watching.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is what she does, I understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack took the time to catch up with Ganora, then got to work fixing up the torture equipment. He got it set up in fairly short order and after a brief test run, had some time to spend with his fish lady.<br /> <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I made a quick fucking stop by my place to grab a shower and a change of clothes, and the grocery for flowers and wine, and made my way to Miranda\u2019s house. Maybe it was guilt. Maybe I just wanted to celebrate the new windfall. Thankfully, I\u2019m a Demon, so Miranda will have never have a reason to know it wasn\u2019t just the latter.<br /> <br /> She eyed me as I set the flowers down and moved in for a kiss. \u201cWhat\u2019s the occasion?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFinished a big case, with a hell of a payout. I thought I\u2019d treat you to a nice lunch?\u201d I grinned over at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI would love that.\u201d She put an arm around my waist. \u201cYou can tell me about your case.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lunch was nice and definitely a fucking cut above my usual. Not something I\u2019d feel comfortable making a habit of, but it was nice to get to treat her, guilt or no. I told her about the case - she already knew some of it, since we\u2019d consulted with her about Crumb\u2019s office. But I filled in the details for her. \u201cAnd as far as the bonus goes - the Undercity\u2019s a hell of a place. We\u2019ll see if we get around to it. We\u2019ve got a number of other cases in the works.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI don\u2019t know much about the Undercity myself. It was before my time, really.\u201d<br /> <br /> I waved that aside. \u201cNo worries, beautiful. Hell, they might even get around to it before we have a chance to, and I won't begrudge him, not after this payout. But I imagine the other irons in the fire are the crystal and the Tik Tok men?\u201d I raised an eyebrow at her. She nodded. \u201cHow\u2019s that going on your end?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Tik Tok men have backed off.\u201d I let out a relieved sigh and she smiled slightly at me. \u201cThe Free Council hasn\u2019t been breathing down my neck, so they probably have some other lead they\u2019re following.\u201d<br /> <br /> After lunch we went back to her place and sat our on the back porch drinking wine, talking and listening to Fido sing. I dunno what I ever had against days off. That was my first mostly sober one in a while, and it wasn\u2019t so bad. Maybe I was starting to settle down...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <b><b> &lt;2014W48-6T07:51-08:00&gt;</b></b><br /> <br /> Vivian and Shelly\u2019s first Thanksgiving together seems to have proven to be quite successful. I was rather curious at how eager she was to introduce Vivian to her parents and extended family given her prior lack of homosexual relationships but I feel I understand the situation more clearly now. I believe that while it is strange to her there is an element of impropriety to it that thrills her on some level now that she has decided that her feelings are not temporary. Moreso, she seemed to enjoy the scandal of it (admittedly mild, her family seemed overall more surprised than disapproving of Vivian\u2019s gender). She also seemed to enjoy the hints of jealousy and interest her cousins showed. It was easier to deal with without compromising Vivian\u2019s history than I anticipated, mostly thanks to Shelly's request to her to play up her \u2018bad girl\u2019 aspect a bit. Having that to focus on would have allowed her to keep her own tumultuous experiences with her own biological and foster families in check. I must confess, I enjoyed the exercise of exploring an unfamiliar social setting as Vivian. Not to mention that getting to flaunt her rebel girlfriend had clearly left Shelly in a rather adventurous mood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b> &lt;2014W48-6T011:57-08:00&gt;</b></b><br /> <br /> I am looking forward to examining the hospital where Madam X has established her lair once we\u2019ve assisted her in returning to her home dimension Sunday. While conferring with her about the details of our return foray to the Water Wheel I was able to learn a few details of her occupation of the former Infrastructure. Whatever the beast of darkness in the basement proves to be it was apparently there before she arrived and proved beyond her means to control or destroy. However, as it seems content to remain in its own environs she has been able to simply avoid it. I do regret that there will be no opportunity to have any sort of meaningful dialog with her before she escapes our reality. She seems like she would enjoy an exchange of ideas and there is much we could both learn for such. But this reality pains her and her presence is disruptive so delaying, even for a good cause, is not an option. Pity we did not come into contact with her sooner, it would have been fascinating to have been party to helping her develop the means to convert the Infrastructure to send her back. I do hope that I am able to observe closely at the Water Wheel. There are many aspects of the process I do not fully grasp yet and it will likely be my only opportunity to observe it in practice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b> &lt;2014W48-6T07:51-08:00&gt;</b></b><br /> <br /> This affair with the stolen books is going to prove complicated. Dr Stein has taken it upon himself to become involved but was apparently not familiar with the particular tomes at the heart of this matter. I wonder if his exclusion was simple oversight or by design. His abrasive demeanor could be a liability in matters of delicate secrecy while his straightforward moralistic focus would be contrary to anything that falls outside of those narrow views. Speed seems intent on fostering a closer rapport with him and her own sense of ethics does give them a common ground. For myself, I find him to be rational and believe that he could prove to be a very useful ally given our interest in keeping the campus intact for our own purposes. He could certainly prove to be a most inconvenient enemy so at the very least we want to remain on neutral terms with him.<br /> <br /> Dr Richardson, the wolf lycanthrope professor, was also taking an interest in the missing books. He was not forthcoming with what he knew about it to Dr Stein or his exact involvement.<br /> <br /> Our investigation of the site offered some useful items. First off, the area has apparently been re-purposed from on old Infrastructure. Above Special Collections is an extra-dimensional space where the command center of a Defense Network was located. It was attacked at some point in the past by a collection of assailants who were very familiar with what it was and very intent on destroying it. There is some minor potential for salvage at some point. More useful is the fact that it indicates that there are most likely three other sites remaining from the network which might include angel storage or repair facilities. At the very least, it seems logical they might be more intact as the assault seemed to be focused on taking out the lynchpin of the whole network.<br /> <br /> The thief wore boots of a nondescript sort.<br /> <br /> The thief had a key to the case itself, but was not familiar with the mechanism to open the secret chamber it was located in.<br /> <br /> There was an idol present, some manner of household god or spirit. It is unclear if it was being kept there for safety or as a measure of security. Most likely safekeeping as there was no evidence of it impeding the thief. Though it might be nothing more than a sentry, in which case it might be that Dr Richardson sought to find out what it had seen. Werewolves are closely tied to spirits.<br /> <br /> Given what we do know, it seems unlikely that the missing professor was involved. He would have known the Gear to open the hidden area and likely closed it behind himself to delay discovery.<br /> <br /> Our next course of action is to question a Dr Hazard on Monday when he should be on campus again. He should know something and might respond to a lighter touch as Speed put it. Dr Stein has agreed to wait for us to attempt to get answers from him before questioning Dr Richardson aggressively.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b> &lt;2014W48-7T01:22-08:00&gt;</b></b><br /> <br /> After the University we spent a few hours investigating the access points to the under-city in the vicinity of our offices for future reference before making our way to Kiki\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Quietus got Nikka\u2019s key to cover the contract he\u2019d drawn up\u2019s effects with the pretense of setting up a security system at her apartment. Apparently while he was out he checked in on Maverick\u2019s and found the Drak and Sleet have things in hand. Apparently he also ran across Kyle but managed to refrain from taking in another stray after Speed made it clear he\u2019d be the one cleaning up after him. For the best, he still hasn\u2019t found a home for the last stray he brought in and I don\u2019t have a second cage.<br /> <br /> I left an alibi of Billy Mack with the others for appearances while I switched to Vivian and settled in at a table in Shelly\u2019s section. She was openly affectionate and drifted by my table several times. We chatted lightly most of the evening and she asked Vivian if she wished to crash at her place again. When I pointed out how much I\u2019ve been over there lately she agreed but said it wasn\u2019t the same without me present. I was quite pleased to hear her say it. But in light of what followed, it has made an issue starkly clear to me.<br /> <br /> Bobby Heartwood was in the bar. Shelly is passingly familiar with Mr Heartwood but dismisses his adventures as a drug trip. I considered approaching him while the opportunity presented, but it seemed ill timed with Shelly being present.<br /> <br /> Also, the discussion of the mind altering effects of supernatural phenomena and how it might be that his tale is simply the best his mind can do to recall what really happened that we had a moment. Kiki\u2019s rampage came up. Shelly has processed the event and convinced herself there was no ghost. It was most sobering when she responded to my comments by patting me on the shoulder the way one does when humoring the eccentricities of one\u2019s lover.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, Vivian betrayed no signs of my internal reaction. But it has raised some very critical concerns and forced me to evaluate my recent behavior and take stock of my emotional motivations in this situation. In order to access this situation, I am going to have to revert to a less emotionally charged form and evaluate recent events carefully. I must determine what, if any, goals I am working toward here. I have allowed myself to become very attached and have lost perspective.<br /> <br /> Proceeding without a clear plan or objective is foolhardy and dangerous. Tomorrow I will be visiting Diablo Lake to finish setting up the suffering collector we took from the Water Wheel. I will have ample time to multi-process while working and consider this while not subject to the increased levels of emotional responses that come with being in cover.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><b> &lt;2014W48-7T05:19-08:00&gt;</b></b><br /> <br /> Shelly is sleeping.<br /> <br /> I have been sitting here far longer than required to see that she settled back to her slumber after the disruption of my waking and extracting myself from her embrace. I am watching her sleep. I find her entrancing\u2026 beautiful\u2026 <br /> <br /> I have become emotionally compromised.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LIV</i><br /> <br /> Dr. Frankenstein is Dr. Stein, and Dr. Talbot is Dr. Richardson. Naomi is a little shit. The \u201cGrazing\u201d comments make more sense if you read closely that Naomi pronounces Penelope as a sound alike for Antelope. Again, Naomi is a little shit.<br /> That bit about human skin and books is totally true, by the way. As is the existence of a Seattle underground.<br /> <br /> Richardson had previously been seen at the Roost. Just in case I had not mentioned it before, the Colony (Werecats) were introduced in War Against the Pure. I am terribly found of them.<br /> <br /> I love weird University shit. Next crossover game I run is gonna be set at a University I think with the PCs as students. But that will be awhile yet.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T17:10:52-07:00","id":998951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=998899#post998899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love weird University shit. Next crossover game I run is gonna be set at a University I think with the PCs as students. But that will be awhile yet.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything. Comments and Questions welcome</div> </div> </div> </div>Any thoughts on what game-line for the University game? Or would it be cross-over?<br /> <br /> And it looks like Kilroy might do something drastic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:27:30-08:00","id":999400,"title":"","content":"Crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-b