\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T13:28:51-08:00","id":1005456,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to Seattle. Bring your umbrella.<br /> <br /> This session was complicated to log. We spent a bit over 1/3 of the session discussing plans for the raid on the water wheel. Then backtracking some and discussing counterplans. These plans drifted out of character a great deal. Speed\u2019s player summarizes things well, but a lot of it is going to be handwaved, and the session seem a bit short for a Night Train session. We had a full session, just a LOT of OOC planning.<br /> <br /> Here goes<br /> <i><br /> Session LV</i><br /> <b><br /> Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Not everyone\u2019s Saturday afternoon was as restful. Billy Mack got done with his fucking fish lady friend and came back with a sacrificial victim in tow, to talk with Kayla about what she\u2019d seen.<br /> <br /> He met her at the office after dropping his victim off at a hotel room courtesy of goddamn petty cash. She looked at him seriously after he\u2019d sat down. \u201cSo, it\u2019s back online. Well, not all of it - a fair amount though. Security is higher - a lot higher. Probably cause it got hit so hard. I\u2019m a little worried.\u201d <br /> <br /> She described what she\u2019d seen: three similar looking angels, blond and beefy, two guarding the lynchpin and one patrolling around the place. There was a fourth angel, she was pretty sure - most kids didn\u2019t fucking hang out in water wheel offices or have glowing red eyes. She figured it was three Guardians and a Destroyer. \u201cAnd that\u2019s not counting any of them that were better at blending in - those four sure weren\u2019t. Or any in the basement. No water goes there, so I couldn\u2019t check it out safely.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe did remove the very tailored Guardian it had. Further reinforcement does make sense, until they feel confident things should die down.\u201d Billy Mack nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe they should?\u201d Kayla put forth. \u201cGoing at them again... it\u2019d be like declaring war. The God-Machine\u2019s not gonna just sit there. And with guards at the lynchpin - she needs 45 minutes, right? That\u2019s a long time to hold out. And you\u2019ll probably have a rough time even without backup.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack sighed. \u201cYou may have a point. I\u2019ll speak with the others.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> We all met up at Kiki\u2019s round-about the usual time for Nikka\u2019s \u2018shift\u2019. We were all there as our detective selves, so we could discuss our plans for Sunday. The place was pretty fucking busy. From the college student regiment, Adria, Louise and Callie were sitting together. Rosanna and Crusher seemed to be having a nice dinner together, if you like gyros. Nikka was there, of course, as well as an attractive black woman in a suit, the one Jack said was named Sondra Benoit, and possibly the one Roadrash told Jack had been talking with Zelda and Gina Sanderson. No one else familiar was among the crowd.<br /> <br /> Once Liz made it so we couldn\u2019t be overheard, I sat back with my sour in one hand. \u201cSo, I\u2019ve got a plan to buy us time. I don\u2019t have particular plans for Glen, but what if he became our fucker who cried wolf? I send him as the Third Man, with a goddamn bomb, to some Infrastructure we\u2019re not attacking. He yells about an attack, blows himself up, maybe with some sort of fucking chemical smell. The first few times it\u2019ll draw attention away from where we\u2019re hitting. And once they start reacting based on that pattern... boom! We hit wherever Glen did.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAbout that...\u201d Billy Mack let us know the shit Kayla had told him, including passing on her warning. \u201cEven if we can deal with the forces there, we will be in no shape to deal with reinforcements,\u201d he pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. Well, if Kayla\u2019s spooked... Glen might have to wait for another day. Though... what other options do we have?\u201d I looked around at the group. \u201cThink she\u2019ll give us an extension if we explain shit to her?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack grimaced. \u201cPerhaps? We might try a more remote facility - not the dam. That deals with the reinforcements problem, and they are likely to not be as prepared.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cThe God-Machine surely didn\u2019t increase security to that level everywhere.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf we did that, we could possibly even get away with it without notice, if we make sure the only traces left behind are hers.\u201d I tapped my fucking glass.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about the defense Infrastructure on campus?\u201d Jack asked.<br /> <br /> I shook my head. \u201cWe don\u2019t want the God-Machine looking into campus. Otherwise, we\u2019d have let them fuck with the Abyssal infestation.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot to mention the negative effects of the event itself,\u201d Billy Mack reminded us. \u201cAnd since it\u2019s abandoned... oh. Oh god.\u201d<br /> <br /> I leaned the hell away from him. \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled widely. \u201cThe Works. We could use the Works.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWithout setting it off?\u201d I asked, goddamn dubious.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere would be a risk. But with Kayla and Terry\u2019s help, we should be able to potentially stabilize it first.\u201d Billy Mack nodded fucking enthusiastically. \u201cThere are multiple pieces in there, we wouldn\u2019t even have to use the power generator we\u2019ve made contact with.\u201d He looked thoughtful. \u201cWhatever happened in there... the God-Machine most likely won\u2019t even look into it after Madame X shifts reality. It seems far more concerned with containment in there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. So tomorrow we meet with Madame X, let her know the difficulties, say we know where a bunch of Infrastructure is, let\u2019s go pick you out a good one?\u201d I glanced around the group again.<br /> <br /> Liz smiled at me. \u201cI\u2019ll have my best pout ready.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grinned over at her and blew my hair out of my eyes. When I glanced back out at the room, I just so happened to see Heroin walk in, Tar following along behind her. She headed straight for Benoit. I raised an eyebrow and nudged Liz with an elbow before putting on my fucking sunglasses. Billy Mack noticed where I was looking and made a goddamn considering noise. \u201cTracking microchips and weapons... that sounds like the kinda combination that leads to something messy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYep.\u201d Jack took a drink. \u201cHeroin is known as someone who gets things for people, and that you don\u2019t fuck with. She tends to leave \u2018overdoses\u2019 behind. She\u2019s the kinda big shot Sondra wants to be, though I think Sondra wants to be more of a fixer than a hireling.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tuned them out and focused on Benoit. She wasn\u2019t supernatural or particularly strongly connected to Heroin - this meeting, whatever it was, was all about getting her some green. And some clout, for that matter. She pretty clearly wanted to be higher up in the food chain of the criminal underworld in this city, and somehow Heroin played into it.<br /> <br /> I got more peeking in on her surface thoughts. All lot of them played on how hot Heroin was, especially after the Changeling leaned back, her arms stretched out behind her head over the back of the seat. But aside from that, Heroin had a reputation as a girl who could get her hands on anything, and what Benoit needed was some hyper-advanced computer chips. Not GPS ones, like Jack had overheard. Something more... God-Machiney. At least, it seemed to be connected to something that poor fuck Martin had been working on.<br /> <br /> I went digging into why she was after them, and got pretty much shit - some texts and emails from a gee going by \u2018Orange\u2019. I let the others know while I kept a close eye on Heroin messing with her unlit cigarette. \u201cMichael White, maybe? There\u2019s the color thing...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy money\u2019s on Valefor - Michael White seems to prefer to toy with people and make it clear but unprovable who they are dealing with.\u201d Billy Mack shrugged.<br /> <br /> I nodded, still focused on her thoughts. Heroin was playing it goddamn coy, trying to get her measure probably. Benoit was started to get aggravated, between that and Heroin\u2019s attention grabbing, but respected her reputation at least. I shook my head and smirked, turning back to the others. \u201cThere was something else you wanted to touch on Billy Mack?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe have determined that we are going to trying and do something to get the apprentices to go after Cornelius, yes?\u201d We all nodded. \u201cHas anyone come up with a course of action as far as how to go about that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI figured we\u2019d send Clytemnestra at her, and after she gets done with her impression of a cardboard recycling center, then the immortal\u2019d do whatever the hell she wanted.\u201d I smirked at Liz, who pouted at me.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack knit his brow. \u201cThe woman is married and has a daughter.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked over at Liz. \u201cThat make a difference?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll have you know, this is the least sexy way anyone has ever made me their whore. And no.\u201d Liz took a drag on her fucking cigarette.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo we really want a group of bloodthirsty Harvesters tied back to us?\u201d Billy Mack asked. <br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cProbably not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have a thought on this,\u201d Billy Mack looked between us and continued, \u201cif nothing else for information gathering before we approach too closely. Why don\u2019t you let me proceed on this?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s goddamn terrifying. Sure.\u201d I knocked my drink back.<br /> <br /> Jack gave him a look. \u201cWhat are you going to do, possess one and...\u201d<br /> <br /> I drowned him out, fingers in my goddamn ears. \u201cNuh-uh, I\u2019m not listening.\u201d Sure, it was childish. Sometimes the little fuckers are smart for their age.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe idea is that if the apprentices go after Cornelius, then mostly likely we will no longer have a band of murderous immortals and just have to deal with Cornelius, or maybe they get lucky and take care of him. Right?\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow. I put my hands up, disavowing all responsibility. \u201cAlright then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz sighed. \u201cNormally, you\u2019d think body-guarding an immortal would be an easy thing to do. Damn these very specific circumstances.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cIt is true. But without that specific set of circumstances, she\u2019d not have hired us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, yes, of course.\u201d Liz waved a hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere are far too many Harvesters here in the city, to be certain.\u201d Billy Mack shook his head. \u201cThis plan should take care of some of that however.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes and cracked his fucking knuckles before standing. \u201cI\u2019ll be right back.\u201d He walked over to the bar, and ordered another round for Rosanna and Crusher\u2019s table, sent with a note that read \u2018After dinner, I\u2019d like to speak with you.\u2019 Roadrash nodded and sent it over. \u201cAnything new on your end?\u201d he asked the bartender.<br /> <br /> \u201cNope.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood.\u201d Jack rapped the bar and came back to our table.<br /> <br /> Right about the time Heroin\u2019s business deal concluded successfully, from the looks of things, Crusher waved Jack over. \u201cHey man, have a seat. What can we do for you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack took the offered seat. \u201cI didn\u2019t want to interrupt dinner - thanks for seeing me.\u201d He smiled at the pair. \u201cThe thing I wanted to talk to 