Skeevy Larry as best I could. At one point Langley glanced back at me, but didn\u2019t say anything.<br /> <br /> Eventually Skeevy Larry stopped at a pair of double doors that led down into the Undercity. He laid his hands on them, and they warped and moved enough so that the two of them could jump in. I elected not to follow, cause I\u2019m not a fucking idiot, and texted Miranda back. \u2018I\u2019m OK. Leaving the situation. See you after work tonight?\u2019<br /> <br /> I texted Gone with the address of the door, letting him know Skeevy Larry had just gone through, and started making my way back to Kiki\u2019s.<br /> <br /> <br /> When I got back to Kiki\u2019s, Heroin was sitting in Liz\u2019s lap. She noticed me right the hell off, and patted the seat beside her, a cocky look in her eyes. I gave her a smile, but made a stop by the bar first, ordering two whiskey sours. Jack looked me over as I waited for them. \u201cYou doing OK?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSkeevy Larry just brought the entire contents of a goddamn electronics shop come to life and attack a vampire-slash-ghoul party. Then he got electrocuted and it made him... happy. And I really don\u2019t want to see a pair of machetes crawl along the ground like snakes and bite people again with their toothy maws, ever.\u201d I tossed the first sour back.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight.\u201d Jack took a sip of his own drink.<br /> <br /> I saluted him and moved back to the table. Once I\u2019d sat down, Heroin moved so she was sitting on my lap, but her legs were across Liz\u2019s lap. \u201cHave fun?\u201d<br /> <br /> I snorted. \u201cActually, no. If I never did that again, I\u2019d be A-OK. Just fucking peachy\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve had an experience or two I\u2019ve felt like that.\u201d She managed to smirk sympathetically, somehow.<br /> <br /> Jack eyed our table, smirking at his fellow barflies. \u201cHow often do you get to see something like this? Cause I don\u2019t get to see it often enough.\u201d<br /> <br /> Roadrash snorted. \u201cYou\u2019d be surprised. You should see that pink haired girl\u2019s crowd.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, no.\u201d Jack made a face. \u201cYou see, she might look nice, but then she talks.\u201d He glanced at Roadrash\u2019s fucking dubious face. \u201cShe\u2019s not nice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cObviously she talks nice to some people.\u201d The bartender shrugged.<br /> <br /> Jack shrugged. \u201cNot to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Roadrash got someone a drink, then got back to Jack. \u201cBecause you\u2019re a guy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA little bit of that. Also, I\u2019m apparently terribly old.\u201d Jack took another sip.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s always been perfectly polite to me.\u201d Roadrash shrugged.<br /> <br /> Jack looked over at Tar. \u201cWhat about you? You see shit like this very often?\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded. \u201cI\u2019m with her.\u201d He indicated Heroin.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh.\u201d Jack grinned at him. \u201cWell then, you\u2019re already a step up on most of us, aren\u2019t ya?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tar frowned, thinking hard. After much deliberation, he nodded. \u201cYeah.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack chuckled. \u201cObviously I need to pay more attention to where you are, so I get a view like this more often.\u201d<br /> <br /> A bit before closing, Nikka sent me a text. \u2018I was planning on leaving soon. Do you need more time?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Nah, doll. It\u2019s your timetable. There\u2019ll be other nights.\u2019<br /> <br /> She smirked at me. \u2018You seem to be having fun though.\u2019<br /> <br /> Heroin leaned back to look at me. \u201cI figure the two traits of a perfect girl are that she can tie knots like she was in girl guides, and finger like she was in reform school.\u201d I smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cAh reform school. That place you send troublemakers to, so that they don\u2019t distract the other students from being brainwashed.\u201d Billy Mack looked goddamn thoughtful. \u201cOf course, it\u2019s allegedly to straighten them out, but really, it\u2019s to keep them from being distracting.\u201d<br /> <br /> Nikka got up to go not too long after that, and I smiled apologetically at Heroin as I shifted her off my lap. \u201cSorry, doll, work calls.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cSee you Monday?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDefinitely.\u201d I smiled at her.<br /> <br /> I followed Nikka out and home, making sure she got there alright. After we pulled up at her place, I got out and leaned against my car. \u201cThat other business might have fall out. I\u2019ll see you to the door, make sure you\u2019re safe inside?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled. \u201cAlright. I had a wonderful time last night. If I don\u2019t sleep alone once and awhile, I will no longer be accustomed to it.\u201d She gave me a kiss at the door.<br /> <br /> <br /> After Heroin kissed Liz and sauntered off to the bar to collect Tar, Liz sighed and turned to Billy Mack. \u201cI think I\u2019m going to turn into Naomi tonight.\u201d She stretched. \u201cIt\u2019s been a productive evening, don\u2019t you think?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed.\u201d Billy Mack nodded. \u201cHave a good night, and I will see you in the morning.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh right, the morning.\u201d Liz shuddered.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled.\u201dYes, 11, at the water wheel to meet Madame X.\u201d<br /> <br /> She let out a long-suffering sigh. \u201cI know.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Kilroy\u2019s Transmissions</b><br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W48-7T15:57-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> It has been some time since I spent so much time outside of a cover. I warned Shelly this morning that I would be off the grid for the better part of the day since the cell phone reception in the subterranean and submerged caverns of Diablo Lake is often spotty at best. Despite the shock of my revelation I remained calm and in cover. I am confident she is unaware of the torrent of jumbled and conflicted thoughts that I was experiencing. It was not until I arrived and shifted that I was finally able to quiet my mind fully.<br /> <br /> I spent the day with Ganora. She spoke to me of how the cult has grown while I worked on the suffering collector. It is not a vast supply of Aether but with loyal cultists willing to endure for their high priestess my darling\u2019s people will not be completely dependent on the Diablo Dam Infrastructure and Miss Crimson. She was quite pleased with the results once it was fully operational. The hungry gleam in her dark eyes as the first trickles of Aether were coaxed from one of her human cultists and she tasted it was positively radiant. The vigor with which she displayed her appreciation at my gift once we were alone was\u2026 intense. We visited the spawning chambers and I gazed at the egg that will hatch into my child. She leaned lazily into my gentle caresses as we stood there and murmured of how strong our spawnling would be and how she hoped to bear many such powerful children. <br /> <br /> I felt a deep sense of contentment standing there basking in languid post-coital bliss with my beautiful ichthyoid queen. I felt a temptation to simply remain there. To join and aid Ganora and her people. To watch over my offspring and guide them. But I know that I would grow bored without an influx of new things. I have obligations to the Agency. I would miss Shelly.<br /> <br /> I believe on some level it is the simplicity of such a life that appeals. I care about Ganora and I believe that she likewise has feelings for me but it is much more straightforward than my relationship with Shelly. I have not spoken to Ganora of her, but only because it is of no consequence to her. It would neither upset her nor be troubling for her to understand. But the same does not hold true for the reverse of that. I cannot fathom exactly how deeply it would disturb Shelly to know how I spent the morning. And yet, as complicated and as inconvenient as maintaining such an elaborate facade is, I am loathe to discontinue it. I want her. I can see that at some point I have allowed myself to not simply play the part but have actually grown emotionally dependent on her presence. Indeed, it seems I have fallen in love. It is a most troublesome development. I am bothered that there is so much that Shelly does not know about me. She knows only one shadow of my being, one of the states that I exist in. She knows nothing of what I truly am or what I deal with on a daily basis. <br /> <br /> Simply put, I love her while she does not even know me.<br /> <br /> It is an untenable situation. Logic dictates that I should step back and re-assess my involvement. I furthered this out of a desire to rewrite the tragic end of Vivian\u2019s life. An emotional and sentimental goal at best. I have since allowed myself to become overly attached to Shelly. She is a weakness that could be leveraged against me. It is a drain on my time and energy to maintain the elaborate deception required to spend so much time with her without revealing the extent of what I and the Agency actually do. The risks and costs of continuing this relationship greatly outweigh the rewards. At least, they do by cold logic. And despite that, I know that I am going to text her when I get back to Seattle. I am looking forward to it. <br /> <br /> Clearly the most reasonable and efficient solution is not an option. I am going to continue to see her despite it not being in the best interests of either of us. It may be an emotional rather than logical choice, but so be it. While I certainly do not indulge in them to the same extent as my fellows, I am not so foolish as to attempt to claim that I am above such things.<br /> <br /> If I were, I would never have fallen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W48-7T16:48-08:00&gt;<br /> </b><br /> Kayla\u2019s assessment of the Water Wheel is troublesome. While it is, indeed, back on line sufficiently to serve Madam X\u2019s needs the increased levels of security that were visible during her reconnaissance are both formidable and indicative of a very high level of response being available. I must discuss this with the others but I fear our likelihood of success is too low to move forward. A smaller and more remote Infrastructure would be an ideal alternative but sadly, we do not know of one and our time-frame is not such to allow us the luxury of hunting for one.<br /> <br /> Speed has already made it abundantly clear the hospital is not allowed. The collateral damage would be an issue even if it were not of such personal import to her. <br /> <br /> I expect the others will agree with Kayla that the Water Wheel is too well secured. Hopefully we will come to a reasonable alternative plan before we meet Madam X tomorrow morning and she will be agreeable to it. And should she prove uncooperative, we will be able to face her without the resources of the Hospital at her beck and call. I do hope she does not force us to destroy her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>&lt;2014W49-1T00:54-08:00&gt;</b><br /> <br /> The evening at Kiki\u2019s has proven informative and productive. As it is Saturday, we were here to watch over Nikka and on that front there were no threats or developments.<br /> <br /> As is often the case, there was a certain amount of clandestine business being conducted. Of note was a meeting between Heroin (with her muscle Tar) and one Sondra Benoit. Miss Benoit is a low level figure in the local underworld who seems intent on moving up the food chain. Quietus had previously seen her speaking to Dmitri about acquiring GPS tracking microchips. But her meeting with Heroin was not about the Changeling\u2019s weapon dealing. She was negotiating a job, the theft of some very high end electronics she was not entirely sure about the purpose of. It touches on one of the numerous companies Mr Martin deals with and she is working to acquire the chips for an individual known to her only as Orange. There was some speculation that it was either Valefor or White but it is only conjecture. Still, it seems a matter worth looking into. One of us should call Mr Martin and see what he knows tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Once her business with Miss Benoit was complete Heroin sauntered over to spend the rest of the evening at our table since she recognized Speed. The banter and flirting between her and Speed and Clytemnestra was entertaining. <br /> <br /> Crusher and Rosanna were there having a quiet dinner and Jack had stepped over to speak to them before Haroin joined us. They warned him about her, much the same we\u2019ve heard from other sources. Her abilities seem quite deadly and she\u2019s apparently not shy about using them if she has been threatened and crossed. We shall need to be mindful of her. And if Crusher\u2019s capabilities are an indication of Tar\u2019s the man is not to be discounted either. While he was speaking to them, he made arrangements for us to meet them sometime after Mass tomorrow to renew the enchantment that allows us to see through Faire glamour. <br /> <br /> And finally, we discovered that Langley Fitzgerald is acquainted with Skeevy Larry, as well as learning more about our alligator murderer himself. The pair arrived together and sat down to share a meal. I called Langley and we met in the men\u2019s room to talk. I warned him that the Free Council was seeking his friend and he shared what he knew of the other man. Skeevy Larry is a Promethean though he is aligned with the destructive and chaotic power of Flux which makes him a very dangerous foe as well as something of a threat to anyone around him. Langley promised to be careful as we parted ways and gave me a peck on the cheek. As we were alone and he had let his usual flamboyant demeanor slide I believe it was a gesture of actual friendship. I am fond of the man myself, I do hope his association with Skeevy Larry does not bring him to misfortune. <br /> <br /> Speed tailed the pair when they left, hoping to be able to give Mr Gone something to go on as far as tracking down his quarry and also considering how to warn him as to what the man is without revealing ourselves. As it turned out, this was easy. Langley and Larry went to an electronics store which was the lair of a vampire and several ghouls and attacked it after dinner. Rather to Speed\u2019s displeasure, Larry was quite blatant with his powers and so she was able to convey the warning aptly by simply describing his actions. Mr Gone was apparently engaged, most likely with the Tik-Tok Men, and advised Speed to withdraw. She did not, but did remain safely concealed and out of the fighting so that she could track them to the Undercity entrance they used and report that as well. She did not follow them into the Undercity. Given Mr Gone\u2019s inability to respond promptly Langley seems safe for now and hopefully he will heed my warning and avoid Skeevy Larry until the matter blows over.<br /> <br /> The evening has drawn to a close. Speed is escorting Nikka home. I do not know if she intends to engage the Immortal is sex or return to her girlfriend. Plans have been set to meet tomorrow morning near the Water Wheel where we will hopefully convince Madam X to delay long enough for us to find her a suitable Infrastructure in the Works. <br /> <br /> As we had decided that our intention is to try to turn the Harvesters against Cornelius I am going to make my way to the home of his apprentice. Possession should allow me to get close to gather intelligence on her and if the opportunity is suitable to motivate her to target her presumably former master. The others, particularly Speed, were less than pleased with the tone my approach will most likely take but did agree that it has the best chance to further our goals. Obviously, I shall not know for certain until I have had a chance to investigate further but leveraging her daughter seems very likely to be the key.<br /> <br /> But first I must call my girlfriend and tell her goodnight. <br /> <br /> <i>End Session LV</i><br /> <br /> So the last part of the session, over 1/3, was an OOC discussion. It\u2019s been summarized IC, and summarized well, but it is part of why the session seemed confined to a single evening. The conversation did involve me stepping into Author stance to say that, well, there were more angels than it appeared, and the structure was very ready for a team of Primum six Demons to raid it, and they should expect casualties unless extremely careful.<br /> <br /> The Third Man is Speed\u2019s Third Cipher power, the one that allows her Alibi to be killed and, as long as the body can fall out of sight, not have any negative repercussions on her Cover.<br /> <br /> Skeevy Larry is not a healthy individual, in Promethian terms. He is a Centimani, part of the Refinement of Flux. And he is, obviously, powerful, even as Centimani go. He is outwardly mostly human, but then the only thing they ever really saw uncovered was his head.<br /> <br /> The original quote was \u201cThe perfect girl can tie knots like she was in Girl Guides, and finger like she was in reform school,\u201d as Speed posted. I translated it (as the game is set in the US) to Girl Scouts, but I was told Girl Scouts don\u2019t learn to tie knots. You have failed me for the last time, Girl Scouts of America. So Speed\u2019s player swapped it back so the line would make more sense.<br /> <br /> I think that is the only unusual thing. But if you have comments and questions they are welcome. <br /> <br /> As a note, changes in the USA have me deeply concerned. I am not just up and fleeing my home, but quite honestly I have to be prepared to leave if things become dangerous. What this means for you is I might abruptly and without warning, and these campaigns end. I don\u2019t want that to happen, but I also want to live. So there you go. Sorry. Be good to yourselves, and nice to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T01:52:40-08:00","id":1011413,"title":"","content":"You guys ready for a dungeon crawl? Because we have a dungeon crawl. Two, technically, but one is pretty short.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> After he left Kiki\u2019s, Billy Mack drove towards the Sandoval\u2019s house. He had a plan to point the apprentice Harvester at her master, Mr. Not-a-Goddamn-Farmer, but first he wanted to get some eyes on the situation.<br /> <br /> When he got there, the SUV Cornelius had pilfered wasn\u2019t in the driveway, though a pair of sedans were. The place was dark and quiet, as you\u2019d fucking expect for a nice quiet suburban house at 3 o\u2019clock in the fucking morning. Billy Mack took a look up and down the street, then transformed into Kilroy. He phased through the wall into the house, moving slowly and quietly.<br /> <br /> He gave the house a cursory once-over, for starters. He didn\u2019t get eyes on the kid\u2019s room quite yet, since the door was shut and locked. He was able to look in on the master bedroom, and saw that the dame wasn\u2019t home. Her husband was there, asleep, but she wasn\u2019t anywhere to be found.<br /> <br /> Even more bothersome was how thick the fucking general atmosphere was. He realized after a moment that it wasn\u2019t anything physical, that he wasn\u2019t having a hard time breathing, but it was just that something was off. He started moving shit around to figure out the cause and was able to discover some kind of warding ritual. It was aimed at spirits and things that used Essence, both making it more expensive to do anything and making it chancy that anything would happen at all, but it was unfocused enough that it interfered with our Aether expenditure too. It made sense if she was going toe to toe with a Purified, apparently. It was advanced work, some kind of hedge magic - the fucking g-man was impressed - with some weird shit for materials that he was pretty sure were from Whacko Bob\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Since he\u2019d gotten eyes on the place and so could check it out with clairvoyance at anytime he wanted, combined with the fact his mark wasn\u2019t there, he headed back out and crashed in his RV until our meet up the next morning.<br /> <br /> <br /> We met up with Madame X a ways away from the water wheel bright and eleven o\u2019clocky Sunday morning. Liz did in fact have on her best pout and wasted no time launching into her spiel about why this place was unsuitable and the Works was a far better idea. Madame X, blood dripping from the bag she had slung over her shoulder, was convinced. Especially when we pointed out we were going to go right now, that this wasn\u2019t some delaying tactic. After all, she\u2019d brought her goddamn bag of viscera and everything.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack volunteered to be the one driving her, since we\u2019d all driven in separately. I sure as hell wasn\u2019t looking forward to having gut juice draining on my nice interior. Jack didn\u2019t look thrilled either, and she wasn\u2019t going in the Maserati. The spirit accepted the g-man\u2019s offer and we were off to the Works.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t encounter any trouble going in. At the shack, I paused for a minute or two outside - the symbol to Tsagogla\u2019lal that we\u2019d seen last time was still there, in the exact same position. Ordinarily, not so weird, but as a sketch in the sand - fucking strange. I smudged a small portion out with my toe and looked around sharply. After a couple of minutes, when nothing happened, I shrugged sheepishly at the rest of them and redrew the picture. \u201cNot sure what the hell I expected there...\u201d<br /> <br /> Inside the tunnel, pre-cave in, there was a strong smell of wet dog, but that faded as soon as we got past the webbed up blockage. There were a lot less condoms and beer bottles in the tunnel than last time, so either the demographic shifted a bit from horny students to dog walkers, or someone had started keeping a closer eye on things, and brought dogs, or Terry\u2019s goddamn cultists with their human eyed dogs were messing around in the area. Or a pack of wild dogs found shelter there from the rain. That last one seemed unlikely, considering the trap door blocking off the tunnel.<br /> <br /> Before we moved past the blockage, we all shifted into Demon form. I returned to my tough compact tunneling machine form - it had better fighting capabilities, and we were moving through a kinda tight space. Even so, Quietus spread his wings out as far as he could when he got them out, blocking the weak light coming in from the shack. I glared at him. \u201cFuckhead, would you cut that out? I like being able to see.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s the problem?\u201d He stared at me with glowing green eyes. I popped up a mechanical arm to flip him off.<br /> <br /> Inside the machinery sounds still dominated, overlapping with the sounds of heavy breathing. Clytemnestra offered to scout, since she could crawl around as a group of spiders. It meant a weird perspective as far as what was around, but also that it was almost fucking impossible for her to be seen. Best of all, if she left a few spiders with us, then even if she did get caught and stomped, she\u2019d be fine and with us in an instant. Madame X watched her transform, a fascinated expression on her face.<br /> <br /> She was back before we got worried. We were hoping for a way up to ground level, so we could find another piece of Infrastructure and not deal with the goddamn rocket scorpions so she\u2019d stopped before leveling this floor. \u201cSo we have some options. There is an elevator, that appears to have power, though I didn\u2019t check. It had lights on - come to think of it, it was strange looking, but I\u2019m pretty sure it was an elevator. There were also artificially made earthen tunnels and some stairs.\u201d She frowned. \u201cI couldn\u2019t locate the source of the breathing. I could hear it everywhere I went, but it\u2019s hard to tell details like direction when I\u2019m a bunch of spiders. It\u2019s not on the route to the ways out at least.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow many tunnels?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cTwo. One goes a very short way before it opens up into the interior of an adjacent structure through a hole that was gnawed, or maybe cut, into the wall. Something over there smelled like wet leaves. A whole pile of them. There was no breathing sound, so that was an improvement. I didn\u2019t check the second one.\u201d She looked between all of us.<br /> <br /> I thought for a moment. \u201cAn adjacent structure might be good...\u201d<br /> <br /> Kilroy nodded. \u201cIt seems likely to get us to another Infrastructure quickly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd avoid being out in the fucking open,\u201d I pointed out. \u201cOtherwise, I\u2019d prefer stairs over elevator.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed,\u201d Kilroy agreed, \u201cthe elevator certainly bears investigation but right now finding a suitable Infrastructure is our primary objective. Let us check the tunnel you scouted out a bit, cautiously.\u201d<br /> <br /> We all moved together carefully, and each of us managed to avoid the infrared sweep of the patrolling robot. Once we got to the tunnels and out of its pattern, Clytemnestra pointed down. \u201cThe breathing is coming from below us.\u201d She smirked slightly. \u201cIt\u2019s much easier to tell, not being a tiny spider.\u201d<br /> <br /> Both tunnels were near the staircase, which looked partially collapsed. Quietus stuck his head in to see how bad it was, and found that the collapsing had only blocked off the way down and that the way up was clear. We stashed that away for later use and headed into the tunnel Clytemnestra indicated.<br /> <br /> I went in first, since I was one of the stealthiest of us, and had my Resistors to take any sort of trap I managed to spring. It felt fucking anticlimactic when nothing happened as I crawled out of the other end and waited there completely still as the others came through as well. Not that it was relaxing or anything - the lights were out except for those high, dim red emergency lights. Not a thing for putting a gee at ease. The slight hum of machinery, oddly, did help.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra collapsed into spiders to make her way through the tunnel more comfortably, and stayed that way to scout out the building. After a couple of minutes, we heard a high pitched \u2018whoosh\u2019 sound, like some kind of goddamn energy weapon being fired, from some distance away. After it, we heard a sound like a herd of car-sized slugs moving around. There was a pause, and another whooshing noise, and then a cluster of spiders came running into view. Clytemnestra reformed and shut the door behind her.<br /> <br /> She took a deep breath. \u201cOK. There is Infrastructure here, and a pair of Angels guarding it. One of them has some kind of energy weapon and the other is covered in saws. There\u2019s also some sort of big, black critters moving around. They seem to be avoiding the Angels, but I don\u2019t know what their deal is. They kinda... reflect light, so they look like light reflecting off an oil slick. It didn\u2019t look like anything had been in that room for a long time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t think the God-Machine had much presence here.\u201d I looked around the group and shrugged. \u201cOur goddamn bad luck. We wanna try the other tunnel?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps they\u2019re still here,\u201d Kilroy pointed out. \u201cA possibility that does make me want to tangle with them less, honestly.\u201d<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra nodded. \u201cI don\u2019t think the linchpin was in there, but I didn\u2019t get a good look.\u201d She frowned cutely. \u201cThose big lugs are pretty good at spotting things. We could skip that room - I just went there because I could tell Infrastructure was there. I could head back out when things calm down.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kilroy shook his head. \u201cLet\u2019s try the other tunnel for now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe should only press our luck when we have to,\u201d Quietus agreed.<br /> <br /> I led the way again down the tunnel, preemptively dreading the hazy red light I could see at the end of it. It was better than the damn emergency lights in the sense that the room at the other end was fully illuminated, at least. That was fucking outweighed by the heavy fog in the room and the fact I couldn\u2019t even fucking see where the light was coming from. Not to mention the sounds of more than two somethings running towards the room on four legs.<br /> <br /> As they got closer, the shapes in the fog formed into three large dogs with horns and glowing yellow-orange eyes. They were making a beeline for the three of us Demons who weren\u2019t a mass of spiders, probably off of scent, since we were all invisible. I didn\u2019t fucking bother to stop to ask though.<br /> <br /> They moved faster than we did, and were on us before any of us could draw a bead on them. Quietus managed to dodge out of the way of his, but Kilroy and I were hit hard, and pinned to the ground by the goddamn heavy dog bodies. Despite all that, we weren\u2019t really hurt. To be fair, my resistors shattered, so I could only do that trick once, but Kilroy\u2019s armor plates were more than a match for the dogs\u2019 teeth no matter how many times they tried it.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra had my back though, and quickly webbed up the dog on me. I still had to struggle my way from under it, but it wasn\u2019t doing anything of the fighting back it looked goddamn capable of. Quietus ignored the dog dancing in front of him in favor of shooting the one on Kilroy, since I seemed alright. His lead thrower bucked hard and the pill hit with way more force than I was expecting. Even after the hit, Kilroy was still stuck under his dog, and didn\u2019t look like he was trying very hard to throw it off, so I figured he\u2019d pulled his new trick and bumped up inertia in the area.<br /> <br /> The dogs - who were apparently Infernal-type little-d demons - were loud and obnoxious. The claws scrabbled noisily (but at least normally) on the hard floor and they snarled, howled and growled up a goddamn storm, their vocal noises echoing oddly. It was loud enough I almost missed Quietus\u2019 derisive cursing. I did catch him fucking off though, turning around and heading back through the tunnel. Then I was distracted by the sight of the dog that had been pinning Kilroy flying towards Clytemnestra, only to have her vanish into a cluster of spiders.<br /> <br /> The other dog had been looking like it wanted to follow its buddy, but didn\u2019t feel like snapping at spiders, so he charged Kilroy. The poor Guardian was pinned again. Even so, when I got a moment to fire again, I aimed carefully at the same one Quietus had, hoping to finish one of the fuckers off. I did so with goddamn fireworks, as far as that bastard was concerned. Kilroy had his own shit in hand though. He still wasn\u2019t trying to throw it off, recognizing it that it was rube\u2019s game for him to go up against a big beefy demon dog mano-a-mano, but he did manage to tweak reality so that the dog tripped over his own four feet and lost his grip on the Guardian.<br /> <br /> Things started getting a little hairy when Clytemnestra buggered off out the tunnel. I was just starting to realize that the motherfucker webbed to the wall had some kind of mind-altering powers shooting from his glowing eyes. I mean, either that, or I have even shittier friends than I thought. I mean, Quietus might have heard something outside - I would have hoped he\u2019d give a heads-up if that were the case, but what can you do? But after two of the motherfuckers just fucked the hell off... something was fishy, and the demon dog watching us from underneath a pile of webbing seemed like a good target. So I shot the shit out of it. It was looking bad after the rivet plowed through it, but it was still glaring at me. I felt something prick along the back of my neck, and man did I want a drink all of a sudden, but my mental resistance chip flared and I glared right back at it.<br /> <br /> When I glanced back at him, I saw Kilroy finally managed to throw the dog off himself, using the momentum of the dog\u2019s last lunge against it. Unfortunately the dog turned right the fuck back around and jumped on me. I didn\u2019t have any of Kilroy\u2019s tricks up my sleeve, so I just got mauled. I bolstered my thick steel skin with Aether to take the hit, and still just barely managed to stay conscious. While I did so, Kilroy finished off the webbed up dog.<br /> <br /> I could tell the dog was planning on fucking off after that, being alone and without much of an upper hand on anyone who wasn\u2019t me. Especially after Kilroy shot the fuck out of him. I wasn\u2019t particularly inclined to let him just fuck off, not after all that, so I burst into flames, swapping out my Aura Sight eye modules for a fire aura generator. The fire swept over him without affecting him, unshockingly once Kilroy let us know what they were, and the thing got the hell away, disappearing into the fog.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you think there\u2019s more?\u201d I looked tiredly at Kilroy.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not sure,\u201d he replied.<br /> <br /> I was a bit distracted however. When I\u2019d glanced down the tunnel, I caught sight of Clytemnestra sitting there at the end, snorting a line of cocaine. \u201cYou! Motherfucker, at least come do that shit over here. And turn your goddamn Halo on.\u201d<br /> <br /> She made her way slowly over. \u201cAlright. You should go into human form so I can snort it off your ass.\u201d She smirked at me. \u201cOr your tits.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can do that too.\u201d She smiled hazily. 