r /> \u201cLet\u2019s try door number 3,\u201d Kilroy agreed.<br /> <br /> The first landing was the level the rocket scorpions were one, so we skipped that one. The next floor up seemed promising, vibrating with a sound of steady mechanical humming. The metal door leading in was locked with a top of the line for the 80s-style electronic keypad. Kilroy took point, tweaking reality to know the password and got us inside.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra had finally stopped coming on to me by the time we got there, and while we waited for him to get us in, she turned to me, still fucking vibrating slightly. \u201cDo you think Symphonic Metal did that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA fuckton of cocaine?\u201d I tilted my head at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo! The Infernal incursion...\u201d<br /> <br /> I spun my wheels. \u201cAh, fuck, I don\u2019t know. Releasing hell onto the God-Machine\u2019s largest Infrastructure hub in Seattle does sound pretty goddamn metal though.\u201d<br /> <br /> She stuck to it though. \u201cThey released some kind of weapon down here and none of them survived it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt does seem to carry a certain degree of irony,\u201d Kilroy pointed out, joining us after propping the door open.<br /> <br /> \u201cFucking irony.\u201d One of Clytemnestra\u2019s legs jiggled for a moment before she jerked her head around to look at me. \u201cI don\u2019t like them anymore.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIrony?\u201d I smirked inwardly.<br /> <br /> She shook her head quickly. \u201cNo Symphonic Metal.\u201d She glanced at the door. \u201cSomeone else should go in there I\u2019m glowing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kilroy nodded. \u201cI can. I can download enough stealth ability to suffice, even though they will not measure up to you two,\u201d he nodded at me and Quietus, \u201cbut I am the more sturdy, now that your resistors have been broken.\u201d<br /> <br /> He found a hall lined with doors and proceeded fucking carefully down it, peering in through the window of each, since they were locked. The first he found held a stash of late 80s-early 90s bleeding edge tech mainframes. The next few were offices. Those were the major find, since they had windows on the outside wall, showing that we had finally found the goddamn ground floor. The other rooms seemed to be server rooms, their contents still humming away.<br /> <br /> When he reached the end of the hallway and peeked around the corner, he saw one of the scout robots we\u2019d evaded two floors down. He didn\u2019t push on past it, just returning to where we were. As he shut the door behind him, he heard the robot run right up to the door then turn around and move away again.<br /> <br /> We decided to hop the window and try for another building, avoiding the one with hellpuppies in its basement. I tweaked things so that we found one of the offices unlocked and we made our way out.<br /> <br /> We looked around to get our bearings to make sure we didn\u2019t double back to either the Angels of the fucking Infernal building. I found the Angel\u2019s building pretty easily, and there was no question as to which was the Infernal building. The center of the Works was sunken in, from the looks of it by the force of a goddamn large explosion. Coming out of the pit was a building that looked, in places, like the rest of the buildings around the pit. The other parts made up a large tower made of basalt. The windows in those bits were lit with a flickering red light, and the shadows looked like they were fucking smiling. From the outside, we\u2019d seen no such tower, especially not one that shot up into the clouds like this one, its ziggurat top barely visible.<br /> <br /> From the looks of it, Symphonic Metal\u2019s secret weapon had been to summon a tower out of Inferno through the center of this place. The gate it had been summoned through was still fucking active, though it looked like the tower itself was blocking it somewhat. Quietus shook his head. \u201cSo that\u2019s what Symphonic Metal did. I\u2019m glad they\u2019re not around. I\u2019d shoot them myself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is fairly metal however.\u201d Kilroy nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure is. Let\u2019s go that way.\u201d I pointed in the opposite direction.<br /> <br /> Quietus looked around at the scorch marks all over the place. \u201cWe might need to fix that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr we could go that way.\u201d I started making scootching movements away from the tower.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don't mean today!\u201d He glared at me.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cMe either. Let\u2019s go that way and just not fucking stop. The rocket scorpion building is a nice building. We can keep that.\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed and we headed off. Between us, we pinpointed two buildings that looked like they might have Infrastructure. One seemed to be a sort of standard two-story building, the same dull gray green that most everything not made of basalt was. The other one was half covered in skin that itself was covered in sores infested by pigeon sized humanoid flies. Guess which ones of the fuckers we went to?<br /> <br /> Quietus pointed at the infested building. \u201cLet\u2019s go with that one. It\u2019s not like she can make it worse, and we\u2019ll never have to go there again.\u201d<br /> <br /> He did have a point. If we didn\u2019t go there now, we\u2019d wanna explore it later and see what useful shit it had. So I shrugged and followed along. \u201cIt does seem to fit with your... idiom.\u201d I looked at Madame X.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can work with that.\u201d She nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan we just open the door and shoot a very large explosive in?\u201d Clytemnestra asked. \u201cSeems like a good way to say hello.\u201d<br /> <br /> I looked to Quietus and Kilroy. \u201cYou two brought grenades, right? Or can make them?\u201d<br /> <br /> Quietus frowned. \u201cYou guys don\u2019t let me keep grenades around.\u201d I shrugged.<br /> <br /> The humanoid flies weren\u2019t afraid of us - they didn\u2019t make any effort to avoid us at least - but they didn\u2019t attack either, just flying in and out of the fucking wounds on the building\u2019s skin. The door was unlocked, and just inside was a way goddamn beyond morbidly obese female demon, her folds oozing over and around the chair made of skin that she was sitting on. She looked up at us as we walked in, but made no other moves. The fleshy walls around her squirmed.<br /> <br /> We walked past her through the goddamn fleshy sphincter which took the place of the main door out of the area she was in without her doing anything but looking at us. As best we could figure, the Infrastructure was going to be down a level, so we headed for the fucking stairs. Clytemnestra looked around. \u201cI guess we had the good fortune to have stumbled upon one of the nicer parts of the Works first.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was the sound of buzzing in the building, that got louder as we got closer to the Infrastructure. The flies were still in evidence, despite the lack of open sores on the inside of the building, so it wasn\u2019t some big mystery what was making the noise. Still we weren\u2019t quite expecting what we saw, I don\u2019t think.<br /> <br /> At the end of the hallway were three doors. One led to a multi-level lobby whose ceiling was covered in the humanoid flies. The centerpiece of the room was what looked like a large brain based on shape, or a large beehive for flies, based on how they were interacting with it. Whatever it was, it gave me the goddamn creeps, and the flies were willing to ignore us for now, so I tried to hurry the boys on to the third door, which was the stairs.<br /> <br /> Quietus insisted on peeking into the other door, but got bored quickly enough when he realized it was just another office. One covered with skin, but that was getting to be goddamn passe at that point. We eventually made our way down the slick stairs. It was sketchy footing