d figured out it was a Defense Infrastructure, a place that would dispatch Angels. Not from there, but it would send the orders out. It did confirm that the Works absolutely had an Angel storage facility within it. That sure made Quietus happy. Of course, Kilroy kept looking at it after she tampered with it, prompting a nose and ear bleed, for good goddamn measure.<br /> <br /> The flies didn\u2019t actually put up any resistance, since she wasn\u2019t messing with their shit directly. She gave us enough warning when she was done and we got the fuck out of there. Once we were a bit away, we turned to watch. She didn\u2019t disappoint - after a moment there was a blinding white flash, and the entire building dropped a couple of floors, collapsing in on itself. The ground moved beneath our feet.<br /> <br /> \u201cShit. Let\u2019s get the fuck out in case someone gets the bright idea to check - that had to have been felt even in Seattle.\u201d I started moving away.<br /> <br /> We retraced our steps without any issue. Even the tunnel was alright - a bit less stable, but not dangerously enough to need to stabilize it right then. We all agreed to leave it for next time. And that there would be a next time. I owed Quietus at least that much.<br /> <br /> I grinned at the others as we shifted back into human form. \u201cSo who\u2019s up for checking out what she left at the hospital?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> We had an arranged meeting with the Changelings first, since it was definitely after fucking Mass by then. Jack called them to firm up details. Crusher answered. \u201cHey.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey man. We\u2019re back and mostly in one piece,\u201d Jack began.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, that\u2019s good, where are you back from?\u201d Crusher sounded concerned.<br /> <br /> Jack stretched his neck. \u201cNot a good place.\u201d<br /> <br /> Crusher paused. \u201cAlright. You still wanna meet, get your eyes opened?\u201d Jack made an affirmative noise. \u201cWhere do you wanna meet?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever\u2019s good for you.\u201d Jack smiled. \u201cNothing\u2019s hanging off, so we can meet wherever.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDinner? We could do the Pledge there without it being a thing. We could even go some place nicer than Kiki\u2019s.\u201d He smirked. \u201cI mean, not super nice, unless you\u2019re buying, but...\u201d<br /> <br /> I nudged him and suggested Bangkok Pies. I figured we might as well kill two goddamn birds and all that, and make sure things had gone alright for Kat last night. The Changelings were up for that, once Crusher got Rosanna\u2019s OK, and we met there.<br /> <br /> We got there first, and I took a moment to contact Esha and make sure she was alright. She was - hunkered down in her hotel room and bored, but alright. I promised her it wouldn\u2019t be long and put my phone away as Rosanna and Crusher showed up and Liz popped up our fucking bubble of silence.<br /> <br /> Rosanna smiled around at everyone. \u201cSo how was your Sunday?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe found a bad place today.\u201d Jack shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhich bad place did you find?\u201d When Jack hesitated, Rosanna raised an eyebrow. \u201cI came through the Hedge sweetie, I can take a lot.\u201d<br /> <br /> He chuckled. \u201cThe Works.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy\u2019d you go to the Works?\u201d She frowned at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cTo see what was there.\u201d<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes at him. \u201cThere was a spirit we needed to send the hell home.\u201d<br /> <br /> She made a face. \u201cI\u2019ve heard doorways to the Hedge just open there sometimes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell shit. It does seem to be the place for doorways - there was a reason we took our spirit there.\u201d I tapped my fingers on the table.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, mostly that it was isolated enough that the effects of her opening a portal back to her dimension would probably be overlooked,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> Rosanna looked between us. \u201cYou guys have interesting friends.\u201d<br /> <br /> I grimaced. \u201cFriends is a fucking strong word.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFascinating acquaintances?\u201d she offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure.\u201d Jack smiled.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThat is an apt descriptor. She had been summoned by a mage, who failed to control her - her presence in this reality did not sit well.\u201d<br /> <br /> We paused our conversation as Kat came by our table. \u201cWhat kind of pies does everyone want?\u201d She smiled brightly at all of us.<br /> <br /> \u201cA Coke and something good.\u201d I smirked at Kat.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I can find something you\u2019ll like.\u201d She winked back.<br /> <br /> The others ordered, Jack getting a see ew beef pizza and Liz a kee mao. When she got back to our table with the drinks, I took a large sip of the Coke and surreptitiously filled it up with whiskey from my flask. Rosanna had a pledge prepared, the same thing we\u2019d had before, so it wasn\u2019t too involved. We chatted for a bit before she got back to any business-y kinda talk. \u201cSo, I\u2019m terribly curious what you are up to with Heroin. I\u2019m sure Jack passed along our warning?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s involved in a case of ours. Mainly we\u2019re just brokering a sit-down meeting as opposed to having anyone skulking around the fucking shadows.\u201d I shrugged nonchalantly.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. She\u2019s not particularly treacherous, but be careful.\u201d Rosanna looked serious. \u201cShe does seem to like you, for what it\u2019s worth.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled. \u201cGabe is a very likable person.\u201d<br /> <br /> I choked on my whiskey and Coke. \u201cCan I get that in writing? Notarized, maybe? I\u2019m not sure anyone\u2019s ever said that before.\u201d<br /> <br /> Crusher smirked. \u201cShe did have her rump pointed towards us. That was the best.\u201d Rosanna gave him a dirty look.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s fine. I just wanted to make sure you knew you weren\u2019t moving in particularly legal circles, dealing with her.\u201d Rosanna looked back towards us.<br /> <br /> \u201cPerils of the job.\u201d I leaned back in my seat, one arm over the back.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI understand. Trust me.\u201d She paused. \u201cOne last thing - she\u2019s very loyal to Tar.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack chuckled. \u201cIt\u2019s fair to say the opposite is also true, it seems.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, well, she is a pretty girl and he is a big not-so-bright guy, so...\u201d Rosanna shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt does speak well to her character, that she has such loyalty,\u201d Billy Mack put forth.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure. I don\u2019t have anything against her, I just know that when she shows up, there\u2019s usually something going on underneath the table.\u201d Rosanna glared at Crusher again as he started laughing and hiding it poorly. Jack also found something amusing.<br /> <br /> He got it under control faster, and smiled fucking apologetically at Rosanna. \u201cAnything we can do to help you guys out? Not that we have a lot of time, I know, I know,\u201d he looked pointedly at me. My eyes widened innocently. \u201cBut I wanna help out if we can.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI am curious about that guy Crusher fought. The, uh, Herb gentleman. How he shrugged off hits that would have dented a car. Can you tell me anything about his deal?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack made a face and paused a moment before answering. \u201cBecause it\u2019s you, yeah. I don\u2019t make a habit of outing people, but I think this is safe. He\u2019s something called a Promethean.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know what that is.\u201d She frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cThink your Frankenstein\u2019s monsters.\u201d I took another sip of my drink. \u201cOr fuck, what is it, your Pygmalion statues, your golems. That kinda shit.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her eyebrows went up. \u201cWell. Oh. I guess it was only a matter of time until something weird showed up at our street fights.\u201d<br /> <br /> Crusher looked thoughtful. \u201cAny suggestions on training to beat him?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe your observations from your previous match with him would give you the most to work with.\u201d Billy Mack took up the thread for the floundering Jack.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am looking for a rematch.\u201d Crusher\u2019s mouth was set in a line.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cI believe Herb will be up for it. I think he quite enjoyed that match.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreat.\u201d The big guy looked goddamn bummed. \u201cI don\u2019t want people to enjoy fights with me too much.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe he enjoyed fighting someone who could stand up to more than a few swings, to be fair.\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow. Crusher looked somewhat cheered.<br /> <br /> Kay came by with our pizzas, giving us all a bright smile. Rosanna watched her as she left. \u201cShe\u2019s cheerful.\u201d We all agreed. \u201cBut something\u2019s not quite right. I can\u2019t put my finger on it...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack tilted his head. \u201cWhatever do you mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s rumors she was an ice giant.\u201d Jack beat me to it, the motherfucker.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would explain why she\u2019s so cold actually.\u201d When I raised an eyebrow at Rosanna, she clarified, \u201cHer arm was near me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head at Jack and I disapprovingly. \u201cNo, that is the vivacious young lady who works at Whacko Bob\u2019s.\u201d<br /> <br /> I put my hand out at shoulder height. \u201cYou mean the one that\u2019s about this tall? That ice giant?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBilly Mack is our expert at ice giants,\u201d Liz explained to the bemused pair of Changelings.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are notoriously clever shapeshifters.\u201d He took a sip of his drink. \u201cNotoriously clever.\u201d<br /> <br /> Crusher nodded. \u201cOh wait, I know who that is. She\u2019s pretty.\u201d<br /> <br /> Rosanna frowned. \u201cYes, she is, isn\u2019t she?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Before we left, I took a moment to get Kat alone and make sure everything went fine the night before. It had, so I gave her a wink and joined the rest to head out to the goddamn hospital. As we got close, Liz started fretting. \u201cI can\u2019t believe I\u2019m going in there again.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019ll be fine. We\u2019re not going to talk to ghosts, or take fucking side passages, or fight monsters, just straight up to the goddamn Infrastructure,\u201d I reassured her.<br /> <br /> At the place, nothing much had changed, though Jack was quick to point out which bloodstain was Terry\u2019s. \u201cThanks ever so much,\u201d Liz said sarcastically. \u201cShame it doesn\u2019t have any of his essential nutrients left.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack ignored them. \u201cWe should probably confer with the Fogmen about the large quantity of ghosts here at some point.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot right now though,\u201d Jack looked around furtively.<br /> <br /> Inside, Billy Mack made a beeline for the elevator. \u201cI wonder if this still works?\u201d He pushed the button.<br /> <br /> Jack\u2019s eyes widened. \u201cIt did last time we were here, and you don\u2019t want to use it like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I just wish to see if it is intact.\u201d There was an odd grinding sound, then the fucking bing sound of an arriving elevator car. The doors opened onto a rather normal looking elevator car, if you ignored the goddamn large bloodstain splattered against the walls and floor, and the handful of bones scattered around. A pair of shoes completed the tableau.<br /> <br /> I marched right past them. \u201cStairs...\u201d<br /> <br /> We were all keeping an eye upwards looking for large falling machinery, so we managed to spot the goddamn gurney that was precariously balanced despite the fact that the door behind us was slamming itself loudly and repeatedly. Jack yelled up the stairs. \u201cCan you guys just throw that down now, or not throw it at us? We know it\u2019s up there.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack walked forward, prompting the gurney to be pushed over onto him. He neatly sidestepped out of the way, into the path of the fallen child that tumbled over with it. The screaming child in a hospital gown fell through him, then through the floor and further down, a look of freedom and happiness on her face. My muscles tensed. \u201cThis is a bad place.\u201d No one disagreed with me.<br /> <br /> We got to the landing that led to my Infrastructure. We could still hear the dogs up above, but all of us had had enough dogs for today. The writing was still there, but the fucking zombies weren\u2019t. My Infrastructure looked better - it was still damaged, but she\u2019d taken all the shit out of it, and damaged was all it was.<br /> <br /> We had a few hours left until Nikka was at work, and it took all of it to disassemble the Infrastructure and get it stashed in my bolthole. It left my bolthole pretty damn full, but was a hell of a sight better than carting it out past the ghosts\u2019 and their large object chucking tendencies. Liz was even nice enough to bundle things together with webbing for easier transport once I got Greg to the theatre.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright, if you\u2019ve got all that down, I\u2019d like to go home, get a massage from my cabana boy and go to sleep, alone.\u201d Liz smiled wanly at the rest of us.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing doll. We\u2019ll be at Kiki\u2019s, but I imagine it\u2019ll be fine. Get your rest.\u201d I gave her a smile.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVI</i><br /> <br /> The Demons were causing people to act according to their Vices, with the Demons being immune to direct consequences of that. This lead to \u201cIndependent\u201d causing Jack to tell us to fuck off, and \u201cDecedent\u201d to Clytemnestra going off for Cocaine &amp; Ass. Neither was quite what the demons hoped for, but they could not read Vices, only activate them. Speed Demon resisted it.<br /> <br /> The comment about going down stairs in the meat building was due to everyone (except Clytemnestra, because Demon form powers) having to make a Dexterity + Athletics roll not to fall, since the stairs were covered in flesh.<br /> <br /> Some odd terminology, but it is all a spin on interaction with Infrastructure. The whole area is Infrastructure, but the Angels, say, down the first earthen path were guarding a part of it for interface. Saying \u201cguarding Infrastructure\u201d is a (very useful) shorthand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T01:33:47-08:00","id":1018376,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look in on the detective agency. It\u2019s Sunday night, and they hope to get a lot of cases cleared up Monday. Let\u2019s see how it goes.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s story takes place at the end of the session, after the last line of Speed\u2019s Journal.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Kiki\u2019s was fucking busy that night. Nikka had a few clients, some that had met with her the night before and some that hadn\u2019t, but nothing that stood out. Still, it seemed she was getting more business than she had the week before, enough to make me nervous. Not that I wanted her business to go poorly, it\u2019s just easier to watch over someone when they\u2019re waiting at a table alone. Sonia was also doing business for the look of things, meeting with the vamp dame that had mind fucked Jack a few times. <br /> <br /> A few college students were there, though not Naomi\u2019s crew. Well, unless Heather counts as being part of Naomi\u2019s crew, and if so, god fucking help the both of them. The other two were there as a couple, the dame Naomi\u2019d been trying to get in the pants of the night before, and a gee who meant nothing to me, but Billy Mack kept frowning at. After I kicked him under the table a few times, he explained that the kid Neil was the other one Heather had a crush on, aside from Adria. I shook my head. Sounded like college bullshit to me, college bullshit the g-man was far too invested in, but he did have a point. Even tiddlywinks had some weight to it when a dragon was playing it.<br /> <br /> Pham Min and Heroin were in a booth, chattering away in Vietnamese. Tar was there as well, nursing a beer and obviously unable to understand a goddamn word they were saying. Still, he didn\u2019t look too displeased with his situation. Drake was there as well, keeping an eye on that same table with even more focus and discretion than Jack and I were. And at a guess, for entirely different reasons.<br /> <br /> Shelley swung by Vivian\u2019s table, who smiled up at her. \u201cHey there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey.\u201d Shelley returned the smile. \u201cHow are you doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMmm. It\u2019s been a long weekend.\u201d Vivian had a rueful note in her voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cStaying busy?\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian chuckled. \u201cAh, you know. Idle hands...\u201d <br /> <br /> Shelley raised an eyebrow. \u201cIdle hands sounds fun.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can think of much better things for them to be doing actually.\u201d Vivian smirked up at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh...\u201d Shelley looked playfully thoughtful. \u201cBut I\u2019m working.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian sighed. \u201cYou are, and I should not distract you from that.\u201d She paused. \u201cDespite the 7 or 8 ways I just thought of in the last minute to do so.\u201d<br /> <br /> Shelley winked and moved back on her way.<br /> <br /> Heather continued to seem pretty goddamn fixated on Neil and Nick, so I sent Clytemnestra a quick text, to the emergency number so she\u2019d interrupt her massage, describing what was going on and asking for her opinion on the best way to cool shit down. I also asked if it was safe to bring out my copper eyes.<br /> <br /> \u2018Copper eyes should be safe. Lemme know what\u2019s there?\u2019<br /> <br /> I popped in Mind Reading and Aura Sight and pried into the college student\u2019s mind. She was well-convinced that Nick was obviously a hussy, manipulating poor Neil with her fucking seductive wiles. She was determining that \u2018tricky\u2019 Nick, with her edgy, Satanic nickname, deserved a good scare, since she was obviously out to hurt poor Neil\u2019s feelings. The way she relished the thought undermined the hell out of the moralistic justifications though. A stray thought occurred to her before I let the others know the situation, that she better not let Naomi know. She didn\u2019t want to deal with that. Not enough to call off the spooky plans, whatever they were, but enough to want to be fucking cautious about it.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra\u2019s first response was quick: \u2018sigh\u2019. She followed it up with a longer winded one, \u2018I don\u2019t really want to have a fight with Heather. Does she seem to want to kill her?\u2019<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u2018Nothing I read suggests that, unless \u201cterrify\u201d is what kids call murder these days.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018I like Nick, but if I want to maintain a more positive relationship with Heather, so that I can maybe steer her away from a more serious matter, I probably should not come and have a big row with her. As long as she is not going to kill Nick, which would make me very cross with her... I think poor Nick is gonna have a bad night.\u2019 She made a good fucking point.<br /> <br /> I replied quickly. \u2018Makes sense. Enjoying the rest of your massage.\u2019<br /> <br /> Billy Mack was still shaking his head. \u201cYou were my best hope, and you fucked it up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, no.\u201d I smirked at him. Reassuringly, of course. \u201cMotherfucker\u2019s coming out of this squeaky clean. Nick\u2019s a shameless hussy and Neil\u2019s just been led astray by her manipulative wiles.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would perhaps be good to move on that plan, before something else like this happens again.\u201d The g-man nodded thoughtfully. I made like I was washing my hands. \u201cI\u2019m just saying, if we can maneuver them into a steady relationship, her likelihood of randomly terrorizing people will be lower.\u201d<br /> <br /> I made a mocking half bow, as best I could over the table. \u201cHave at it. Lemme know if I can detective anything into your goddamn meet-cute.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his fucking eyes and took his drink off to go bother Drake. He found him nursing a coffee. \u201cYou\u2019re drinking coffee in here, so you\u2019re obviously busy or terrified. So, you too busy to talk?\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake gave him a slight smile. \u201cNah, siddown.\u201d Jack settled in. \u201cI\u2019m just keeping an eye on the other Fae in the room.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cContract work, or personal?\u201d Jack took a sip of his beer.<br /> <br /> \u201cContract.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cWhat have Tar and Heroin gotten up to now?\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake kept his eyes on the pair. \u201cI can\u2019t go into too much detail. I\u2019ll just say... one of the people they\u2019re working for, I\u2019ve been contracting to find out who it is.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re working for people?\u201d Jack raised a goddamn eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. They tend to freelance out.\u201d Drake took a sip of his coffee. \u201cReally I\u2019m trying to keep an eye on them while they\u2019re not at the Bowling Alley of Sex. I\u2019m not a prude or anything, but visiting the Bowling Alley of Sex was definitely not something I had on my bucket list. Or any list.\u201d He shook his head. \u201cHopefully I won\u2019t have to break into their office. Well, her office. Tar\u2019s not an office kinda guy.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack chuckled. \u201cHe\u2019s not a bad guy, for the 'stands there and looks big' type.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake shrugged. \u201cI\u2019m not looking to move against them or anything - I\u2019m not dumb. I do know the woman they\u2019re with now is supernatural. They seem to be friends, but my client thinks the person they\u2019re working for is supernatural.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know they\u2019re friends, certainly.\u201d The fixer smirked. \u201cFriends, lovers, a little column A, a little of column B.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake nodded and changed the subject. \u201cSo how you been doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack leaned back in the seat. \u201cAlright. A little excitement here and there. Still in one piece though. You seem to have dropped back into the swing of things pretty well.\u201d Drake shrugged and nodded. \u201cI\u2019ll let you know if I hear anything about those two. We do have some dealings around them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKnow of any supernatural creatures, probably Changelings but maybe not, that she has been engaged with for smuggling, particularly weapons smuggling?\u201d Drake raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> Jack thought for a fucking moment. \u201cNot yet. I know of someone she\u2019s been working with, but she\u2019s not supernatural.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake made a considering noise. \u201cThe people that hired me think they\u2019re a supernatural person. I don\u2019t know why they think that\u2019s the case.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack nodded subtly in Sonia\u2019s direction. \u201cSee the bottle blond with the African-American lady over there?\u201d Drake nodded. \u201cThe non-blonde met with her recently.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s not supernatural,\u201d Drake said after a moment\u2019s discrete inspection. \u201cStill, worth looking into, I appreciate it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure thing.\u201d Jack leaned into the table a bit. \u201cSteer clear of the blonde though. I\u2019m told, although I can\u2019t prove it, that she put the mind whammy on me.\u201d At Drake's raised eyebrow, he continued, \u201cA vampire.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded sagely. \u201cThey do that. So, what do you know about her cute friend?\u201d A quick glance to Heroin\u2019s table let Jack know they were back to talking about the Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe goes by Pham Min.\u201d Jack took a swig of beer. \u201cSin-Eater, smart mouth, gorgeous. Probably one you don\u2019t want to fuck with either.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know anything about Sin-eaters, not being Catholic.\u201d Drake sipped his coffee.<br /> <br /> The fixer chuckled. \u201cWell, they\u2019re not that. It\u2019s not so much that she\u2019s a super bad-ass, though she\u2019s probably not too bad off, but they run in packs. Or... I dunno what they call their groups. But the Rain City Mafia is not one to fuck with.\u201d He paused. \u201cWe still haven\u2019t met their leader, cause he doesn\u2019t like a lot of things, and we\u2019re on the list.\u201d<br /> <br /> Drake nodded solemnly. \u201cAlright, I\u2019ll be careful with Pham Min.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smirked. \u201cI mean, I flirt with her, but, just saying, I don\u2019t know which direction pushing goes, so...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d Drake went to take a sip, then put the coffee down. \u201cWait, are you saying she\u2019s your girl?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo...\u201d Jack raised his hands. \u201cNo, no, no. Not making any assumptions down that line.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust wanted to make sure...\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack took a drink. \u201cOh. Dumb question - do you know anything about what happened to the dumbass furry in the rabbit suit?\u201d Drake looked at him oddly. \u201cDovetonsils.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked around. \u201cNo. I hadn\u2019t noticed until you mentioned.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s been missing a couple of weeks, is all.\u201d Jack sat back.<br /> <br /> Drake looked fucking apologetic. \u201cThis is only the second time I\u2019ve been here, since I got out of the Hedge.\u201d<br /> <br /> They talked for a bit more, and after a few minutes Drake indicated Heather. \u201cSo, that girl over there seems really inten -\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t. Ever. For any reason, without lots of help and a damn good explanation as to why, deal with her. She doesn\u2019t like many people, and really doesn\u2019t like me. And she\u2019s dangerous.\u201d Jack held his gaze goddamn intently.<br /> <br /> \u201cNoted.\u201d<br /> <br /> While Jack was off there, I decided to look in on Sonia, see if her current business happened to be for the same God-Machine reminiscent motherfucker that had sent her to Heroin. Her thoughts were pretty regimented and goddamn focused, except for when they wandered off to think about Heroin, since she knew she was dealing with a vampire and knew the kinda mind-whammy bullshit they could pull off. More interesting was that Jack\u2019s vampire friend was connected to Sanderson\u2019s corporation, some kind of operative.<br /> <br /> She was meeting with her in order to get some kind of AI boosting hardware. She knew what Sanderson could do with Pandorans, even if she didn\u2019t know what they were, and was hoping to use his tech to create a sentient computer, cause that\u2019s worked out real great in the literature so fucking far. Even better, she planned on connecting it to the God-Machine reminiscent tech and-or weapons she\u2019d been dealing with otherwise. She was a sharp one. Ignorant on certain fronts, but a hell of a thinker<br /> <br /> I passed all that along via text to the others: \u2018Sonia wants to use Sanderson\u2019s Pandoran generating powers to create sentient computers with weapons systems.\u2019 I sent a follow-up quickly. \u2018Oh, and the blonde vamp works for Sanderson.\u2019. Jack got up from Drake\u2019s booth immediately. <br /> <br /> \u2018You know, Team Tomorrow and Sanderson seem to be in the background of every not God-Machine related scheme going on in this city.\u2019 Liz responded quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy Cyberdyne?\u201d Jack sat down goddamn heavily.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy not?\u201d Billy Mack asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, no, not the right answer,\u201d Jack snapped back.<br /> <br /> I cleared my throat. Jack rolled his eyes at me. \u201cI think a better question is what are we going to do about it.\u201d I glared at Billy Mack. \u201cWhich is not a discussion we can have right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are correct.\u201d I flipped Jack off.<br /> <br /> I turned back to glance at the college couple, figuring I\u2019d throw them a bone and change the goddamn subject. Turns out Neil was not supernatural, which was good, had a vague idea that Heather was some girl from his school, which was not great. I let Billy Mack and Vivian know via text about that, his reckless tendencies, and that it actually had been Nick\u2019s \u201cmanipulative wiles\u201d that started things off, not that Neil wasn\u2019t 100 percent into it. <br /> <br /> Vivian looked him over herself, using Sum of All Fears. He didn\u2019t seem half bad - he cared about his parents and was enough of a thinker to hedge his bets with sports involvement in case his grades tanked, not that he was having any difficulties. Long term, he wanted his name to be remembered and afraid he\u2019d just wind up being inconsequential.<br /> <br /> After a while, the college couple headed out, Heather following discretely behind. Billy Mack sighed goddamn noisily. I shrugged at him. The vampire dame was the next of our marked targets to leave. Sonia stuck around to talk to Heroin for a few minutes, but not too long. The crowd itself was thinning, though Heroin, Tar and Pham were sticking around for the long haul, as was Nikka, of course.<br /> <br /> With the crowd thinned out, it was easy to see Louise stop by and duck her head in for a quick sweep of the room. She didn\u2019t seem to find what she was looking for, which didn\u2019t stop me from wanting to know what that was, but my sight faltered a bit and I couldn\u2019t get a fucking handle on anything. She didn\u2019t stay long - she hardly came into the room - and disappeared back into the night. At least we knew she wasn\u2019t hunting Billy Mack or Vivian.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Nikka packed up and headed out. I followed her out discretely. In the parking lot, I leaned on the wall near her bike. She smiled over at me. \u201cIt was a productive night. Much better than last weekend - that was nothing but a waste of time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGlad it\u2019s going well.\u201d I smirked at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI'm getting nervous - I haven\u2019t seen this Cornelius in awhile. I believe he is waiting for you to lose interest.\u201d She frowned.<br /> <br /> I spared a brief glance around. \u201cPossibly, but that\u2019s not gonna happen. Our guy has a plan for the next step.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked at me wryly. \u201cI will run out of cash before you run out of patience, so that is good to hear.\u201d<br /> <br /> One of the patrons was leaving the bar so I moved in close for a kiss and whispered in her ear. \u201cThe apprentice has wards against spirits, so be careful. Probably learned it from the big guy. They are a little crude.\u201d I stepped back, a teasing grin on my face. I continued at a more normal volume. \u201cWe\u2019ll just have to speed things along.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will be out of town for a few days, some business near LA. I have made arrangements, false names and the like, and will be back probably Thursday night. I don't think I need to be followed unless you think it is necessary.\u201d She ran a finger down my collar.<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds like you hit the high points.\u201d I smirked at her and sent a text, arranging for a code and countercode for when she got back. I glanced fucking significantly down at her phone as it beeped and peered over her shoulder as she read it. <br /> <br /> She shook her head as if I\u2019d sent something inappropriate and winked at me. \u201cWill you be seeing me home tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTo the door.\u201d I grinned at her and rubbed my shoulder. \u201cIt\u2019s been a hell of a day.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I went on home, but Vivian stuck around until closing, using clairvoyance to pick up more intel while she waited for her girlfriend to get off work. She started with the apprentice, seeing her on a fucking quayside in the goddamn Undercity. The dark water lapped slightly on the ground that her and three of her buddies were standing on. They were smoking, and waiting on someone.<br /> <br /> She sent texts out, and I knew roughly where she was - there weren\u2019t too many quays down there. The general area was near-ish to the entrance fucking Skeevy Larry had used, and nowhere near the glowing mushrooms, thanks for goddamn small favors. I texted him back to let him know.<br /> <br /> \u2018Maybe they\u2019re waiting for him. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u2019 I rolled my eyes at Vivian\u2019s text on my phone.<br /> <br /> \u2018So we wanna jump them, or wait to carry out the plan that I know nothing of, and don\u2019t want to know anything of?\u2019 I was hoping for the latter, as horrible a plan as it may goddamn be. I needed to sleep it the hell off.<br /> <br /> There was a pause. \u2018I was hoping to get a better read on her. Sum of All Fears could definitely get us a better handle on their relationship.\u2019<br /> <br /> I shrugged out of my jacket. \u2018Fine by me.\u2019<br /> <br /> Vivian kept an eye on them, and eventually they were met by a handful of business suited people with briefcases. Based on the branding, they were Team Tomorrow. Team Tomorrow mooks, not Dr. Gist level. From the looks of it, Team Tomorrow were trying to hire them for... something. The briefcases were full of paperwork, a contract most likely. Unfortunately, she couldn\u2019t hear, just see, and no one was kinda enough to use sign language, or hold the paperwork up to the fucking camera.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T01:34:23-08:00","id":1018377,"title":"","content":"The next day came at its usual fucking time, and we made our way to the office. I had texted Esha the night before, and asked her to let me know how the meeting with her bosses went. She\u2019d let me know that it was scheduled for 10 AM, so I made sure to be up and about and at the office by then.<br /> <br /> Naomi showed up a little after me, and as soon as Cecilia got up to do something, the pink haired dame plopped down on her chair, put her feet up on the goddamn desk and started playing with her phone. I rolled my eyes and headed up to my office to play some darts and drink some laced coffee.<br /> <br /> Even there I could hear Cecilia telling her off, and imagine the way she was standing, hands on her hips, glaring at Naomi. \u201cI can\u2019t believe we\u2019re related! You\u2019re so boorish.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen I\u2019m old like you, will I be boring like you?\u201d Goddamn, but Naomi was an ass.<br /> <br /> After a few minutes, Billy Mack came by and asked to have a discussion in the conference room. He picked up Naomi and Jack on the way. Once we got there, he started musing, \u201cOn one hand, if Team Tomorrow isn\u2019t hiring the Harvesters to collect a spirit for them, they may be occupied. I really need to get a better angle on what they\u2019re up to.\u201d He paused. \u201cIt is possible they\u2019ve decided that this target is not worth going after and are moving on to other things.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi shrugged, sprawling out in her chair. \u201cOr they\u2019re trying to get Team Tomorrow to sell her out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cThat is a possibility.\u201d<br /> <br /> I got a text from Esha right about then. \u2018They\u2019re sending a couple of people to grab and interrogate the people watching me.\u2019 I started to reply when I got another message. \u2018Apparently the operation is too critical to allow that kind of interference. So, probably handled, assuming we didn\u2019t just escalate something. The boss is going.\u2019 That kept me from checking to make sure it would be under control. If the fucking Angel in charge of watching over that project couldn\u2019t figure out what was going on, either it was a lot deeper than I could help with, or we had a lot less to fear from Blue Sun that I\u2019d figured.<br /> <br /> \u201cTeam Tomorrow\u2019s agents after Esha are going to be interviewed by an Angel, so that shit\u2019s probably under control,\u201d I informed others. I leaned back in my chair. \u201cSo is there anything you need for the investigation into the apprentice? Even if they\u2019ve moved on from Nikka, we can still turn them against Cornelius, possibly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFirst step is to get a read on her fears - we need to know where they stand and what they are up to.\u201d Billy Mack frowned. <br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cSo where\u2019s she now? Presumably not having any more back-alley, underground meetings with Team Tomorrow...\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack\u2019s eyes clouded over. \u201cShe is at work.\u201d He paused. \u201cWe are fairly certain the meeting with Heroin and Kat is on the level, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not sure what vested interest she\u2019d have in it being otherwise.\u201d Naomi swung her seat around, fiddling with her phone. \u201cHeather\u2019s in a good mood, by the way. She apparently wrote another fanfiction last night.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNick is alive, by the way,\u201d Billy Mack said. \u201cStill asleep at the moment, but alive. As is Neil. He is in class.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi\u2019s eyes got large. \u201cSomeone needs to explain to that girl how penile engorgement works, cause she does not understand.\u201d She shoved her phone in my fucking face. \u201cRead this!\u201d I made a face as I accidentally read the first few lines on the screen. \u201cIt\u2019s not a balloon!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you considered...\u201d Billy Mack stopped, and walked out of the room.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t lecture her on how dicks work, that would be cover damaging.\u201d Naomi shrugged at his retreating back.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack returned with the copy of Cocklords of Mars he kept on his desk. \u201cHere. She should read this.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow at him. \u201cSuch altruism. Giving up your cocklords.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere are a lot of dicks in that book.\u201d Billy Mack shrugged. \u201cAnd they work, quite well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnce she realizes that, maybe we'll... no, we still won\u2019t enjoy her fanfiction.\u201d Naomi looked goddamn resignedly down at her phone.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cYes, but if she doesn\u2019t realize it\u2019s not a balloon animal before we hook her up with Neil, that could go badly. She might try to tie it in a knot.\u201d<br /> <br /> I stumbled up out of my chair. \u201cI had a dart board. And a bottle of whisky. Right over there. Lemme know if I can help.\u201d<br /> <br /> They kept on. \u201cShe\u2019s also not too sharp on except and accept. I\u2019m not even a native speaker and I got that one down, come on woman!\u201d Naomi complained as she kept reading.<br /> <br /> \u201cHas she taken a creative writing class?\u201d Billy Mack asked. \u201cI\u2019m sure she could work it in as an elective, surely it would help.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose...\u201d Naomi muttered. \u201cHang on - look how she writes kissing. I\u2019m pretty sure she\u2019s never kissed anyone either.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned at the fucking screen. \u201cPerhaps we should accelerate that plan.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi sighed. \u201cYou know she wants me to illustrate some of her stories? I asked her what she was going to pay me for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid she have an answer?\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cWell, this sorta sad pouty face that made me not use that flippant a tone next time. I kinda felt bad. She doesn\u2019t know she can\u2019t write. I hope she knows she only has a dim idea how to fuck.\u201d She kept reading. \u201cPeople don\u2019t throw covers aside like a cape! Argh, I\u2019m done.\u201d She put the phone down.<br /> <br /> \u201cApparently terrorizing Nick put her in a mood,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> Naomi nodded. \u201cYeah. Now every time she\u2019s cheerful I\u2019ll wonder.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked around to Jack and Naomi with his fucking clouded eyes. \u201cAnyone have someone or place I should look up on while I have these going?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe vampire that works for Sanderson? Maybe get an eye on her haven?\u201d Jack suggested.<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cShe\u2019s asleep in a nicely appointed bedroom, with blackout curtains. Not a crypt, or a coffin. In fact, I believe it\u2019s a Sleep Number bed. It appears she\u2019s a 7.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Naomi left shortly after that to hang out at the college. I was headed that way myself eventually, to try the fucking soft touch with Dr. Hazard. Judging from his schedule posted online, his last class ended at 4, and he didn\u2019t have office hours or anything like that after. So I planned to show up around then and see if I could get a moment with him alone.<br /> <br /> Just before I was about to leave, Cecilia came to my door. \u201cThere is a Dr. Kathryn Cross to see you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow, and put away my goddamn bottle. \u201cShow her on up.\u201d I nodded to Billy Mack as he came in and sat at the other seat on my side of the desk. When she got there, I gestured towards the other seat. \u201cWhat can I do for you, Dr. Cross?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know that you had some dealings with the Asbury Room situation,\u201d she nodded to both of us, \u201cI know that your agency had something to do with closing it. I don\u2019t know all the details but I know enough... there\u2019s been another strange occurrence at the university.\u201d<br /> <br /> She could say that again. I didn\u2019t let on that we knew anything, just had on my usual expression of professional interest. She continued, \u201cSome books have been stolen, and people are being awful cagey about discussing it. Usually when something goes missing from Special Collections, it\u2019s a big deal - last time there was a search of the students\u2019 dorms even. There hasn\u2019t been anything like that. In fact, they\u2019re denying anything\u2019s missing.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cBut you think there is?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d overheard people talking about something like that and based on a little... investigation, if you get my meaning,\u201d I gave her an understanding smile, \u201cI know there are books missing and people are worried about it. I wanted to ask you about the possibility of hiring you in a private capacity.\u201d She looked away. \u201cThis would get me in hot water with some of my peers, if it were to get out.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe will be discreet,\u201d Billy Mack assured her.<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cI\u2019m particularly worried about Dr. Stein knowing too much. He\u2019s already had a conversation with me where he assured me that nothing is missing and I don\u2019t need to worry about it - there was an implied threat involved. So I don\u2019t want him to know I hired you.\u201d She looked goddamn frustrated. \u201cI know he knows something about it, but it is remarkably difficult to read his mind.\u201d<br /> <br /> I drew up a quick contract for her. \u201cWe certainly will be discrete. Do you have any suggestions as to who we should talk to about it? I mean, Dr. Stein seems obvious, but anyone else?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think that Dr. Stein is responsible, but I think he knows what\u2019s going on. I know Dr. Hazard is involved with that part of Special Collections.\u201d She frowned, looking away. \u201cIt is also very hard to read his mind. One of the professors left very abruptly for Iowa, right after it was reported. He\u2019s still there - someone else is covering his classes. He probably had access to that area. He was elsewhere at the time of the theft - I\u2019ve read witnesses\u2019 minds to confirm that much.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWould what was in there be dangerous? Maybe he\u2019s just afraid of whoever took it having it,\u201d I suggested.<br /> <br /> She nodded, somewhat distractedly. \u201cThat\u2019s my guess. But here\u2019s the thing - I asked a few questions and did some light... mind reading, but I didn\u2019t push. Still, Dr. Stein knew.\u201d<br /> <br /> I let out a noisy breath. \u201cHe has his fingers to the pulse of something. He had a similar way of knowing about stuff in the Asbury Room.\u201d Billy Mack nodded in agreement.<br /> <br /> \u201cLike I said, I don\u2019t think he stole them, I just think he knows what\u2019s going on.\u201d She took a fucking deep breath. \u201cWhat I want to hire you for is to determine if they are dangerous to the university, and retrieve them only if they are. If you determine they\u2019re not, then it\u2019s a shame they were stolen, but I\u2019m not worried about retrieving them - I don\u2019t want to put you on retainer for a dangerous recovery of stolen property job unless I have to.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded towards the contract. \u201cThat\u2019s what I figured.\u201d I had maybe lowballed the fucking numbers a little, but she was only asking us to do what we were going to already.<br /> <br /> She described the collection a little, about what Stein had told us with a little less detail. After that, she took another deep breath. \u201cI\u2019ve asked Cassandra, and Cassandra did not have access to anything there. I... believe you figured out that we were... close.\u201d I nodded, non-judgmentally. \u201cWe\u2019re still close. We are... closer.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe isn\u2019t my student, so...\u201d She stared at my desk. <br /> <br /> I held up my hands. \u201cNo worries here doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cIt\u2019s just... Dr. Stein intimated he knew I was sleeping with a student. In the less physical portion of the threatening. What he told me boils down to I would really regret it if I kept looking into this.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I recommend you not. We\u2019re working it now, and there\u2019s no call for you to go getting yourself in trouble.\u201d I ran a coin across my knuckles. \u201cI\u2019m thinking I\u2019m going to try to work with Stein - I don\u2019t want to work at odds with him again, and he doesn\u2019t have threats to hold over my head. No matter how buddy buddy we get though, your name will not enter into it, I promise. We obviously have contacts at the university, it won\u2019t be too out of the ordinary.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cYou did right by us with the Asbury Room thing, I know from my... friendship with Cassandra that you set things right.\u201d She bit her lip. \u201cI worried about the school, and the students. Especially with how bristly it has Dr. Hazard and Dr. Stein.\u201d She paused. \u201cI think Dr. Carpenter might have been looking into it too. He and I don\u2019t get along too well, so I haven\u2019t tried to reach out to him. If Dr. Carpenter is as bristly as Dr. Stein and Dr. Hazard... I don\u2019t want more people threatening me right now.\u201d She drew in on herself, looking a little lost.<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstandable.\u201d Billy Mack nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m kinda afraid to meet up with Cassandra, cause I don\u2019t know if I\u2019m being watched on campus or not.\u201d Her face turned sad. She was far too goddamn pretty a dame to be this worked up. \u201cI would really like to just... feel safe with her for a little bit. We might try and meet somewhere away from campus. I...\u201d She cut herself short a bit. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, I\u2019m babbling.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled. \u201cNo worries doll.\u201d I left her take another deep breath. \u201cOur first order of business is to try and talk with these folks. Any suggestions as far as a good time?\u201d I\u2019d been fiddling with my computer a little bit more than strictly fucking necessary to put in her information, so it wouldn\u2019t be obvious I had Dr. Hazard\u2019s webpage open before she got there. I turned it around to show her. \u201cAny I-don\u2019t-realize-it-cause-I-haven\u2019t-been-to-college-in-a-long-time reason why I shouldn\u2019t grab him after his last class today?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cDr. Hazard is usually pretty approachable, but like I said, he\u2019s bristly right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut the timing - that\u2019d be a good time, if it were... a better time, if that made sense?\u201d I grinned over at her.<br /> <br /> She smiled slightly back. \u201cIt does. And yes. I\u2019m sorry to come and talk your ear off like this.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cNot a problem.\u201d I glanced back over at my computer. \u201cThough if I want to catch him today, I better get a move on.\u201d I stood and she did as well, offering me her hand to shake. I shook it, giving her a reassuring squeeze. \u201cWe\u2019re on this, and we\u2019ll let you know, discretely, what we find. You though...\u201d I pointed at her, \u201cshould lay low for a bit. Don\u2019t get in their way.\u201d She nodded.<br /> <br /> As she reached the door, she turned. \u201cOne other complication...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d I raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy husband and I are going through a divorce. He might be jittery at women he perceives as wanting to talk to me for any reason. He might get... abrasive.\u201d She frowned. \u201cHe knows I\u2019m dating someone, but he doesn\u2019t know who they are. I\u2019d prefer he didn\u2019t decide it might be you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cI can deal with abrasive, doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> I left right after Dr. Cross. Back at the office, about 10 minutes after I\u2019d left, Jack and Billy Mack heard loud yelling from the front desk. They went downstairs quickly to find some fucker yelling at Cecilia. \u201cCan we help you?\u201d Jack growled out.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy wife was here.\u201d The man puffed out his chest, looking between the two new arrivals goddamn angrily. \u201cKathryn. What did she want?\u201d Jack frowned, hiding his puzzled look.<br /> <br /> \u201cI believe you are going to leave now sir.\u201d Billy Mack held his gaze levelly. \u201cWe do not answer questions concerning our business dealings.\u201d <br /> <br /> The man glared at the two of them for a moment, then stormed the hell out. After a moment, Cecilia looked at Billy Mack. \u201cSo, I think he just accused me of sleeping with his wife?\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack frowned at the door. \u201cAre you OK?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah.\u201d She nodded. \u201cJust kinda dumbfounded.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cIs Gabe sleeping with his wife? Just curious. I mean, thumbs up to her if she is.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man smiled. \u201cNo, that is not one of the many entries on Gabe\u2019s social calendar.\u201d <br /> <br /> Cecilia laughed, the jackass. \u201cThinking about it, when he asked if I was sleeping with his wife, I probably shouldn\u2019t have said \u2018I don\u2019t think so\u2019. Maybe more like, \u2018No, I am straight, I do not do sex things with other females\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe not like that.\u201d Jack