ssandra\u2019s. I think that kinda fuels their affair. Dr. Cross has a real problem with getting involved with people she really shouldn\u2019t, which describes Cassandra on every level, down to Dr. Cross\u2019 being Christian and Cassandra being a practicing Pagan witch.\u201d Liz shook her head. \u201cAnyway, Stein really doesn\u2019t like her, and she even thinks there\u2019s a chance that Stein might be colluding with the private investigator.\u201d<br /> <br /> Bill Mack frowned. \u201cBy chance does she know anything about this investigator?\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz shook her head. \u201cShe asked me if it was you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe wouldn\u2019t do that, Dr. Cross is cute.\u201d I smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat was my response. She was hoping it was and that we would accept the job and just not give him anything, I told her we have a professional code - we would just refuse to take the case and possibly tell him where to go stick it.\u201d She smiled sweetly for a moment, before her face fell. \u201cCassandra is really worried about her, particularly in relation to Dr. Stein.\u201d She sighed. \u201cI feel slightly bad about seducing her that one time. I don\u2019t regret it - it was a hell of a lot of fun - but I feel bad.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack sipped his fucking coffee. \u201cWell, at this point at the think the best thing for her to do would be to avoid any further entanglements in the situation, for her own safety.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz agreed. \u201cShe\u2019s being very discreet, not even using social media, since she doesn\u2019t know what has or has not been hacked.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can look into that,\u201d Billy Mack offered.<br /> <br /> \u201cUntil then, when she is communicating with her student who is also her lover...\u201d Liz shrugged. \u201cWell, she\u2019s not her student, just a student..\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack smiled wryly. \u201cIt is still an ethical violation.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz nodded. \u201cAnd it would get her expelled.\u201d She sighed. \u201cI think she tentatively wants to get together with her after Cassandra\u2019s graduated, and a little time has passed. But that\u2019s neither here nor there...\u201d She paused for a moment. \u201cAngela has been placed in a specific part of the library, downstairs at the customer service desk, as far away from Special Collections as possible. She hasn\u2019t been told not to go up to Special Collections, but she has been told she doesn\u2019t have any reason to leave the desk while she\u2019s there, which was not a comment made to any of the other workers there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, it\u2019s probably a good thing. That \u2018small god\u2019 is apparently a creature that likes to attach itself on to human lives and either make them better or worse, depending on whether it likes them or not, with no regard to human life.\u201d I gave them the full description that Dr. Hazard had given me.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s magical...\u201d Liz looked at me goddamn wide eyed.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cSo maybe Angela should stay the hell away from Special Collections.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shook his head ruefully. \u201cSomehow I have no doubt that it would decide to attach itself to Angela.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAngela does have a very powerful soul,\u201d Liz put out there. \u201cShe is a very skilled magician. Almost as skilled as Cassandra, even without training. And a reasonably strong psychic, though not as strong as Dr. Cross.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat does seem likely to draw the attention of such a spirit,\u201d Billy Mack agreed.<br /> <br /> Liz looked thoughtful. \u201cI definitely want to keep her as a long term asset, even after she graduates, as she will accomplish a lot. She does have a reckless fascination with darkness, which will need to be kept in check, but also helps with keeping her in bed.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack grinned at her. \u201cJust make sure she doesn\u2019t find another source of darkness more enticing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWill do.\u201d Liz tapped the side of her glass with a long fingernail. \u201cI\u2019m keeping a close eye on her and so is Am. I mean, Am is her closest friend, and feels guilty about spying on her, but she understands it is in Angela\u2019s best interests, since she knows Angela really could have been tainted by the Room and we might have had to put her down.\u201d She paused. \u201cI do have one question that Cassandra had, that I said I would pass along because I wasn\u2019t sure of the professional ethics of it all...\u201d She looked at me questioningly. <br /> <br /> \u201cShoot.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWould it be possible for us to find out who Henry has hired and possibly make their lives a little difficult, strictly in terms of the job?\u201d She looked goddamn hopeful.<br /> <br /> I thought for a moment. \u201cCountersurveillance type stuff? Sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIn this case it also crosses into defending our assets as well,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is a pretty powerful psychic who gets visions of the future and visions of threat to people she cares about...\u201d Liz played up the angle.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cAlso, it could spill over into messing with Cassandra.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised my hands. \u201cLook, no need to convert me, I said sure. For starters, how about I figure out what they know, how they\u2019re looking into her, and what kinds of freedom she does have? Then, depending, we\u2019ll see what needs to be done to get in the way. If he\u2019s hired a bunch of sleazebags, fuck \u2018em.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlright. I don\u2019t want to put too much on our plate...\u201d Liz had on at least her third best pout.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cWell, if this goes well, and I don\u2019t get emergency signals back from Esha, our plate gets a lot clearer after today. It\u2019s fine, doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> Something occurred to me that I wanted to make sure everyone was on board with, so I changed the subject back a little. \u201cSo, if we wind up representing Miranda, we will be tying the agency to the Asburys in the eyes of a group of people for whom that has some fucking meaning.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs a client.\u201d Billy Mack shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s true, I just wanted to make sure we\u2019re OK with that. I don\u2019t have a problem with it, obviously.\u201d I grinned.<br /> <br /> <br /> We stuck around for the rest of the evening. I got a text from Esha a little before closing. \u2018They\u2019ve been brought in. I\u2019m not in danger anymore, they say, and they\u2019ll let me know if they learn something I need to know. I dunno the plan.\u2019<br /> <br /> I frowned at the screen. \u2018Anymore? They do acknowledge that there was a problem?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Yes.\u2019 She replied quickly, then another after a pause. \u2018It was weird and I think I should let you know. They called the police and had them arrested, but the officers brought them to Blue Sun, not to the station.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018Your bosses have some pull in city hall then. Good they\u2019re on our side, right?\u2019 I smirked. No harm in injecting a little more fucking discomfort there.<br /> <br /> \u2018I guess? It scares me a little, to be honest with you. But I guess I\u2019ll go on home now?\u2019<br /> <br /> This was definitely leverage we could use later. \u2018Feel free to let me know if you feel unsafe. But it does sound like they\u2019ve got it handled, at least. Which is good for you. I\u2019m sure there\u2019s some kind of non-sinister explanation for it all.\u2019<br /> <br /> Near closing time, Tar and Heroin showed up. They lingered over their meal until everyone but us and Kat had left, at which point I made introductions, using Heroin\u2019s less street name. I looked to Kat. \u201cYou still want us to wait outside? It\u2019s your call, doll.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey can be in here, that\u2019s fine.\u201d Heroin shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cUm...\u201d Kat eyed Tar. \u201cIf everybody else would be outside, that would be good.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tar crossed his fucking arms. \u201cWell I\u2019m not moving.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heroin started stroking his head, and he leaned towards her almost subconsciously. \u201cWould you go outside please?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah...\u201d he said with a goddamn dopey grin starting to show before he noticed we were still in the room and started to glower again. Heroin gently turned his head so that he was facing the door, then gave him a gentle push. I followed along behind him, and the others with me.<br /> <br /> As we were leaving, I could hear Heroin ask Kat in not very good Thai, \u201cIs Thai OK?\u201d<br /> <br /> Kat, in much better Thai, responded. \u201cYes, this is fine.\u201d <br /> <br /> Once we got outside, Tar started patting his fucking pockets, then looked inside, frowning and thinking. He looked to us. \u201cI left my smokes in there, d\u2019you think...?\u201d I offered him a pill and a light. \u201cOh. Thank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked somewhat more contented as he smoked. I wasn\u2019t, cause Billy Mack lit up one of his foul smelling cigars, but what can you do?<br /> <br /> The conversation seemed to be going well. The tension faded fucking quickly, especially clear once they got out smart phones and touched them together. They seemed to be negotiating after a while, looking like they were up to something, and I got curious, so I turned on my Mind Reading. I flipped a coin, and went looking into Kat\u2019s surface thoughts for starters.<br /> <br /> From the sound of her surface thoughts, Kat was hiring Heroin to do two things: for starters, she wanted her to look into a group of Thai fuckers that she thought might be hunters. I was a bit put out that she didn\u2019t ask us, but then I realized that for one, she didn\u2019t know we could read Thai, and two, she thought we didn\u2019t know she was a vampire. In addition, Heroin had tempted Kat with stories of hard to acquire and goddamn expensive spices that the Changeling could steal with no one noticing any went missing. So, Kat was promising to purchase any of these spices that she brought in, at a reasonable price.<br /> <br /> I turned to the others with a smirk. \u201cI think we\u2019ve done a good thing here, making friends like this.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, my mind powers aren\u2019t working yet, they haven\u2019t kissed.\u201d Liz grinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust wait,\u201d Tar rumbled.<br /> <br /> After a while, not too long, Heroin came over to the door and beckoned us in. \u201cYou guys can come in, where it\u2019s warm, and, you know, not raining.\u201d <br /> <br /> Tar stopped to put his cigarette out before coming in. He looked over at Liz, who still had hers lit. \u201cNo smoking indoors.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you\u2019re a criminal enforcer that doesn\u2019t want people to smoke indoors?\u201d Liz raised a goddamn eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll enforce not smoking indoors.\u201d He glowered at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cFine!\u201d She rolled her eyes.<br /> <br /> The ladies were still conversing in Thai. Heroin was clearly not the master of the language that Kat was, which was obvious both by how Kat had to repeat herself a few times, and how many double entendres Kat managed to work in. Technically, you could say Heroin wasn\u2019t flirting back, she just smiled a lot whenever she caught one of them.<br /> <br /> I smiled at both of them in a lull of the conversation. \u201cI\u2019m glad things got worked out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Kat smiled back at me. \u201cYes, this was actually very productive.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood.\u201d Billy Mack nodded at the two of them.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s going to help me with a couple of things with some Thai that have entered the area. Probably nothing, but something I would want a native speaker for.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, I\u2019m not a native speaker,\u201d Heroin protested.<br /> <br /> Kat laughed brightly. \u201cOh but you fooled me! Your Thai is so good. You make it sound quite beautiful.\u201d Heroin smiled at her, not fooled a goddamn bit. I smirked. Kat turned to me. \u201cThank you for your help in resolving this. You should definitely come visit often - you will find that your discount continues anytime you come here to enjoy a pie.\u201d<br /> <br /> Heroin smirked at me. \u201cComing here to enjoy a pie just moved up on my to-do list.\u201d Tar sighed. \u201cOh come on sweetie.\u201d She reached over to pet Tar. He leaned into her hand.<br /> <br /> We split up after that - I went to Miranda\u2019s, Naomi to campus to be on watch and feed her addiction to Am, Kilroy to... whatever the hell he had planned and Jack to check over the campus for those other bits of Infrastructure. After a short whispered conversation, Tar rode off alone on the motorcycle, while Heroin hitched a ride with Kat. It's always good to leave the world a little brighter. Or something...<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Clytemnestra\u2019s Yarns</b><br /> <br /> <b>A Night at the Pagan Club</b><br /> <br /> The Spider entered the Pagan Club\u2019s main room, and plopped down on the couch. She was wearing the face of Naomi Cruz, infamous Latina artist. It did not stop others of the Pagan Club from recognizing her, however. <br /> <br /> \u201cHow did it go?\u201d Cassandra Bale approached her master. <br /> <br /> \u201cOur last case? Perhaps too well. Two beautiful women are making beautiful music together right now. \u201c The Spider shrugged. <br /> <br /> \u201cKathryn.\u201d The Witch specified.<br /> <br /> \u201cHenry came by the office to threaten Cec\u00edlia. Jack and Billy Mack sent him packing.\u201d The artist shrugged. <br /> <br /> \u201cDid you pass on my request?\u201d Cassandra\u2019s intense gaze fell on her master.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah.\u201d The pink haired girl leaned back. \u201cOf course Gabe is willing to help. She has ethics to consider, but she will make some enquiries. Mainly to see how safe it is for you two to talk online. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. I don\u2019t want this to cost her career.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBe careful, but I have my ways. If the worst happens, then I will intervene. Try not to drain my power.\u201d Naomi looked uncharacteristically serious, but those who knew Elizabeth Covington would recognize the expression.<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you Master. You will not regret it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood. Are you holding up okay, Cassandra?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell enough. Worried Dr. Frankenstein knows something.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Spider turned, \u201cWe will deal with him as necessary. I require Amsterdam to feed. I will stay here with her tonight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cassandra Bale bowed and left the room. A few minutes later, China \u201cAmsterdam\u201d Garcetti arrived. She wore a white robe and her feet were bare. The Spider rose, now in her full glory. She glowed, and golden legs set down on the floor. Except one, which used to draw Am to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy sweet. Welcome.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am this world\u2019s gift to you.\u201d Amsterdam smiled. Rarely in her life had she felt such purpose before she met Clytemnestra. Now it was common and bolstering. She smiled and closed her eyes as she felt the first bite, golden fangs sinking into her throat.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> China Garcetti opened her eyes. She felt woozy, but her Goddess\u2019s love, in the form of a glowing aura, had kept her alive. Clytemnestra shifted in the bedroom, golden legs tapping the floor. <br /> <br /> \u201cThank you master. I hope you enjoyed your dinner and dessert.\u201d She smiled at her master. Clytemnestra smiled back. \u201cAs always, you were wonderful, Amsterdam.\u201d The Spider chuckled good-naturedly. <br /> <br /> \u201cBoss?\u201d A knock on the door. It was Angela Wilcox, Amsterdam\u2019s best friend. <br /> <br /> \u201cEnter.\u201d<br /> <br /> The young witch entered, and saw her friend sitting naked on the bed. \u201cBoss I\u2026whoa! Am, I am going to class in a few minutes and you two make me gayer by the second I I\u2026God you are gorgeous.\u201d She just stared.<br /> <br /> Clytemnestra cleared her throat.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight! Um, Boss I think Dr. Frankenstein suspects something is up with me. Heather said he was around the Dorm last night. He let himself in my room.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDid he take anything?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot that I know of. I did not have the books, and did not notice anything missing. Or moved. I would not have known had Heather not told me. Maybe because of her creepy good mood. Maybe she finally got laid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOne can only hope.\u201d Absently. The Spider tapped her chin with a golden leg.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway, I am going to be careful. He has a class now so did not know I was coming here. So\u2026\u201d Her eyes flicked between Amsterdam and Clytemnestra.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot now. I need to get to the Office. Maybe later today, if there is time. Not speaking for Amsterdam of course\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, take care Boss.\u201d And she popped out.<br /> <br /> \u201cDress.\u201d The Spider walked to wait at the doorway. When Amsterdam had her robe on, she walked out, along with Elizabeth Covington and Naomi Cruz. Elizabeth stretched like a cat, while Naomi rolled her eyes and looked at the other two women. <br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, yeah, I am not doing that again without a brace and probably ecstasy. \u201cI gotta get to class, Liz try not to get any more old on Am.\u201d And the artist walked out.<br /> <br /> Amsterdam bit her lip, a part of a special secret few knew. Liz gently put an arm around her. \u201cGot class too sweetie?\u201d The younger girl nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood.\u201d Elizabeth, and the Spider, smirked. \u201cYou are ahead of Naomi already.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVII</i><br /> <br /> Clairvoyance is a crazy power.<br /> <br /> Worth noting, Speed\u2019s player had this weird idea most of the professors looked like they were gonna eat someone\u2019s liver. Dr. Carpenter, Hazard, and Stein especially. Dr. Cross less so, nor Dr. Hargrove. I blame the insanity.<br /> <br /> Okay so there were a lot of names here. Does anyone need a reminder who is who? This game has a big cast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T20:43:01-08:00","id":1018667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=1018377#post1018377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so there were a lot of names here. Does anyone need a reminder who is who? This game has a big cast.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know in some RPGs where it lists the character portrait next to their lines? Sometimes I wish we had that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","a