":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T06:53:42-08:00","id":1018791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play?p=1018740#post1018740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's fine. You've got a big world there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T02:09:24-08:00","id":1024676,"title":"","content":"Free food, fearsome academics, a little B&amp;E and rival Mages. Step on board the Night Train.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> Billy Mack made his way to the Harvester apprentice\u2019s house, parking his Crown Vic a ways away. He shifted into Demonic form quickly, hoping to take advantage of his increased stealthiness to get through unseen and his ability to walk through goddamn walls to get in without Jack or my tricks. It worked, on both accounts, as best he could fucking tell.<br /> <br /> The house was dark and quiet and Amy was home this time, so Kilroy fanned through her potential leverage. He fucking smiled when he saw how much she cared for her students, kids and husband, but then frowned again with the rest of it. Someone had gotten there before him, some Illuminati-esque \u2018Brotherhood\u2019 that she and Cornelius, or Ernesto as she knew him, was a part of. She was terrified to move against them, was certain that they would know as soon as she did and then take it out on her family. She was also afraid of Skeevy Larry...<br /> <br /> That put an interesting angle on her attack on Nikka. He didn\u2019t find any feeling in her fears that she was moving directly against Cornelius\u2019 - Ernesto\u2019s - interests, contrary to the shit he had told us. In fact, she seemed a little afraid of him. So either it was a goddamn Brotherhood job, in which case there\u2019s no way we were putting her off Nikka; they were doing it completely on his orders; she and her group were trying to impress him; or they were trying to beat Ernesto to the kill. The last one seemed unlikely, and the first was the worst fucking case scenario. <br /> <br /> Abandoning whatever his fucking plan to leverage her family against her had been, Kilroy decided to go through her phone, tweaking reality to get into her head enough to know her password once he found it on the kitchen table. He flipped past the lock screen picture of her daughter holding their schnauzer, then spent a couple of hours going through every inch of it. He got one name, someone who had sent her a text letting her know about the meeting last night, and so was probably another of the apprentice batch. He got a bunch of other names that meant nothing yet, but he was hoping to be able to cross reference it with however we decided to look into her next. <br /> <br /> With what he could get got, he drifted with the tide and made his way back to his car before slipping back into Billy Mack and home to his RV.<br /> <br /> <br /> Jack made his way to the university. He straightened his jacket and made sure his knock-off badge was easy to get to as he got close to the campus security building. The guy in charge heard him out, as he used Authorize to request access to all of the buildings, and the privacy to look into it alone. He hemmed and fucking hawed over it for a few minutes before sighing. \u201cYou\u2019ve got the badge, so...\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cI feel ya, man, I\u2019m not here to run roughshod over you.\u201d Jack looked sympathetic. \u201cYou don\u2019t have to just give me keys, if it makes you feel better. I have to insist on being able to go through the building alone though.\u201d<br /> <br /> Another officer clapped the shoulder of the guy in charge. \u201cFBI can\u2019t be that bad. I\u2019ll go along with where I can, make sure he doesn\u2019t break any door handles.\u201d She smiled over at Jack.<br /> <br /> The lead officer rolled his fucking eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s on us if he does.\u201d He handed her a set of keys.<br /> <br /> She jerked her head towards the door and walked out, holding it for Jack. \u201cName\u2019s Daria, Daria Lopez.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJack Stone.\u201d He grinned over at her, matching her pace. \u201cSo, anything strange been going on?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSomething weird at the library,\u201d she said matter of factly, \u201cthat we aren\u2019t allowed to look into, because it will make Dr. Stein upset and if you make him upset, you get fired.\u201d She jerked her head back towards the security headquarters. \u201cA lot those folks know they\u2019re on the hook for whatever you do, and if you happen to make Stein upset... he takes things personally.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack didn\u2019t react outwardly, but made a note to bring it up later. \u201cI see. This Dr. Stein\u2019s got leverage on someone then.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cProbably.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cThe Asbury Room is weird - something happened there where we got cut off from accessing it a bit back. Not even if we heard screams, Dr. Stein said.\u201d She paused. \u201cAre you investigating Dr. Stein? Name\u2019s Norman, Norman Stein? Kids call him Dr. Frankenstein?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m aware of him.\u201d He looked fucking rueful. \u201cI cannot discuss ongoing investigations.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, those two are the big things. Was there a different kind of unusual you meant?\u201d she asked.<br /> <br /> Jack chuckled. \u201cI meant a little more... normal unusual. Previous offenders, suspicious activities, that kind of thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cThere\u2019s a cocaine operation, we think, though we can\u2019t find any hard evidence or who it is. It seems to have stepped up recently, folks coming to campus from off it to purchase it from students. We\u2019ve even stopped students we were pretty sure had some, but we couldn\u2019t find it on them.\u201d Jack looked interested. \u201cAs far as we know, that\u2019s not to do with Stein - we don\u2019t think any teachers have anything to do with it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf anything involving that turns up, I\u2019m certain it\u2019ll find its way to the local authorities for the collar.\u201d Jack gave her a smile. He looked around. \u201cAs to where we\u2019re going - any buildings with machinery, any particular concentrations of technology or mechanical infrastructure, built before the 90s, anything like that that stands out to you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe science building.\u201d She shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cSounds great.\u201d<br /> <br /> They moved quickly in the goddamn cold night air to the science building. When it looked like Daria was gearing up to stand out in the cold, chafing her arms a little, Jack shook his head and indicated the door. \u201cCome on in, just... stay near the door, alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded and moved just inside, leaning on the wall and looking much more comfortable. \u201cAlright.\u201d<br /> <br /> Daria didn\u2019t have keys to the labs or major equipment rooms, and they hadn\u2019t had time to requisition them. Still, without her following him along, if he went through the rest of the building without finding anything, a little bit of B&amp;E should have been able to get him wherever he wanted.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, he didn\u2019t have to. It took him a while to go through the whole goddamn building - it didn\u2019t help that he started on the fourth floor and made his way down - but in the basement there was an odd janitor\u2019s closet that opened up into a long hallway, one that he was certain mortals wouldn\u2019t be seeing a single tile of. He stepped back out, shifted in his electrical sight, night vision and mirrored skin and gave it a look-see.<br /> <br /> Set up near the end of the hallway were a pair of big fucking cannons and beyond them, a computer station. Running along the ceiling was a motion detector, its infrared beam wide enough to cover the whole hallway. The cannons didn\u2019t respond to his presence but he could see they still had power going to them. As best he could tell, this had been a center for coordinating a defensive response, back when the full Infrastructure had been online.<br /> <br /> His robotic eyes gave him the edge to dance around it, and he managed to get to the computers without setting triggering the alert and almost certainly getting the living shit shot out of him. Standing there in front of the computer, still in the beam\u2019s path, he wasn\u2019t much better off however. He gave it a go, regularly dodging the sweeping beam, which was a much easier task with him standing in one place and able to see it. He made some progress, but it still wasn\u2019t enough even once he hit the edges of his capabilities. So he ducked and weaved his way back out, determined to bring Kilroy back for round two.<br /> <br /> He met Daria at the entrance he left her. \u201cAny others that might fit the bill?\u201d he asked, blank faced. <br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s the engineering building. And... admin, I guess?\u201d She narrowed her eyes, thinking hard. \u201cCan\u2019t get into much there. Some of us are minorities, you know, can\u2019t be trusted walking around with the keys.\u201d She smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cEngineering first. Lead on.\u201d He bowed and smiled.<br /> <br /> He spent about an hour checking out the place and didn\u2019t find either locked doors, or Infrastructure. It was getting on dawn, but he decided to at least give the parts of the admin building he could get to a look. At least there was less goddamn ground to cover. He didn\u2019t find anything there but locked doors, unfortunately. From the labels and windows he could peek in, there were meeting rooms, offices, a nice alum lounge and an entire hallway. All in all, he probably got to less than a third of it.<br /> <br /> He gave a thought to that idea of B&amp;E he\u2019d had, but most of the places were blocked off with a fucking serious security system, one requiring two keys and a pass-code. No cannon and infrared sensors for him to Mission Impossible over here, but enough he decided to fuck back off. He went back to the security office with Daria, making sure to wipe himself from every but her\u2019s memory. He\u2019d already made sure he left no forensic evidence. He\u2019d have blocked himself from her memory as well, but he\u2019d been a bit too goddamn integral to her night. He managed to not piss her off though, so he felt alright with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I made my way back to Miranda\u2019s, letting myself in to find her sitting at her father\u2019s desk. I walked up behind her and put my arms around her. \u201cSo, how\u2019s it going?\u201d I kissed the top of her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s been rough going, but I\u2019m getting through things.\u201d She brushed her hair back from her face idly. \u201cI\u2019ll probably find it tomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAbsolutely.\u201d I pulled a chair from nearby and spun it around to sit in it backwards. \u201cBilly Mack had a thought - he\u2019s good for those sometimes - that we could save you a lot of shit and risk of exposure if we acted your, well, mystical power of attorney. Just for this matter, just for this instance.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded thoughtfully. \u201cThe trick would be... I think I\u2019m legally dead. You\u2019d have to prove that I am who I am anyway. I don\u2019t think they know I\u2019m here.\u201d<br /> <br /> My eyes widened. \u201cRight. Fuck, I hadn\u2019t thought about that. Is there any sorta proof we could offer that wouldn\u2019t leave \u2018em sure you\u2019re Scelesti?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I gave you a copy of the documentation, that might suffice, and a signed letter... still, they just might assume you stole it from the house. It might work though. I\u2019m willing to try it, so long as you have an escape clause in case they become highly suspicious. Worse case scenario, you have them call me, and I come down. I\u2019m willing to do that, for you.\u201d She smiled slightly and tapped me on the shoulder. \u201cI don\u2019t mind your friends being with you, but you would be the one representing my family.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smiled over at her. \u201cSo, just in case, I\u2019d probably wanna take it to Professor Werewolf.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cI don\u2019t know Dr. Hazard, and haven\u2019t decided to ask Gone about him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair.\u201d I smirked. \u201cWe could maybe even teleconference you in, if a Skype conversation would work for confirming who you are.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked uncertain. \u201cYou\u2019d have to set it up for me.\u201d She paused. \u201cI am willing to go in. If it\u2019s only Dr. Hazard... it would be regrettable to eviscerate him in a sorcerer's duel, but if he insists on causing a problem, I will crush him like an insect.\u201d She thought for a moment. \u201cOr I could key it up so that any magic would cause a backlash, and once that happens to him a time or two, he might be willing to talk like civilized people.<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cThat\u2019s fair, and certainly two of the ways it\u2019d go down, but I\u2019d rather it not come to that. How about we meet with Dr. Carpenter, he vouches you\u2019re alive, you never have to risk being around Dr. Hazard...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat works.\u201d She bit her lip. \u201cI don\u2019t know how strong the Diamond Orders are here, and I don\u2019t know how connected he is. A Seer would be the only guaranteed problem...\u201d She drew a sigil on a scrap of paper at the desk. Nothing I\u2019d seen before, on Hazard or anywhere else. \u201cDid he have anything like this on him?\u201d I shook my head. \u201cOK, he\u2019s not definitely a Seer then.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell that\u2019s good.\u201d I stood up and stretched. \u201cTea?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled up at me. \u201cTea would be wonderful.\u201d I hadn\u2019t had much occasion to know anything about that before, but it had grown on me. Especially when I put a little whiskey in it. Hey, she needed to relax, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> When Billy Mack woke up in his RV, he got a weird feeling. He looked carefully and quietly around his bed area, moving as little as fucking possible. When he figured out no one was actually lingering around, he gave things a closer once over. The place had been tossed. Not roughly, like that word usually implies. These fuckers had tried to keep it on the down low. But not well enough - the g-man\u2019s cell phone had been moved, a few of his things left out of place, his cushions slightly askew and his glove compartment hadn\u2019t quite closed properly.<br /> <br /> He searched both his vehicles for trackers and found one on both of them, the RV and the Crown Vic, stuck up under the carriage. He checked his phone for tampering, and didn\u2019t find anything. Still, he pulled out Vivian\u2019s laptop and sent us all a message. \u2018I appear to have been compromised.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018I hope it was sexy.\u2019 Liz\u2019s responses were quick. \u2018Every time I get compromised it is.\u2019<br /> <br /> I rolled my eyes. \u2018By who?\u2019 <br /> <br /> Jack\u2019s response was shorter. \u2018Capital C?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018The Brotherhood.\u2019 As usual, Billy Mack was cryptic as shit. Still, unless he\u2019d come up with a particularly odd nickname all of the sudden, it meant it wasn\u2019t the God-Machine, so there was that. \u2018Not sure if watched, tracking device on car and RV.\u2019<br /> <br /> I gave Miranda a quick kiss as I grabbed my jacket. \u201cGotta jet sweetheart. Talk to you later.\u201d I burned fucking rubber to get to where I knew Billy Mack parked his RV and did a quick sweep, not finding any peepers. There were people around, but no one that seemed out of place. Once I was sure of it, I drove to the nearest Starbucks, keeping an eye out on the way, and sent a message to Billy Mack, \u2018Starbucks.\u2019<br /> <br /> Billy Mack sent a message back. \u2018The good one, or the one across the street that\u2019s not as good?\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018The close one.\u2019<br /> <br /> Billy Mack closed the curtains and shifted states into Vivian, activating Data Form as she sent me the message, \u2018Go into the bathroom.\u2019 Once I sent her a confirmation, she slipped through my phone and popped up there.<br /> <br /> \u201cConvenient.\u201d I nodded to her. I grabbed the fucking coffees on the way out, handing one to Vivian.<br /> <br /> <br /> I took a goddamn roundabout route home, still making it there about the time Jack did. Liz was already there. Once we got in, I gestured the other two up to the lab. Jack looked questioningly at Vivian as she got the coffee machine started. \u201cMakes less waves if she shows up in a Starbucks bathroom.\u201d I turned to Vivian myself. \u201cSo... the fuck?\u201d <br /> <br /> Liz chuckled. \u201cIf I may, before we get into everything Billy Mack has to tell us about being compromised, this morning, after I was compromised three times, Angela came in - apparently Dr. Stein went into her room while she was gone, and looked through it. Heather told her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cStein has some leverage on somebody,\u201d Jack let us know, filling us in on the shit that the security guard had told him. \u201cShe really could not stand the guy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe doesn\u2019t seem to be the friend maker.\u201d Liz smirked.<br /> <br /> Jack frowned. \u201cHe\u2019s got enough power to get away with it, which is the problem.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cThere is clearly something to him we haven\u2019t uncovered yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe certainly seems to have gone a long way from when he worked at the morgue.\u201d Liz lit her cigarette. \u201cAnyway, Angela wasn\u2019t sure what he was looking for, and didn\u2019t notice anything missing. She\u2019s guessing he was looking for the books.\u201d <br /> <br /> I made a face. \u201cWhy the fuck would she report them stolen then? She\u2019s the only reason the theft was discovered so early.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cAnd he thinks she\u2019s dumb enough to stash them in her room?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is a witch.\u201d Liz shrugged. \u201cRegardless, he was in her room while she wasn\u2019t. Heather was gonna go fuck with him, but apparently she was still sated from before, so she decided to just make a note of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat would be fascinating.\u201d Vivian had a far off look in her eyes. \u201cI can\u2019t say for certain who would win that fight, but it would be fascinating. We have seen him being shot in the head, and clear evidence of her biting someone in half. It would certainly be a spectacle, though I imagine, much like Godzilla vs any number of mechanical beasts, it would probably level most of Tokyo, or in this case, Seattle.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack snorted. \u201cBut that\u2019s where I keep my stuff.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz shook her head. \u201cI\u2019m not sure that\u2019s the scale Heather works on.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, just the university then?\u201d I offered. <br /> <br /> \u201cOr perhaps the building they are in, at least.\u201d Vivian shrugged. \u201cIt is peculiar, but not entirely out of the ordinary for him to check up on her in this library matter.\u201d<br /> <br /> I spun around in my chair. It didn\u2019t seem to add up, to me, that he\u2019d go looking for the books in the dorm room of the person who reported them stolen. \u201cI guess... he might think she didn\u2019t know that she took them. I mean, she didn\u2019t seem to be fully driving that train in the Asbury Room situation.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian nodded. \u201cShe does also have a reputation for not leaving well enough alone, so he might have been looking for anything she may have dug up.\u201d She took a sip of her coffee. \u201cAt any rate, I found some very interesting things in Mrs. Sandoval\u2019s mind.\u201d She gave us the rundown of the Harvester\u2019s fears, including her knowledge of Skeevy Larry, Cornelius\u2019 other name and some nearly-fucking-derisive praise for possessing the level of human decency she\u2019d expected. <br /> <br /> \u201cHuh.\u201d Liz shook her head. \u201cWell, that\u2019s an organization I would certainly join, one that might murder me...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, it does mean you can be certain other people in it won\u2019t betray you, at least.\u201d I raised an eyebrow at her. She shrugged. \u201cJust saying, there are some fucking upsides, so long as you don\u2019t plan on betraying them.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked at me. \u201cI suppose I do occasionally get involved with people I don\u2019t intend to betray.\u201d<br /> <br /> Vivian continued on. \u201cShe is quite convinced that the Brotherhood would know immediately if she ever turned on them, so I gave up on attempting to try to turn her against the local head of the Brotherhood and did not make contact with her. I did go through her phone - I collected some potentially useful information, but took the time to do a thorough search. And when I woke up this morning, someone had clearly been through my RV, and I did find a fairly standard GPS tracker on both the Crown Vic and the RV. Billy Mack\u2019s phone did not appear to be tampered with., though it was moved.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow light a sleeper are you?\u201d Liz asked.<br /> <br /> \u201cAverage.\u201d Vivian shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo it\u2019s not particularly odd that you stayed asleep, it wouldn\u2019t require some sort of power to do so?\u201d she elaborated.<br /> <br /> Vivian shook her head. \u201cI can\u2019t be certain, but I\u2019m not a light enough sleeper to discount the possibility that someone at least practiced in stealth could have snuck around. I did spend a couple of hours in the Sandoval home without waking any of them up.\u201d She sighed. \u201cThough perhaps I do need to find a way around this sleep thing. It is certainly proving to be inconvenient.\u201d<br /> <br /> Liz fucking smirked. \u201cI suggest you always make sure to have some else there. It\u2019s what I do.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled. \u201cSo, you\u2019ll be spending some time as Vivian?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey have not seen Vivian, and despite the fact she lives out of that RV, it is under Billy Mack\u2019s name. They should have no reason to connect it to her. There\u2019s nothing in Billy Mack\u2019s phone to tie them together either.\u201d She paused. \u201cThey should be able to find that Billy Mack works for this agency however, and if they tracked me back from the house, they likely saw me in Demon form.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is the house that has the advanced wards against spirits in it?\u201d Liz asked.<br /> <br /> I nodded thoughtfully. \u201cWe might wanna take a visit to Whacko Bob\u2019s, see who\u2019s been buying shit like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack\u2019s eyes lit up. \u201cAnd maybe also figure out how to make the wards ourselves.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt seemed a fairly standard hedge magic. I imagine Miranda could construct a much better one.\u201d Vivian raised an eyebrow at me.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cSpeaking of magic, Miranda\u2019s still looking for that contract. She\u2019s fairly certain she\u2019ll find it this afternoon. The plan we sorta settled on last night has me with the mystical power of attorney thing, once Miranda confirms to Dr. Carpenter that she\u2019s alive and is giving me the authority.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack nodded. \u201cSounds good. On the topic of the university, a few things...\u201d He turned to Liz. \u201cAre you dealing cocaine out of the university?\u201d She shook her head. \u201cSomeone is, and it\u2019s apparently getting to be a problem. Large quantities, that they can never catch anyone with.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCause it\u2019s in the cell phones. In the cases, really. At least Nick\u2019s is.\u201d Liz waved her hand airily. \u201cI dunno if she bought it, or if she\u2019s dealing it. Naomi doesn't do cocaine, so I don't know any details.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHrm. I would get some pull with the local security if I could get Daria the tip on that. But...\u201d He looked goddamn questioningly at Liz.<br /> <br /> She frowned. \u201cI would prefer Nick not get sold up the river. Sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cNo worries. I did find a seriously defended piece of Infrastructure, he