school, to keep them from falling into the wrong hands. So I have a rather vested interest in the situation.\u201d Right about then, Miranda showed up and walked over to us. His eyes got fucking wide. \u201cAh! Good lord...\u201d She smiled at him. \u201cThe years have been kind.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smirked. Miranda slid into the seat beside me, placing a hand on my arm. \u201cI suppose they have.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked her over. \u201cSo how long has it been? 30, 40...?\u201d<br /> <br /> She waved her other hand. \u201cBest not to worry about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you are not upset about the...\u201d he trailed off.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, but I am, but it\u2019s not quite your fault, is it?\u201d There was enough of a purr in her tone that I had to stop myself from getting jealous. \u201cI just want the books found, and I\u2019m empowering Ms Norton to help me with that. She will be my advocate here. I don\u2019t want any wrinkles due to my appearance or presence, so it seems easiest if I don\u2019t have to make too many personal appearances.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded, still eying her. \u201cIt is good of you to show up, I had no idea you were still alive. Your house has been empty for some time.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked to the side. \u201cYes, well, things happened.\u201d<br /> <br /> He took the hint and addressed all of us. \u201cAt this time, we don\u2019t have any information other than whoever took them knew where they were, but not precisely how to get to them. Dr. Hazard believes it\u2019s imperative Dr. Stein knows nothing of the books whatsoever. However, he stumbled upon their existence very quickly, and has been attempting to commandeer any investigations. He appears to have the ear of the provost on this matter. Certainly the library director.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cHow many books are missing?\u201d I asked.<br /> <br /> \u201c8.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWould it be possible to know the titles?\u201d It was a stretch, but it might have been useful. He made several unhappy faces. I held my hands up. \u201cNot pushing there. My only thought was to see if there were any patterns in what was stolen, anything that might indicate what the thief wanted them for.\u201d<br /> <br /> He frowned. \u201cIf necessary. Lady Asbury is a surviving member of an alumni bloodline, so that information cannot be withheld from her representative. It was the entire collection that was taken however.\u201d<br /> <br /> I frowned as well. \u201cSo no help there anyway. Ah well.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA number of them, but not all, had to do with spirits and spiritual entities and what kind of pacts you can make.\u201d He sighed. \u201cThose are the ones I was tasked to keep watch over. They would allow a relatively inexperienced summoner call upon things they did not have the wherewithal to control, unfortunately.\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cTitles would be helpful to check if they\u2019ve been sold,\u201d Jack put out there. <br /> <br /> Dr. Carpenter nodded. \u201cI know Dr. Hazard has been looking into that.\u201d He glanced at Miranda. \u201cOn that note - he and I are united against Dr. Stein.\u201d He paused. \u201cMy loyalties do not lie with him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course they don\u2019t dear.\u201d Miranda smiled. \u201cI know precisely where your loyalties lie.\u201d Yep, definite fucking spike of jealousy there. It helped that her hand stayed on my arm. \u201cI appreciate your understanding in this matter. Do keep us apprised, and work with Ms. Norton whenever possible. She is a very skilled investigator with some unique advantages. And at the end of the day, the most important thing is to get those books back to where they were, or to a place Dr. Stein will not find them.\u201d She frowned slightly. \u201cI do not like the idea of my book being found by someone who will keep it from me. I don\u2019t like being kept from my books, you understand.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI understand fully.\u201d He smiled.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cAs unfortunate as it will be to cut this reunion short, I believe that with the heightened state of alert from both Dr. Stein and Dr. Hazard, it would be best if I left for now. We can talk some other time, of course. Ms. Norton can arrange a meeting if needed.\u201d She gave me a kiss on the cheek and headed out.<br /> <br /> He watched her go. \u201cSorry I couldn\u2019t be more help to you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot a problem. It\u2019ll just be nice not to get fucking stonewalled at every turn.\u201d I smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cThese books, as she wells knows, are very dangerous. If the person who took them is knowledgeable, the books will provide some dangerous resources. If they aren\u2019t, then it\u2019s actually worse.\u201d His brow knit. \u201cI have to get to my office hours.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry to keep you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo problem. Pleasure to meet you.\u201d He shook our hands and handed me a card. As he left the table, I gestured to Liz to cut the no eavesdropping field. With any luck, Louise\u2019d pin it on the werewolf. I started a completely innocuous conversation, stopping the boys from saying anything until we were back in the car headed to the office.<br /> <br /> In the car, Liz looked at me, somewhat concerned. \u201cHe wants to find the books. He wants to know what Dr. Hazard and Dr. Stein\u2019s deals are and why they dislike each other. He also wants to mate with the goddess of the moon.\u201d<br /> <br /> I raised an eyebrow, but Jack responded first. \u201cI was with you til that last one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don't think he\u2019s in love with Miranda.\u201d That made her bringing it all up make more sense. \u201cI think there is something between them, but love might be taking it a little far.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cThere was definitely some goddamn history there.\u201d<br /> <br /> She made a face. \u201cI didn\u2019t use it on Miranda, just him, so I can\u2019t say for sure what she was thinking. But he didn\u2019t have any designs on wooing her back or anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s alright doll.\u201d I winked at her and gunned it for the office. \u201cGood to know I won\u2019t need to punch a werewolf. He seemed alright.\u201d <br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVIII</i><br /> <br /> I\u2019d love to tell you I made up the Hadron Collider thing and that it is not a real conspiracy theory. Sadly, I would be wrong.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think much here requires much clarification. I asked Kilroy\u2019s player if he was going to stay the time it took to go through the Bulk of Amy\u2019s email and such, and that gave her back up time to arrive and do most of what they wanted or needed.<br /> <br /> Man, there is a lot with that school, isn\u2019t there?<br /> <br /> Okay, so tonight is New Years Eve. We will mostly be at parties or with families that night, so no game. Won\u2019t have a chance to make it up but this signifies the end of the holiday season so hopefully, unless there is snow, we won\u2019t miss more sessions until summer vacation time at earliest. I am going to try to get something, maybe a story up in two weeks, but it depends on my time, player\u2019s time, etc. Worst case it will be stats for a character or two. We will see. <br /> <br /> Hope folks are enjoying the game. Comments and Questions welcome. Happy New Year.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T16:09:55-08:00","id":1024934,"title":"","content":"Happy New Year everyone; let 2017 be an improvement, or at least not more of a backslide than 2016 proved to be.<br /> <br /> Schools are a fun place to host supernatural events. It has regular attendees but few that actually live there, unless it has dorms; plenty of places for students to be selling, dealing or buying illicit or dangerous goods; just as many teachers who could become mentors or informants with unusual traits from their own pasts; and even more chances for youth to make stupid mistakes the players need to address...or cause. Plus, there's something about protecting youth that makes them more immediately pertinent to protecting, though this needs to be done well lest they become grating to deal with.<br /> <br /> As always, very much enjoying the game. I love how realistically busy the characters are, and how well they're balancing everything that's going on around them. It feels like they're juggling all the cases at once, rather than placing plotlines around them and picking them up when they come near. There's merit to both methods, but the former tends to be more dynamic than the latter (if more stressful for the GM and the players).<br /> <br /> Also, can I say that Gabe/Speed and Miranda make the cutest couple?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T00:38:07-08:00","id":1025022,"title":"","content":"Indeed. <br /> <br /> Yeah my University game is slowly coming along. Looking like I may use a generic system for it and custom create the world. Still not sure. If I don't use WoD I will at least put a link somewhere.<br /> <br /> Well I actually do better with the latter than the former as a GM, and the players hold up pretty well. My games are dynamic, will give them that.<br /> <br /> Gabe and Miranda are pretty cute, aren't they!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" a