(Rebellious/Selfish)<br /> Incarnation: Messenger<br /> Agenda: Tempter<br /> Place of Arrival: Olympia, Washington, USA<br /> <br /> Intelligence: 2<br /> Wits: 4<br /> Resolve: 3<br /> <br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 4<br /> Stamina: 3<br /> <br /> Presence: 5<br /> Manipulation: 6<br /> Composure: 3<br /> <br /> Academics: 1<br /> Computer: 1<br /> Crafts: 1<br /> Investigation: 1<br /> Medicine: 2<br /> Occult: 1<br /> Politics: 2 [Asset]<br /> Science: 0 <br /> <br /> Athletics: 2 (Climbing)<br /> Brawl: 2 (Grappling)<br /> Drive: 0<br /> Firearms: 0<br /> Larceny: 2<br /> Stealth: 2<br /> Survival: 0<br /> Weaponry: 0<br /> <br /> Animal Ken: 0<br /> Empathy: 3<br /> Expression: 4<br /> Intimidation: 1<br /> Persuasion: 4 (Seduction, Vice) [Asset]<br /> Socialize: 4 (Clubs, Dancing) [Asset]<br /> Streetwise: 1 (Drugs)<br /> Subterfuge: 2<br /> <br /> Across a Crowded Room, Alibi, Ambush, Heart's Desire, Idle Conversation, Marco Polo, Muse, Occam\u2019s Razor, Quick Change, Read Hostility, Shift Consequence, Social Dynamics, Vox, Wave Function Collapse<br /> <br /> Addictive Presence, Four Minutes Ago, Halo, Raise Dead, Sermon, Swarm<br /> <br /> Kiss of Death<br /> Welcome to My Parlor<br /> What A Tangled Web<br /> <br /> Demon Form:<br /> Modifications: Claws and Fangs, Low Density, Night Vision, Olfactory Enhancers, Sonic Acuity<br /> Technologies: Acid Spit, Adhesive, Essence Drain, Inhuman Beauty<br /> Propulsion: Long Limbs, Tether<br /> Processes: Extra Mechanical Limbs, Insect Swarm<br /> <br /> Primum: 6<br /> Willpower: 6<br /> Cover: 7 (Liz)<br /> Cover: 6 (Naomi)<br /> Health: 8<br /> Aether: 15<br /> Size: 5<br /> Defense: 6/9<br /> Initiative: 6<br /> Speed 11/16<br /> <br /> Contacts: (Socialite) 2<br /> Cult 4<br /> Cult 1<br /> Living the Lie 1<br /> Resources 4<br /> Professional: Socialite 5<br /> Pusher 1<br /> Striking Looks 2 (4)<br /> Style: Terrifying Form 4<br /> Suborned Infrastructure 3<br /> Sympathetic 1<br /> <br /> <br /> Cipher<br /> <br /> Key 1: Heart's Desire<br /> <br /> Key 2: Ambush<br /> <br /> Interlock: Kiss of Death<br /> <br /> The allure of the black widow is powerful and deadly, often causing her prey to watch in helpless fascination as she closes in for the kill. <br /> <br /> This Interlock effects a single target, which must be able to see Clytemnestra. If the target of this power is engaged in active combat Clytemnestra's roll is at -3.<br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Intimidation \u2013 Composure + Power Stat<br /> <br /> Cost: 1 Aether<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: The target's fear of Clytemnestra causes them to defend more vigorously. Their defense against Clytemnestra's attacks is +3 until the end of the scene and she cannot use this power against them again. <br /> <br /> Failure: The target is able to defend normally.<br /> <br /> Success: Target loses their defense against Clytemnestra's next attack as per a successful surprise attack.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Clytemnestra's next attack against the target is a killing blow<br /> <br /> Key 3: Read Hostility<br /> <br /> Interlock: Welcome to my Parlor<br /> <br /> A spider has an instinctive awareness of webs even those she did not make herself. Clytemnestra can sense traps and alarms within her field of vision. <br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Wits + Larceny<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Clytemnestra receives one or more false readings from safe places/items. <br /> <br /> Failure: Clytemnestra detects nothing<br /> <br /> Success: Clytemnestra becomes aware of all physical triggers (tripwires, pressure plates, motion sensors and the like) within her field of vision. Most can be avoided freely, and any rolls to pass without setting one off they are made with a bonus equal to her Primum <br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: As above. In addition, Clytemnestra can sense and avoid magical traps and alarms in the area as well.<br /> <br /> Key 4: Social Dynamics<br /> <br /> Interlock: What a Tangled Web<br /> <br /> Any demon with Social Dynamics can see the web of connections between the members of a group, but with this interlock Clytemnestra can weave and change those threads to suit her needs. She can modify the thread between any two individuals in her presence. This power works within the same perimeters as Social Dynamics, an executive will still be her secretary's boss but this power could make them view each other as equal partners and friends (or any other possible work relationship). <br /> <br /> This power can add threads that did not previously exist, temporarily adding someone to a social web though it does not edit memories so there is a potential risk of compromise if the change is too extreme. <br /> <br /> The changes wrought by this power are only as permanent as most social interactions. The altered threads will always hold for at least a scene and then in most cases will begin to drift back to normal based on the individuals in question. Depending on the people involved and their reactions to the experience the changes may last longer or lead to lingering alterations in the dynamic. <br /> <br /> Dice Pool: Presence + Socialize<br /> <br /> Dramatic Failure: Clytemnestra losses sight of the social webs entirely. Any changes made previously remain in effect but she loses any bonuses to social rolls from Social Dynamics and cannot attempt to use What A Tangled Web on this group again for the rest of the scene. <br /> <br /> Failure: Clytemnestra is unable to pluck the thread properly. She may roll again at a cumulative penalty of -1 per attempt beyond the first.<br /> <br /> Success: Clytemnestra's power alters the social connection as Clytemnestra wishes. While some long term effects are possible depending on what behavior the new dynamic brought to the surface established relationships will tend to normalize after the effect is over.<br /> <br /> Exceptional Success: Clytemnestra may alter a number threads equal to her Primum at once with this activation of the power. <br /> <br /> Quote: <i>\u201cOh Darling, you look good enough to eat!\u201d<br /> </i><br /> --<br /> <br /> Should be a session tonight, so I will see you in two weeks with a story update. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T19:10:48-08:00","id":1031919,"title":"","content":"Kinda surprised at Speed's other Covers - we only ever see Gabe, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T02:02:44-08:00","id":1032048,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Glen is a more throwaway/risky business cover - we had an awesome plan for using him when we were thinking of taking on the Waterwheel again, but that got trashed, sadly. Maybe we'll get to use it at some other point though. :-D Greg is fairly new. I got to bring him out a little this session, and he'll have some more stuff to do next session. Gabe's pretty set on him being completely separate from the Agency, just in case, so he has less... action on screen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1471-levinserra","name":"LevinSerra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1471_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T01:28:42-08:00","id":1039883,"title":"","content":"We are back! <br /> <br /> <i>Session LIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Speed Demon\u2019s Monologues</b><br /> <br /> To make timing work out, we split up for various bits of business. I shifted over into Greg and he finished up some business and visited the theatre site. It took him a few hours to get everything out of the bolthole, but Clytemnestra\u2019s webbed up bundles made it much easier to schlep around. He didn\u2019t really have the time to put shit together, but everything was safely stashed away, and there was room in my bolthole for the other Infrastructure we were about to scavenge. He also grabbed a spare door left over in the props room, to help keep things secure in the fucking science building.<br /> <br /> While he was doing that, Jack talked to some of his pals and zeroed in on a name for the gee who was following Dr. Cross. It was one Francisco Guzman, a PI who specialized in divorce cases. Pretty unslimy, for his type. Not likely to manufacture evidence, so as long as Cross was careful, she should be alright. He wasn\u2019t strong on the modern technological end of bugging, more old school, but even so, they asked her to stop by so they could check her cell phone. Not that they fucking told her that.<br /> <br /> As soon as she walked in, Jack held a hand out. \u201cCan I see your phone?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMay I ask why first?\u201d She looked down at his hand and back to him, not getting out her phone.<br /> <br /> \u201cI promise I\u2019ll give it back, and explain after I\u2019ve checked something.\u201d Jack took out a piece of paper and wrote the word \u2018BUG\u2019 on it.<br /> <br /> She gave him a look, carefully considering him. Probably reading his surface thoughts, if I had to guess. After a moment, she handed it over slowly, still goddamn suspicious. Jack handed it over to Billy Mack who went over it. There were definitely no mechanical bugs, and nothing in her apps stood out. He handed it back. \u201cThanks.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack smiled. \u201cSorry about that. We did some looking and found the PI your husband hired, and he\u2019s pretty big into bugs. You seem clean though. Your apartment is most likely not.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t meet her there, or talk to her. Would it be better for my case if he just found nothing?\u201d She asked hesitantly.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cIndeed. Now that you know about the bugs, so long as you are comfortable, it would make sense to allow him to gather untainted evidence that points to no wrongdoing. He is likely also following you.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded sadly. \u201cI figured. That\u2019s why I haven\u2019t really been meeting her at all.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat is most likely the wisest course of action.\u201d Billy Mack showed her the picture. \u201cThis is the man your husband has hired, in case you see him around. Francisco Guzman.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI haven\u2019t seen him around yet...\u201d She gave the picture a good look.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack set the picture down. \u201cHe is not very tech savvy, so he is not likely to have hacked into your digital communications. Do be careful of any new Facebook friends, or the like.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled slightly. \u201cI mostly use Snapchat. I don\u2019t know much about it, she introduced me to it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf I might ask - your husband\u2019s suspicions... did he come into possession of any evidence or proof himself?\u201d Billy Mack asked gently.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe suspected I had a girlfriend. After I told him I liked girls. I\u2019ve been very careful with Cassandra, since, while she\u2019s not my student, she is a student...\u201dA look of guilt crossed her face briefly. \u201cSo we\u2019ve been careful since the beginning.\u201d<br /> <br /> The g-man looked fucking pleased. \u201cGood. If the private investigator continues to find nothing, then your husband\u2019s suspicions will likely not be taken with a great deal of salt.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThus far, when Henry\u2019s confronted me with it, he\u2019s said \u2018You have a girlfriend.\u2019 He\u2019s never said a name, or anything like that. He hasn't even specifically said he thinks it\u2019s a student.\u201d Dr. Cross shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe did accuse Cecilia of being your girlfriend, so it seems unlikely that he knows any specifics,\u201d Jack offered. Dr. Cross smirked a little.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack looked thoughtful. \u201cMay I see your phone again?\u201d She passed it back over, a confused look on her face. He flipped quickly through her text messages, looking for the ones from her husband. After finding a particular one full of accusations about her having a girlfriend, he smiled slightly, nodded, and handed it back. \u201cI do suggest that you not give him any confirmation and hopefully this business will run its course.\u201d<br /> <br /> She sighed. \u201cThe only problem with the waiting game, I\u2019ll be completely honest, is that while I do love Cassandra, I worry... we aren\u2019t really communicating, and I don't know what\u2019s going on in her head. The temptation to just go and see her has been growing. I\u2019ve been fighting it, but it\u2019s gotten increasingly hard. I know, I know, I am an adult, I can deal with it... but I worry about her. She\u2019s still young. Wise beyond her years, but not necessarily patient beyond her years.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHer friend does work for us, we might be able to get some assurances to her...\u201d Billy Mack began.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. Her.\u201d Dr. Cross frowned.<br /> <br /> Jack smirked. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, I feel the same way.\u201d<br /> <br /> That fucking guilty look was back. \u201cNot quite the same way.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave Jack a quelling look. \u201cIt is merely a legitimate avenue to get her this same information, and encourage patience.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAt risk of being horribly judged, there\u2019s something I should tell you before we involve her too much.\u201d She took a deep breath, then let it out and started again. \u201cNo, I\u2019m not gonna put this in a way that blames anyone else. I had a moment of weakness and slept with Naomi. It\u2019s why I\u2019ve been concerned about dealing with her too often. I don\u2019t know what she\u2019s thinking, and she\u2019s a very selfish person. Not wanting to say anything bad about your employee, but she\u2019s a very selfish person. I mean, Cassandra was her friend! She did forgive her fairly easily... and I know they have history, so maybe Naomi was jealous, and... anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf it\u2019s official business, she\u2019ll behave,\u201d Jack promised.<br /> <br /> She looked goddamn dubious. \u201cThat all was over a month ago, before Cassandra and I were serious enough for me to start taking the first steps, towards, in my mind, being honest and changing the direction of my life. I don\u2019t like lying. I felt I owed it to Henry to not lie to him in particular.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstandable - most of us don\u2019t.\u201d Billy Mack smiled. \u201cI do believe that ultimately you are doing the best thing for both of you, even if he doesn\u2019t like it. It\u2019s less harmful than the alternatives, and certainly better for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Just after Greg finished and I popped back into Gabe, Billy Mack let me know that Amy was leaving work. So we decided to hop on that shit before we hit up the Infrastructure at the school. Jack gave Billy Mack a ride over, dropping him off at the parking lot of the school she worked at, then heading around the block. I had grabbed a spot nearby so I could keep an eye on things, without revealing any more of us to these Brotherhood motherfuckers.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack leaned against the hood of the car, cigar lit. Amy stopped when she saw him, a deer in the headlights look on her face. \u201cHello Mrs. Sandoval.\u201d He knocked some ash off his cigar. \u201cI believe it would be in our mutual best interests to have a discussion.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked like she was about to bolt, but she stopped. \u201cWho are you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHas the Brotherhood informed you that someone broke into your house last night?\u201d <br /> <br /> Her jaw tightened. \u201cLet\u2019s say I know what you\u2019re talking about.\u201d She took a step forward, still keeping distance between them. \u201cWhat do you want?\u201d<br /> <br /> He sighed. \u201cWhat I want is to have a discussion with you, that I hope will allow us to resolve a dispute without harm coming to either party.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs this going to be a conversation that involves money changing hands?\u201d she asked suspiciously.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot at this time.\u201d Billy Mack crossed his arms. \u201cMy aim is to determine what course of action could resolve this peaceably.\u201d<br /> <br /> She moved closer. \u201cThis probably isn\u2019t the best place to talk then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded his agreement. \u201cWere would you be more comfortable?\u201d She named a particular Starbucks, and Billy Mack repeated it, mostly for my and Jack\u2019s benefit over the Bluetooth. \u201cI know where that is.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMeet there in ten minutes?\u201d she suggested. Now, the place was about five minutes away, but seeing as that wasn\u2019t precisely time to mobilize a goddamn army she\u2019d need to take us on, a few minutes wouldn\u2019t hurt.<br /> <br /> \u201cI suppose there is no need to drive overly quickly.\u201d He smiled at her and backed away from her car. She kept her eyes on him until she got in, and she drove off quickly. I left myself, figuring Jack would be by to pick him up shortly.<br /> <br /> <br /> She went straight there, and picked a table for two. I got a table a bit away, somewhere I could keep an unobtrusive eye on her. A minute or two before Billy Mack got there, a pair of women came in, taking a seat a bit closer. They seemed interested in her table, so I gave them a glance. After a moment I realized they were two more of the fuckers who\u2019d jumped Nikka. So she had called in a little back up at least. I mentioned it over Bluetooth, quietly.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack, as I said, got there a little later, and Jack a little after him, presumably after having driven around or parked a bit away. Billy Mack got his black coffee and joined her. After he sat down, he got right to the fucking point. \u201cThere is a woman. Nikka.\u201d She didn\u2019t say anything, but it was clear she knew the name. Especially to me, since I already had an eye on her surface thoughts. \u201cI believe we are currently working at cross purposes, regarding her. And, as I said, what I would like is to find some means to resolve this conflict without any further unfortunate incidents like the one that happened at the parking lots outside of Kiki\u2019s\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want us to back off from that woman?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI would at least like to know what it would talk to convince you to.\u201d He inclined his head.<br /> <br /> She glanced away, then back. \u201cLet me give you what context I can. I hope you can understand that I can\u2019t say much, or both of us will end up dead.\u201d <br /> <br /> He smiled. \u201cAnd I wouldn\u2019t want that. It would be terribly inconvenient.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cErnesto is a man whose position in the organization is such that requests are made of him, not demands. The organization wants his services. He is in the middle of a stalking. The organization would like the entire process sped up, as he tends to like to savor his hunts and kills for an extraordinary amount of time.\u201d She took a deep breath. \u201cAnd so a particularly large amount of money was offered to us if we were to,\u201d she paused, \u201cto get him back on track. It was thought that the backlash on us would be minimal. There are some very very old feuds that he is involved with, there is a power balance... I don\u2019t know half of the weird labyrinthian things going on.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d Billy Mack nodded thoughtfully.<br /> <br /> She shrugged slightly, looking off to the side. \u201cI certainly wasn\u2019t going to be the one to actually kill her - I think it\u2019s fairly likely that he will kill the one who does that, at least, to make an example of them. And if he comes for all of us, that way I am likely to not be first, which would give me some time to run. I would rather run from him than the Brotherhood. His resources are more limited.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack took a sip of coffee. \u201cMy interest in this is in keeping her alive. I have my reasons for that. Having discovered what I have, I had been concerned that this was more than a personal hunt on his part.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Brotherhood has bigger fish to fry than a small time organ vendor and drug dealer. But she is powerful enough to she provides him an actual challenge, which the Brotherhood missions, to his mind, don\u2019t. They are work and this is pleasure.\u201d She shrugged again.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo dissuading you is going to be far easier than dissuading him,\u201d Billy Mack suggested. <br /> <br /> She frowned. \u201cProbably? He hunts for pleasure. He\u2019s been hunting her for a while, I think. He\u2019s had us do some surveillance, but it\u2019s important to him that it is his project, his hunt, his kill.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack nodded. \u201cI believe I can understand that mentality.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSeems like mostly macho posturing to me. But at the end of the day, they are not going to command us to do something in contrary to what the organization wants. We were offered the job through an anonymous cats-paw, so that he would not be able to confront the person who put us up to it. And most importantly, there is no sanctioned-by-the-leadership mission to take his kill away. Just \u2018someone important\u2019 that will make it worth our while, presuming he does not kill us.\u201d She sipped her drink. \u201cIt\u2019s what everyone decided to do, and it\u2019s the kinda thing where deciding you\u2019re going to make a moral objection probably won\u2019t work in your favor. I don\u2019t care myself. If it was an actual job, I wouldn\u2019t have a problem doing it, but I don\u2019t see any need for it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, in your opinion, if something happens to him in the course of this, are they likely to take action?\u201d Billy Mack raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> She let out a deep breath. \u201cI have no idea. He\u2019s a major enough asset that he can tell them to just wait a few weeks or months or years or whatever to finish what he\u2019s doing. So they must value him. But I don\u2019t know if they would come after you just for interfering with him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd it would just be him? This is not official business?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs far as what was told to me, and I get told things on a need to know basis. It\u2019s possible I was told that and still have it be that he\u2019s been stalking her for someone else in the Brotherhood. They don\u2019t usually work like that though.\u201d She tapped on the side of her cup fucking nervously.<br /> <br /> The g-man nodded. \u201cIt would be inefficient and counterproductive.\u201d<br /> <br /> She chuckled wryly. \u201cNot sure that\u2019s an issue. He always has a large number of apprentices, so that he can lose a large number of them on jobs and have the few who stick around rise in the organization.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou seem to be doing well.\u201d Billy Mack saluted her with his cup.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m the only one whose house you infiltrated and who has had her role in this job compromised. I\u2019m doing less well than any of us who are still alive.\u201d She looked down at the table.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack shrugged. \u201cIf he hadn\u2019t driven your car to a meeting, I wouldn\u2019t have had any way to find you. It is his fault, not yours.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged back. \u201cWe do as instructed.\u201d After a moment of silence, she continued, \u201cHe didn\u2019t even seem angry. He just said of course we failed, anyone we could successfully kill wouldn\u2019t be the target of one of his hunts. And laughed it off.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe had been under the impression that he had sent you, perhaps to test her defenses, intending you to fail,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is not impossible that he set up someone to pay us to do it, to see if we would go along with it or not, or test her defenses or something. I don\u2019t have any way of knowing really.\u201d She looked into her cup.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack frowned sympathetically. \u201cIt has put you in a very difficult position. I do not envy you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA lot of us have had little coincidental problems since we decided to go after her. You noticed my car, other people have found themselves, while not actually at risk, in potentially compromising situations since then, in order to remind us of our place.\u201d From her mind, I picked up that one of the apprentices\u2019 car had been the only car in the parking lot of a bank as it got robbed. The thieves didn\u2019t drive off in it, but it was in clear fucking view, and made its way back to the apprentice\u2019s house before investigators did. They had an alibi, and there wasn\u2019t any further evidence linking them to the crime, so like she said, not actually at risk, just compromising situations. \u201cIt does make me think he is not behind it, as he is not quite that capricious.\u201d She sighed. \u201cIt does pay better than a teacher\u2019s salary.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI should hope so, considering the poor state of educational funding in this nation.\u201d Billy Mack nodded gravely.<br /> <br /> My mind reading showed she was on the level, other than hiding the fact she was attracted to Mr. Not-a-Farmer with how much she simultaneously disliked him. I went looking for a memory of her introduction to the organization, and got a montage of research, prompted by one of her student\u2019s report on Egyptian-looking architecture found in the city. She saw a pattern in it, and tracked it down to a particular set of GPS coordinates. When she went to the coordinates, she found a man who knew what she\u2019d been investigating, who introduced her to the organization.<br /> <br /> Digging a little further, I found that she did work for them as a shadowy assassin, \u2018nudging\u2019 history into the right track, as far as the Brotherhood was concerned. All in all, from all the glimpses I got, this had the God-Machine\u2019s fingerprints all the fuck over it. Either an Angel was behind it, and was using this network to fulfill goddamn occult matrices, or a Demon was and they were using it to foil them. It didn\u2019t make me feel better to pop up my mental map of the city and realize those coordinates Amy had calculated were in spitting distance of Blue Sun\u2019s headquarters.<br /> <br /> Cornelius\u2019s part in this was about what she\u2019d said. According to what he\u2019d told them, he was over 200 years old and the \u2018Grand Master\u2019. He trained the Harvesters contingent, and put them through the ritual to become one. He made large groups of them, and weeded them out, leaving a handful of competent Harvesters to become the new leaders in that city when he was called elsewhere.<br /> <br /> For curiosity and not much else, I looked into her memory of the meeting with Team Tomorrow. They\u2019d heard of her group as a group of assassins for hire, nothing to do with the Brotherhood. They\u2019d wanted to hire them to kill certain mages, as best I could fucking tell - they talked about people who could alter reality, and the implications were much more mage than Angels or Demons. They wouldn\u2019t tell them anything more personal about the targets without them accepting, and the Harvesters did turn them down.<br /> <br /> I checked into her memories of Skeevy Larry, since it had come up she was scared of him. It turns out he was Team Tomorrow\u2019s backup plan - she\u2019d crossed paths with him as he was going in after their meeting. She didn\u2019t know whether he accepted, but I couldn\u2019t blame her for being scared after just the one meeting. He was carrying a pair of large snakes, both with human eyes and one of them with two heads. When he greeted them, he made a suggestive tongue gesture at hr, and his tongue had a face. Jesus fuck that guy was creepy. I made a note to warn Miranda, in case she got caught in whatever it was. If we were lucky, Team Tomorrow was sending him after the Tik Tok men and there would be some mutual destruction going around.<br /> <br /> Lastly, before Billy Mack wrapped things up, I looked into the wards that were set up in her house. I found a memory of a gee named Gabe. A black man in a trench coat and sunglasses, he was the Brotherhood\u2019s go to guy for that sort of thing, as far as Amy knew. She\u2019d met him three times, each for that kind of occult or warding thing.<br /> <br /> When I gave him the signal, he smiled at her. \u201cWhile I fear I won\u2019t be able to resolve things with Ernesto quite this civilly...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is a very civil individual.\u201d She smirked to the side.<br /> <br /> He chuckled. \u201cYes, but I suspect we will at best have a very civil conversation about how he is not going to break off this hunt.\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged. \u201cI don\u2019t really know enough about him or his history to know how well that will work.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t suppose you can give me a way to get a hold of him to have our civil conversation?\u201d Her response made it obvious she did, and I got a brief glimpse of her using a phone, calling one Wayne Hardy. Billy Mack didn\u2019t push it when she didn\u2019t give it up to him though. \u201cI don\u2019t want to ask you anything that would get you or your family in trouble.\u201d She gave him a brief smile in thanks.<br /> <br /> She got out of there as quickly as fucking possible once Billy Mack wrapped things up. We all left separately, as we\u2019d come and I warned Billy Mack via text to stay himself, so anyone with clairvoyance wouldn\u2019t get his other forms if they hadn\u2019t already. Not that I put it in those terms, but I could clarify later. <br /> <br /> <br /> Naomi had had a few conversations to have with some of her girls at the school, so she met us there. Again, we staggered our arrivals, going in the closet in the science building one at a time to minimize suspicion. We had to time things fucking carefully, shifting in what bits we needed before we went into the closet, since it would be that much harder in there. Still, there wasn\u2019t much of a problem, being as it was late afternoon and the closet was tucked kinda out of the way.<br /> <br /> I popped in my rivet gun, and Naomi her venom spitting mandibles. Billy Mack had a rivet gun out, and had switched on his increased intelligence circuits for once we got the guns down. Jack had better eyes and brains himself. He didn\u2019t need any demonic form bits to tear through their armor plating.<br /> <br /> Once we were all in, we all aimed carefully and I set things up to Check the Backdrop. After our first shots, the guns activated and started firing wildly, not coming near to any of us. Between Jack\u2019s fists, mine and the g-man\u2019s guns and Naomi\u2019s venom, they went down quickly, but not before blasting the door to the hallway outside down, and scorching the wall behind it.<br /> <br /> I thought quick and asked Naomi if she carried any hairspray. I considered the scene for a moment, then tossed the hairspray and my spare lighter on the ground, as if a student had been playing around with a homemade \u2018flamethrower\u2019 and it had gotten out of hand, so they fled the scene. Then I brought out the prop door from my bolthole and had Naomi web it shut.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack had already started on hacking the computer there. Once I rejoined them, Naomi looked over at me. \u201cSo how\u2019d your meeting go?\u201d The mandibles made it fucking weird.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo...\u201d I gave them the rundown on what I\u2019d gotten from her memories.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat sounds like a line of bullshit Kilroy would feed a bunch of minions...\u201d Naomi glanced over at the g-man when I described what the Brotherhood did.<br /> <br /> Jack quirked an eyebrow. \u201cAnd you\u2019re certain you didn\u2019t do this?\u201d he asked Billy Mack.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave him a dirty look. \u201cI\u2019m certain.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou do have that compartmentalized brain power.\u201d Naomi shook a finger at him.<br /> <br /> I went on to describe the Harvester Grand master shit. \u201cYou think he ever actually\u2019s left and started a new group, or that this is just a this city thing and that\u2019s just a story they\u2019re feeding them?\u201d Naomi asked. I shrugged. When I brought up Team Tomorrow, her eyes got big. \u201cSo, Team Tomorrow knows about the Brotherhood? Is there a Rolodex of villains just lying around?\u201d<br /> <br /> I shook my head quickly. \u201cThey know about the Harvesters. I didn\u2019t get any indication they knew about the organization behind them.\u201d I kept going.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack chuckled when I got to the part about Skeevy Larry. \u201cPerhaps they were sending him after the Tik Tok men. Then, even if he fails, it would mean he gets erased from history. A win in itself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou mean like Fernando the devil was erased from history?\u201d Naomi asked. <br /> <br /> \u201cNot at all like that if you know about it.\u201d I rolled my shoulders, ignoring her pout.<br /> <br /> \u201cSpeaking of erasing people,\u201d Billy Mack began in one of the most goddamn ominous speaker/sentence opening combinations I\u2019d ever experienced up until that point, \u201cDr. Cross...\u201d<br /> <br /> Naomi interrupted him. \u201cOh yeah, how is Dr. Criss Cross?\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack gave her a stern look and continued, \u201cis being watched and followed by a Francisco Guzman.\u201d I knew the guy. Decent enough. Billy Mack gave his rundown on what those two had learned and told Dr. Cross about. \u201cAnd at any rate, her husband has forgotten that he once strongly believed that she was having an affair with someone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s handy.\u201d I gave him an approving nod.<br /> <br /> \u201cIndeed. That particular item of data has been erased. It should expedite things by decreasing his patience with the whole affair at least.\u201d He looked back down at the computer.<br /> <br /> \u201cSee, that\u2019s a power I don\u2019t need to have,\u201d Naomi mused. \u201cI would so abuse that.\u201d Jack passed along Dr. Cross\u2019s concerns for Cassandra\u2019s patience. \u201cI\u2019ll tell her - well, her goddess will tell her. You guys need to hurry this up so we can have a threeway.\u201d She stretched, all but fucking preening. \u201cOkay, my turn. Nick is not a regular distributor of cocaine, but she does do it sometimes. She was cagey about telling me much, and just said if I wanted to buy, I needed to go through her. You know, so that if things get busted no one would know my face. I suggested my appreciation and where I was gonna put my face and she held me at bay cause she\u2019s a fucking tease.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot according to Heather,\u201d Billy Mack muttered.<br /> <br /> Naomi pouted. \u201cShe talked about her new flavored lipstick and everything. And then she just left!\u201d She blew her hair out of her face. \u201cBitch. Still gonna fuck her though.\u201d She crossed her arms. \u201cI know about playing hard to get.\u201d<br /> <br /> Billy Mack raised an eyebrow. \u201cI was about to say, such behavior does not seem unfamiliar.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t do that, Liz does!\u201d Naomi countered.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo about that potential in-road with security...?\u201d Jack raised an eyebrow questioningly.<br /> <br /> Naomi shook her head. \u201cI haven\u2019t slept with Nick yet, you can\u2019t do that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Jack rolled his eyes. \u201cI\u2019m just saying, it would be nice if you could get information and then extricate her from the situation. I don\u2019t necessarily want her specifically caught.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Right.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is now forewarned, after all.\u201d Billy Mack turned to us. \u201cWe are in.\u201d<br /> <br /> From what the g-man found, this was the central control for defenses, but without the hub, it had no way to actually communicate with the other spokes. Billy Mack kept working as he explained, typing away on Vivian\u2019s laptop, looking back at the screen frequently. \u201cI should be able to use the command code here to write myself a control program that I can transmit to them, so our future forays into the campus\u2019 old Infrastructure will involve much less laser fire.\u201d<br /> <br /> The other pieces of Infrastructure were under the gym and, of course, the goddamn admin building. Those were for a different night though, some time after I had a chance to unload this Infrastructure. All in all, we loaded the shit fairly efficiently, Naomi and Billy Mack breaking it down and handing it off to Jack, who schlepped it over to me keeping the door to my bolthole open. We got it done in about an hour and a half.<br /> <br /> <br /> We left like we came, one at a time. Naomi looked at me questioningly as we left, but I shooed her on. I was just behind Naomi though, so I saw Adria stop her, looking a little agitated, but that may have just been because she was talking to Naomi. I started walking slower to make sure nothing was up, but after not too long, they parted ways, Naomi indicating she wanted to be kissed just before Adria stormed off. Naomi sent a text a few minutes later, \u2018Adria says campus is about to be crawling with vampires and wanted to let me know in case they were a threat to my master.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u2018The timing of this with the loss of the books is suspicious to me...\u2019 I sent out that text and called Dr. Carpenter. <br /> <br /> \u201cHello?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHello Dr. Carpenter, this is Gabe Norton, again. Sorry to bother but I was wondering if the fact that I was just informed there will be a large number of vampires gathering on campus tonight possibly have anything to do with the books?\u201d I leaned against my car.<br /> <br /> There was a pause. \u201cNot that I know of. Hargrave is aware of part of what\u2019s going on, but he doesn\u2019t really interact with the books. He knows they are gone, I don't know how much of an interest he has in them though.\u201d<br /> <br /> I tapped my fingers on my car window. \u201cCould he be the leak? Known enough to know where they were kept but not exactly which book to pull?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s possible. I hope not. Dr. Hargrave is older than I am...\u201d He let out a sigh. \u201cHe\u2019s focused on mind and emotion control. I don\u2019t know his powers list, but he\u2019s been kicking around a bit, moving from university to university, fudging records for his age. We leave him alone, and we get to ask him questions about weird things he might have come across. Also, student corpses don\u2019t show up. It would be out of character for him to compromise the university, unless he really wanted or needed something in there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI getcha.\u201d I stood up and started pacing a little. \u201cAs a question, so I don\u2019t have to bother you every time I hear any little thing, do you mind telling me who all is involved in watching over the books?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe only people who really know are myself, Dr. Hazard and Dr. Isaacs, the one who fled to Iowa. He's a magic using shapeshifter.\u201d He chuckled. \u201cSomewhat ideal to finish out our trio, though he's not the same... sort of shapeshifter as I am. Dr. Hazard is fairly certain he did not take them, however. Others know it as a very special collection, donors, etc.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nodded. \u201cSo if someone else shows up knowing more than that, there would be a cause for concern.\u201d<br /> <br /> He made an affirmative noise. \u201cDr. Hargrave only knows as part of the deal, him being left alone and kept informed, and us having an old, powerful resource for consulting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow does he get along with Stein?\u201d I flipped my silver dollar in the air and caught it.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey avoid each other.\u201d He thought a moment. \u201cI don\u2019t believe I\u2019ve ever seen them together. They are rather opposites, since Stein wants to be involved with absolutely everything and Hargrave mostly wants to be left alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shifted the phone to my other shoulder. \u201cFair enough. Well, again, sorry to bother you, it\u2019s just the timing seemed fucking suspicious, and I realized I didn\u2019t know who on campus should or shouldn\u2019t know things. Thanks for the heads up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo problem.\u201d He cleared his throat. \u201cA further heads up - part of the deal is that if someone messes with him, we will back him up, and vice versa. He\u2019s more likely to get help from me than Dr. Hazard - Hazard\u2019s a little leery of him because he\u2019s a vampire. Also, he\u2019s told us about some other entity on campus, along those lines. He was cagey about what it was, but he said it didn\u2019t think it was going to affect us. Called it a feeder.\u201d<br /> <br /> I chuckled to myself. Not sure Clytemnestra would like that name. \u201cGotcha. Thanks again.\u201d I called the rest of them and passed along everything to them, including my suspicions. <br /> <br /> \u201cI wonder if they are who he was threatening me with. I assumed other vampires, but...\u201d Naomi mused. \u201cHe did just say \u2018other powerful people\u2019. I\u2019m not sure about being called a feeder. I guess it works as a taxonomy though.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s more of a classification, really,\u201d Billy Mack pointed out.<br /> <br /> <br /> There was time before sundown, so we all went to Whacko Bob\u2019s to go memory fishing. On the way there, I got a text from Liz, \u2018Ha ha, Naomi is so horny-pissed at Nick right now. It\u2019s aggravating to be rattling around in her head, but it\u2019s kinda hilarious from an outside perspective.\u2019 I shook my head and rolled my eyes at Naomi when I passed her in the shop.<br /> <br /> Mary was there at the shop as expected, and Billy Mack immediately got to flirting. I started browsing, watching her through my sunglasses. There was way more resistance getting in than was usual, but I did manage to get eyes on her surface thoughts, which were pretty goddamn focused on how things were in order and that was good, and it was good that they were in order. A little obsessive for my taste, but to Billy Mack his own, for fucking sure.<br /> <br /> Going back for specific memories was difficult, like wading through molasses. There was nothing human about her thought processes - she was not and never had been human. I got there in time, finding a memory of Gabe the trench-coated sunglasses wearing guy. It didn\u2019t help that \u2018now\u2019 for her was any time in the past decade or so. A lot of the time I spent looking was just being more precise than that.<br /> <br /> I did manage to get that the most recent time he\u2019d come in was earlier today. He was in good spirits, and greeted Mary warmly as he started wandering around the store, whistling \u2018Every Breath You Take\u2019. I made a note all the shit he bought. It didn\u2019t mean anything to me, but I figured that Billy Mack would be able to make something of it. I also got a credit card name and number, but the name was about a mile long and Greek. Despite its length, \u2018Gabe\u2019 couldn\u2019t be gotten from any of it, so I didn\u2019t have a hell of a lot of hope for it being his real name.<br /> <br /> I wasn\u2019t really one to talk, but the man was a stickler for his sunglasses. At no point in any of the memories I got of him, Mary\u2019s or Amy\u2019s, did he ever show his eyes. Still, \u2018doesn\u2019t show his eyes\u2019, \u2018black\u2019, \u2018knows his way around Whacko Bob\u2019s\u2019 and \u2018answers to Gabe\u2019 doesn\u2019t get you very far on an identity search. I mean, half of them apply to me most of the time, and I was working on another quarter, what with all the visits lately. I had seen him at Kiki\u2019s before, so there was that.<br /> <br /> Because it was a day for satisfying curiosity, I went looking into her background, into that sword that Billy Mack said she was afraid of. I got a faraway memory of an Icelandic looking fucker who\u2019d summoned away from soaring through the Shadow and bound her exceedingly powerful self into the form she had now, setting her to the task of guarding a particular chalice with Hindu symbology on it. The sword was the focus of her binding and served as a Bane for her. As long as she kept it safe, he said, fate would conspire to keep the sword away from her. If she lost it, fate would ensure it found her in the worst way. The deal was to guard it for 1001 years, then he would come and collect it and summon another guardian. A brush with her surface thoughts with the added context let me know she had 546 years, 11 months and 8 days of service left, before she could go home and be the apex predator she was supposed to be.<br /> <br /> I was losing focus, but while I was in there, and by no fucking means guaranteed to be able to get back in again, I decided to check on Whacko Bob himself. He was a raggedy looking bastard, definitely not the same Icelandic gee, with a color scheme to blind a bat. He\u2019d left her to watch the shop while he went acquiring things, promising to be back in a year or two. He did know about her task with the chalice. <br /> <br /> Billy Mack got out of there with a pair of watermelons. I bought a few things for Miranda, things that looked like the sort of supplies she kept stocked and a couple of things that looked nice, at least as nice as my budget allows. When we got to the car, I grinned at Billy Mack. \u201cShe is way out of your league, pal.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know about that,\u201d he protested.<br /> <br /> I passed along what I learned. \u201cShe was far more interested in everything being in place than any part of your conversation.\u201d <br /> <br /> He shrugged. \u201cThat just makes sense. It\u2019s not as if she is human. Or as if I am attempting to engage her in a long term relationship after all.\u201d I shook my head and got back to the task at hand. When I passed along the supply list, Billy Mack thought for a moment. \u201cHe is most likely a Hedge maze of the Apostle of the Dark One variety. They call upon a greater power for their magical paradigm, usually one of an odd or sinister nature. That particular set of ingredients would likely be for some sort of divination.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is my shocked face.\u201d I smirked at him.<br /> <br /> <br /> Naomi took the lead on the vampire situation, watching Hargrave\u2019s office and planning to split off into spiders and scattering herself around the meeting. The rest of us loitered vaguely nearby, trying to get eyes on who the fuck showed up. At the least, we could likely figure out which of the three factions Hargrave was with.<br /> <br /> Naomi let us know when Hargrave left, and when he arrived at the admin building, but of fucking course that\u2019s where they were meeting. We managed to get into place in time to see Valefar\u2019s vampire contact, and Sanderson\u2019s pet mind fucker walk in, pegging this meeting - and Sanderson\u2019s mind fucker - firmly in the young punks\u2019 camp. At least, if this were a political meeting.<br /> <br /> Spiders do in fact make pretty damn good spies, so after the vampires all dispersed, and Naomi undispersed herself, she was able to give us a pretty good accounting. \u201cShort version - he didn\u2019t take the book. Long version - he let folks know that the books were stolen, and was wondering if a group called the Ordo Dracul have them, as they were interested in them at one point in time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s the magic ones, the ones who Langley works for,\u201d I mused.<br /> <br /> She nodded. \u201cIf someone can determine whether they have it, he will give them a boon. If someone just finds them, he might be able to work out a boon, but it\u2019s only guaranteed if it\u2019s about the Ordo Dracul. There was other business I could parrot, but nothing that meant anything to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> I walked a coin over my knuckles. \u201cWas he the bossman?\u201d<br /> <br /> She shook her head. \u201cHe was just hosting. They rotate meeting places, apparently, and he\u2019d asked for it to be here, since he had the business about the books. They don\u2019t seem to have a real leader.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell damn it.\u201d I stood up for the bench.<br /> <br /> Billy Mack stood as well. \u201cIt does rule him out.\u201d<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cWhich is good, I guess. And we do have contacts with the Ordo Dracul. Not great ones, but...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt does seem like something Langley is not likely to be privy to.\u201d Billy Mack nodded. \u201cWe would have to actually speak to the vampires in question, who may or may not be inclined to share such information with us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd may be inclined to shove us in a box for asking questions about things we shouldn\u2019t know about,\u201d Jack pointed out.<br /> <br /> Naomi frowned. \u201cI don\u2019t like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> I snorted. \u201cWe could always trade them one of the fucking Angels in my bolthole.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs long as we\u2019re not giving them a live one. I could use a bite.\u201d Naomi pouted. \u201cIn the meantime, I have Capri Sun.\u201d She matched actions to words and started sucking on the fucking straw.<br /> <br /> \u201cAssuming we\u2019re comfortable assisting in their studies in such a direction,\u201d Billy Mack looked to me.<br /> <br /> I shrugged. \u201cI was mostly kidding. The ones we have left are mostly low ranking. They might not be worth enough, but they\u2019re probably not too big a risk to us. Anyway, it\u2019s a direction to go. But that\u2019s tomorrow\u2019s shit to deal with.\u201d<br /> <br /> I got a text from Liz. \u2018Naomi\u2019s probably gonna go strike out with Nick, then go seduce someone else to get her self esteem up. Unless you guys need me, and then I\u2019ll have to switch to Liz to get her away from here.\u2019<br /> <br /> \u201cI think all our shit is tomorrow\u2019s shit, as far as I\u2019m concerned. I need to hit the hay. You guys do whatever the fuck you feel like.\u201d I waved, and headed back to my car. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I did get to sleep eventually. It turns out Miranda did kinda like the presents I\u2019d bought, which were definitely nothing but a romantic gesture that also happened to back up my detective little-c cover. They certainly weren\u2019t to prove that I\u2019m a much better partner than any old flame who may have suddenly learned she\u2019s still alive, who'd obviously never bothered to fucking check properly. Why would you ask?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LIX</i><br /> <br /> Check Backdrop proved very helpful on automated guns. They pretty much couldn\u2019t hit.<br /> <br /> I am short on time and don\u2019t have a lot else to add, but Comments and Questions are welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core